nto de software"],"ru":["тестирование в nim","std/unittest","ошибки компиляции c++","сложные типы ffi","проектные конвенции","отладка ошибок","организация тестов","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["الاختبارات في نيم","std/unittest","أخطاء ترجمة c++","أنواع ffi معقدة","اتفاقيات المشروع","تصحيح الأخطاء","تنظيم الاختبارات","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"mratsim","repo":"tattletale","repoPath":"mratsim/tattletale","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.477Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"testing","description":"Nim testing conventions, unittest framework, and C++ compatibility patterns","bodyPreview":"## What I do\n\nI provide guidance for writing tests in Nim that:\n- Work correctly with the `std/unittest` framework\n- Avoid C++ compilation errors with complex FFI types like `TorchTensor`\n- Follow project conventions for test organization\n\n## When to use me\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Writing new tests for any workspace module\n- Debugging C++ compilation errors in test code\n- Organizing test fixtures and test data\n\n## The unittest framework\n\nNim''s standard library provides a simple testing framework","body":"## What I do\n\nI provide guidance for writing tests in Nim that:\n- Work correctly with the `std/unittest` framework\n- Avoid C++ compilation errors with complex FFI types like `TorchTensor`\n- Follow project conventions for test organization\n\n## When to use me\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Writing new tests for any workspace module\n- Debugging C++ compilation errors in test code\n- Organizing test fixtures and test data\n\n## The unittest framework\n\nNim''s standard library provides a simple testing framework:\n\n```nim\nimport std/unittest\n\nsuite \"my module tests\":\n  test \"addition works\":\n    check 1 + 1 == 2\n\n  test \"string handling\":\n    let result = \"hello\".toUpperAscii()\n    check result == \"HELLO\"\n```\n\n**Key procs:**\n- `suite(name, body)` - Group related tests\n- `test(name, body)` - Define a single test\n- `check(expr)` - Assert expression is true, prints failed value on failure\n- `doAssert(expr)` - Like `check` but raises on failure (use for invariants)\n- `submitTest(result)` - Submit test result from a procedure\n\n## Critical pattern: Wrap tests in a proc\n\n### The problem\n\nWhen you declare variables at module scope (top-level) in Nim tests, the generated C++ code uses `= {}` initialization:\n\n```cpp\nTorchTensor expectedTensor = {};  // This fails!\nexpectedTensor = myFunction(a, b);\n```\n\nThe C++ `torch::Tensor` type (and other FFI types with `cppNonPod`) does not accept brace initialization. This causes:\n```\nerror: ambiguous overload for ''operator='' (operand types are ''at::Tensor'' and ''<brace-enclosed initializer list>'')\n```\n\n### The solution\n\nAlways wrap test code in a `proc main()`:\n\n```nim\nimport std/unittest, workspace/libtorch\n\nproc generateTensor(): TorchTensor =\n  # This works - Nim generates:\n  # auto result = myFunction(a, b);\n  arange(10, kFloat32)\n\nproc runTests*() =\n  suite \"tensor tests\":\n    test \"generate tensor\":\n      let tensor = generateTensor()\n      check tensor.numel() == 10\n\nwhen isMainModule:\n  runTests()\n```\n\nThis generates proper C++:\n```cpp\nauto tensor = generateTensor();  // No {} initialization\n```\n\n## Test organization\n\n### Fixture file pattern\n\nTests that load files should follow this pattern:\n\n```nim\nimport std/unittest, std/os, workspace/safetensors, workspace/libtorch\n\nconst FIXTURES_DIR = currentSourcePath().parentDir() / \"fixtures\"\n\nproc main() =\n  suite \"safetensors loading\":\n    test \"load fixture\":\n      let fixturePath = FIXTURES_DIR / \"model.safetensors\"\n      check fileExists(fixturePath)\n\n      var mf = memfiles.open(fixturePath, mode = fmRead)\n      defer: mf.close()\n\n      let (st, offset) = safetensors.load(mf)\n      check st.tensors.len > 0\n\nwhen isMainModule:\n  main()\n```\n\nKey points:\n- Use `currentSourcePath().parentDir() / \"fixtures\"` for fixture paths\n- Use `memfiles.open` with `defer: mf.close()`\n- Return early or use `continue` for missing fixtures\n\n### Test constants\n\nDefine test parameters as `const` at module level:\n\n```nim\nconst Patterns = [\"gradient\", \"alternating\", \"repeating\"]\nconst Shapes: array[4, seq[int64]] = [\n  @[int64 8],\n  @[int64 4, 4],\n  @[int64 2, 3, 4],\n  @[int64 3, 2, 2, 2]\n]\nconst TestedDtypes = [F64, F32, F16, I64, I32, I16, I8, U64, U32, U16, U8]\n```\n\n### Helper procedures\n\nExtract reusable logic into `proc` with `*` export:\n\n```nim\nproc generateExpectedTensor*(pattern: string, shape: seq[int64], dtype: ScalarKind): TorchTensor =\n  let shapeRef = shape.asTorchView()\n  let numel = shape.product()\n\n  case pattern\n  of \"gradient\":\n    arange(numel, dtype).reshape(shapeRef).to(dtype)\n  of \"alternating\":\n    let flat = arange(numel, kInt64)\n    let modVal = (flat % 2).to(kFloat64)\n    modVal.reshape(shapeRef).to(dtype)\n  else:\n    raise newException(ValueError, \"Unknown pattern: \" & pattern)\n```\n\nNote: Each branch of a `case` must assign to `result`.\n\n## Running tests\n\nEach module has a task defined in `config.nims` for running its tests:\n\n```bash\n# Test toktoktok\nnim test_toktoktok\n\n# Test libtorch\nnim test_libtorch\n\n# Test safetensors\nnim test_safetensors\n```\n\nThe command `nim test_toktoktok` compiles and runs all test files in `workspace/toktoktok/tests/` that start with `test_` or `t_`.\n\n### Compilation settings\n\nThe project uses:\n- `--path:.` - Makes `workspace/module` imports work\n- Tests compiled with: `nim cpp -r` plus flags for output and cache directories\n\n### Fixture files\n\nFor this project, fixtures are in:\n```bash\nworkspace/toktoktok/tests/tokenizers/\n```\n\nReference fixtures using:\n```nim\nconst FIXTURES_DIR = currentSourcePath().parentDir() / \"tokenizers\"\n```\n\n## Common errors and fixes\n\n### \"undeclared field\" with parameter shadowing\n\nIf you have a parameter named `shape` and access a field `info.shape`:\n```nim\nproc generateExpectedTensor*(pattern: string, shape: seq[int64], ...): TorchTensor =\n  for info in tensors:  # error: ''shape'' shadows info.shape\n    check info.shape == shape\n```\n\nFix: Rename parameter to avoid shadowing:\n```nim\nproc generateExpectedTensor*(pattern: string, shapeSeq: seq[int64], ...): TorchTensor =\n  for info in tensors:\n    check info.shape == shapeSeq  # Now works\n```\n\n### Case statement not returning\n\nEach branch of a case must explicitly assign to `result`:\n```nim\nproc foo(x: int): int =\n  case x\n  of 1: result = 10  # Must use ''result =''\n  of 2: 20             # ERROR: doesn''t assign!\n```\n\n## How to add a new test\n\n### Step 1: Create the test file\n\nFollow the naming convention: `test_*.nim` or `t_*.nim` in the module''s `tests/` directory.\n\n```nim\n# workspace/my_module/tests/test_myfeature.nim\n\nimport std/unittest, std/os\nimport workspace/my_module\n\nproc runMyFeatureTests*() =\n  suite \"my feature tests\":\n    test \"basic functionality\":\n      let result = myModule.function()\n      check result == expectedValue\n\nwhen isMainModule:\n  runMyFeatureTests()\n```\n\n### Step 2: Run the test\n\nThe test will be discovered automatically by the test command:\n\n```bash\n# If it''s in my_module:\nnim c -r --task:test_my_module\n```\n\nOr run all tests for the module:\n```bash\nnim test_my_module\n```\n\n### Step 3: Add test fixtures (if needed)\n\nCreate a `fixtures/` directory and add test data:\n\n```bash\nworkspace/my_module/tests/fixtures/\n```\n\nReference in test code:\n```nim\nconst FIXTURES_DIR = currentSourcePath().parentDir() / \"fixtures\"\nlet fixturePath = FIXTURES_DIR / \"test_data.bin\"\n```\n\n### Checklist for new tests\n\n- [ ] File name starts with `test_` or `t_`\n- [ ] Located in `workspace/module/tests/`\n- [ ] Test code wrapped in `proc runTests*()`\n- [ ] Has `when isMainModule: runTests()` at the end\n- [ ] Uses `defer` for resource cleanup (files, etc.)\n- [ ] Helper procedures exported with `*`\n- [ ] Constants defined at module level with `const`\n\n## Python test vector generation\n\nFor AI/ML modules, test vectors are generated via Python scripts using torch and safetensors.\n\n### Directory structure\n\n```\nworkspace/module/\n├── tests/\n│   ├── test_module.nim          # Nim tests\n│   ├── fixtures/                # Generated fixture files\n│   │   ├── model.safetensors\n│   │   └── tokenizer.json\n│   └── testgen/                 # Python test vector generators\n│       └── generate_vectors.py\n```\n\n### Convention\n\n- **Python 3.12** standard for all test vector generation (matches vLLM/SGLang)\n- **Single root `pyproject.toml`** with `[dependency-groups]` for shared dependencies:\n  ```toml\n  [dependency-groups]\n  test-vectors = [\n      \"torch>=2.0.0\",\n      \"safetensors>=0.7.0\",\n      \"transformers>=4.40.0\",\n      \"numpy>=2.4.2\",\n  ]\n  ```\n- **Run generators** with: `uv run --group test-vectors python workspace/module/tests/testgen/generate_vectors.py`\n\n### Example testgen script\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport numpy as np\nfrom safetensors.numpy import save_file\nimport os\n\nFIXTURES_DIR = os.path.join(\n    os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(__file__)),\n    \"fixtures\",\n)\n\ndef generate_vandermonde():\n    x = torch.arange(1, 6, dtype=torch.float32)\n    vandermonde = torch.vander(x, increasing=True).T\n    return vandermonde.to(torch.bfloat16).view(torch.uint16).numpy()\n\ndef main():\n    fixtures = {\n        \"BF16_vandermonde_5x5\": generate_vandermonde(),\n    }\n    save_file(fixtures, os.path.join(FIXTURES_DIR, \"vandermonde.safetensors\"))\n    print(\"Fixtures generated\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\n### Fixture regeneration\n\nWhen adding new test vectors, regenerate the fixture files:\n\n```bash\nuv run --group test-vectors python workspace/module/tests/testgen/generate_vectors.py\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:24:55.664Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Nim Development Agents requiring standardized testing frameworks and C++ compatibility.","zh":"适用于需要标准化测试框架和C++兼容性的Nim开发代理。","ja":"Nim開発エージェントが標準化されたテストフレームワークとC++の互換性を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"표준화된 테스트 프레임워크와 C++ 호환성을 요구하는 Nim 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo Nim que requieren marcos de prueba estandarizados y compatibilidad con C++.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement Nim nécessitant des cadres de tests standardisés et une compatibilité C++.","de":"Ideal für Nim-Entwicklungsagenten, die standardisierte Testframeworks und C++-Kompatibilität erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de desenvolvimento Nim que exigem estruturas de teste padronizadas e compatibilidade com C++.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки Nim, требующих стандартизированных тестовых фреймворков и совместимости с C++.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير Nim الذين يحتاجون إلى إطارات اختبار معيارية ومتوافقة مع C++."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write robust tests leveraging Nim''s std/unittest framework, handle complex FFI types like TorchTensor, and adhere to project conventions for test organization and debugging C++ compilation errors.","zh":"赋予代理编写强大的测试的能力，利用Nim的std/unittest框架，处理复杂的FFI类型，如TorchTensor，并遵循项目惯例进行测试组织和调试C++编译错误。","ja":"エージェントに強力なテストを書く能力を与え、Nimのstd/unittestフレームワークを利用し、TorchTensorのような複雑なFFIタイプを処理し、テストの組織とC++コンパイルエラーのデバッグについてプロジェクトの規約に従う。","ko":"에이전트가 강력한 테스트를 작성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 Nim의 std/unittest 프레임워크를 활용하고 TorchTensor와 같은 복잡한 FFI 타입을 처리하며 테스트 조직과 C++ 컴파일 오류 디버깅을 위해 프로젝트 규약을 따름으로써","es":"Permite a los agentes escribir pruebas robustas aprovechando el framework std/unittest de Nim, manejar tipos FFI complejos como TorchTensor y adherirse a las convenciones del proyecto para la organización de pruebas y la depuración de errores de compilación de C++.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire des tests robustes en exploitant le framework std/unittest de Nim, de gérer des types FFI complexes comme TorchTensor et de se conformer aux conventions de projet pour l''organisation des tests et le débogage des erreurs de compilation C++.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, robuste Tests zu schreiben, die Nim''s std/unittest-Framework nutzen, komplexe FFI-Typen wie TorchTensor zu verarbeiten und den Projektvorschriften für die Testorganisation und die Fehlersuche bei C++-Kompilierfehlern zu entsprechen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes escrevam testes robustos utilizando o framework std/unittest do Nim, lidem com tipos FFI complexos como TorchTensor e adiram às convenções do projeto para organização de testes e depuração de erros de compilação C++.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать прочные тесты, используя фреймворк std/unittest от Nim, обрабатывать сложные типы FFI, такие как TorchTensor, и следовать проектным конвенциям для организации тестов и отладки ошибок компиляции C++.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على كتابة اختبارات قوية باستخدام إطار عمل std/unittest من Nim، وتحديد أنواع FFI المعقدة مثل TorchTensor، والامتثال للاتفاقيات المشروعية لتنظيم الاختباراتและการتصحيح أخطاء الترجمة C++."},"useCases":{"en":["Writing new tests for workspace modules","Debugging C++ compilation errors in test code","Organizing test fixtures and test data"],"zh":["为工作空间模块编写新的测试","调试测试代码中的C++编译错误","组织测试夹具和测试数据"],"ja":["ワークスペースモジュールのための新しいテストを書く","テストコードの中のC++コンパイルエラーをデバッグする","テストフィクスチャとテストデータを組織する"],"ko":["작업공간 모듈을 위한 새로운 테스트를 작성하기","테스트 코드에서 발생하는 C++ 컴파일 오류를 디버깅 하기","테스트 픽스처와 테스트 데이터를 조직하기"],"es":["Escribir nuevas pruebas para módulos de espacio de trabajo","Depurar errores de compilación de C++ en el código de prueba","Organizar fixtures y datos de prueba"],"fr":["Écrire de nouvelles tests pour les modules d''espace de travail","Déboguer les erreurs de compilation C++ dans le code de test","Organiser les fixtures et les données de test"],"de":["Neue Tests für Arbeitsbereichsmodule schreiben","C++-Kompilierfehler im Testcode debuggen","Testfixtures und Testdaten organisieren"],"pt":["Escrita de novos testes para módulos de espaço de trabalho","Depuração de erros de compilação C++ no código de teste","Organização de testes e dados de teste"],"ru":["Написание новых тестов для модулей рабочего пространства","Отладка ошибок компиляции C++ в тестовом коде","Организация тестовых установок и тестовых данных"],"ar":["كتابة اختبارات جديدة لمكونات مساحة العمل","تصحيح أخطاء الترجمة C++ في 코드 الاختبار","تنظيم إعدادات الاختبار وبيانات الاختبار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Nim environment","Limited to std/unittest framework","Nim-specific testing"],"zh":["需要Nim环境","仅限于std/unittest框架","Nim特定的测试"],"ja":["Nim環境が必要","std/unittestフレームワークに限定される","Nim固有のテスト"],"ko":["Nim 환경이 필요함","std/unittest 프레임워크로 제한됨","Nim 전용 테스트"],"es":["Requiere entorno Nim","Limitado al framework std/unittest","Pruebas específicas de Nim"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Nim","Limité au framework std/unittest","Tests spécifiques à Nim"],"de":["Benötigt Nim-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf std/unittest-Framework","Nim-spezifische Tests"],"pt":["Exige ambiente Nim","Limitado ao framework std/unittest","Testes específicos do Nim"],"ru":["Требует среды Nim","Ограничен фреймворком std/unittest","Тестирование, специфичное для Nim"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Nim","محدود بإطار عمل std/unittest","اختبارات محددة لبرنامج Nim"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
