k Auth + Swagger","Mobile avec React Native + Expo (optionnel)","Qualité avec Vitest (80% de couverture) + Biome + Husky + GitHub Actions CI/CD","Gestionnaire de paquets bun"],"de":["Frontend mit NextJS 16 + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind + @agenticindiedev/ui","Backend mit NestJS 11 + MongoDB + Clerk Auth + Swagger","Mobile mit React Native + Expo (optional)","Qualität mit Vitest (80% Abdeckung) + Biome + Husky + GitHub Actions CI/CD","Paket-Manager bun"],"pt":["Frontend com NextJS 16 + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind + @agenticindiedev/ui","Backend com NestJS 11 + MongoDB + Clerk Auth + Swagger","Mobile com React Native + Expo (opcional)","Qualidade com Vitest (80% de cobertura) + Biome + Husky + GitHub Actions CI/CD","Gerenciador de pacotes bun"],"ru":["Фронтенд с NextJS 16 + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind + @agenticindiedev/ui","Бэкенд с NestJS 11 + MongoDB + Clerk Auth + Swagger","Мобильное приложение с React Native + Expo (опционально)","Качество с Vitest (80% покрытия) + Biome + Husky + GitHub Actions CI/CD","Менеджер пакетов bun"],"ar":["واجهة المستخدم الأمامية مع NextJS 16 + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind + @agenticindiedev/ui","الخلفية مع NestJS 11 + MongoDB + Clerk Auth + Swagger","التطبيق المحمول مع React Native + Expo (اختياري)","الجودة مع Vitest (80% تغطية) + Biome + Husky + GitHub Actions CI/CD","مدير حزمة bun"]},"keywords":{"zh":["全栈工作空间","production-ready","monorepo","NextJS","NestJS","React Native","Vitest","GitHub Actions"],"ja":["フルスタックワークスペース","production-ready","monorepo","NextJS","NestJS","React Native","Vitest","GitHub Actions"],"ko":["전체 스택 작업공간","production-ready","monorepo","NextJS","NestJS","React Native","Vitest","GitHub Actions"],"es":["fullstack","monorepo","NextJS","React","TypeScript","Tailwind","NestJS","MongoDB","Clerk Auth","Swagger"],"fr":["fullstack","monorepo","NextJS","React","TypeScript","Tailwind","NestJS","MongoDB","Clerk Auth","Swagger"],"de":["fullstack","monorepo","NextJS","React","TypeScript","Tailwind","NestJS","MongoDB","Clerk Auth","Swagger"],"pt":["full stack","monorepo","NextJS","NestJS","React Native","TypeScript","Tailwind","MongoDB","Clerk Auth","Swagger"],"ru":["full stack","monorepo","NextJS","NestJS","React Native","TypeScript","Tailwind","MongoDB","Clerk Auth","Swagger"],"ar":["الكاملة الحزمة","مستودع وحيد","NextJS","NestJS","React Native","TypeScript","Tailwind","MongoDB","Clerk Auth","Swagger"]}},"owner":"xiangteng007","repo":"light-keepers","repoPath":"xiangteng007/light-keepers","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.477Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fullstack-workspace-init","description":"Scaffold a production-ready full-stack monorepo with working MVP features, tests, and CI/CD. Generates complete CRUD functionality, Clerk authentication, and quality gates that run immediately with `bun dev`.","bodyPreview":"# Full Stack Workspace Init\n\nCreate a **production-ready** monorepo with working MVP features:\n\n- **Frontend:** NextJS 16 + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind + @agenticindiedev/ui\n- **Backend:** NestJS 11 + MongoDB + Clerk Auth + Swagger\n- **Mobile:** React Native + Expo (optional)\n- **Quality:** Vitest (80% coverage) + Biome + Husky + GitHub Actions CI/CD\n- **Package Manager:** bun\n\n## What Makes This Different\n\nThis skill generates **working applications**, not empty scaffolds:\n\n- Complete CRUD","body":"# Full Stack Workspace Init\n\nCreate a **production-ready** monorepo with working MVP features:\n\n- **Frontend:** NextJS 16 + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind + @agenticindiedev/ui\n- **Backend:** NestJS 11 + MongoDB + Clerk Auth + Swagger\n- **Mobile:** React Native + Expo (optional)\n- **Quality:** Vitest (80% coverage) + Biome + Husky + GitHub Actions CI/CD\n- **Package Manager:** bun\n\n## What Makes This Different\n\nThis skill generates **working applications**, not empty scaffolds:\n\n- Complete CRUD operations for your main entities\n- Clerk authentication configured and working\n- Tests with 80% coverage threshold\n- GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline\n- Runs immediately with `bun dev`\n\n---\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Phase 1: PRD Brief Intake\n\n**Ask the user for a 1-2 paragraph product description**, then extract and confirm:\n\n```\nI''ll help you build [Project Name]. Based on your description, I understand:\n\n**Entities:**\n- [Entity1]: [fields]\n- [Entity2]: [fields]\n\n**Features:**\n- [Feature 1]\n- [Feature 2]\n\n**Routes:**\n- / - Home/Dashboard\n- /[entity] - List view\n- /[entity]/[id] - Detail view\n\n**API Endpoints:**\n- GET/POST /api/[entity]\n- GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/[entity]/:id\n\nIs this correct? Any adjustments?\n```\n\n### Phase 2: Auth Setup (Always Included)\n\nGenerate Clerk authentication:\n\n**Backend:**\n\n- `auth/guards/clerk-auth.guard.ts` - Token verification guard\n- `auth/decorators/current-user.decorator.ts` - User extraction decorator\n\n**Frontend:**\n\n- `providers/clerk-provider.tsx` - ClerkProvider wrapper\n- `app/sign-in/[[...sign-in]]/page.tsx` - Sign in page\n- `app/sign-up/[[...sign-up]]/page.tsx` - Sign up page\n- `middleware.ts` - Protected route middleware\n\n**Environment:**\n\n- `.env.example` with all required variables\n\n### Phase 3: Entity Generation\n\nFor each extracted entity, generate complete CRUD **with tests**:\n\n**Backend (NestJS):**\n\n```\napi/apps/api/src/collections/{entity}/\n├── {entity}.module.ts\n├── {entity}.controller.ts         # Full CRUD + Swagger + ClerkAuthGuard\n├── {entity}.controller.spec.ts    # Controller unit tests\n├── {entity}.service.ts            # Business logic\n├── {entity}.service.spec.ts       # Service unit tests\n├── schemas/\n│   └── {entity}.schema.ts         # Mongoose schema with userId\n└── dto/\n    ├── create-{entity}.dto.ts     # class-validator decorators\n    └── update-{entity}.dto.ts     # PartialType of create\n\napi/apps/api/test/\n├── {entity}.e2e-spec.ts           # E2E tests with supertest\n└── setup.ts                       # Test setup with MongoDB Memory Server\n```\n\n**Frontend (NextJS):**\n\n```\nfrontend/apps/dashboard/\n├── app/{entity}/\n│   ├── page.tsx                   # List view (protected)\n│   └── [id]/page.tsx              # Detail view (protected)\n├── src/test/\n│   └── setup.ts                   # Test setup with Clerk mocks\n└── vitest.config.ts               # Frontend test config (jsdom)\n\nfrontend/packages/components/\n├── {entity}-list.tsx\n├── {entity}-list.spec.tsx         # Component tests\n├── {entity}-form.tsx\n├── {entity}-form.spec.tsx         # Component tests\n└── {entity}-item.tsx\n\nfrontend/packages/hooks/\n├── use-{entities}.ts              # React hook for state management\n└── use-{entities}.spec.ts         # Hook tests\n\nfrontend/packages/services/\n└── {entity}.service.ts            # API client with auth headers\n```\n\n### Phase 4: Quality Setup\n\n**Vitest Configuration:**\n\n- `vitest.config.ts` in each project\n- 80% coverage threshold for lines, functions, branches\n- `@vitest/coverage-v8` provider\n\n**GitHub Actions:**\n\n- `.github/workflows/ci.yml`\n- Runs on push to main and PRs\n- Steps: install → lint → test → build\n\n**Husky Hooks:**\n\n- Pre-commit: `lint-staged` (Biome check)\n- Pre-push: `bun run typecheck`\n\n**Biome:**\n\n- `biome.json` in each project\n- 100 character line width\n- Double quotes, semicolons\n\n### Phase 5: Verification\n\nRun quality gate and report results:\n\n```\n✅ Generation complete!\n\nQuality Report:\n- bun install: ✓ succeeded\n- bun run lint: ✓ 0 errors\n- bun run test: ✓ 24 tests passed\n- Coverage: 82% (threshold: 80%)\n\nReady to run:\n  cd [project]\n  bun dev\n```\n\n---\n\n## Usage\n\n```bash\n# Create workspace with PRD-style prompt\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/fullstack-workspace-init/scripts/init-workspace.py \\\n  --root ~/www/myproject \\\n  --name \"My Project\" \\\n  --brief \"A task management app where users can create tasks with titles and due dates, organize them into projects, and mark them complete.\"\n\n# Or interactive mode (prompts for brief)\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/fullstack-workspace-init/scripts/init-workspace.py \\\n  --root ~/www/myproject \\\n  --name \"My Project\" \\\n  --interactive\n```\n\n---\n\n## Generated Structure\n\n```\nmyproject/\n├── .github/\n│   └── workflows/\n│       └── ci.yml              # GitHub Actions CI/CD\n├── .husky/\n│   ├── pre-commit              # Lint staged files\n│   └── pre-push                # Type check\n├── .agents/                     # AI documentation\n├── package.json                # Workspace root\n├── biome.json                  # Root linting config\n│\n├── api/                        # NestJS backend\n│   ├── apps/api/src/\n│   │   ├── main.ts\n│   │   ├── app.module.ts\n│   │   ├── auth/\n│   │   │   ├── guards/clerk-auth.guard.ts\n│   │   │   ├── guards/clerk-auth.guard.spec.ts  # Auth guard tests\n│   │   │   └── decorators/current-user.decorator.ts\n│   │   └── collections/\n│   │       └── {entity}/\n│   │           ├── {entity}.controller.ts\n│   │           ├── {entity}.controller.spec.ts  # Controller tests\n│   │           ├── {entity}.service.ts\n│   │           └── {entity}.service.spec.ts     # Service tests\n│   ├── apps/api/test/\n│   │   ├── {entity}.e2e-spec.ts                 # E2E tests\n│   │   └── setup.ts                             # E2E test setup\n│   ├── vitest.config.ts\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── .env.example\n│\n├── frontend/                   # NextJS apps\n│   ├── apps/dashboard/\n│   │   ├── app/\n│   │   │   ├── layout.tsx\n│   │   │   ├── page.tsx\n│   │   │   ├── sign-in/[[...sign-in]]/page.tsx\n│   │   │   ├── sign-up/[[...sign-up]]/page.tsx\n│   │   │   └── {entity}/       # Generated per entity\n│   │   ├── src/test/\n│   │   │   └── setup.ts        # Test setup with Clerk mocks\n│   │   ├── middleware.ts       # Clerk route protection\n│   │   └── providers/\n│   │       └── clerk-provider.tsx\n│   ├── packages/\n│   │   ├── components/\n│   │   │   ├── {entity}-list.tsx\n│   │   │   ├── {entity}-list.spec.tsx   # Component tests\n│   │   │   ├── {entity}-form.tsx\n│   │   │   └── {entity}-form.spec.tsx   # Component tests\n│   │   ├── hooks/\n│   │   │   ├── use-{entities}.ts\n│   │   │   └── use-{entities}.spec.ts   # Hook tests\n│   │   ├── services/           # API clients\n│   │   └── interfaces/\n│   ├── vitest.config.ts        # Frontend test config (jsdom)\n│   └── package.json\n│\n├── mobile/                     # React Native + Expo (optional)\n│   └── ...\n│\n└── packages/                   # Shared packages\n    └── packages/\n        ├── common/\n        │   ├── interfaces/\n        │   └── enums/\n        └── helpers/\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n### Backend Controller Pattern\n\n```typescript\n@ApiTags(''tasks'')\n@ApiBearerAuth()\n@UseGuards(ClerkAuthGuard)\n@Controller(''tasks'')\nexport class TasksController {\n  constructor(private readonly tasksService: TasksService) {}\n\n  @Post()\n  @ApiOperation({ summary: ''Create a new task'' })\n  create(\n    @Body() createTaskDto: CreateTaskDto,\n    @CurrentUser() user: { userId: string },\n  ) {\n    return this.tasksService.create(createTaskDto, user.userId);\n  }\n  // ... full CRUD\n}\n```\n\n### Backend Service Pattern\n\n```typescript\n@Injectable()\nexport class TasksService {\n  constructor(\n    @InjectModel(Task.name) private taskModel: Model<TaskDocument>,\n  ) {}\n\n  async create(createTaskDto: CreateTaskDto, userId: string): Promise<Task> {\n    const task = new this.taskModel({ ...createTaskDto, userId });\n    return task.save();\n  }\n  // ... full CRUD with userId filtering\n}\n```\n\n### Frontend Component Pattern\n\n```typescript\n''use client'';\n\nimport { useEffect, useState } from ''react'';\nimport { TaskService } from ''@services/task.service'';\nimport { Task } from ''@interfaces/task.interface'';\n\nexport function TaskList() {\n  const [tasks, setTasks] = useState<Task[]>([]);\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const controller = new AbortController();\n    TaskService.getAll({ signal: controller.signal })\n      .then(setTasks)\n      .finally(() => setLoading(false));\n    return () => controller.abort();\n  }, []);\n\n  // ... render\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Additional Scripts\n\n```bash\n# Add a new entity to existing project\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/fullstack-workspace-init/scripts/add-entity.py \\\n  --root ~/www/myproject \\\n  --name \"comment\" \\\n  --fields \"content:string,taskId:string\"\n\n# Add a new frontend app\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/fullstack-workspace-init/scripts/add-frontend-app.py \\\n  --root ~/www/myproject/frontend \\\n  --name admin\n```\n\n---\n\n## Development Commands\n\nAfter scaffolding:\n\n```bash\ncd myproject\n\n# Install all dependencies\nbun install\n\n# Start all services (backend + frontend)\nbun dev\n\n# Or start individually\nbun run dev:api      # Backend on :3001\nbun run dev:frontend # Frontend on :3000\nbun run dev:mobile   # Mobile via Expo\n\n# Quality commands\nbun run lint         # Check code style\nbun run test         # Run tests\nbun run test:coverage # Run with coverage\nbun run typecheck    # Type checking\n```\n\n---\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nCreate `.env` files based on `.env.example`:\n\n**API (.env):**\n\n```\nPORT=3001\nMONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/myproject\nCLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...\n```\n\n**Frontend (.env.local):**\n\n```\nNEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...\nNEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001\n```\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- `references/templates/` - Code generation templates\n  - `service.spec.template.ts` - NestJS service unit test template\n  - `controller.spec.template.ts` - NestJS controller unit test template\n  - `e2e.spec.template.ts` - E2E test template with supertest + MongoDB Memory Server\n  - `component.spec.template.tsx` - React component test template\n  - `hook.spec.template.ts` - React hook test template\n  - `test-setup.template.ts` - Frontend test setup with Clerk mocks\n- `references/vitest.config.ts` - Backend Vitest configuration (80% coverage)\n- `references/vitest.config.frontend.ts` - Frontend Vitest configuration (jsdom)\n- `references/github-actions/ci.yml` - CI/CD workflow\n- `references/architecture-guide.md` - Architectural decisions\n- `references/coding-standards.md` - Coding rules\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:24:21.413Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Developer Agents needing rapid monorepo setup with NextJS, React, and NestJS for production-ready MVPs.","zh":"适合需要快速设置单体仓库的全栈开发者代理，使用 NextJS、React 和 NestJS 进行生产就绪的 MVP。","ja":"NextJS、React、NestJS を使用して、モノリポ設定が迅速に必要なフルスタック開発者エージェントに最適です。","ko":"NextJS, React, NestJS를 사용하여 빠른 모노레포 설정이 필요한 풀스택 개발자 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo de Pilas Complejas que necesitan una configuración rápida de monorepo con NextJS, React y NestJS para MVP listos para producción.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développement de Piles Complètes ayant besoin d''une configuration rapide de monorepo avec NextJS, React et NestJS pour des MVP prêts pour la production.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Entwickler-Agenten, die eine schnelle Monorepo-Einrichtung mit NextJS, React und NestJS für produktionssbereite MVPs benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedores Full Stack que necessitam de configuração rápida de monorepo com NextJS, React e NestJS para MVPs prontos para produção.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработчиков Full Stack, которым требуется быстрая настройка монорепозитория с NextJS, React и NestJS для производственных MVP.","ar":"مثالي لعميل وكلاء تطوير كامل العمود الذي يحتاج إلى إعداد سريع لمستودع واحد مع NextJS و React و NestJS من أجل إم في بي جاهز للانتاج."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate fully functional, production-ready monorepos with features like complete CRUD operations, authentication via Clerk Auth, and CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions, all managed with bun as the package manager and secured with 80% Vitest coverage.","zh":"赋予代理生成完全功能、生产就绪的单体仓库的能力，具有完整的 CRUD 操作、通过 Clerk Auth 进行身份验证以及使用 GitHub Actions 的 CI/CD 管道等功能，全程由 bun 包管理器管理，并使用 Vitest 实现 80% 的代码覆盖率。","ja":"エージェントが完全な機能を備え、生产就绪のモノリポを生成する能力を付与します。Clerk Auth を使用した認証、GitHub Actions を使用した CI/CD パイプラインなど、bun パッケージマネージャーで管理され、Vitest で 80% のコードカバレッジを実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 완전한 기능을 갖춘 생산 준비 모노레포를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. Clerk Auth를 사용한 인증, GitHub Actions를 사용한 CI/CD 파이프라인 등이 bun 패키지 관리자로 관리되고 Vitest로 80%의 코드 커버리지를 달성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar monorepos completamente funcionales y listos para producción con características como operaciones CRUD completas, autenticación mediante Clerk Auth y pipelines de CI/CD mediante GitHub Actions, todo gestionado con bun como administrador de paquetes y seguro con una cobertura de Vitest del 80%.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des monorepos entièrement fonctionnels et prêts pour la production avec des fonctionnalités telles que des opérations CRUD complètes, une authentification via Clerk Auth et des pipelines CI/CD via GitHub Actions, le tout géré avec bun en tant que gestionnaire de paquets et sécurisé avec une couverture Vitest de 80%.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, voll funktionsfähige und produktionssbereite Monorepos mit Funktionen wie vollständigen CRUD-Operationen, Authentifizierung über Clerk Auth und CI/CD-Pipelines mit GitHub Actions zu generieren, alles verwaltet mit bun als Paket-Manager und gesichert mit 80% Vitest-Abdeckung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar monorepos completamente funcionais e prontos para produção com recursos como operações CRUD completas, autenticação via Clerk Auth e pipelines CI/CD usando GitHub Actions, todos gerenciados com bun como gerenciador de pacotes e seguros com 80% de cobertura do Vitest.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать полностью функциональные, производственные монорепозитории с функциями, такими как полные операции CRUD, аутентификация через Clerk Auth и конвейеры CI/CD, использующие GitHub Actions, все управляемые bun в качестве менеджера пакетов и защищенные 80% покрытием Vitest.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إنشاء مستودعات واحدة完全 تعمل و جاهزة للانتاج مع ميزات مثل عمليات CRUD الكاملة وتأشير عبر Clerk Auth وخطوط أنابيب CI/CD باستخدام GitHub Actions ، جميعها متوفرة مع bun كمدير حزم وأمن مع 80٪ من تغطية Vitest."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing monorepos for web applications with NextJS and React","Setting up backend services with NestJS, MongoDB, and Swagger documentation","Creating mobile applications with React Native and Expo","Implementing quality assurance with Vitest, Biome, Husky, and GitHub Actions CI/CD"],"zh":["为 Web 应用程序初始化单体仓库，使用 NextJS 和 React","使用 NestJS、MongoDB 和 Swagger 文档设置后端服务","使用 React Native 和 Expo 创建移动应用程序","使用 Vitest、Biome、Husky 和 GitHub Actions CI/CD 实现质量保证"],"ja":["NextJS と React を使用して Web アプリケーションのモノリポを初期化する","NestJS、MongoDB、Swagger ドキュメントを使用してバックエンドサービスを設定する","React Native と Expo を使用してモバイルアプリケーションを作成する","Vitest、Biome、Husky、GitHub Actions CI/CD を使用して品質保証を実現する"],"ko":["NextJS와 React를 사용하여 웹 애플리케이션의 모노레포를 초기화합니다.","NestJS, MongoDB, Swagger 문서를 사용하여 백엔드 서비스를 설정합니다.","React Native와 Expo를 사용하여 모바일 애플리케이션을 생성합니다.","Vitest, Biome, Husky, GitHub Actions CI/CD를 사용하여 품질 보증을 구현합니다."],"es":["Inicialización de monorepos para aplicaciones web con NextJS y React","Configuración de servicios de backend con NestJS, MongoDB y documentación de Swagger","Creación de aplicaciones móviles con React Native y Expo","Implementación de garantía de calidad con Vitest, Biome, Husky y pipelines de CI/CD de GitHub Actions"],"fr":["Initialisation de monorepos pour des applications Web avec NextJS et React","Configuration de services de backend avec NestJS, MongoDB et documentation de Swagger","Création d''applications mobiles avec React Native et Expo","Mise en œuvre de l''assurance qualité avec Vitest, Biome, Husky et pipelines CI/CD de GitHub Actions"],"de":["Initialisierung von Monorepos für Webanwendungen mit NextJS und React","Einrichtung von Backendservices mit NestJS, MongoDB und Swagger-Dokumentation","Erstellung von mobilen Anwendungen mit React Native und Expo","Implementierung von Qualitätsicherung mit Vitest, Biome, Husky und CI/CD-Pipelines von GitHub Actions"],"pt":["Inicializar monorepos para aplicações web com NextJS e React","Configurar serviços de backend com NestJS, MongoDB e documentação Swagger","Criar aplicações móveis com React Native e Expo","Implementar garantia de qualidade com Vitest, Biome, Husky e pipelines CI/CD do GitHub Actions"],"ru":["Инициализировать монорепозитории для веб-приложений с NextJS и React","Настроить сервисы бэкэнда с NestJS, MongoDB и документацией Swagger","Создать мобильные приложения с React Native и Expo","Реализовать обеспечение качества с Vitest, Biome, Husky и конвейерами CI/CD GitHub Actions"],"ar":["تهيئة مستودعات واحدة للتطبيقات الويب مع NextJS و React","ضبط خدمات الخادم الخلفي مع NestJS و MongoDB و وثائق Swagger","إنشاء تطبيقات الهاتف المحمول مع React Native و Expo","تنفيذ ضمان الجودة مع Vitest و Biome و Husky وخطوط أنابيب CI/CD من GitHub Actions"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires bun as the package manager","Specific to NextJS 16, React 19, NestJS 11, and MongoDB","Optional mobile application setup with React Native and Expo"],"zh":["需要使用 bun 作为包管理器","特定于 NextJS 16、React 19、NestJS 11 和 MongoDB","可选的移动应用程序设置，使用 React Native 和 Expo"],"ja":["bun をパッケージマネージャーとして使用する必要がある","NextJS 16、React 19、NestJS 11、MongoDB に特化している","React Native と Expo を使用したモバイルアプリケーションの設定が任意"],"ko":["bun을 패키지 관리자로 사용해야 합니다.","NextJS 16, React 19, NestJS 11, MongoDB에 특화되어 있습니다.","React Native와 Expo를 사용한 모바일 애플리케이션 설정이 선택사항입니다."],"es":["Requiere bun como administrador de paquetes","Específico para NextJS 16, React 19, NestJS 11 y MongoDB","Configuración de aplicaciones móviles opcional con React Native y Expo"],"fr":["Nécessite bun en tant que gestionnaire de paquets","Spécifique à NextJS 16, React 19, NestJS 11 et MongoDB","Configuration d''applications mobiles optionnelle avec React Native et Expo"],"de":["Benötigt bun als Paket-Manager","Spezifisch für NextJS 16, React 19, NestJS 11 und MongoDB","Optional: Einrichtung von mobilen Anwendungen mit React Native und Expo"],"pt":["Exige bun como gerenciador de pacotes","Específico para NextJS 16, React 19, NestJS 11 e MongoDB","Configuração de aplicação móvel opcional com React Native e Expo"],"ru":["Требует bun в качестве менеджера пакетов","Специфичен для NextJS 16, React 19, NestJS 11 и MongoDB","Опциональная настройка мобильного приложения с React Native и Expo"],"ar":["يتطلب bun كمدير حزم","محدد ل NextJS 16 و React 19 و NestJS 11 و MongoDB","الإعداد الاختياري للتطبيق المحمول مع React Native و Expo"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Sri-Krishna-V/Derived-WMD/components', 'community', 'Sri-Krishna-V', 'Derived-WMD', 'Sri-Krishna-V/Derived-WMD', 'components', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.477Z', '2026-02-18T09:24:34.765Z', NULL, '{"id":"Sri-Krishna-V/Derived-WMD/components","name":"components","description":{"zh":"Tambo 组件是用于生成 React 应用的 AI 平台，支持两种类型的组件：生成式和交互式","ja":"Tambo コンポーネントは React アプリを生成するための AI プラットフォームであり、2 種類のコンポーネント（生成式とインタラクティブ）をサポートしています","ko":"Tambo 컴포넌트는 React 애플리케이션을 생성하기 위한 AI 플랫폼으로, 2 種의 컴포넌트(생성 및 상호 작용)를 지원합니다","es":"Tambo es una plataforma de UI generativa que transforma el lenguaje natural en aplicaciones React listas para producir en segundos. Ofrece componentes generativos y preestablecidos","fr":"Tambo est une plateforme d''UI générative qui transforme le langage naturel en applications React prêtes à produire en quelques secondes. Elle propose des composants génératifs et préétablis","de":"Tambo ist eine UI-Generierungsplattform, die natürliche Sprache in produzierbare React-Anwendungen umwandelt. Bietet generative und vorkonfigurierte Komponenten","pt":"A plataforma Tambo permite transformar linguagem natural em aplicativos React prontos para produção em segundos, com componentes generativos e interativos","ru":"Платформа Tambo позволяет преобразовать естественный язык в готовые к производству приложения React за секунды, с генеративными и интерактивными компонентами","ar":"تسمح منصة تامبو بتحويل اللغة الطبيعية إلى تطبيقات ري액ت جاهزة للإنتاج في ثوان، مع مكونات توليدية وتفاعلية","en":"The Agentic Generative UI Platform: Transform natural language into production-ready React apps in seconds. Featuring autonomous Tambo agents, Model Context Protocol (MCP) for codebase grounding, and secure E2B sandboxed execution."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Tambo 组件：AI 生成 React 应用","ja":"Tambo コンポーネント：AI による React アプリ生成","ko":"Tambo 컴포넌트: AI 기반 React 애플리케이션 생성","es":"Componentes de Tambo: Generación de UI con IA","fr":"Composants Tambo: Génération d''UI avec l''IA","de":"Tambo-Komponenten: UI-Generierung mit KI","pt":"Componentes Tambo: Crie Aplicativos React em Segundos","ru":"Компоненты Tambo: Создавайте Приложения React за Секунды","ar":"مكونات تامبو: أنشئ تطبيقات ري액ت في ثوان","en":"components"},"description":{"zh":"Tambo 组件是用于生成 React 应用的 AI 平台，支持两种类型的组件：生成式和交互式","ja":"Tambo コンポーネントは React アプリを生成するための AI プラットフォームであり、2 種類のコンポーネント（生成式とインタラクティブ）をサポートしています","ko":"Tambo 컴포넌트는 React 애플리케이션을 생성하기 위한 AI 플랫폼으로, 2 種의 컴포넌트(생성 및 상호 작용)를 지원합니다","es":"Tambo es una plataforma de UI generativa que transforma el lenguaje natural en aplicaciones React listas para producir en segundos. Ofrece componentes genera...","fr":"Tambo est une plateforme d''UI générative qui transforme le langage naturel en applications React prêtes à produire en quelques secondes. Elle propose des com...","de":"Tambo ist eine UI-Generierungsplattform, die natürliche Sprache in produzierbare React-Anwendungen umwandelt. Bietet generative und vorkonfigurierte Komponenten","pt":"A plataforma Tambo permite transformar linguagem natural em aplicativos React prontos para produção em segundos, com componentes generativos e interativos","ru":"Платформа Tambo позволяет преобразовать естественный язык в готовые к производству приложения React за секунды, с генеративными и интерактивными компонентами","ar":"تسمح منصة تامبو بتحويل اللغة الطبيعية إلى تطبيقات ري액ت جاهزة للإنتاج في ثوان، مع مكونات توليدية وتفاعلية","en":"The Agentic Generative UI Platform: Transform natural language into production-ready React apps in seconds. Featuring autonomous Tambo agents, Model Context ..."},"definition":{"en":"The Agentic Generative UI Platform: Transform natural language into production-ready React apps in seconds. Featuring autonomous Tambo agents, Model Context Protocol (MCP) for codebase grounding, and secure E2B sandboxed execution."},"features":{"zh":["生成式组件：AI 创建所需组件","交互式组件：预置组件，AI 更新","支持 Model Context Protocol (MCP) 代码库接地","安全的 E2B 沙盒执行","快速生成生产就绪的 React 应用"],"ja":["生成式コンポーネント：AI によって必要なコンポーネントを生成","インタラクティブ コンポーネント：事前に配置されたコンポーネント、AI によって更新","Model Context Protocol (MCP) コードベースの接地をサポート","安全な E2B サンドボックス実行","生産可能な React アプリの迅速な生成"],"ko":["생성 컴포넌트: AI가 필요한 컴포넌트를 생성","상호 작용 컴포넌트: 미리 배치된 컴포넌트, AI가 업데이트함","Model Context Protocol (MCP) 코드베이스 고정 지원","안전한 E2B 샌드박스 실행","생산 준비가 된 React 애플리케이션을 빠르게 생성"],"es":["Componentes generativos creados por IA","Componentes interactuables preestablecidos","Integración con React","Ejecución sandbox segura","Protocolo de contexto de modelo (MCP) para anclaje de código"],"fr":["Composants génératifs créés par l''IA","Composants interactifs préétablis","Intégration avec React","Exécution sandbox sécurisée","Protocole de contexte de modèle (MCP) pour l''ancre de code"],"de":["KI-generierte generative Komponenten","Vorkonfigurierte interaktive Komponenten","Integration mit React","Sichere Sandbox-Ausführung","Modellkontextprotokoll (MCP) für Code-Verankerung"],"pt":["Geração de componentes em tempo real","Interação com componentes pré-colocados","Execução segura em sandbox","Protocolo de contexto de modelo (MCP) para ancoragem de código","Agentes autônomos Tambo"],"ru":["Генерация компонентов в режиме реального времени","Взаимодействие с предварительно размещенными компонентами","Безопасное выполнение в песочнице","Протокол контекста модели (MCP) для якорения кода","Автономные агенты Tambo"],"ar":["توليد المكونات في الوقت الفعلي","التفاعل مع المكونات الموضوعة مسبقًا","تنفيذ آمن في حاوية رملية","بروتوكول سياق النموذج (MCP) لتثبيت رمز","وكلاء تامبو المستقلون"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Tambo 组件","AI 生成 React 应用","生成式组件","交互式组件","Model Context Protocol","E2B 沙盒执行","React 应用开发"],"ja":["Tambo コンポーネント","AI による React アプリ生成","生成式コンポーネント","インタラクティブ コンポーネント","Model Context Protocol","E2B サンドボックス実行","React アプリ開発"],"ko":["Tambo 컴포넌트","AI 기반 React 애플리케이션 생성","생성 컴포넌트","상호 작용 컴포넌트","Model Context Protocol","E2B 샌드박스 실행","React 애플리케이션 개발"],"es":["componentes de Tambo","generación de UI","IA en desarrollo web","aplicaciones React personalizadas","integración de IA en React","desarrollo de UI con IA"],"fr":["composants Tambo","génération d''UI","IA dans le développement web","applications React personnalisées","intégration de l''IA dans React","développement d''UI avec l''IA"],"de":["Tambo-Komponenten","UI-Generierung","KI im Webentwicklung","benutzerdefinierte React-Anwendungen","KI-Integration in React","UI-Entwicklung mit KI"],"pt":["componentes Tambo","aplicativos React","linguagem natural","geração de componentes","interação com componentes","execução segura","protocolo de contexto de modelo","agentes autônomos"],"ru":["компоненты Tambo","приложения React","естественный язык","генерация компонентов","взаимодействие с компонентами","безопасное выполнение","протокол контекста модели","автономные агенты"],"ar":["مكونات تامبو","تطبيقات ري액ت","لغة طبيعية","توليد المكونات","التفاعل مع المكونات","تنفيذ آمن","بروتوكول سياق النموذج","وكلاء مستقلون"]}},"owner":"Sri-Krishna-V","repo":"Derived-WMD","repoPath":"Sri-Krishna-V/Derived-WMD","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.477Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"components","description":"Creates and registers Tambo components - generative (AI creates on-demand) and interactable (pre-placed, AI updates). Use when defining components, working with TamboComponent, withInteractable, propsSchema, or registering components for AI to render or update.","bodyPreview":"# Tambo Components\n\nTwo component types: **generative** (AI creates on-demand) and **interactable** (pre-placed, AI updates).\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```tsx\n// Generative: AI creates when needed\nconst components: TamboComponent[] = [\n  {\n    name: \"WeatherCard\",\n    component: WeatherCard,\n    description: \"Shows weather. Use when user asks about weather.\",\n    propsSchema: z.object({ city: z.string(), temp: z.number() }),\n  },\n];\n\n<TamboProvider components={components}>\n  <App />\n</TamboProvider>;\n```","body":"# Tambo Components\n\nTwo component types: **generative** (AI creates on-demand) and **interactable** (pre-placed, AI updates).\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```tsx\n// Generative: AI creates when needed\nconst components: TamboComponent[] = [\n  {\n    name: \"WeatherCard\",\n    component: WeatherCard,\n    description: \"Shows weather. Use when user asks about weather.\",\n    propsSchema: z.object({ city: z.string(), temp: z.number() }),\n  },\n];\n\n<TamboProvider components={components}>\n  <App />\n</TamboProvider>;\n```\n\n## Generative Components\n\nAI dynamically selects and renders these in response to user messages.\n\n```tsx\nimport { TamboProvider, TamboComponent } from \"@tambo-ai/react\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst WeatherCardSchema = z.object({\n  city: z.string().describe(\"City name\"),\n  temperature: z.number().describe(\"Temperature in Celsius\"),\n  condition: z.string().describe(\"Weather condition\"),\n});\n\nconst components: TamboComponent[] = [\n  {\n    name: \"WeatherCard\",\n    component: WeatherCard,\n    description:\n      \"Displays weather for a city. Use when user asks about weather.\",\n    propsSchema: WeatherCardSchema,\n  },\n];\n\n<TamboProvider apiKey={apiKey} components={components}>\n  <App />\n</TamboProvider>;\n```\n\n### Generative Key Points\n\n- **propsSchema**: Zod object with `.describe()` on each field\n- **description**: Tells AI when to use the component\n- **Streaming**: Props start `undefined`, make them optional or handle gracefully\n- Use `z.infer<typeof Schema>` for TypeScript props type\n\n## Interactable Components\n\nPre-place in your UI; AI can observe and update props via natural language.\n\n```tsx\nimport { withInteractable } from \"@tambo-ai/react\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst NoteSchema = z.object({\n  title: z.string().describe(\"Note title\"),\n  content: z.string().describe(\"Note content\"),\n  color: z.enum([\"white\", \"yellow\", \"blue\"]).optional(),\n});\n\nfunction Note({ title, content, color = \"white\" }: Props) {\n  return (\n    <div style={{ backgroundColor: color }}>\n      <h3>{title}</h3>\n      <p>{content}</p>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n\nexport const InteractableNote = withInteractable(Note, {\n  componentName: \"Note\",\n  description: \"A note with editable title, content, and color\",\n  propsSchema: NoteSchema,\n});\n```\n\n### Interactable How It Works\n\n1. **Auto-registration**: Component registers when mounted\n2. **Context sending**: Current props automatically visible to AI\n3. **Tool registration**: Update tools registered automatically\n4. **Bidirectional**: User edits and AI updates both work\n\n### When to Use Each\n\n| Generative                 | Interactable                 |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| AI creates on-demand       | You pre-place in UI          |\n| One-time render            | Persistent across session    |\n| Props generated once       | AI can update props          |\n| Chat responses, dashboards | Settings, forms, task boards |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:24:34.765Z","qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT/kaizen', 'community', 'xiangteng007', 'XXT-AGENT', 'xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT', 'kaizen', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.477Z', '2026-02-18T09:25:09.669Z', NULL, '{"id":"xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT/kaizen","name":"kaizen","description":{"zh":"Kaizen,","ja":"Kaizen","ko":"Kaizen ","es":"Kaizen es una filosofía de mejora continua que se centra en pequeñas mejoras incrementales para optimizar el código y los procesos.","fr":"Kaizen est une philosophie d''amélioration continue qui se concentre sur de petites améliorations incrémentales pour optimiser le code et les processus.","de":"Kaizen ist eine Philosophie der kontinuierlichen Verbesserung, die sich auf kleine, inkrementale Verbesserungen konzentriert, um Code und Prozesse zu optimieren.","pt":"Kaizen é uma abordagem de melhoria contínua que busca pequenas melhorias incrementais em código, arquitetura e processos","ru":"Кайдзен - это подход к постоянному улучшению, который стремится к pequenos улучшениям в коде, архитектуре и процессах","ar":"كايزن هي نهج تحسين مستمر يسعى إلى تحسينات صغيرة متزايدة في الكود والهيكل والعمليات","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Kaizen: ","ja":"Kaizen","ko":"Kaizen ","es":"Kaizen: Mejora Continua para Desarrolladores","fr":"Kaizen : Amélioration Continue pour les Développeurs","de":"Kaizen: Kontinuierliche Verbesserung für Entwickler","pt":"Kaizen: Melhoria Contínua em Desenvolvimento","ru":"Кайдзен: Постоянное Улучшение в Разработке","ar":"كايزن: تحسين مستمر في التطوير","en":"kaizen"},"description":{"zh":"Kaizen,","ja":"Kaizen","ko":"Kaizen ","es":"Kaizen es una filosofía de mejora continua que se centra en pequeñas mejoras incrementales para optimizar el código y los procesos.","fr":"Kaizen est une philosophie d''amélioration continue qui se concentre sur de petites améliorations incrémentales pour optimiser le code et les processus.","de":"Kaizen ist eine Philosophie der kontinuierlichen Verbesserung, die sich auf kleine, inkrementale Verbesserungen konzentriert, um Code und Prozesse zu optimie...","pt":"Kaizen é uma abordagem de melhoria contínua que busca pequenas melhorias incrementais em código, arquitetura e processos","ru":"Кайдзен - это подход к постоянному улучшению, который стремится к pequenos улучшениям в коде, архитектуре и процессах","ar":"كايزن هي نهج تحسين مستمر يسعى إلى تحسينات صغيرة متزايدة في الكود والهيكل والعمليات","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["","","",""],"ja":["","","",""],"ko":["","","",""],"es":["Mejora continua del código","Optimización de procesos","Enfoque incremental","Prevención de errores","Validación y refactorización"],"fr":["Amélioration continue du code","Optimisation des processus","Approche incrémentale","Prévention des erreurs","Validation et refactoring"],"de":["Kontinuierliche Verbesserung des Codes","Optimierung von Prozessen","Inkrementaler Ansatz","Fehlerprävention","Validierung und Refactoring"],"pt":["Melhoria contínua em código e arquitetura","Prevenção de erros em tempo de design","Desenvolvimento incremental de processos","Validação e tratamento de erros","Refatoração de código e melhoria de desempenho","Tomada de decisões baseada em dados"],"ru":["Постоянное улучшение кода и архитектуры","Предотвращение ошибок в tiempo де дизайна","Инкрементальное развитие процессов","Валидация и обработка ошибок","Рефакторинг кода и улучшение производительности","Принятие решений на основе данных"],"ar":["تحسين مستمر في الكود والهيكل","منع الأخطاء في وقت التصميم","تطوير تدريجي للعمليات","التحقق من صحة الأخطاء ومعالجتها","إعادة هيكلة الكود وتحسين الأداء","اتخاذ القرارات المستندة إلى البيانات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kaizen","","","","",""],"ja":["Kaizen","","","","",""],"ko":["Kaizen","","","","",""],"es":["kaizen para desarrolladores","mejora continua","optimización de código","procesos de desarrollo","filosofía de desarrollo","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software"],"fr":["kaizen pour les développeurs","amélioration continue","optimisation de code","processus de développement","philosophie de développement","développement de logiciels","ingénierie de logiciels"],"de":["kaizen für entwickler","kontinuierliche verbesserung","optimierung von code","entwicklungsprozesse","entwicklungsphilosophie","softwareentwicklung","softwareingenieurwesen"],"pt":["kaizen","melhoria contínua","desenvolvimento de software","arquitetura de software","processos de desenvolvimento","prevenção de erros","refatoração de código","validação de dados"],"ru":["кайдзен","постоянное улучшение","разработка программного обеспечения","архитектура программного обеспечения","процессы разработки","предотвращение ошибок","рефакторинг кода","валидация данных"],"ar":["كايزن","تحسين مستمر","تطوير البرمجيات","هيكل البرمجيات","عمليات التطوير","منع الأخطاء","إعادة هيكلة الكود","تحقق من صحة البيانات"]}},"owner":"xiangteng007","repo":"XXT-AGENT","repoPath":"xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.477Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kaizen","description":"Guide for continuous improvement, error proofing, and standardization. Use this skill when the user wants to improve code quality, refactor, or discuss process improvements.","bodyPreview":"# Kaizen: Continuous Improvement\n\n## Overview\n\nSmall improvements, continuously. Error-proof by design. Follow what works. Build only what''s needed.\n\n**Core principle:** Many small improvements beat one big change. Prevent errors at design time, not with fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always applied for:**\n\n- Code implementation and refactoring\n- Architecture and design decisions\n- Process and workflow improvements\n- Error handling and validation\n\n**Philosophy:** Quality through incremental progress","body":"# Kaizen: Continuous Improvement\n\n## Overview\n\nSmall improvements, continuously. Error-proof by design. Follow what works. Build only what''s needed.\n\n**Core principle:** Many small improvements beat one big change. Prevent errors at design time, not with fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\n**Always applied for:**\n\n- Code implementation and refactoring\n- Architecture and design decisions\n- Process and workflow improvements\n- Error handling and validation\n\n**Philosophy:** Quality through incremental progress and prevention, not perfection through massive effort.\n\n## The Four Pillars\n\n### 1. Continuous Improvement (Kaizen)\n\nSmall, frequent improvements compound into major gains.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**Incremental over revolutionary:**\n\n- Make smallest viable change that improves quality\n- One improvement at a time\n- Verify each change before next\n- Build momentum through small wins\n\n**Always leave code better:**\n\n- Fix small issues as you encounter them\n- Refactor while you work (within scope)\n- Update outdated comments\n- Remove dead code when you see it\n\n**Iterative refinement:**\n\n- First version: make it work\n- Second pass: make it clear\n- Third pass: make it efficient\n- Don''t try all three at once\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Iteration 1: Make it work\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]) => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n    total += items[i].price * items[i].quantity;\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\n// Iteration 2: Make it clear (refactor)\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\nreturn items.reduce((total, item) => {\nreturn total + (item.price \\* item.quantity);\n}, 0);\n};\n\n// Iteration 3: Make it robust (add validation)\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\nif (!items?.length) return 0;\n\nreturn items.reduce((total, item) => {\nif (item.price < 0 || item.quantity < 0) {\nthrow new Error(''Price and quantity must be non-negative'');\n}\nreturn total + (item.price \\* item.quantity);\n}, 0);\n};\n\n````\nEach step is complete, tested, and working\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Trying to do everything at once\nconst calculateTotal = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  // Validate, optimize, add features, handle edge cases all together\n  if (!items?.length) return 0;\n  const validItems = items.filter(item => {\n    if (item.price < 0) throw new Error(''Negative price'');\n    if (item.quantity < 0) throw new Error(''Negative quantity'');\n    return item.quantity > 0; // Also filtering zero quantities\n  });\n  // Plus caching, plus logging, plus currency conversion...\n  return validItems.reduce(...); // Too many concerns at once\n};\n````\n\nOverwhelming, error-prone, hard to verify\n</Bad>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**When implementing features:**\n\n1. Start with simplest version that works\n2. Add one improvement (error handling, validation, etc.)\n3. Test and verify\n4. Repeat if time permits\n5. Don''t try to make it perfect immediately\n\n**When refactoring:**\n\n- Fix one smell at a time\n- Commit after each improvement\n- Keep tests passing throughout\n- Stop when \"good enough\" (diminishing returns)\n\n**When reviewing code:**\n\n- Suggest incremental improvements (not rewrites)\n- Prioritize: critical → important → nice-to-have\n- Focus on highest-impact changes first\n- Accept \"better than before\" even if not perfect\n\n### 2. Poka-Yoke (Error Proofing)\n\nDesign systems that prevent errors at compile/design time, not runtime.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**Make errors impossible:**\n\n- Type system catches mistakes\n- Compiler enforces contracts\n- Invalid states unrepresentable\n- Errors caught early (left of production)\n\n**Design for safety:**\n\n- Fail fast and loudly\n- Provide helpful error messages\n- Make correct path obvious\n- Make incorrect path difficult\n\n**Defense in layers:**\n\n1. Type system (compile time)\n2. Validation (runtime, early)\n3. Guards (preconditions)\n4. Error boundaries (graceful degradation)\n\n#### Type System Error Proofing\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Error: string status can be any value\ntype OrderBad = {\n  status: string; // Can be \"pending\", \"PENDING\", \"pnding\", anything!\n  total: number;\n};\n\n// Good: Only valid states possible\ntype OrderStatus = ''pending'' | ''processing'' | ''shipped'' | ''delivered'';\ntype Order = {\nstatus: OrderStatus;\ntotal: number;\n};\n\n// Better: States with associated data\ntype Order =\n| { status: ''pending''; createdAt: Date }\n| { status: ''processing''; startedAt: Date; estimatedCompletion: Date }\n| { status: ''shipped''; trackingNumber: string; shippedAt: Date }\n| { status: ''delivered''; deliveredAt: Date; signature: string };\n\n// Now impossible to have shipped without trackingNumber\n\n````\nType system prevents entire classes of errors\n</Good>\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Make invalid states unrepresentable\ntype NonEmptyArray<T> = [T, ...T[]];\n\nconst firstItem = <T>(items: NonEmptyArray<T>): T => {\n  return items[0]; // Always safe, never undefined!\n};\n\n// Caller must prove array is non-empty\nconst items: number[] = [1, 2, 3];\nif (items.length > 0) {\n  firstItem(items as NonEmptyArray<number>); // Safe\n}\n````\n\nFunction signature guarantees safety\n</Good>\n\n#### Validation Error Proofing\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Error: Validation after use\nconst processPayment = (amount: number) => {\n  const fee = amount * 0.03; // Used before validation!\n  if (amount <= 0) throw new Error(''Invalid amount'');\n  // ...\n};\n\n// Good: Validate immediately\nconst processPayment = (amount: number) => {\nif (amount <= 0) {\nthrow new Error(''Payment amount must be positive'');\n}\nif (amount > 10000) {\nthrow new Error(''Payment exceeds maximum allowed'');\n}\n\nconst fee = amount \\* 0.03;\n// ... now safe to use\n};\n\n// Better: Validation at boundary with branded type\ntype PositiveNumber = number & { readonly \\_\\_brand: ''PositiveNumber'' };\n\nconst validatePositive = (n: number): PositiveNumber => {\nif (n <= 0) throw new Error(''Must be positive'');\nreturn n as PositiveNumber;\n};\n\nconst processPayment = (amount: PositiveNumber) => {\n// amount is guaranteed positive, no need to check\nconst fee = amount \\* 0.03;\n};\n\n// Validate at system boundary\nconst handlePaymentRequest = (req: Request) => {\nconst amount = validatePositive(req.body.amount); // Validate once\nprocessPayment(amount); // Use everywhere safely\n};\n\n````\nValidate once at boundary, safe everywhere else\n</Good>\n\n#### Guards and Preconditions\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Early returns prevent deeply nested code\nconst processUser = (user: User | null) => {\n  if (!user) {\n    logger.error(''User not found'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (!user.email) {\n    logger.error(''User email missing'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  if (!user.isActive) {\n    logger.info(''User inactive, skipping'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  // Main logic here, guaranteed user is valid and active\n  sendEmail(user.email, ''Welcome!'');\n};\n````\n\nGuards make assumptions explicit and enforced\n</Good>\n\n#### Configuration Error Proofing\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Error: Optional config with unsafe defaults\ntype ConfigBad = {\n  apiKey?: string;\n  timeout?: number;\n};\n\nconst client = new APIClient({ timeout: 5000 }); // apiKey missing!\n\n// Good: Required config, fails early\ntype Config = {\napiKey: string;\ntimeout: number;\n};\n\nconst loadConfig = (): Config => {\nconst apiKey = process.env.API_KEY;\nif (!apiKey) {\nthrow new Error(''API_KEY environment variable required'');\n}\n\nreturn {\napiKey,\ntimeout: 5000,\n};\n};\n\n// App fails at startup if config invalid, not during request\nconst config = loadConfig();\nconst client = new APIClient(config);\n\n````\nFail at startup, not in production\n</Good>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**When designing APIs:**\n- Use types to constrain inputs\n- Make invalid states unrepresentable\n- Return Result<T, E> instead of throwing\n- Document preconditions in types\n\n**When handling errors:**\n- Validate at system boundaries\n\n- Use guards for preconditions\n- Fail fast with clear messages\n- Log context for debugging\n\n**When configuring:**\n- Required over optional with defaults\n- Validate all config at startup\n- Fail deployment if config invalid\n- Don''t allow partial configurations\n\n### 3. Standardized Work\nFollow established patterns. Document what works. Make good practices easy to follow.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**Consistency over cleverness:**\n- Follow existing codebase patterns\n- Don''t reinvent solved problems\n- New pattern only if significantly better\n- Team agreement on new patterns\n\n**Documentation lives with code:**\n- README for setup and architecture\n- CLAUDE.md for AI coding conventions\n- Comments for \"why\", not \"what\"\n- Examples for complex patterns\n\n**Automate standards:**\n- Linters enforce style\n- Type checks enforce contracts\n- Tests verify behavior\n- CI/CD enforces quality gates\n\n#### Following Patterns\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Existing codebase pattern for API clients\nclass UserAPIClient {\n  async getUser(id: string): Promise<User> {\n    return this.fetch(`/users/${id}`);\n  }\n}\n\n// New code follows the same pattern\nclass OrderAPIClient {\n  async getOrder(id: string): Promise<Order> {\n    return this.fetch(`/orders/${id}`);\n  }\n}\n````\n\nConsistency makes codebase predictable\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Existing pattern uses classes\nclass UserAPIClient { /* ... */ }\n\n// New code introduces different pattern without discussion\nconst getOrder = async (id: string): Promise<Order> => {\n// Breaking consistency \"because I prefer functions\"\n};\n\n````\nInconsistency creates confusion\n</Bad>\n\n#### Error Handling Patterns\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Project standard: Result type for recoverable errors\ntype Result<T, E> = { ok: true; value: T } | { ok: false; error: E };\n\n// All services follow this pattern\nconst fetchUser = async (id: string): Promise<Result<User, Error>> => {\n  try {\n    const user = await db.users.findById(id);\n    if (!user) {\n      return { ok: false, error: new Error(''User not found'') };\n    }\n    return { ok: true, value: user };\n  } catch (err) {\n    return { ok: false, error: err as Error };\n  }\n};\n\n// Callers use consistent pattern\nconst result = await fetchUser(''123'');\nif (!result.ok) {\n  logger.error(''Failed to fetch user'', result.error);\n  return;\n}\nconst user = result.value; // Type-safe!\n````\n\nStandard pattern across codebase\n</Good>\n\n#### Documentation Standards\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n/**\n * Retries an async operation with exponential backoff.\n *\n * Why: Network requests fail temporarily; retrying improves reliability\n * When to use: External API calls, database operations\n * When not to use: User input validation, internal function calls\n *\n * @example\n * const result = await retry(\n *   () => fetch(''https://api.example.com/data''),\n *   { maxAttempts: 3, baseDelay: 1000 }\n * );\n */\nconst retry = async <T>(\n  operation: () => Promise<T>,\n  options: RetryOptions\n): Promise<T> => {\n  // Implementation...\n};\n```\nDocuments why, when, and how\n</Good>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**Before adding new patterns:**\n\n- Search codebase for similar problems solved\n- Check CLAUDE.md for project conventions\n- Discuss with team if breaking from pattern\n- Update docs when introducing new pattern\n\n**When writing code:**\n\n- Match existing file structure\n- Use same naming conventions\n- Follow same error handling approach\n- Import from same locations\n\n**When reviewing:**\n\n- Check consistency with existing code\n- Point to examples in codebase\n- Suggest aligning with standards\n- Update CLAUDE.md if new standard emerges\n\n### 4. Just-In-Time (JIT)\n\nBuild what''s needed now. No more, no less. Avoid premature optimization and over-engineering.\n\n#### Principles\n\n**YAGNI (You Aren''t Gonna Need It):**\n\n- Implement only current requirements\n- No \"just in case\" features\n- No \"we might need this later\" code\n- Delete speculation\n\n**Simplest thing that works:**\n\n- Start with straightforward solution\n- Add complexity only when needed\n- Refactor when requirements change\n- Don''t anticipate future needs\n\n**Optimize when measured:**\n\n- No premature optimization\n- Profile before optimizing\n- Measure impact of changes\n- Accept \"good enough\" performance\n\n#### YAGNI in Action\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Current requirement: Log errors to console\nconst logError = (error: Error) => {\n  console.error(error.message);\n};\n```\nSimple, meets current need\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Over-engineered for \"future needs\"\ninterface LogTransport {\n  write(level: LogLevel, message: string, meta?: LogMetadata): Promise<void>;\n}\n\nclass ConsoleTransport implements LogTransport { /_... _/ }\nclass FileTransport implements LogTransport { /_ ... _/ }\nclass RemoteTransport implements LogTransport { /_ ..._/ }\n\nclass Logger {\nprivate transports: LogTransport[] = [];\nprivate queue: LogEntry[] = [];\nprivate rateLimiter: RateLimiter;\nprivate formatter: LogFormatter;\n\n// 200 lines of code for \"maybe we''ll need it\"\n}\n\nconst logError = (error: Error) => {\nLogger.getInstance().log(''error'', error.message);\n};\n\n````\nBuilding for imaginary future requirements\n</Bad>\n\n**When to add complexity:**\n- Current requirement demands it\n- Pain points identified through use\n- Measured performance issues\n- Multiple use cases emerged\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Start simple\nconst formatCurrency = (amount: number): string => {\n  return `$${amount.toFixed(2)}`;\n};\n\n// Requirement evolves: support multiple currencies\nconst formatCurrency = (amount: number, currency: string): string => {\n  const symbols = { USD: ''$'', EUR: ''€'', GBP: ''£'' };\n  return `${symbols[currency]}${amount.toFixed(2)}`;\n};\n\n// Requirement evolves: support localization\nconst formatCurrency = (amount: number, locale: string): string => {\n  return new Intl.NumberFormat(locale, {\\n    style: ''currency'',\n    currency: locale === ''en-US'' ? ''USD'' : ''EUR'',\n  }).format(amount);\n};\n````\n\nComplexity added only when needed\n</Good>\n\n#### Premature Abstraction\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// One use case, but building generic framework\nabstract class BaseCRUDService<T> {\n  abstract getAll(): Promise<T[]>;\n  abstract getById(id: string): Promise<T>;\n  abstract create(data: Partial<T>): Promise<T>;\n  abstract update(id: string, data: Partial<T>): Promise<T>;\n  abstract delete(id: string): Promise<void>;\n}\n\nclass GenericRepository<T> { /_300 lines _/ }\nclass QueryBuilder<T> { /_ 200 lines_/ }\n// ... building entire ORM for single table\n\n````\nMassive abstraction for uncertain future\n</Bad>\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Simple functions for current needs\nconst getUsers = async (): Promise<User[]> => {\n  return db.query(''SELECT * FROM users'');\n};\n\nconst getUserById = async (id: string): Promise<User | null> => {\n  return db.query(''SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1'', [id]);\n};\n\n// When pattern emerges across multiple entities, then abstract\n````\n\nAbstract only when pattern proven across 3+ cases\n</Good>\n\n#### Performance Optimization\n\n<Good>\n```typescript\n// Current: Simple approach\nconst filterActiveUsers = (users: User[]): User[] => {\n  return users.filter(user => user.isActive);\n};\n\n// Benchmark shows: 50ms for 1000 users (acceptable)\n// ✓ Ship it, no optimization needed\n\n// Later: After profiling shows this is bottleneck\n// Then optimize with indexed lookup or caching\n\n````\nOptimize based on measurement, not assumptions\n</Good>\n\n<Bad>\n```typescript\n// Premature optimization\nconst filterActiveUsers = (users: User[]): User[] => {\n  // \"This might be slow, so let''s cache and index\"\n  const cache = new WeakMap();\n  const indexed = buildBTreeIndex(users, ''isActive'');\n  // 100 lines of optimization code\n  // Adds complexity, harder to maintain\n  // No evidence it was needed\n};\\\n````\n\nComplex solution for unmeasured problem\n</Bad>\n\n#### In Practice\n\n**When implementing:**\n\n- Solve the immediate problem\n- Use straightforward approach\n- Resist \"what if\" thinking\n- Delete speculative code\n\n**When optimizing:**\n\n- Profile first, optimize second\n- Measure before and after\n- Document why optimization needed\n- Keep simple version in tests\n\n**When abstracting:**\n\n- Wait for 3+ similar cases (Rule of Three)\n- Make abstraction as simple as possible\n- Prefer duplication over wrong abstraction\n- Refactor when pattern clear\n\n## Integration with Commands\n\nThe Kaizen skill guides how you work. The commands provide structured analysis:\n\n- **`/why`**: Root cause analysis (5 Whys)\n- **`/cause-and-effect`**: Multi-factor analysis (Fishbone)\n- **`/plan-do-check-act`**: Iterative improvement cycles\n- **`/analyse-problem`**: Comprehensive documentation (A3)\n- **`/analyse`**: Smart method selection (Gemba/VSM/Muda)\n\nUse commands for structured problem-solving. Apply skill for day-to-day development.\n\n## Red Flags\n\n**Violating Continuous Improvement:**\n\n- \"I''ll refactor it later\" (never happens)\n- Leaving code worse than you found it\n- Big bang rewrites instead of incremental\n\n**Violating Poka-Yoke:**\n\n- \"Users should just be careful\"\n- Validation after use instead of before\n- Optional config with no validation\n\n**Violating Standardized Work:**\n\n- \"I prefer to do it my way\"\n- Not checking existing patterns\n- Ignoring project conventions\n\n**Violating Just-In-Time:**\n\n- \"We might need this someday\"\n- Building frameworks before using them\n- Optimizing without measuring\n\n## Remember\n\n**Kaizen is about:**\n\n- Small improvements continuously\n- Preventing errors by design\n- Following proven patterns\n- Building only what''s needed\n\n**Not about:**\n\n- Perfection on first try\n- Massive refactoring projects\n- Clever abstractions\n- Premature optimization\n\n**Mindset:** Good enough today, better tomorrow. Repeat.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:25:09.669Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Refactoring Agents seeking to implement continuous improvement methodologies like kaizen.","zh":"适合寻求实施持续改进方法（如改善）的代码重构代理。","ja":"コードリファクタリングエージェントが継続的改善方法論 seperti カイゼンを実装するのによく適しています。","ko":"코드 리팩토링 에이전트가 계속적인 개선 방법론을 구현하려고 하는 경우에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de refactorización de código que buscan implementar metodologías de mejora continua como kaizen.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de refactoring de code cherchant à mettre en œuvre des méthodologies d''amélioration continue comme le kaizen.","de":"Ideal für Code-Refactoring-Agents, die kontinuierliche Verbesserungsmethoden wie Kaizen umsetzen möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Refatoração de Código que buscam implementar metodologias de melhoria contínua, como o kaizen.","ru":"Идеально для агентов рефакторинга кода, стремящихся реализовать методологии непрерывного совершенствования, такие как кайдзен.","ar":"مثالي لعميل إعادة هيكلة الشفرة الذين يسعون لتنفيذ منهجيات التحسين المستمر مثل كايزن."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply incremental progress principles, preventing errors at design time through error-proofing by design, and building only what''s needed, utilizing core principles like many small improvements beating one big change, with applications in code implementation, architecture, and process improvements.","zh":"赋予代理应用增量进展原则，通过设计时的错误防范防止设计时的错误，并仅构建所需的内容，利用诸如许多小改进优于一个大变化的核心原则，并将其应用于代码实现、体系结构和流程改进。","ja":"エージェントがインクリメンタル進歩の原則を適用できるようにし、設計時にはエラープルーフによる設計でエラーを防止し、必要なものだけを構築し、小さな改善が1つの大きな変更よりも優れているなどのコア原則を利用し、コードの実装、設計、アーキテクチャ、プロセスの改善に適用します。","ko":"에이전트가 점진적인 개선 원칙을 적용할 수 있도록 하여 설계 시 오류를 방지하고 필요한 것만 구축하며 많은 작은 개선이 하나의 큰 변화보다 나은 등 핵심 원칙을 활용하여 코드 구현, 아키텍처 및 프로세스 개선에 적용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes aplicar principios de progreso incremental, evitando errores en el momento del diseño a través de una concepción a prueba de errores y construyendo solo lo necesario, utilizando principios básicos como muchas pequeñas mejoras que superan un gran cambio, con aplicaciones en la implementación de código, arquitectura y mejoras de procesos.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des principes de progrès incrémental, en évitant les erreurs au moment de la conception grâce à une conception robuste, et en ne construisant que ce qui est nécessaire, en utilisant des principes de base tels que de nombreuses petites améliorations surpassant un grand changement, avec des applications dans la mise en œuvre de code, l''architecture et les améliorations de processus.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, inkrementelle Fortschrittsprinzipien anzuwenden, Fehler bei der Entwurfszeit durch eine fehlerfreie Konstruktion zu vermeiden und nur das zu bauen, was benötigt wird, unter Verwendung von Grundprinzipien wie vielen kleinen Verbesserungen, die eine große Änderung überbieten, mit Anwendungen in der Codeimplementierung, Architektur und Prozessverbesserungen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar princípios de progresso incremental, prevenindo erros no tempo de design por meio de uma concepção de prova de erros e construindo apenas o que é necessário, utilizando princípios básicos como muitas pequenas melhorias superando uma grande mudança, com aplicações na implementação de código, arquitetura e melhorias de processo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять принципы инкрементального прогресса, предотвращая ошибки на этапе проектирования посредством разработки, не допускающей ошибок, и создания только того, что необходимо, используя основные принципы, такие как много небольших улучшений, превосходящих одну большую изменение, с применением в реализации кода, архитектуре и процессных улучшениях.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء تطبيق مبادئ التقدم التكراري، ومنع الأخطاء في وقت التصميم من خلال تصميم لمنع الأخطاء، وبناء ما هو ضروري فقط، باستخدام المبادئ الأساسية مثل العديد من التحسينات الصغيرة التي تغلب على التغيير الكبير، مع التطبيقات في تنفيذ الشفرة والهيكلة والتحسينات العملية."},"useCases":{"en":["Refactoring codebases for optimal performance","Implementing error handling and validation protocols","Streamlining workflow processes through continuous improvement"],"zh":["为获得最佳性能而重构代码库","实施错误处理和验证协议","通过持续改进简化工作流程"],"ja":["最適なパフォーマンスを得るためにコードベースをリファクタリングする","エラーハンドリングと検証プロトコルを実装する","継続的改善を通じてワークフロープロセスを最適化する"],"ko":["최적의 성능을 얻기 위해 코드베이스를 리팩토링하는 것","오류 처리 및 검증 프로토콜을 구현하는 것","계속적인 개선을 통해 워크플로우 프로세스를 최적화하는 것"],"es":["Reorganización de bases de código para un rendimiento óptimo","Implementación de protocolos de control y validación de errores","Optimización de procesos de flujo de trabajo a través de la mejora continua"],"fr":["Réorganisation de bases de code pour un rendement optimal","Mise en œuvre de protocoles de gestion et de validation des erreurs","Optimisation des processus de workflow grâce à l''amélioration continue"],"de":["Neuorganisation von Codebasen für optimale Leistung","Implementierung von Fehlerbehandlungs- und Validierungsprotokollen","Optimierung von Workflow-Prozessen durch kontinuierliche Verbesserung"],"pt":["Refatoração de bases de código para desempenho ótimo","Implementação de protocolos de tratamento de erros e validação","Otimização de processos de trabalho por meio da melhoria contínua"],"ru":["Рефакторинг кодовых баз для оптимальной производительности","Реализация протоколов обработки ошибок и проверки","Оптимизация рабочих процессов посредством непрерывного совершенствования"],"ar":["إعادة هيكلة قواعد الشفرة لأداء مثالي","تنفيذ بروتوكولات معالجة الأخطاء والتحقق","تحسين العمليات العملية من خلال التحسين المستمر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires ongoing iterative design and development","Dependent on human feedback for improvement"],"zh":["需要持续的迭代设计和开发","依赖于人类反馈来改进"],"ja":["継続的なイテレーティブ設計と開発が必要","改善には人間のフィードバックに依存する"],"ko":["계속적인 반복 설계 및 개발이 필요함","개선을 위해서는 인간의 피드백에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere un diseño y desarrollo iterativos continuos","Depende de la retroalimentación humana para la mejora"],"fr":["Nécessite une conception et un développement itératifs continus","Dépend de la rétroaction humaine pour l''amélioration"],"de":["Erfordert ein kontinuierliches iteratives Design und Entwicklung","Hängt von der menschlichen Rückmeldung für die Verbesserung ab"],"pt":["Exige design e desenvolvimento iterativos contínuos","Depende do feedback humano para a melhoria"],"ru":["Требует постоянного итеративного проектирования и разработки","Зависит от обратной связи человека для улучшения"],"ar":["يتطلب تصميمًا وتطويرًا متكررين مستمرين","يعتمد على رد الفعل البشري للتحسين"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
