um: Автономное развитие программного обеспечения","ar":"رالف ويغوم: تطوير البرمجيات الأوتوماتيكي","en":"ralph-wiggum"},"description":{"zh":"Ralph Wiggum AI技能结合Geoffrey Huntley的迭代bash循环和规格驱动开发，实现全自主AI辅助软件开发","ja":"Ralph Wiggum スキルは、Geoffrey Huntleyのイテレーティブbashループと仕様駆動開発を組み合わせて、完全に自治されたAIアシストソフトウェア開発を実現します","ko":"Ralph Wiggum 스킬은 Geoffrey Huntley의 반복 bash 루프와 사양 주도 개발을 결합하여 완전히 자율적인 AI辅助 소프트웨어 개발을 구현합니다","es":"Ralph Wiggum combina iteración y desarrollo basado en especificaciones para un desarrollo de software autónomo","fr":"Ralph Wiggum combine itération et développement basé sur des spécifications pour un développement logiciel autonome","de":"Ralph Wiggum kombiniert Iteration und spezifikationsbasierte Entwicklung für eine autonome Software-Entwicklung","pt":"Ralph Wiggum é um agente de cozinha que combina desenvolvimento iterativo com spec-driven development para desenvolvimento de software autônomo","ru":"Ralph Wiggum - это агент для кухни, который сочетает итеративное развитие с разработкой, основанной на спецификациях, для автономного развития программного о...","ar":"رالف ويغوم هو وكلاء الطهي الذي ي 结ب التطوير التكراري مع تطوير معايير للبرمجيات الأوتوماتيكي","en":"AI-powered cooking agent for ingredient recognition, recipe discovery, and shopping list management"},"definition":{"en":"AI-powered cooking agent for ingredient recognition, recipe discovery, and shopping list management"},"features":{"zh":["自动化编码","食材识别","食谱发现","购物清单管理","规格驱动开发"],"ja":["自動化コーディング","食材認識","レシピ発見","ショッピングリスト管理","仕様駆動開発"],"ko":["자동화 코딩","식자재 인식","레시피 발견","쇼핑 리스트 관리","사양 주도 개발"],"es":["Reconocimiento de ingredientes","Descubrimiento de recetas","Gestión de listas de compras","Desarrollo basado en especificaciones","Iteración autónoma","Prevenir la degradación del contexto"],"fr":["Reconnaissance d''ingrédients","Découverte de recettes","Gestion de listes de courses","Développement basé sur des spécifications","Itération autonome","Prévenir la dégradation du contexte"],"de":["Zutaten-Erkennung","Rezeptideen-Entdeckung","Einkaufslisten-Verwaltung","Spezifikationsbasierte Entwicklung","Autonome Iteration","Kontext-Abbau verhindern"],"pt":["Reconhecimento de ingredientes","Descoberta de receitas","Gerenciamento de lista de compras","Desenvolvimento iterativo","Spec-driven development","Contexto fresco a cada iteração"],"ru":["Признание ингредиентов","Обнаружение рецептов","Управление списком покупок","Итеративное развитие","Разработка, основанная на спецификациях","Свежий контекст на каждой итерации"],"ar":["تحديد المكونات","اكتشاف الوصفات","إدارة قائمة التسوق","التطوير التكراري","تطوير معايير","سياق جديد في كل تكرار"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Ralph Wiggum","AI技能","自动化编码","食材识别","食谱发现","购物清单管理","规格驱动开发"],"ja":["Ralph Wiggum","AIスキル","自動化コーディング","食材認識","レシピ発見","ショッピングリスト管理","仕様駆動開発"],"ko":["Ralph Wiggum","AI 스킬","자동화 코딩","식자재 인식","레시피 발견","쇼핑 리스트 관리","사양 주도 개발"],"es":["desarrollo de software autónomo","agente de cocina","reconocimiento de ingredientes","gestión de listas de compras","desarrollo basado en especificaciones","iteración autónoma","inteligencia artificial","cocina inteligente"],"fr":["développement logiciel autonome","agent de cuisine","reconnaissance d''ingrédients","gestion de listes de courses","développement basé sur des spécifications","itération autonome","intelligence artificielle","cuisine intelligente"],"de":["autonome Software-Entwicklung","Koch-Agent","Zutaten-Erkennung","Einkaufslisten-Verwaltung","spezifikationsbasierte Entwicklung","autonome Iteration","künstliche Intelligenz","intelligente Küche"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de software autônomo","agente de cozinha","reconhecimento de ingredientes","descoberta de receitas","gerenciamento de lista de compras","spec-driven development","desenvolvimento iterativo","contexto fresco"],"ru":["автономное развитие программного обеспечения","агент для кухни","признание ингредиентов","обнаружение рецептов","управление списком покупок","разработка, основанная на спецификациях","итеративное развитие","свежий контекст"],"ar":["تطوير البرمجيات الأوتوماتيكي","وكلاء الطهي","تحديد المكونات","اكتشاف الوصفات","إدارة قائمة التسوق","تطوير معايير","التطوير التكراري","سياق جديد"]}},"owner":"JStoweYouKnow","repo":"ai_cooking_agent","repoPath":"JStoweYouKnow/ai_cooking_agent","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.477Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ralph-wiggum","description":"Autonomous AI coding with spec-driven development. Implements Geoffrey Huntleys iterative bash loop methodology where agents work through specs one at a time, outputting a completion signal only when acceptance criteria are 100% met.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# Ralph Wiggum\n\n> Autonomous AI coding with spec-driven development\n\n## What is Ralph Wiggum?\n\nRalph Wiggum combines **Geoffrey Huntley''s iterative bash loop** with **spec-driven development** for fully autonomous AI-assisted software development.\n\nThe key insight: **Fresh context each iteration**. Each loop starts a new agent process with a clean context window, preventing context overflow and degradation.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse Ralph Wiggum when:\n\n- You have multiple specifications/fe","body":"# Ralph Wiggum\n\n> Autonomous AI coding with spec-driven development\n\n## What is Ralph Wiggum?\n\nRalph Wiggum combines **Geoffrey Huntley''s iterative bash loop** with **spec-driven development** for fully autonomous AI-assisted software development.\n\nThe key insight: **Fresh context each iteration**. Each loop starts a new agent process with a clean context window, preventing context overflow and degradation.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse Ralph Wiggum when:\n\n- You have multiple specifications/features to implement\n- You want the AI to work autonomously through tasks\n- You need consistent, verifiable completion of acceptance criteria\n- You want to avoid context window problems in long sessions\n\n## How It Works\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     RALPH LOOP                              │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  Loop 1: Pick spec A → Implement → Test → Commit → DONE    │\n│  Loop 2: Pick spec B → Implement → Test → Commit → DONE    │\n│  Loop 3: Pick spec C → Implement → Test → Commit → DONE    │\n│  ...                                                        │\n│                                                             │\n│  Each iteration = Fresh context window                      │\n│  Shared state = Files on disk (specs, plan, history)        │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Installation\n\n### Quick Install (via Skill Installers)\n\n```bash\n# Using Vercel''s add-skill\nnpx add-skill fstandhartinger/ralph-wiggum\n\n# Using OpenSkills\nopenskills install fstandhartinger/ralph-wiggum\n```\n\n### Full Setup (Recommended)\n\nFor full Ralph Wiggum setup with constitution and interview:\n\n```bash\n# Tell your AI agent:\n\"Set up Ralph Wiggum using https://github.com/fstandhartinger/ralph-wiggum\"\n```\n\nThe agent will guide you through a **lightweight, pleasant setup**:\n\n1. **Quick Setup** (~1 min) — Create directories, download scripts\n2. **Project Interview** — Focus on your **vision and goals** (not tech details)\n3. **Constitution** — Create a guiding document for all sessions\n4. **Next Steps** — Clear guidance on creating specs and starting Ralph\n\nFor existing projects, the agent detects your tech stack automatically. The interview prioritizes understanding *what you''re building and why*.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Fresh Context Each Loop\n\nEach iteration of the Ralph loop starts a new AI agent process. This means:\n- No context window overflow\n- No degradation over time\n- Clean slate for each task\n\n### 2. Shared State on Disk\n\nState persists between loops via files:\n- `specs/` — Feature specifications with acceptance criteria\n- `ralph_history.txt` — Log of breakthroughs, blockers, learnings\n- `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` — Optional detailed task breakdown\n\n### 3. Completion Signal\n\nThe agent outputs `<promise>DONE</promise>` **ONLY** when:\n- All acceptance criteria are verified\n- Tests pass\n- Changes are committed and pushed\n\nThe bash loop checks for this phrase. If not found, it retries.\n\n### 4. Backpressure via Tests\n\nTests, lints, and builds act as guardrails. The agent must fix issues before outputting the completion signal.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Creating Specifications\n\n**The key to success:** Each spec needs **clear, testable acceptance criteria**. This is what tells Ralph when a task is truly \"done.\"\n\n```markdown\n# Feature: User Authentication\n\n## Requirements\n- OAuth login with Google\n- Session management\n- Logout functionality\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] User can log in with Google\n- [ ] Session persists across page reloads\n- [ ] User can log out\n- [ ] Tests pass\n\n**Output when complete:** `<promise>DONE</promise>`\n```\n\n**Good criteria:** \"User can log in with Google and session persists\"\n**Bad criteria:** \"Auth works correctly\"\n\nThe more specific your acceptance criteria, the better Ralph performs.\n\n### Running the Loop\n\n```bash\n# Start building (Claude Code)\n./scripts/ralph-loop.sh\n\n# With max iterations\n./scripts/ralph-loop.sh 20\n\n# Using Codex CLI\n./scripts/ralph-loop-codex.sh\n```\n\n### Logging (All Output Captured)\n\nEvery loop run writes **all output** to log files in `logs/`:\n\n- **Session log:** `logs/ralph_*_session_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.log` (entire run, including CLI output)\n- **Iteration logs:** `logs/ralph_*_iter_N_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.log` (per-iteration CLI output)\n- **Codex last message:** `logs/ralph_codex_output_iter_N_*.txt`\n\n### RLM Mode (Experimental)\n\nProvide a large context file and the agent will treat it as external environment.\nThis is **optional and experimental** — it does not implement the full recursive runtime from the paper, but it **does** preserve all loop outputs on disk and guides the agent to query them as needed.\n\n```bash\n./scripts/ralph-loop.sh --rlm-context ./rlm/context.txt\n./scripts/ralph-loop-codex.sh --rlm-context ./rlm/context.txt\n```\n\nRLM workspace (when enabled):\n- `rlm/trace/` — Prompt snapshots per iteration\n- `rlm/index.tsv` — Index of all iterations\n- `logs/` — Full CLI output per iteration\n\nOptional recursive subcalls:\n\n```bash\n./scripts/rlm-subcall.sh --query rlm/queries/q1.md\n```\n\nThis mirrors the Recursive Language Model (RLM) idea: handle huge prompts by inspecting only the slices you need.\n\n## Two Modes\n\n| Mode | Purpose | Command |\n|------|---------|---------|\n| **build** (default) | Pick spec, implement, test, commit | `./scripts/ralph-loop.sh` |\n| **plan** (optional) | Create detailed task breakdown | `./scripts/ralph-loop.sh plan` |\n\n## Key Principles\n\n### Let Ralph Ralph\n\nTrust the AI to self-identify, self-correct, and self-improve. Observe patterns and adjust prompts.\n\n### YOLO Mode\n\nFor Ralph to work effectively, enable full autonomy:\n- Claude Code: `--dangerously-skip-permissions`\n- Codex: `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`\n\n⚠️ **Use at your own risk.** Only in sandboxed environments.\n\n## Links\n\n- **GitHub:** https://github.com/fstandhartinger/ralph-wiggum\n- **Website:** https://ralph-wiggum.ai\n- **Original methodology:** [Geoffrey Huntley''s how-to-ralph-wiggum](https://github.com/ghuntley/how-to-ralph-wiggum)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:25:34.678Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Autonomous AI Coding Agents needing spec-driven development and iterative bash loop capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要基于规范驱动开发和迭代Bash循环能力的自主AI编码代理。","ja":"規範駆動開発と反復Bashループ機能を必要とする自律AIコーディングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"규약 기반 개발 및 반복적 Bash 루프 기능이 필요한 자율적 AI 코딩 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Codificación de IA Autónomos que necesitan desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones y capacidades de bucle bash iterativo.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Codage de l''IA Autonome ayant besoin d''un développement piloté par des spécifications et de capacités de boucle bash itérative.","de":"Perfekt für autonome AI-Coding-Agenten, die spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklung und iterative Bash-Schleifenfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Codificação de IA Autônoma que necessitam de desenvolvimento orientado por especificações e capacidades de loop bash iterativo.","ru":"Идеально подходит для автономных агентов кодирования ИИ, которым необходимы разработка, управляемая спецификациями, и итеративные возможности цикла bash.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الترميز الذكية المستقلة التي تحتاج إلى تطوير مدفوع بالمواصفات وقدرات الحلقات التكرارية لBASH."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform fully autonomous AI-assisted software development using Geoffrey Huntley''s iterative bash loop with spec-driven development, providing fresh context each iteration and preventing context overflow and degradation through clean context windows.","zh":"赋予代理使用杰弗里·亨特利的反复Bash循环与规范驱动开发进行完全自主的AI辅助软件开发的能力，提供每次迭代的新背景，并通过清晰的上下文窗口防止上下文溢出和退化。","ja":"ジェフリー・ハントリーの反復Bashループと規範駆動開発を使用して、完全に自律的なAI支援ソフトウェア開発を実行するエージェントを可能にし、各反復で新しいコンテキストを提供し、クリーンなコンテキストウィンドウを介してコンテキストオーバーフローと退化を防ぐ。","ko":"제프리 헌틀리의 반복 Bash 루프와 규약 기반 개발을 사용하여 완전히 자율적인 AI 지원 소프트웨어 개발을 수행할 수 있는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, 각 반복에서 새로운 컨텍스트를 제공하고 깨끗한 컨텍스트 창을 통해 컨텍스트 오버플로우와 저하를 방지합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar un desarrollo de software completamente autónomo asistido por IA utilizando el bucle bash iterativo de Geoffrey Huntley con desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones, proporcionando un contexto fresco en cada iteración y evitando el desbordamiento y la degradación del contexto a través de ventanas de contexto limpias.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réaliser un développement de logiciels entièrement autonome assisté par l''IA en utilisant la boucle bash itérative de Geoffrey Huntley avec un développement piloté par des spécifications, fournissant un contexte frais à chaque itération et empêchant le débordement et la dégradation du contexte grâce à des fenêtres de contexte propres.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, vollständig autonome AI-gestützte Softwareentwicklung durchzuführen, indem sie die iterative Bash-Schleife von Geoffrey Huntley mit spezifikationsgetriebener Entwicklung verwenden, wodurch bei jeder Iteration ein frischer Kontext bereitgestellt und ein Kontextüberlauf und -abbau durch saubere Kontextfenster verhindert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar desenvolvimento de software totalmente autônomo com assistência de IA, usando o loop bash iterativo de Geoffrey Huntley com desenvolvimento orientado por especificações, fornecendo um contexto fresco a cada iteração e prevenindo o transbordamento e degradação do contexto por meio de janelas de contexto limpas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять полностью автономное разработку программного обеспечения с помощью ИИ, используя итеративный цикл bash Джоффри Хантли с разработкой, управляемой спецификациями, предоставляя свежий контекст на каждой итерации и предотвращая переполнение и ухудшение контекста посредством чистых контекстных окон.","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من أداء التطوير البرمجي المستقل بالكامل بمساعدة الذكاء الاصطناعي باستخدام حلقة باش التكرارية لجوفري هانتلي مع التطوير الموجه بالمواصفات، مع توفير سياق جديد في كل تكرار ومنع فيضان السياق والانحدار من خلال نوافذ سياق نظيفة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating software development with spec-driven development","Generating autonomous AI coding solutions using iterative bash loops","Managing context overflow and degradation in AI-assisted development"],"zh":["使用规范驱动开发自动化软件开发","使用反复Bash循环生成自主AI编码解决方案","在AI辅助开发中管理上下文溢出和退化"],"ja":["規範駆動開発を使用してソフトウェア開発を自動化する","反復Bashループを使用して自律AIコーディングソリューションを生成する","AI支援開発におけるコンテキストオーバーフローと退化を管理する"],"ko":["규약 기반 개발을 사용하여 소프트웨어 개발을 자동화하는 것","반복 Bash 루프를 사용하여 자율적 AI 코딩 솔루션을 생성하는 것","AI 지원 개발에서 컨텍스트 오버플로우와 저하를 관리하는 것"],"es":["Automatización del desarrollo de software con desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones","Generación de soluciones de codificación de IA autónoma utilizando bucles bash iterativos","Gestión del desbordamiento y la degradación del contexto en el desarrollo asistido por IA"],"fr":["Automatisation du développement de logiciels avec un développement piloté par des spécifications","Génération de solutions de codage de l''IA autonome en utilisant des boucles bash itératives","Gestion du débordement et de la dégradation du contexte dans le développement assisté par l''IA"],"de":["Automatisierung der Softwareentwicklung mit spezifikationsgetriebener Entwicklung","Generierung autonomer AI-Coding-Lösungen unter Verwendung iterativer Bash-Schleifen","Verwaltung des Kontextüberlaufs und -abbaus in der AI-gestützten Entwicklung"],"pt":["Automatizar o desenvolvimento de software com desenvolvimento orientado por especificações","Gerar soluções de codificação de IA autônoma usando loops bash iterativos","Gerenciar o transbordamento e degradação do contexto no desenvolvimento assistido por IA"],"ru":["Автоматизация разработки программного обеспечения с помощью разработки, управляемой спецификациями","Генерация автономных решений кодирования ИИ с помощью итеративных циклов bash","Управление переполнением и ухудшением контекста в разработке с помощью ИИ"],"ar":["أتمتة التطوير البرمجي بالاعتماد على التطوير الموجه بالمواصفات","генерация حلول الترميز الذكية المستقلة باستخدام الحلقات التكرارية لBASH","إدارة فيضان السياق والانحدار في التطوير بمساعدة الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires spec-driven development setup","Dependent on Geoffrey Huntley''s iterative bash loop","May require additional configuration for context window management"],"zh":["需要规范驱动开发设置","依赖于杰弗里·亨特利的反复Bash循环","可能需要额外的配置来管理上下文窗口"],"ja":["規範駆動開発の設定が必要","ジェフリー・ハントリーの反復Bashループに依存","コンテキストウィンドウの管理には追加の設定が必要になる場合がある"],"ko":["규약 기반 개발 설정이 필요합니다.","제프리 헌틀리의 반복 Bash 루프에 의존합니다.","컨텍스트 창 관리를 위해 추가 구성이 필요할 수 있습니다."],"es":["Requiere configuración de desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones","Dependiente del bucle bash iterativo de Geoffrey Huntley","Puede requerir configuración adicional para la gestión de ventanas de contexto"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de développement piloté par des spécifications","Dépendante de la boucle bash itérative de Geoffrey Huntley","Peut nécessiter une configuration supplémentaire pour la gestion des fenêtres de contexte"],"de":["Benötigt eine Konfiguration für spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklung","Abhängig von der iterativen Bash-Schleife von Geoffrey Huntley","Kann zusätzliche Konfiguration für die Verwaltung von Kontextfenstern erfordern"],"pt":["Requer configuração de desenvolvimento orientado por especificações","Depende do loop bash iterativo de Geoffrey Huntley","Pode requerer configuração adicional para gerenciamento de janelas de contexto"],"ru":["Требует настройки разработки, управляемой спецификациями","Зависит от итеративного цикла bash Джоффри Хантли","Может потребовать дополнительной настройки для управления контекстными окнами"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد التطوير الموجه بالمواصفات","يعتمد على حلقة باش التكرارية لجوفري هانتلي","يمكن أن يتطلب إعدادًا إضافيًا لإدارة نوافذ السياق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('andrewle9510/design-skill-orchestrator/fd-accessibility', 'community', 'andrewle9510', 'design-skill-orchestrator', 'andrewle9510/design-skill-orchestrator', 'fd-accessibility', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.477Z', '2026-02-18T09:26:21.979Z', NULL, '{"id":"andrewle9510/design-skill-orchestrator/fd-accessibility","name":"fd-accessibility","description":{"zh":"提供专家级的无障碍指导，确保产品满足 WCAG 标准和无障碍设计要求。帮助开发者创建更具包容性的产品。","ja":"アクセシビリティの専門知識を提供し、製品が WCAG 標準とアクセシビリティ設計要件を満たすことを保証します。開発者がより包摂的な製品を作成するのを支援します。","ko":"접근성에 대한 전문 지식을 제공하여 제품이 WCAG 규정 및 접근성 디자인 요구 사항을满足하도록 합니다. 개발자가 더包容적인 제품을 만들 수 있도록 지원합니다.","es":"El experto en accesibilidad garantiza que los productos sean utilizables por todos, incluidas personas con discapacidades","fr":"L''expert en accessibilité garantit que les produits soient utilisables par tous, y compris les personnes handicapées","de":"Der Barrierefreie-Experte stellt sicher, dass Produkte von allen verwendet werden können, einschließlich Menschen mit Behinderungen","pt":"O fd-accessibility fornece orientação especializada em conformidade WCAG e design inclusivo. Certifique-se de que seu produto seja acessível a todos","ru":"Доступность веба fd-accessibility предоставляет экспертные рекомендации по соответствию WCAG и инклюзивному дизайну. Убедитесь, что ваш продукт доступен всем","ar":"يقدم fd-accessibility إرشادات خاصة في مطابقة WCAG والتصميم الشامل. تأكد من أن منتجك يمكن الوصول إليه من قبل الجميع","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"无障碍专家 - WCAG 合规与无障碍设计","ja":"アクセシビリティ専門家 - WCAG 適合とアクセシビリティ設計","ko":"접근성 전문가 - WCAG 규정 및 접근성 디자인","es":"Experto en Accesibilidad Web","fr":"Expert en Accessibilité Web","de":"Barrierefreie Web-Experten","pt":"Acessibilidade Web: Expert em Conformidade WCAG","ru":"Доступность Веба: Эксперт по соответствию WCAG","ar":"إمكانية الوصول إلى الويب: خبير في مطابقة WCAG","en":"fd-accessibility"},"description":{"zh":"提供专家级的无障碍指导，确保产品满足 WCAG 标准和无障碍设计要求。帮助开发者创建更具包容性的产品。","ja":"アクセシビリティの専門知識を提供し、製品が WCAG 標準とアクセシビリティ設計要件を満たすことを保証します。開発者がより包摂的な製品を作成するのを支援します。","ko":"접근성에 대한 전문 지식을 제공하여 제품이 WCAG 규정 및 접근성 디자인 요구 사항을满足하도록 합니다. 개발자가 더包容적인 제품을 만들 수 있도록 지원합니다.","es":"El experto en accesibilidad garantiza que los productos sean utilizables por todos, incluidas personas con discapacidades","fr":"L''expert en accessibilité garantit que les produits soient utilisables par tous, y compris les personnes handicapées","de":"Der Barrierefreie-Experte stellt sicher, dass Produkte von allen verwendet werden können, einschließlich Menschen mit Behinderungen","pt":"O fd-accessibility fornece orientação especializada em conformidade WCAG e design inclusivo. Certifique-se de que seu produto seja acessível a todos","ru":"Доступность веба fd-accessibility предоставляет экспертные рекомендации по соответствию WCAG и инклюзивному дизайну. Убедитесь, что ваш продукт доступен всем","ar":"يقدم fd-accessibility إرشادات خاصة في مطابقة WCAG والتصميم الشامل. تأكد من أن منتجك يمكن الوصول إليه من قبل الجميع","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["WCAG 合规","无障碍设计模式","屏幕阅读器支持","键盘导航","可访问组件实现"],"ja":["WCAG 適合","アクセシビリティ設計パターン","スクリーンリーダーのサポート","キーボードナビゲーション","アクセシブルコンポーネントの実装"],"ko":["WCAG 규정","접근성 디자인 패턴","화면 리더 지원","키보드 탐색","접근 가능한 구성 요소 구현"],"es":["Cumplimiento de la norma WCAG","Diseño de patrones inclusivos","Soporte de lectores de pantalla","Navegación por teclado","Implementación de componentes accesibles"],"fr":["Conformité à la norme WCAG","Conception de modèles inclusifs","Prise en charge des lecteurs d''écran","Navigation au clavier","Mise en œuvre de composants accessibles"],"de":["Einhaltung der WCAG-Norm","Entwicklung von inklusiven Designmustern","Unterstützung von Bildschirmlesern","Tastaturnavigation","Implementierung von barrierefreien Komponenten"],"pt":["Conformidade WCAG","Padrões de design inclusivos","Suporte a leitores de tela","Navegação por teclado","Implementação de componentes acessíveis"],"ru":["Соответствие WCAG","Инклюзивные шаблоны дизайна","Поддержка экранных читателей","Навигация с помощью клавиатуры","Реализация доступных компонентов"],"ar":["مطابقة WCAG","أنماط من التصميم الشامل","دعم قراء الشاشة","الملاحة باللوحة","تنفيذ مكونات يمكن الوصول إليها"]},"keywords":{"zh":["无障碍设计","WCAG 合规","屏幕阅读器","键盘导航","可访问组件","包容性设计"],"ja":["アクセシビリティ設計","WCAG 適合","スクリーンリーダー","キーボードナビゲーション","アクセシブルコンポーネント","包摂性設計"],"ko":["접근성 디자인","WCAG 규정","화면 리더","키보드 탐색","접근 가능한 구성 요소","포용적 디자인"],"es":["accesibilidad web","WCAG","diseño inclusivo","lectores de pantalla","navegación por teclado","componentes accesibles","experto en accesibilidad"],"fr":["accessibilité web","WCAG","conception inclusive","lecteurs d''écran","navigation au clavier","composants accessibles","expert en accessibilité"],"de":["Web-Accessibility","WCAG","inklusive Design","Bildschirmleser","Tastaturnavigation","barrierefreie Komponenten","Barrierefreie-Experte"],"pt":["acessibilidade web","conformidade WCAG","design inclusivo","leitores de tela","navegação por teclado","componentes acessíveis","desenvolvimento web acessível"],"ru":["доступность веба","соответствие WCAG","инклюзивный дизайн","экранные читатели","навигация с помощью клавиатуры","доступные компоненты","разработка веба с учетом доступности"],"ar":["إمكانية الوصول إلى الويب","مطابقة WCAG","تصميم شامل","قراء الشاشة","الملاحة باللوحة","مكونات يمكن الوصول إليها","تطوير الويب مع إمكانية الوصول"]}},"owner":"andrewle9510","repo":"design-skill-orchestrator","repoPath":"andrewle9510/design-skill-orchestrator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.477Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"fd-accessibility","description":"Expert skill for WCAG compliance, inclusive design, contrast requirements, screen readers, keyboard navigation, and focus states. Use when ensuring accessibility, auditing for a11y issues, or implementing inclusive patterns.","bodyPreview":"# Accessibility Expert\n\nProvide expert guidance on WCAG compliance, inclusive design patterns, screen reader support, keyboard navigation, and accessible component implementation.\n\n## Role Definition\n\nYou are an **Accessibility Expert** — responsible for ensuring the product is usable by everyone, including people with disabilities. You verify that all design decisions meet accessibility standards and provide inclusive alternatives.\n\n## User Context\n\n- **User Profile**: Domain expert (film curat","body":"# Accessibility Expert\n\nProvide expert guidance on WCAG compliance, inclusive design patterns, screen reader support, keyboard navigation, and accessible component implementation.\n\n## Role Definition\n\nYou are an **Accessibility Expert** — responsible for ensuring the product is usable by everyone, including people with disabilities. You verify that all design decisions meet accessibility standards and provide inclusive alternatives.\n\n## User Context\n\n- **User Profile**: Domain expert (film curation), not a design specialist\n- **Product**: Short-form film curation platform for content creators\n- **Tech Stack**: Next.js 16+, React 19, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui\n- **A11y Target**: WCAG 2.1 AA minimum compliance\n\n---\n\n## Core Responsibilities\n\n### 1. WCAG 2.1 Compliance\n\n**Four Core Principles (POUR)**\n\n| Principle | Meaning | Key Requirements |\n|-----------|---------|------------------|\n| **Perceivable** | Users can perceive content | Alt text, captions, contrast |\n| **Operable** | Users can navigate/interact | Keyboard access, no seizures |\n| **Understandable** | Content is clear | Readable, predictable, error help |\n| **Robust** | Works with assistive tech | Valid HTML, ARIA, semantic markup |\n\n### 2. Contrast Requirements\n\n| Level | Normal Text | Large Text | UI Components |\n|-------|-------------|------------|---------------|\n| **AA** | 4.5:1 | 3:1 | 3:1 |\n| **AAA** | 7:1 | 4.5:1 | 4.5:1 |\n\n**Large text** = 18pt (24px) regular OR 14pt (18.66px) bold\n\n```tsx\n// Verify contrast before using colors\n// Tools: WebAIM Contrast Checker, Figma plugins\n\n// Good: High contrast\n<p className=\"text-foreground bg-background\">Readable text</p>\n\n// Caution: Muted text must still meet 4.5:1\n<p className=\"text-muted-foreground\">Secondary text</p>\n```\n\n### 3. Keyboard Navigation\n\n**All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible:**\n\n| Key | Action |\n|-----|--------|\n| `Tab` | Move focus forward |\n| `Shift+Tab` | Move focus backward |\n| `Enter` | Activate buttons/links |\n| `Space` | Activate buttons, toggle checkboxes |\n| `Arrow keys` | Navigate within components |\n| `Escape` | Close modals/dropdowns |\n\n```tsx\n// Proper focus management\n<button \n  className=\"focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2\"\n  onKeyDown={(e) => {\n    if (e.key === ''Escape'') closeModal();\n  }}\n>\n  Action\n</button>\n```\n\n### 4. Focus States\n\n**Every focusable element needs a visible focus indicator:**\n\n```tsx\n// Tailwind focus classes\n<button className=\"\n  focus:outline-none \n  focus-visible:ring-2 \n  focus-visible:ring-ring \n  focus-visible:ring-offset-2 \n  focus-visible:ring-offset-background\n\">\n\n// For dark backgrounds\n<input className=\"\n  focus:ring-2 \n  focus:ring-primary \n  focus:border-primary\n\"/>\n```\n\n### 5. Screen Reader Support\n\n**Semantic HTML & ARIA**\n\n```tsx\n// Use semantic elements\n<nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\">\n  <ul role=\"list\">\n    <li><a href=\"/\">Home</a></li>\n  </ul>\n</nav>\n\n<main id=\"main-content\">\n  <article>\n    <h1>Film Title</h1>\n    <p>Description...</p>\n  </article>\n</main>\n\n// ARIA for dynamic content\n<div \n  role=\"status\" \n  aria-live=\"polite\"\n  aria-atomic=\"true\"\n>\n  {statusMessage}\n</div>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Accessibility Patterns\n\n### Images & Media\n\n```tsx\n// Informative images need alt text\n<img \n  src=\"/film-poster.jpg\" \n  alt=\"Film poster for ''The Journey'' showing a lone figure on a mountain path\"\n/>\n\n// Decorative images\n<img src=\"/decorative-bg.jpg\" alt=\"\" role=\"presentation\" />\n\n// Video with captions\n<video>\n  <source src=\"/video.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\" />\n  <track kind=\"captions\" src=\"/captions.vtt\" srclang=\"en\" label=\"English\" />\n</video>\n```\n\n### Forms\n\n```tsx\n// Properly labeled inputs\n<div className=\"space-y-2\">\n  <label htmlFor=\"email\" className=\"text-sm font-medium\">\n    Email address\n  </label>\n  <input\n    id=\"email\"\n    type=\"email\"\n    aria-describedby=\"email-error\"\n    aria-invalid={hasError}\n    className=\"...\"\n  />\n  {hasError && (\n    <p id=\"email-error\" className=\"text-sm text-destructive\" role=\"alert\">\n      Please enter a valid email address\n    </p>\n  )}\n</div>\n\n// Required fields\n<label htmlFor=\"name\">\n  Name <span aria-hidden=\"true\">*</span>\n  <span className=\"sr-only\">(required)</span>\n</label>\n```\n\n### Buttons & Links\n\n```tsx\n// Icon-only buttons need accessible names\n<button aria-label=\"Close modal\">\n  <XIcon aria-hidden=\"true\" />\n</button>\n\n// Links vs buttons\n<a href=\"/films/123\">View Film</a>  // Navigation\n<button onClick={handleAction}>Like</button>  // Action\n\n// Button loading states\n<button disabled aria-busy=\"true\">\n  <Spinner aria-hidden=\"true\" />\n  <span className=\"sr-only\">Loading...</span>\n</button>\n```\n\n### Modals & Dialogs\n\n```tsx\n// Accessible modal pattern\n<div\n  role=\"dialog\"\n  aria-modal=\"true\"\n  aria-labelledby=\"modal-title\"\n  aria-describedby=\"modal-description\"\n>\n  <h2 id=\"modal-title\">Confirm Action</h2>\n  <p id=\"modal-description\">Are you sure you want to proceed?</p>\n  \n  <button onClick={onConfirm}>Confirm</button>\n  <button onClick={onClose}>Cancel</button>\n</div>\n\n// Focus trap: Focus should stay within modal\n// Return focus to trigger element when closed\n```\n\n### Skip Links\n\n```tsx\n// Allow keyboard users to skip navigation\n<a \n  href=\"#main-content\" \n  className=\"sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-50 focus:p-4 focus:bg-background focus:ring-2\"\n>\n  Skip to main content\n</a>\n\n<main id=\"main-content\" tabIndex={-1}>\n  {/* Page content */}\n</main>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Accessibility Checklist\n\n### Visual Design\n- [ ] Color contrast meets WCAG AA (4.5:1 for text)\n- [ ] Color is not the only way to convey information\n- [ ] Focus indicators are visible\n- [ ] Text can be resized to 200% without breaking\n- [ ] No content flashes more than 3 times per second\n\n### Keyboard Navigation\n- [ ] All interactive elements are keyboard accessible\n- [ ] Tab order follows logical reading order\n- [ ] Focus is never trapped (except in modals)\n- [ ] Keyboard shortcuts don''t conflict with assistive tech\n- [ ] Skip links available for navigation\n\n### Screen Readers\n- [ ] All images have appropriate alt text\n- [ ] Headings follow proper hierarchy (h1 → h2 → h3)\n- [ ] Links have descriptive text (not \"click here\")\n- [ ] Form inputs have associated labels\n- [ ] Error messages are announced\n- [ ] Dynamic content updates are announced\n\n### Content\n- [ ] Language is specified (`<html lang=\"en\">`)\n- [ ] Page titles are descriptive and unique\n- [ ] Error messages explain how to fix issues\n- [ ] Instructions don''t rely on sensory characteristics\n\n---\n\n## Testing Tools\n\n### Automated Testing\n```markdown\n- **axe DevTools** - Browser extension for automated testing\n- **WAVE** - Web accessibility evaluation tool\n- **Lighthouse** - Chrome DevTools accessibility audit\n- **eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y** - Catch issues during development\n```\n\n### Manual Testing\n```markdown\n- **Keyboard only** - Navigate without mouse\n- **Screen reader** - Test with VoiceOver (Mac) or NVDA (Windows)\n- **Zoom 200%** - Ensure content reflows properly\n- **High contrast mode** - Test on Windows high contrast\n```\n\n### Research Commands\n\n```\nweb_search: \"WCAG 2.1 checklist\"\nread_web_page: https://webaim.org/resources/contrastchecker/\nread_web_page: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/quickref/\nweb_search: \"accessible [component type] pattern\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## shadcn/ui Accessibility\n\nshadcn/ui components are built on Radix UI primitives with accessibility baked in:\n\n```tsx\n// Dialog with built-in accessibility\nimport {\n  Dialog,\n  DialogContent,\n  DialogHeader,\n  DialogTitle,\n  DialogDescription,\n} from \"@/components/ui/dialog\";\n\n<Dialog>\n  <DialogTrigger>Open</DialogTrigger>\n  <DialogContent>\n    <DialogHeader>\n      <DialogTitle>Edit Profile</DialogTitle>\n      <DialogDescription>\n        Make changes to your profile here.\n      </DialogDescription>\n    </DialogHeader>\n    {/* Focus trapped, Escape closes, screen reader announced */}\n  </DialogContent>\n</Dialog>\n```\n\n**Always include:**\n- `DialogTitle` for screen reader announcement\n- `DialogDescription` for context\n- Proper trigger elements\n\n---\n\n## Common Accessibility Issues\n\n| Issue | Problem | Solution |\n|-------|---------|----------|\n| Missing alt text | Images not described | Add descriptive alt or alt=\"\" |\n| Low contrast | Text hard to read | Increase contrast to 4.5:1+ |\n| Missing labels | Forms inaccessible | Associate labels with inputs |\n| No focus styles | Keyboard users lost | Add visible focus indicators |\n| Auto-playing media | Disorienting | Add pause controls |\n| Click-only handlers | Keyboard excluded | Add keyboard event handlers |\n| Div buttons | Not accessible | Use semantic `<button>` |\n| Missing headings | No structure | Use proper h1-h6 hierarchy |\n\n---\n\n## Handoff Guidance\n\n| To Expert | Accessibility Requirements |\n|-----------|---------------------------|\n| `fd-color-systems` | Verify all color combinations meet contrast |\n| `fd-typography` | Minimum 16px body, scalable text |\n| `fd-components` | Keyboard accessible, ARIA labels |\n| `fd-states-feedback` | Error states announced to screen readers |\n| `fd-animations` | Respect prefers-reduced-motion |\n\n---\n\n## Key Principles\n\n1. **Inclusive by Default** — Accessibility is not an afterthought\n2. **Semantic HTML First** — Use proper elements before ARIA\n3. **Keyboard Everything** — If you can click it, you can tab to it\n4. **Test with Real Tools** — Use screen readers, not just automated tests\n5. **Announce Changes** — Dynamic content needs ARIA live regions\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:26:21.979Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Interface Agents needing expert guidance on WCAG compliance and inclusive design patterns","zh":"非常适合需要专家指导的界面代理来遵守WCAG标准和包容性设计模式","ja":"WCAG準拠とインクルーシブなデザインパターンに関する専門家の指導が必要なインターフェースエージェントに最適","ko":"WCAG 규정 및 포용적 디자인 패턴에 대한 전문가 지침이 필요한 인터페이스 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Interfaz que necesitan orientación experta sobre cumplimiento de WCAG y patrones de diseño inclusivo","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''interface ayant besoin de conseils d''experts sur la conformité WCAG et les modèles de conception inclusive","de":"Perfekt für Interface-Agents, die Expertenleitfäden zur WCAG-Konformität und inklusiven Designmustern benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Interface que precisam de orientação especializada sobre conformidade com WCAG e padrões de design inclusivo","ru":"Идеально для Интерфейсных Агентов, которым требуется экспертное руководство по соблюдению требований WCAG и моделей инклюзивного дизайна","ar":"مثالي لعميل الواجهة الذي يحتاج إلى إرشادات خبيرة بشأن امتثال WCAG وأنماط التصميم الشامل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement screen reader support, keyboard navigation, and accessible component implementation using WCAG standards and best practices for inclusive design, ensuring products are usable by everyone, including people with disabilities","zh":"赋予代理实现屏幕阅读器支持、键盘导航和使用WCAG标准及最佳实践的可访问组件实现，确保产品可被每个人使用，包括残障人士","ja":"WCAG標準とベストプラクティスを使用したスクリーンリーダーのサポート、キーボードナビゲーション、及びアクセシブルなコンポーネントの実装をエージェントに実装させることで、製品が誰でも利用できるようにし、障害者の利用も可能にする","ko":"WCAG 표준 및 최고의 실践을 사용하여 화면 판독기 지원, 키보드 탐색 및 접근 가능한 구성 요소 구현을 에이전트에 구현하여 모든 사람이 사용할 수 있도록 하며, 장애인도 사용할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar soporte de lectura de pantalla, navegación por teclado y implementación de componentes accesibles utilizando estándares WCAG y mejores prácticas para diseño inclusivo, asegurando que los productos sean utilizables por todos, incluidas las personas con discapacidades","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre une prise en charge de lecteur d''écran, une navigation au clavier et une mise en œuvre de composants accessibles en utilisant les normes WCAG et les meilleures pratiques pour la conception inclusive, en garantissant que les produits soient utilisables par tous, y compris les personnes handicapées","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Bildschirmleseunterstützung, Tastaturnavigation und barrierefreie Komponentenimplementierung mithilfe von WCAG-Standards und Best Practices für inklusives Design umzusetzen, um sicherzustellen, dass Produkte von allen nutzen können, einschließlich Menschen mit Behinderungen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar suporte a leitor de tela, navegação por teclado e implementação de componentes acessíveis usando padrões WCAG e as melhores práticas para design inclusivo, garantindo que os produtos sejam usáveis por todos, incluindo pessoas com deficiência","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовать поддержку программ для чтения с экрана, навигацию с помощью клавиатуры и реализацию доступных компонентов с использованием стандартов WCAG и лучших практик инклюзивного дизайна, обеспечивая возможность использования продуктов всеми, включая людей с ограниченными возможностями","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية تنفيذ دعم قارئ الشاشة والتنقل باللوحة وتنفيذ مكونات قابلة للوصول باستخدام معايير WCAG وأفضل الممارسات لتصميم شامل، مما يضمن أن تكون المنتجات قابلة للاستخدام من قبل الجميع، بما في ذلك الأشخاص ذوي الإعاقة"},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing web applications for WCAG compliance","Implementing accessible navigation patterns for keyboard users","Designing inclusive components for screen reader compatibility"],"zh":["审计Web应用程序以遵守WCAG标准","为键盘用户实现可访问的导航模式","设计可与屏幕阅读器兼容的组件"],"ja":["WCAG準拠を確認するためのWebアプリケーションの監査","キーボードユーザーのためのアクセシブルなナビゲーションパターンの実装","スクリーンリーダーとの互換性のあるコンポーネントの設計"],"ko":["WCAG 규정 준수를 확인하기 위한 웹 애플리케이션 감사","키보드 사용자를 위한 접근 가능한 탐색 패턴 구현","화면 판독기와의 호환성을 가진 구성 요소 설계"],"es":["Auditoría de aplicaciones web para cumplimiento de WCAG","Implementación de patrones de navegación accesibles para usuarios de teclado","Diseño de componentes inclusivos para compatibilidad con lectores de pantalla"],"fr":["Audit de applications web pour conformité WCAG","Mise en œuvre de modèles de navigation accessibles pour utilisateurs de clavier","Conception de composants inclusifs pour compatibilité avec les lecteurs d''écran"],"de":["Auditing von Webanwendungen für WCAG-Konformität","Implementierung von barrierefreien Navigationsmustern für Tastaturnutzer","Entwurf von inklusiven Komponenten für Bildschirmlesekompatibilität"],"pt":["Auditoria de aplicações web para conformidade com WCAG","Implementação de padrões de navegação acessíveis para usuários de teclado","Projeto de componentes inclusivos para compatibilidade com leitor de tela"],"ru":["Аудит веб-приложений на соответствие требованиям WCAG","Реализация доступных моделей навигации для пользователей клавиатуры","Разработка инклюзивных компонентов для совместимости с программами для чтения с экрана"],"ar":["فحص تطبيقات الويب لامتثالها لمعايير WCAG","تنفيذ أنماط التنقل القابلة للوصول لمستخدمي لوحة المفاتيح","تصميم مكونات شاملة لتوافق قارئ الشاشة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of WCAG guidelines and accessibility standards","May require additional testing with screen readers and other assistive technologies"],"zh":["需要了解WCAG指南和无障碍标准","可能需要使用屏幕阅读器和其他辅助技术进行额外测试"],"ja":["WCAGガイドラインとアクセシビリティ標準の知識が必要","スクリーンリーダーなどの補助技術を使用した追加テストが必