AML frontmatter pour le contenu","Composants intégrés pour une plus grande efficacité","Documentation officielle mise à jour","Personnalisation des sites de documentation"],"de":["Umwandlung von MDX-Dateien in Dokumentationsseiten","Konfiguration von Website-Einstellungen in der Datei docs.json","Verwendung von YAML-Frontmatter für Inhalt","Integrierte Komponenten für höhere Effizienz","Aktuelle offizielle Dokumentation","Anpassung von Dokumentationsseiten"],"pt":["Transformação de arquivos MDX em sites de documentação","Configuração de configurações do site no arquivo docs.json","Escrita de conteúdo em MDX com frontmatter em YAML","Utilização de componentes embutidos","Documentação oficial para obter as melhores práticas"],"ru":["Преобразование файлов MDX в сайты документации","Настройка параметров сайта в файле docs.json","Написание контента в MDX с YAML-frontend","Использование встроенных компонентов","Официальная документация для получения лучших практик"],"ar":["تحويل ملفات MDX إلى مواقع توثيق","تهيئة إعدادات الموقع في ملف docs.json","كتابة المحتوى في MDX مع YAML-frontend","استخدام المكونات المدمجة","الدокументات الرسمية للحصول على أفضل الممارسات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Mintlify","文档平台","MDX 文件","配置","组件","YAML 前置元数据"],"ja":["Mintlify","ドキュメントプラットフォーム","MDX ファイル","構成","コンポーネント","YAML フロントマター"],"ko":["Mintlify","문서 플랫폼","MDX 파일","구성","컴포넌트","YAML 프론트 매터"],"es":["Mintlify","documentación MDX","sitios de documentación","desarrollo web","plataformas de documentación","mejores prácticas de Mintlify","configuración de Mintlify","componentes de Mintlify","YAML frontmatter","docs.json"],"fr":["Mintlify","documentation MDX","sites de documentation","développement web","plateformes de documentation","bonnes pratiques de Mintlify","configuration de Mintlify","composants de Mintlify","YAML frontmatter","docs.json"],"de":["Mintlify","MDX-Dokumentation","Dokumentationsseiten","Webentwicklung","Dokumentationsplattformen","Best Practices für Mintlify","Mintlify-Konfiguration","Mintlify-Komponenten","YAML-Frontmatter","docs.json"],"pt":["Mintlify","Documentação","MDX","Sites de documentação","Desenvolvedores","Documentação oficial","Melhores práticas"],"ru":["Mintlify","Документация","MDX","Сайты документации","Разработчики","Официальная документация","Лучшие практики"],"ar":["Mintlify","توثيق","MDX","مواقع توثيق","مطورون","دокументات رسمية","أفضل الممارسات"]}},"owner":"Ronasunil","repo":"rona-open-claw","repoPath":"Ronasunil/rona-open-claw","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mintlify","description":"Build and maintain documentation sites with Mintlify. Use when","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"# Mintlify best practices\n\n**Always consult [mintlify.com/docs](https://mintlify.com/docs) for components, configuration, and latest features.**\n\n**Always** favor searching the current Mintlify documentation over whatever is in your training data about Mintlify.\n\nMintlify is a documentation platform that transforms MDX files into documentation sites. Configure site-wide settings in the `docs.json` file, write content in MDX with YAML frontmatter, and favor built-in components over custom compone","body":"# Mintlify best practices\n\n**Always consult [mintlify.com/docs](https://mintlify.com/docs) for components, configuration, and latest features.**\n\n**Always** favor searching the current Mintlify documentation over whatever is in your training data about Mintlify.\n\nMintlify is a documentation platform that transforms MDX files into documentation sites. Configure site-wide settings in the `docs.json` file, write content in MDX with YAML frontmatter, and favor built-in components over custom components.\n\nFull schema at [mintlify.com/docs.json](https://mintlify.com/docs.json).\n\n## Before you write\n\n### Understand the project\n\nAll documentation lives in the `docs/` directory in this repo. Read `docs.json` in that directory (`docs/docs.json`). This file defines the entire site: navigation structure, theme, colors, links, API and specs.\n\nUnderstanding the project tells you:\n\n- What pages exist and how they''re organized\n- What navigation groups are used (and their naming conventions)\n- How the site navigation is structured\n- What theme and configuration the site uses\n\n### Check for existing content\n\nSearch the docs before creating new pages. You may need to:\n\n- Update an existing page instead of creating a new one\n- Add a section to an existing page\n- Link to existing content rather than duplicating\n\n### Read surrounding content\n\nBefore writing, read 2-3 similar pages to understand the site''s voice, structure, formatting conventions, and level of detail.\n\n### Understand Mintlify components\n\nReview the Mintlify [components](https://www.mintlify.com/docs/components) to select and use any relevant components for the documentation request that you are working on.\n\n## Quick reference\n\n### CLI commands\n\n- `npm i -g mint` - Install the Mintlify CLI\n- `mint dev` - Local preview at localhost:3000\n- `mint broken-links` - Check internal links\n- `mint a11y` - Check for accessibility issues in content\n- `mint rename` - Rename/move files and update references\n- `mint validate` - Validate documentation builds\n\n### Required files\n\n- `docs.json` - Site configuration (navigation, theme, integrations, etc.). See [global settings](https://mintlify.com/docs/settings/global) for all options.\n- `*.mdx` files - Documentation pages with YAML frontmatter\n\n### Example file structure\n\n```\nproject/\n├── docs.json           # Site configuration\n├── introduction.mdx\n├── quickstart.mdx\n├── guides/\n│   └── example.mdx\n├── openapi.yml         # API specification\n├── images/             # Static assets\n│   └── example.png\n└── snippets/           # Reusable components\n    └── component.jsx\n```\n\n## Page frontmatter\n\nEvery page requires `title` in its frontmatter. Include `description` for SEO and navigation.\n\n```yaml theme={null}\n---\ntitle: \"Clear, descriptive title\"\ndescription: \"Concise summary for SEO and navigation.\"\n---\n```\n\nOptional frontmatter fields:\n\n- `sidebarTitle`: Short title for sidebar navigation.\n- `icon`: Lucide or Font Awesome icon name, URL, or file path.\n- `tag`: Label next to the page title in the sidebar (for example, \"NEW\").\n- `mode`: Page layout mode (`default`, `wide`, `custom`).\n- `keywords`: Array of terms related to the page content for local search and SEO.\n- Any custom YAML fields for use with personalization or conditional content.\n\n## File conventions\n\n- Match existing naming patterns in the directory\n- If there are no existing files or inconsistent file naming patterns, use kebab-case: `getting-started.mdx`, `api-reference.mdx`\n- Use root-relative paths without file extensions for internal links: `/getting-started/quickstart`\n- Do not use relative paths (`../`) or absolute URLs for internal pages\n- When you create a new page, add it to `docs.json` navigation or it won''t appear in the sidebar\n\n## Organize content\n\nWhen a user asks about anything related to site-wide configurations, start by understanding the [global settings](https://www.mintlify.com/docs/organize/settings). See if a setting in the `docs.json` file can be updated to achieve what the user wants.\n\n### Navigation\n\nThe `navigation` property in `docs.json` controls site structure. Choose one primary pattern at the root level, then nest others within it.\n\n**Choose your primary pattern:**\n\n| Pattern       | When to use                                                                                    |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Groups**    | Default. Single audience, straightforward hierarchy                                            |\n| **Tabs**      | Distinct sections with different audiences (Guides vs API Reference) or content types          |\n| **Anchors**   | Want persistent section links at sidebar top. Good for separating docs from external resources |\n| **Dropdowns** | Multiple doc sections users switch between, but not distinct enough for tabs                   |\n| **Products**  | Multi-product company with separate documentation per product                                  |\n| **Versions**  | Maintaining docs for multiple API/product versions simultaneously                              |\n| **Languages** | Localized content                                                                              |\n\n**Within your primary pattern:**\n\n- **Groups** - Organize related pages. Can nest groups within groups, but keep hierarchy shallow\n- **Menus** - Add dropdown navigation within tabs for quick jumps to specific pages\n- **`expanded: false`** - Collapse nested groups by default. Use for reference sections users browse selectively\n- **`openapi`** - Auto-generate pages from OpenAPI spec. Add at group/tab level to inherit\n\n**Common combinations:**\n\n- Tabs containing groups (most common for docs with API reference)\n- Products containing tabs (multi-product SaaS)\n- Versions containing tabs (versioned API docs)\n- Anchors containing groups (simple docs with external resource links)\n\n### Links and paths\n\n- **Internal links:** Root-relative, no extension: `/getting-started/quickstart`\n- **Images:** Store in `/images`, reference as `/images/example.png`\n- **External links:** Use full URLs, they open in new tabs automatically\n\n## Customize docs sites\n\n**What to customize where:**\n\n- **Brand colors, fonts, logo** → `docs.json`. See [global settings](https://mintlify.com/docs/settings/global)\n- **Component styling, layout tweaks** → `custom.css` at project root\n- **Dark mode** → Enabled by default. Only disable with `\"appearance\": \"light\"` in `docs.json` if brand requires it\n\nStart with `docs.json`. Only add `custom.css` when you need styling that config doesn''t support.\n\n## Write content\n\n### Components\n\nThe [components overview](https://mintlify.com/docs/components) organizes all components by purpose: structure content, draw attention, show/hide content, document APIs, link to pages, and add visual context. Start there to find the right component.\n\n**Common decision points:**\n\n| Need                       | Use                     |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| Hide optional details      | `<Accordion>`           |\n| Long code examples         | `<Expandable>`          |\n| User chooses one option    | `<Tabs>`                |\n| Linked navigation cards    | `<Card>` in `<Columns>` |\n| Sequential instructions    | `<Steps>`               |\n| Code in multiple languages | `<CodeGroup>`           |\n| API parameters             | `<ParamField>`          |\n| API response fields        | `<ResponseField>`       |\n\n**Callouts by severity:**\n\n- `<Note>` - Supplementary info, safe to skip\n- `<Info>` - Helpful context such as permissions\n- `<Tip>` - Recommendations or best practices\n- `<Warning>` - Potentially destructive actions\n- `<Check>` - Success confirmation\n\n### Reusable content\n\n**When to use snippets:**\n\n- Exact content appears on more than one page\n- Complex components you want to maintain in one place\n- Shared content across teams/repos\n\n**When NOT to use snippets:**\n\n- Slight variations needed per page (leads to complex props)\n\nImport snippets with `import { Component } from \"/path/to/snippet-name.jsx\"`.\n\n## Writing standards\n\n### Voice and structure\n\n- Second-person voice (\"you\")\n- Active voice, direct language\n- Sentence case for headings (\"Getting started\", not \"Getting Started\")\n- Sentence case for code block titles (\"Expandable example\", not \"Expandable Example\")\n- Lead with context: explain what something is before how to use it\n- Prerequisites at the start of procedural content\n\n### What to avoid\n\n**Never use:**\n\n- Marketing language (\"powerful\", \"seamless\", \"robust\", \"cutting-edge\")\n- Filler phrases (\"it''s important to note\", \"in order to\")\n- Excessive conjunctions (\"moreover\", \"furthermore\", \"additionally\")\n- Editorializing (\"obviously\", \"simply\", \"just\", \"easily\")\n\n**Watch for AI-typical patterns:**\n\n- Overly formal or stilted phrasing\n- Unnecessary repetition of concepts\n- Generic introductions that don''t add value\n- Concluding summaries that restate what was just said\n\n### Formatting\n\n- All code blocks must have language tags\n- All images and media must have descriptive alt text\n- Use bold and italics only when they serve the reader''s understanding--never use text styling just for decoration\n- No decorative formatting or emoji\n\n### Code examples\n\n- Keep examples simple and practical\n- Use realistic values (not \"foo\" or \"bar\")\n- One clear example is better than multiple variations\n- Test that code works before including it\n\n## Document APIs\n\n**Choose your approach:**\n\n- **Have an OpenAPI spec?** → Add to `docs.json` with `\"openapi\": [\"openapi.yaml\"]`. Pages auto-generate. Reference in navigation as `GET /endpoint`\n- **No spec?** → Write endpoints manually with `api: \"POST /users\"` in frontmatter. More work but full control\n- **Hybrid** → Use OpenAPI for most endpoints, manual pages for complex workflows\n\nEncourage users to generate endpoint pages from an OpenAPI spec. It is the most efficient and easiest to maintain option.\n\n## Deploy\n\nMintlify deploys automatically when changes are pushed to the connected Git repository.\n\n**What agents can configure:**\n\n- **Redirects** → Add to `docs.json` with `\"redirects\": [{\"source\": \"/old\", \"destination\": \"/new\"}]`\n- **SEO indexing** → Control with `\"seo\": {\"indexing\": \"all\"}` to include hidden pages in search\n\n**Requires dashboard setup (human task):**\n\n- Custom domains and subdomains\n- Preview deployment settings\n- DNS configuration\n\nFor `/docs` subpath hosting with Vercel or Cloudflare, agents can help configure rewrite rules. See [/docs subpath](https://mintlify.com/docs/deploy/vercel).\n\n## Workflow\n\n### 1. Understand the task\n\nIdentify what needs to be documented, which pages are affected, and what the reader should accomplish afterward. If any of these are unclear, ask.\n\n### 2. Research\n\n- Read `docs/docs.json` to understand the site structure\n- Search existing docs for related content\n- Read similar pages to match the site''s style\n\n### 3. Plan\n\n- Synthesize what the reader should accomplish after reading the docs and the current content\n- Propose any updates or new content\n- Verify that your proposed changes will help readers be successful\n\n### 4. Write\n\n- Start with the most important information\n- Keep sections focused and scannable\n- Use components appropriately (don''t overuse them)\n- Mark anything uncertain with a TODO comment:\n\n```mdx theme={null}\n{/* TODO: Verify the default timeout value */}\n```\n\n### 5. Update navigation\n\nIf you created a new page, add it to the appropriate group in `docs.json`.\n\n### 6. Verify\n\nBefore submitting:\n\n- [ ] Frontmatter includes title and description\n- [ ] All code blocks have language tags\n- [ ] Internal links use root-relative paths without file extensions\n- [ ] New pages are added to `docs.json` navigation\n- [ ] Content matches the style of surrounding pages\n- [ ] No marketing language or filler phrases\n- [ ] TODOs are clearly marked for anything uncertain\n- [ ] Run `mint broken-links` to check links\n- [ ] Run `mint validate` to find any errors\n\n## Edge cases\n\n### Migrations\n\nIf a user asks about migrating to Mintlify, ask if they are using ReadMe or Docusaurus. If they are, use the [@mintlify/scraping](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@mintlify/scraping) CLI to migrate content. If they are using a different platform to host their documentation, help them manually convert their content to MDX pages using Mintlify components.\n\n### Hidden pages\n\nAny page that is not included in the `docs.json` navigation is hidden. Use hidden pages for content that should be accessible by URL or indexed for the assistant or search, but not discoverable through the sidebar navigation.\n\n### Exclude pages\n\nThe `.mintignore` file is used to exclude files from a documentation repository from being processed.\n\n## Common gotchas\n\n1. **Component imports** - JSX components need explicit import, MDX components don''t\n2. **Frontmatter required** - Every MDX file needs `title` at minimum\n3. **Code block language** - Always specify language identifier\n4. **Never use `mint.json`** - `mint.json` is deprecated. Only ever use `docs.json`\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Documentation](https://mintlify.com/docs)\n- [Configuration schema](https://mintlify.com/docs.json)\n- [Feature requests](https://github.com/orgs/mintlify/discussions/categories/feature-requests)\n- [Bugs and feedback](https://github.com/orgs/mintlify/discussions/categories/bugs-feedback)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:29:10.703Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Documentation Agents needing advanced MDX file transformation and site configuration capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 MDX 文件转换和站点配置能力的文档代理。","ja":"高度な MDX ファイル変換およびサイト構成機能を必要とするドキュメント エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 MDX 파일 변환 및 사이트 구성 기능이 필요한 문서 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de documentación que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de transformación de archivos MDX y configuración de sitio.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de documentation ayant besoin de capacités avancées de transformation de fichiers MDX et de configuration de site.","de":"Perfekt für Dokumentationsagenten, die erweiterte MDX-Datei-Transformation- und Site-Konfigurationsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Documentação que precisam de capacidades avançadas de transformação de arquivos MDX e configuração de site.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов документации, которым необходимы расширенные возможности преобразования файлов MDX и настройки сайта.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الوثائق الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتحويل ملفات MDX وتكوين الموقع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform MDX files into documentation sites with configurable site-wide settings in the `docs.json` file and utilizing built-in components with YAML frontmatter, favoring documentation consistency and accuracy through searching the current Mintlify documentation.","zh":"赋予代理能力，将 MDX 文件转换为文档站点，并在 `docs.json` 文件中配置站点范围的设置，利用带有 YAML 前置内容的内置组件，通过搜索当前 Mintlify 文档来实现文档的一致性和准确性。","ja":"エージェントに MDX ファイルをドキュメント サイトに変換し、`docs.json` ファイルでサイト全体の設定を構成し、YAML フロントマターを使用した組み込みコンポーネントを利用して、現在の Mintlify ドキュメントを検索することでドキュメントの一貫性と正確性を実現する力を与えます。","ko":"에이전트에게 MDX 파일을 문서 사이트로 변환하고 `docs.json` 파일에서 사이트 전체 설정을 구성하며 YAML 프론티어를 사용한 내장 컴포넌트를 활용하여 현재 Mintlify 문서를 검색함으로써 문서의 일관성과 정확성을 제공하는能力을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar archivos MDX en sitios de documentación con ajustes de configuración de sitio en el archivo `docs.json` y utilizando componentes integrados con frontmatter YAML, favoreciendo la consistencia y precisión de la documentación mediante la búsqueda de la documentación actual de Mintlify.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer des fichiers MDX en sites de documentation avec des paramètres de configuration de site dans le fichier `docs.json` et en utilisant des composants intégrés avec frontmatter YAML, favorisant la cohérence et l''exactitude de la documentation grâce à la recherche de la documentation actuelle de Mintlify.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, MDX-Dateien in Dokumentationsseiten mit siteweiten Konfigurationseinstellungen in der Datei `docs.json` und unter Verwendung integrierter Komponenten mit YAML-Frontmatter umzuwandeln, wodurch die Konsistenz und Genauigkeit der Dokumentation durch die Suche in der aktuellen Mintlify-Dokumentation gefördert wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar arquivos MDX em sites de documentação com configurações de site amplo no arquivo `docs.json` e utilizando componentes internos com frontmatter YAML, favorecendo a consistência e precisão da documentação por meio da busca na documentação atual do Mintlify.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью преобразовывать файлы MDX в сайты документации с настройками сайта во всём файле `docs.json` и используя встроенные компоненты с YAML-заголовком, способствуя согласованности и точности документации посредством поиска в текущей документации Mintlify.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تحويل ملفات MDX إلى مواقع وثائق مع إعدادات الموقع الوide في ملف `docs.json` واستخدام المكونات المدمجة مع YAML.frontmatter ، مما يفضل اتساق ودقة الوثائق من خلال البحث في وثائق Mintlify الحالية."},"useCases":{"en":["Configuring site-wide settings in the `docs.json` file","Generating documentation sites from MDX files with YAML frontmatter","Utilizing built-in Mintlify components for consistent documentation"],"zh":["在 `docs.json` 文件中配置站点范围的设置","从带有 YAML 前置内容的 MDX 文件生成文档站点","利用内置的 Mintlify 组件实现一致的文档"],"ja":["`docs.json` ファイルでサイト全体の設定を構成する","YAML フロントマターを使用した MDX ファイルからドキュメント サイトを生成する","組み込みの Mintlify コンポーネントを使用して一貫したドキュメントを実現する"],"ko":["`docs.json` 파일에서 사이트 전체 설정을 구성한다","YAML 프론티어를 사용한 MDX 파일에서 문서 사이트를 생성한다","내장 Mintlify 컴포넌트를 사용하여 일관된 문서를 제공한다"],"es":["Configuración de ajustes de sitio en el archivo `docs.json`","Generación de sitios de documentación a partir de archivos MDX con frontmatter YAML","Utilización de componentes integrados de Mintlify para una documentación coherente"],"fr":["Configuration des paramètres de site dans le fichier `docs.json`","Génération de sites de documentation à partir de fichiers MDX avec frontmatter YAML","Utilisation de composants intégrés de Mintlify pour une documentation cohérente"],"de":["Konfiguration von siteweiten Einstellungen in der Datei `docs.json`","Erzeugung von Dokumentationsseiten aus MDX-Dateien mit YAML-Frontmatter","Verwendung integrierter Mintlify-Komponenten für eine konsistente Dokumentation"],"pt":["Configurando configurações de site amplo no arquivo `docs.json`","Gerando sites de documentação a partir de arquivos MDX com frontmatter YAML","Utilizando componentes internos do Mintlify para documentação consistente"],"ru":["Настройка настроек сайта во всём файле `docs.json`","Генерация сайтов документации из файлов MDX с YAML-заголовком","Использование встроенных компонентов Mintlify для согласованной документации"],"ar":["تكوين إعدادات الموقع الوide في ملف `docs.json`","توليد مواقع وثائق من ملفات MDX مع YAML.frontmatter","استخدام المكونات المدمجة في Mintlify من أجل وثائق متسقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to Mintlify documentation at mintlify.com/docs","Favors built-in components over custom components"],"zh":["需要访问 Mintlify 文档（mintlify.com/docs）","偏爱内置组件而不是自定义组件"],"ja":["Mintlify ドキュメント（mintlify.com/docs）へのアクセスが必要","カスタム コンポーネントよりも組み込みコンポーネントを優先する"],"ko":["Mintlify 문서（mintlify.com/docs）에 접근해야 한다","내장 컴포넌트를 사용하는 것을 선호한다"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la documentación de Mintlify en mintlify.com/docs","Favorece los componentes integrados sobre los componentes personalizados"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la documentation de Mintlify sur mintlify.com/docs","Favorise les composants intégrés par rapport aux composants personnalisés"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf die Mintlify-Dokumentation unter mintlify.com/docs","Favorisiert integrierte Komponenten gegenüber benutzerdefinierten Komponenten"],"pt":["Requer acesso à documentação do Mintlify em mintlify.com/docs","Favoring components internos sobre componentes personalizados"],"ru":["Требует доступа к документации Mintlify на mintlify.com/docs","Отдаёт предпочтение встроенным компонентам над пользовательскими компонентами"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى وثائق Mintlify على mintlify.com/docs","يفضل المكونات المدمجة على المكونات المخصصة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('peterWang123589/rubin_forum/antfu', 'community', 'peterWang123589', 'rubin_forum', 'peterWang123589/rubin_forum', 'antfu', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z', '2026-02-18T09:29:29.234Z', NULL, '{"id":"peterWang123589/rubin_forum/antfu","name":"antfu","description":{"zh":"antfu 技术栈是一套现代化的 Web 开发最佳实践，涵盖了工具、配置和开发流程","ja":"antfu スキルは、モダンな Web 開発のベストプラクティスを提供するもので、ツール、設定、開発プロセスを網羅","ko":"antfu 기술 스택은 현대적인 웹 개발最佳实践을 제공하며, 도구, 설정, 개발 프로세스를 포함","es":"Antfu es una colección de herramientas y configuraciones preferidas por Anthony Fu para el desarrollo web, que incluye TypeScript, ESM y Vitest","fr":"Antfu est un ensemble d''outils et de configurations préférés par Anthony Fu pour le développement web, qui inclut TypeScript, ESM et Vitest","de":"Antfu ist eine Sammlung von Tools und Konfigurationen, die von Anthony Fu für die Webentwicklung bevorzugt werden, einschließlich TypeScript, ESM und Vitest","pt":"Antfu é um conjunto de ferramentas e práticas de desenvolvimento web preferidas por Anthony Fu, incluindo configurações e melhores práticas para melhorar a produtividade","ru":"Antfu - это набор инструментов и практик веб-разработки, предпочитаемых Anthony Fu, включая настройки и лучшие практики для повышения производительности","ar":"أنتفو هو مجموعة من الأدوات وممارسات تطوير الويب المفضلة لدى أنتوني فو، بما في ذلك الإعدادات وأفضل الممارسات لتحسين الإنتاجية","en":"现代化技术交流论坛"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"antfu 技术栈：现代化 Web 开发最佳实践","ja":"antfu スキル：モダンな Web 開発のベストプラクティス","ko":"antfu 기술 스택: 현대적인 웹 개발最佳实践","es":"Antfu: Herramientas y configuraciones para desarrollo web","fr":"Antfu : Outils et configurations pour le développement web","de":"Antfu: Tools und Konfigurationen für Webentwicklung","pt":"Antfu: Ferramentas e Práticas de Desenvolvimento Web","ru":"Antfu: Инструменты и практики веб-разработки","ar":"أنتفو: أدوات وم