理服务器，用于创建结构化的产品需求文档，实现可行且清晰的实施","ja":"prdは軽量ノードJS RPCプロキシサーバーであり、構造化された製品要件文書を作成し、実行可能で明確な実施を実現します","ko":"prd는 경량 노드JS RPC 프록시 서버로서 구조화된 제품 요구 사항 문서를 생성하여 실행 가능하며 명확한 구현을 달성합니다","es":"PRD es un servidor proxy RPC de NodeJS ligero que genera documentos de requisitos de producto claros y precisos","fr":"PRD est un serveur proxy RPC NodeJS léger qui génère des documents de exigences de produit clairs et précis","de":"PRD ist ein leichter NodeJS-RPC-Proxy-Server, der klare und präzise Produktanforderungsdokumente generiert","pt":"O PRD Generator é um servidor proxy RPC NodeJS leve que cria documentos de requisitos de produto claros e detalhados, com comportamentos caóticos","ru":"PRD Generator - это легкий прокси-сервер RPC NodeJS, который создает ясные и подробные документы требований к продукту с хаотическим поведением","ar":"PRD Generator هو خادم وكيل RPC NodeJS الخفيف الذي يولد مستندات متطلبات المنتج الواضحة والمفصلة مع السلوك العشوائي","en":"A lightweight NodeJS RPC proxy server with chaotic behaviours"},"definition":{"en":"A lightweight NodeJS RPC proxy server with chaotic behaviours"},"features":{"zh":["轻量级NodeJS RPC代理服务器","生成结构化的产品需求文档","支持实现可行且清晰的实施","简单易用","快速生成文档"],"ja":["軽量ノードJS RPCプロキシサーバー","構造化された製品要件文書を生成","実行可能で明確な実施を実現","シンプルで使いやすい","迅速に文書を生成"],"ko":["경량 노드JS RPC 프록시 서버","구조화된 제품 요구 사항 문서를 생성","실행 가능하며 명확한 구현을 달성","간단하고 사용하기 쉽다","迅速하게 문서를 생성"],"es":["Generación de documentos de requisitos de producto claros y precisos","Compatibilidad con NodeJS","Comportamientos caóticos para pruebas y simulaciones","Capacidad para guardar documentos en formato Markdown","Interfaz de usuario simple y fácil de usar"],"fr":["Génération de documents de exigences de produit clairs et précis","Compatibilité avec NodeJS","Comportements chaotiques pour les tests et les simulations","Capacité à enregistrer des documents au format Markdown","Interface utilisateur simple et facile à utiliser"],"de":["Erstellung klarer und präziser Produktanforderungsdokumente","Kompatibilität mit NodeJS","Chaotisches Verhalten für Tests und Simulationen","Fähigkeit, Dokumente im Markdown-Format zu speichern","Einfache und benutzerfreundliche Oberfläche"],"pt":["Criação de documentos de requisitos de produto detalhados","Comportamentos caóticos para simular cenários reais","Servidor proxy RPC NodeJS leve e eficiente","Geração de documentos em formato Markdown","Salva documentos em pasta `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`"],"ru":["Создание подробных документов требований к продукту","Хаотическое поведение для模拟 реальных сценариев","Легкий и эффективный прокси-сервер RPC NodeJS","Генерация документов в формате Markdown","Сохранение документов в папке `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`"],"ar":["إنشاء مستندات متطلبات المنتج المفصلة","السلوك العشوائي لمحاكاة السيناريوهات الحقيقية","خادم وكيل RPC NodeJS الخفيف والكفء","توليد المستندات في صيغة Markdown","حفظ المستندات في مجلد `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`"]},"keywords":{"zh":["NodeJS RPC代理服务器","产品需求文档","结构化文档","轻量级服务器","prd","实现可行","清晰实施"],"ja":["ノードJS RPCプロキシサーバー","製品要件文書","構造化文書","軽量サーバー","prd","実行可能","明確な実施"],"ko":["노드JS RPC 프록시 서버","제품 요구 사항 문서","구조화된 문서","경량 서버","prd","실행 가능","명확한 구현"],"es":["PRD","servidor proxy RPC","NodeJS","documentos de requisitos de producto","generación de documentos","comportamientos caóticos","testing","simulación"],"fr":["PRD","serveur proxy RPC","NodeJS","documents de exigences de produit","génération de documents","comportements chaotiques","testing","simulation"],"de":["PRD","RPC-Proxy-Server","NodeJS","Produktanforderungsdokumente","Erstellung von Dokumenten","chaotisches Verhalten","Testing","Simulation"],"pt":["PRD Generator","Servidor proxy RPC NodeJS","Comportamentos caóticos","Documentos de requisitos de produto","Geração de documentos","NodeJS","RPC","Proxy","Desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["PRD Generator","Прокси-сервер RPC NodeJS","Хаотическое поведение","Документы требований к продукту","Генерация документов","NodeJS","RPC","Прокси","Разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["PRD Generator","خادم وكيل RPC NodeJS","السلوك العشوائي","مستندات متطلبات المنتج","توليد المستندات","NodeJS","RPC","وكيل","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"aodhgan","repo":"eth-rpc-proxy","repoPath":"aodhgan/eth-rpc-proxy","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"prd","description":"Generate a Product Requirements Document (PRD) for a new feature. Use when planning a feature, starting a new project, or when asked to create a PRD. Triggers on: create a prd, write prd for, plan this feature, requirements for, spec out.","bodyPreview":"# PRD Generator\n\nCreate detailed Product Requirements Documents that are clear, actionable, and suitable for implementation.\n\n---\n\n## The Job\n\n1. Receive a feature description from the user\n2. Ask 3-5 essential clarifying questions (with lettered options)\n3. Generate a structured PRD based on answers\n4. Save to `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`\n\n**Important:** Do NOT start implementing. Just create the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAsk only critical questions where the initial prompt i","body":"# PRD Generator\n\nCreate detailed Product Requirements Documents that are clear, actionable, and suitable for implementation.\n\n---\n\n## The Job\n\n1. Receive a feature description from the user\n2. Ask 3-5 essential clarifying questions (with lettered options)\n3. Generate a structured PRD based on answers\n4. Save to `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`\n\n**Important:** Do NOT start implementing. Just create the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Clarifying Questions\n\nAsk only critical questions where the initial prompt is ambiguous. Focus on:\n\n- **Problem/Goal:** What problem does this solve?\n- **Core Functionality:** What are the key actions?\n- **Scope/Boundaries:** What should it NOT do?\n- **Success Criteria:** How do we know it''s done?\n\n### Format Questions Like This:\n\n```\n1. What is the primary goal of this feature?\n   A. Improve user onboarding experience\n   B. Increase user retention\n   C. Reduce support burden\n   D. Other: [please specify]\n\n2. Who is the target user?\n   A. New users only\n   B. Existing users only\n   C. All users\n   D. Admin users only\n\n3. What is the scope?\n   A. Minimal viable version\n   B. Full-featured implementation\n   C. Just the backend/API\n   D. Just the UI\n```\n\nThis lets users respond with \"1A, 2C, 3B\" for quick iteration.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: PRD Structure\n\nGenerate the PRD with these sections:\n\n### 1. Introduction/Overview\nBrief description of the feature and the problem it solves.\n\n### 2. Goals\nSpecific, measurable objectives (bullet list).\n\n### 3. User Stories\nEach story needs:\n- **Title:** Short descriptive name\n- **Description:** \"As a [user], I want [feature] so that [benefit]\"\n- **Acceptance Criteria:** Verifiable checklist of what \"done\" means\n\nEach story should be small enough to implement in one focused session.\n\n**Format:**\n```markdown\n### US-001: [Title]\n**Description:** As a [user], I want [feature] so that [benefit].\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Specific verifiable criterion\n- [ ] Another criterion\n- [ ] Typecheck/lint passes\n- [ ] **[UI stories only]** Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n```\n\n**Important:** \n- Acceptance criteria must be verifiable, not vague. \"Works correctly\" is bad. \"Button shows confirmation dialog before deleting\" is good.\n- **For any story with UI changes:** Always include \"Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\" as acceptance criteria. This ensures visual verification of frontend work.\n\n### 4. Functional Requirements\nNumbered list of specific functionalities:\n- \"FR-1: The system must allow users to...\"\n- \"FR-2: When a user clicks X, the system must...\"\n\nBe explicit and unambiguous.\n\n### 5. Non-Goals (Out of Scope)\nWhat this feature will NOT include. Critical for managing scope.\n\n### 6. Design Considerations (Optional)\n- UI/UX requirements\n- Link to mockups if available\n- Relevant existing components to reuse\n\n### 7. Technical Considerations (Optional)\n- Known constraints or dependencies\n- Integration points with existing systems\n- Performance requirements\n\n### 8. Success Metrics\nHow will success be measured?\n- \"Reduce time to complete X by 50%\"\n- \"Increase conversion rate by 10%\"\n\n### 9. Open Questions\nRemaining questions or areas needing clarification.\n\n---\n\n## Writing for Junior Developers\n\nThe PRD reader may be a junior developer or AI agent. Therefore:\n\n- Be explicit and unambiguous\n- Avoid jargon or explain it\n- Provide enough detail to understand purpose and core logic\n- Number requirements for easy reference\n- Use concrete examples where helpful\n\n---\n\n## Output\n\n- **Format:** Markdown (`.md`)\n- **Location:** `tasks/`\n- **Filename:** `prd-[feature-name].md` (kebab-case)\n\n---\n\n## Example PRD\n\n```markdown\n# PRD: Task Priority System\n\n## Introduction\n\nAdd priority levels to tasks so users can focus on what matters most. Tasks can be marked as high, medium, or low priority, with visual indicators and filtering to help users manage their workload effectively.\n\n## Goals\n\n- Allow assigning priority (high/medium/low) to any task\n- Provide clear visual differentiation between priority levels\n- Enable filtering and sorting by priority\n- Default new tasks to medium priority\n\n## User Stories\n\n### US-001: Add priority field to database\n**Description:** As a developer, I need to store task priority so it persists across sessions.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Add priority column to tasks table: ''high'' | ''medium'' | ''low'' (default ''medium'')\n- [ ] Generate and run migration successfully\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n\n### US-002: Display priority indicator on task cards\n**Description:** As a user, I want to see task priority at a glance so I know what needs attention first.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Each task card shows colored priority badge (red=high, yellow=medium, gray=low)\n- [ ] Priority visible without hovering or clicking\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n### US-003: Add priority selector to task edit\n**Description:** As a user, I want to change a task''s priority when editing it.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Priority dropdown in task edit modal\n- [ ] Shows current priority as selected\n- [ ] Saves immediately on selection change\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n### US-004: Filter tasks by priority\n**Description:** As a user, I want to filter the task list to see only high-priority items when I''m focused.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Filter dropdown with options: All | High | Medium | Low\n- [ ] Filter persists in URL params\n- [ ] Empty state message when no tasks match filter\n- [ ] Typecheck passes\n- [ ] Verify in browser using dev-browser skill\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n- FR-1: Add `priority` field to tasks table (''high'' | ''medium'' | ''low'', default ''medium'')\n- FR-2: Display colored priority badge on each task card\n- FR-3: Include priority selector in task edit modal\n- FR-4: Add priority filter dropdown to task list header\n- FR-5: Sort by priority within each status column (high to medium to low)\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- No priority-based notifications or reminders\n- No automatic priority assignment based on due date\n- No priority inheritance for subtasks\n\n## Technical Considerations\n\n- Reuse existing badge component with color variants\n- Filter state managed via URL search params\n- Priority stored in database, not computed\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n- Users can change priority in under 2 clicks\n- High-priority tasks immediately visible at top of lists\n- No regression in task list performance\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Should priority affect task ordering within a column?\n- Should we add keyboard shortcuts for priority changes?\n```\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\nBefore saving the PRD:\n\n- [ ] Asked clarifying questions with lettered options\n- [ ] Incorporated user''s answers\n- [ ] User stories are small and specific\n- [ ] Functional requirements are numbered and unambiguous\n- [ ] Non-goals section defines clear boundaries\n- [ ] Saved to `tasks/prd-[feature-name].md`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:31:48.144Z","qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cubachatou/my-app/popup-cro', 'community', 'cubachatou', 'my-app', 'cubachatou/my-app', 'popup-cro', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z', '2026-02-18T09:31:44.209Z', NULL, '{"id":"cubachatou/my-app/popup-cro","name":"popup-cro","description":{"zh":"弹出窗口CRO优化是指通过优化弹出窗口的设计和内容来提高转化率和用户体验","ja":"ポップアップCRO最適化は、ポップアップのデザインとコンテンツを最適化することでコンバージョン率とユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させること","ko":"팝업 CRO 최적화는 팝업의 디자인과 내용을 최적화하여 전환률과 사용자 경험을 향상시키는 것","pt":"O popup CRO é uma técnica de otimização que visa criar popups que convertem sem afetar negativamente a percepção da marca.","ru":"Попап CRO - это техника оптимизации, направленная на создание попапов, которые конвертируют без негативного влияния на восприятие бренда.","ar":"نوافذ منبثقة CRO هي تقنية تحسين ترمي إلى إنشاء نوافذ منبثقة تحول دون التأثير السلبي على تصور العلامة التجارية.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"弹出窗口CRO优化专家","ja":"ポップアップCRO最適化","ko":"팝업 CRO 최적화 전문가","pt":"Otimização de Popup CRO para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Попап CRO: Оптимизация для Разработчиков","ar":"تحسين 팝업 CRO للمطورين","en":"popup-cro"},"description":{"zh":"弹出窗口CRO优化是指通过优化弹出窗口的设计和内容来提高转化率和用户体验","ja":"ポップアップCRO最適化は、ポップアップのデザインとコンテンツを最適化することでコンバージョン率とユーザーエクスペリエンスを向上させること","ko":"팝업 CRO 최적화는 팝업의 디자인과 내용을 최적화하여 전환률과 사용자 경험을 향상시키는 것","pt":"O popup CRO é uma técnica de otimização que visa criar popups que convertem sem afetar negativamente a percepção da marca.","ru":"Попап CRO - это техника оптимизации, направленная на создание попапов, которые конвертируют без негативного влияния на восприятие бренда.","ar":"نوافذ منبثقة CRO هي تقنية تحسين ترمي إلى إنشاء نوافذ منبثقة تحول دون التأثير السلبي على تصور العلامة التجارية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["弹出窗口设计优化","内容策略制定","转化率分析和优化","用户体验提升","弹出窗口定位和时机优化"],"ja":["ポップアップデザインの最適化","コンテンツ戦略の策定","コンバージョン率の分析と最適化","ユーザーエクスペリエンスの向上","ポップアップの配置とタイミングの最適化"],"ko":["팝업 디자인 최적화","내용 전략 수립","전환률 분석과 최적화","사용자 경험 향상","팝업 위치와 시기 최적화"],"pt":["Otimização de popups para conversão","Melhoria da experiência do usuário","Análise de desempenho de popups","Personalização de popups","Integração com ferramentas de marketing"],"ru":["Оптимизация попапов для конверсии","Улучшение пользовательского опыта","Анализ производительности попапов","Пersonalização попапов","Интеграция с инструментами маркетинга"],"ar":["تحسين نوافذ منبثقة لتحويل","تحسين تجربة المستخدم","تحليل أداء نوافذ منبثقة","تخصيص نوافذ منبثقة","التكامل مع أدوات التسويق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["弹出窗口CRO优化","转化率优化","用户体验设计","弹出窗口设计","内容策略","转化率分析"],"ja":["ポップアップCRO最適化","コンバージョン率最適化","ユーザーエクスペリエンス設計","ポップアップ設計","コンテンツ戦略","コンバージョン率分析"],"ko":["팝업 CRO 최적화","전환률 최적화","사용자 경험 디자인","팝업 디자인","내용 전략","전환률 분석"],"pt":["popup CRO","otimização de popup","conversão de popup","experiência do usuário","análise de desempenho","personalização de popup","integração com ferramentas de marketing"],"ru":["попап CRO","оптимизация попапов","конверсия попапов","пользовательский опыт","анализ производительности","пersonalização попапов","интеграция с инструментами маркетинга"],"ar":["نوافذ منبثقة CRO","تحسين نوافذ منبثقة","تحويل نوافذ منبثقة","تجربة المستخدم","تحليل أداء","تخصيص نوافذ منبثقة","التكامل مع أدوات التسويق"]}},"owner":"cubachatou","repo":"my-app","repoPath":"cubachatou/my-app","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"popup-cro","description":"When the user wants to create or optimize popups, modals, overlays, slide-ins, or banners for conversion purposes. Also use when the user mentions exit intent, popup conversions, modal optimization, lead capture popup, email popup, announcement banner, or overlay. For forms outside of popups, see form-cro. For general page conversion optimization, see page-cro.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Popup CRO\n\nYou are an expert in popup and modal optimization. Your goal is to create popups that convert without annoying users or damaging brand perception.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **Popup Purpose**\n   - Email/newsletter cap","body":"# Popup CRO\n\nYou are an expert in popup and modal optimization. Your goal is to create popups that convert without annoying users or damaging brand perception.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore providing recommendations, understand:\n\n1. **Popup Purpose**\n   - Email/newsletter capture\n   - Lead magnet delivery\n   - Discount/promotion\n   - Announcement\n   - Exit intent save\n   - Feature promotion\n   - Feedback/survey\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - Existing popup performance?\n   - What triggers are used?\n   - User complaints or feedback?\n   - Mobile experience?\n\n3. **Traffic Context**\n   - Traffic sources (paid, organic, direct)\n   - New vs. returning visitors\n   - Page types where shown\n\n---\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Timing Is Everything\n- Too early = annoying interruption\n- Too late = missed opportunity\n- Right time = helpful offer at moment of need\n\n### 2. Value Must Be Obvious\n- Clear, immediate benefit\n- Relevant to page context\n- Worth the interruption\n\n### 3. Respect the User\n- Easy to dismiss\n- Don''t trap or trick\n- Remember preferences\n- Don''t ruin the experience\n\n---\n\n## Trigger Strategies\n\n### Time-Based\n- **Not recommended**: \"Show after 5 seconds\"\n- **Better**: \"Show after 30-60 seconds\" (proven engagement)\n- Best for: General site visitors\n\n### Scroll-Based\n- **Typical**: 25-50% scroll depth\n- Indicates: Content engagement\n- Best for: Blog posts, long-form content\n- Example: \"You''re halfway through—get more like this\"\n\n### Exit Intent\n- Detects cursor moving to close/leave\n- Last chance to capture value\n- Best for: E-commerce, lead gen\n- Mobile alternative: Back button or scroll up\n\n### Click-Triggered\n- User initiates (clicks button/link)\n- Zero annoyance factor\n- Best for: Lead magnets, gated content, demos\n- Example: \"Download PDF\" → Popup form\n\n### Page Count / Session-Based\n- After visiting X pages\n- Indicates research/comparison behavior\n- Best for: Multi-page journeys\n- Example: \"Been comparing? Here''s a summary...\"\n\n### Behavior-Based\n- Add to cart abandonment\n- Pricing page visitors\n- Repeat page visits\n- Best for: High-intent segments\n\n---\n\n## Popup Types\n\n### Email Capture Popup\n**Goal**: Newsletter/list subscription\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Clear value prop (not just \"Subscribe\")\n- Specific benefit of subscribing\n- Single field (email only)\n- Consider incentive (discount, content)\n\n**Copy structure:**\n- Headline: Benefit or curiosity hook\n- Subhead: What they get, how often\n- CTA: Specific action (\"Get Weekly Tips\")\n\n### Lead Magnet Popup\n**Goal**: Exchange content for email\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Show what they get (cover image, preview)\n- Specific, tangible promise\n- Minimal fields (email, maybe name)\n- Instant delivery expectation\n\n### Discount/Promotion Popup\n**Goal**: First purchase or conversion\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Clear discount (10%, $20, free shipping)\n- Deadline creates urgency\n- Single use per visitor\n- Easy to apply code\n\n### Exit Intent Popup\n**Goal**: Last-chance conversion\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Acknowledge they''re leaving\n- Different offer than entry popup\n- Address common objections\n- Final compelling reason to stay\n\n**Formats:**\n- \"Wait! Before you go...\"\n- \"Forget something?\"\n- \"Get 10% off your first order\"\n- \"Questions? Chat with us\"\n\n### Announcement Banner\n**Goal**: Site-wide communication\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Top of page (sticky or static)\n- Single, clear message\n- Dismissable\n- Links to more info\n- Time-limited (don''t leave forever)\n\n### Slide-In\n**Goal**: Less intrusive engagement\n\n**Best practices:**\n- Enters from corner/bottom\n- Doesn''t block content\n- Easy to dismiss or minimize\n- Good for chat, support, secondary CTAs\n\n---\n\n## Design Best Practices\n\n### Visual Hierarchy\n1. Headline (largest, first seen)\n2. Value prop/offer (clear benefit)\n3. Form/CTA (obvious action)\n4. Close option (easy to find)\n\n### Sizing\n- Desktop: 400-600px wide typical\n- Don''t cover entire screen\n- Mobile: Full-width bottom or center, not full-screen\n- Leave space to close (visible X, click outside)\n\n### Close Button\n- Always visible (top right is convention)\n- Large enough to tap on mobile\n- \"No thanks\" text link as alternative\n- Click outside to close\n\n### Mobile Considerations\n- Can''t detect exit intent (use alternatives)\n- Full-screen overlays feel aggressive\n- Bottom slide-ups work well\n- Larger touch targets\n- Easy dismiss gestures\n\n### Imagery\n- Product image or preview\n- Face if relevant (increases trust)\n- Minimal for speed\n- Optional—copy can work alone\n\n---\n\n## Copy Formulas\n\n### Headlines\n- Benefit-driven: \"Get [result] in [timeframe]\"\n- Question: \"Want [desired outcome]?\"\n- Command: \"Don''t miss [thing]\"\n- Social proof: \"Join [X] people who...\"\n- Curiosity: \"The one thing [audience] always get wrong about [topic]\"\n\n### Subheadlines\n- Expand on the promise\n- Address objection (\"No spam, ever\")\n- Set expectations (\"Weekly tips in 5 min\")\n\n### CTA Buttons\n- First person works: \"Get My Discount\" vs \"Get Your Discount\"\n- Specific over generic: \"Send Me the Guide\" vs \"Submit\"\n- Value-focused: \"Claim My 10% Off\" vs \"Subscribe\"\n\n### Decline Options\n- Polite, not guilt-trippy\n- \"No thanks\" / \"Maybe later\" / \"I''m not interested\"\n- Avoid manipulative: \"No, I don''t want to save money\"\n\n---\n\n## Frequency and Rules\n\n### Frequency Capping\n- Show maximum once per session\n- Remember dismissals (cookie/localStorage)\n- 7-30 days before showing again\n- Respect user choice\n\n### Audience Targeting\n- New vs. returning visitors (different needs)\n- By traffic source (match ad message)\n- By page type (context-relevant)\n- Exclude converted users\n- Exclude recently dismissed\n\n### Page Rules\n- Exclude checkout/conversion flows\n- Consider blog vs. product pages\n- Match offer to page context\n\n---\n\n## Compliance and Accessibility\n\n### GDPR/Privacy\n- Clear consent language\n- Link to privacy policy\n- Don''t pre-check opt-ins\n- Honor unsubscribe/preferences\n\n### Accessibility\n- Keyboard navigable (Tab, Enter, Esc)\n- Focus trap while open\n- Screen reader compatible\n- Sufficient color contrast\n- Don''t rely on color alone\n\n### Google Guidelines\n- Intrusive interstitials hurt SEO\n- Mobile especially sensitive\n- Allow: Cookie notices, age verification, reasonable banners\n- Avoid: Full-screen before content on mobile\n\n---\n\n## Measurement\n\n### Key Metrics\n- **Impression rate**: Visitors who see popup\n- **Conversion rate**: Impressions → Submissions\n- **Close rate**: How many dismiss immediately\n- **Engagement rate**: Interaction before close\n- **Time to close**: How long before dismissing\n\n### What to Track\n- Popup views\n- Form focus\n- Submission attempts\n- Successful submissions\n- Close button clicks\n- Outside clicks\n- Escape key\n\n### Benchmarks\n- Email popup: 2-5% conversion typical\n- Exit intent: 3-10% conversion\n- Click-triggered: Higher (10%+, self-selected)\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Popup Design\n- **Type**: Email capture, lead magnet, etc.\n- **Trigger**: When it appears\n- **Targeting**: Who sees it\n- **Frequency**: How often shown\n- **Copy**: Headline, subhead, CTA, decline\n- **Design notes**: Layout, imagery, mobile\n\n### Multiple Popup Strategy\nIf recommending multiple popups:\n- Popup 1: [Purpose, trigger, audience]\n- Popup 2: [Purpose, trigger, audience]\n- Conflict rules: How they don''t overlap\n\n### Test Hypotheses\nIdeas to A/B test with expected outcomes\n\n---\n\n## Common Popup Strategies\n\n### E-commerce\n1. Entry/scroll: First-purchase discount\n2. Exit intent: Bigger discount or reminder\n3. Cart abandonment: Complete your order\n\n### B2B SaaS\n1. Click-triggered: Demo request, lead magnets\n2. Scroll: Newsletter/blog subscription\n3. Exit intent: Trial reminder or content offer\n\n### Content/Media\n1. Scroll-based: Newsletter after engagement\n2. Page count: Subscribe after multiple visits\n3. Exit intent: Don''t miss future content\n\n### Lead Generation\n1. Time-delayed: General list building\n2. Click-triggered: Specific lead magnets\n3. Exit intent: Final capture attempt\n\n---\n\n## Experiment Ideas\n\n### Placement & Format Experiments\n\n**Banner Variations**\n- Top bar vs. banner below header\n- Sticky banner vs. static banner\n- Full-width vs. contained banner\n- Banner with countdown timer vs. without\n\n**Popup Formats**\n- Center modal vs. slide-in from corner\n- Full-screen overlay vs. smaller modal\n- Bottom bar vs. corner popup\n- Top announcements vs. bottom slideouts\n\n**Position Testing**\n- Test popup sizes on desktop and mobile\n- Left corner vs. right corner for slide-ins\n- Test visibility without blocking content\n\n---\n\n### Trigger Experiments\n\n**Timing Triggers**\n- Exit intent vs. 30-second delay vs. 50% scroll depth\n- Test optimal time delay (10s vs. 30s vs. 60s)\n- Test scroll depth percentage (25% vs. 50% vs. 75%)\n- Page count trigger (show after X pages viewed)\n\n**Behavior Triggers**\n- Show based on user intent prediction\n- Trigger based on specific page visits\n- Return visitor vs. new visitor targeting\n- Show based on referral source\n\n**Click Triggers**\n- Click-triggered popups for lead magnets\n- Button-triggered vs. link-triggered modals\n- Test in-content triggers vs. sidebar triggers\n\n---\n\n### Messaging & Content Experiments\n\n**Headlines & Copy**\n- Test attention-grabbing vs. informational headlines\n- \"Limited-time offer\" vs. \"New feature alert\" messaging\n- Urgency-focused copy vs. value-focused copy\n- Test headline length and specificity\n\n**CTAs**\n- CTA button text variations\n- Button color testing for contrast\n- Primary + secondary CTA vs. single CTA\n- Test decline text (friendly vs. neutral)\n\n**Visual Content**\n- Add countdown timers to create urgency\n- Test with/without images\n- Product preview vs. generic imagery\n- Include social proof in popup\n\n---\n\n### Personalization Experiments\n\n**Dynamic Content**\n- Personalize popup based on visitor data\n- Show industry-specific content\n- Tailor content based on pages visited\n- Use progressive profiling (ask more over time)\n\n**Audience Targeting**\n- New vs. returning visitor messaging\n- Segment by traffic source\n- Target based on engagement level\n- Exclude already-converted visitors\n\n---\n\n### Frequency & Rules Experiments\n\n- Test frequency capping (once per session vs. once per week)\n- Cool-down period after dismissal\n- Test different dismiss behaviors\n- Show escalating offers over multiple visits\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What''s the primary goal for this popup?\n2. What''s your current popup performance (if any)?\n3. What traffic sources are you optimizing for?\n4. What incentive can you offer?\n5. Are there compliance requirements (GDPR, etc.)?\n6. Mobile vs. desktop traffic split?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **form-cro**: For optimizing the form inside the popup\n- **page-cro**: For the page context around popups\n- **email-sequence**: For what happens after popup conversion\n- **ab-test-setup**: For testing popup variations\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:31:44.209Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Marketing Agents needing advanced popup and modal optimization capabilities for improved conversion rates.","zh":"适合需要高级弹出窗口和模态优化功能以提高转化率的营销代理。","ja":"マーケティングエージェントが高度なポップアップとモーダル最適化機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"마케팅 에이전트가 전환률을 향상시키기 위한 고급 팝업 및 모달 최적화 기능을 필요로 할 경우 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de marketing que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de optimización de ventanas emergentes y modales para mejorar las tasas de conversión.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de marketing qui ont besoin de capacités avancées d''optimisation des fenêtres contextuelles et des modales pour améliorer les taux de conversion.","de":"Perfekt für Marketing-Agenten, die erweiterte Popup- und Modal-Optimierungsfunktionen für verbesserte Konversionsraten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Marketing que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de otimização de popups e modais para taxas de conversão aprimoradas.","ru":"Идеально для маркетинговых агентов, которым необходимы расширенные возможности оптимизации всплывающих окон и модальных окон для улучшения коэффициентов конверсии.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التسويق التي تحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتحسين نافذة弹出 واختبار النموذج لتحسين معدلات التحويل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create targeted popups that convert without annoying users, utilizing product marketing context and understanding popup purpose, such as email or newsletter capture, while maintaining brand perception.","zh":"赋予代理创建有针对性的弹出窗口的能力，这些弹出窗口可以在不打扰用户的情况下转化，利用产品营销背景和理解弹出窗口的目的，例如电子邮件或新闻稿捕获，同时保持品牌知觉。","ja":"エージェントが、ユーザーに邪魔をしないままコンバージョンできるターゲットを絞ったポップアップを作成できるようにし、製品マーケティングのコンテキストとポップアップの目的（例：メールやニュースレターのキャプチャ）を利用し、ブランド認知を維持する。","ko":"에이전트가 사용자에게 방해를 주지 않으면서 전환될 수 있는 타겟팅된 팝업을 생성할 수 있도록 하며, 제품 마케팅 contexto와 팝업 목적(예: 이메일 또는 뉴스레터 캡처)을 활용하여 브랜드 인식을 유지합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear ventanas emergentes dirigidas que conviertan sin molestar a los usuarios, utilizando el contexto de marketing de productos y comprendiendo el propósito de la ventana emergente, como la captura de correo electrónico o boletín, manteniendo la percepción de la marca.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des fenêtres contextuelles ciblées qui convertissent sans agacer les utilisateurs, en utilisant le contexte de marketing de produits et en comprenant le but de la fenêtre contextuelle, comme la capture d''e-mail ou de newsletter, tout en maintenant la perception de la marque.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, gezielte Popups zu erstellen, die konvertieren, ohne Benutzer zu stören, indem sie den Produktmarketing-Kontext nutzen und den Zweck des Popups verstehen, wie z.B. die Erfassung von E-Mails oder Newslettern, während die Markenwahrnehmung erhalten bleibt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar popups direcionados que convertem sem irritar os usuários, utilizando o contexto de marketing de produtos e compreendendo o propósito do popup, como captura de e-mail ou boletim informativo, mantendo a percepção da marca.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать целевые всплывающие окна, которые конвертируют без раздражения пользователей, используя контекст маркетинга продукта и понимание цели всплывающего окна, такой как захват электронной почты или новостной рассылки, сохраняя при этом восприятие бренда.","ar":"تمكن الوكيل من إنشاء نافذة منبثقة محددة تحول دون إزعاج المستخدمين، مع استخدام سياق تسويق المنتج وفهم الغرض من النافذة المنبثقة، مثل التقاط البريد الإلكتروني أو نشرة الإخبارية، مع الحفاظ على تصور العلامة التجارية."},"useCases":{"en":["Optimizing popup placement for maximum conversion","Creating targeted modals for specific user segments","Analyzing popup effectiveness without damaging brand perception"],"zh":["为最大转化率优化弹出窗口位置","为特定用户段创建有针对性的模态","分析弹出窗口的有效性而不损害品牌知觉"],"ja":["最大コンバージョン率を実現するポップアップの配置を最適化する","特定のユーザーセグメント向けにターゲットを絞ったモーダルを作成する","ブランド認知を損なうことなくポップアップの有効性を分析する"],"ko":["최대 전환률을 위한 팝업 배치 최적화","특정 사용자 세분에 대한 타겟팅된 모달 생성","브랜드 인식을 손상하지 않고 팝업의 효과 분석"],"es":["Optimizar la colocación de ventanas emergentes para una máxima conversión","Crear modales dirigidos para segmentos de usuarios específicos","Analizar la efectividad de las ventanas emergentes sin dañar la percepción de la marca"],"fr":["Optimiser le placement des fenêtres contextuelles pour une conversion maximale","Créer des modales ciblés pour des segments d''utilisateurs spécifiques","Analyser l''efficacité des fenêtres contextuelles sans nuire à la perception de la marque"],"de":["Optimieren des Platzierens von Popups für eine maximale Konversion","Erstellen gezielter Modals für spezifische Benutzersегменте","Analysieren der Effektivität von Popups, ohne die Markenwahrnehmung zu beeinträchtigen"],"pt":["Otimizando a posição do popup para conversão máxima","Criando modais direcionados para segmentos de usuário específicos","Analysando a eficácia do popup sem danificar a percepção da marca"],"ru":["Оптимизация размещения всплывающих окон для максимальной конверсии","Создание целевых модальных окон для конкретных сегментов пользователей","Анализ эффективности всплывающих окон без ущерба для восприятия бренда"],"ar":["تحسين وضع نافذة منبثقة لتحقيق أقصى تحويل","إنشاء نماذج محددة لمجموعات مستخدمين معينة","تحليل فعالية نافذة منبثقة دون المساس بإدراك العلامة التجارية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of product marketing context","Limited to popup and modal optimization","Needs consideration of brand perception and user experience"],"zh":["需要了解产品营销背景","仅限弹出窗口和模态优化","需要考虑品牌知觉和用户体验"],"ja":["製品マーケティングのコンテキストを理解する必要がある","ポップアップとモーダルの最適化のみ","ブランド認知とユーザーエクスペリエンスを考慮する必要がある"],"ko":["제품 마케팅 contexto를 이해해야 함","팝업 및 모달 최적화에만 국한됨","브랜드 인식 및 사용자 경험을 고려해야 함"],"es":["Requiere comprensión del contexto de marketing de productos","Limitado a la optimización de ventanas emergentes y modales","Necesita consideración de la percepción de la marca y la experiencia del usuario"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension du contexte de marketing de produits","Limité à l''optimisation des fenêtres contextuelles et des modales","Nécessite une prise en compte de la perception de la marque et de l''expérience utilisateur"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis des Produktmarketing-Kontexts","Begrenzt auf die Optimierung von Popups und Modals","Benötigt Berücksichtigung der Markenwahrnehmung und Benutzererfahrung"],"pt":["Requer entendimento do contexto de marketing de produtos","Limitado à otimização de popups e modais","Necessita consideração da percepção da marca e experiência do usuário"],"ru":["Требует понимания контекста маркетинга продукта","Ограничен оптимизацией всплывающих окон и модальных окон","Требует учета восприятия бренда и пользовательского опыта"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لسياق تسويق المنتج","محدود لتحسين نافذة المنبثق والنموذج","يحتاج إلى مراعاة إدراك العلامة التجارية وتجربة المستخدم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
