s applications SaaS","Création d''interfaces cohérentes et efficaces","Utilisation de modèles et de principes de conception","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur","Compatibilité avec différents appareils et plateformes"],"de":["Erstellung von Benutzeroberflächen für Dashboards und SaaS-Anwendungen","Erstellung konsistenter und effektiver Benutzeroberflächen","Verwendung von Mustern und Designprinzipien","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung","Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen Geräten und Plattformen"],"pt":["Criação de dashboards personalizados","Desenvolvimento de painéis de administração","Design de interfaces para aplicativos SaaS","Otimização da experiência do usuário","Integração com tecnologias de desenvolvimento web"],"ru":["Создание персонализированных дашбордов","Разработка панелей администрирования","Проектирование интерфейсов для приложений SaaS","Оптимизация пользовательского опыта","Интеграция с веб-технологиями"],"ar":["إنشاء لوحات قيادة مخصصة","تصميم ألواح التحكم والإدارة","تصميم واجهات لتطبيقات SaaS","تحسين تجربة المستخدم","التكامل مع تقنيات تطوير الويب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["界面设计","AI Setup MarkDown","仪表盘设计","管理面板设计","SaaS应用设计","界面构建","一致性设计","精心设计"],"ja":["インターフェースデザイン","AI Setup MarkDown","ダッシュボードデザイン","管理パネルデザイン","SaaSアプリケーションデザイン","インターフェース構築","一貫性デザイン","精度の高いデザイン"],"ko":["인터페이스 디자인","AI Setup MarkDown","대시보드 디자인","관리 패널 디자인","SaaS 애플리케이션 디자인","인터페이스 구축","일관성 디자인","정교한 디자인"],"es":["diseño de interfaz","interfaz de usuario","dashboards","aplicaciones SaaS","experiencia del usuario","patrones de diseño","principios de diseño","compatibilidad","dispositivos","plataformas"],"fr":["conception d''interface","interface utilisateur","tableaux de bord","applications SaaS","expérience utilisateur","modèles de conception","principes de conception","compatibilité","appareils","plateformes"],"de":["Benutzeroberflächendesign","Benutzeroberfläche","Dashboards","SaaS-Anwendungen","Benutzererfahrung","Designmuster","Designprinzipien","Kompatibilität","Geräte","Plattformen"],"pt":["design de interface","dashboards personalizados","painéis de administração","aplicativos SaaS","experiência do usuário","desenvolvimento web","interface de usuário"],"ru":["разработка интерфейса","персонализированные дашборды","панели администрирования","приложения SaaS","пользовательский опыт","веб-разработка","интерфейс пользователя"],"ar":["تصميم الواجهة","لوحات قيادة مخصصة","ألواح التحكم والإدارة","تطبيقات SaaS","تجربة المستخدم","تطوير الويب","واجهة المستخدم"]}},"owner":"raudyagdel","repo":"ai_setup_and_tips","repoPath":"raudyagdel/ai_setup_and_tips","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"interface-design","description":"This skill is for interface design — dashboards, admin panels, apps, tools, and interactive products. NOT for marketing design (landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns).","bodyPreview":"# Interface Design\n\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\n\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\n\n---\n\n# The Problem\n\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\n\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state your intent — and","body":"# Interface Design\n\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\n\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\n\n---\n\n# The Problem\n\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\n\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state your intent — and still produce a template. Warm colors on cold structures. Friendly fonts on generic layouts. \"Kitchen feel\" that looks like every other app.\n\nThis happens because intent lives in prose, but code generation pulls from patterns. The gap between them is where defaults win.\n\nThe process below helps. But process alone doesn''t guarantee craft. You have to catch yourself.\n\n---\n\n# Where Defaults Hide\n\nDefaults don''t announce themselves. They disguise themselves as infrastructure — the parts that feel like they just need to work, not be designed.\n\n**Typography feels like a container.** Pick something readable, move on. But typography isn''t holding your design — it IS your design. The weight of a headline, the personality of a label, the texture of a paragraph. These shape how the product feels before anyone reads a word. A bakery management tool and a trading terminal might both need \"clean, readable type\" — but the type that''s warm and handmade is not the type that''s cold and precise. If you''re reaching for your usual font, you''re not designing.\n\n**Navigation feels like scaffolding.** Build the sidebar, add the links, get to the real work. But navigation isn''t around your product — it IS your product. Where you are, where you can go, what matters most. A page floating in space is a component demo, not software. The navigation teaches people how to think about the space they''re in.\n\n**Data feels like presentation.** You have numbers, show numbers. But a number on screen is not design. The question is: what does this number mean to the person looking at it? What will they do with it? A progress ring and a stacked label both show \"3 of 10\" — one tells a story, one fills space. If you''re reaching for number-on-label, you''re not designing.\n\n**Token names feel like implementation detail.** But your CSS variables are design decisions. `--ink` and `--parchment` evoke a world. `--gray-700` and `--surface-2` evoke a template. Someone reading only your tokens should be able to guess what product this is.\n\nThe trap is thinking some decisions are creative and others are structural. There are no structural decisions. Everything is design. The moment you stop asking \"why this?\" is the moment defaults take over.\n\n---\n\n# Intent First\n\nBefore touching code, answer these. Not in your head — out loud, to yourself or the user.\n\n**Who is this human?**\nNot \"users.\" The actual person. Where are they when they open this? What''s on their mind? What did they do 5 minutes ago, what will they do 5 minutes after? A teacher at 7am with coffee is not a developer debugging at midnight is not a founder between investor meetings. Their world shapes the interface.\n\n**What must they accomplish?**\nNot \"use the dashboard.\" The verb. Grade these submissions. Find the broken deployment. Approve the payment. The answer determines what leads, what follows, what hides.\n\n**What should this feel like?**\nSay it in words that mean something. \"Clean and modern\" means nothing — every AI says that. Warm like a notebook? Cold like a terminal? Dense like a trading floor? Calm like a reading app? The answer shapes color, type, spacing, density — everything.\n\nIf you cannot answer these with specifics, stop. Ask the user. Do not guess. Do not default.\n\n## Every Choice Must Be A Choice\n\nFor every decision, you must be able to explain WHY.\n\n- Why this layout and not another?\n- Why this color temperature?\n- Why this typeface?\n- Why this spacing scale?\n- Why this information hierarchy?\n\nIf your answer is \"it''s common\" or \"it''s clean\" or \"it works\" — you haven''t chosen. You''ve defaulted. Defaults are invisible. Invisible choices compound into generic output.\n\n**The test:** If you swapped your choices for the most common alternatives and the design didn''t feel meaningfully different, you never made real choices.\n\n## Sameness Is Failure\n\nIf another AI, given a similar prompt, would produce substantially the same output — you have failed.\n\nThis is not about being different for its own sake. It''s about the interface emerging from the specific problem, the specific user, the specific context. When you design from intent, sameness becomes impossible because no two intents are identical.\n\nWhen you design from defaults, everything looks the same because defaults are shared.\n\n## Intent Must Be Systemic\n\nSaying \"warm\" and using cold colors is not following through. Intent is not a label — it''s a constraint that shapes every decision.\n\nIf the intent is warm: surfaces, text, borders, accents, semantic colors, typography — all warm. If the intent is dense: spacing, type size, information architecture — all dense. If the intent is calm: motion, contrast, color saturation — all calm.\n\nCheck your output against your stated intent. Does every token reinforce it? Or did you state an intent and then default anyway?\n\n---\n\n# Product Domain Exploration\n\nThis is where defaults get caught — or don''t.\n\nGeneric output: Task type → Visual template → Theme\nCrafted output: Task type → Product domain → Signature → Structure + Expression\n\nThe difference: time in the product''s world before any visual or structural thinking.\n\n## Required Outputs\n\n**Do not propose any direction until you produce all four:**\n\n**Domain:** Concepts, metaphors, vocabulary from this product''s world. Not features — territory. Minimum 5.\n\n**Color world:** What colors exist naturally in this product''s domain? Not \"warm\" or \"cool\" — go to the actual world. If this product were a physical space, what would you see? What colors belong there that don''t belong elsewhere? List 5+.\n\n**Signature:** One element — visual, structural, or interaction — that could only exist for THIS product. If you can''t name one, keep exploring.\n\n**Defaults:** 3 obvious choices for this interface type — visual AND structural. You can''t avoid patterns you haven''t named.\n\n## Proposal Requirements\n\nYour direction must explicitly reference:\n- Domain concepts you explored\n- Colors from your color world exploration\n- Your signature element\n- What replaces each default\n\n**The test:** Read your proposal. Remove the product name. Could someone identify what this is for? If not, it''s generic. Explore deeper.\n\n---\n\n# The Mandate\n\n**Before showing the user, look at what you made.**\n\nAsk yourself: \"If they said this lacks craft, what would they mean?\"\n\nThat thing you just thought of — fix it first.\n\nYour first output is probably generic. That''s normal. The work is catching it before the user has to.\n\n## The Checks\n\nRun these against your output before presenting:\n\n- **The swap test:** If you swapped the typeface for your usual one, would anyone notice? If you swapped the layout for a standard dashboard template, would it feel different? The places where swapping wouldn''t matter are the places you defaulted.\n\n- **The squint test:** Blur your eyes. Can you still perceive hierarchy? Is anything jumping out harshly? Craft whispers.\n\n- **The signature test:** Can you point to five specific elements where your signature appears? Not \"the overall feel\" — actual components. A signature you can''t locate doesn''t exist.\n\n- **The token test:** Read your CSS variables out loud. Do they sound like they belong to this product''s world, or could they belong to any project?\n\nIf any check fails, iterate before showing.\n\n---\n\n# Craft Foundations\n\n## Subtle Layering\n\nThis is the backbone of craft. Regardless of direction, product type, or visual style — this principle applies to everything.\n\n**Surfaces must be barely different but still distinguishable.** Study Vercel, Supabase, Linear. Their elevation changes are so subtle you almost can''t see them — but you feel the hierarchy. Not dramatic jumps. Not obviously different colors. Whisper-quiet shifts.\n\n**Borders must be light but not invisible.** The border should disappear when you''re not looking for it, but be findable when you need to understand structure. If borders are the first thing you notice, they''re too strong. If you can''t tell where regions begin and end, they''re too weak.\n\n**The squint test:** Blur your eyes at the interface. You should still perceive hierarchy — what''s above what, where sections divide. But nothing should jump out. No harsh lines. No jarring color shifts. Just quiet structure.\n\nThis separates professional interfaces from amateur ones. Get this wrong and nothing else matters.\n\n## Infinite Expression\n\nEvery pattern has infinite expressions. **No interface should look the same.**\n\nA metric display could be a hero number, inline stat, sparkline, gauge, progress bar, comparison delta, trend badge, or something new. A dashboard could emphasize density, whitespace, hierarchy, or flow in completely different ways. Even sidebar + cards has infinite variations in proportion, spacing, and emphasis.\n\n**Before building, ask:**\n- What''s the ONE thing users do most here?\n- What products solve similar problems brilliantly? Study them.\n- Why would this interface feel designed for its purpose, not templated?\n\n**NEVER produce identical output.** Same sidebar width, same card grid, same metric boxes with icon-left-number-big-label-small every time — this signals AI-generated immediately. It''s forgettable.\n\nThe architecture and components should emerge from the task and data, executed in a way that feels fresh. Linear''s cards don''t look like Notion''s. Vercel''s metrics don''t look like Stripe''s. Same concepts, infinite expressions.\n\n## Color Lives Somewhere\n\nEvery product exists in a world. That world has colors.\n\nBefore you reach for a palette, spend time in the product''s world. What would you see if you walked into the physical version of this space? What materials? What light? What objects?\n\nYour palette should feel like it came FROM somewhere — not like it was applied TO something.\n\n**Beyond Warm and Cold:** Temperature is one axis. Is this quiet or loud? Dense or spacious? Serious or playful? Geometric or organic? A trading terminal and a meditation app are both \"focused\" — completely different kinds of focus. Find the specific quality, not the generic label.\n\n**Color Carries Meaning:** Gray builds structure. Color communicates — status, action, emphasis, identity. Unmotivated color is noise. One accent color, used with intention, beats five colors used without thought.\n\n---\n\n# Design Principles\n\n## Spacing\nPick a base unit and stick to multiples. Consistency matters more than the specific number. Random values signal no system.\n\n## Padding\nKeep it symmetrical. If one side is 16px, others should match unless there''s a clear reason.\n\n## Depth\nChoose ONE approach and commit:\n- **Borders-only** — Clean, technical. For dense tools.\n- **Subtle shadows** — Soft lift. For approachable products.\n- **Layered shadows** — Premium, dimensional. For cards that need presence.\n\nDon''t mix approaches.\n\n## Border Radius\nSharper feels technical. Rounder feels friendly. Pick a scale and apply consistently.\n\n## Typography\nHeadlines need weight and tight tracking. Body needs readability. Data needs monospace. Build a hierarchy.\n\n## Color & Surfaces\nBuild from primitives: foreground (text hierarchy), background (surface elevation), border (separation hierarchy), brand, and semantic (destructive, warning, success). Every color should trace back to these. No random hex values — everything maps to the system.\n\n## Animation\nFast micro-interactions (~150ms), smooth easing. No bouncy/spring effects.\n\n## States\nEvery interactive element needs states: default, hover, active, focus, disabled. Data needs states too: loading, empty, error. Missing states feel broken.\n\n## Controls\nNative `<select>` and `<input type=\"date\">` can''t be styled. Build custom components.\n\n---\n\n# Avoid\n\n- **Harsh borders** — if borders are the first thing you see, they''re too strong\n- **Dramatic surface jumps** — elevation changes should be whisper-quiet\n- **Inconsistent spacing** — the clearest sign of no system\n- **Mixed depth strategies** — pick one approach and commit\n- **Missing interaction states** — hover, focus, disabled, loading, error\n- **Dramatic drop shadows** — shadows should be subtle, not attention-grabbing\n- **Large radius on small elements**\n- **Pure white cards on colored backgrounds**\n- **Thick decorative borders**\n- **Gradients and color for decoration** — color should mean something\n- **Multiple accent colors** — dilutes focus\n\n---\n\n# Workflow\n\n## Communication\nBe invisible. Don''t announce modes or narrate process.\n\n**Never say:** \"I''m in ESTABLISH MODE\", \"Let me check system.md...\"\n\n**Instead:** Jump into work. State suggestions with reasoning.\n\n## Suggest + Ask\nLead with your exploration and recommendation, then confirm:\n```\n\"Domain: [5+ concepts from the product''s world]\nColor world: [5+ colors that exist in this domain]\nSignature: [one element unique to this product]\nRejecting: [default 1] → [alternative], [default 2] → [alternative], [default 3] → [alternative]\n\nDirection: [approach that connects to the above]\"\n\n[AskUserQuestion: \"Does that direction feel right?\"]\n```\n\n## If Project Has system.md\nRead `.interface-design/system.md` and apply. Decisions are made.\n\n## If No system.md\n1. Explore domain — Produce all four required outputs\n2. Propose — Direction must reference all four\n3. Confirm — Get user buy-in\n4. Build — Apply principles\n5. **Evaluate** — Run the mandate checks before showing\n6. Offer to save\n\n---\n\n# After Completing a Task\n\nWhen you finish building something, **always offer to save**:\n\n```\n\"Want me to save these patterns for future sessions?\"\n```\n\nIf yes, write to `.interface-design/system.md`:\n- Direction and feel\n- Depth strategy (borders/shadows/layered)\n- Spacing base unit\n- Key component patterns\n\nThis compounds — each save makes future work faster and more consistent.\n\n---\n\n# Deep Dives\n\nFor more detail on specific topics:\n- `references/principles.md` — Code examples, specific values, dark mode\n- `references/validation.md` — Memory management, when to update system.md\n\n# Commands\n\n- `/interface-design:status` — Current system state\n- `/interface-design:audit` — Check code against system\n- `/interface-design:extract` — Extract patterns from code\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:32:52.736Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing advanced interface design capabilities for dashboards and admin panels","zh":"非常适合需要高级界面设计功能的AI代理，用于仪表盘和管理面板","ja":"ダッシュボードと管理パネル向けの高級インターフェース設計機能を必要とするAIエージェントに最適","ko":"대시보드 및 관리자 패널용 고급 인터페이스 디자인 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan capacidades de diseño de interfaz avanzadas para paneles de control y paneles de administración","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA nécessitant des capacités de conception d''interface avancées pour les tableaux de bord et les panneaux d''administration","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die erweiterte Schnittstellen-Designfunktionen für Dashboards und Administrationspanels benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de design de interface para dashboards e painéis de administração","ru":"Идеально для ИИ-агентов, которым требуются продвинутые возможности дизайна интерфейса для панелей управления и административных панелей","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات تصميم واجهة متقدمة للوحات التحكم واللوحات الإدارية"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft consistent interfaces using Markdown for AI setup, supporting Copilot, Claude, Codex, and Gemini, with capabilities for generating generic output and exploring domain-specific patterns, leveraging protocols and file formats like Markdown","zh":"赋予代理创建使用Markdown进行AI设置的统一接口的能力，支持Copilot、Claude、Codex和Gemini，并具有生成通用输出和探索特定领域模式的能力，利用Markdown等协议和文件格式","ja":"エージェントがCopilot、Claude、Codex、Geminiをサポートするマークダウンを使用したAI設定のための統一されたインターフェースを作成する能力を与え、汎用的な出力を生成し、特定のドメインのパターンを探索する能力を持ち、Markdownなどのプロトコルやファイル形式を利用","ko":"에이전트가 마크다운을 사용하여 AI 설정의 일관된 인터페이스를 생성하는 능력을 부여하며, Copilot, Claude, Codex 및 Gemini를 지원하고, 일반적인 출력을 생성하고 특정 도메인의 패턴을 탐색하는 능력을 가지고 있으며, Markdown와 같은 프로토콜 및 파일 형식을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear interfaces coherentes utilizando Markdown para la configuración de IA, compatible con Copilot, Claude, Codex y Gemini, con capacidades para generar salida genérica y explorar patrones específicos de dominio, aprovechando protocolos y formatos de archivo como Markdown","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des interfaces cohérentes en utilisant Markdown pour la configuration de l''IA, compatible avec Copilot, Claude, Codex et Gemini, avec des capacités pour générer une sortie générique et explorer des modèles spécifiques de domaine, en exploitant des protocoles et des formats de fichiers comme Markdown","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, konsistente Schnittstellen mit Markdown für die KI-Konfiguration zu erstellen, kompatibel mit Copilot, Claude, Codex und Gemini, mit Fähigkeiten zur Generierung generischer Ausgaben und zur Erkundung domänen-spezifischer Muster, unter Ausnutzung von Protokollen und Dateiformaten wie Markdown","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar interfaces consistentes usando Markdown para configuração de IA, suportando Copilot, Claude, Codex e Gemini, com capacidades para gerar saída genérica e explorar padrões específicos de domínio, aproveitando protocolos e formatos de arquivo como Markdown","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать последовательные интерфейсы с помощью Markdown для настройки ИИ, поддерживая Copilot, Claude, Codex и Gemini, с возможностями генерации общего вывода и изучения домен-специфичных шаблонов, используя протоколы и форматы файлов, такие как Markdown","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء واجهات متسقة باستخدام Markdown لإعداد الذكاء الاصطناعي، ودعم Copilot و Claude و Codex و Gemini، مع القدرة على生成 مخرجات عامة واستكشاف أنماط محددة للنطاق، والاستفادة من البروتوكولات وتنسيقات الملفات مثل Markdown"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing dashboards for SaaS apps","Creating admin panels with consistent layouts","Building data interfaces for tools and settings pages"],"zh":["为SaaS应用程序设计仪表盘","使用一致的布局创建管理面板","为工具和设置页面构建数据接口"],"ja":["SaaSアプリケーションのダッシュボードを設計","一貫したレイアウトを使用して管理パネルを作成","ツールと設定ページのためのデータインターフェースを構築"],"ko":["SaaS 애플리케이션의 대시보드를 설계","일관된 레이아웃을 사용하여 관리 패널을 생성","도구 및 설정 페이지를 위한 데이터 인터페이스를 구축"],"es":["Diseñar paneles de control para aplicaciones SaaS","Crear paneles de administración con diseños coherentes","Crear interfaces de datos para herramientas y páginas de configuración"],"fr":["Concevoir des tableaux de bord pour les applications SaaS","Créer des panneaux d''administration avec des dispositions cohérentes","Créer des interfaces de données pour les outils et les pages de paramètres"],"de":["Dashboards für SaaS-Anwendungen entwerfen","Administrationspanels mit konsistenten Layouts erstellen","Daten-Schnittstellen für Tools und Einstellungsseiten erstellen"],"pt":["Projetar dashboards para aplicativos SaaS","Criar painéis de administração com layouts consistentes","Construir interfaces de dados para ferramentas e páginas de configurações"],"ru":["Проектирование панелей управления для приложений SaaS","Создание административных панелей с последовательными макетами","Построение интерфейсов данных для инструментов и страниц настроек"],"ar":["تصميم لوحات تحكم لتطبيقات SaaS","إنشاء لوحات إدارية ذات تخطيطات متسقة","بناء واجهات بيانات لأدوات وصفحات الإعدادات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not suitable for landing pages or marketing sites","Redirects campaigns to /frontend-design"],"zh":["不适合用于登陆页面或营销网站","将活动重定向到/frontend-design"],"ja":["ランディングページやマーケティングサイトには不適","/frontend-designへのキャンペーンのリダイレクト"],"ko":["랜딩 페이지 또는 마케팅 사이트에는 적합하지 않음","/frontend-design로의 캠페인 리디렉션"],"es":["No es adecuado para páginas de destino o sitios de marketing","Redirige campañas a /frontend-design"],"fr":["N''est pas adapté pour les pages de destination ou les sites de marketing","Redirige les campagnes vers /frontend-design"],"de":["Nicht geeignet für Zielseiten oder Marketing-Websites","Leitet Kampagnen zu /frontend-design weiter"],"pt":["Não é adequado para páginas de destino ou sites de marketing","Redireciona campanhas para /frontend-design"],"ru":["Не подходит для целевых страниц или маркетинговых сайтов","Перенаправляет кампании на /frontend-design"],"ar":["لا يصلح للصفحات المستهدفة أو المواقع التسويقية","إعادة توجيه الحملات إلى /frontend-design"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT/inngest', 'community', 'xiangteng007', 'XXT-AGENT', 'xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT', 'inngest', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z', '2026-02-18T09:32:53.273Z', NULL, '{"id":"xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT/inngest","name":"inngest","description":{"zh":"Inngest是一种构建可靠后台处理的方式，无需管理基础设施。它允许您构建耐用、长时间运行的工作流程","ja":"Inngestは、インフラストラクチャを管理せずに信頼性の高いバックグラウンド処理を構築する方法です。耐久性のある長時間実行ワークフローを構築できます","ko":"Inngest는 인프라 관리 없이 안정적인 백그라운드 처리를 구축하는 방법입니다. 지속性과 장시간 실행 워크플로우를 구축할 수 있습니다","es":"Inngest es una plataforma que permite construir flujos de trabajo en segundo plano sin necesidad de gestionar infraestructura, ideal para desarrolladores que buscan escalabilidad y confiabilidad","fr":"Inngest est une plateforme qui permet de créer des flux de travail en arrière-plan sans gérer d''infrastructures, idéale pour les développeurs qui recherchent de la scalabilité et de la fiabilité","de":"Inngest ist eine Plattform, die es ermöglicht, Hintergrundverarbeitungen ohne Infrastrukturverwaltung zu erstellen, ideal für Entwickler, die Skalierbarkeit und Zuverlässigkeit suchen","pt":"Inngest é uma solução de processamento em segundo plano confiável que não requer gerenciamento de infraestrutura","ru":"Inngest - это надежное решение для фоновой обработки, не требующее управления инфраструктурой","ar":"Inngest هو حل لمعالجة الخلفية الموثوقة الذي لا يتطلب إدارة البنية التحتية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Inngest集成：可靠的后台处理","ja":"Inngest統合：信頼性の高いバックグラウンド処理","ko":"Inngest 통합: 안정적인 백그라운드 처리","es":"Inngest: Procesamiento en segundo plano sin infraestructura","fr":"Inngest : Traitement en arrière-plan sans infrastructure","de":"Inngest: Hintergrundverarbeitung ohne Infrastruktur","pt":"Inngest: Processamento em Segundo Plano Confiável","ru":"Inngest: Надежная Фоновая Обработка","ar":"Inngest: معالجة الخلفية الموثوقة","en":"inngest"},"description":{"zh":"Inngest是一种构建可靠后台处理的方式，无需管理基础设施。它允许您构建耐用、长时间运行的工作流程","ja":"Inngestは、インフラストラクチャを管理せずに信頼性の高いバックグラウンド処理を構築する方法です。耐久性のある長時間実行ワークフローを構築できます","ko":"Inngest는 인프라 관리 없이 안정적인 백그라운드 처리를 구축하는 방법입니다. 지속性과 장시간 실행 워크플로우를 구축할 수 있습니다","es":"Inngest es una plataforma que permite construir flujos de trabajo en segundo plano sin necesidad de gestionar infraestructura, ideal para desarrolladores que...","fr":"Inngest est une plateforme qui permet de créer des flux de travail en arrière-plan sans gérer d''infrastructures, idéale pour les développeurs qui recherchent...","de":"Inngest ist eine Plattform, die es ermöglicht, Hintergrundverarbeitungen ohne Infrastrukturverwaltung zu erstellen, ideal für Entwickler, die Skalierbarkeit ...","pt":"Inngest é uma solução de processamento em segundo plano confiável que não requer gerenciamento de infraestrutura","ru":"Inngest - это надежное решение для фоновой обработки, не требующее управления инфраструктурой","ar":"Inngest هو حل لمعالجة الخلفية الموثوقة الذي لا يتطلب إدارة البنية التحتية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["无需管理基础设施","耐久性和长时间运行的工作流程","支持AI管道和事件驱动系统","自动故障恢复","灵活的工作流程定义"],"ja":["インフラストラクチャの管理不要","耐久性と長時間実行ワークフロー","AIパイプラインとイベントドリブンシステムのサポート","自動障害復旧","柔軟なワークフローの定義"],"ko":["인프라 관리 필요 없음","지속성 및 장시간 실행 워크플로우","AI 파이프라인 및 이벤트 드리븐 시스템 지원","자동 장애 복구","유연한 워크플로우 정의"],"es":["Procesamiento en segundo plano sin infraestructura","Flujos de trabajo escalables y duraderos","Puntos de control que sobreviven a los fallos","Integración con pipelines de AI y flujos de eventos","Onboarding y procesamiento de eventos en tiempo real"],"fr":["Traitement en arrière-plan sans infrastructure","Flux de travail évolutifs et durables","Points de contrôle qui survivent aux défaillances","Intégration avec des pipelines d''IA et des flux d''événements","Intégration et traitement d''événements en temps réel"],"de":["Hintergrundverarbeitung ohne Infrastruktur","Skalierbare und zuverlässige Workflows","Prüfpunkte, die Ausfälle überstehen","Integration mit AI-Pipelines und Ereignisflüssen","Onboarding und Echtzeit-Ereignisverarbeitung"],"pt":["Processamento em segundo plano confiável","Fluxos de trabalho duradouros","Sem gerenciamento de infraestrutura","Suporte a pipelines de IA","Suporte a fluxos de onboarding","Processamento de eventos em grande escala"],"ru":["Надежная фоновая обработка","Долгосрочные рабочие процессы","Без управления инфраструктурой","Поддержка конвейеров ИИ","Поддержка процессов онбординга","Обработка событий в большом масштабе"],"ar":["معالجة الخلفية الموثوقة","عمليات العمل الطويلة الأمد","بدون إدارة البنية التحتية","دعم أنابيب الذكاء الاصطناعي","دعم عمليات التسجيل","معالجة الأحداث على نطاق كبير"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Inngest","无服务器","后台处理","工作流程","耐久性","长时间运行","AI管道","事件驱动系统"],"ja":["Inngest","サーバーレス","バックグラウンド処理","ワークフロー","耐久性","長時間実行","AIパイプライン","イベントドリブンシステム"],"ko":["Inngest","서버리스","백그라운드 처리","워크플로우","지속성","장시간 실행","AI 파이프라인","이벤트 드리븐 시스템"],"es":["inngest","procesamiento en segundo plano","flujos de trabajo escalables","pipelines de ai","flujos de eventos","onboarding","infraestructura como servicio","desarrollo de software","arquitectura de software"],"fr":["inngest","traitement en arrière-plan","flux de travail évolutifs","pipelines d''ia","flux d''événements","intégration","infrastructure en tant que service","développement de logiciels","architecture de logiciels"],"de":["inngest","hintergrundverarbeitung","skalierbare workflows","ai-pipelines","ereignisflüsse","onboarding","infrastruktur als service","softwareentwicklung","softwarearchitektur"],"pt":["inngest","processamento em segundo plano","fluxos de trabalho duradouros","serviços de processamento","pipelines de ia","onboarding","eventos em grande escala"],"ru":["inngest","фоновая обработка","долгосрочные рабочие процессы","сервисы обработки","конвейеры ИИ","онбординг","события в большом масштабе"],"ar":["inngest","معالجة الخلفية","عمليات العمل الطويلة الأمد","خدمات المعالجة","أنابيب الذكاء الاصطناعي","التسجيل","الأحداث على نطاق كبير"]}},"owner":"xiangteng007","repo":"XXT-AGENT","repoPath":"xiangteng007/XXT-AGENT","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"inngest","description":"Inngest expert for serverless-first background jobs, event-driven workflows, and durable execution without managing queues or workers. Use when: inngest, serverless background job, event-driven workflow, step function, durable execution.","bodyPreview":"# Inngest Integration\n\nYou are an Inngest expert who builds reliable background processing without\nmanaging infrastructure. You understand that serverless doesn''t mean you can''t\nhave durable, long-running workflows - it means you don''t manage the workers.\n\nYou''ve built AI pipelines that take minutes, onboarding flows that span days,\nand event-driven systems that process millions of events. You know that the\nmagic of Inngest is in its steps - each one a checkpoint that survives failures.\n\nYour co","body":"# Inngest Integration\n\nYou are an Inngest expert who builds reliable background processing without\nmanaging infrastructure. You understand that serverless doesn''t mean you can''t\nhave durable, long-running workflows - it means you don''t manage the workers.\n\nYou''ve built AI pipelines that take minutes, onboarding flows that span days,\nand event-driven systems that process millions of events. You know that the\nmagic of Inngest is in its steps - each one a checkpoint that survives failures.\n\nYour core philosophy:\n1. Event\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- inngest-functions\n- event-driven-workflows\n- step-functions\n- serverless-background-jobs\n- durable-sleep\n- fan-out-patterns\n- concurrency-control\n- scheduled-functions\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Basic Function Setup\n\nInngest function with typed events in Next.js\n\n### Multi-Step Workflow\n\nComplex workflow with parallel steps and error handling\n\n### Scheduled/Cron Functions\n\nFunctions that run on a schedule\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### ❌ Not Using Steps\n\n### ❌ Huge Event Payloads\n\n### ❌ Ignoring Concurrency\n\n## Related Skills\n\nWorks well with: `nextjs-app-router`, `vercel-deployment`, `supabase-backend`, `email-systems`, `ai-agents-architect`, `stripe-integration`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:32:53.273Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Serverless Agents needing reliable background processing and durable workflows","zh":"非常适合需要可靠的后台处理和耐用的工作流的无服务器代理","ja":"信頼性の高いバックグラウンド処理と耐久性のあるワークフローが必要なサーバーレス エージェントに最適","ko":"신뢰할 수 있는 백그라운드 처리와 내구성이 뛰어난 워크플로가 필요한 서버리스 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes sin servidor que necesitan procesamiento de fondo confiable y flujos de trabajo duraderos","fr":"Parfait pour les agents sans serveur nécessitant un traitement en arrière-plan fiable et des flux de travail durables","de":"Perfekt für serverlose Agenten, die zuverlässige Hintergrundverarbeitung und belastbare Workflows benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Sem Servidor que necessitam de processamento de fundo confiável e fluxos de trabalho duráveis","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов без сервера, которым требуется надежная фоновая обработка и устойчивые рабочие процессы","ar":"مثالي لعمليات العميل بدون خادم التي تحتاج إلى معالجة الخلفية الموثوقة والتدفقات العملية المتينة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build long-running workflows with checkpointed steps, leveraging Inngest''s serverless architecture for event-driven systems and AI pipelines, while ensuring durable and fault-tolerant processing of millions of events","zh":"赋予代理构建长时间运行的工作流的能力，具有检查点步骤，利用Inngest的无服务器架构进行事件驱动系统和AI管道，同时确保数百万事件的耐用和容错处理","ja":"チェックポイントの付いたステップを備えた長時間実行されるワークフローを構築できるようにエージェントをEmpowerし、Inngestのサーバーレスアーキテクチャを利用してイベント駆動型システムとAIパイプラインを実現し、数百万のイベントの耐久性と障害耐性のある処理を保証する","ko":"체크포인트가 있는 단계를 갖춘 장기 실행 워크플로를 구축할 수 있도록 에이전트를 강화하여 Inngest의 서버리스 아키텍처를 사용하여 이벤트 驱动 시스템과 AI 파이프라인을 구현하고 수백만 개의 이벤트에 대한 내구성과 장애 허용 처리를 보장","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear flujos de trabajo de larga duración con pasos con puntos de control, aprovechando la arquitectura sin servidor de Inngest para sistemas y pipelines de inteligencia artificial impulsados por eventos, garantizando al mismo tiempo un procesamiento duradero y tolerante a fallos de millones de eventos","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des flux de travail de longue durée avec des étapes avec des points de contrôle, en exploitant l''architecture sans serveur d''Inngest pour les systèmes et les pipelines d''intelligence artificielle à base d''événements, tout en assurant un traitement durable et tolérant aux défaillances de millions d''événements","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, lange laufende Workflows mit Kontrollpunkten zu erstellen, die serverlose Architektur von Inngest für ereignisgetriebene Systeme und KI-Pipelines nutzt und gleichzeitig ein dauerhaftes und fehlertolerantes Verarbeiten von Millionen von Ereignissen sicherstellt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir fluxos de trabalho de longa duração com etapas de verificação, aproveitando a arquitetura sem servidor da Inngest para sistemas e pipelines de IA acionados por eventos, garantindo processamento durável e tolerante a falhas de milhões de eventos","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать долгие рабочие процессы с контрольными точками, используя серверную архитектуру Inngest для событийно-ориентированных систем и конвейеров ИИ, обеспечивая надежную и отказоустойчивую обработку миллионов событий","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء تدفقات عمل طويلة الأمد بخطوات محددة، مستفيدة من هندسة خادم غير متصل من Inngest لأنظمة وأنابيب ذكاء اصطناعي مدفوعة بالأحداث، مما يضمن معالجة متينة ومتسامحة مع الأخطاء لملايين الأحداث"},"useCases":{"en":["Building AI pipelines that span minutes or days","Creating onboarding flows with multiple steps and checkpoints","Processing large volumes of events with durable, long-running workflows"],"zh":["构建跨分钟或天的AI管道","创建具有多个步骤和检查点的入职流程","处理大量事件的耐用、长时间运行的工作流"],"ja":["数分または数日のAIパイプラインを構築する","複数のステップとチェックポイントを備えたオンボーディングフローを作成する","大量のイベントを扱う耐久性と長時間実行されるワークフロー"],"ko":["분 또는 일 단위의 AI 파이프라인 구축","여러 단계와 체크포인트가 있는 온보딩 흐름 생성","大量의 이벤트를 처리하는 내구성과 장기 실행 워크플로"],"es":["Creación de pipelines de inteligencia artificial que abarcan minutos o días","Creación de flujos de incorporación con varios pasos y puntos de control","Procesamiento de grandes cantidades de eventos con flujos de trabajo duraderos y de larga duración"],"fr":["Création de pipelines d''intelligence artificielle qui s''étendent sur des minutes ou des jours","Création de flux d''intégration avec plusieurs étapes et points de contrôle","Traitement de grands volumes d''événements avec des flux de travail durables et de longue durée"],"de":["Erstellung von KI-Pipelines, die Minuten oder Tage umfassen","Erstellung von Onboarding-Flows mit mehreren Schritten und Kontrollpunkten","Verarbeitung großer Mengen an Ereignissen mit dauerhaften und lang laufenden Workflows"],"pt":["Construir pipelines de IA que abrangem minutos ou dias","Criar fluxos de integração com várias etapas e pontos de verificação","Processar grandes volumes de eventos com fluxos de trabalho duráveis e de longa duração"],"ru":["Построение конвейеров ИИ, охватывающих минуты или дни","Создание потоков ввода с несколькими шагами и контрольными точками","Обработка больших объемов событий с помощью долгих и устойчивых рабочих процессов"],"ar":["بناء أنابيب ذكاء اصطناعي تمتد لمدة دقائق أو أيام","إنشاء تدفقات إدخال متعددة الخطوات والنقاط المحددة","معالجة أحجام كبيرة من الأحداث بالتدفقات العملية المتينة والطويلة الأمد"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Inngest infrastructure integration","Serverless workflow management limitations apply"],"zh":["需要Inngest基础设施集成","服务器无工作流管理限制适用"],"ja":["Inngestインフラストラクチャの統合が必要","サーバーレスワークフローの管理制限が適用される"],"ko":["Inngest 인프라 통합 필요","서버리스 워크플로 관리 제한 사항 적용"],"es":["Requiere integración de infraestructura de Inngest","Se aplican limitaciones de gestión de flujos de trabajo sin servidor"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration d''infrastructure Inngest","Les limites de gestion des flux de travail sans serveur s''appliquent"],"de":["Benötigt Inngest-Infrastruktur-Integration","Serverlose Workflow-Management-Beschränkungen gelten"],"pt":["Requer integração de infraestrutura da Inngest","Se aplicam limitações de gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho sem servidor"],"ru":["Требуется интеграция с инфраструктурой Inngest","Применяются ограничения управления рабочим процессом без сервера"],"ar":["يتطلب تكامل البنية التحتية لشركة Inngest","تسري قيود إدارة تدفق العمل بدون خادم"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ma1orek/replay/nx-workspace-patterns', 'community', 'ma1orek', 'replay', 'ma1orek/replay', 'nx-workspace-patterns', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z', '2026-02-18T09:32:26.387Z', NULL, '{"id":"ma1orek/replay/nx-workspace-patterns","name":"nx-workspace-patterns","description":{"zh":"Nx 工作空间模式提供了生产级的 monorepo 管理解决方案，帮助您优化开发流程","ja":"Nx ワークスペースパターンは、開発プロセスを最適化するためのプロダクションレベルの monorepo 管理ソリューションを提供します","ko":"Nx 작업공간 패턴은 개발 프로세스를 최적화하는ための 프로덕션급 monorepo 관리 솔루션을 제공합니다","es":"Nx Workspace Patterns es una habilidad para mejorar la gestión de monorepos. Incluye configuración de proyectos y optimización de CI","fr":"Nx Workspace Patterns est une compétence pour améliorer la gestion des monorepos. Elle inclut la configuration des projets et l''optimisation de l''IC","de":"Nx-Arbeitsbereichsmuster ist eine Fähigkeit zur Verbesserung der Verwaltung von Monorepos. Enthält Projekt-Konfiguration und CI-Optimierung","pt":"Os padrões de espaço de trabalho Nx são projetados para ajudar a configurar e otimizar monorepos para melhorar a produtividade do desenvolvedor","ru":"Шаблоны рабочего пространства Nx предназначены для帮助 в настройке и оптимизации монорепозиториев для повышения производительности разработчика","ar":"تم تصميم نماذج مساحة العمل Nx لمساعدة في تعيين وتحسين المستودعات الفردية لتحسين إنتاجية المطور","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Nx 工作空间模式","ja":"Nx ワークスペースパターン","ko":"Nx 작업공간 패턴","es":"Patrones de espacio de trabajo Nx para desarrolladores","fr":"Modèles d''espace de travail Nx pour les développeurs","de":"Nx-Arbeitsbereichsmuster für Entwickler","pt":"Padrões de Espaço de Trabalho Nx","ru":"Шаблоны рабочего пространства Nx","ar":"نماذج مساحة العمل Nx","en":"nx-workspace-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"Nx 工作空间模式提供了生产级的 monorepo 管理解决方案，帮助您优化开发流程","ja":"Nx ワークスペースパターンは、開発プロセスを最適化するためのプロダクションレベルの monorepo 管理ソリューションを提供します","ko":"Nx 작업공간 패턴은 개발 프로세스를 최적화하는ための 프로덕션급 monorepo 관리 솔루션을 제공합니다","es":"Nx Workspace Patterns es una habilidad para mejorar la gestión de monorepos. Incluye configuración de proyectos y optimización de CI","fr":"Nx Workspace Patterns est une compétence pour améliorer la gestion des monorepos. Elle inclut la configuration des projets et l''optimisation de l''IC","de":"Nx-Arbeitsbereichsmuster ist eine Fähigkeit zur Verbesserung der Verwaltung von Monorepos. Enthält Projekt-Konfiguration und CI-Optimierung","pt":"Os padrões de espaço de trabalho Nx são projetados para ajudar a configurar e otimizar monorepos para melhorar a produtividade do desenvolvedor","ru":"Шаблоны рабочего пространства Nx предназначены для帮助 в настройке и оптимизации монорепозиториев для повышения производительности разработчика","ar":"تم تصميم نماذج مساحة العمل Nx لمساعدة في تعيين وتحسين المستودعات الفردية لتحسين إنتاجية المطور","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["设置新的 Nx 工作空间","配置项目边界","优化 CI 以使用受影响的命令","实现远程缓存","管理项目之间的依赖关系","迁移到 Nx"],"ja":["新しい Nx ワークスペースの設定","プロジェクト境界の構成","CI の最適化に影響を受けるコマンドを使用","リモートキャッシュの実装","プロジェクト間の依存関係の管理","Nx への移行"],"ko":["새로운 Nx 작업공간 설정","프로젝트 경계 구성","CI 최적화에 영향을 받는 명령 사용","원격 캐시 구현","프로젝트 간 의존성 관리","Nx로의 마이그레이션"],"es":["Configuración de proyectos","Optimización de CI con comandos afectados","Implementación de caché remoto","Gestión de dependencias entre proyectos","Migración a Nx","Arquitectura Nx"],"fr":["Configuration des projets","Optimisation de l''IC avec des commandes affectées","Mise en œuvre d''un cache distant","Gestion des dépendances entre les projets","Migration vers Nx","Architecture Nx"],"de":["Projekt-Konfiguration","CI-Optimierung mit betroffenen Befehlen","Implementierung von Remote-Caching","Verwaltung von Abhängigkeiten zwischen Projekten","Migration zu Nx","Nx-Architektur"],"pt":["Configuração de novos espaços de trabalho Nx","Otimização de limites de projeto","Implementação de cache remoto","Gerenciamento de dependências entre projetos","Migração para Nx"],"ru":["Настройка новых рабочих пространств Nx","Оптимизация границ проекта","Реализация удаленного кэширования","Управление зависимостями между проектами","Миграция на Nx"],"ar":["تعيين مساحات العمل الجديدة Nx","تحسين حدود المشروع","تنفيذ التخزين المؤقت عن بعد","إدارة التبعيات بين المشاريع","هجرة إلى Nx"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Nx 工作空间模式","monorepo 管理","开发流程优化","CI 优化","远程缓存","项目依赖管理","Nx 迁移"],"ja":["Nx ワークスペースパターン","monorepo 管理","開発プロセス最適化","CI 最適化","リモートキャッシュ","プロジェクト依存関係管理","Nx 移行"],"ko":["Nx 작업공간 패턴","monorepo 관리","개발 프로세스 최적화","CI 최적화","원격 캐시","프로젝트 의존성 관리","Nx 마이그레이션"],"es":["nx workspace patterns","monorepo management","nx monorepo","ci optimization","remote caching","dependency management","nx migration","nx architecture"],"fr":["modèles d''espace de travail nx","gestion de monorepo","monorepo nx","optimisation de l''ic","cache distant","gestion des dépendances","migration vers nx","architecture nx"],"de":["nx-arbeitsbereichsmuster","monorepo-verwaltung","nx-monorepo","ci-optimierung","remote-caching","abhängigkeitsverwaltung","migration zu nx","nx-architektur"],"pt":["nx workspace","monorepo","desenvolvimento de software","produtividade do desenvolvedor","gerenciamento de dependências","otimização de CI"],"ru":["nx рабочее пространство","монорепозиторий","разработка программного обеспечения","производительность разработчика","управление зависимостями","оптимизация CI"],"ar":["مساحة العمل Nx","مستودع فردي","تطوير البرمجيات","إنتاجية المطور","إدارة التبعيات","تحسين CI"]}},"owner":"ma1orek","repo":"replay","repoPath":"ma1orek/replay","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"nx-workspace-patterns","description":"Configure and optimize Nx monorepo workspaces. Use when setting up Nx, configuring project boundaries, optimizing build caching, or implementing affected commands.","bodyPreview":"# Nx Workspace Patterns\n\nProduction patterns for Nx monorepo management.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up new Nx workspaces\n- Configuring project boundaries\n- Optimizing CI with affected commands\n- Implementing remote caching\n- Managing dependencies between projects\n- Migrating to Nx\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Nx Architecture\n\n```\nworkspace/\n├── apps/              # Deployable applications\n│   ├── web/\n│   └── api/\n├── libs/              # Shared libraries\n│   ├── shared/\n│   │   ├── ui/","body":"# Nx Workspace Patterns\n\nProduction patterns for Nx monorepo management.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up new Nx workspaces\n- Configuring project boundaries\n- Optimizing CI with affected commands\n- Implementing remote caching\n- Managing dependencies between projects\n- Migrating to Nx\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Nx Architecture\n\n```\nworkspace/\n├── apps/              # Deployable applications\n│   ├── web/\n│   └── api/\n├── libs/              # Shared libraries\n│   ├── shared/\n│   │   ├── ui/\n│   │   └── utils/\n│   └── feature/\n│       ├── auth/\n│       └── dashboard/\n├── tools/             # Custom executors/generators\n├── nx.json            # Nx configuration\n└── workspace.json     # Project configuration\n```\n\n### 2. Library Types\n\n| Type            | Purpose                          | Example             |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| **feature**     | Smart components, business logic | `feature-auth`      |\n| **ui**          | Presentational components        | `ui-buttons`        |\n| **data-access** | API calls, state management      | `data-access-users` |\n| **util**        | Pure functions, helpers          | `util-formatting`   |\n| **shell**       | App bootstrapping                | `shell-web`         |\n\n## Templates\n\n### Template 1: nx.json Configuration\n\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"./node_modules/nx/schemas/nx-schema.json\",\n  \"npmScope\": \"myorg\",\n  \"affected\": {\n    \"defaultBase\": \"main\"\n  },\n  \"tasksRunnerOptions\": {\n    \"default\": {\n      \"runner\": \"nx/tasks-runners/default\",\n      \"options\": {\n        \"cacheableOperations\": [\n          \"build\",\n          \"lint\",\n          \"test\",\n          \"e2e\",\n          \"build-storybook\"\n        ],\n        \"parallel\": 3\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"targetDefaults\": {\n    \"build\": {\n      \"dependsOn\": [\"^build\"],\n      \"inputs\": [\"production\", \"^production\"],\n      \"cache\": true\n    },\n    \"test\": {\n      \"inputs\": [\"default\", \"^production\", \"{workspaceRoot}/jest.preset.js\"],\n      \"cache\": true\n    },\n    \"lint\": {\n      \"inputs\": [\"default\", \"{workspaceRoot}/.eslintrc.json\"],\n      \"cache\": true\n    },\n    \"e2e\": {\n      \"inputs\": [\"default\", \"^production\"],\n      \"cache\": true\n    }\n  },\n  \"namedInputs\": {\n    \"default\": [\"{projectRoot}/**/*\", \"sharedGlobals\"],\n    \"production\": [\n      \"default\",\n      \"!{projectRoot}/**/?(*.)+(spec|test).[jt]s?(x)?(.snap)\",\n      \"!{projectRoot}/tsconfig.spec.json\",\n      \"!{projectRoot}/jest.config.[jt]s\",\n      \"!{projectRoot}/.eslintrc.json\"\n    ],\n    \"sharedGlobals\": [\n      \"{workspaceRoot}/babel.config.json\",\n      \"{workspaceRoot}/tsconfig.base.json\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"generators\": {\n    \"@nx/react\": {\n      \"application\": {\n        \"style\": \"css\",\n        \"linter\": \"eslint\",\n        \"bundler\": \"webpack\"\n      },\n      \"library\": {\n        \"style\": \"css\",\n        \"linter\": \"eslint\"\n      },\n      \"component\": {\n        \"style\": \"css\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Template 2: Project Configuration\n\n```json\n// apps/web/project.json\n{\n  \"name\": \"web\",\n  \"$schema\": \"../../node_modules/nx/schemas/project-schema.json\",\n  \"sourceRoot\": \"apps/web/src\",\n  \"projectType\": \"application\",\n  \"tags\": [\"type:app\", \"scope:web\"],\n  \"targets\": {\n    \"build\": {\n      \"executor\": \"@nx/webpack:webpack\",\n      \"outputs\": [\"{options.outputPath}\"],\n      \"defaultConfiguration\": \"production\",\n      \"options\": {\n        \"compiler\": \"babel\",\n        \"outputPath\": \"dist/apps/web\",\n        \"index\": \"apps/web/src/index.html\",\n        \"main\": \"apps/web/src/main.tsx\",\n        \"tsConfig\": \"apps/web/tsconfig.app.json\",\n        \"assets\": [\"apps/web/src/assets\"],\n        \"styles\": [\"apps/web/src/styles.css\"]\n      },\n      \"configurations\": {\n        \"development\": {\n          \"extractLicenses\": false,\n          \"optimization\": false,\n          \"sourceMap\": true\n        },\n        \"production\": {\n          \"optimization\": true,\n          \"outputHashing\": \"all\",\n          \"sourceMap\": false,\n          \"extractLicenses\": true\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"serve\": {\n      \"executor\": \"@nx/webpack:dev-server\",\n      \"defaultConfiguration\": \"development\",\n      \"options\": {\n        \"buildTarget\": \"web:build\"\n      },\n      \"configurations\": {\n        \"development\": {\n          \"buildTarget\": \"web:build:development\"\n        },\n        \"production\": {\n          \"buildTarget\": \"web:build:production\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"test\": {\n      \"executor\": \"@nx/jest:jest\",\n      \"outputs\": [\"{workspaceRoot}/coverage/{projectRoot}\"],\n      \"options\": {\n        \"jestConfig\": \"apps/web/jest.config.ts\",\n        \"passWithNoTests\": true\n      }\n    },\n    \"lint\": {\n      \"executor\": \"@nx/eslint:lint\",\n      \"outputs\": [\"{options.outputFile}\"],\n      \"options\": {\n        \"lintFilePatterns\": [\"apps/web/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}\"]\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Template 3: Module Boundary Rules\n\n```json\n// .eslintrc.json\n{\n  \"root\": true,\n  \"ignorePatterns\": [\"**/*\"],\n  \"plugins\": [\"@nx\"],\n  \"overrides\": [\n    {\n      \"files\": [\"*.ts\", \"*.tsx\", \"*.js\", \"*.jsx\"],\n      \"rules\": {\n        \"@nx/enforce-module-boundaries\": [\n          \"error\",\n          {\n            \"enforceBuildableLibDependency\": true,\n            \"allow\": [],\n            \"depConstraints\": [\n              {\n                \"sourceTag\": \"type:app\",\n                \"onlyDependOnLibsWithTags\": [\n                  \"type:feature\",\n                  \"type:ui\",\n                  \"type:data-access\",\n                  \"type:util\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"sourceTag\": \"type:feature\",\n                \"onlyDependOnLibsWithTags\": [\n                  \"type:ui\",\n                  \"type:data-access\",\n                  \"type:util\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"sourceTag\": \"type:ui\",\n                \"onlyDependOnLibsWithTags\": [\"type:ui\", \"type:util\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"sourceTag\": \"type:data-access\",\n                \"onlyDependOnLibsWithTags\": [\"type:data-access\", \"type:util\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"sourceTag\": \"type:util\",\n                \"onlyDependOnLibsWithTags\": [\"type:util\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"sourceTag\": \"scope:web\",\n                \"onlyDependOnLibsWithTags\": [\"scope:web\", \"scope:shared\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"sourceTag\": \"scope:api\",\n                \"onlyDependOnLibsWithTags\": [\"scope:api\", \"scope:shared\"]\n              },\n              {\n                \"sourceTag\": \"scope:shared\",\n                \"onlyDependOnLibsWithTags\": [\"scope:shared\"]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Template 4: Custom Generator\n\n```typescript\n// tools/generators/feature-lib/index.ts\nimport {\n  Tree,\n  formatFiles,\n  generateFiles,\n  joinPathFragments,\n  names,\n  readProjectConfiguration,\n} from \"@nx/devkit\";\nimport { libraryGenerator } from \"@nx/react\";\n\ninterface FeatureLibraryGeneratorSchema {\n  name: string;\n  scope: string;\n  directory?: string;\n}\n\nexport default async function featureLibraryGenerator(\n  tree: Tree,\n  options: FeatureLibraryGeneratorSchema,\n) {\n  const { name, scope, directory } = options;\n  const projectDirectory = directory\n    ? `${directory}/${name}`\n    : `libs/${scope}/feature-${name}`;\n\n  // Generate base library\n  await libraryGenerator(tree, {\n    name: `feature-${name}`,\n    directory: projectDirectory,\n    tags: `type:feature,scope:${scope}`,\n    style: \"css\",\n    skipTsConfig: false,\n    skipFormat: true,\n    unitTestRunner: \"jest\",\n    linter: \"eslint\",\n  });\n\n  // Add custom files\n  const projectConfig = readProjectConfiguration(\n    tree,\n    `${scope}-feature-${name}`,\n  );\n  const projectNames = names(name);\n\n  generateFiles(\n    tree,\n    joinPathFragments(__dirname, \"files\"),\n    projectConfig.sourceRoot,\n    {\n      ...projectNames,\n      scope,\n      tmpl: \"\",\n    },\n  );\n\n  await formatFiles(tree);\n}\n```\n\n### Template 5: CI Configuration with Affected\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [main]\n\nenv:\n  NX_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NX_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN }}\n\njobs:\n  main:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 20\n          cache: \"npm\"\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Derive SHAs for affected commands\n        uses: nrwl/nx-set-shas@v4\n\n      - name: Run affected lint\n        run: npx nx affected -t lint --parallel=3\n\n      - name: Run affected test\n        run: npx nx affected -t test --parallel=3 --configuration=ci\n\n      - name: Run affected build\n        run: npx nx affected -t build --parallel=3\n\n      - name: Run affected e2e\n        run: npx nx affected -t e2e --parallel=1\n```\n\n### Template 6: Remote Caching Setup\n\n```typescript\n// nx.json with Nx Cloud\n{\n  \"tasksRunnerOptions\": {\n    \"default\": {\n      \"runner\": \"nx-cloud\",\n      \"options\": {\n        \"cacheableOperations\": [\"build\", \"lint\", \"test\", \"e2e\"],\n        \"accessToken\": \"your-nx-cloud-token\",\n        \"parallel\": 3,\n        \"cacheDirectory\": \".nx/cache\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"nxCloudAccessToken\": \"your-nx-cloud-token\"\n}\n\n// Self-hosted cache with S3\n{\n  \"tasksRunnerOptions\": {\n    \"default\": {\n      \"runner\": \"@nx-aws-cache/nx-aws-cache\",\n      \"options\": {\n        \"cacheableOperations\": [\"build\", \"lint\", \"test\"],\n        \"awsRegion\": \"us-east-1\",\n        \"awsBucket\": \"my-nx-cache-bucket\",\n        \"awsProfile\": \"default\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Common Commands\n\n```bash\n# Generate new library\nnx g @nx/react:lib feature-auth --directory=libs/web --tags=type:feature,scope:web\n\n# Run affected tests\nnx affected -t test --base=main\n\n# View dependency graph\nnx graph\n\n# Run specific project\nnx build web --configuration=production\n\n# Reset cache\nnx reset\n\n# Run migrations\nnx migrate latest\nnx migrate --run-migrations\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Use tags consistently** - Enforce with module boundaries\n- **Enable caching early** - Significant CI savings\n- **Keep libs focused** - Single responsibility\n- **Use generators** - Ensure consistency\n- **Document boundaries** - Help new developers\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t create circular deps** - Graph should be acyclic\n- **Don''t skip affected** - Test only what changed\n- **Don''t ignore boundaries** - Tech debt accumulates\n- **Don''t over-granularize** - Balance lib count\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Nx Documentation](https://nx.dev/getting-started/intro)\n- [Module Boundaries](https://nx.dev/core-features/enforce-module-boundaries)\n- [Nx Cloud](https://nx.app/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:32:26.387Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Monorepo Management Agents needing advanced Nx workspace configuration capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级 Nx 工作空间配置功能的 Monorepo 管理代理的理想选择。","ja":"Nx ワークスペースの高度な設定機能を必要とする Monorepo 管理エージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 Nx 작업공간 구성 기능을 필요로 하는 Monorepo 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de administración de monorepo que necesitan capacidades de configuración avanzada de espacio de trabajo Nx.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de gestion de monorepo nécessitant des capacités de configuration avancée de l''espace de travail Nx.","de":"Ideal für Monorepo-Management-Agents, die erweiterte Nx-Arbeitsbereichskonfigurationsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Monorepo que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de configuração do espaço de trabalho Nx.","ru":"Идеально для агентов управления монорепозиторием, которым необходимы расширенные возможности конфигурации рабочего пространства Nx.","ar":"مثالي لعميل إدارة مونوريبو الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتكوين مساحة العمل Nx."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to optimize CI with affected commands, implement remote caching, and manage dependencies between projects using Nx architecture, leveraging libraries and apps for efficient monorepo management.","zh":"赋予代理优化 CI 的能力，使用受影响的命令，实现远程缓存，并使用 Nx 架构管理项目之间的依赖，利用库和应用程序实现高效的 Monorepo 管理。","ja":"エージェントに CI を最適化する能力を与え、影響を受けるコマンドを使用し、リモートキャッシングを実装し、Nx アーキテクチャを使用してプロジェクト間の依存関係を管理し、ライブラリとアプリケーションを使用してモノレポ管理を効率化する。","ko":"에이전트에 CI를 최적화하는 능력을 부여하여 영향을 받는 명령을 사용하고, 원격 캐싱을 구현하며, Nx 아키텍처를 사용하여 프로젝트 간의 종속성을 관리하고, 라이브러리와 애플리케이션을 사용하여 모노레포 관리를 효율화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a optimizar la integración continua con comandos afectados, implementar la caché remota y gestionar las dependencias entre proyectos que utilizan la arquitectura Nx, aprovechando las bibliotecas y aplicaciones para una gestión de monorepo eficiente.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''optimiser l''intégration continue avec des commandes affectées, de mettre en œuvre le cache distant et de gérer les dépendances entre les projets utilisant l''architecture Nx, en exploitant les bibliothèques et les applications pour une gestion de monorepo efficace.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die kontinuierliche Integration mit betroffenen Befehlen zu optimieren, Remote-Caching zu implementieren und Abhängigkeiten zwischen Projekten zu verwalten, die die Nx-Architektur verwenden, indem es Bibliotheken und Apps für eine effiziente Monorepo-Verwaltung nutzt.","pt":"Permite que os agentes otimizem o CI com comandos afetados, implementem cache remoto e gerenciem dependências entre projetos usando a arquitetura Nx, aproveitando bibliotecas e aplicativos para gerenciamento eficiente de monorepo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью оптимизировать CI с помощью затронутых команд, реализовать удаленный кэш и управлять зависимостями между проектами с использованием архитектуры Nx, используя библиотеки и приложения для эффективного управления монорепозиторием.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تحسين CI بأوامر متأثرة وتنفيذ ذاكرة مؤقتة عن بعد وإدارة التبعيات بين المشاريع باستخدام هندسة Nx، واستخدام المكتبات والتطبيقات لإدارة مونوريبو فعالة."},"useCases":{"en":["Configuring project boundaries for new Nx workspaces","Implementing remote caching for optimized build performance","Migrating existing projects to Nx for streamlined monorepo management"],"zh":["为新 Nx 工作空间配置项目边界","实现远程缓存以优化构建性能","将现有项目迁移到 Nx 以实现流畅的 Monorepo 管理"],"ja":["新しい Nx ワークスペースのプロジェクト境界を設定する","リモートキャッシングを実装してビルド性能を最適化する","既存のプロジェクトを Nx に移行してモノレポ管理を効率化する"],"ko":["새로운 Nx 작업공간을 위한 프로젝트 경계 설정","원격 캐싱을 구현하여 빌드 성능을 최적화","기존 프로젝트를 Nx로 마이그레이션하여 모노레포 관리를 효율화"],"es":["Configuración de límites de proyecto para nuevos espacios de trabajo Nx","Implementación de la caché remota para un rendimiento de compilación optimizado","Migración de proyectos existentes a Nx para una gestión de monorepo optimizada"],"fr":["Configuration des limites de projet pour de nouveaux espaces de travail Nx","Mise en œuvre du cache distant pour un rendement de construction optimisé","Migration de projets existants vers Nx pour une gestion de monorepo rationalisée"],"de":["Konfiguration von Projektgrenzen für neue Nx-Arbeitsbereiche","Implementierung von Remote-Caching für optimierte Build-Leistung","Migration von bestehenden Projekten zu Nx für eine optimierte Monorepo-Verwaltung"],"pt":["Configurando limites de projeto para novos espaços de trabalho Nx","Implementando cache remoto para desempenho de compilação otimizado","Migrando projetos existentes para Nx para gerenciamento de monorepo simplificado"],"ru":["Настройка границ проекта для новых рабочих пространств Nx","Реализация удаленного кэша для оптимизированного выполнения сборки","Миграция существующих проектов в Nx для упрощенного управления монорепозиторием"],"ar":["تكوين حدود المشروع للفراغات العمل الجديدة Nx","تنفيذ ذاكرة مؤقتة عن بعد لأداء بناء محسّن","نقل المشاريع الحالية إلى Nx لإدارة مونوريبو مبسطة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Nx monorepo setup","Limited to Nx-specific configurations and optimizations"],"zh":["需要 Nx モノレポ設定","仅限 Nx 特定的配置和优化"],"ja":["Nx モノレポ設定が必要","Nx 固有の設定と最適化のみ"],"ko":["Nx 모노레포 설정이 필요","Nx 전용 구성 및 최적화에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere configuración de monorepo Nx","Limitado a configuraciones y optimizaciones específicas de Nx"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de monorepo Nx","Limité aux configurations et optimisations spécifiques à Nx"],"de":["Erfordert Nx-Monorepo-Setup","Begrenzt auf Nx-spezifische Konfigurationen und Optimierungen"],"pt":["Exige configuração de monorepo Nx","Limitado a configurações e otimizações específicas do Nx"],"ru":["Требует настройки монорепозитория Nx","Ограничен конфигурациями и оптимизациями, специфичными для Nx"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد مونوريبو Nx","محدود بإعدادات وتنظيمات محددة ل Nx"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
