cia","fr":"Conception d''interface : Créez des interfaces avec art et...","de":"Benutzeroberflächendesign: Erstelle Benutzeroberflächen m...","pt":"Design de Interface: Crie Dashboards Personalizados","ru":"Дизайн Интерфейса: Создавайте Индивидуальные Панели","ar":"تصميم الواجهة: قم بإنشاء لوحات القيادة المخصصة","en":"interface-design"},"description":{"zh":"界面设计技能用于构建仪表盘、管理面板、SaaS 应用等的用户界面","ja":"インターフェースデザインスキルは、ダッシュボード、管理パネル、SaaS アプリなどのユーザーインターフェースを構築するために使用されます","ko":"인터페이스 디자인 스킬은 대시보드, 관리 패널, SaaS 앱 등의 사용자 인터페이스를 구축하는 데 사용됩니다","es":"El diseño de interfaz es fundamental para crear experiencias de usuario eficaces. Aprende a diseñar interfaces con arte y consistencia","fr":"La conception d''interface est essentielle pour créer des expériences utilisateur efficaces. Apprenez à concevoir des interfaces avec art et cohérence","de":"Das Benutzeroberflächendesign ist entscheidend für die Erstellung effektiver Benutzererfahrungen. Lernen Sie, Benutzeroberflächen mit Handwerk und Konsistenz...","pt":"O design de interface é fundamental para criar experiências de usuário personalizadas e eficazes para dashboards e aplicativos SaaS. Aprenda a criar interfac...","ru":"Дизайн интерфейса имеет решающее значение для создания персонализированных и эффективных пользовательских опытов для панелей управления и приложений SaaS. Уз...","ar":"تصميم الواجهة أمر بالغ الأهمية لإنشاء تجارب مستخدم مخصصة وفعالة للوحات القيادة وتطبيقات SaaS. تعلم كيفية إنشاء واجهات مستخدم مخصصة باستخدام مهارة تصميم الواج...","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["构建仪表盘","设计管理面板","创建 SaaS 应用","开发工具和设置页面","构建数据接口"],"ja":["ダッシュボードの構築","管理パネルの設計","SaaS アプリの作成","ツールと設定ページの開発","データインターフェースの構築"],"ko":["대시보드 구축","관리 패널 디자인","SaaS 앱 생성","도구 및 설정 페이지 개발","데이터 인터페이스 구축"],"es":["Diseño de interfaces de usuario para dashboards y paneles de administración","Creación de interfaces consistentes y coherentes","Mejora de la experiencia del usuario","Diseño de interfaces para aplicaciones SaaS y herramientas","Optimización de la usabilidad y la accesibilidad"],"fr":["Conception d''interfaces utilisateur pour les tableaux de bord et les panneaux d''administration","Création d''interfaces cohérentes et consistantes","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur","Conception d''interfaces pour les applications SaaS et les outils","Optimisation de l''utilisabilité et de l''accessibilité"],"de":["Entwurf von Benutzeroberflächen für Dashboards und Admin-Panels","Erstellung von konsistenten und zusammenhängenden Benutzeroberflächen","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung","Entwurf von Benutzeroberflächen für SaaS-Anwendungen und Tools","Optimierung der Benutzerfreundlichkeit und Barrierefreiheit"],"pt":["Criação de interfaces de usuário personalizadas","Desenvolvimento de dashboards e painéis de administração","Design de aplicativos SaaS","Otimização da experiência do usuário","Criação de interfaces de usuário responsivas"],"ru":["Создание персонализированных интерфейсов пользователя","Разработка панелей управления и административных панелей","Дизайн приложений SaaS","Оптимизация пользовательского опыта","Создание адаптивных интерфейсов пользователя"],"ar":["إنشاء واجهات مستخدم مخصصة","تطوير لوحات القيادة وألواح التحكم والإدارة","تصميم تطبيقات SaaS","تحسين تجربة المستخدم","إنشاء واجهات مستخدم متجاوبة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["界面设计","用户界面","仪表盘设计","管理面板设计","SaaS 应用设计","工具设计","设置页面设计"],"ja":["インターフェースデザイン","ユーザーインターフェース","ダッシュボード設計","管理パネル設計","SaaS アプリ設計","ツール設計","設定ページ設計"],"ko":["인터페이스 디자인","사용자 인터페이스","대시보드 디자인","관리 패널 디자인","SaaS 앱 디자인","도구 디자인","설정 페이지 디자인"],"es":["diseño de interfaz","interfaces de usuario","experiencia del usuario","dashboards","paneles de administración","aplicaciones SaaS","usabilidad","accesibilidad"],"fr":["conception d''interface","interfaces utilisateur","expérience utilisateur","tableaux de bord","panneaux d''administration","applications SaaS","utilisabilité","accessibilité"],"de":["Benutzeroberflächendesign","Benutzeroberflächen","Benutzererfahrung","Dashboards","Admin-Panels","SaaS-Anwendungen","Benutzerfreundlichkeit","Barrierefreiheit"],"pt":["design de interface","dashboards personalizados","painéis de administração","aplicativos SaaS","experiência do usuário","interfaces de usuário responsivas"],"ru":["дизайн интерфейса","панели управления","административные панели","приложения SaaS","пользовательский опыт","адаптивные интерфейсы пользователя"],"ar":["تصميم الواجهة","لوحات القيادة المخصصة","ألواح التحكم والإدارة","تطبيقات SaaS","تجربة المستخدم","واجهات المستخدم المتجاوبة"]}},"owner":"AntonioPiattiFadda","repo":"pediclick-frontend","repoPath":"AntonioPiattiFadda/pediclick-frontend","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"interface-design","description":"This skill is for interface design — dashboards, admin panels, apps, tools, and interactive products. NOT for marketing design (landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns).","bodyPreview":"# Interface Design\n\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\n\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\n\n---\n\n# The Problem\n\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\n\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state your intent — and","body":"# Interface Design\n\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\n\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\n\n---\n\n# The Problem\n\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\n\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state your intent — and still produce a template. Warm colors on cold structures. Friendly fonts on generic layouts. \"Kitchen feel\" that looks like every other app.\n\nThis happens because intent lives in prose, but code generation pulls from patterns. The gap between them is where defaults win.\n\nThe process below helps. But process alone doesn''t guarantee craft. You have to catch yourself.\n\n---\n\n# Where Defaults Hide\n\nDefaults don''t announce themselves. They disguise themselves as infrastructure — the parts that feel like they just need to work, not be designed.\n\n**Typography feels like a container.** Pick something readable, move on. But typography isn''t holding your design — it IS your design. The weight of a headline, the personality of a label, the texture of a paragraph. These shape how the product feels before anyone reads a word. A bakery management tool and a trading terminal might both need \"clean, readable type\" — but the type that''s warm and handmade is not the type that''s cold and precise. If you''re reaching for your usual font, you''re not designing.\n\n**Navigation feels like scaffolding.** Build the sidebar, add the links, get to the real work. But navigation isn''t around your product — it IS your product. Where you are, where you can go, what matters most. A page floating in space is a component demo, not software. The navigation teaches people how to think about the space they''re in.\n\n**Data feels like presentation.** You have numbers, show numbers. But a number on screen is not design. The question is: what does this number mean to the person looking at it? What will they do with it? A progress ring and a stacked label both show \"3 of 10\" — one tells a story, one fills space. If you''re reaching for number-on-label, you''re not designing.\n\n**Token names feel like implementation detail.** But your CSS variables are design decisions. `--ink` and `--parchment` evoke a world. `--gray-700` and `--surface-2` evoke a template. Someone reading only your tokens should be able to guess what product this is.\n\nThe trap is thinking some decisions are creative and others are structural. There are no structural decisions. Everything is design. The moment you stop asking \"why this?\" is the moment defaults take over.\n\n---\n\n# Intent First\n\nBefore touching code, answer these. Not in your head — out loud, to yourself or the user.\n\n**Who is this human?**\nNot \"users.\" The actual person. Where are they when they open this? What''s on their mind? What did they do 5 minutes ago, what will they do 5 minutes after? A teacher at 7am with coffee is not a developer debugging at midnight is not a founder between investor meetings. Their world shapes the interface.\n\n**What must they accomplish?**\nNot \"use the dashboard.\" The verb. Grade these submissions. Find the broken deployment. Approve the payment. The answer determines what leads, what follows, what hides.\n\n**What should this feel like?**\nSay it in words that mean something. \"Clean and modern\" means nothing — every AI says that. Warm like a notebook? Cold like a terminal? Dense like a trading floor? Calm like a reading app? The answer shapes color, type, spacing, density — everything.\n\nIf you cannot answer these with specifics, stop. Ask the user. Do not guess. Do not default.\n\n## Every Choice Must Be A Choice\n\nFor every decision, you must be able to explain WHY.\n\n- Why this layout and not another?\n- Why this color temperature?\n- Why this typeface?\n- Why this spacing scale?\n- Why this information hierarchy?\n\nIf your answer is \"it''s common\" or \"it''s clean\" or \"it works\" — you haven''t chosen. You''ve defaulted. Defaults are invisible. Invisible choices compound into generic output.\n\n**The test:** If you swapped your choices for the most common alternatives and the design didn''t feel meaningfully different, you never made real choices.\n\n## Sameness Is Failure\n\nIf another AI, given a similar prompt, would produce substantially the same output — you have failed.\n\nThis is not about being different for its own sake. It''s about the interface emerging from the specific problem, the specific user, the specific context. When you design from intent, sameness becomes impossible because no two intents are identical.\n\nWhen you design from defaults, everything looks the same because defaults are shared.\n\n## Intent Must Be Systemic\n\nSaying \"warm\" and using cold colors is not following through. Intent is not a label — it''s a constraint that shapes every decision.\n\nIf the intent is warm: surfaces, text, borders, accents, semantic colors, typography — all warm. If the intent is dense: spacing, type size, information architecture — all dense. If the intent is calm: motion, contrast, color saturation — all calm.\n\nCheck your output against your stated intent. Does every token reinforce it? Or did you state an intent and then default anyway?\n\n---\n\n# Product Domain Exploration\n\nThis is where defaults get caught — or don''t.\n\nGeneric output: Task type → Visual template → Theme\nCrafted output: Task type → Product domain → Signature → Structure + Expression\n\nThe difference: time in the product''s world before any visual or structural thinking.\n\n## Required Outputs\n\n**Do not propose any direction until you produce all four:**\n\n**Domain:** Concepts, metaphors, vocabulary from this product''s world. Not features — territory. Minimum 5.\n\n**Color world:** What colors exist naturally in this product''s domain? Not \"warm\" or \"cool\" — go to the actual world. If this product were a physical space, what would you see? What colors belong there that don''t belong elsewhere? List 5+.\n\n**Signature:** One element — visual, structural, or interaction — that could only exist for THIS product. If you can''t name one, keep exploring.\n\n**Defaults:** 3 obvious choices for this interface type — visual AND structural. You can''t avoid patterns you haven''t named.\n\n## Proposal Requirements\n\nYour direction must explicitly reference:\n- Domain concepts you explored\n- Colors from your color world exploration\n- Your signature element\n- What replaces each default\n\n**The test:** Read your proposal. Remove the product name. Could someone identify what this is for? If not, it''s generic. Explore deeper.\n\n---\n\n# The Mandate\n\n**Before showing the user, look at what you made.**\n\nAsk yourself: \"If they said this lacks craft, what would they mean?\"\n\nThat thing you just thought of — fix it first.\n\nYour first output is probably generic. That''s normal. The work is catching it before the user has to.\n\n## The Checks\n\nRun these against your output before presenting:\n\n- **The swap test:** If you swapped the typeface for your usual one, would anyone notice? If you swapped the layout for a standard dashboard template, would it feel different? The places where swapping wouldn''t matter are the places you defaulted.\n\n- **The squint test:** Blur your eyes. Can you still perceive hierarchy? Is anything jumping out harshly? Craft whispers.\n\n- **The signature test:** Can you point to five specific elements where your signature appears? Not \"the overall feel\" — actual components. A signature you can''t locate doesn''t exist.\n\n- **The token test:** Read your CSS variables out loud. Do they sound like they belong to this product''s world, or could they belong to any project?\n\nIf any check fails, iterate before showing.\n\n---\n\n# Craft Foundations\n\n## Subtle Layering\n\nThis is the backbone of craft. Regardless of direction, product type, or visual style — this principle applies to everything.\n\n**Surfaces must be barely different but still distinguishable.** Study Vercel, Supabase, Linear. Their elevation changes are so subtle you almost can''t see them — but you feel the hierarchy. Not dramatic jumps. Not obviously different colors. Whisper-quiet shifts.\n\n**Borders must be light but not invisible.** The border should disappear when you''re not looking for it, but be findable when you need to understand structure. If borders are the first thing you notice, they''re too strong. If you can''t tell where regions begin and end, they''re too weak.\n\n**The squint test:** Blur your eyes at the interface. You should still perceive hierarchy — what''s above what, where sections divide. But nothing should jump out. No harsh lines. No jarring color shifts. Just quiet structure.\n\nThis separates professional interfaces from amateur ones. Get this wrong and nothing else matters.\n\n## Infinite Expression\n\nEvery pattern has infinite expressions. **No interface should look the same.**\n\nA metric display could be a hero number, inline stat, sparkline, gauge, progress bar, comparison delta, trend badge, or something new. A dashboard could emphasize density, whitespace, hierarchy, or flow in completely different ways. Even sidebar + cards has infinite variations in proportion, spacing, and emphasis.\n\n**Before building, ask:**\n- What''s the ONE thing users do most here?\n- What products solve similar problems brilliantly? Study them.\n- Why would this interface feel designed for its purpose, not templated?\n\n**NEVER produce identical output.** Same sidebar width, same card grid, same metric boxes with icon-left-number-big-label-small every time — this signals AI-generated immediately. It''s forgettable.\n\nThe architecture and components should emerge from the task and data, executed in a way that feels fresh. Linear''s cards don''t look like Notion''s. Vercel''s metrics don''t look like Stripe''s. Same concepts, infinite expressions.\n\n## Color Lives Somewhere\n\nEvery product exists in a world. That world has colors.\n\nBefore you reach for a palette, spend time in the product''s world. What would you see if you walked into the physical version of this space? What materials? What light? What objects?\n\nYour palette should feel like it came FROM somewhere — not like it was applied TO something.\n\n**Beyond Warm and Cold:** Temperature is one axis. Is this quiet or loud? Dense or spacious? Serious or playful? Geometric or organic? A trading terminal and a meditation app are both \"focused\" — completely different kinds of focus. Find the specific quality, not the generic label.\n\n**Color Carries Meaning:** Gray builds structure. Color communicates — status, action, emphasis, identity. Unmotivated color is noise. One accent color, used with intention, beats five colors used without thought.\n\n---\n\n# Design Principles\n\n## Spacing\nPick a base unit and stick to multiples. Consistency matters more than the specific number. Random values signal no system.\n\n## Padding\nKeep it symmetrical. If one side is 16px, others should match unless there''s a clear reason.\n\n## Depth\nChoose ONE approach and commit:\n- **Borders-only** — Clean, technical. For dense tools.\n- **Subtle shadows** — Soft lift. For approachable products.\n- **Layered shadows** — Premium, dimensional. For cards that need presence.\n\nDon''t mix approaches.\n\n## Border Radius\nSharper feels technical. Rounder feels friendly. Pick a scale and apply consistently.\n\n## Typography\nHeadlines need weight and tight tracking. Body needs readability. Data needs monospace. Build a hierarchy.\n\n## Color & Surfaces\nBuild from primitives: foreground (text hierarchy), background (surface elevation), border (separation hierarchy), brand, and semantic (destructive, warning, success). Every color should trace back to these. No random hex values — everything maps to the system.\n\n## Animation\nFast micro-interactions (~150ms), smooth easing. No bouncy/spring effects.\n\n## States\nEvery interactive element needs states: default, hover, active, focus, disabled. Data needs states too: loading, empty, error. Missing states feel broken.\n\n## Controls\nNative `<select>` and `<input type=\"date\">` can''t be styled. Build custom components.\n\n---\n\n# Avoid\n\n- **Harsh borders** — if borders are the first thing you see, they''re too strong\n- **Dramatic surface jumps** — elevation changes should be whisper-quiet\n- **Inconsistent spacing** — the clearest sign of no system\n- **Mixed depth strategies** — pick one approach and commit\n- **Missing interaction states** — hover, focus, disabled, loading, error\n- **Dramatic drop shadows** — shadows should be subtle, not attention-grabbing\n- **Large radius on small elements**\n- **Pure white cards on colored backgrounds**\n- **Thick decorative borders**\n- **Gradients and color for decoration** — color should mean something\n- **Multiple accent colors** — dilutes focus\n\n---\n\n# Workflow\n\n## Communication\nBe invisible. Don''t announce modes or narrate process.\n\n**Never say:** \"I''m in ESTABLISH MODE\", \"Let me check system.md...\"\n\n**Instead:** Jump into work. State suggestions with reasoning.\n\n## Suggest + Ask\nLead with your exploration and recommendation, then confirm:\n```\n\"Domain: [5+ concepts from the product''s world]\nColor world: [5+ colors that exist in this domain]\nSignature: [one element unique to this product]\nRejecting: [default 1] → [alternative], [default 2] → [alternative], [default 3] → [alternative]\n\nDirection: [approach that connects to the above]\"\n\n[AskUserQuestion: \"Does that direction feel right?\"]\n```\n\n## If Project Has system.md\nRead `.interface-design/system.md` and apply. Decisions are made.\n\n## If No system.md\n1. Explore domain — Produce all four required outputs\n2. Propose — Direction must reference all four\n3. Confirm — Get user buy-in\n4. Build — Apply principles\n5. **Evaluate** — Run the mandate checks before showing\n6. Offer to save\n\n---\n\n# After Completing a Task\n\nWhen you finish building something, **always offer to save**:\n\n```\n\"Want me to save these patterns for future sessions?\"\n```\n\nIf yes, write to `.interface-design/system.md`:\n- Direction and feel\n- Depth strategy (borders/shadows/layered)\n- Spacing base unit\n- Key component patterns\n\nThis compounds — each save makes future work faster and more consistent.\n\n---\n\n# Deep Dives\n\nFor more detail on specific topics:\n- `references/principles.md` — Code examples, specific values, dark mode\n- `references/validation.md` — Memory management, when to update system.md\n\n# Commands\n\n- `/interface-design:status` — Current system state\n- `/interface-design:audit` — Check code against system\n- `/interface-design:extract` — Extract patterns from code\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:32:55.312Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for UI-focused Agents like Cursor and Claude Code needing advanced interface design capabilities for dashboards and admin panels.","zh":"适用于Cursor和Claude Code等面向UI的Agent，需要为仪表盘和管理面板提供高级界面设计能力。","ja":"CursorやClaude CodeなどのUIに重点を置いたエージェントに適しており、ダッシュボードや管理パネルに高度なインターフェイス設計機能を必要とする。","ko":"Cursor와 Claude Code 같은 UI에 중점을 둔 에이전트에게 적합하며, 대시보드와 관리자 패널에 고급 인터페이스 디자인 기능이 필요한 경우에 사용됩니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes centrados en la interfaz de usuario como Cursor y Claude Code que necesitan capacidades de diseño de interfaz avanzadas para paneles de control y paneles de administración.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents axés sur l''interface utilisateur comme Cursor et Claude Code nécessitant des capacités de conception d''interface avancées pour les tableaux de bord et les panneaux d''administration.","de":"Ideal für benutzeroberflächenorientierte Agenten wie Cursor und Claude Code, die erweiterte Schnittstellen-Design-Funktionen für Dashboards und Admin-Panel benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes focados em UI, como Cursor e Claude Code, que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de design de interface para dashboards e painéis de administração.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, ориентированных на UI, таких как Cursor и Claude Code, которые требуют продвинутых возможностей проектирования интерфейса для панелей управления и административных панелей.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الوكلاء مركزة على واجهة المستخدم مثل Cursor و Claude Code التي تحتاج إلى مميزات تصميم واجهة متقدمة للوحات القيادة ولوحات التحكم الإدارية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft consistent and user-friendly interfaces using design patterns and best practices for tools, settings pages, and data interfaces, leveraging protocols like HTML and CSS for seamless integration.","zh":"赋予代理人使用设计模式和最佳实践，创建一致且用户友好的界面，用于工具、设置页面和数据接口，并利用HTML和CSS等协议实现无缝集成。","ja":"エージェントに、設計パターンとベストプラクティスを使用して、一貫性のあるユーザーフレンドリーなインターフェイスを作成する力を与え、ツール、設定ページ、データインターフェイスに使用し、HTMLやCSSなどのプロトコルを使用してシームレスな統合を実現する。","ko":"에이전트에게 일관성 있고 사용자 친화적인 인터페이스를 만들 수 있는 능력을 부여하여, 도구, 설정 페이지, 데이터 인터페이스에 디자인 패턴과 최선의 관행을 사용하고, HTML 및 CSS와 같은 프로토콜을 활용하여无缝集成을 구현합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear interfaces consistentes y fáciles de usar mediante patrones de diseño y mejores prácticas para herramientas, páginas de configuración e interfaces de datos, aprovechando protocolos como HTML y CSS para una integración sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des interfaces cohérentes et conviviales en utilisant des modèles de conception et les meilleures pratiques pour les outils, les pages de paramètres et les interfaces de données, en exploitant des protocoles tels que HTML et CSS pour une intégration sans problème.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, konsistente und benutzerfreundliche Schnittstellen unter Verwendung von Designmustern und Best Practices für Werkzeuge, Einstellungsseiten und Daten-Schnittstellen zu erstellen, indem Protokolle wie HTML und CSS für eine nahtlose Integration genutzt werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem interfaces consistentes e amigáveis ao usuário, utilizando padrões de design e boas práticas para ferramentas, páginas de configurações e interfaces de dados, aproveitando protocolos como HTML e CSS para integração sem problemas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать последовательные и удобные для пользователя интерфейсы, используя шаблоны проектирования и лучшие практики для инструментов, страниц настроек и интерфейсов данных, используя протоколы, такие как HTML и CSS, для бесшовной интеграции.","ar":"تمكن العميل من إنشاء واجهات مستخدم متسقة ومرنة باستخدام أنماط التصميم وأفضل الممارسات للأدوات وصفحات الإعدادات وواجهات البيانات، واستخدام بروتوكولات مثل HTML و CSS من أجل التكامل السلس."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing responsive dashboards","Generating admin panel layouts","Creating consistent data interfaces"],"zh":["设计响应式仪表盘","生成管理面板布局","创建一致的数据接口"],"ja":["レスポンシブなダッシュボードの設計","管理パネルのレイアウトの生成","一貫性のあるデータインターフェイスの作成"],"ko":["반응형 대시보드 설계","관리 패널 레이아웃 생성","일관된 데이터 인터페이스 생성"],"es":["Diseñar paneles de control responsivos","Generar diseños de paneles de administración","Crear interfaces de datos consistentes"],"fr":["Concevoir des tableaux de bord réactifs","Générer des dispositions de panneaux d''administration","Créer des interfaces de données cohérentes"],"de":["Reaktive Dashboards entwerfen","Admin-Panel-Layouts generieren","Konsistente Daten-Schnittstellen erstellen"],"pt":["Projeto de dashboards responsivos","Geração de layouts de painéis de administração","Criação de interfaces de dados consistentes"],"ru":["Проектирование адаптивных панелей управления","Генерация макетов административных панелей","Создание последовательных интерфейсов данных"],"ar":["تصميم لوحات القيادة المرنة","توليد تخطيطات لوحات التحكم الإدارية","إنشاء واجهات بيانات متسقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not suitable for landing pages or marketing sites","Redirects non-dashboard tasks to /frontend-design"],"zh":["不适用于着陆页或营销网站","将非仪表盘任务重定向到/frontend-design"],"ja":["ランディングページやマーケティングサイトには適していない","ダッシュボード以外のタスクを/frontend-designにリダイレクト"],"ko":["랜딩 페이지 또는 마케팅 사이트에 적합하지 않음","대시보드 이외의 작업을 /frontend-design로 리디렉션"],"es":["No es adecuado para páginas de destino o sitios de marketing","Redirige tareas no de panel de control a /frontend-design"],"fr":["N''est pas adapté pour les pages de destination ou les sites de marketing","Redirige les tâches non de tableau de bord vers /frontend-design"],"de":["Nicht geeignet für Ziel- oder Marketingseiten","Leitet Nicht-Dashboard-Aufgaben an /frontend-design weiter"],"pt":["Não é adequado para páginas de destino ou sites de marketing","Redireciona tarefas não relacionadas a dashboards para /frontend-design"],"ru":["Не подходит для посадочных страниц или сайтов маркетинга","Перенаправляет задачи, не связанные с панелями управления, в /frontend-design"],"ar":["لا يصلح للصفحات المستهدفة أو المواقع التسويقية","يحول المهام غير المرتبطة باللوحات إلى /frontend-design"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block/inngest', 'community', 'andre-sugai', 'cine-explorer-mvp-block', 'andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block', 'inngest', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z', '2026-02-18T09:33:08.269Z', NULL, '{"id":"andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block/inngest","name":"inngest","description":{"zh":"Inngest是一种可靠的后台处理工具，支持serverless工作流和长时间运行的工作流程","ja":"Inngestは信頼性の高いバックグラウンド処理ツールで、サーバーレスワークフローと長時間実行するワークフローをサポート","ko":"Inngest는 신뢰할 수 있는 백그라운드 처리 도구로서 서버리스 워크플로와 장기간 실행되는 워크플로를 지원","es":"Inngest es una herramienta para crear flujos de trabajo duraderos y escalables sin necesidad de gestionar infraestructura. Permite la creación de pipelines de AI y flujos de trabajo complejos.","fr":"Inngest est un outil pour créer des flux de travail durables et évolutifs sans nécessité de gérer l''infrastructure. Il permet la création de pipelines d''IA et de flux de travail complexes.","de":"Inngest ist ein Tool zum Erstellen dauerhafter und skalierbarer Workflows ohne die Notwendigkeit, Infrastruktur zu verwalten. Es ermöglicht die Erstellung von AI-Pipelines und komplexen Workflows.","pt":"Inngest é uma solução para processamento em segundo plano que permite criar fluxos de trabalho duráveis e confiáveis sem gerenciamento de infraestrutura.","ru":"Inngest - это решение для фоновой обработки, которое позволяет создавать надежные и долгосрочные рабочие процессы без управления инфраструктурой.","ar":"إنغست هو حل لمعالجة الخلفية يسمح بإنشاء سير عمل دائم وموثوق بدون إدارة البنية التحتية","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Inngest集成：可靠的后台处理","ja":"Inngest統合：信頼性の高いバックグラウンド処理","ko":"Inngest 통합: 신뢰할 수 있는 백그라운드 처리","es":"Inngest: Procesamiento en segundo plano sin infraestructura","fr":"Inngest : Traitement en arrière-plan sans infrastructure","de":"Inngest: Hintergrundverarbeitung ohne Infrastruktur","pt":"Inngest: Processamento em Segundo Plano Confiável","ru":"Inngest: Надежная Фоновая Обработка","ar":"إنغست: معالجة خلفية موثوقة","en":"inngest"},"description":{"zh":"Inngest是一种可靠的后台处理工具，支持serverless工作流和长时间运行的工作流程","ja":"Inngestは信頼性の高いバックグラウンド処理ツールで、サーバーレスワークフローと長時間実行するワークフローをサポート","ko":"Inngest는 신뢰할 수 있는 백그라운드 처리 도구로서 서버리스 워크플로와 장기간 실행되는 워크플로를 지원","es":"Inngest es una herramienta para crear flujos de trabajo duraderos y escalables sin necesidad de gestionar infraestructura. Permite la creación de pipelines d...","fr":"Inngest est un outil pour créer des flux de travail durables et évolutifs sans nécessité de gérer l''infrastructure. Il permet la création de pipelines d''IA e...","de":"Inngest ist ein Tool zum Erstellen dauerhafter und skalierbarer Workflows ohne die Notwendigkeit, Infrastruktur zu verwalten. Es ermöglicht die Erstellung vo...","pt":"Inngest é uma solução para processamento em segundo plano que permite criar fluxos de trabalho duráveis e confiáveis sem gerenciamento de infraestrutura.","ru":"Inngest - это решение для фоновой обработки, которое позволяет создавать надежные и долгосрочные рабочие процессы без управления инфраструктурой.","ar":"إنغست هو حل لمعالجة الخلفية يسمح بإنشاء سير عمل دائم وموثوق بدون إدارة البنية التحتية","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持serverless工作流","长时间运行的工作流程","事件驱动系统","可靠的后台处理","AI管道支持","入门流程支持"],"ja":["サーバーレスワークフローのサポート","長時間実行するワークフロー","イベントドリブンシステム","信頼性の高いバックグラウンド処理","AIパイプラインのサポート","オンボーディングフローのサポート"],"ko":["서버리스 워크플로 지원","장기간 실행되는 워크플로","이벤트驱动 시스템","신뢰할 수 있는 백그라운드 처리","AI 파이프라인 지원","온보딩 플로우 지원"],"es":["Procesamiento en segundo plano sin infraestructura","Flujos de trabajo duraderos y escalables","Creación de pipelines de AI","Flujos de trabajo complejos","Tolerancia a fallos y recuperación automática"],"fr":["Traitement en arrière-plan sans infrastructure","Flux de travail durables et évolutifs","Création de pipelines d''IA","Flux de travail complexes","Tolérance aux pannes et récupération automatique"],"de":["Hintergrundverarbeitung ohne Infrastruktur","Dauerhafte und skalierbare Workflows","Erstellung von AI-Pipelines","Komplexe Workflows","Fehlertoleranz und automatische Wiederherstellung"],"pt":["Processamento em segundo plano confiável","Fluxos de trabalho duráveis e longos","Sistemas acionados por eventos","Checkpoints para sobrevivência a falhas","Integração com pipelines de AI","Onboarding de fluxos que abrangem dias"],"ru":["Надежная фоновая обработка","Долгосрочные и надежные рабочие процессы","Системы, запускаемые событиями","Контрольные точки для выживания при сбоях","Интеграция с конвейерами ИИ","Ввод в эксплуатацию потоков, охватывающих дни"],"ar":["معالجة خلفية موثوقة","سير عمل دائم وموثوق","أنظمة مدفوعة بالأحداث","نقاط تحقق للبقاء عند الفشل","التكامل مع خطوط أنابيب الذكاء الاصطناعي","تشغيل سير العمل التي تمتد لعدة أيام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Inngest","serverless","后台处理","工作流程","事件驱动系统","AI管道","入门流程","可靠性"],"ja":["Inngest","サーバーレス","バックグラウンド処理","ワークフロー","イベントドリブンシステム","AIパイプライン","オンボーディングフロー","信頼性"],"ko":["Inngest","서버리스","백그라운드 처리","워크플로","이벤트驱동 시스템","AI 파이프라인","온보딩 플로우","신뢰성"],"es":["inngest","procesamiento en segundo plano","flujos de trabajo duraderos","pipelines de ai","tolerancia a fallos","escalabilidad","infrastructure como servicio","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["inngest","traitement en arrière-plan","flux de travail durables","pipelines d''ia","tolérance aux pannes","évolvabilité","infrastructure en tant que service","développement de logiciels"],"de":["inngest","hintergrundverarbeitung","dauerhafte workflows","ai-pipelines","fehlertoleranz","skalierbarkeit","infrastructure als service","softwareentwicklung"],"pt":["inngest","processamento em segundo plano","fluxos de trabalho duráveis","sistemas acionados por eventos","pipelines de AI","onboarding de fluxos","infraestrutura como serviço","serviços de nuvem"],"ru":["inngest","фоновая обработка","долгосрочные рабочие процессы","системы, запускаемые событиями","конвейеры ИИ","ввод в эксплуатацию потоков","инфраструктура как сервис","облачные сервисы"],"ar":["إنغست","معالجة خلفية","سير عمل دائم","أنظمة مدفوعة بالأحداث","خطوط أنابيب الذكاء الاصطناعي","تشغيل سير العمل","البنية التحتية كخدمة","خدمات السحابة"]}},"owner":"andre-sugai","repo":"cine-explorer-mvp-block","repoPath":"andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.478Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"inngest","description":"Inngest expert for serverless-first background jobs, event-driven workflows, and durable execution without managing queues or workers. Use when: inngest, serverless background job, event-driven workflow, step function, durable execution.","bodyPreview":"# Inngest Integration\n\nYou are an Inngest expert who builds reliable background processing without\nmanaging infrastructure. You understand that serverless doesn''t mean you can''t\nhave durable, long-running workflows - it means you don''t manage the workers.\n\nYou''ve built AI pipelines that take minutes, onboarding flows that span days,\nand event-driven systems that process millions of events. You know that the\nmagic of Inngest is in its steps - each one a checkpoint that survives failures.\n\nYour co","body":"# Inngest Integration\n\nYou are an Inngest expert who builds reliable background processing without\nmanaging infrastructure. You understand that serverless doesn''t mean you can''t\nhave durable, long-running workflows - it means you don''t manage the workers.\n\nYou''ve built AI pipelines that take minutes, onboarding flows that span days,\nand event-driven systems that process millions of events. You know that the\nmagic of Inngest is in its steps - each one a checkpoint that survives failures.\n\nYour core philosophy:\n1. Event\n\n## Capabilities\n\n- inngest-functions\n- event-driven-workflows\n- step-functions\n- serverless-background-jobs\n- durable-sleep\n- fan-out-patterns\n- concurrency-control\n- scheduled-functions\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Basic Function Setup\n\nInngest function with typed events in Next.js\n\n### Multi-Step Workflow\n\nComplex workflow with parallel steps and error handling\n\n### Scheduled/Cron Functions\n\nFunctions that run on a schedule\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### ❌ Not Using Steps\n\n### ❌ Huge Event Payloads\n\n### ❌ Ignoring Concurrency\n\n## Related Skills\n\nWorks well with: `nextjs-app-router`, `vercel-deployment`, `supabase-backend`, `email-systems`, `ai-agents-architect`, `stripe-integration`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:33:08.269Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Workflow Automation Agents needing reliable background processing and durable, long-running workflows without managing infrastructure.","zh":"非常适合需要可靠的后台处理和长时间运行工作流的工作流自动化代理，不需要管理基础设施。","ja":"インフラストラクチャの管理不要で、信頼性の高いバックグラウンド処理と長時間実行されるワークフローが必要なワークフローオートメーションエージェントに最適。","ko":"인프라 관리가 필요하지 않은 안정적인 백그라운드 처리와 장시간 실행되는 워크플로우가 필요한 워크플로 자동화 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de automatización de flujo de trabajo que necesitan un procesamiento en segundo plano confiable y flujos de trabajo duraderos y de larga duración sin administrar infraestructura.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''automatisation de workflow nécessitant un traitement en arrière-plan fiable et des flux de travail durables et à long terme sans gérer d''infrastructure.","de":"Perfekt für Workflow-Automatisierungsagenten, die zuverlässige Hintergrundverarbeitung und langlebige, lang laufende Workflows ohne Infrastrukturverwaltung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Automação de Fluxo de Trabalho que necessitam de processamento em segundo plano confiável e fluxos de trabalho duráveis e de longa duração sem gerenciar infraestrutura.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации рабочих процессов, которым требуется надежная фоновая обработка и долгосрочные рабочие процессы без управления инфраструктурой.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل آلي للتشغيل الآلي التي تحتاج إلى معالجة موثوقة في الخلفية وعمليات عمل متينة وطويلة الأمد دون الحاجة إلى إدارة البنية التحتية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build serverless workflows with durable, long-running processes, leveraging Inngest''s checkpoint-based steps for failure survival and event-driven systems processing millions of events, utilizing protocols like serverless architecture.","zh":"赋予代理构建无服务器工作流的能力，具有持久的长时间运行的进程，利用Inngest的基于检查点的步骤来实现故障恢复和处理数百万事件的事件驱动系统，使用无服务器架构等协议。","ja":"エージェントがサーバーレスワークフローを構築できるようにし、チェックポイントベースのステップを使用して長時間実行されるプロセスを実現し、数百万のイベントを処理するイベント駆動型システムで障害耐性を実現し、サーバーレスアーキテクチャなどのプロトコルを利用する。","ko":"에이전트가 서버리스 워크플로를 구축할 수 있도록 하며, 체크포인트 기반 단계를 사용하여 장시간 실행되는 프로세스를 구현하고, 수백만 개의 이벤트를 처리하는 이벤트 驱动 시스템에서 장애 생존성을 달성하며, 서버리스 아키텍처 등의 프로토콜을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear flujos de trabajo sin servidor con procesos duraderos y de larga duración, aprovechando los pasos basados en puntos de control de Inngest para la supervivencia a fallos y el procesamiento de sistemas orientados a eventos que procesan millones de eventos, utilizando protocolos como arquitectura sin servidor.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des flux de travail sans serveur avec des processus durables et à long terme, en exploitant les étapes basées sur les points de contrôle d''Inngest pour la survie aux défaillances et le traitement des systèmes à base d''événements traitant des millions d''événements, en utilisant des protocoles tels que l''architecture sans serveur.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, serverlose Workflows mit langlebigen, lang laufenden Prozessen zu erstellen, indem es die schrittweise, auf Prüfpunkten basierende Ausführung von Inngest für die Überlebensfähigkeit bei Fehlern und die Verarbeitung von ereignisgesteuerten Systemen, die Millionen von Ereignissen verarbeiten, nutzt und Protokolle wie serverlose Architektur verwendet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir fluxos de trabalho sem servidor com processos duráveis e de longa duração, aproveitando as etapas baseadas em pontos de verificação da Inngest para sobrevivência a falhas e processamento de sistemas orientados a eventos que processam milhões de eventos, utilizando protocolos como arquitetura sem servidor.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать серверные рабочие процессы с долгосрочными процессами, использующими шаги на основе контрольных точек Inngest для выживания при сбоях и обработки событийных систем, обрабатывающих миллионы событий, используя протоколы, такие как архитектура без сервера.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من بناء تدفقات عمل بدون خادم مع عمليات متينة وطويلة الأمد، مستفيدة من خطوات إنجيست القائمة على نقاط التحقق للتغلب على الأعطال ومعالجة أنظمة مستندة إلى الأحداث التي تعالج ملايين الأحداث، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل هندسة بلا خادم."},"useCases":{"en":["Building AI pipelines that take minutes to complete","Creating onboarding flows that span days","Processing millions of events with event-driven systems"],"zh":["构建需要几分钟才能完成的AI管道","创建需要数天才能完成的入职流程","使用事件驱动系统处理数百万个事件"],"ja":["数分で完了するAIパイプラインの構築","数日で完了するオンボーディングフローの作成","イベント駆動型システムを使用した数百万イベントの処理"],"ko":["수분 내에 완료되는 AI 파이프라인 구축","수일 내에 완료되는 온보딩 흐름 생성","이벤트 드리븐 시스템을 사용한 수백만 개의 이벤트 처리"],"es":["Crear tuberías de IA que tardan minutos en completarse","Crear flujos de incorporación que abarcan días","Procesar millones de eventos con sistemas orientados a eventos"],"fr":["Créer des pipelines d''IA qui prennent quelques minutes pour se compléter","Créer des flux d''intégration qui s''étendent sur plusieurs jours","Traiter des millions d''événements avec des systèmes à base d''événements"],"de":["Erstellen von KI-Pipelines, die Minuten dauern, um abgeschlossen zu werden","Erstellen von Onboarding-Fluss, der sich über Tage erstreckt","Verarbeiten von Millionen von Ereignissen mit ereignisgesteuerten Systemen"],"pt":["Construir pipelines de IA que levam minutos para ser concluídas","Criar fluxos de integração que abrangem dias","Processar milhões de eventos com sistemas orientados a eventos"],"ru":["Построение конвейеров ИИ, которые занимают минуты для завершения","Создание потоков интеграции, которые охватывают дни","Обработка миллионов событий с событийными системами"],"ar":["بناء خطوط أنابيب ذكاء اصطناعي تستغرق دقائق لإكمالها","إنشاء تدفقات للتسجيل التي تمتد لأيام","معالجة ملايين الأحداث بنظم مبنية على الأحداث"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Inngest integration","Serverless architecture only","Dependent on step-based workflow design"],"zh":["需要Inngest集成","仅支持服务器less架构","依赖于基于步骤的工作流设计"],"ja":["Inngest統合が必要","サーバーレスアーキテクチャのみのサポート","ステップベースのワークフロー設計への依存"],"ko":["Inngest 통합이 필요합니다","서버리스 아키텍처만 지원합니다","단계 기반 워크플로우 디자인에 의존합니다"],"es":["Requiere integración con Inngest","Solo arquitectura sin servidor","Dependiente del diseño de flujo de trabajo basado en pasos"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration à Inngest","Architecture sans serveur uniquement","Dépendant de la conception de flux de travail basée sur les étapes"],"de":["Benötigt Inngest-Integration","Nur serverlose Architektur","Abhängig vom schrittweisen Workflow-Design"],"pt":["Requer integração com a Inngest","Arquitetura sem servidor apenas","Dependente do design de fluxo de trabalho baseado em etapas"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с Inngest","Только архитектура без сервера","Зависит от дизайна рабочего процесса на основе шагов"],"ar":["يتطلب دمجًا مع إنجيست","هندسة بلا خادم فقط","يعتمد على تصميم سير عمل قائم على الخطوات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
