자 경험 향상","검색 엔진 순위 모니터링과 분석"],"es":["Identificación de problemas de SEO","Recomendaciones personalizadas para mejorar el rendimiento","Análisis de la estructura del sitio web","Evaluación de la optimización de contenido","Análisis de enlaces y autoridad del sitio web"],"fr":["Identification des problèmes de SEO","Recommandations personnalisées pour améliorer les performances","Analyse de la structure du site web","Évaluation de l''optimisation du contenu","Analyse des liens et de l''autorité du site web"],"de":["Identifizierung von SEO-Problemen","Individuelle Empfehlungen zur Leistungsverbesserung","Analyse der Website-Struktur","Bewertung der Inhalts-Optimierung","Analyse von Links und Website-Autorität"],"pt":["Análise de problemas de SEO","Recomendações para melhorar o desempenho de busca","Identificação de oportunidades de otimização","Análise de site context","Verificação de product marketing context"],"ru":["Анализ проблем с SEO","Рекомендации для улучшения органического поиска","Выявление возможностей оптимизации","Анализ контекста сайта","Проверка контекста маркетинга продукта"],"ar":["تحليل مشاكل محركات البحث","توصيات لتحسين البحث العضوي","تحديد فرص التحسين","تحليل سياق الموقع","التحقق من سياق تسويق المنتج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SEO审计","搜索引擎优化","网站优化","关键词优化","元标签优化","页面加载速度","用户体验"],"ja":["SEOオーディット","検索エンジン最適化","ウェブサイト最適化","キーワード最適化","メタタグ最適化","ページロード速度","ユーザーエクスペリエンス"],"ko":["SEO 감사","검색 엔진 최적화","웹사이트 최적화","키워드 최적화","메타 태그 최적화","페이지 로드 속도","사용자 경험"],"es":["análisis de SEO","optimización de motores de búsqueda","mejora de posicionamiento","recomendaciones de SEO","problemas de SEO","audit de SEO"],"fr":["audit SEO","optimisation des moteurs de recherche","amélioration du référencement","recommandations SEO","problèmes de SEO","analyse de SEO"],"de":["SEO-Analyse","Suchmaschinen-Optimierung","Leistungsverbesserung","SEO-Empfehlungen","SEO-Probleme","SEO-Audit"],"pt":["SEO Audit","Otimização de Motores de Busca","Análise de SEO","Melhoria de Desempenho de Busca","Visibilidade do Site","Otimização Técnica"],"ru":["Аудит SEO","Оптимизация поисковых систем","Анализ SEO","Улучшение органического поиска","Видимость сайта","Техническая оптимизация"],"ar":["تحليل محركات البحث","تحسين محرك البحث","تحليل محركات البحث","تحسين البحث العضوي","وضوح الموقع","التحسين الفني"]}},"owner":"RexO77","repo":"axiomUI","repoPath":"RexO77/axiomUI","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"seo-audit","description":"When the user wants to audit, review, or diagnose SEO issues on their site. Also use when the user mentions SEO audit, technical SEO, why am I not ranking, SEO issues, on-page SEO, meta tags review, or SEO health check. For building pages at scale to target keywords, see programmatic-seo. For adding structured data, see schema-markup.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (Sa","body":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (SaaS, e-commerce, blog, etc.)\n   - What''s the primary business goal for SEO?\n   - What keywords/topics are priorities?\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - Any known issues or concerns?\n   - Current organic traffic level?\n   - Recent changes or migrations?\n\n3. **Scope**\n   - Full site audit or specific pages?\n   - Technical + on-page, or one focus area?\n   - Access to Search Console / analytics?\n\n---\n\n## Audit Framework\n\n### Priority Order\n1. **Crawlability & Indexation** (can Google find and index it?)\n2. **Technical Foundations** (is the site fast and functional?)\n3. **On-Page Optimization** (is content optimized?)\n4. **Content Quality** (does it deserve to rank?)\n5. **Authority & Links** (does it have credibility?)\n\n---\n\n## Technical SEO Audit\n\n### Crawlability\n\n**Robots.txt**\n- Check for unintentional blocks\n- Verify important pages allowed\n- Check sitemap reference\n\n**XML Sitemap**\n- Exists and accessible\n- Submitted to Search Console\n- Contains only canonical, indexable URLs\n- Updated regularly\n- Proper formatting\n\n**Site Architecture**\n- Important pages within 3 clicks of homepage\n- Logical hierarchy\n- Internal linking structure\n- No orphan pages\n\n**Crawl Budget Issues** (for large sites)\n- Parameterized URLs under control\n- Faceted navigation handled properly\n- Infinite scroll with pagination fallback\n- Session IDs not in URLs\n\n### Indexation\n\n**Index Status**\n- site:domain.com check\n- Search Console coverage report\n- Compare indexed vs. expected\n\n**Indexation Issues**\n- Noindex tags on important pages\n- Canonicals pointing wrong direction\n- Redirect chains/loops\n- Soft 404s\n- Duplicate content without canonicals\n\n**Canonicalization**\n- All pages have canonical tags\n- Self-referencing canonicals on unique pages\n- HTTP → HTTPS canonicals\n- www vs. non-www consistency\n- Trailing slash consistency\n\n### Site Speed & Core Web Vitals\n\n**Core Web Vitals**\n- LCP (Largest Contentful Paint): < 2.5s\n- INP (Interaction to Next Paint): < 200ms\n- CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift): < 0.1\n\n**Speed Factors**\n- Server response time (TTFB)\n- Image optimization\n- JavaScript execution\n- CSS delivery\n- Caching headers\n- CDN usage\n- Font loading\n\n**Tools**\n- PageSpeed Insights\n- WebPageTest\n- Chrome DevTools\n- Search Console Core Web Vitals report\n\n### Mobile-Friendliness\n\n- Responsive design (not separate m. site)\n- Tap target sizes\n- Viewport configured\n- No horizontal scroll\n- Same content as desktop\n- Mobile-first indexing readiness\n\n### Security & HTTPS\n\n- HTTPS across entire site\n- Valid SSL certificate\n- No mixed content\n- HTTP → HTTPS redirects\n- HSTS header (bonus)\n\n### URL Structure\n\n- Readable, descriptive URLs\n- Keywords in URLs where natural\n- Consistent structure\n- No unnecessary parameters\n- Lowercase and hyphen-separated\n\n---\n\n## On-Page SEO Audit\n\n### Title Tags\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique titles for each page\n- Primary keyword near beginning\n- 50-60 characters (visible in SERP)\n- Compelling and click-worthy\n- Brand name placement (end, usually)\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate titles\n- Too long (truncated)\n- Too short (wasted opportunity)\n- Keyword stuffing\n- Missing entirely\n\n### Meta Descriptions\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique descriptions per page\n- 150-160 characters\n- Includes primary keyword\n- Clear value proposition\n- Call to action\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate descriptions\n- Auto-generated garbage\n- Too long/short\n- No compelling reason to click\n\n### Heading Structure\n\n**Check for:**\n- One H1 per page\n- H1 contains primary keyword\n- Logical hierarchy (H1 → H2 → H3)\n- Headings describe content\n- Not just for styling\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Multiple H1s\n- Skip levels (H1 → H3)\n- Headings used for styling only\n- No H1 on page\n\n### Content Optimization\n\n**Primary Page Content**\n- Keyword in first 100 words\n- Related keywords naturally used\n- Sufficient depth/length for topic\n- Answers search intent\n- Better than competitors\n\n**Thin Content Issues**\n- Pages with little unique content\n- Tag/category pages with no value\n- Doorway pages\n- Duplicate or near-duplicate content\n\n### Image Optimization\n\n**Check for:**\n- Descriptive file names\n- Alt text on all images\n- Alt text describes image\n- Compressed file sizes\n- Modern formats (WebP)\n- Lazy loading implemented\n- Responsive images\n\n### Internal Linking\n\n**Check for:**\n- Important pages well-linked\n- Descriptive anchor text\n- Logical link relationships\n- No broken internal links\n- Reasonable link count per page\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Orphan pages (no internal links)\n- Over-optimized anchor text\n- Important pages buried\n- Excessive footer/sidebar links\n\n### Keyword Targeting\n\n**Per Page**\n- Clear primary keyword target\n- Title, H1, URL aligned\n- Content satisfies search intent\n- Not competing with other pages (cannibalization)\n\n**Site-Wide**\n- Keyword mapping document\n- No major gaps in coverage\n- No keyword cannibalization\n- Logical topical clusters\n\n---\n\n## Content Quality Assessment\n\n### E-E-A-T Signals\n\n**Experience**\n- First-hand experience demonstrated\n- Original insights/data\n- Real examples and case studies\n\n**Expertise**\n- Author credentials visible\n- Accurate, detailed information\n- Properly sourced claims\n\n**Authoritativeness**\n- Recognized in the space\n- Cited by others\n- Industry credentials\n\n**Trustworthiness**\n- Accurate information\n- Transparent about business\n- Contact information available\n- Privacy policy, terms\n- Secure site (HTTPS)\n\n### Content Depth\n\n- Comprehensive coverage of topic\n- Answers follow-up questions\n- Better than top-ranking competitors\n- Updated and current\n\n### User Engagement Signals\n\n- Time on page\n- Bounce rate in context\n- Pages per session\n- Return visits\n\n---\n\n## Common Issues by Site Type\n\n### SaaS/Product Sites\n- Product pages lack content depth\n- Blog not integrated with product pages\n- Missing comparison/alternative pages\n- Feature pages thin on content\n- No glossary/educational content\n\n### E-commerce\n- Thin category pages\n- Duplicate product descriptions\n- Missing product schema\n- Faceted navigation creating duplicates\n- Out-of-stock pages mishandled\n\n### Content/Blog Sites\n- Outdated content not refreshed\n- Keyword cannibalization\n- No topical clustering\n- Poor internal linking\n- Missing author pages\n\n### Local Business\n- Inconsistent NAP\n- Missing local schema\n- No Google Business Profile optimization\n- Missing location pages\n- No local content\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Audit Report Structure\n\n**Executive Summary**\n- Overall health assessment\n- Top 3-5 priority issues\n- Quick wins identified\n\n**Technical SEO Findings**\nFor each issue:\n- **Issue**: What''s wrong\n- **Impact**: SEO impact (High/Medium/Low)\n- **Evidence**: How you found it\n- **Fix**: Specific recommendation\n- **Priority**: 1-5 or High/Medium/Low\n\n**On-Page SEO Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Content Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Prioritized Action Plan**\n1. Critical fixes (blocking indexation/ranking)\n2. High-impact improvements\n3. Quick wins (easy, immediate benefit)\n4. Long-term recommendations\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- [AI Writing Detection](references/ai-writing-detection.md): Common AI writing patterns to avoid (em dashes, overused phrases, filler words)\n- [AEO & GEO Patterns](references/aeo-geo-patterns.md): Content patterns optimized for answer engines and AI citation\n\n---\n\n## Tools Referenced\n\n**Free Tools**\n- Google Search Console (essential)\n- Google PageSpeed Insights\n- Bing Webmaster Tools\n- Rich Results Test\n- Mobile-Friendly Test\n- Schema Validator\n\n**Paid Tools** (if available)\n- Screaming Frog\n- Ahrefs / Semrush\n- Sitebulb\n- ContentKing\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What pages/keywords matter most?\n2. Do you have Search Console access?\n3. Any recent changes or migrations?\n4. Who are your top organic competitors?\n5. What''s your current organic traffic baseline?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **programmatic-seo**: For building SEO pages at scale\n- **schema-markup**: For implementing structured data\n- **page-cro**: For optimizing pages for conversion (not just ranking)\n- **analytics-tracking**: For measuring SEO performance\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:33:34.787Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Digital Marketing Agents needing advanced SEO analysis capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 SEO 分析能力的数字营销代理。","ja":"デジタルマーケティングエージェントが高度な SEO 分析機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 SEO 분석 기능이 필요한 디지털 마케팅 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de marketing digital que necesitan capacidades de análisis de SEO avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de marketing numérique ayant besoin de capacités d''analyse de SEO avancées.","de":"Perfekt für digitale Marketing-Agenten, die erweiterte SEO-Analysefunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Marketing Digital que precisam de capacidades avançadas de análise de SEO.","ru":"Идеально для агентов цифрового маркетинга, которым необходимы расширенные возможности анализа SEO.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التسويقيين الرقميين الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات تحليل متقدمة لتحسين محركات البحث."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations using site context, product marketing context, and technical SEO audits, leveraging files like `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` and analyzing site types, layouts, and system logic.","zh":"赋予代理识别 SEO 问题和提供可执行建议的能力，利用站点上下文、产品营销上下文和技术 SEO 审计，利用诸如 `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` 之类的文件，并分析站点类型、布局和系统逻辑。","ja":"エージェントが SEO の問題を特定し、サイトのコンテキスト、製品マーケティングコンテキスト、技術 SEO 監査を利用して実行可能な推奨事項を提供する能力を付与します。`.claude/product-marketing-context.md` などのファイルを利用し、サイトタイプ、レイアウト、システムロジックを分析します。","ko":"에이전트가 SEO 문제를 식별하고 사이트 컨텍스트, 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트, 기술 SEO 감사를 사용하여 실행 가능한 추천을 제공할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`와 같은 파일을 활용하고 사이트 유형, 레이아웃, 시스템 논리를 분석합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes identificar problemas de SEO y proporcionar recomendaciones con acciones utilizando el contexto del sitio, el contexto de marketing de productos y auditorías de SEO técnicas, aprovechando archivos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` y analizando los tipos de sitios, diseños y lógica del sistema.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les problèmes de SEO et de fournir des recommandations avec des actions en utilisant le contexte du site, le contexte de marketing de produits et les audits de SEO techniques, en exploitant des fichiers tels que `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` et en analysant les types de sites, les dispositions et la logique du système.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, SEO-Probleme zu identifizieren und handhabbare Empfehlungen unter Verwendung des Seitenkontexts, des Produktmarketing-Kontexts und technischer SEO-Audits zu liefern, indem Dateien wie `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` genutzt und Seitentypen, Layouts und Systemlogik analysiert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar problemas de SEO e fornecer recomendações eficazes usando o contexto do site, o contexto de marketing de produtos e auditorias técnicas de SEO, aproveitando arquivos como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` e analisando tipos de sites, layouts e lógica do sistema.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять проблемы SEO и предоставлять действенные рекомендации, используя контекст сайта, контекст маркетинга продукции и технические аудиты SEO, опираясь на файлы типа `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` и анализируя типы сайтов, макеты и системную логику.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تحديد مشاكل تحسين محركات البحث وتقديم توصيات قابلة للتنفيذ باستخدام سياق الموقع وسياق تسويق المنتج واضبطات تحسين محركات البحث الفنية، مستفيدا من الملفات مثل `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` وتحليل أنواع المواقع والتصاميم ومنطق النظام."},"useCases":{"en":["Auditing website layouts for SEO optimization","Analyzing site context for improved search performance","Generating recommendations for color, typography, and component adjustments"],"zh":["审计网站布局以优化 SEO","分析网站上下文以提高搜索性能","生成颜色、字体、组件调整的建议"],"ja":["SEO 最適化のために Web サイトのレイアウトを監査する","検索パフォーマンスを向上させるためにサイトコンテキストを分析する","色、字体、コンポーネント調整の推奨事項を生成する"],"ko":["SEO 최적화를 위해 웹사이트 레이아웃을 감사하는 것","검색 성능을 개선하기 위해 사이트 컨텍스트를 분석하는 것","색상, 글꼴, 구성 요소 조정에 대한 추천을 생성하는 것"],"es":["Auditoría de diseños de sitios web para la optimización de SEO","Análisis del contexto del sitio para una mejor búsqueda de rendimiento","Generación de recomendaciones para ajustes de color, tipografía y componentes"],"fr":["Audit des dispositions de sites web pour l''optimisation de SEO","Analyse du contexte du site pour une meilleure performance de recherche","Génération de recommandations pour des ajustements de couleur, de typographie et de composants"],"de":["Prüfung von Website-Layouts für die SEO-Optimierung","Analyse des Seitenkontexts für eine verbesserte Suchleistung","Erzeugung von Empfehlungen für Farb-, Typografie- und Komponenten-Anpassungen"],"pt":["Auditoria de layouts de sites para otimização de SEO","Análise do contexto do site para melhoria do desempenho de busca","Geração de recomendações para ajustes de cor, tipografia e componentes"],"ru":["Аудит макетов сайтов для оптимизации SEO","Анализ контекста сайта для улучшения результатов поиска","Генерация рекомендаций для корректировки цвета, типографики и компонентов"],"ar":["تدقيق تصاميم مواقع الويب لتحسين تحسين محركات البحث","تحليل سياق الموقع لتحسين أداء البحث","توليد التوصيات لتعديلات الألوان والكتابة والعناصر"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to site context and product marketing context files","Limited to analyzing sites with available `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` files"],"zh":["需要访问站点上下文和产品营销上下文文件","仅限分析具有 `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` 文件的站点"],"ja":["サイトコンテキストと製品マーケティングコンテキストファイルへのアクセスが必要","`.claude/product-marketing-context.md` ファイルを持つサイトのみを分析可能"],"ko":["사이트 컨텍스트와 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다.","`.claude/product-marketing-context.md` 파일을 갖는 사이트만 분석 가능합니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a archivos de contexto del sitio y contexto de marketing de productos","Limitado a analizar sitios con archivos `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` disponibles"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux fichiers de contexte du site et de contexte de marketing de produits","Limité à l''analyse des sites avec des fichiers `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` disponibles"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Seitenkontext- und Produktmarketing-Kontext-Dateien","Begrenzt auf die Analyse von Seiten mit verfügbaren `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`-Dateien"],"pt":["Requer acesso a arquivos de contexto do site e contexto de marketing de produtos","Limitado à análise de sites com arquivos `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` disponíveis"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файлам контекста сайта и контекста маркетинга продукции","Ограничен анализом сайтов с доступными файлами `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملفات سياق الموقع وسياق تسويق المنتج","محدود بتحليل المواقع التي تحتوي على ملفات `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` المتاحة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cbemstar/thestash.xyz/seo-audit', 'community', 'cbemstar', 'thestash.xyz', 'cbemstar/thestash.xyz', 'seo-audit', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z', '2026-02-18T09:33:49.673Z', NULL, '{"id":"cbemstar/thestash.xyz/seo-audit","name":"seo-audit","description":{"zh":"SEO1-2","ja":"SEO","ko":"SEO50-80","es":"Análisis de SEO para identificar problemas y mejorar el rendimiento de búsqueda orgánica","fr":"Audit SEO pour identifier les problèmes et améliorer les performances de recherche organique","de":"SEO-Analyse zur Identifizierung von Problemen und Verbesserung der organischen Suchleistung","pt":"A análise de SEO é um processo que identifica problemas de otimização e fornece recomendações para melhorar o desempenho de busca do seu site.","ru":"Аудит SEO - это процесс, который выявляет проблемы оптимизации и предоставляет рекомендации для улучшения результатов поиска вашего сайта.","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث هو عملية تحدد مشاكل التحسين وتقدم توصيات لتحسين أداء البحث لموقعك الإلكتروني.","en":"Stashing all of the web resource into a single place because let''s face it, Slack is not the best place for it."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"SEOAudit","ja":"SEO","ko":"SEO","es":"Análisis de SEO para desarrolladores","fr":"Audit SEO pour les développeurs","de":"SEO-Analyse für Entwickler","pt":"Análise de SEO: Otimização do Desempenho de Busca","ru":"Аудит SEO: Улучшение Результатов Поиска","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث: تحسين أداء البحث","en":"seo-audit"},"description":{"zh":"SEO1-2","ja":"SEO","ko":"SEO50-80","es":"Análisis de SEO para identificar problemas y mejorar el rendimiento de búsqueda orgánica","fr":"Audit SEO pour identifier les problèmes et améliorer les performances de recherche organique","de":"SEO-Analyse zur Identifizierung von Problemen und Verbesserung der organischen Suchleistung","pt":"A análise de SEO é um processo que identifica problemas de otimização e fornece recomendações para melhorar o desempenho de busca do seu site.","ru":"Аудит SEO - это процесс, который выявляет проблемы оптимизации и предоставляет рекомендации для улучшения результатов поиска вашего сайта.","ar":"فحص تحسين محركات البحث هو عملية تحدد مشاكل التحسين وتقدم توصيات لتحسين أداء البحث لموقعك الإلكتروني.","en":"Stashing all of the web resource into a single place because let''s face it, Slack is not the best place for it."},"definition":{"en":"Stashing all of the web resource into a single place because let''s face it, Slack is not the best place for it."},"features":{"zh":["SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO"],"ja":["SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO"],"ko":["SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO"],"es":["Identificación de problemas de SEO","Análisis de contexto de sitio web","Recomendaciones para mejorar el rendimiento de búsqueda","Optimización de contenido y estructura de sitio web","Mejora de la experiencia del usuario","Análisis de competidores"],"fr":["Identification des problèmes de SEO","Analyse du contexte du site web","Recommandations pour améliorer les performances de recherche","Optimisation du contenu et de la structure du site web","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur","Analyse des concurrents"],"de":["Identifizierung von SEO-Problemen","Analyse des Kontexts der Website","Empfehlungen zur Verbesserung der Suchleistung","Optimierung von Inhalt und Struktur der Website","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung","Analyse der Wettbewerber"],"pt":["Identificação de problemas de otimização","Análise de estrutura de site","Otimização de conteúdo","Melhoria de meta tags","Análise de links internos e externos"],"ru":["Выявление проблем оптимизации","Анализ структуры сайта","Оптимизация контента","Улучшение meta тегов","Анализ внутренних и внешних ссылок"],"ar":["تحديد مشاكل التحسين","تحليل هيكل الموقع","تحسين المحتوى","تحسين علامات الميتا","تحليل الروابط الداخلية والخارجية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO"],"ja":["SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO"],"ko":["SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO","SEO"],"es":["análisis de SEO","optimización de búsqueda","desarrollo web","mejora de rendimiento","experiencia del usuario","competidores en línea","SEO para desarrolladores","guía de SEO","herramientas de SEO"],"fr":["audit SEO","optimisation de recherche","développement web","amélioration des performances","expérience utilisateur","concurrents en ligne","SEO pour les développeurs","guide SEO","outils SEO"],"de":["SEO-Analyse","Suchmaschinen-Optimierung","Web-Entwicklung","Leistungsverbesserung","Benutzererfahrung","Online-Wettbewerber","SEO für Entwickler","SEO-Leitfaden","SEO-Tools"],"pt":["análise de SEO","otimização de site","desempenho de busca","recomendações de SEO","melhoria de visibilidade online","estratégia de SEO"],"ru":["аудит SEO","оптимизация сайта","результаты поиска","рекомендации SEO","улучшение онлайн-видимости","стратегия SEO"],"ar":["فحص تحسين محركات البحث","تحسين موقع إلكتروني","أداء بحث","توصيات تحسين محركات البحث","تحسين ظهور على الإنترنت","استراتيجية تحسين محركات البحث"]}},"owner":"cbemstar","repo":"thestash.xyz","repoPath":"cbemstar/thestash.xyz","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"seo-audit","description":"When the user wants to audit, review, or diagnose SEO issues on their site. Also use when the user mentions SEO audit, technical SEO, why am I not ranking, SEO issues, on-page SEO, meta tags review, or SEO health check. For building pages at scale to target keywords, see programmatic-seo. For adding structured data, see schema-markup.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (Sa","body":"# SEO Audit\n\nYou are an expert in search engine optimization. Your goal is to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations to improve organic search performance.\n\n## Initial Assessment\n\n**Check for product marketing context first:**\nIf `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` exists, read it before asking questions. Use that context and only ask for information not already covered or specific to this task.\n\nBefore auditing, understand:\n\n1. **Site Context**\n   - What type of site? (SaaS, e-commerce, blog, etc.)\n   - What''s the primary business goal for SEO?\n   - What keywords/topics are priorities?\n\n2. **Current State**\n   - Any known issues or concerns?\n   - Current organic traffic level?\n   - Recent changes or migrations?\n\n3. **Scope**\n   - Full site audit or specific pages?\n   - Technical + on-page, or one focus area?\n   - Access to Search Console / analytics?\n\n---\n\n## Audit Framework\n\n### Priority Order\n1. **Crawlability & Indexation** (can Google find and index it?)\n2. **Technical Foundations** (is the site fast and functional?)\n3. **On-Page Optimization** (is content optimized?)\n4. **Content Quality** (does it deserve to rank?)\n5. **Authority & Links** (does it have credibility?)\n\n---\n\n## Technical SEO Audit\n\n### Crawlability\n\n**Robots.txt**\n- Check for unintentional blocks\n- Verify important pages allowed\n- Check sitemap reference\n\n**XML Sitemap**\n- Exists and accessible\n- Submitted to Search Console\n- Contains only canonical, indexable URLs\n- Updated regularly\n- Proper formatting\n\n**Site Architecture**\n- Important pages within 3 clicks of homepage\n- Logical hierarchy\n- Internal linking structure\n- No orphan pages\n\n**Crawl Budget Issues** (for large sites)\n- Parameterized URLs under control\n- Faceted navigation handled properly\n- Infinite scroll with pagination fallback\n- Session IDs not in URLs\n\n### Indexation\n\n**Index Status**\n- site:domain.com check\n- Search Console coverage report\n- Compare indexed vs. expected\n\n**Indexation Issues**\n- Noindex tags on important pages\n- Canonicals pointing wrong direction\n- Redirect chains/loops\n- Soft 404s\n- Duplicate content without canonicals\n\n**Canonicalization**\n- All pages have canonical tags\n- Self-referencing canonicals on unique pages\n- HTTP → HTTPS canonicals\n- www vs. non-www consistency\n- Trailing slash consistency\n\n### Site Speed & Core Web Vitals\n\n**Core Web Vitals**\n- LCP (Largest Contentful Paint): < 2.5s\n- INP (Interaction to Next Paint): < 200ms\n- CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift): < 0.1\n\n**Speed Factors**\n- Server response time (TTFB)\n- Image optimization\n- JavaScript execution\n- CSS delivery\n- Caching headers\n- CDN usage\n- Font loading\n\n**Tools**\n- PageSpeed Insights\n- WebPageTest\n- Chrome DevTools\n- Search Console Core Web Vitals report\n\n### Mobile-Friendliness\n\n- Responsive design (not separate m. site)\n- Tap target sizes\n- Viewport configured\n- No horizontal scroll\n- Same content as desktop\n- Mobile-first indexing readiness\n\n### Security & HTTPS\n\n- HTTPS across entire site\n- Valid SSL certificate\n- No mixed content\n- HTTP → HTTPS redirects\n- HSTS header (bonus)\n\n### URL Structure\n\n- Readable, descriptive URLs\n- Keywords in URLs where natural\n- Consistent structure\n- No unnecessary parameters\n- Lowercase and hyphen-separated\n\n---\n\n## On-Page SEO Audit\n\n### Title Tags\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique titles for each page\n- Primary keyword near beginning\n- 50-60 characters (visible in SERP)\n- Compelling and click-worthy\n- Brand name placement (end, usually)\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate titles\n- Too long (truncated)\n- Too short (wasted opportunity)\n- Keyword stuffing\n- Missing entirely\n\n### Meta Descriptions\n\n**Check for:**\n- Unique descriptions per page\n- 150-160 characters\n- Includes primary keyword\n- Clear value proposition\n- Call to action\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Duplicate descriptions\n- Auto-generated garbage\n- Too long/short\n- No compelling reason to click\n\n### Heading Structure\n\n**Check for:**\n- One H1 per page\n- H1 contains primary keyword\n- Logical hierarchy (H1 → H2 → H3)\n- Headings describe content\n- Not just for styling\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Multiple H1s\n- Skip levels (H1 → H3)\n- Headings used for styling only\n- No H1 on page\n\n### Content Optimization\n\n**Primary Page Content**\n- Keyword in first 100 words\n- Related keywords naturally used\n- Sufficient depth/length for topic\n- Answers search intent\n- Better than competitors\n\n**Thin Content Issues**\n- Pages with little unique content\n- Tag/category pages with no value\n- Doorway pages\n- Duplicate or near-duplicate content\n\n### Image Optimization\n\n**Check for:**\n- Descriptive file names\n- Alt text on all images\n- Alt text describes image\n- Compressed file sizes\n- Modern formats (WebP)\n- Lazy loading implemented\n- Responsive images\n\n### Internal Linking\n\n**Check for:**\n- Important pages well-linked\n- Descriptive anchor text\n- Logical link relationships\n- No broken internal links\n- Reasonable link count per page\n\n**Common issues:**\n- Orphan pages (no internal links)\n- Over-optimized anchor text\n- Important pages buried\n- Excessive footer/sidebar links\n\n### Keyword Targeting\n\n**Per Page**\n- Clear primary keyword target\n- Title, H1, URL aligned\n- Content satisfies search intent\n- Not competing with other pages (cannibalization)\n\n**Site-Wide**\n- Keyword mapping document\n- No major gaps in coverage\n- No keyword cannibalization\n- Logical topical clusters\n\n---\n\n## Content Quality Assessment\n\n### E-E-A-T Signals\n\n**Experience**\n- First-hand experience demonstrated\n- Original insights/data\n- Real examples and case studies\n\n**Expertise**\n- Author credentials visible\n- Accurate, detailed information\n- Properly sourced claims\n\n**Authoritativeness**\n- Recognized in the space\n- Cited by others\n- Industry credentials\n\n**Trustworthiness**\n- Accurate information\n- Transparent about business\n- Contact information available\n- Privacy policy, terms\n- Secure site (HTTPS)\n\n### Content Depth\n\n- Comprehensive coverage of topic\n- Answers follow-up questions\n- Better than top-ranking competitors\n- Updated and current\n\n### User Engagement Signals\n\n- Time on page\n- Bounce rate in context\n- Pages per session\n- Return visits\n\n---\n\n## Common Issues by Site Type\n\n### SaaS/Product Sites\n- Product pages lack content depth\n- Blog not integrated with product pages\n- Missing comparison/alternative pages\n- Feature pages thin on content\n- No glossary/educational content\n\n### E-commerce\n- Thin category pages\n- Duplicate product descriptions\n- Missing product schema\n- Faceted navigation creating duplicates\n- Out-of-stock pages mishandled\n\n### Content/Blog Sites\n- Outdated content not refreshed\n- Keyword cannibalization\n- No topical clustering\n- Poor internal linking\n- Missing author pages\n\n### Local Business\n- Inconsistent NAP\n- Missing local schema\n- No Google Business Profile optimization\n- Missing location pages\n- No local content\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Audit Report Structure\n\n**Executive Summary**\n- Overall health assessment\n- Top 3-5 priority issues\n- Quick wins identified\n\n**Technical SEO Findings**\nFor each issue:\n- **Issue**: What''s wrong\n- **Impact**: SEO impact (High/Medium/Low)\n- **Evidence**: How you found it\n- **Fix**: Specific recommendation\n- **Priority**: 1-5 or High/Medium/Low\n\n**On-Page SEO Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Content Findings**\nSame format as above\n\n**Prioritized Action Plan**\n1. Critical fixes (blocking indexation/ranking)\n2. High-impact improvements\n3. Quick wins (easy, immediate benefit)\n4. Long-term recommendations\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n- [AI Writing Detection](references/ai-writing-detection.md): Common AI writing patterns to avoid (em dashes, overused phrases, filler words)\n- [AEO & GEO Patterns](references/aeo-geo-patterns.md): Content patterns optimized for answer engines and AI citation\n\n---\n\n## Tools Referenced\n\n**Free Tools**\n- Google Search Console (essential)\n- Google PageSpeed Insights\n- Bing Webmaster Tools\n- Rich Results Test\n- Mobile-Friendly Test\n- Schema Validator\n\n**Paid Tools** (if available)\n- Screaming Frog\n- Ahrefs / Semrush\n- Sitebulb\n- ContentKing\n\n---\n\n## Task-Specific Questions\n\n1. What pages/keywords matter most?\n2. Do you have Search Console access?\n3. Any recent changes or migrations?\n4. Who are your top organic competitors?\n5. What''s your current organic traffic baseline?\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **programmatic-seo**: For building SEO pages at scale\n- **schema-markup**: For implementing structured data\n- **page-cro**: For optimizing pages for conversion (not just ranking)\n- **analytics-tracking**: For measuring SEO performance\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:33:49.673Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Digital Marketing Agents needing advanced SEO analysis and optimization capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级SEO分析和优化能力的数字营销代理。","ja":"デジタルマーケティングエージェントが高度なSEO分析および最適化機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 SEO 분석 및 최적화 기능이 필요한 디지털 마케팅 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de marketing digital que necesitan capacidades de análisis y optimización de SEO avanzadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de marketing numérique ayant besoin d''une analyse et d''optimisation de référencement avancées.","de":"Perfekt für digitale Marketing-Agenten, die erweiterte SEO-Analyse- und Optimierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Marketing Digital que necessitam de análise e capacidades de otimização de SEO avançadas.","ru":"Идеально для цифровых маркетинговых агентов, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности анализа и оптимизации SEO.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التسويق الرقمي الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل وتحسين متقدمين لقدرات SEO."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify SEO issues and provide actionable recommendations using product marketing context, understanding site context, and analyzing organic search performance, leveraging Markdown files like `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","zh":"赋予代理识别SEO问题和提供可行建议的能力，利用产品营销背景、理解网站背景、分析有机搜索性能，并利用Markdown文件，如`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`。","ja":"エージェントがSEOの問題を特定し、製品マーケティングコンテキスト、サイトコンテキストの理解、オーガニック検索パフォーマンスの分析を利用して、実行可能な推奨事項を提供する機能を提供します。例えば、`.claude/product-marketing-context.md`などのMarkdownファイルを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 SEO 문제를 식별하고 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트, 사이트 컨텍스트 이해, 유기적 검색 성능 분석을 활용하여 실행 가능한 추천을 제공할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 예를 들어, `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`와 같은 Markdown 파일을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar problemas de SEO y proporcionar recomendaciones accionables utilizando el contexto de marketing de productos, entendiendo el contexto del sitio y analizando el rendimiento de la búsqueda orgánica, aprovechando archivos Markdown como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les problèmes de SEO et de fournir des recommandations actionnables en utilisant le contexte de marketing de produits, en comprenant le contexte du site et en analysant les performances de recherche organique, en exploitant des fichiers Markdown tels que `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, SEO-Probleme zu identifizieren und handhabbare Empfehlungen bereitzustellen, indem sie den Produktmarketing-Kontext verwenden, den Kontext der Website verstehen und die Leistung der organischen Suche analysieren, indem sie Markdown-Dateien wie `.claude/product-marketing-context.md` nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar problemas de SEO e fornecer recomendações eficazes usando o contexto de marketing de produto, compreendendo o contexto do site e analisando o desempenho de pesquisa orgânica, aproveitando arquivos Markdown como `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять проблемы SEO и предоставлять действенные рекомендации, используя контекст продукта маркетинга, понимание контекста сайта и анализ результатов органического поиска, используя файлы Markdown типа `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تحديد مشاكل SEO وتقديم توصيات قابلة للتنفيذ باستخدام سياق تسويق المنتج وفهم سياق الموقع وتحليل أداء البحث العضوي، واستخدام ملفات Markdown مثل `.claude/product-marketing-context.md`."},"useCases":{"en":["Conducting initial SEO assessments","Analyzing site context for optimization opportunities","Providing actionable recommendations for organic search improvement"],"zh":["进行初步SEO评估","分析网站背景以寻找优化机会","为有机搜索改进提供可行建议"],"ja":["初期SEO評価の実施","サイトコンテキストの分析による最適化の機会の特定","オーガニック検索の改善に関する実行可能な推奨事項の提供"],"ko":["초기 SEO 평가 수행","사이트 컨텍스트 분석을 통한 최적화 기회 식별","유기적 검색 개선에 대한 실행 가능한 추천 제공"],"es":["Realizar evaluaciones iniciales de SEO","Analizar el contexto del sitio para oportunidades de optimización","Proporcionar recomendaciones accionables para la mejora de la búsqueda orgánica"],"fr":["Réalisant les évaluations initiales de SEO","Analyser le contexte du site pour les opportunités d''optimisation","Fournir des recommandations actionnables pour l''amélioration de la recherche organique"],"de":["Durchführung von initialen SEO-Bewertungen","Analyse des Kontexts der Website für Optimierungsmöglichkeiten","Bereitstellung von handhabbaren Empfehlungen für die Verbesserung der organischen Suche"],"pt":["Realizar avaliações iniciais de SEO","Analisar o contexto do site para oportunidades de otimização","Fornecer recomendações eficazes para melhoria da pesquisa orgânica"],"ru":["Проведение начальных оценок SEO","Анализ контекста сайта для возможностей оптимизации","Предоставление действенных рекомендаций для улучшения органического поиска"],"ar":["إجراء تقييمات أولية لتحليل SEO","تحليل سياق الموقع لفرص تحسين","تقديم توصيات قابلة للتنفيذ لتحسين البحث العضوي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to site context information","Limited to analyzing existing web resources","Dependent on product marketing context for accuracy"],"zh":["需要访问网站背景信息","仅限分析现有的网络资源","依赖产品营销背景以保证准确性"],"ja":["サイトコンテキスト情報へのアクセスが必要","既存のWebリソースのみを分析可能","精度の確保のため製品マーケティングコンテキストに依存"],"ko":["사이트 컨텍스트 정보에 대한 액세스가 필요","기존 웹 리소스만 분석 가능","정확성을 보장하기 위해 제품 마케팅 컨텍스트에 의존"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la información del contexto del sitio","Limitado al análisis de los recursos web existentes","Dependiente del contexto de marketing de productos para la precisión"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''information du contexte du site","Limité à l''analyse des ressources web existantes","Dépendant du contexte de marketing de produits pour la précision"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Kontextinformationen der Website","Begrenzt auf die Analyse der vorhandenen Webressourcen","Abhängig vom Produktmarketing-Kontext für die Genauigkeit"],"pt":["Requer acesso às informações de contexto do site","Limitado à análise de recursos web existentes","Dependente do contexto de marketing do produto para precisão"],"ru":["Требует доступа к информации контекста сайта","Ограничен анализом существующих веб-ресурсов","Зависит от контекста продукта маркетинга для точности"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى معلومات سياق الموقع","محدود بتحليل الموارد الإلكترونية الحالية","يعتمد على سياق تسويق المنتج لالدقة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Dknight203/AesopIDE/systematic-debugging', 'community', 'Dknight203', 'AesopIDE', 'Dknight203/AesopIDE', 'systematic-debugging', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z', '2026-02-18T09:34:20.261Z', NULL, '{"id":"Dknight203/AesopIDE/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种找到问题根源的方法，避免随机修复和新错误。它遵循铁律：在调查根源之前不提出修复方案","ja":"体系的デバッグは、問題の根源を発見し、ランダムな修正と新しいエラーを避ける方法です。鉄則を遵守します：根源の調査を行う前に修正案を提出しない","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 문제의 근본 원인을 찾는 방법으로 무작위 수정과 새로운 오류를 피합니다. 철칙을 준수합니다: 근본 원인 조사를 수행하기 전에 수정안을 제안하지 않음","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para identificar y resolver problemas de manera eficiente. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones.","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes de manière efficace. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions.","de":"Das systematische Debugging ist ein Ansatz, um Probleme effizient zu identifizieren und zu lösen. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen vorschlagen.","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem metodológica para identificar e resolver problemas técnicos, garantindo que as soluções sejam eficazes e duradouras","ru":"Системная отладка - это методологический подход к выявлению и решению технических проблем, гарантирующий, что решения будут эффективными и долговечными","ar":"التصحيح النظامي هو نهج منهجي لتحديد ومعالجة المشاكل الفنية، مما يضمن أن تكون الحلول فعالة ومستدامة","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"系统调试技术","ja":"体系的デバッグ","ko":"시스템 디버깅 기술","es":"Depuración Sistemática: Encontrar la Causa Raíz","fr":"Débogage Systématique: Trouver la Cause Profonde","de":"Systematisches Debugging: Die Ursache Finden","pt":"Depuração Sistemática: Encontre a Causa Raiz","ru":"Системная отладка: найдите коренную причину","ar":"تصحيح 系统ي: اعثر على السبب الجذري","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种找到问题根源的方法，避免随机修复和新错误。它遵循铁律：在调查根源之前不提出修复方案","ja":"体系的デバッグは、問題の根源を発見し、ランダムな修正と新しいエラーを避ける方法です。鉄則を遵守します：根源の調査を行う前に修正案を提出しない","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 문제의 근본 원인을 찾는 방법으로 무작위 수정과 새로운 오류를 피합니다. 철칙을 준수합니다: 근본 원인 조사를 수행하기 전에 수정안을 제안하지 않음","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para identificar y resolver problemas de manera eficiente. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones.","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes de manière efficace. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant de proposer...","de":"Das systematische Debugging ist ein Ansatz, um Probleme effizient zu identifizieren und zu lösen. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen vorschlagen.","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem metodológica para identificar e resolver problemas técnicos, garantindo que as soluções sejam eficazes e duradouras","ru":"Системная отладка - это методологический подход к выявлению и решению технических проблем, гарантирующий, что решения будут эффективными и долговечными","ar":"التصحيح النظامي هو نهج منهجي لتحديد ومعالجة المشاكل الفنية، مما يضمن أن تكون الحلول فعالة ومستدامة","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"zh":["找到问题的根源","避免随机修复","遵循铁律","提高调试效率","减少新错误"],"ja":["問題の根源を発見","ランダムな修正を避ける","鉄則を遵守","デバッグ効率を向上","新しいエラーを減らす"],"ko":["문제의 근본 원인을 찾음","무작위 수정을 피함","철칙을 준수","디버깅 효율성을 향상","새로운 오류를 줄임"],"es":["Identificación de la causa raíz","Análisis estructurado de problemas","Evitación de soluciones temporales","Mejora de la eficiencia en la resolución de problemas","Reducción de errores y bugs"],"fr":["Identification de la cause profonde","Analyse structurée des problèmes","Évitement des solutions temporaires","Amélioration de l''efficacité dans la résolution de problèmes","Réduction des erreurs et des bugs"],"de":["Identifizierung der Ursache","Strukturierte Analyse von Problemen","Vermeidung von temporären Lösungen","Verbesserung der Effizienz bei der Problemlösung","Reduzierung von Fehlern und Bugs"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz dos problemas","Abordagem metodológica para resolução de problemas","Garantia de soluções eficazes e duradouras","Redução do tempo de depuração","Melhoria da qualidade do código"],"ru":["Выявление коренной причины проблем","Методологический подход к решению проблем","Гарантия эффективных и долговечных решений","Сокращение времени отладки","Улучшение качества кода"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري للمشاكل","نهج منهجي لحل المشاكل","ضمان حلول فعالة ومستدامة","تقليل وقت التصحيح","تحسين جودة الكود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统调试","调试方法","问题根源","铁律","随机修复","新错误","调试效率"],"ja":["体系的デバッグ","デバッグ方法","問題の根源","鉄則","ランダムな修正","新しいエラー","デバッグ効率"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","디버깅 방법","문제의 근본 원인","철칙","무작위 수정","새로운 오류","디버깅 효율성"],"es":["depuración sistemática","debugging","causa raíz","análisis de problemas","eficiencia en la resolución de problemas","reducción de errores","desarrollo de software","pruebas de software"],"fr":["débogage systématique","debugging","cause profonde","analyse de problèmes","efficacité dans la résolution de problèmes","réduction des erreurs","développement de logiciel","tests de logiciel"],"de":["systematisches Debugging","Debugging","Ursache","Problemanalyse","Effizienz bei der Problemlösung","Fehlerreduzierung","Softwareentwicklung","Softwaretests"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","resolução de problemas","causa raiz","soluções eficazes","qualidade do código","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["системная отладка","решение проблем","коренная причина","эффективные решения","качество кода","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تصحيح نظامي","حل المشاكل","السبب الجذري","حلول فعالة","جودة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:34:20.261Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing structured issue resolution and root cause analysis capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化问题解决和根因分析能力的调试代理。","ja":"デバッグエージェントが構造化された問題解決と根本原因分析の機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"구조화된 문제 해결 및根本 원인 분석 기능이 필요한 디버깅 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de depuración que necesitan una resolución de problemas estructurada y capacidades de análisis de causa raíz.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de débogage nécessitant une résolution de problèmes structurée et des capacités d''analyse de cause racine.","de":"Perfekt für Debugging-Agents, die eine strukturierte Problembehebung und Wurzelursachenanalysefähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing structured issue resolution and root cause analysis capabilities.","ru":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing structured issue resolution and root cause analysis capabilities.","ar":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing structured issue resolution and root cause analysis capabilities."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to investigate root causes using the Iron Law, ensuring no fixes are proposed without thorough investigation, and providing a systematic approach to debugging using Phase 1 analysis and symptom fixes avoidance.","zh":"赋予代理调查根本原因的能力，使用铁律确保在彻底调查之前不会提出任何解决方案，并提供使用第1阶段分析和避免症状修复的系统化方法来进行调试。","ja":"エージェントが根本原因を調査する能力を付与し、鉄則を使用して徹底的な調査を行わない場合に修正を提案しないことを保証し、第1相分析と症状の修正の回避を使用したデバッグの体系的なアプローチを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가根本 원인을 조사할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 철의 법칙을 사용하여 철저한 조사 없이 수정을 제안하지 않도록 하며, 1단계 분석 및 증상 수정 회피를 사용하여 디버깅에 대한 체계적인 접근 방식을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a investigar las causas raíces utilizando la Ley de Hierro, garantizando que no se propongan soluciones sin una investigación exhaustiva y proporcionando un enfoque sistemático para la depuración utilizando el análisis de la Fase 1 y la evitación de soluciones de síntomas.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''enquêter sur les causes racines en utilisant la Loi de Fer, en garantissant qu''aucune solution n''est proposée sans une enquête approfondie et en fournissant une approche systématique du débogage en utilisant l''analyse de la Phase 1 et l''évitement des solutions de symptômes.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Wurzeln mit dem Eisernen Gesetz zu untersuchen, stellt sicher, dass keine Lösungen ohne gründliche Untersuchung vorgeschlagen werden und bietet einen systematischen Ansatz für das Debugging unter Verwendung der Phase-1-Analyse und der Vermeidung von Symptommitteln.","pt":"Empowers agents to investigate root causes using the Iron Law, ensuring no fixes are proposed without thorough investigation, and providing a systematic approach to debugging using Phase 1 analysis and symptom fixes avoidance.","ru":"Empowers agents to investigate root causes using the Iron Law, ensuring no fixes are proposed without thorough investigation, and providing a systematic approach to debugging using Phase 1 analysis and symptom fixes avoidance.","ar":"Empowers agents to investigate root causes using the Iron Law, ensuring no fixes are proposed without thorough investigation, and providing a systematic approach to debugging using Phase 1 analysis and symptom fixes avoidance."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging test failures","Identifying root causes of bugs","Implementing systematic fixes for technical issues"],"zh":["调试测试失败","识别bug的根因","为技术问题实施系统修复"],"ja":["テストの失敗のデバッグ","バグの根本原因の特定","技術的な問題に対する体系的な修正の実装"],"ko":["테스트 실패의 디버깅","버그의根本 원인 식별","기술적인 문제에 대한 체계적인 수정 구현"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba","Identificación de las causas raíces de los errores","Implementación de soluciones sistemáticas para problemas técnicos"],"fr":["Débogage des échecs de test","Identification des causes racines des bogues","Mise en œuvre de solutions systématiques pour les problèmes techniques"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei Testfehlern","Identifizierung der Wurzeln von Fehlern","Implementierung systematischer Lösungen für technische Probleme"],"pt":["Debugging test failures","Identifying root causes of bugs","Implementing systematic fixes for technical issues"],"ru":["Debugging test failures","Identifying root causes of bugs","Implementing systematic fixes for technical issues"],"ar":["Debugging test failures","Identifying root causes of bugs","Implementing systematic fixes for technical issues"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the Iron Law","Violating the letter of the process is violating the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要遵守铁律","违反流程的字面意思就是违反了调试的精神"],"ja":["鉄則への遵守が必要","プロセスの文字通りに違反することはデバッグの精神に違反することになる"],"ko":["철의 법칙을 준수해야 함","프로세스의 문자 그대로의 위반은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것"],"es":["Requiere adherirse a la Ley de Hierro","Violando la letra del proceso es violar el espíritu de la depuración"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion à la Loi de Fer","Enfreindre la lettre du processus est enfreindre l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des Eisernen Gesetzes","Die Verletzung des Buchstabens des Prozesses ist die Verletzung des Geistes des Debuggings"],"pt":["Requires adherence to the Iron Law","Violating the letter of the process is violating the spirit of debugging"],"ru":["Requires adherence to the Iron Law","Violating the letter of the process is violating the spirit of debugging"],"ar":["Requires adherence to the Iron Law","Violating the letter of the process is violating the spirit of debugging"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('PaulPio/FinFlow-/systematic-debugging', 'community', 'PaulPio', 'FinFlow-', 'PaulPio/FinFlow-', 'systematic-debugging', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z', '2026-02-18T09:33:47.454Z', NULL, '{"id":"PaulPio/FinFlow-/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种根据根本原因进行调试的方法，帮助开发者快速找到技术问题的根源","ja":"体系的デバッグは、根本原因を調べることで技術的な問題を迅速に解決する方法です","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 분석하여 기술적인 문제를迅速히 해결하는 방법입니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque metódico para identificar y solucionar problemas técnicos. Este proceso implica encontrar la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones.","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche méthodique pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes techniques. Ce processus implique de trouver la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions.","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein methodischer Ansatz zur Identifizierung und Lösung von technischen Problemen. Dieser Prozess beinhaltet das Finden der Ursache bevor Lösungen vorgeschlagen werden.","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem metódica para identificar e resolver problemas técnicos, focando na causa raiz em vez de apenas nos sintomas","ru":"Системная отладка - это методический подход к выявлению и решению технических проблем, фокусирующийся на коренной причине, а не только на симптомах","ar":"التصحيح المنهجي هو نهج منهجي لتحديد ومعالجة المشكلات الفنية، يركز على السبب الجذري بدلاً من الأعراض فقط","en":"AI-powered budget assistant that predicts spending, detects anomalies, and helps you reach financial goals faster with real-time insights."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"系统调试 - 根据根本原因进行调试","ja":"体系的デバッグ - 根本原因を調べる","ko":"시스템 디버깅 - 근본 원인 분석","es":"Depuración Sistemática: Encontrar la Causa Raíz","fr":"Débogage Systématique: Trouver la Cause Profonde","de":"Systematische Fehlersuche: Die Ursache Finden","pt":"Depuração Sistemática - Encontre a Causa Raiz","ru":"Системная отладка - найдите коренную причину","ar":"تصحيح منهجي - إ找 العلة الأساسية","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种根据根本原因进行调试的方法，帮助开发者快速找到技术问题的根源","ja":"体系的デバッグは、根本原因を調べることで技術的な問題を迅速に解決する方法です","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 근본 원인을 분석하여 기술적인 문제를迅速히 해결하는 방법입니다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque metódico para identificar y solucionar problemas técnicos. Este proceso implica encontrar la causa raíz antes de prop...","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche méthodique pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes techniques. Ce processus implique de trouver la cause profonde...","de":"Die systematische Fehlersuche ist ein methodischer Ansatz zur Identifizierung und Lösung von technischen Problemen. Dieser Prozess beinhaltet das Finden der ...","pt":"A depuração sistemática é uma abordagem metódica para identificar e resolver problemas técnicos, focando na causa raiz em vez de apenas nos sintomas","ru":"Системная отладка - это методический подход к выявлению и решению технических проблем, фокусирующийся на коренной причине, а не только на симптомах","ar":"التصحيح المنهجي هو نهج منهجي لتحديد ومعالجة المشكلات الفنية، يركز على السبب الجذري بدلاً من الأعراض فقط","en":"AI-powered budget assistant that predicts spending, detects anomalies, and helps you reach financial goals faster with real-time insights."},"definition":{"en":"AI-powered budget assistant that predicts spending, detects anomalies, and helps you reach financial goals faster with real-time insights."},"features":{"zh":["根据根本原因进行调试","避免随机的修复和新bug","快速找到技术问题的根源","提高开发效率","减少维护成本"],"ja":["根本原因を調べることでデバッグを行う","ランダムな修正と新しいバグを避ける","技術的な問題の根本原因を迅速に特定","開発効率の向上","メンテナンスコストの削減"],"ko":["근본 원인을 분석하여 디버깅","임의의 수정과 새로운 버그를 피함","기술적인 문제의 근본 원인을迅速히 찾음","개발 효율성 향상","유지 보수 비용 절감"],"es":["Enfoque metódico para identificar problemas","Encontrar la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones","Evitar soluciones temporales","Aplicar el principio de no arreglar sin investigación","Utilizar el proceso de depuración en cualquier problema técnico"],"fr":["Approche méthodique pour identifier les problèmes","Trouver la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions","Éviter les solutions temporaires","Appliquer le principe de ne pas réparer sans investigation","Utiliser le processus de débogage pour tout problème technique"],"de":["Methodischer Ansatz zur Identifizierung von Problemen","Finden der Ursache bevor Lösungen vorgeschlagen werden","Vermeiden von temporären Lösungen","Anwenden des Prinzips, nicht zu reparieren ohne Untersuchung","Verwenden des Fehlersuchprozesses für jedes technische Problem"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz de problemas técnicos","Abordagem metódica para resolver problemas","Economia de tempo e recursos","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Redução de bugs e erros"],"ru":["Выявление коренной причины технических проблем","Методический подход к решению проблем","Экономия времени и ресурсов","Улучшение качества кода","Снижение количества багов и ошибок"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري للمشكلات الفنية","نهج منهجي لحل المشكلات","توفير الوقت والموارد","تحسين جودة الكود","تقليل الأخطاء والعيوب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统调试","软件开发","技术问题","根本原因","随机修复","新bug","开发效率","维护成本"],"ja":["体系的デバッグ","ソフトウェア開発","技術的な問題","根本原因","ランダムな修正","新しいバグ","開発効率","メンテナンスコスト"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","소프트웨어 개발","기술적인 문제","근본 원인","임의의 수정","新的 버그","개발 효율성","유지 보수 비용"],"es":["depuración sistemática","encontrar causa raíz","solución de problemas técnicos","principio de no arreglar sin investigación","proceso de depuración","soluciones temporales","identificación de problemas","análisis de problemas","solución eficiente"],"fr":["débogage systématique","trouver la cause profonde","résolution de problèmes techniques","principe de ne pas réparer sans investigation","processus de débogage","solutions temporaires","identification de problèmes","analyse de problèmes","solution efficace"],"de":["systematische Fehlersuche","Finden der Ursache","Lösung von technischen Problemen","Prinzip, nicht zu reparieren ohne Untersuchung","Fehlersuchprozess","temporäre Lösungen","Identifizierung von Problemen","Analyse von Problemen","effiziente Lösung"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","resolução de problemas","causa raiz","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade do código","otimização de desempenho"],"ru":["системная отладка","решение проблем","коренная причина","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["التصحيح المنهجي","حل المشكلات","السبب الجذري","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الكود","تحسين الأداء"]}},"owner":"PaulPio","repo":"FinFlow-","repoPath":"PaulPio/FinFlow-","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:33:47.454Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT requiring methodical issue resolution through systematic-debugging","zh":"适合于像 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 这样的高级 AI Agent，需要通过系统调试来解决问题","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT などの高度な AI エージェントに適しており、体系的な問題解決が必要","ko":"Claude Code와 AutoGPT 같은 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합하며, 체계적인 문제 해결을 통해 방법론적인 문제 해결이 필요","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA avanzados como Claude Code y AutoGPT que requieren una resolución de problemas metódica a través de depuración sistemática","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA avancés comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant une résolution de problèmes méthodique par débogage systématique","de":"Ideal für fortgeschrittene KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die eine methodische Problemlösung durch systematisches Debugging erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Avançados de IA, como Claude Code e AutoGPT, que exigem resolução metódica de problemas por meio de depuração sistemática","ru":"Идеально подходит для продвинутых агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, требующих методического решения проблем посредством системной отладки","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي المتقدمة مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT التي تتطلب حلًا منهجيًا للمشكلات من خلال تصحيح الأخطاء المنهجي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify root causes of technical issues using the Iron Law, ensuring NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, thereby preventing quick patches that mask underlying problems and reducing debug time by focusing on symptom fixes as failures","zh":"赋予代理识别技术问题的根本原因的能力，使用铁律，确保在调查根本原因之前不进行修复，防止掩盖潜在问题的快速修复，并通过关注症状修复来减少调试时间","ja":"エージェントに技術的な問題の根本原因を特定する能力を与え、鉄則を適用して根本原因の調査を行う前に修正をしないことを保証し、根本的な問題を隠すような迅速な修正を防ぎ、症状の修正に焦点を当てることでデバッグ時間を短縮する","ko":"에이전트가 기술적인 문제의 근본적인 원인을 식별할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 철칙을 적용하여 근본적인 원인의 조사 없이 수정을 하지 않도록 보장하고, 기본적인 문제를 가리는 빠른 수정을 방지하며, 증상 수정에 중점을 두어 디버깅 시간을 단축","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar las causas raíz de los problemas técnicos utilizando la Ley de Hierro, asegurando NO HAY REPARACIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE LA CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, lo que evita soluciones rápidas que ocultan problemas subyacentes y reduce el tiempo de depuración centrándose en soluciones de síntomas como fallos","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les causes profondes des problèmes techniques en utilisant la Loi de Fer, en garantissant AUCUNE CORRECTION SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE PROFONDE D''ABORD, ce qui empêche les correctifs rapides qui masquent les problèmes sous-jacents et réduit le temps de débogage en se concentrant sur les correctifs de symptômes comme des défaillances","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, die Ursachen von technischen Problemen mithilfe des Eisengesetzes zu identifizieren, indem sie KEINE REPARATUREN OHNE UNTERSUCHUNG DER URSACHE ZUERST gewährleisten, was schnelle Patches verhindert, die zugrunde liegende Probleme verbergen, und die Debug-Zeit reduziert, indem sie sich auf Symptombehebungen als Ausfälle konzentrieren","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar as causas raiz dos problemas técnicos usando a Lei de Ferro, garantindo NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DA CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, prevenindo assim correções rápidas que mascaram problemas subjacentes e reduzindo o tempo de depuração ao se concentrar em correções de sintomas como falhas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выявлять коренные причины технических проблем с помощью Железного Закона, гарантируя НЕТ ИСПРАВЛЕНИЙ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, тем самым предотвращая быстрые исправления, которые маскируют основные проблемы и сокращая время отладки, сосредотачиваясь на исправлении симптомов как неисправностей","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من تحديد الأسباب الجذرية للمشكلات الفنية باستخدام قانون الحديد، مما يضمن عدم وجود إصلاحات بدون تحقيق في السبب الجذري أولاً، ومنع الإصلاحات السريعة التي تخفي المشكلات الكامنة وتقليل时间 التصحيح من خلال التركيز على إصلاح الأعراض كأعطال"},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging test failures with systematic approaches","Resolving bugs by always finding the root cause first","Applying the Iron Law to prevent premature fixes"],"zh":["使用系统方法调试测试失败","通过始终找到根本原因来解决错误","应用铁律来防止过早的修复"],"ja":["体系的なアプローチでテストの失敗をデバッグする","根本原因を常に最初に特定してバグを解決する","鉄則を適用して早期の修正を防ぐ"],"ko":["체계적인 접근 방식을 사용하여 테스트 실패를 디버깅","루트 원인을 항상 먼저 찾는 방식으로 버그를 해결","철칙을 적용하여 미ATURE한 수정을 방지"],"es":["Depuración de fallos de prueba con enfoques sistemáticos","Resolución de errores encontrando siempre la causa raíz primero","Aplicación de la Ley de Hierro para prevenir soluciones prematuras"],"fr":["Débogage des défaillances de test avec des approches systématiques","Résolution de bogues en trouvant toujours la cause profonde d''abord","Application de la Loi de Fer pour prévenir les correctifs prématurés"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung von Testfehlern mit systematischen Ansätzen","Behebung von Fehlern, indem man immer die Ursache zuerst findet","Anwendung des Eisengesetzes, um vorzeitige Patches zu verhindern"],"pt":["Depuração de falhas de teste com abordagens sistemáticas","Resolução de bugs encontrando sempre a causa raiz primeiro","Aplicação da Lei de Ferro para prevenir correções prematuras"],"ru":["Отладка неудач тестирования с системными подходами","Исправление ошибок, всегда находя коренную причину сначала","Применение Железного Закона для предотвращения преждевременных исправлений"],"ar":["تصحيح اختبار الأعطال بالمنهجيات المنهجية","حل العيوب بالبحث دائمًا عن السبب الجذري أولاً","تطبيق قانون الحديد لمنع الإصلاحات المسبقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the systematic-debugging process","Violating the core principle may lead to increased debug time and new bugs"],"zh":["需要遵守系统调试过程","违反核心原则可能会导致调试时间增加和新的错误"],"ja":["体系的なデバッグプロセスに従う必要がある","コアプリンシプルを違反するとデバッグ時間の増加と新しいバグが発生する可能性がある"],"ko":["체계적인 디버깅 프로세스를 따라야 함","핵심 원칙을 위반하면 디버깅 시간이 증가하고 새로운 버그가 발생할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere adherencia al proceso de depuración sistemática","Violación del principio fundamental puede llevar a un aumento del tiempo de depuración y nuevos errores"],"fr":["Nécessite l''adhésion au processus de débogage systématique","La violation du principe fondamental peut entraîner une augmentation du temps de débogage et de nouveaux bogues"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des systematischen Debug-Prozesses","Verletzung des Kernprinzips kann zu einer erhöhten Debug-Zeit und neuen Fehlern führen"],"pt":["Exige aderência ao processo de depuração sistemática","Violar o princípio básico pode levar a aumento do tempo de depuração e novos bugs"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения системного процесса отладки","Нарушение основополагающего принципа может привести к увеличению времени отладки и появлению новых ошибок"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بعملية تصحيح الأخطاء المنهجية","خرق المبدأ الأساسي قد يؤدي إلى زيادة وقت التصحيح وأعطال جديدة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Faizan1421/skills-Ai/systematic-debugging', 'community', 'Faizan1421', 'skills-Ai', 'Faizan1421/skills-Ai', 'systematic-debugging', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z', '2026-02-18T09:34:22.920Z', NULL, '{"id":"Faizan1421/skills-Ai/systematic-debugging","name":"systematic-debugging","description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种高效的解决技术问题的方法，通过找到问题的根源而非症状来解决问题","ja":"体系的デバッグは、テクニカルな問題を解決するための方法で、根本原因を探して解決する","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 기술적인 문제를 해결하는 방법으로, 근본 원인을 탐색하여 해결한다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para identificar y solucionar problemas técnicos de manera eficiente. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de proponer soluciones","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes techniques de manière efficace. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant de proposer des solutions","de":"Das systematische Debugging ist ein Ansatz, um technische Probleme effizient zu identifizieren und zu lösen. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen vorschlagen","pt":"A depuração sistemática é um processo que ajuda a identificar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos, evitando soluções rápidas que podem criar novos bugs","ru":"Системная отладка - это процесс, который помогает определить коренную причину технических проблем, избегая быстрых решений, которые могут создать новые ошибки","ar":"تصحيح الأخطاء بشكل منهجي هو عملية تساعد على تحديد السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية، وتجنب الحلول السريعة التي قد تسبب أخطاء جديدة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"系统调试技术","ja":"体系的デバッグ","ko":"시스템 디버깅","es":"Depuración Sistemática: Encontrar la Causa Raíz","fr":"Débogage Systématique: Trouver la Cause Profonde","de":"Systematisches Debugging: Die Ursache Finden","pt":"Depuração Sistemática: Encontre a Causa Raiz","ru":"Системная отладка: найдите коренную причину","ar":"تصحيح 系统ي: اعثر على السبب الجذري","en":"systematic-debugging"},"description":{"zh":"系统调试是一种高效的解决技术问题的方法，通过找到问题的根源而非症状来解决问题","ja":"体系的デバッグは、テクニカルな問題を解決するための方法で、根本原因を探して解決する","ko":"시스템 디버깅은 기술적인 문제를 해결하는 방법으로, 근본 원인을 탐색하여 해결한다","es":"La depuración sistemática es un enfoque para identificar y solucionar problemas técnicos de manera eficiente. Siempre encuentra la causa raíz antes de propon...","fr":"Le débogage systématique est une approche pour identifier et résoudre les problèmes techniques de manière efficace. Trouvez toujours la cause profonde avant ...","de":"Das systematische Debugging ist ein Ansatz, um technische Probleme effizient zu identifizieren und zu lösen. Finden Sie immer die Ursache, bevor Sie Lösungen...","pt":"A depuração sistemática é um processo que ajuda a identificar a causa raiz dos problemas técnicos, evitando soluções rápidas que podem criar novos bugs","ru":"Системная отладка - это процесс, который помогает определить коренную причину технических проблем, избегая быстрых решений, которые могут создать новые ошибки","ar":"تصحيح الأخطاء بشكل منهجي هو عملية تساعد على تحديد السبب الجذري للمشاكل الفنية، وتجنب الحلول السريعة التي قد تسبب أخطاء جديدة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["找到问题的根源","避免随机修复","减少新 bug 的产生","提高解决问题的效率","适用于任何技术问题"],"ja":["根本原因を探す","ランダムな修復を避ける","新しいバグの発生を減らす","問題解決の効率を高める","テクニカルな問題に適する"],"ko":["근본 원인을 탐색","임의의 수정을 피함","새로운 버그의 발생을 줄임","문제 해결의 효율을 높임","기술적인 문제에 적합"],"es":["Encontrar la causa raíz de los problemas técnicos","Evitar soluciones temporales","Proporcionar un enfoque sistemático para la depuración","Reducir el tiempo de depuración","Mejorar la calidad del código"],"fr":["Trouver la cause profonde des problèmes techniques","Éviter les solutions temporaires","Fournir une approche systématique pour le débogage","Réduire le temps de débogage","Améliorer la qualité du code"],"de":["Die Ursache von technischen Problemen finden","Temporäre Lösungen vermeiden","Ein systematischer Ansatz für das Debugging bieten","Die Debugging-Zeit reduzieren","Die Code-Qualität verbessern"],"pt":["Identificação da causa raiz","Evita soluções rápidas que mascaram problemas","Reduz perdas de tempo","Melhora a qualidade do código","Aplicável a qualquer problema técnico"],"ru":["Определение коренной причины","Избегает быстрых решений, которые маскируют проблемы","Сокращает потери времени","Улучшает качество кода","Применимо к любой технической проблеме"],"ar":["تحديد السبب الجذري","تجنب الحلول السريعة التي تخفي المشاكل","تقليل فقدان الوقت","تحسين جودة الكود","يمكن تطبيقها على أي مشكلة فنية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["系统调试","技术问题解决","根源分析","高效解决","避免随机修复","减少新 bug"],"ja":["体系的デバッグ","テクニカルな問題解決","根本原因分析","効率的解決","ランダムな修復を避ける","新しいバグの減少"],"ko":["시스템 디버깅","기술적인 문제 해결","근본 원인 분석","효율적인 해결","임의의 수정을 피함","新的 버그의 감소"],"es":["depuración sistemática","causa raíz","problemas técnicos","soluciones temporales","enfoque sistemático","calidad del código"],"fr":["débogage systématique","cause profonde","problèmes techniques","solutions temporaires","approche systématique","qualité du code"],"de":["systematisches Debugging","Ursache","technische Probleme","temporäre Lösungen","systematischer Ansatz","Code-Qualität"],"pt":["depuração sistemática","causa raiz","soluções rápidas","problemas técnicos","qualidade do código","otimização de tempo"],"ru":["системная отладка","коренная причина","быстрые решения","технические проблемы","качество кода","оптимизация времени"],"ar":["تصحيح الأخطاء بشكل منهجي","السبب الجذري","الحلول السريعة","المشاكل الفنية","جودة الكود","تحسين الوقت"]}},"owner":"Faizan1421","repo":"skills-Ai","repoPath":"Faizan1421/skills-Ai","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","bodyPreview":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs","body":"# Systematic Debugging\n\n## Overview\n\nRandom fixes waste time and create new bugs. Quick patches mask underlying issues.\n\n**Core principle:** ALWAYS find root cause before attempting fixes. Symptom fixes are failure.\n\n**Violating the letter of this process is violating the spirit of debugging.**\n\n## The Iron Law\n\n```\nNO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST\n```\n\nIf you haven''t completed Phase 1, you cannot propose fixes.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse for ANY technical issue:\n- Test failures\n- Bugs in production\n- Unexpected behavior\n- Performance problems\n- Build failures\n- Integration issues\n\n**Use this ESPECIALLY when:**\n- Under time pressure (emergencies make guessing tempting)\n- \"Just one quick fix\" seems obvious\n- You''ve already tried multiple fixes\n- Previous fix didn''t work\n- You don''t fully understand the issue\n\n**Don''t skip when:**\n- Issue seems simple (simple bugs have root causes too)\n- You''re in a hurry (rushing guarantees rework)\n- Manager wants it fixed NOW (systematic is faster than thrashing)\n\n## The Four Phases\n\nYou MUST complete each phase before proceeding to the next.\n\n### Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation\n\n**BEFORE attempting ANY fix:**\n\n1. **Read Error Messages Carefully**\n   - Don''t skip past errors or warnings\n   - They often contain the exact solution\n   - Read stack traces completely\n   - Note line numbers, file paths, error codes\n\n2. **Reproduce Consistently**\n   - Can you trigger it reliably?\n   - What are the exact steps?\n   - Does it happen every time?\n   - If not reproducible → gather more data, don''t guess\n\n3. **Check Recent Changes**\n   - What changed that could cause this?\n   - Git diff, recent commits\n   - New dependencies, config changes\n   - Environmental differences\n\n4. **Gather Evidence in Multi-Component Systems**\n\n   **WHEN system has multiple components (CI → build → signing, API → service → database):**\n\n   **BEFORE proposing fixes, add diagnostic instrumentation:**\n   ```\n   For EACH component boundary:\n     - Log what data enters component\n     - Log what data exits component\n     - Verify environment/config propagation\n     - Check state at each layer\n\n   Run once to gather evidence showing WHERE it breaks\n   THEN analyze evidence to identify failing component\n   THEN investigate that specific component\n   ```\n\n   **Example (multi-layer system):**\n   ```bash\n   # Layer 1: Workflow\n   echo \"=== Secrets available in workflow: ===\"\n   echo \"IDENTITY: ${IDENTITY:+SET}${IDENTITY:-UNSET}\"\n\n   # Layer 2: Build script\n   echo \"=== Env vars in build script: ===\"\n   env | grep IDENTITY || echo \"IDENTITY not in environment\"\n\n   # Layer 3: Signing script\n   echo \"=== Keychain state: ===\"\n   security list-keychains\n   security find-identity -v\n\n   # Layer 4: Actual signing\n   codesign --sign \"$IDENTITY\" --verbose=4 \"$APP\"\n   ```\n\n   **This reveals:** Which layer fails (secrets → workflow ✓, workflow → build ✗)\n\n5. **Trace Data Flow**\n\n   **WHEN error is deep in call stack:**\n\n   See `root-cause-tracing.md` in this directory for the complete backward tracing technique.\n\n   **Quick version:**\n   - Where does bad value originate?\n   - What called this with bad value?\n   - Keep tracing up until you find the source\n   - Fix at source, not at symptom\n\n### Phase 2: Pattern Analysis\n\n**Find the pattern before fixing:**\n\n1. **Find Working Examples**\n   - Locate similar working code in same codebase\n   - What works that''s similar to what''s broken?\n\n2. **Compare Against References**\n   - If implementing pattern, read reference implementation COMPLETELY\n   - Don''t skim - read every line\n   - Understand the pattern fully before applying\n\n3. **Identify Differences**\n   - What''s different between working and broken?\n   - List every difference, however small\n   - Don''t assume \"that can''t matter\"\n\n4. **Understand Dependencies**\n   - What other components does this need?\n   - What settings, config, environment?\n   - What assumptions does it make?\n\n### Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing\n\n**Scientific method:**\n\n1. **Form Single Hypothesis**\n   - State clearly: \"I think X is the root cause because Y\"\n   - Write it down\n   - Be specific, not vague\n\n2. **Test Minimally**\n   - Make the SMALLEST possible change to test hypothesis\n   - One variable at a time\n   - Don''t fix multiple things at once\n\n3. **Verify Before Continuing**\n   - Did it work? Yes → Phase 4\n   - Didn''t work? Form NEW hypothesis\n   - DON''T add more fixes on top\n\n4. **When You Don''t Know**\n   - Say \"I don''t understand X\"\n   - Don''t pretend to know\n   - Ask for help\n   - Research more\n\n### Phase 4: Implementation\n\n**Fix the root cause, not the symptom:**\n\n1. **Create Failing Test Case**\n   - Simplest possible reproduction\n   - Automated test if possible\n   - One-off test script if no framework\n   - MUST have before fixing\n   - Use the `superpowers:test-driven-development` skill for writing proper failing tests\n\n2. **Implement Single Fix**\n   - Address the root cause identified\n   - ONE change at a time\n   - No \"while I''m here\" improvements\n   - No bundled refactoring\n\n3. **Verify Fix**\n   - Test passes now?\n   - No other tests broken?\n   - Issue actually resolved?\n\n4. **If Fix Doesn''t Work**\n   - STOP\n   - Count: How many fixes have you tried?\n   - If < 3: Return to Phase 1, re-analyze with new information\n   - **If ≥ 3: STOP and question the architecture (step 5 below)**\n   - DON''T attempt Fix #4 without architectural discussion\n\n5. **If 3+ Fixes Failed: Question Architecture**\n\n   **Pattern indicating architectural problem:**\n   - Each fix reveals new shared state/coupling/problem in different place\n   - Fixes require \"massive refactoring\" to implement\n   - Each fix creates new symptoms elsewhere\n\n   **STOP and question fundamentals:**\n   - Is this pattern fundamentally sound?\n   - Are we \"sticking with it through sheer inertia\"?\n   - Should we refactor architecture vs. continue fixing symptoms?\n\n   **Discuss with your human partner before attempting more fixes**\n\n   This is NOT a failed hypothesis - this is a wrong architecture.\n\n## Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process\n\nIf you catch yourself thinking:\n- \"Quick fix for now, investigate later\"\n- \"Just try changing X and see if it works\"\n- \"Add multiple changes, run tests\"\n- \"Skip the test, I''ll manually verify\"\n- \"It''s probably X, let me fix that\"\n- \"I don''t fully understand but this might work\"\n- \"Pattern says X but I''ll adapt it differently\"\n- \"Here are the main problems: [lists fixes without investigation]\"\n- Proposing solutions before tracing data flow\n- **\"One more fix attempt\" (when already tried 2+)**\n- **Each fix reveals new problem in different place**\n\n**ALL of these mean: STOP. Return to Phase 1.**\n\n**If 3+ fixes failed:** Question the architecture (see Phase 4.5)\n\n## your human partner''s Signals You''re Doing It Wrong\n\n**Watch for these redirections:**\n- \"Is that not happening?\" - You assumed without verifying\n- \"Will it show us...?\" - You should have added evidence gathering\n- \"Stop guessing\" - You''re proposing fixes without understanding\n- \"Ultrathink this\" - Question fundamentals, not just symptoms\n- \"We''re stuck?\" (frustrated) - Your approach isn''t working\n\n**When you see these:** STOP. Return to Phase 1.\n\n## Common Rationalizations\n\n| Excuse | Reality |\n|--------|---------|\n| \"Issue is simple, don''t need process\" | Simple issues have root causes too. Process is fast for simple bugs. |\n| \"Emergency, no time for process\" | Systematic debugging is FASTER than guess-and-check thrashing. |\n| \"Just try this first, then investigate\" | First fix sets the pattern. Do it right from the start. |\n| \"I''ll write test after confirming fix works\" | Untested fixes don''t stick. Test first proves it. |\n| \"Multiple fixes at once saves time\" | Can''t isolate what worked. Causes new bugs. |\n| \"Reference too long, I''ll adapt the pattern\" | Partial understanding guarantees bugs. Read it completely. |\n| \"I see the problem, let me fix it\" | Seeing symptoms ≠ understanding root cause. |\n| \"One more fix attempt\" (after 2+ failures) | 3+ failures = architectural problem. Question pattern, don''t fix again. |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Phase | Key Activities | Success Criteria |\n|-------|---------------|------------------|\n| **1. Root Cause** | Read errors, reproduce, check changes, gather evidence | Understand WHAT and WHY |\n| **2. Pattern** | Find working examples, compare | Identify differences |\n| **3. Hypothesis** | Form theory, test minimally | Confirmed or new hypothesis |\n| **4. Implementation** | Create test, fix, verify | Bug resolved, tests pass |\n\n## When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"\n\nIf systematic investigation reveals issue is truly environmental, timing-dependent, or external:\n\n1. You''ve completed the process\n2. Document what you investigated\n3. Implement appropriate handling (retry, timeout, error message)\n4. Add monitoring/logging for future investigation\n\n**But:** 95% of \"no root cause\" cases are incomplete investigation.\n\n## Supporting Techniques\n\nThese techniques are part of systematic debugging and available in this directory:\n\n- **`root-cause-tracing.md`** - Trace bugs backward through call stack to find original trigger\n- **`defense-in-depth.md`** - Add validation at multiple layers after finding root cause\n- **`condition-based-waiting.md`** - Replace arbitrary timeouts with condition polling\n\n**Related skills:**\n- **superpowers:test-driven-development** - For creating failing test case (Phase 4, Step 1)\n- **superpowers:verification-before-completion** - Verify fix worked before claiming success\n\n## Real-World Impact\n\nFrom debugging sessions:\n- Systematic approach: 15-30 minutes to fix\n- Random fixes approach: 2-3 hours of thrashing\n- First-time fix rate: 95% vs 40%\n- New bugs introduced: Near zero vs common\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:34:22.920Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Troubleshooting Agents needing structured root cause analysis capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要结构化根因分析能力的技术故障排除代理。","ja":"技術トラブルシューティングエージェントが構造化された根本原因分析機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"구조화된 근본 원인 분석 기능이 필요한 기술 문제 해결 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Resolución Técnica que necesitan capacidades de análisis de causa raíz estructuradas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de dépannage technique ayant besoin de capacités d''analyse de cause racine structurées.","de":"Perfekt für technische Troubleshooting-Agenten, die strukturierte Root-Cause-Analysefunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Resolução Técnica que necessitam de capacidades de análise de causa raiz estruturada.","ru":"Идеально подходит для технических агентов по устранению неполадок, которым необходимы возможности структурированного анализа коренной причины.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات إصلاح الفنيين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات تحليل السبب الجذري المهيكلة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to conduct thorough root cause investigations using the Iron Law, ensuring NO FIXES WITHOUT ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION FIRST, and providing a systematic approach to debugging technical issues like test failures and bugs.","zh":"赋予代理进行彻底的根本原因调查的能力，使用铁律，确保在进行根本原因调查之前不进行修复，并提供一种系统性的方法来调试技术问题，如测试失败和错误。","ja":"エージェントが鉄則を使用して徹底的な根本原因調査を実施できるようにし、根本原因調査を先に実施することを保証し、テストの失敗やバグなどの技術的な問題をデバッグするための体系的なアプローチを提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 철법을 사용하여 철저한 근본 원인 조사를 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 근본 원인 조사를 먼저 수행하는 것을 보장하며, 테스트 실패 및 버그와 같은 기술적인 문제를 디버깅하는 체계적인 접근 방식을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar investigaciones exhaustivas de causa raíz utilizando la Ley de Hierro, asegurando NO HAY REPARACIONES SIN INVESTIGACIÓN DE CAUSA RAÍZ PRIMERO, y proporcionando un enfoque sistemático para depurar problemas técnicos como fallos de prueba y errores.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mener des enquêtes approfondies sur les causes racines en utilisant la Loi de Fer, en garantissant AUCUNE CORRECTION SANS ENQUÊTE SUR LA CAUSE RACINE D''ABORD, et en fournissant une approche systématique pour déboguer les problèmes techniques tels que les défaillances de test et les bogues.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, gründliche Root-Cause-Untersuchungen mit dem Eisernen Gesetz durchzuführen, um SICHERZUSTELLEN, DASS ES KEINE REPARATUREN OHNE VORHERIGE ROOT-CAUSE-UNTERSUCHUNG GIBT, und bietet einen systematischen Ansatz zur Fehlersuche bei technischen Problemen wie Testfehlern und Fehlern.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar investigações aprofundadas de causa raiz usando a Lei de Ferro, garantindo NENHUMA CORREÇÃO SEM INVESTIGAÇÃO DE CAUSA RAIZ EM PRIMEIRO LUGAR, e fornecendo uma abordagem sistemática para depurar problemas técnicos como falhas de teste e bugs.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить тщательные расследования коренной причины с использованием Железного закона, гарантируя НИ ОДНОГО ИСПРАВЛЕНИЯ БЕЗ РАССЛЕДОВАНИЯ КОРЕННОЙ ПРИЧИНЫ СНАЧАЛА, и обеспечивая системный подход к отладке технических проблем, таких как сбой тестов и ошибки.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء إمكانية إجراء تحقيقات شاملة لتحليل السبب الجذري باستخدام قانون الحديد، مما ي đảmن عدم وجود أي إصلاح دون تحقيق السبب الجذري أولا، وتوفير نهج منهجي لتصحيح الأخطاء الفنية مثل فشل الاختبار والاخطاء البرمجية."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging complex software issues","Investigating test failures","Identifying root causes of recurring bugs"],"zh":["调试复杂的软件问题","调查测试失败","识别反复出现的错误的根因"],"ja":["複雑なソフトウェアの問題をデバッグする","テストの失敗を調査する","繰り返し発生するバグの根本原因を特定する"],"ko":["복잡한 소프트웨어 문제 디버깅","테스트 실패 조사","반복되는 버그의 근본 원인 식별"],"es":["Depuración de problemas de software complejos","Investigación de fallos de prueba","Identificación de las causas raíz de errores recurrentes"],"fr":["Débogage de problèmes de logiciel complexes","Enquête sur les défaillances de test","Identification des causes racines d''erreurs récurrentes"],"de":["Fehlersuche bei komplexen Softwareproblemen","Untersuchung von Testfehlern","Identifizierung der Root-Causes wiederkehrender Fehler"],"pt":["Depuração de problemas de software complexos","Investigação de falhas de teste","Identificação de causas raiz de bugs recorrentes"],"ru":["Отладка сложных проблем программного обеспечения","Расследование сбоя тестов","Определение коренной причины повторяющихся ошибок"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء البرمجيات المعقدة","تحقيق فشل الاختبار","تحديد السبب الجذري للأخطاء البرمجية المتكررة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to the Iron Law","Violating the letter of the process is considered violating the spirit of debugging"],"zh":["需要遵守铁律","违反流程的字母精神被认为是违反调试的精神"],"ja":["鉄則に従う必要がある","プロセスの文字を違反することはデバッグの精神を違反することとみなされる"],"ko":["철법을 준수해야 함","프로세스의 문자를 위반하는 것은 디버깅의 정신을 위반하는 것으로 간주됨"],"es":["Requiere adherencia a la Ley de Hierro","Violación de la letra del proceso se considera violación del espíritu de la depuración"],"fr":["Exige l''adhésion à la Loi de Fer","La violation de la lettre du processus est considérée comme une violation de l''esprit du débogage"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung des Eisernen Gesetzes","Verletzung des Buchstabens des Prozesses gilt als Verletzung des Geistes der Fehlersuche"],"pt":["Exige aderência à Lei de Ferro","Violar a letra do processo é considerado violar o espírito da depuração"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения Железного закона","Нарушение буквы процесса считается нарушением духа отладки"],"ar":["يتطلب الالتزام بقانون الحديد","مخالفة حرفية العملية تعتبر مخالفة لروح التصحيح"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block/tavily-web', 'community', 'andre-sugai', 'cine-explorer-mvp-block', 'andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block', 'tavily-web', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z', '2026-02-18T09:34:48.977Z', NULL, '{"id":"andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block/tavily-web","name":"tavily-web","description":{"zh":"Tavily Web技能提供网页搜索、内容提取和爬虫功能，帮助开发者快速获取所需信息","ja":"Tavily Webスキルは、ウェブ検索、コンテンツ抽出、クロール機能を提供し、開発者が必要な情報を迅速に取得するのに役立ちます","ko":"타빌리 웹 스킬은 웹 검색, 콘텐츠 추출 및 크롤링 기능을 제공하여 개발자가 필요한 정보를 빠르게 얻을 수 있습니다","pt":"A habilidade Tavily-Web fornece capacidades de busca, extração de conteúdo, crawling e pesquisa na web usando a API Tavily.","ru":"Навык Tavily-Web предоставляет возможности поиска, извлечения контента, crawling и исследования в сети с помощью API Tavily.","ar":"الوظيفة Tavily-Web توفر إمكانيات البحث واستخراج المحتوى والزحف والبحث على الويب باستخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات Tavily.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Tavily Web技能：网页搜索和内容提取","ja":"Tavily Webスキル：ウェブ検索とコンテンツ抽出","ko":"타빌리 웹 스킬: 웹 검색 및 콘텐츠 추출","pt":"Tavily-Web: Busca e Extração de Conteúdo na Web","ru":"Tavily-Web: Поиск и извлечение контента в сети","ar":"تافيلي-ويب: بحث و استخراج المحتوى على الويب","en":"tavily-web"},"description":{"zh":"Tavily Web技能提供网页搜索、内容提取和爬虫功能，帮助开发者快速获取所需信息","ja":"Tavily Webスキルは、ウェブ検索、コンテンツ抽出、クロール機能を提供し、開発者が必要な情報を迅速に取得するのに役立ちます","ko":"타빌리 웹 스킬은 웹 검색, 콘텐츠 추출 및 크롤링 기능을 제공하여 개발자가 필요한 정보를 빠르게 얻을 수 있습니다","pt":"A habilidade Tavily-Web fornece capacidades de busca, extração de conteúdo, crawling e pesquisa na web usando a API Tavily.","ru":"Навык Tavily-Web предоставляет возможности поиска, извлечения контента, crawling и исследования в сети с помощью API Tavily.","ar":"الوظيفة Tavily-Web توفر إمكانيات البحث واستخراج المحتوى والزحف والبحث على الويب باستخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات Tavily.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"fea