,"fr":"Les modèles de microservices permettent de concevoir des architectures distribuées évolutives et résilientes","de":"Muster für Microservices ermöglichen das Entwerfen verteilter Architekturen, die skalierbar und fehlertolerant sind","pt":"Padrões de microserviços para construir sistemas distribuídos escaláveis e resilientes","ru":"Шаблоны микросервисов для построения масштабируемых и отказоустойчивых распределенных систем","ar":"أنماط الميكروسيرفس لتصميم أنظمة موزعة قابلة للتوسع والتحمل","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["服务边界设计","服务间通信实现","数据管理和事务处理","弹性和容错性设计","服务发现和负载均衡"],"ja":["サービス境界設計","サービス間通信の実装","データ管理とトランザクション処理","耐久性と障害耐性の設計","サービス発見と負荷分散"],"ko":["서비스 경계設計","서비스 간 통신 구현","데이터 관리 및 트랜잭션 처리","탄력성 및 장애 허용 설계","서비스 발견 및 부하 분산"],"es":["Descomposición de monolitos en microservicios","Diseño de límites y contratos de servicio","Implementación de comunicación entre servicios","Gestión de datos y transacciones distribuidas","Construcción de sistemas distribuidos resilientes"],"fr":["Décomposition de monolithes en microservices","Conception de limites et de contrats de service","Mise en œuvre de la communication entre services","Gestion de données et de transactions distribuées","Construction de systèmes distribués résilients"],"de":["Zerlegung von Monolithen in Microservices","Entwurf von Dienstgrenzen und -verträgen","Implementierung der Kommunikation zwischen Diensten","Verwaltung von verteilten Daten und Transaktionen","Aufbau von fehlertoleranten verteilten Systemen"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de limites de serviço","Comunicação entre serviços","Gerenciamento de dados distribuídos","Padrões de resiliência","Descoberta de serviço e balanceamento de carga"],"ru":["Разработка границ сервиса","Межсервисное взаимодействие","Управление распределенными данными","Шаблоны отказоустойчивости","Обнаружение сервиса и балансировка нагрузки"],"ar":["تصميم حدود الخدمة","التواصل بين الخدمات","إدارة البيانات الموزعة","أنماط التحمل","اكتشاف الخدمة وتوازن الحمل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["微服务","分布式系统","服务边界","服务间通信","数据管理","弹性","容错性","服务发现","负载均衡"],"ja":["マイクロサービス","分散システム","サービス境界","サービス間通信","データ管理","耐久性","障害耐性","サービス発見","負荷分散"],"ko":["마이크로 서비스","분산 시스템","서비스 경계","서비스 간 통신","데이터 관리","탄력성","장애 허용","서비스 발견","부하 분산"],"es":["patrones de microservicios","arquitecturas distribuidas","diseño de microservicios","comunicación entre servicios","gestión de datos distribuidos","sistemas distribuidos resilientes"],"fr":["modèles de microservices","architectures distribuées","conception de microservices","communication entre services","gestion de données distribuées","systèmes distribués résilients"],"de":["Muster für Microservices","verteile Architekturen","Entwurf von Microservices","Kommunikation zwischen Diensten","Verwaltung von verteilten Daten","fehlertolerante verteilte Systeme"],"pt":["microserviços","arquitetura de microserviços","sistemas distribuídos","padrões de microserviços","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software"],"ru":["микросервисы","архитектура микросервисов","распределенные системы","шаблоны микросервисов","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения"],"ar":["الميكروسيرفس","هندسة الميكروسيرفس","أنظمة موزعة","أنماط الميكروسيرفس","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"yashvinthan","repo":"DuskSpendr","repoPath":"yashvinthan/DuskSpendr","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.479Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"microservices-patterns","description":"Design microservices architectures with service boundaries, event-driven communication, and resilience patterns. Use when building distributed systems, decomposing monoliths, or implementing microservices.","bodyPreview":"# Microservices Patterns\n\nMaster microservices architecture patterns including service boundaries, inter-service communication, data management, and resilience patterns for building distributed systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Decomposing monoliths into microservices\n- Designing service boundaries and contracts\n- Implementing inter-service communication\n- Managing distributed data and transactions\n- Building resilient distributed systems\n- Implementing service discovery and load balancing","body":"# Microservices Patterns\n\nMaster microservices architecture patterns including service boundaries, inter-service communication, data management, and resilience patterns for building distributed systems.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Decomposing monoliths into microservices\n- Designing service boundaries and contracts\n- Implementing inter-service communication\n- Managing distributed data and transactions\n- Building resilient distributed systems\n- Implementing service discovery and load balancing\n- Designing event-driven architectures\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Service Decomposition Strategies\n\n**By Business Capability**\n\n- Organize services around business functions\n- Each service owns its domain\n- Example: OrderService, PaymentService, InventoryService\n\n**By Subdomain (DDD)**\n\n- Core domain, supporting subdomains\n- Bounded contexts map to services\n- Clear ownership and responsibility\n\n**Strangler Fig Pattern**\n\n- Gradually extract from monolith\n- New functionality as microservices\n- Proxy routes to old/new systems\n\n### 2. Communication Patterns\n\n**Synchronous (Request/Response)**\n\n- REST APIs\n- gRPC\n- GraphQL\n\n**Asynchronous (Events/Messages)**\n\n- Event streaming (Kafka)\n- Message queues (RabbitMQ, SQS)\n- Pub/Sub patterns\n\n### 3. Data Management\n\n**Database Per Service**\n\n- Each service owns its data\n- No shared databases\n- Loose coupling\n\n**Saga Pattern**\n\n- Distributed transactions\n- Compensating actions\n- Eventual consistency\n\n### 4. Resilience Patterns\n\n**Circuit Breaker**\n\n- Fail fast on repeated errors\n- Prevent cascade failures\n\n**Retry with Backoff**\n\n- Transient fault handling\n- Exponential backoff\n\n**Bulkhead**\n\n- Isolate resources\n- Limit impact of failures\n\n## Service Decomposition Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: By Business Capability\n\n```python\n# E-commerce example\n\n# Order Service\nclass OrderService:\n    \"\"\"Handles order lifecycle.\"\"\"\n\n    async def create_order(self, order_data: dict) -> Order:\n        order = Order.create(order_data)\n\n        # Publish event for other services\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\n            OrderCreatedEvent(\n                order_id=order.id,\n                customer_id=order.customer_id,\n                items=order.items,\n                total=order.total\n            )\n        )\n\n        return order\n\n# Payment Service (separate service)\nclass PaymentService:\n    \"\"\"Handles payment processing.\"\"\"\n\n    async def process_payment(self, payment_request: PaymentRequest) -> PaymentResult:\n        # Process payment\n        result = await self.payment_gateway.charge(\n            amount=payment_request.amount,\n            customer=payment_request.customer_id\n        )\n\n        if result.success:\n            await self.event_bus.publish(\n                PaymentCompletedEvent(\n                    order_id=payment_request.order_id,\n                    transaction_id=result.transaction_id\n                )\n            )\n\n        return result\n\n# Inventory Service (separate service)\nclass InventoryService:\n    \"\"\"Handles inventory management.\"\"\"\n\n    async def reserve_items(self, order_id: str, items: List[OrderItem]) -> ReservationResult:\n        # Check availability\n        for item in items:\n            available = await self.inventory_repo.get_available(item.product_id)\n            if available < item.quantity:\n                return ReservationResult(\n                    success=False,\n                    error=f\"Insufficient inventory for {item.product_id}\"\n                )\n\n        # Reserve items\n        reservation = await self.create_reservation(order_id, items)\n\n        await self.event_bus.publish(\n            InventoryReservedEvent(\n                order_id=order_id,\n                reservation_id=reservation.id\n            )\n        )\n\n        return ReservationResult(success=True, reservation=reservation)\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: API Gateway\n\n```python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Depends\nimport httpx\nfrom circuitbreaker import circuit\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nclass APIGateway:\n    \"\"\"Central entry point for all client requests.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.order_service_url = \"http://order-service:8000\"\n        self.payment_service_url = \"http://payment-service:8001\"\n        self.inventory_service_url = \"http://inventory-service:8002\"\n        self.http_client = httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=5.0)\n\n    @circuit(failure_threshold=5, recovery_timeout=30)\n    async def call_order_service(self, path: str, method: str = \"GET\", **kwargs):\n        \"\"\"Call order service with circuit breaker.\"\"\"\n        response = await self.http_client.request(\n            method,\n            f\"{self.order_service_url}{path}\",\n            **kwargs\n        )\n        response.raise_for_status()\n        return response.json()\n\n    async def create_order_aggregate(self, order_id: str) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Aggregate data from multiple services.\"\"\"\n        # Parallel requests\n        order, payment, inventory = await asyncio.gather(\n            self.call_order_service(f\"/orders/{order_id}\"),\n            self.call_payment_service(f\"/payments/order/{order_id}\"),\n            self.call_inventory_service(f\"/reservations/order/{order_id}\"),\n            return_exceptions=True\n        )\n\n        # Handle partial failures\n        result = {\"order\": order}\n        if not isinstance(payment, Exception):\n            result[\"payment\"] = payment\n        if not isinstance(inventory, Exception):\n            result[\"inventory\"] = inventory\n\n        return result\n\n@app.post(\"/api/orders\")\nasync def create_order(\n    order_data: dict,\n    gateway: APIGateway = Depends()\n):\n    \"\"\"API Gateway endpoint.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Route to order service\n        order = await gateway.call_order_service(\n            \"/orders\",\n            method=\"POST\",\n            json=order_data\n        )\n        return {\"order\": order}\n    except httpx.HTTPError as e:\n        raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=\"Order service unavailable\")\n```\n\n## Communication Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Synchronous REST Communication\n\n```python\n# Service A calls Service B\nimport httpx\nfrom tenacity import retry, stop_after_attempt, wait_exponential\n\nclass ServiceClient:\n    \"\"\"HTTP client with retries and timeout.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, base_url: str):\n        self.base_url = base_url\n        self.client = httpx.AsyncClient(\n            timeout=httpx.Timeout(5.0, connect=2.0),\n            limits=httpx.Limits(max_keepalive_connections=20)\n        )\n\n    @retry(\n        stop=stop_after_attempt(3),\n        wait=wait_exponential(multiplier=1, min=2, max=10)\n    )\n    async def get(self, path: str, **kwargs):\n        \"\"\"GET with automatic retries.\"\"\"\n        response = await self.client.get(f\"{self.base_url}{path}\", **kwargs)\n        response.raise_for_status()\n        return response.json()\n\n    async def post(self, path: str, **kwargs):\n        \"\"\"POST request.\"\"\"\n        response = await self.client.post(f\"{self.base_url}{path}\", **kwargs)\n        response.raise_for_status()\n        return response.json()\n\n# Usage\npayment_client = ServiceClient(\"http://payment-service:8001\")\nresult = await payment_client.post(\"/payments\", json=payment_data)\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Asynchronous Event-Driven\n\n```python\n# Event-driven communication with Kafka\nfrom aiokafka import AIOKafkaProducer, AIOKafkaConsumer\nimport json\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, asdict\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\n@dataclass\nclass DomainEvent:\n    event_id: str\n    event_type: str\n    aggregate_id: str\n    occurred_at: datetime\n    data: dict\n\nclass EventBus:\n    \"\"\"Event publishing and subscription.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, bootstrap_servers: List[str]):\n        self.bootstrap_servers = bootstrap_servers\n        self.producer = None\n\n    async def start(self):\n        self.producer = AIOKafkaProducer(\n            bootstrap_servers=self.bootstrap_servers,\n            value_serializer=lambda v: json.dumps(v).encode()\n        )\n        await self.producer.start()\n\n    async def publish(self, event: DomainEvent):\n        \"\"\"Publish event to Kafka topic.\"\"\"\n        topic = event.event_type\n        await self.producer.send_and_wait(\n            topic,\n            value=asdict(event),\n            key=event.aggregate_id.encode()\n        )\n\n    async def subscribe(self, topic: str, handler: callable):\n        \"\"\"Subscribe to events.\"\"\"\n        consumer = AIOKafkaConsumer(\n            topic,\n            bootstrap_servers=self.bootstrap_servers,\n            value_deserializer=lambda v: json.loads(v.decode()),\n            group_id=\"my-service\"\n        )\n        await consumer.start()\n\n        try:\n            async for message in consumer:\n                event_data = message.value\n                await handler(event_data)\n        finally:\n            await consumer.stop()\n\n# Order Service publishes event\nasync def create_order(order_data: dict):\n    order = await save_order(order_data)\n\n    event = DomainEvent(\n        event_id=str(uuid.uuid4()),\n        event_type=\"OrderCreated\",\n        aggregate_id=order.id,\n        occurred_at=datetime.now(),\n        data={\n            \"order_id\": order.id,\n            \"customer_id\": order.customer_id,\n            \"total\": order.total\n        }\n    )\n\n    await event_bus.publish(event)\n\n# Inventory Service listens for OrderCreated\nasync def handle_order_created(event_data: dict):\n    \"\"\"React to order creation.\"\"\"\n    order_id = event_data[\"data\"][\"order_id\"]\n    items = event_data[\"data\"][\"items\"]\n\n    # Reserve inventory\n    await reserve_inventory(order_id, items)\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Saga Pattern (Distributed Transactions)\n\n```python\n# Saga orchestration for order fulfillment\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom typing import List, Callable\n\nclass SagaStep:\n    \"\"\"Single step in saga.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        name: str,\n        action: Callable,\n        compensation: Callable\n    ):\n        self.name = name\n        self.action = action\n        self.compensation = compensation\n\nclass SagaStatus(Enum):\n    PENDING = \"pending\"\n    COMPLETED = \"completed\"\n    COMPENSATING = \"compensating\"\n    FAILED = \"failed\"\n\nclass OrderFulfillmentSaga:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrated saga for order fulfillment.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.steps: List[SagaStep] = [\n            SagaStep(\n                \"create_order\",\n                action=self.create_order,\n                compensation=self.cancel_order\n            ),\n            SagaStep(\n                \"reserve_inventory\",\n                action=self.reserve_inventory,\n                compensation=self.release_inventory\n            ),\n            SagaStep(\n                \"process_payment\",\n                action=self.process_payment,\n                compensation=self.refund_payment\n            ),\n            SagaStep(\n                \"confirm_order\",\n                action=self.confirm_order,\n                compensation=self.cancel_order_confirmation\n            )\n        ]\n\n    async def execute(self, order_data: dict) -> SagaResult:\n        \"\"\"Execute saga steps.\"\"\"\n        completed_steps = []\n        context = {\"order_data\": order_data}\n\n        try:\n            for step in self.steps:\n                # Execute step\n                result = await step.action(context)\n                if not result.success:\n                    # Compensate\n                    await self.compensate(completed_steps, context)\n                    return SagaResult(\n                        status=SagaStatus.FAILED,\n                        error=result.error\n                    )\n\n                completed_steps.append(step)\n                context.update(result.data)\n\n            return SagaResult(status=SagaStatus.COMPLETED, data=context)\n\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Compensate on error\n            await self.compensate(completed_steps, context)\n            return SagaResult(status=SagaStatus.FAILED, error=str(e))\n\n    async def compensate(self, completed_steps: List[SagaStep], context: dict):\n        \"\"\"Execute compensating actions in reverse order.\"\"\"\n        for step in reversed(completed_steps):\n            try:\n                await step.compensation(context)\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Log compensation failure\n                print(f\"Compensation failed for {step.name}: {e}\")\n\n    # Step implementations\n    async def create_order(self, context: dict) -> StepResult:\n        order = await order_service.create(context[\"order_data\"])\n        return StepResult(success=True, data={\"order_id\": order.id})\n\n    async def cancel_order(self, context: dict):\n        await order_service.cancel(context[\"order_id\"])\n\n    async def reserve_inventory(self, context: dict) -> StepResult:\n        result = await inventory_service.reserve(\n            context[\"order_id\"],\n            context[\"order_data\"][\"items\"]\n        )\n        return StepResult(\n            success=result.success,\n            data={\"reservation_id\": result.reservation_id}\n        )\n\n    async def release_inventory(self, context: dict):\n        await inventory_service.release(context[\"reservation_id\"])\n\n    async def process_payment(self, context: dict) -> StepResult:\n        result = await payment_service.charge(\n            context[\"order_id\"],\n            context[\"order_data\"][\"total\"]\n        )\n        return StepResult(\n            success=result.success,\n            data={\"transaction_id\": result.transaction_id},\n            error=result.error\n        )\n\n    async def refund_payment(self, context: dict):\n        await payment_service.refund(context[\"transaction_id\"])\n```\n\n## Resilience Patterns\n\n### Circuit Breaker Pattern\n\n```python\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom typing import Callable, Any\n\nclass CircuitState(Enum):\n    CLOSED = \"closed\"  # Normal operation\n    OPEN = \"open\"      # Failing, reject requests\n    HALF_OPEN = \"half_open\"  # Testing if recovered\n\nclass CircuitBreaker:\n    \"\"\"Circuit breaker for service calls.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        failure_threshold: int = 5,\n        recovery_timeout: int = 30,\n        success_threshold: int = 2\n    ):\n        self.failure_threshold = failure_threshold\n        self.recovery_timeout = recovery_timeout\n        self.success_threshold = success_threshold\n\n        self.failure_count = 0\n        self.success_count = 0\n        self.state = CircuitState.CLOSED\n        self.opened_at = None\n\n    async def call(self, func: Callable, *args, **kwargs) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Execute function with circuit breaker.\"\"\"\n\n        if self.state == CircuitState.OPEN:\n            if self._should_attempt_reset():\n                self.state = CircuitState.HALF_OPEN\n            else:\n                raise CircuitBreakerOpenError(\"Circuit breaker is open\")\n\n        try:\n            result = await func(*args, **kwargs)\n            self._on_success()\n            return result\n\n        except Exception as e:\n            self._on_failure()\n            raise\n\n    def _on_success(self):\n        \"\"\"Handle successful call.\"\"\"\n        self.failure_count = 0\n\n        if self.state == CircuitState.HALF_OPEN:\n            self.success_count += 1\n            if self.success_count >= self.success_threshold:\n                self.state = CircuitState.CLOSED\n                self.success_count = 0\n\n    def _on_failure(self):\n        \"\"\"Handle failed call.\"\"\"\n        self.failure_count += 1\n\n        if self.failure_count >= self.failure_threshold:\n            self.state = CircuitState.OPEN\n            self.opened_at = datetime.now()\n\n        if self.state == CircuitState.HALF_OPEN:\n            self.state = CircuitState.OPEN\n            self.opened_at = datetime.now()\n\n    def _should_attempt_reset(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Check if enough time passed to try again.\"\"\"\n        return (\n            datetime.now() - self.opened_at\n            > timedelta(seconds=self.recovery_timeout)\n        )\n\n# Usage\nbreaker = CircuitBreaker(failure_threshold=5, recovery_timeout=30)\n\nasync def call_payment_service(payment_data: dict):\n    return await breaker.call(\n        payment_client.process_payment,\n        payment_data\n    )\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/service-decomposition-guide.md**: Breaking down monoliths\n- **references/communication-patterns.md**: Sync vs async patterns\n- **references/saga-implementation.md**: Distributed transactions\n- **assets/circuit-breaker.py**: Production circuit breaker\n- **assets/event-bus-template.py**: Kafka event bus implementation\n- **assets/api-gateway-template.py**: Complete API gateway\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Service Boundaries**: Align with business capabilities\n2. **Database Per Service**: No shared databases\n3. **API Contracts**: Versioned, backward compatible\n4. **Async When Possible**: Events over direct calls\n5. **Circuit Breakers**: Fail fast on service failures\n6. **Distributed Tracing**: Track requests across services\n7. **Service Registry**: Dynamic service discovery\n8. **Health Checks**: Liveness and readiness probes\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Distributed Monolith**: Tightly coupled services\n- **Chatty Services**: Too many inter-service calls\n- **Shared Databases**: Tight coupling through data\n- **No Circuit Breakers**: Cascade failures\n- **Synchronous Everything**: Tight coupling, poor resilience\n- **Premature Microservices**: Starting with microservices\n- **Ignoring Network Failures**: Assuming reliable network\n- **No Compensation Logic**: Can''t undo failed transactions\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:37:23.826Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Distributed System Agents needing advanced microservices architecture patterns for building resilient distributed systems.","zh":"非常适合需要高级微服务架构模式来构建强健分布式系统的分布式系统代理。","ja":"高度なマイクロサービスアーキテクチャパターンを使用して堅牢な分散システムを構築する必要がある分散システムエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 마이크로 서비스 아키텍처 패턴을 사용하여 강건한 분산 시스템을 구축하는 분산 시스템 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Sistemas Distribuidos que necesitan patrones de arquitectura de microservicios avanzados para construir sistemas distribuidos resistentes.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Systèmes Distribués ayant besoin de modèles d''architecture de microservices avancés pour construire des systèmes distribués résistants.","de":"Perfekt für verteilte Systemagenten, die erweiterte Muster für Mikrodienstarchitekturen zum Aufbau resilienter verteilter Systeme benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Sistemas Distribuídos que necessitam de padrões avançados de arquitetura de microsserviços para construir sistemas distribuídos resilientes.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов распределенных систем, которым необходимы продвинутые шаблоны микросервисной архитектуры для создания устойчивых распределенных систем.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء أنظمة التوزيع التي تحتاج إلى أنماط متقدمة من هندسة الخدمات الدقيقة لبناء نظم موزعة مرنة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design service boundaries and contracts, implement inter-service communication using protocols such as REST or gRPC, and manage distributed data and transactions with patterns like event sourcing or CQRS, ensuring resilient distributed systems through service discovery and load balancing.","zh":"使代理能够设计服务边界和契约，使用REST或gRPC等协议实现服务间通信，并使用事件源或CQRS等模式管理分布式数据和事务，通过服务发现和负载均衡确保强健的分布式系统。","ja":"エージェントがサービス境界と契約を設計し、RESTまたはgRPCなどのプロトコルを使用してサービス間の通信を実装し、イベントソーシングまたはCQRSなどのパターンを使用して分散データとトランザクションを管理し、サービス発見と負荷分散によって堅牢な分散システムを保証する。","ko":"에이전트가 서비스 경계와 계약을 설계하고 REST 또는 gRPC와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 서비스 간의 통신을 구현하며 이벤트 소싱 또는 CQRS와 같은 패턴을 사용하여 분산 데이터와 트랜잭션을 관리하여 서비스 발견과 부하 분산을 통해 강건한 분산 시스템을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar límites y contratos de servicio, implementar la comunicación entre servicios utilizando protocolos como REST o gRPC, y gestionar datos y transacciones distribuidas con patrones como la fuente de eventos o CQRS, garantizando sistemas distribuidos resistentes a través del descubrimiento de servicios y el equilibrio de carga.","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir les limites et les contrats de service, de mettre en œuvre la communication entre services en utilisant des protocoles tels que REST ou gRPC, et de gérer les données et les transactions distribuées avec des modèles tels que la source d''événements ou CQRS, garantissant ainsi des systèmes distribués résistants grâce à la découverte de services et à l''équilibrage de charge.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Dienstgrenzen und -verträge zu entwerfen, die Kommunikation zwischen Diensten mithilfe von Protokollen wie REST oder gRPC zu implementieren und verteilte Daten und Transaktionen mit Mustern wie Ereignisquellen oder CQRS zu verwalten, wodurch resiliente verteilte Systeme durch Diensterkennung und Lastenausgleich gewährleistet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar limites e contratos de serviço, implementar comunicação entre serviços usando protocolos como REST ou gRPC e gerenciar dados e transações distribuídas com padrões como fonte de eventos ou CQRS, garantindo sistemas distribuídos resilientes por meio de descoberta de serviço e balanceamento de carga.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать границы и контракты сервисов, реализовывать межсервисное общение с использованием таких протоколов, как REST или gRPC, и управлять распределенными данными и транзакциями с помощью шаблонов, таких как источник событий или CQRS, обеспечивая устойчивые распределенные системы посредством службы обнаружения и балансировки нагрузки.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تصميم حدود و عقود الخدمة وتنفيذ الاتصالات بين الخدمات باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل REST أو gRPC وإدارة البيانات والoperations الموزعة باستخدام أنماط مثل مصدر الحدث أو CQRS، مما يضمن نظم موزعة مرنة من خلال اكتشاف الخدمة وتوازن الحمل."},"useCases":{"en":["Decomposing monolithic applications into scalable microservices","Implementing inter-service communication and data management for distributed systems","Building resilient distributed systems with service discovery and load balancing"],"zh":["将单体应用程序分解为可扩展的微服务","为分布式系统实现服务间通信和数据管理","使用服务发现和负载均衡构建强健的分布式系统"],"ja":["モノリシックアプリケーションをスケーラブルなマイクロサービスに分解する","分散システムのサービス間通信とデータ管理を実装する","サービス発見と負荷分散を使用して堅牢な分散システムを構築する"],"ko":["모놀리틱 애플리케이션을 확장 가능한 마이크로 서비스로 분해하는 것","분산 시스템을 위한 서비스 간 통신 및 데이터 관리 구현","서비스 발견 및 부하 분산을 사용하여 강건한 분산 시스템을 구축하는 것"],"es":["Descomponer aplicaciones monolíticas en microservicios escalables","Implementar la comunicación y gestión de datos entre servicios para sistemas distribuidos","Construir sistemas distribuidos resistentes con descubrimiento de servicios y equilibrio de carga"],"fr":["Décomposer les applications monolithiques en microservices évolutifs","Mettre en œuvre la communication et la gestion des données entre services pour les systèmes distribués","Construire des systèmes distribués résistants avec la découverte de services et l''équilibrage de charge"],"de":["Monolithische Anwendungen in skalierbare Mikrodienste zerlegen","Implementierung der Kommunikation und Datenverwaltung zwischen Diensten für verteilte Systeme","Aufbau resilienter verteilter Systeme mit Diensterkennung und Lastenausgleich"],"pt":["Decompor aplicações monolíticas em microsserviços escaláveis","Implementar comunicação entre serviços e gerenciamento de dados para sistemas distribuídos","Construir sistemas distribuídos resilientes com descoberta de serviço e balanceamento de carga"],"ru":["Разделение монолитных приложений на масштабируемые микросервисы","Реализация межсервисного общения и управления данными для распределенных систем","Создание устойчивых распределенных систем с помощью службы обнаружения и балансировки нагрузки"],"ar":["تجزئة التطبيقات أحادية البنية إلى خدمات دقيقة قابلة للتوسيع","تنفيذ الاتصالات بين الخدمات وإدارة البيانات لأنظمة التوزيع","بناء نظم موزعة مرنة باستخدام اكتشاف الخدمة وتوازن الحمل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of distributed system fundamentals","Limited to microservices architecture patterns, not applicable to monolithic architectures"],"zh":["需要理解分布式系统的基本知识","仅限于微服务架构模式，不适用于单体架构"],"ja":["分散システムの基本を理解する必要がある","マイクロサービスアーキテクチャパターンに限定され、モノリシックアーキテクチャには適用できない"],"ko":["분산 시스템의 기본 지식 이해 필요","마이크로 서비스 아키텍처 패턴으로 제한되며 모놀리틱 아키텍처에는 적용할 수 없음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de los fundamentos de los sistemas distribuidos","Limitado a patrones de arquitectura de microservicios, no aplicable a arquitecturas monolíticas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension des principes fondamentaux des systèmes distribués","Limité aux modèles d''architecture de microservices, non applicable aux architectures monolithiques"],"de":["Erfordert Verständnis der Grundlagen verteilter Systeme","Begrenzt auf Muster für Mikrodienstarchitekturen, nicht anwendbar auf monolithische Architekturen"],"pt":["Exige entendimento dos fundamentos de sistemas distribuídos","Limitado a padrões de arquitetura de microsserviços, não se aplica a arquiteturas monolíticas"],"ru":["Требует понимания основ распределенных систем","Ограничен шаблонами микросервисной архитектуры, не применимо к монолитным архитектурам"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم أساسيات أنظمة التوزيع","محدود لأنماط هندسة الخدمات الدقيقة، لا ينطبق على البنيات أحادية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
