nbitlang/moon","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.480Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"snapbox-testing","description":"Write and maintain Rust CLI/integration tests with snapbox 0.6+ using command assertions, inline snapshots, and minimal wildcard/redaction patterns. Use when replacing manual `get_output` parsing, stabilizing cross-platform snapshots, or refining existing snapbox assertions.","bodyPreview":"# Snapbox Testing\n\nUse this skill to make Rust command-output tests simpler, more stable, and easier to review.\n\n## Follow This Workflow\n\n1. Replace manual output plumbing with direct snapbox assertions.\n2. Start from empty inline snapshots (`snapbox::str![\"\"]`) for unstable/unknown output.\n3. Run tests with `SNAPSHOTS=overwrite` to capture real output.\n4. Tighten snapshots by keeping stable text exact and wildcarding only volatile parts.\n5. Re-run tests and clippy.\n\nUse:\n\n```bash\nSNAPSHOTS=over","body":"# Snapbox Testing\n\nUse this skill to make Rust command-output tests simpler, more stable, and easier to review.\n\n## Follow This Workflow\n\n1. Replace manual output plumbing with direct snapbox assertions.\n2. Start from empty inline snapshots (`snapbox::str![\"\"]`) for unstable/unknown output.\n3. Run tests with `SNAPSHOTS=overwrite` to capture real output.\n4. Tighten snapshots by keeping stable text exact and wildcarding only volatile parts.\n5. Re-run tests and clippy.\n\nUse:\n\n```bash\nSNAPSHOTS=overwrite cargo test -p <crate> --test <test-target>\n```\n\n## Prefer These Patterns\n\n- Assert command result directly:\n  - `.assert().success().stdout_eq(...)`\n  - `.assert().failure().stderr_eq(...)`\n- Prefer inline snapshots:\n  - `snapbox::str![[r#\"...\\n\"#]]` for multi-line outputs\n  - string literals for short exact lines\n- Keep assertions local and readable:\n  - inline expected value when used once\n  - avoid temporary `expected_*` bindings unless reused\n\n## Minimize Redaction\n\n- Prefer built-in wildcard filters first:\n  - `[..]` for variable substrings within a line\n  - `...` on its own line for variable trailing frames/lines\n- Keep stable semantics visible:\n  - preserve meaningful suffixes like `/_build/.../main.wasm`\n  - avoid over-redacting fixed tokens (for example, exact error kind/message)\n- Add custom `Redactions` only when wildcard patterns cannot express the instability clearly.\n\n## Cross-Platform Guidance\n\n- Rely on snapbox default path normalization before adding platform-specific `cfg` snapshots.\n- Use one snapshot when separator normalization is sufficient.\n- Add `cfg(windows)`/`cfg(not(windows))` split only for truly semantic OS differences.\n\n## Avoid\n\n- Manual `.get_output().stdout/stderr` + UTF-8 parsing when direct assertions work.\n- Hand-written normalization helpers for paths/stack traces when snapbox patterns can express intent.\n- Broad wildcarding that hides behavior regressions.\n\n## Quick Checklist\n\n- `cargo fmt --all`\n- `cargo test -p <crate> --test <target>`\n- `cargo clippy -p <crate> --tests -- -D warnings`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:40:08.604Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Rust-focused AI Agents seeking to streamline command-output testing with snapbox assertions.","zh":"适用于专注于Rust的AI代理，旨在使用snapbox断言简化命令输出测试的场景。","ja":"Rustに重点を置いたAIエージェントが、snapboxアサーションを使用してコマンド出力テストを簡素化する場合に適しています。","ko":"Rust를 중점으로 하는 AI 에이전트가 스냅박스(assertion)을 사용하여 명령어 출력 테스트를 간소화하려는 경우에 이상적입니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de AI enfocados en Rust que buscan simplificar la prueba de la salida de comandos con aserciones de snapbox.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA axés sur Rust cherchant à rationaliser les tests de sortie de commande avec des assertions snapbox.","de":"Ideal für Rust-fokussierte KI-Agents, die die Kommando-Ausgabetestung mit Snapbox-Assertions rationalisieren möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA com foco em Rust que buscam simplificar os testes de saída de comando com afirmações do snapbox.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на Rust, стремящихся оптимизировать тестирование вывода команд с помощью утверждений snapbox.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يركز على Rust والذي يسعى لتبسيط اختبار إخراج الأوامر باستخدام تأكيدات snapbox."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to simplify Rust command-output tests using direct snapbox assertions, facilitating more stable and reviewable tests with features like inline snapshots and wildcarding for volatile output parts, all leveraging the snapbox library.","zh":"赋予代理简化Rust命令输出测试的能力，使用直接的snapbox断言，通过内联快照和对易变输出部分的通配等功能，促进更稳定和可审查的测试，所有这些都依赖于snapbox库。","ja":"エージェントにRustのコマンド出力テストを簡素化する能力を提供します。直接のsnapboxアサーションを使用し、インラインスナップショットや不安定な出力部分のワイルドカードなどの機能を活用して、より安定したレビュー可能なテストを促進します。すべてこれらはsnapboxライブラリを活用しています。","ko":"에이전트가 러스트 명령어 출력 테스트를 간소화할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 직접 스냅박스(assertion)을 사용하여 인라인 스냅샷 및 변동성 있는 출력 부분에 대한 와일드카드 등의 기능을 통해 더 안정적이고 검토 가능한 테스트를促進하며, 모든 이는 스냅박스 라이브러리를 활용하는 것입니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes simplificar las pruebas de salida de comandos de Rust utilizando aserciones de snapbox directas, lo que facilita pruebas más estables y revisables con características como instantáneas en línea y comodines para partes de salida volátiles, todo aprovechando la biblioteca snapbox.","fr":"Permet aux agents de simplifier les tests de sortie de commande Rust en utilisant des assertions snapbox directes, facilitant ainsi des tests plus stables et révisables avec des fonctionnalités comme des instantanés en ligne et des caractères génériques pour les parties de sortie volatiles, le tout en exploitant la bibliothèque snapbox.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Rust-Kommando-Ausgabetests mithilfe direkter Snapbox-Assertions zu vereinfachen, wodurch stabilere und überprüfbare Tests mit Funktionen wie Inline-Snapshot und Platzhalter für volatile Ausgabeanteile ermöglicht werden, all dies unter Ausnutzung der Snapbox-Bibliothek.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a simplificar os testes de saída de comando Rust usando afirmações diretas do snapbox, facilitando testes mais estáveis e revisáveis com recursos como capturas de tela inline e wildcarding para partes voláteis de saída, tudo aproveitando a biblioteca snapbox.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью упростить тесты вывода команд Rust с помощью прямых утверждений snapbox, облегчая более стабильные и просматриваемые тесты с функциями, такими как инлайн-снимки и подстановочные знаки для волатильных частей вывода, все это, используя библиотеку snapbox.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تبسيط اختبارات إخراج الأوامر في Rust باستخدام تأكيدات snapbox المباشرة، وبالتالي تسهيل الاختبارات الأكثر استقرارًا ومراجعة باستخدام ميزات مثل اللقطات المضمنة وتحديد النمط للجزء المتغير من الإخراج، وكل ذلك بالاستفادة من مكتبة snapbox."},"useCases":{"en":["Simplifying manual output plumbing in Rust tests","Generating and managing inline snapshots for unstable output","Tightening snapshots to ensure test stability and reliability"],"zh":["简化Rust测试中的手动输出管道","为不稳定输出生成和管理内联快照","通过紧密的快照来确保测试的稳定性和可靠性"],"ja":["Rustテストにおける手動出力パイプラインの簡素化","不安定な出力に対するインラインスナップショットの生成と管理","スナップショットを絞ってテストの安定性と信頼性を確保する"],"ko":["러스트 테스트의 수동 출력 파이프라인을 간소화하는こと","불안정한 출력에 대한 인라인 스냅샷 생성 및 관리","스냅샷을 조여 테스트의 안정성과 신뢰성을 확보하는 것"],"es":["Simplificar la configuración manual de la salida en las pruebas de Rust","Generar y administrar instantáneas en línea para salidas inestables","Ajustar las instantáneas para garantizar la estabilidad y confiabilidad de las pruebas"],"fr":["Simplifier le raccordement manuel de la sortie dans les tests Rust","Générer et gérer des instantanés en ligne pour des sorties instables","Resserrer les instantanés pour assurer la stabilité et la fiabilité des tests"],"de":["Vereinfachen der manuellen Ausgabe-Verrohrung in Rust-Tests","Erzeugen und Verwalten von Inline-Snapshots für instabile Ausgaben","Anpassen der Snapshots, um die Teststabilität und -zuverlässigkeit zu gewährleisten"],"pt":["Simplificando a plomeria manual de saída em testes Rust","Gerando e gerenciando capturas de tela inline para saída instável","Ajustando capturas de tela para garantir a estabilidade e confiabilidade dos testes"],"ru":["Упрощая ручную прокладку вывода в тестах Rust","Генерируя и управляя инлайн-снимками для нестабильного вывода","Затягивая снимки для обеспечения стабильности и надежности тестов"],"ar":["تبسيط صنبور الإخراج اليدوي في اختبارات Rust","генерируя وتشغيل اللقطات المضمنة للإخراج غير المستقر","固定 اللقطات لضمان استقرار اختبار وثباته"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust environment","Specific to command-output testing","Needs SNAPSHOTS=overwrite for capturing real output"],"zh":["需要Rust环境","仅限于命令输出测试","需要SNAPSHOTS=overwrite来捕获真实输出"],"ja":["Rust環境が必要","コマンド出力テストに限定される","SNAPSHOTS=overwriteが必要で、実際の出力をキャプチャする"],"ko":["러스트 환경이 필요함","명령어 출력 테스트에만 국한됨","SNAPSHOTS=overwrite가 필요하여 실제 출력을 캡처하는 것"],"es":["Requiere entorno de Rust","Específico para pruebas de salida de comandos","Necesita SNAPSHOTS=overwrite para capturar la salida real"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Rust","Spécifique aux tests de sortie de commande","Nécessite SNAPSHOTS=overwrite pour capturer la sortie réelle"],"de":["Benötigt Rust-Umgebung","Spezifisch für Kommando-Ausgabetests","Benötigt SNAPSHOTS=overwrite, um die reale Ausgabe aufzuzeichnen"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Rust","Específico para testes de saída de comando","Necessita SNAPSHOTS=overwrite para capturar saída real"],"ru":["Требует среды Rust","Конкретно для тестирования вывода команд","Требует SNAPSHOTS=overwrite для захвата реального вывода"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Rust","محدد لاختبار إخراج الأوامر","يحتاج SNAPSHOTS=overwrite لالتقاط الإخراج الفعلي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('edgeandnode/amp/code-review', 'community', 'edgeandnode', 'amp', 'edgeandnode/amp', 'code-review', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.480Z', '2026-02-18T09:40:48.123Z', NULL, '{"id":"edgeandnode/amp/code-review","name":"code-review","description":{"zh":"代码审查技能为代码变更提供全面评估，确保代码质量和安全","ja":"コードレビュースキルはコードの変更に対して包括的な評価を提供し、コード品質とセキュリティを確保","ko":"코드 리뷰 스킬은 코드 변경에 대한 완벽한 평가를 제공하여 코드 품질과 보안을 확보","es":"La revisión de código es crucial para garantizar la calidad y seguridad de tu proyecto de blockchain. Esta habilidad proporciona una guía detallada para evaluar cambios en el código.","fr":"La revue de code est cruciale pour garantir la qualité et la sécurité de votre projet de blockchain. Cette compétence fournit un guide détaillé pour évaluer les modifications du code.","de":"Die Code-Review ist entscheidend, um die Qualität und Sicherheit Ihres Blockchain-Projekts zu gewährleisten. Diese Fähigkeit bietet eine detaillierte Anleitung zur Bewertung von Code-Änderungen.","en":"The blockchain native database"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码审查技能 - 提高代码质量","ja":"コードレビュースキル - コード品質の向上","ko":"코드 리뷰 스킬 - 코드 품질 향상","es":"Revisión de código para blockchain","fr":"Revue de code pour blockchain","de":"Code-Review für Blockchain","en":"code-review"},"description":{"zh":"代码审查技能为代码变更提供全面评估，确保代码质量和安全","ja":"コードレビュースキルはコードの変更に対して包括的な評価を提供し、コード品質とセキュリティを確保","ko":"코드 리뷰 스킬은 코드 변경에 대한 완벽한 평가를 제공하여 코드 품질과 보안을 확보","es":"La revisión de código es crucial para garantizar la calidad y seguridad de tu proyecto de blockchain. Esta habilidad proporciona una guía detallada para eval...","fr":"La revue de code est cruciale pour garantir la qualité et la sécurité de votre projet de blockchain. Cette compétence fournit un guide détaillé pour évaluer ...","de":"Die Code-Review ist entscheidend, um die Qualität und Sicherheit Ihres Blockchain-Projekts zu gewährleisten. Diese Fähigkeit bietet eine detaillierte Anleitu...","en":"The blockchain native database"},"definition":{"en":"The blockchain native database"},"features":{"zh":["代码变更评估","代码质量检查","安全性评估","代码风格检查","性能优化建议"],"ja":["コード変更の評価","コード品質のチェック","セキュリティの評価","コードスタイルのチェック","パフォーマンスの最適化提案"],"ko":["코드 변경 평가","코드 품질 검사","보안성 평가","코드 스타일 검사","성능 최적화 제안"],"es":["Revisión de solicitudes de extracción","Revisión de cambios de código antes de los commits","Auditoría de la calidad del código","Proporcionar comentarios sobre la implementación correcta"],"fr":["Revue des demandes d''extraction","Revue des modifications de code avant les commits","Audit de la qualité du code","Fournir des commentaires sur la mise en œuvre correcte"],"de":["Überprüfung von Pull-Requests","Überprüfung von Code-Änderungen vor Commits","Prüfung der Code-Qualität","Bereitstellung von Feedback zur Implementierung"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码质量","代码安全","代码风格","代码优化","代码评估","代码检查"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード品質","コードセキュリティ","コードスタイル","コード最適化","コード評価","コードチェック"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 품질","코드 보안","코드 스타일","코드 최적화","코드 평가","코드 검사"],"es":["revisión de código","blockchain","calidad del código","seguridad del código","desarrollo de software","mejora del código"],"fr":["revue de code","blockchain","qualité du code","sécurité du code","développement de logiciels","amélioration du code"],"de":["Code-Review","Blockchain","Code-Qualität","Code-Sicherheit","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Optimierung"]}},"owner":"edgeandnode","repo":"amp","repoPath":"edgeandnode/amp","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.480Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"code-review","description":"Review code changes for bugs, pattern violations, security, and quality. Use when reviewing PRs, code changes, or before commits.","bodyPreview":"# Code Review Skill\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive code review guidance for evaluating changes to the codebase.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Review pull requests\n- Review code changes before commits\n- Audit code quality and adherence to project standards\n- Provide feedback on implementation correctness and patterns\n\n## Review Checklist\n\nPlease review this code change and provide feedback on:\n\n### 1. Potential Bugs\n\nLook for common programming errors such as:","body":"# Code Review Skill\n\nThis skill provides comprehensive code review guidance for evaluating changes to the codebase.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Review pull requests\n- Review code changes before commits\n- Audit code quality and adherence to project standards\n- Provide feedback on implementation correctness and patterns\n\n## Review Checklist\n\nPlease review this code change and provide feedback on:\n\n### 1. Potential Bugs\n\nLook for common programming errors such as:\n- Off-by-one errors\n- Incorrect conditionals\n- Use of wrong variable when multiple variables of same type are in scope\n- `min` vs `max`, `first` vs `last`, flipped ordering\n- Iterating over hashmap/hashset in order-sensitive operations\n\n### 2. Panic Branches\n\nIdentify panic branches that cannot be locally proven to be unreachable:\n- `unwrap` or `expect` calls\n- Indexing operations\n- Panicking operations on external data\n\n**Note**: This overlaps with the error handling patterns documented in `docs/code/errors-handling.md`. Verify compliance with the project''s error handling standards.\n\n### 3. Dead Code\n\nFind dead code that is not caught by warnings:\n- Overriding values that should be read first\n- Silently dead code due to `pub`\n- `todo!()` or `dbg!()` macros left in production code\n\n### 4. Performance\n\nCheck for performance issues:\n- Blocking operations in async code\n- DB connection with lifetimes that exceed a local scope\n- Inefficient algorithms or data structures\n\n### 5. Inconsistencies\n\nLook for inconsistencies between comments and code:\n- Documentation that doesn''t match implementation\n- Misleading variable names or comments\n- Outdated comments after refactoring\n\n### 6. Backwards Compatibility\n\nVerify backwards compatibility is maintained:\n- Changes to `Deserialize` structs that break existing data\n- Check that DB migrations keep compatibility when possible:\n  - Use `IF NOT EXISTS`\n  - Avoid dropping columns or altering their data types\n  - Check if migration can be made friendly to rollbacks\n- Breaking changes to HTTP APIs or CLIs\n\n### 7. Documentation\n\nEnsure documentation is up-to-date:\n- The `config.sample.toml` should be kept up-to-date\n- API changes are reflected in OpenAPI specs\n- README and architectural docs reflect current behavior\n\n### 8. Security Concerns\n\nReview for security vulnerabilities:\n- Exposed secrets or credentials\n- Input validation and sanitization\n- SQL injection, XSS, or other OWASP Top 10 vulnerabilities\n- Authentication and authorization bypasses\n- For security-sensitive crates (admin-api, metadata-db), verify compliance with crate-specific security patterns in `docs/code/`\n\n### 9. Testing\n\nEvaluate test coverage and quality:\n- Reduced test coverage without justification\n- Tests that don''t actually test the intended behavior\n- Tests with race conditions or non-deterministic behavior\n- Integration tests that should be unit tests (or vice versa)\n- Changes to existing tests that weaken assertions\n- Changes to tests that are actually a symptom of breaking changes to user-visible behaviour\n\n### 10. Coding Pattern Violations\n\nReview the changeset against coding pattern groups. Follow these three steps in order.\n\n#### Step 1: Discover pattern groups\n\nRun the Glob tool with pattern `docs/code/*.md`. For each file, extract the **first kebab-case segment** of the filename (everything before the first `-`, or the whole name if there is no `-`). Group files that share the same first segment. Files whose first segment is unique form a single-file group.\n\nAlways include all non-crate groups. Only include `crate-<crate-name>` groups when the diff modifies files inside that crate''s directory.\n\nExamples of current groups:\n\n- `errors` — errors-handling, errors-reporting\n- `rust` — rust-modules, rust-modules-members, rust-types, rust-documentation, rust-service, rust-crate, rust-workspace\n- `test` — test-strategy, test-files, test-functions\n- `logging` — logging, logging-errors\n- `apps` — apps-cli\n- `services` — services\n- `extractors` — extractors\n- `crate-<crate-name>` — all `crate-<crate-name>*` files for that crate (e.g., `crate-admin-api` includes crate-admin-api and crate-admin-api-security)\n\n#### Step 2: Spawn one Task agent per group — in parallel\n\nFor **every** applicable group from Step 1, spawn a `general-purpose` Task agent. Send **all** Task tool calls in a single message so they run concurrently.\n\nEach agent''s prompt MUST include:\n\n1. **Which pattern files to read** — list the full paths (e.g., `docs/code/errors-handling.md`, `docs/code/errors-reporting.md`).\n2. **How to obtain the diff** — instruct the agent to run `git diff main...HEAD` (or the appropriate base) via the Bash tool.\n3. **What to do** — read every pattern file in the group, then review the diff for violations of any rule described in those patterns.\n4. **What to return** — a list of violations, each with: file path, line number or range, the violated rule (quote or paraphrase), and a brief explanation. If no violations are found, return `No violations found for group: <group>`.\n\nExample prompt for the `errors` group:\n\n> You are a code-review agent. Your job is to check a code diff for violations of the coding patterns in your assigned group.\n>\n> **Your group**: errors\n>\n> **Step 1**: Read these pattern docs using the Read tool:\n> - `docs/code/errors-handling.md`\n> - `docs/code/errors-reporting.md`\n>\n> **Step 2**: Get the diff by running: `git diff main...HEAD`\n>\n> **Step 3**: Review every changed line in the diff against every rule in the pattern docs you read. Only flag actual violations — do not flag code that is compliant.\n>\n> **Step 4**: Return your findings as a list. Each item must include:\n> - File path and line number(s)\n> - The specific rule violated (quote or paraphrase from the pattern doc)\n> - Brief explanation of why it is a violation\n>\n> If no violations are found, return: `No violations found for group: errors`\n\n#### Step 3: Collect findings and report\n\nAfter all Task agents complete, compile their results into the review output. Deduplicate any overlapping findings. Omit groups that reported no violations.\n\n### 11. Documentation Validation\n\nWhen reviewing PRs, validate documentation alignment:\n\n#### Format Validation\n\n- **Feature docs** (`docs/features/*.md`): Invoke `/feature-fmt-check` to validate format compliance\n- **Pattern docs** (`docs/code/*.md`): Invoke `/code-pattern-fmt-check` to validate format compliance\n\n#### Implementation Alignment\n\n- **Feature docs**: Invoke `/feature-validate` to verify feature documentation aligns with actual code implementation\n- Check whether code changes require feature doc updates (new features, changed behavior)\n- Check whether feature doc changes reflect actual implementation state\n\n**Process:**\n1. Check if PR modifies files in `docs/features/` or `docs/code/`\n2. If feature docs changed: Run `/feature-fmt-check` skill for format validation\n3. If pattern docs changed: Run `/code-pattern-fmt-check` skill for format validation\n4. If PR changes feature-related code OR feature docs: Run `/feature-validate` to verify alignment\n5. Report any format violations or implementation mismatches in the review\n\n## Important Guidelines\n\n### Focus on Actionable Feedback\n\n- Provide specific, actionable feedback on actual lines of code\n- Avoid general comments without code references\n- Reference specific file paths and line numbers\n- Suggest concrete improvements\n\n### Pattern Compliance is Critical\n\nPattern violations should be treated seriously as they:\n- Reduce codebase consistency\n- Make maintenance harder\n- May introduce security vulnerabilities (in security-sensitive crates)\n- Conflict with established architectural decisions\n\nAlways run the pattern violation review (section 10) as part of every code review.\n\n### Review Priority\n\nReview items in this priority order:\n1. **Security concerns** (highest priority)\n2. **Potential bugs** and **panic branches**\n3. **Backwards compatibility** issues\n4. **Coding pattern violations**\n5. **Testing** gaps\n6. **Performance** issues\n7. **Documentation** and **dead code**\n\n## Next Steps\n\nAfter completing the code review:\n1. Provide clear, prioritized feedback\n2. Distinguish between blocking issues (bugs, security) and suggestions (style, performance)\n3. Reference specific patterns from `docs/code/` when flagging violations\n4. Suggest using `/code-format`, `/code-check`, and `/code-test` skills to validate fixes\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:40:48.123Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing advanced code analysis and review capabilities for blockchain native databases","zh":"非常适合需要高级代码分析和审查能力的区块链本地数据库开发代理","ja":"ブロックチェーンネイティブデータベースを開発するエージェントが高度なコード分析およびレビュー機能を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"블록체인 네이티브 데이터베이스 개발 에이전트가 고급 코드 분석 및 검토 기능을 필요로 할 경우 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de análisis y revisión de código para bases de datos nativas de blockchain","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement qui nécessitent des capacités avancées d''analyse et de révision de code pour les bases de données natives de blockchain","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die erweiterte Code-Analyse- und Überprüfungsfunktionen für blockchain-native Datenbanken benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de análise e revisão de código para bancos de dados nativos de blockchain","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки, которым необходимы расширенные возможности анализа и проверки кода для баз данных, родных для блокчейна","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الناشئين الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات متقدمة للتحليل والمراجعة الشاملة للرمز البرمجي للقواعد المحلية لسلسلة الكتل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to detect potential bugs, audit code quality, and provide feedback on implementation correctness using comprehensive review checklists and adherence to project standards, including code changes and pull requests","zh":"赋予代理检测潜在错误、审计代码质量、并使用全面审查清单和项目标准提供对实现正确性的反馈，包括代码更改和拉取请求","ja":"エージェントが潜在的なバグを検出してコード品質を監査し、実装の正しさについてフィードバックを提供することを可能にします。包括的なレビュー チェックリストとプロジェクト標準の遵守、コードの変更とプルリクエストを含む","ko":"에이전트가 잠재적인 버그를 감지하고 코드 품질을 감사하며 구현의 올바름에 대한 피드백을 제공할 수 있도록 합니다. 포괄적인 검토 체크리스트 및 프로젝트 표준 준수, 코드 변경 및 풀 리퀘스트 포함","es":"Habilita a los agentes para detectar posibles errores, auditar la calidad del código y proporcionar retroalimentación sobre la corrección de la implementación utilizando listas de verificación de revisión comprehensiva y adherencia a los estándares del proyecto, incluyendo cambios de código y solicitudes de extracción","fr":"Permet aux agents de détecter les bogues potentiels, d''auditer la qualité du code et de fournir des commentaires sur la correction de la mise en œuvre en utilisant des listes de vérification de révision complète et le respect des normes du projet, y compris les modifications de code et les demandes d''extraction","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, potenzielle Fehler zu erkennen, die Codequalität zu überprüfen und Feedback zur Implementierungskorrektur zu geben, indem umfassende Überprüfungsprüflisten und die Einhaltung der Projektnormen verwendet werden, einschließlich Codeänderungen und Pull-Requests","pt":"Habilita os agentes a detectar possíveis bugs, auditar a qualidade do código e fornecer feedback sobre a correção da implementação usando listas de verificação abrangentes e aderência aos padrões do projeto, incluindo alterações de código e solicitações de pull","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обнаруживать потенциальные ошибки, аудировать качество кода и предоставлять обратную связь о правильности реализации с использованием всесторонних контрольных списков и соблюдением стандартов проекта, включая изменения кода и запросы на включение","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على اكتشاف الأخطاء المحتملة ومراجعة جودة الرمز البرمجي وتقديم ملاحظات حول صحة التنفيذ باستخدام قوائم مراجعة شاملة والامتثال لمعايير المشروع، بما في ذلك تغييرات الرمز البرمجي والطلبات السحابية"},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing pull requests for blockchain database projects","Auditing code quality and adherence to project standards","Providing feedback on implementation correctness and patterns for database development"],"zh":["审查区块链数据库项目的拉取请求","审计代码质量和遵守项目标准","对数据库开发的实现正确性和模式提供反馈"],"ja":["ブロックチェーンデータベースプロジェクトのプルリクエストをレビューする","コード品質とプロジェクト標準の遵守を監査する","データベース開発の実装の正しさとパターンについてフィードバックを提供する"],"ko":["블록체인 데이터베이스 프로젝트의 풀 리퀘스트 검토","코드 품질 및 프로젝트 표준 준수 감사","데이터베이스 개발의 구현 올바름 및 패턴에 대한 피드백 제공"],"es":["Revisar solicitudes de extracción para proyectos de bases de datos de blockchain","Auditar la calidad del código y la adherencia a los estándares del proyecto","Proporcionar retroalimentación sobre la corrección de la implementación y patrones para el desarrollo de bases de datos"],"fr":["Réviser les demandes d''extraction pour les projets de bases de données de blockchain","Auditer la qualité du code et le respect des normes du projet","Fournir des commentaires sur la correction de la mise en œuvre et les modèles pour le développement de bases de données"],"de":["Überprüfen von Pull-Requests für blockchain-Datenbankprojekte","Überprüfen der Codequalität und der Einhaltung der Projektnormen","Bereitstellen von Feedback zur Implementierungskorrektur und Muster für die Datenbankentwicklung"],"pt":["Revisar solicitações de pull para projetos de banco de dados de blockchain","Auditar a qualidade do código e aderência aos padrões do projeto","Fornecer feedback sobre a correção da implementação e padrões para desenvolvimento de banco de dados"],"ru":["Просмотр запросов на включение для проектов баз данных блокчейна","Аудит качества кода и соблюдения стандартов проекта","Предоставление обратной связи о правильности реализации и шаблонов для разработки баз данных"],"ar":["مراجعة الطلبات السحابية لمشاريع قواعد بيانات سلسلة الكتل","مراجعة جودة الرمز البرمجي والامتثال لمعايير المشروع","تقديم ملاحظات حول صحة التنفيذ وأنماط التطوير للقواعد المحلية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to codebase and project standards","Limited to reviewing code changes and pull requests"],"zh":["需要访问代码库和项目标准","仅限于审查代码更改和拉取请求"],"ja":["コードベースとプロジェクト標準へのアクセスが必要","コードの変更とプルリクエストのレビューのみに限定"],"ko":["코드베이스 및 프로젝트 표준에 대한 액세스가 필요","코드 변경 및 풀 리퀘스트의 검토만으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la base de código y los estándares del proyecto","Limitado a la revisión de cambios de código y solicitudes de extracción"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès à la base de code et aux normes du projet","Limité à la révision des modifications de code et des demandes d''extraction"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf den Codebase und die Projektnormen","Begrenzt auf die Überprüfung von Codeänderungen und Pull-Requests"],"pt":["Requer acesso à base de código e padrões do projeto","Limitado à revisão de alterações de código e solicitações de pull"],"ru":["Требует доступа к кодовой базе и стандартам проекта","Ограничен просмотром изменений кода и запросов на включение"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة الشفرة والقواعد الخاصة بالمشروع","محدود بمراجعة تغييرات الشفرة والطلبات السحابية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
