],"ru":["Очистка истории коммитов","Применение определенных коммитов к веткам","Поиск коммитов, которые ввели баги","Работа над несколькими функциями одновременно","Восстановление после ошибок или потерянных коммитов","Управление сложными рабочими процессами"],"ar":["تنظيف سجل الالتزامات","تطبيق الالتزامات المحددة على الفروع","العثور على الالتزامات التي أدخلت أخطاء","العمل على الميزات المتعددة في نفس الوقت","استعادة الأخطاء أو الالتزامات المفقودة","إدارة سير العمل المعقد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git 高级工作流","Git 技术","提交历史","合作","恢复","Git 错误","丢失提交","分支工作流"],"ja":["Git のアドバンスドワークフロー","Git テクニック","コミット履歴","コラボレーション","復旧","Git エラー","失われたコミット","ブランチワークフロー"],"ko":["Git 고급 워크플로","Git 기술","커밋 기록","협업","복구","Git 오류","잃어버린 커밋","브랜치 워크플로"],"es":["Git avanzado","flujos de trabajo de Git","colaboración en Git","recuperación de errores de Git","limpieza del historial de commits","aplicación de commits específicos","búsqueda de commits que introdujeron errores","trabajo en múltiples características simultáneamente"],"fr":["Git avancé","workflows Git","collaboration Git","récupération d''erreurs Git","nettoyage de l''historique des commits","application de commits spécifiques","recherche de commits qui ont introduit des bogues","travail sur plusieurs fonctionnalités simultanément"],"de":["Erweitertes Git","Git-Workflows","Git-Kollaboration","Wiederherstellung von Git-Fehlern","Bereinigung des Commit-Historie","Anwenden von spezifischen Commits","Suchen von Commits, die Fehler eingeführt haben","Arbeiten an mehreren Funktionen gleichzeitig"],"pt":["Git avançado","fluxos de trabalho do Git","técnicas do Git","colaboração efetiva","histórico limpo","recuperação de erros","gerenciamento de branches","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["Продвинутый Git","рабочие процессы Git","техники Git","эффективное сотрудничество","чистая история","восстановление после ошибок","управление ветками","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["جيت متقدم","سير عمل جيت","تقنيات جيت","التعاون الفعال","سجل نظيف","استعادة الأخطاء","إدارة الفروع","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"pythoninthegrasses","repo":"mt","repoPath":"pythoninthegrasses/mt","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.480Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"git-advanced-workflows","description":"Master advanced Git workflows including rebasing, cherry-picking, bisect, worktrees, and reflog to maintain clean history and recover from any situation. Use when managing complex Git histories, collaborating on feature branches, or troubleshooting repository issues.","bodyPreview":"# Git Advanced Workflows\n\nMaster advanced Git techniques to maintain clean history, collaborate effectively, and recover from any situation with confidence.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Cleaning up commit history before merging\n- Applying specific commits across branches\n- Finding commits that introduced bugs\n- Working on multiple features simultaneously\n- Recovering from Git mistakes or lost commits\n- Managing complex branch workflows\n- Preparing clean PRs for review\n- Synchronizing diverged b","body":"# Git Advanced Workflows\n\nMaster advanced Git techniques to maintain clean history, collaborate effectively, and recover from any situation with confidence.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Cleaning up commit history before merging\n- Applying specific commits across branches\n- Finding commits that introduced bugs\n- Working on multiple features simultaneously\n- Recovering from Git mistakes or lost commits\n- Managing complex branch workflows\n- Preparing clean PRs for review\n- Synchronizing diverged branches\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Interactive Rebase\n\nInteractive rebase is the Swiss Army knife of Git history editing.\n\n**Common Operations:**\n\n- `pick`: Keep commit as-is\n- `reword`: Change commit message\n- `edit`: Amend commit content\n- `squash`: Combine with previous commit\n- `fixup`: Like squash but discard message\n- `drop`: Remove commit entirely\n\n**Basic Usage:**\n\n```bash\n# Rebase last 5 commits\ngit rebase -i HEAD~5\n\n# Rebase all commits on current branch\ngit rebase -i $(git merge-base HEAD main)\n\n# Rebase onto specific commit\ngit rebase -i abc123\n```\n\n### 2. Cherry-Picking\n\nApply specific commits from one branch to another without merging entire branches.\n\n```bash\n# Cherry-pick single commit\ngit cherry-pick abc123\n\n# Cherry-pick range of commits (exclusive start)\ngit cherry-pick abc123..def456\n\n# Cherry-pick without committing (stage changes only)\ngit cherry-pick -n abc123\n\n# Cherry-pick and edit commit message\ngit cherry-pick -e abc123\n```\n\n### 3. Git Bisect\n\nBinary search through commit history to find the commit that introduced a bug.\n\n```bash\n# Start bisect\ngit bisect start\n\n# Mark current commit as bad\ngit bisect bad\n\n# Mark known good commit\ngit bisect good v1.0.0\n\n# Git will checkout middle commit - test it\n# Then mark as good or bad\ngit bisect good  # or: git bisect bad\n\n# Continue until bug found\n# When done\ngit bisect reset\n```\n\n**Automated Bisect:**\n\n```bash\n# Use script to test automatically\ngit bisect start HEAD v1.0.0\ngit bisect run ./test.sh\n\n# test.sh should exit 0 for good, 1-127 (except 125) for bad\n```\n\n### 4. Worktrees\n\nWork on multiple branches simultaneously without stashing or switching.\n\n```bash\n# List existing worktrees\ngit worktree list\n\n# Add new worktree for feature branch\ngit worktree add ../project-feature feature/new-feature\n\n# Add worktree and create new branch\ngit worktree add -b bugfix/urgent ../project-hotfix main\n\n# Remove worktree\ngit worktree remove ../project-feature\n\n# Prune stale worktrees\ngit worktree prune\n```\n\n### 5. Reflog\n\nYour safety net - tracks all ref movements, even deleted commits.\n\n```bash\n# View reflog\ngit reflog\n\n# View reflog for specific branch\ngit reflog show feature/branch\n\n# Restore deleted commit\ngit reflog\n# Find commit hash\ngit checkout abc123\ngit branch recovered-branch\n\n# Restore deleted branch\ngit reflog\ngit branch deleted-branch abc123\n```\n\n## Practical Workflows\n\n### Workflow 1: Clean Up Feature Branch Before PR\n\n```bash\n# Start with feature branch\ngit checkout feature/user-auth\n\n# Interactive rebase to clean history\ngit rebase -i main\n\n# Example rebase operations:\n# - Squash \"fix typo\" commits\n# - Reword commit messages for clarity\n# - Reorder commits logically\n# - Drop unnecessary commits\n\n# Force push cleaned branch (safe if no one else is using it)\ngit push --force-with-lease origin feature/user-auth\n```\n\n### Workflow 2: Apply Hotfix to Multiple Releases\n\n```bash\n# Create fix on main\ngit checkout main\ngit commit -m \"fix: critical security patch\"\n\n# Apply to release branches\ngit checkout release/2.0\ngit cherry-pick abc123\n\ngit checkout release/1.9\ngit cherry-pick abc123\n\n# Handle conflicts if they arise\ngit cherry-pick --continue\n# or\ngit cherry-pick --abort\n```\n\n### Workflow 3: Find Bug Introduction\n\n```bash\n# Start bisect\ngit bisect start\ngit bisect bad HEAD\ngit bisect good v2.1.0\n\n# Git checks out middle commit - run tests\nnpm test\n\n# If tests fail\ngit bisect bad\n\n# If tests pass\ngit bisect good\n\n# Git will automatically checkout next commit to test\n# Repeat until bug found\n\n# Automated version\ngit bisect start HEAD v2.1.0\ngit bisect run npm test\n```\n\n### Workflow 4: Multi-Branch Development\n\n```bash\n# Main project directory\ncd ~/projects/myapp\n\n# Create worktree for urgent bugfix\ngit worktree add ../myapp-hotfix hotfix/critical-bug\n\n# Work on hotfix in separate directory\ncd ../myapp-hotfix\n# Make changes, commit\ngit commit -m \"fix: resolve critical bug\"\ngit push origin hotfix/critical-bug\n\n# Return to main work without interruption\ncd ~/projects/myapp\ngit fetch origin\ngit cherry-pick hotfix/critical-bug\n\n# Clean up when done\ngit worktree remove ../myapp-hotfix\n```\n\n### Workflow 5: Recover from Mistakes\n\n```bash\n# Accidentally reset to wrong commit\ngit reset --hard HEAD~5  # Oh no!\n\n# Use reflog to find lost commits\ngit reflog\n# Output shows:\n# abc123 HEAD@{0}: reset: moving to HEAD~5\n# def456 HEAD@{1}: commit: my important changes\n\n# Recover lost commits\ngit reset --hard def456\n\n# Or create branch from lost commit\ngit branch recovery def456\n```\n\n## Advanced Techniques\n\n### Rebase vs Merge Strategy\n\n**When to Rebase:**\n\n- Cleaning up local commits before pushing\n- Keeping feature branch up-to-date with main\n- Creating linear history for easier review\n\n**When to Merge:**\n\n- Integrating completed features into main\n- Preserving exact history of collaboration\n- Public branches used by others\n\n```bash\n# Update feature branch with main changes (rebase)\ngit checkout feature/my-feature\ngit fetch origin\ngit rebase origin/main\n\n# Handle conflicts\ngit status\n# Fix conflicts in files\ngit add .\ngit rebase --continue\n\n# Or merge instead\ngit merge origin/main\n```\n\n### Autosquash Workflow\n\nAutomatically squash fixup commits during rebase.\n\n```bash\n# Make initial commit\ngit commit -m \"feat: add user authentication\"\n\n# Later, fix something in that commit\n# Stage changes\ngit commit --fixup HEAD  # or specify commit hash\n\n# Make more changes\ngit commit --fixup abc123\n\n# Rebase with autosquash\ngit rebase -i --autosquash main\n\n# Git automatically marks fixup commits\n```\n\n### Split Commit\n\nBreak one commit into multiple logical commits.\n\n```bash\n# Start interactive rebase\ngit rebase -i HEAD~3\n\n# Mark commit to split with ''edit''\n# Git will stop at that commit\n\n# Reset commit but keep changes\ngit reset HEAD^\n\n# Stage and commit in logical chunks\ngit add file1.py\ngit commit -m \"feat: add validation\"\n\ngit add file2.py\ngit commit -m \"feat: add error handling\"\n\n# Continue rebase\ngit rebase --continue\n```\n\n### Partial Cherry-Pick\n\nCherry-pick only specific files from a commit.\n\n```bash\n# Show files in commit\ngit show --name-only abc123\n\n# Checkout specific files from commit\ngit checkout abc123 -- path/to/file1.py path/to/file2.py\n\n# Stage and commit\ngit commit -m \"cherry-pick: apply specific changes from abc123\"\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Always Use --force-with-lease**: Safer than --force, prevents overwriting others'' work\n2. **Rebase Only Local Commits**: Don''t rebase commits that have been pushed and shared\n3. **Descriptive Commit Messages**: Future you will thank present you\n4. **Atomic Commits**: Each commit should be a single logical change\n5. **Test Before Force Push**: Ensure history rewrite didn''t break anything\n6. **Keep Reflog Aware**: Remember reflog is your safety net for 90 days\n7. **Branch Before Risky Operations**: Create backup branch before complex rebases\n\n```bash\n# Safe force push\ngit push --force-with-lease origin feature/branch\n\n# Create backup before risky operation\ngit branch backup-branch\ngit rebase -i main\n# If something goes wrong\ngit reset --hard backup-branch\n```\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n- **Rebasing Public Branches**: Causes history conflicts for collaborators\n- **Force Pushing Without Lease**: Can overwrite teammate''s work\n- **Losing Work in Rebase**: Resolve conflicts carefully, test after rebase\n- **Forgetting Worktree Cleanup**: Orphaned worktrees consume disk space\n- **Not Backing Up Before Experiment**: Always create safety branch\n- **Bisect on Dirty Working Directory**: Commit or stash before bisecting\n\n## Recovery Commands\n\n```bash\n# Abort operations in progress\ngit rebase --abort\ngit merge --abort\ngit cherry-pick --abort\ngit bisect reset\n\n# Restore file to version from specific commit\ngit restore --source=abc123 path/to/file\n\n# Undo last commit but keep changes\ngit reset --soft HEAD^\n\n# Undo last commit and discard changes\ngit reset --hard HEAD^\n\n# Recover deleted branch (within 90 days)\ngit reflog\ngit branch recovered-branch abc123\n```\n\n## Resources\n\n- **references/git-rebase-guide.md**: Deep dive into interactive rebase\n- **references/git-conflict-resolution.md**: Advanced conflict resolution strategies\n- **references/git-history-rewriting.md**: Safely rewriting Git history\n- **assets/git-workflow-checklist.md**: Pre-PR cleanup checklist\n- **assets/git-aliases.md**: Useful Git aliases for advanced workflows\n- **scripts/git-clean-branches.sh**: Clean up merged and stale branches\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:41:58.093Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing advanced Git workflow management and version control capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 Git 工作流管理和版本控制能力的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが高度な Git ワークフロー管理とバージョン管理機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 고급 Git 워크플로우 관리 및 버전 관리 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una gestión de flujo de trabajo de Git avanzada y capacidades de control de versiones.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une gestion de workflow Git avancée et de capacités de contrôle de version.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine erweiterte Git-Workflow-Verwaltung und Versionskontrollfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho do Git avançado e capacidades de controle de versão.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходим продвинутый менеджмент рабочего процесса Git и возможности контроля версий.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة متقدمة لتدفق العمل جيت وقدرات التحكم في الإصدار."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to maintain clean commit history, collaborate effectively across branches, and recover from Git mistakes using techniques like cherry-picking and rebasing, while managing complex branch workflows and preparing clean pull requests for review.","zh":"赋予代理维护干净的提交历史、在分支间有效合作、使用 cherry-picking 和 rebasing 等技术从 Git 错误中恢复的能力，同时管理复杂的分支工作流并准备干净的拉取请求供审查。","ja":"エージェントがクリーンなコミット履歴を維持し、ブランチ間で効果的に協力し、cherry-picking や rebasing などのテクニックを使用して Git のミスから復旧し、同時に複雑なブランチワークフローを管理し、クリーンなプルリクエストをレビューのために準備する能力を付与します。","ko":"에이전트가 깨끗한 커밋 기록을 유지하고 브랜치 간에 효과적으로 협력하며 체리 피킹 및 리베이스 등의 기술을 사용하여 Git 오류에서 복구하며 동시에 복잡한 브랜치 워크플로우를 관리하고 깨끗한 풀 리퀘스트를 검토를 위해 준비하는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mantener un historial de confirmaciones limpio, colaborar de manera efectiva en ramas y recuperarse de errores de Git utilizando técnicas como cherry-picking y rebasing, mientras gestiona flujos de trabajo de ramas complejos y prepara solicitudes de extracción limpias para revisión.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maintenir un historique de commits propre, de collaborer efficacement entre les branches et de se rétablir des erreurs Git en utilisant des techniques comme le cherry-picking et le rebasing, tout en gérant des flux de travail de branches complexes et en préparant des demandes d''extraction propres pour examen.","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, ein sauberes Commits-Historie beizubehalten, effektiv über Zweige hinweg zusammenzuarbeiten und von Git-Fehlern unter Verwendung von Techniken wie Cherry-Picking und Rebasing zu erholen, während komplexe Zweig-Workflows verwaltet und saubere Pull-Requests für die Überprüfung vorbereitet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a manter um histórico de confirmação limpo, colaborar de forma eficaz entre branches e se recuperar de erros do Git usando técnicas como cherry-picking e rebasing, enquanto gerencia fluxos de trabalho de branch complexos e prepara solicitações de pull limpas para revisão.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью поддерживать чистую историю коммитов, эффективно сотрудничать между ветками и восстанавливаться после ошибок Git с помощью техник, таких как cherry-picking и rebasing, а также управлять сложными рабочими процессами веток и готовить чистые запросы на принятие для рассмотрения.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من الحفاظ على تاريخ تحديثات نظيف، والتعاون بفعالية عبر الفروع، والتعافي من الأخطاء جيت باستخدام تقنيات مثل cherry-picking و rebasing، مع إدارة سير عمل الفروع المعقدة وإعداد طلبات سحب نظيفة للمراجعة."},"useCases":{"en":["Cleaning up commit history before merging","Applying specific commits across branches","Recovering from Git mistakes or lost commits"],"zh":["合并前清理提交历史","在分支间应用特定提交","从 Git 错误或丢失提交中恢复"],"ja":["マージ前のコミット履歴のクリーンアップ","ブランチ間で特定のコミットを適用","Git のミスまたは失われたコミットからの復旧"],"ko":["병합 전 커밋 기록 정리","브랜치 간에 특정 커밋 적용","Git 오류 또는 잃어버린 커밋에서 복구"],"es":["Limpieza del historial de confirmaciones antes de la fusión","Aplicación de confirmaciones específicas en ramas","Recuperación de errores de Git o confirmaciones perdidas"],"fr":["Nettoyage de l''historique des commits avant la fusion","Application de commits spécifiques entre les branches","Récupération des erreurs Git ou des commits perdus"],"de":["Bereinigung des Commits-Historie vor dem Zusammenführen","Anwenden spezifischer Commits über Zweige hinweg","Wiederherstellung von Git-Fehlern oder verlorenen Commits"],"pt":["Limpar o histórico de confirmação antes de mesclar","Aplicar confirmações específicas em branches","Recuperar-se de erros do Git ou confirmações perdidas"],"ru":["Очистка истории коммитов перед слиянием","Применение определенных коммитов к веткам","Восстановление после ошибок Git или потерянных коммитов"],"ar":["تنظيف تاريخ التحديثات قبل الدمج","تطبيق التحديثات المحددة عبر الفروع","استعادة الأخطاء جيت أو التحديثات المفقودة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation and configuration","Command-line interface interaction necessary"],"zh":["需要 Git 安装和配置","命令行接口交互必要"],"ja":["Git のインストールと設定が必要","コマンドラインインターフェイスの操作が必要"],"ko":["Git 설치 및 구성 필요","명령줄 인터페이스 상호작용 필요"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de Git","Interacción con la interfaz de línea de comandos necesaria"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de Git","Interaction avec l''interface de ligne de commande nécessaire"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Installation und -Konfiguration","Interaktion mit der Kommandozeilenoberfläche erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do Git","Interação com interface de linha de comando necessária"],"ru":["Требуется установка и конфигурация Git","Необходимо взаимодействие с командной строкой"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين جيت","يتطلب التفاعل مع واجهة سطر الأوامر"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
