标准","心理健康平台","日志消息格式","结构化日志数据"],"ja":["C#ログ記録","ログ規格","精神衛生プラットフォーム","ログメッセージ形式","構造化ログデータ"],"ko":["C# 로깅","로깅 표준","정신 건강 플랫폼","로그 메시지 형식","구조화된 로그 데이터"],"es":["registro C#","estándares de registro","journalización de aplicaciones","requisitos de plataforma de bienestar mental","guías de registro","registro estructurado"],"fr":["journalisation C#","normes de journalisation","journalisation d''applications","exigences de la plateforme de bien-être mental","directives de journalisation","journalisation structurée"],"de":["C#-Protokoll","Protokollstandards","Anwendungsprotokoll","Anforderungen der Plattform für psychische Gesundheit","Protokollrichtlinien","strukturiertes Protokoll"],"pt":["logging c#","padrões de logging","bem-estar mental","desenvolvimento de aplicativos","manutenção de software","depuração de erros"],"ru":["логирование c#","стандарты логирования","психическое здоровье","разработка приложений","обслуживание программного обеспечения","отладка ошибок"],"ar":["التسجيل c#","معيارات التسجيل","الصحة النفسية","تطوير البرامج","صيانة البرمجيات","تصحيح الأخطاء"]}},"owner":"ninjasitm","repo":"contracting-marketing-template","repoPath":"ninjasitm/contracting-marketing-template","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.480Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"logging","description":"Comprehensive logging standards for C# applications including structured logging, log levels, message formatting, and compliance guidelines","version":"1.0.0","tags":"","bodyPreview":"# Logging Standards for C# Applications\n\nComprehensive logging guidelines for consistent, structured, and maintainable logging across C# applications with emphasis on mental wellness platform requirements.\n\n## Core Logging Principles\n\n### Message Format Pattern\n\n**REQUIRED**: All log messages MUST follow this pattern:\n\n```\n[CLASS_NAME_OR_SERVICE]: MESSAGE\n```\n\nThe prefix should be the **actual class name or service name** where the logging occurs, enclosed in square brackets.\n\n### Examples by Lo","body":"# Logging Standards for C# Applications\n\nComprehensive logging guidelines for consistent, structured, and maintainable logging across C# applications with emphasis on mental wellness platform requirements.\n\n## Core Logging Principles\n\n### Message Format Pattern\n\n**REQUIRED**: All log messages MUST follow this pattern:\n\n```\n[CLASS_NAME_OR_SERVICE]: MESSAGE\n```\n\nThe prefix should be the **actual class name or service name** where the logging occurs, enclosed in square brackets.\n\n### Examples by Log Level\n\n#### Information Level\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[SystemNotificationService]: Notification {NotificationId} sent to user {UserId}\",\n    notificationId, userId);\n\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[ActivityController.Store]: Activity saved to database - ActivityId: {ActivityId}\",\n    activity.Id);\n\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[ContentService]: Retrieved {Count} published meditations for institution {InstitutionId}\",\n    count, institutionId);\n```\n\n#### Warning Level\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogWarning(\"[DeviceTokenService]: User {UserId} has no registered device tokens\", userId);\n\n_logger.LogWarning(\"[AnalyticsService]: Failed to queue event - {EventType}: {EventName} for UserId: {UserId}\",\n    eventType, eventName, userId);\n\n_logger.LogWarning(\"[BadgeEvaluationService]: Badge definition {BadgeId} not found during evaluation\", badgeId);\n```\n\n#### Error Level\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogError(ex, \"[BadgeService]: Failed to award badge {BadgeId} to user {UserId}\", badgeId, userId);\n\n_logger.LogError(ex, \"[NotificationService]: Failed to send notification {NotificationId}\", notificationId);\n\n_logger.LogError(ex, \"[ActivityController.Store]: Failed to track activity analytics for user {UserId}\", userId);\n```\n\n#### Debug Level\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogDebug(\"[CachedContentService]: Cache hit for content type {ContentType}\", contentType);\n\n_logger.LogDebug(\"[AnalyticsService]: Track event sent - Event: {EventName}, UserId: {UserId}, SessionId: {SessionId}\",\n    eventName, userId, sessionId);\n\n_logger.LogDebug(\"[ActivityController.Store]: MapEventToActivityType result - Event: {Event}, ContentType: {ContentType}, MappedActivityType: {ActivityType}\",\n    activity.Event, activity.ContentType, activityType ?? \"NULL\");\n```\n\n## Structured Logging Best Practices\n\n### 1. Use Named Parameters\n\n**✅ DO THIS** - Structured logging with named parameters:\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[NotificationService]: Notification {NotificationId} sent to user {UserId} at {Timestamp}\",\n    notificationId, userId, DateTime.UtcNow);\n```\n\n**❌ AVOID THIS** - String interpolation or concatenation:\n\n```csharp\n// Bad - loses structured logging benefits\n_logger.LogInformation($\"[NotificationService]: Notification {notificationId} sent to user {userId}\");\n```\n\n### 2. Include Relevant Entity IDs\n\nAlways include key identifiers for troubleshooting:\n\n- `UserId`\n- `NotificationId`\n- `ActivityId`\n- `BadgeId`\n- `ContentId`\n- `SessionId`\n- `InstitutionId`\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[BadgeService]: Badge {BadgeId} awarded to user {UserId} - TotalPoints: {Points}\",\n    badgeId, userId, totalPoints);\n```\n\n### 3. Exception Logging Format\n\n**Always use exception-first format**:\n\n```csharp\n// Correct - exception as first parameter\n_logger.LogError(ex, \"[ServiceName]: Error message with {ContextParam}\", contextValue);\n\n// Incorrect - exception in message\n_logger.LogError($\"[ServiceName]: Error occurred: {ex.Message}\");\n```\n\n## Log Levels Guide\n\n### Debug\n\n- **When**: Diagnostic information useful during development\n- **Examples**: Cache hits/misses, method entry/exit, internal state changes\n- **Audience**: Developers debugging specific issues\n- **Production**: Typically disabled in production\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogDebug(\"[UserActivityTrackingService]: Processing activity event - ActivityType: {ActivityType}, EntityId: {EntityId}\",\n    activityType, entityId);\n```\n\n### Information\n\n- **When**: Normal application flow, significant events\n- **Examples**: Successful operations, user actions, state transitions\n- **Audience**: Operations team, system monitoring\n- **Production**: Enabled, but should not be excessive\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[AnalyticsService]: Initialized with Segment integration (write key configured)\");\n```\n\n### Warning\n\n- **When**: Unexpected but recoverable situations\n- **Examples**: Missing optional data, fallback behavior triggered, performance degradation\n- **Audience**: Operations team for monitoring\n- **Production**: Always enabled\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogWarning(\"[ActivityController.Store]: {ErrorMessage}\", errorMessage);\n```\n\n### Error\n\n- **When**: Operation failures, exceptions\n- **Examples**: Database errors, external API failures, validation failures\n- **Audience**: Operations team, on-call engineers\n- **Production**: Always enabled, may trigger alerts\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogError(ex, \"[AnalyticsService]: Failed to send analytics event {EventName} for user {UserId}\",\n    eventName, userId);\n```\n\n### Critical\n\n- **When**: Application-threatening failures\n- **Examples**: Database connection lost, critical service unavailable\n- **Audience**: Immediate escalation to on-call\n- **Production**: Always enabled, triggers immediate alerts\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogCritical(ex, \"[DatabaseService]: Unable to establish database connection after {RetryAttempts} attempts\",\n    retryAttempts);\n```\n\n## Common Patterns by Component Type\n\n### Controllers\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[ActivityController.Store]: Received activity - Event: {Event}, ContentType: {ContentType}, SessionId: {SessionId}\",\n    data.Event, data.ContentType, data.SessionId);\n\n_logger.LogWarning(\"[ActivityController.Store]: {ErrorMessage}\", errorMessage);\n```\n\n### Services\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[BadgeService]: Evaluating badges for user {UserId} - ActivityType: {ActivityType}\",\n    userId, activityType);\n\n_logger.LogError(ex, \"[NotificationService]: Failed to process notification for user {UserId}\", userId);\n```\n\n### Background Jobs\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[NotificationSchedulingJobService]: Starting scheduled notification job\");\n\n_logger.LogWarning(\"[NotificationSchedulingJobService]: No notifications scheduled for processing\");\n```\n\n### Analytics & Tracking\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogDebug(\"[AnalyticsService]: Added sessionId {SessionId} to Segment context for user {UserId}\",\n    sessionId, userId);\n\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[AnalyticsService]: {EventType}: {EventName} - UserId: {UserId}, Properties: {Properties}\",\n    eventType, eventName, userId, FormatProperties(properties));\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n### ❌ Don''t Use Generic Prefixes\n\n```csharp\n// Bad - not specific enough\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[Service]: Operation completed\");\n\n// Good - identifies exact service\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[BadgeEvaluationService]: Badge evaluation completed for user {UserId}\", userId);\n```\n\n### ❌ Don''t Use \"SEGMENT\" or Technology Names\n\n```csharp\n// Bad - uses technology name instead of class name\n_logger.LogDebug(\"SEGMENT Track: {eventName}\");\n\n// Good - uses actual class name\n_logger.LogDebug(\"[AnalyticsService]: Track event sent - Event: {EventName}\", eventName);\n```\n\n### ❌ Don''t Log Sensitive Data\n\n```csharp\n// Bad - logs sensitive information\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[AuthService]: User logged in - Password: {Password}\", password);\n\n// Good - logs only non-sensitive identifiers\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[AuthService]: User {UserId} logged in successfully\", userId);\n```\n\n### ❌ Don''t Use String Interpolation in Log Messages\n\n```csharp\n// Bad - loses structured logging\n_logger.LogInformation($\"[Service]: User {userId} performed action\");\n\n// Good - uses structured logging\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[Service]: User {UserId} performed action\", userId);\n```\n\n### ❌ Don''t Log in Tight Loops Without Throttling\n\n```csharp\n// Bad - can flood logs\nforeach (var item in largeCollection)\n{\n    _logger.LogDebug(\"[Service]: Processing item {ItemId}\", item.Id);\n}\n\n// Good - log summary instead\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[Service]: Processing {Count} items\", largeCollection.Count);\n// Log only errors or specific cases\n```\n\n## Log Message Guidelines\n\n### Be Specific and Actionable\n\n```csharp\n// Bad - vague\n_logger.LogError(\"[Service]: Error occurred\");\n\n// Good - specific and actionable\n_logger.LogError(ex, \"[NotificationService]: Failed to send push notification to device {DeviceToken} - User: {UserId}\",\n    deviceToken, userId);\n```\n\n### Use Present Tense for Actions\n\n```csharp\n// Preferred\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[Service]: Processing request\");\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[Service]: Request processed successfully\");\n\n// Not preferred\n_logger.LogInformation(\"[Service]: Will process request\");\n```\n\n### Include Context for Troubleshooting\n\n```csharp\n_logger.LogWarning(\"[CachedContentService]: Cache miss for content type {ContentType} - InstitutionId: {InstitutionId}\",\n    contentType, institutionId);\n```\n\n## Performance Considerations\n\n### Use LogLevel Checks for Expensive Operations\n\n```csharp\nif (_logger.IsEnabled(LogLevel.Debug))\n{\n    var detailedInfo = ExpensiveSerializationMethod(data);\n    _logger.LogDebug(\"[Service]: Detailed state - {DetailedInfo}\", detailedInfo);\n}\n```\n\n### Avoid Logging in Hot Paths\n\nOnly log at Information level or higher in performance-critical code. Use Debug level sparingly.\n\n## Testing Logging\n\nWhen writing unit tests, verify logging behavior:\n\n```csharp\n_mockLogger.Verify(\n    x => x.Log(\n        LogLevel.Information,\n        It.IsAny<EventId>(),\n        It.Is<It.IsAnyType>((o, t) => o.ToString().Contains(\"[BadgeService]\")),\n        null,\n        It.IsAny<Func<It.IsAnyType, Exception, string>>()),\n    Times.Once);\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Scenario                | Log Level   | Include                           |\n| ----------------------- | ----------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Successful operation    | Information | Entity IDs, key parameters        |\n| Operation started       | Debug       | Context parameters                |\n| Unexpected but handled  | Warning     | What happened, how it was handled |\n| Operation failed        | Error       | Exception, entity IDs, context    |\n| System critical failure | Critical    | Exception, impact scope           |\n| Development debugging   | Debug       | Detailed state information        |\n\n## Compliance & Privacy\n\n### HIPAA/GDPR Considerations\n\n- **NEVER** log Protected Health Information (PHI)\n- **NEVER** log personally identifiable information (PII) beyond user IDs\n- **NEVER** log passwords, tokens, or credentials\n- Use hashed/anonymized identifiers where appropriate\n\n```csharp\n// Good - logs hashed user identifier\n_logger.LogDebug(\"[AnalyticsService]: Using hashed user ID for Segment\");\n\n// Bad - would log sensitive data\n// _logger.LogDebug(\"[AnalyticsService]: User email: {Email}\", userEmail);\n```\n\n---\n\n**Remember**: Consistent, structured logging is essential for troubleshooting production issues, monitoring application health, and maintaining a high-quality codebase. Follow these standards religiously to ensure logs are useful and actionable.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:42:49.488Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for C# Analysis Agents needing standardized logging practices with emphasis on mental wellness platform requirements.","zh":"非常适合需要标准化日志记录实践并强调心理健康平台要求的C#分析代理。","ja":"C#分析エージェントが標準化されたログ記録の実践を必要としており、メンタルウェルネスプラットフォームの要件を強調している場合に最適です。","ko":"표준화된 로깅 실践이 필요하고 정신 건강 플랫폼 요구 사항을 강조하는 C# 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de C# que necesitan prácticas de registro estandarizadas con énfasis en los requisitos de la plataforma de bienestar mental.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse C# ayant besoin de pratiques de journalisation standardisées avec une emphase sur les exigences de la plate-forme de bien-être mental.","de":"Perfekt für C#-Analyseagenten, die standardisierte Protokollpraktiken mit Schwerpunkt auf die Anforderungen der Plattform für psychische Gesundheit benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise C# que necessitam de práticas de registro padronizadas com ênfase nos requisitos da plataforma de bem-estar mental.","ru":"Идеально для агентов анализа C#, которым необходимы стандартизированные практики ведения журнала с учетом требований платформы психического благополучия.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل C# الذي يحتاج إلى ممارسات تسجيل معيارية مع التركيز على متطلبات منصة الرفاهية النفسية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement consistent and structured logging using the message format pattern, incorporating class names or service names for enhanced debugging and troubleshooting capabilities with protocols like C# logging standards.","zh":"赋予代理实现一致且结构化的日志记录，使用消息格式模式，结合类名或服务名以增强调试和故障排除能力，并支持C#日志标准等协议。","ja":"エージェントに一貫性と構造化されたログ記録を実装することを可能にし、メッセージ形式パターンを使用し、クラス名またはサービス名を組み込んでデバッグとトラブルシューティングの機能を強化し、C#ログ標準などのプロトコルをサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 일관성 있고 구조화된 로깅을 구현하도록 허용하며, 메시지 형식 패턴을 사용하고 클래스 이름 또는 서비스 이름을 포함하여 디버깅 및 문제 해결 기능을 강화하며 C# 로깅 표준 등의 프로토콜을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar un registro coherente y estructurado utilizando el patrón de formato de mensaje, incorporando nombres de clase o nombres de servicio para mejorar las capacidades de depuración y solución de problemas con protocolos como los estándares de registro de C#.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre un journalisation cohérente et structurée en utilisant le modèle de format de message, en incorporant des noms de classe ou des noms de service pour améliorer les capacités de débogage et de dépannage avec des protocoles comme les normes de journalisation C#.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, konsistentes und strukturiertes Protokollieren mithilfe des Nachrichtenformatmusters umzusetzen, wobei Klassennamen oder Dienstnamen für verbesserte Fehlersuche- und Debugging-Fähigkeiten mit Protokollen wie den C#-Protokollstandard integriert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a implementar um registro consistente e estruturado usando o padrão de formato de mensagem, incorporando nomes de classe ou nomes de serviço para capacidades de depuração e solução de problemas aprimoradas com protocolos como os padrões de registro C#.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью реализовывать последовательное и структурированное ведение журнала с использованием шаблона формата сообщения, включающего имена классов или имена служб для улучшения возможностей поиска и устранения неисправностей с протоколами, такими как стандарты ведения журнала C#.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تنفيذ تسجيل متسق ومنظم باستخدام نمط تنسيق الرسالة، وضمن أسماء الفئات أو أسماء الخدمة لتعزيز возможности فحص الأخطاء ومعالجتها ببروتوكولات مثل معايير تسجيل C#."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing logging standards for C# applications","Debugging issues using consistent log message formats","Maintaining logging consistency across mental wellness platforms"],"zh":["为C#应用程序实现日志记录标准","使用一致的日志消息格式调试问题","在心理健康平台中维护日志一致性"],"ja":["C#アプリケーションへのログ記録標準の実装","一貫したログメッセージ形式を使用した問題のデバッグ","メンタルウェルネスプラットフォームでのログの一貫性の維持"],"ko":["C# 애플리케이션에 대한 로깅 표준 구현","일관된 로그 메시지 형식을 사용한 문제 디버깅","정신 건강 플랫폼에서 로깅 일관성 유지"],"es":["Implementar estándares de registro para aplicaciones de C#","Depurar problemas mediante formatos de mensaje de registro coherentes","Mantener la coherencia de registro en plataformas de bienestar mental"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des normes de journalisation pour les applications C#","Déboguer les problèmes à l''aide de formats de message de journalisation cohérents","Maintenir la cohérence de la journalisation sur les plateformes de bien-être mental"],"de":["Implementierung von Protokollstandard für C#-Anwendungen","Fehlerbehebung mithilfe konsistenter Protokollnachrichtenformate","Aufrechterhaltung der Protokollkonsistenz auf Plattformen für psychische Gesundheit"],"pt":["Implementação de padrões de registro para aplicações C#","Depuração de problemas usando formatos de mensagens de registro consistentes","Manutenção da consistência do registro em plataformas de bem-estar mental"],"ru":["Реализация стандартов ведения журнала для приложений C#","Отладка проблем с использованием последовательных форматов записей журнала","Поддержание согласованности ведения журнала на платформах психического благополучия"],"ar":["تنفيذ معايير التسجيل لتطبيقات C#","فحص الأخطاء باستخدام تنسيقات رسائل التسجيل المتسقة","الحفاظ على συνέفات التسجيل عبر منصات الرفاهية النفسية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires C# application environment","Specific to C# logging standards"],"zh":["需要C#应用程序环境","特定于C#日志标准"],"ja":["C#アプリケーション環境が必要","C#ログ標準に特有"],"ko":["C# 애플리케이션 환경 필요","C# 로깅 표준에 특정"],"es":["Requiere entorno de aplicación de C#","Específico para los estándares de registro de C#"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement d''application C#","Spécifique aux normes de journalisation C#"],"de":["Benötigt C#-Anwendungsumgebung","Spezifisch für die C#-Protokollstandards"],"pt":["Requer ambiente de aplicação C#","Específico para padrões de registro C#"],"ru":["Требуется среда приложения C#","Конкретно для стандартов ведения журнала C#"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة تطبيق C#","محدد لمعايير تسجيل C#"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
