viços"],"ru":["Принципы принятия решений","Эффективное разработка программного обеспечения","Паттерны разработки Python","Улучшение навыков разработки","Разработка API и микросервисов"],"ar":["مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات","تطوير برمجيات فعال","نماذج تطوير بايثون","تحسين مهارات التطوير","تطوير واجهات برمجة التطبيقات ومايكروسيرفيس"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Python 设计模式","开发原则","框架选择","异步编程","同步编程","决策树"],"ja":["Python パターン","開発の原則","フレームワークの選択","非同期プログラミング","同期プログラミング","決定木"],"ko":["파이썬 디자인 패턴","개발 원칙","프레임워크 선택","비동기 프로그래밍","동기 프로그래밍","결정 트리"],"es":["patrones de python","desarrollo de python","principios de desarrollo","framework de python","programación asíncrona","programación síncrona","decisiones informadas"],"fr":["modèles python","développement python","principes de développement","framework python","programmation asynchrone","programmation synchrone","décisions éclairées"],"de":["python-muster","python-entwicklung","entwicklungsprinzipien","python-framework","asynchrone programmierung","synchrone programmierung","fundierte entscheidungen"],"pt":["desenvolvimento python","padrões python","princípios de desenvolvimento","tomada de decisão","desenvolvimento de software","api","microserviços"],"ru":["разработка python","паттерны python","принципы разработки","принятие решений","разработка программного обеспечения","api","микросервисы"],"ar":["تطوير بايثون","نماذج بايثون","مبادئ التطوير","اتخاذ القرارات","تطوير البرمجيات","واجهات برمجة التطبيقات","مايكروسيرفيس"]}},"owner":"boomNDS","repo":"soop-discoard-bot","repoPath":"boomNDS/soop-discoard-bot","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.481Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-patterns","description":"Python development principles and decision-making. Framework selection, async patterns, type hints, project structure. Teaches thinking, not copying.","bodyPreview":"# Python Patterns\n\n> Python development principles and decision-making for 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for framework preference when unclear\n- Choose async vs sync based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t default to same framework every time\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework Selection (2025)\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat are you building?\n│\n├── API-first / Microservices\n│   └── Fas","body":"# Python Patterns\n\n> Python development principles and decision-making for 2025.\n> **Learn to THINK, not memorize patterns.**\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ How to Use This Skill\n\nThis skill teaches **decision-making principles**, not fixed code to copy.\n\n- ASK user for framework preference when unclear\n- Choose async vs sync based on CONTEXT\n- Don''t default to same framework every time\n\n---\n\n## 1. Framework Selection (2025)\n\n### Decision Tree\n\n```\nWhat are you building?\n│\n├── API-first / Microservices\n│   └── FastAPI (async, modern, fast)\n│\n├── Full-stack web / CMS / Admin\n│   └── Django (batteries-included)\n│\n├── Simple / Script / Learning\n│   └── Flask (minimal, flexible)\n│\n├── AI/ML API serving\n│   └── FastAPI (Pydantic, async, uvicorn)\n│\n└── Background workers\n    └── Celery + any framework\n```\n\n### Comparison Principles\n\n| Factor | FastAPI | Django | Flask |\n|--------|---------|--------|-------|\n| **Best for** | APIs, microservices | Full-stack, CMS | Simple, learning |\n| **Async** | Native | Django 5.0+ | Via extensions |\n| **Admin** | Manual | Built-in | Via extensions |\n| **ORM** | Choose your own | Django ORM | Choose your own |\n| **Learning curve** | Low | Medium | Low |\n\n### Selection Questions to Ask:\n1. Is this API-only or full-stack?\n2. Need admin interface?\n3. Team familiar with async?\n4. Existing infrastructure?\n\n---\n\n## 2. Async vs Sync Decision\n\n### When to Use Async\n\n```\nasync def is better when:\n├── I/O-bound operations (database, HTTP, file)\n├── Many concurrent connections\n├── Real-time features\n├── Microservices communication\n└── FastAPI/Starlette/Django ASGI\n\ndef (sync) is better when:\n├── CPU-bound operations\n├── Simple scripts\n├── Legacy codebase\n├── Team unfamiliar with async\n└── Blocking libraries (no async version)\n```\n\n### The Golden Rule\n\n```\nI/O-bound → async (waiting for external)\nCPU-bound → sync + multiprocessing (computing)\n\nDon''t:\n├── Mix sync and async carelessly\n├── Use sync libraries in async code\n└── Force async for CPU work\n```\n\n### Async Library Selection\n\n| Need | Async Library |\n|------|---------------|\n| HTTP client | httpx |\n| PostgreSQL | asyncpg |\n| Redis | aioredis / redis-py async |\n| File I/O | aiofiles |\n| Database ORM | SQLAlchemy 2.0 async, Tortoise |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Type Hints Strategy\n\n### When to Type\n\n```\nAlways type:\n├── Function parameters\n├── Return types\n├── Class attributes\n├── Public APIs\n\nCan skip:\n├── Local variables (let inference work)\n├── One-off scripts\n├── Tests (usually)\n```\n\n### Common Type Patterns\n\n```python\n# These are patterns, understand them:\n\n# Optional → might be None\nfrom typing import Optional\ndef find_user(id: int) -> Optional[User]: ...\n\n# Union → one of multiple types\ndef process(data: str | dict) -> None: ...\n\n# Generic collections\ndef get_items() -> list[Item]: ...\ndef get_mapping() -> dict[str, int]: ...\n\n# Callable\nfrom typing import Callable\ndef apply(fn: Callable[[int], str]) -> str: ...\n```\n\n### Pydantic for Validation\n\n```\nWhen to use Pydantic:\n├── API request/response models\n├── Configuration/settings\n├── Data validation\n├── Serialization\n\nBenefits:\n├── Runtime validation\n├── Auto-generated JSON schema\n├── Works with FastAPI natively\n└── Clear error messages\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Project Structure Principles\n\n### Structure Selection\n\n```\nSmall project / Script:\n├── main.py\n├── utils.py\n└── requirements.txt\n\nMedium API:\n├── app/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── main.py\n│   ├── models/\n│   ├── routes/\n│   ├── services/\n│   └── schemas/\n├── tests/\n└── pyproject.toml\n\nLarge application:\n├── src/\n│   └── myapp/\n│       ├── core/\n│       ├── api/\n│       ├── services/\n│       ├── models/\n│       └── ...\n├── tests/\n└── pyproject.toml\n```\n\n### FastAPI Structure Principles\n\n```\nOrganize by feature or layer:\n\nBy layer:\n├── routes/ (API endpoints)\n├── services/ (business logic)\n├── models/ (database models)\n├── schemas/ (Pydantic models)\n└── dependencies/ (shared deps)\n\nBy feature:\n├── users/\n│   ├── routes.py\n│   ├── service.py\n│   └── schemas.py\n└── products/\n    └── ...\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Django Principles (2025)\n\n### Django Async (Django 5.0+)\n\n```\nDjango supports async:\n├── Async views\n├── Async middleware\n├── Async ORM (limited)\n└── ASGI deployment\n\nWhen to use async in Django:\n├── External API calls\n├── WebSocket (Channels)\n├── High-concurrency views\n└── Background task triggering\n```\n\n### Django Best Practices\n\n```\nModel design:\n├── Fat models, thin views\n├── Use managers for common queries\n├── Abstract base classes for shared fields\n\nViews:\n├── Class-based for complex CRUD\n├── Function-based for simple endpoints\n├── Use viewsets with DRF\n\nQueries:\n├── select_related() for FKs\n├── prefetch_related() for M2M\n├── Avoid N+1 queries\n└── Use .only() for specific fields\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. FastAPI Principles\n\n### async def vs def in FastAPI\n\n```\nUse async def when:\n├── Using async database drivers\n├── Making async HTTP calls\n├── I/O-bound operations\n└── Want to handle concurrency\n\nUse def when:\n├── Blocking operations\n├── Sync database drivers\n├── CPU-bound work\n└── FastAPI runs in threadpool automatically\n```\n\n### Dependency Injection\n\n```\nUse dependencies for:\n├── Database sessions\n├── Current user / Auth\n├── Configuration\n├── Shared resources\n\nBenefits:\n├── Testability (mock dependencies)\n├── Clean separation\n├── Automatic cleanup (yield)\n```\n\n### Pydantic v2 Integration\n\n```python\n# FastAPI + Pydantic are tightly integrated:\n\n# Request validation\n@app.post(\"/users\")\nasync def create(user: UserCreate) -> UserResponse:\n    # user is already validated\n    ...\n\n# Response serialization\n# Return type becomes response schema\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Background Tasks\n\n### Selection Guide\n\n| Solution | Best For |\n|----------|----------|\n| **BackgroundTasks** | Simple, in-process tasks |\n| **Celery** | Distributed, complex workflows |\n| **ARQ** | Async, Redis-based |\n| **RQ** | Simple Redis queue |\n| **Dramatiq** | Actor-based, simpler than Celery |\n\n### When to Use Each\n\n```\nFastAPI BackgroundTasks:\n├── Quick operations\n├── No persistence needed\n├── Fire-and-forget\n└── Same process\n\nCelery/ARQ:\n├── Long-running tasks\n├── Need retry logic\n├── Distributed workers\n├── Persistent queue\n└── Complex workflows\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Error Handling Principles\n\n### Exception Strategy\n\n```\nIn FastAPI:\n├── Create custom exception classes\n├── Register exception handlers\n├── Return consistent error format\n└── Log without exposing internals\n\nPattern:\n├── Raise domain exceptions in services\n├── Catch and transform in handlers\n└── Client gets clean error response\n```\n\n### Error Response Philosophy\n\n```\nInclude:\n├── Error code (programmatic)\n├── Message (human readable)\n├── Details (field-level when applicable)\n└── NOT stack traces (security)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 9. Testing Principles\n\n### Testing Strategy\n\n| Type | Purpose | Tools |\n|------|---------|-------|\n| **Unit** | Business logic | pytest |\n| **Integration** | API endpoints | pytest + httpx/TestClient |\n| **E2E** | Full workflows | pytest + DB |\n\n### Async Testing\n\n```python\n# Use pytest-asyncio for async tests\n\nimport pytest\nfrom httpx import AsyncClient\n\n@pytest.mark.asyncio\nasync def test_endpoint():\n    async with AsyncClient(app=app, base_url=\"http://test\") as client:\n        response = await client.get(\"/users\")\n        assert response.status_code == 200\n```\n\n### Fixtures Strategy\n\n```\nCommon fixtures:\n├── db_session → Database connection\n├── client → Test client\n├── authenticated_user → User with token\n└── sample_data → Test data setup\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Decision Checklist\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n- [ ] **Asked user about framework preference?**\n- [ ] **Chosen framework for THIS context?** (not just default)\n- [ ] **Decided async vs sync?**\n- [ ] **Planned type hint strategy?**\n- [ ] **Defined project structure?**\n- [ ] **Planned error handling?**\n- [ ] **Considered background tasks?**\n\n---\n\n## 11. Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n### ❌ DON''T:\n- Default to Django for simple APIs (FastAPI may be better)\n- Use sync libraries in async code\n- Skip type hints for public APIs\n- Put business logic in routes/views\n- Ignore N+1 queries\n- Mix async and sync carelessly\n\n### ✅ DO:\n- Choose framework based on context\n- Ask about async requirements\n- Use Pydantic for validation\n- Separate concerns (routes → services → repos)\n- Test critical paths\n\n---\n\n> **Remember**: Python patterns are about decision-making for YOUR specific context. Don''t copy code—think about what serves your application best.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:44:19.992Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing advanced framework selection and decision-making principles.","zh":"非常适合需要高级框架选择和决策原则的 Python 开发代理。","ja":"Python開発エージェントが高度なフレームワークの選択と意思決定原則を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 프레임워크 선택 및 의사 결정 원칙이 필요한 Python 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de Python que necesitan una selección de marco avanzada y principios de toma de decisiones.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement Python ayant besoin d''une sélection de cadre avancée et de principes de prise de décision.","de":"Perfekt für Python-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine erweiterte Rahmenauswahl und Entscheidungsprinzipien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Python que necessitam de seleção avançada de estruturas e princípios de tomada de decisões.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки Python, которым необходим продвинутый выбор каркаса и принципов принятия решений.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يطورون بايثون وهم بحاجة إلى اختيار إطار متقدم ومبادئ اتخاذ القرارات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to choose between async and sync programming based on context, select appropriate frameworks for API-first or microservices development, and apply decision-making principles for optimal Python development in 2025, utilizing frameworks like FastAPI.","zh":"赋予代理选择在异步和同步编程之间的上下文，选择适合API优先或微服务开发的框架，并应用决策原则以实现2025年Python开发的最佳效果，利用如FastAPI的框架。","ja":"エージェントがコンテキストに基づいて非同期と同期プログラミングの間で選択し、API優先またはマイクロサービス開発に適したフレームワークを選択し、2025年のPython開発の最適化のために意思決定原則を適用することができるようにし、FastAPIなどのフレームワークを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 컨텍스트에 따라 비동기 및 동기 프로그래밍 사이에서 선택하고, API 우선 또는 마이크로 서비스 개발에 적합한 프레임워크를 선택하며, 2025년 Python 개발의 최적화를 위해 의사 결정 원칙을 적용할 수 있도록 하며, FastAPI와 같은 프레임워크를 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes elegir entre programación asíncrona y síncrona según el contexto, seleccionar marcos adecuados para el desarrollo de API-first o microservicios y aplicar principios de toma de decisiones para un desarrollo óptimo de Python en 2025, utilizando marcos como FastAPI.","fr":"Permet aux agents de choisir entre la programmation asynchrone et synchrone en fonction du contexte, de sélectionner des cadres appropriés pour le développement d''API-first ou de microservices et d''appliquer des principes de prise de décision pour un développement optimal de Python en 2025, en utilisant des cadres tels que FastAPI.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, zwischen asynchroner und synchroner Programmierung je nach Kontext zu wählen, geeignete Rahmen für API-First- oder Microservices-Entwicklung auszuwählen und Entscheidungsprinzipien für ein optimales Python-Entwicklung in 2025 anzuwenden, unter Verwendung von Rahmen wie FastAPI.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escolher entre programação assíncrona e síncrona com base no contexto, selecionar estruturas apropriadas para desenvolvimento de API-first ou microsserviços e aplicar princípios de tomada de decisões para desenvolvimento ótimo de Python em 2025, utilizando estruturas como FastAPI.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выбирать между асинхронным и синхронным программированием в зависимости от контекста, выбирать подходящие каркасы для разработки API-first или микросервисов и применять принципы принятия решений для оптимальной разработки Python в 2025 году, используя каркасы seperti FastAPI.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من اختيار البرمجة التزامنية أو غير التزامنية بناءً على السياق، واختيار الإطارات المناسبة لتطوير واجهة برمجة التطبيقات أولاً أو微 الخدمات، وتطبيق مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات من أجل تطوير بايثون الأمثل في عام 2025، باستخدام إطارات مثل FastAPI."},"useCases":{"en":["Selecting optimal frameworks for API-first development","Deciding between async and sync programming for specific projects","Applying decision-making principles for microservices architecture"],"zh":["选择适合API优先开发的最佳框架","决定特定项目的异步和同步编程之间","应用微服务架构的决策原则"],"ja":["API優先開発に最適なフレームワークを選択する","特定のプロジェクトの非同期と同期プログラミングの間で選択する","マイクロサービスアーキテクチャの意思決定原則を適用する"],"ko":["API 우선 개발을 위한 최적의 프레임워크 선택","특정 프로젝트의 비동기 및 동기 프로그래밍 사이에서 결정","마이크로 서비스 아키텍처의 의사 결정 원칙 적용"],"es":["Seleccionar marcos óptimos para el desarrollo de API-first","Decidir entre programación asíncrona y síncrona para proyectos específicos","Aplicar principios de toma de decisiones para la arquitectura de microservicios"],"fr":["Sélectionner des cadres optimaux pour le développement d''API-first","Décider entre la programmation asynchrone et synchrone pour des projets spécifiques","Appliquer des principes de prise de décision pour l''architecture de microservices"],"de":["Auswahl optimaler Rahmen für API-First-Entwicklung","Entscheidung zwischen asynchroner und synchroner Programmierung für spezifische Projekte","Anwendung von Entscheidungsprinzipien für die Mikro-Dienst-Architektur"],"pt":["Selecionar estruturas ótimas para desenvolvimento de API-first","Decidir entre programação assíncrona e síncrona para projetos específicos","Aplicar princípios de tomada de decisões para arquitetura de microsserviços"],"ru":["Выбирать оптимальные каркасы для разработки API-first","Решать между асинхронным и синхронным программированием для конкретных проектов","Применять принципы принятия решений для архитектуры микросервисов"],"ar":["اختيار الإطارات المثالية لتطوير واجهة برمجة التطبيقات أولاً","التحديد بين البرمجة التزامنية وغير التزامنية لمشاريع محددة","تطبيق مبادئ اتخاذ القرارات لعمارة微 الخدمات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Python development principles","Limited to Python 2025 development principles"],"zh":["需要了解Python开发原则","仅限于2025年Python开发原则"],"ja":["Python開発原則の理解が必要","2025年Python開発原則に限定される"],"ko":["Python 개발 원칙에 대한 이해가 필요","2025년 Python 개발 원칙에 한정"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de los principios de desarrollo de Python","Limitado a los principios de desarrollo de Python 2025"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance des principes de développement Python","Limité aux principes de développement Python 2025"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Python-Entwicklungsprinzipien","Begrenzt auf die Python-Entwicklungsprinzipien 2025"],"pt":["Exige compreensão dos princípios de desenvolvimento Python","Limitado a princípios de desenvolvimento Python 2025"],"ru":["Требует понимания принципов разработки Python","Ограничен принципами разработки Python 2025"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم مبادئ تطوير بايثون","محدود بمبادئ تطوير بايثون 2025"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
