idiomatische Muster","Go für Entwickler","Systemprogrammierung in Go"],"pt":["Desenvolvimento de backend","Linguagem de programação Go","Padrões de Go","Estruturação de pacotes","Tratamento de erros","Serviços de backend robustos"],"ru":["Разработка backend","Язык программирования Go","Шаблоны Go","Структурирование пакетов","Обработка ошибок","Надежные backend-сервисы"],"ar":["تطوير الخلفية","لغة برمجة Go","أنماط لغة Go","هيكلة الحزم","معالجة الأخطاء","خدمات خلفية قوية"]}},"owner":"KrystianYCSilva","repo":"hefesto-skill-generator","repoPath":"KrystianYCSilva/hefesto-skill-generator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.481Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"go-fundamentals","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Go Fundamentals\n\nGo was designed for simple, maintainable systems programming with first-class concurrency and fast builds. This skill helps the agent apply idiomatic Go patterns for robust backend services.\n\n## How to structure packages and modules\n\n1. Use Go modules as dependency boundaries.\n2. Keep package APIs small and cohesive.\n3. Organize by domain responsibility instead of technical layers only.\n4. Avoid public exports unless required by other packages.\n\n## How to handle errors idiomat","body":"# Go Fundamentals\n\nGo was designed for simple, maintainable systems programming with first-class concurrency and fast builds. This skill helps the agent apply idiomatic Go patterns for robust backend services.\n\n## How to structure packages and modules\n\n1. Use Go modules as dependency boundaries.\n2. Keep package APIs small and cohesive.\n3. Organize by domain responsibility instead of technical layers only.\n4. Avoid public exports unless required by other packages.\n\n## How to handle errors idiomatically\n\n1. Return errors as values and handle them close to the source.\n2. Wrap errors with context using `%w`.\n3. Use sentinel errors sparingly and document their meaning.\n4. Avoid panic for expected operational failures.\n\n## How to use context and cancellation correctly\n\n1. Pass `context.Context` as first parameter on request-scoped operations.\n2. Enforce timeouts/deadlines for outbound calls.\n3. Stop goroutines when context is canceled.\n4. Avoid storing context in structs.\n\n## How to design safe concurrency\n\n1. Use goroutines only with explicit lifecycle ownership.\n2. Use channels for coordination, not as global event buses.\n3. Protect shared state with mutexes where appropriate.\n4. Prefer simple patterns before advanced synchronization primitives.\n\n## How to test and observe Go services\n\n1. Use table-driven tests for behavior coverage.\n2. Separate fast unit tests from integration tests.\n3. Add benchmarks for hot paths before optimization.\n4. Include structured logs and metrics for operational visibility.\n\n## Common Warnings & Pitfalls\n\n- Goroutine leaks due missing cancellation paths.\n- Ignored errors in I/O and network code.\n- Overusing channels where plain function calls are clearer.\n- Global mutable state causing race conditions.\n- Premature micro-optimizations without profiling.\n\n## Common Errors and Fixes\n\n| Symptom | Root Cause | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rising memory usage over time | Goroutine/resource leak | Add cancellation, close resources, and inspect with profiling tools |\n| `context deadline exceeded` frequently | Timeout too low or downstream latency spikes | Rebalance timeout budgets and optimize downstream call chain |\n| Data race in tests | Unsynchronized shared state | Run with race detector and protect critical sections |\n| Module import chaos | Inconsistent module/version management | Normalize `go.mod` dependencies and tidy regularly |\n\n## Advanced Tips\n\n- Use `pprof` and tracing before deep performance changes.\n- Keep interfaces small and defined by consumers.\n- Build resilience wrappers for outbound dependencies.\n- Add chaos/failure tests for critical concurrent workflows.\n\n## How to use extended references\n\n- Read [Version History](references/version-history.md) before upgrades, migrations, or compatibility decisions.\n- Read [Java and Kotlin Examples](references/java-kotlin-examples.md) for implementation-ready snippets and language-specific guidance.\n- Read [Advanced Techniques](references/advanced-techniques.md) for specialist playbooks, incident tactics, and performance patterns.\n\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:44:37.719Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for Code Generation Agents building concurrent backend services in Go.","zh":"适用于构建使用Go语言的并发后端服务的代码生成代理。","ja":"Go言語を使用したコンカレントバックエンドサービスを構築するコード生成エージェントに不可欠。","ko":"Go를 사용하여 동시 백엔드 서비스를 구축하는 코드 생성 에이전트에 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para los agentes de generación de código que construyen servicios de backend concurrentes en Go.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents de génération de code qui construisent des services de backend concurrents en Go.","de":"Wesentlich für Code-Generierungsagenten, die konkurrierende Backend-Dienste in Go erstellen.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Geração de Código que constroem serviços de backend concorrentes em Go.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов генерации кода, строящих конкурирующие бэкенд-сервисы на Go.","ar":"ضروري لعميل توليد الكود الذي يبني خدمات الخلفية المتزامنة في Go."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables agents to apply idiomatic Go patterns including module-based dependency management, cohesive package APIs, and domain-driven organization for robust systems programming with first-class concurrency support.","zh":"使代理能够应用惯用的Go模式，包括基于模块的依赖管理、紧凑的包API和面向领域的组织，以实现具有一流并发支持的强大的系统编程。","ja":"エージェントが、モジュールベースの依存関係管理、凝縮されたパッケージAPI、ドメイン駆動の組織など、慣用的Goパターンを適用できるようにし、第一級のコンカレンシー支援を備えた堅牢なシステムプログラミングを実現する。","ko":"에이전트가 고유한 Go 패턴을 적용할 수 있도록 하여, 모듈 기반 의존성 관리, 응집된 패키지 API 및 도메인 주도적인 조직을 통해 1차적인 동시성 지원을 갖춘 강력한 시스템 프로그래밍을 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes aplicar patrones idiomáticos de Go, incluyendo gestión de dependencias basada en módulos, API de paquetes cohesivas y organización impulsada por dominios para programación de sistemas robustos con soporte de concurrencia de primera clase.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des modèles idiomatiques de Go, y compris la gestion des dépendances basée sur les modules, les API de packages cohésives et l''organisation pilotée par le domaine pour une programmation de systèmes robuste avec un support de concurrence de première classe.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, idiomatische Go-Muster anzuwenden, einschließlich modulbasierter Abhängigkeitsverwaltung, kohärenter Paket-APIs und domänengetriebener Organisation für robuste Systemprogrammierung mit erstklassiger Konkurrenzenunterstützung.","pt":"Permite que os agentes apliquem padrões idiomáticos do Go, incluindo gerenciamento de dependência baseado em módulos, APIs de pacotes coesas e organização orientada a domínio para programação de sistemas robustos com suporte a concorrência de primeira classe.","ru":"Позволяет агентам применять идиоматические шаблоны Go, включая управление зависимостями на основе модулей, связанные API пакетов и организацию, ориентированную на домен, для надежной программирования систем с поддержкой конкурентности первого класса.","ar":"يسمح للعميل بتطبيق أنماط جو متوافقة ، بما في ذلك إدارة التبعيات القائمة على الوحدة النمطية وواجهات برمجة التطبيقات المترابطة وتنظيم التوجيه القائم على المجال من أجل برمجة أنظمة قوية مع دعم التزامن من الدرجة الأولى."},"useCases":{"en":["Structuring Go modules as dependency boundaries","Organizing packages by domain responsibility","Implementing idiomatic error handling patterns","Designing maintainable concurrent systems"],"zh":["将Go模块作为依赖边界进行结构化","根据领域职责组织包","实现惯用的错误处理模式","设计可维护的并发系统"],"ja":["Goモジュールを依存関係境界として構造化する","ドメインの責任に基づいてパッケージを整理する","慣用的エラーハンドリングパターンを実装する","メンテナンス可能なコンカレントシステムを設計する"],"ko":["Go 모듈을 의존성 경계로 구조화한다","도메인 책임에 따라 패키지를 조직한다","고유한 오류 처리 패턴을 구현한다","유지 보수가 가능한 동시성 시스템을 설계한다"],"es":["Estructuración de módulos de Go como límites de dependencia","Organización de paquetes por responsabilidad de dominio","Implementación de patrones de manejo de errores idiomáticos","Diseño de sistemas concurrentes mantenibles"],"fr":["Structuration des modules Go en tant que limites de dépendance","Organisation des packages par responsabilité de domaine","Mise en œuvre de modèles de gestion des erreurs idiomatiques","Conception de systèmes concurrents maintainables"],"de":["Strukturierung von Go-Modulen als Abhängigkeitsgrenzen","Organisation von Paketen nach Domänenverantwortung","Implementierung idiomatischer Fehlerbehandlungsmuster","Entwurf von wartbaren konkurrierenden Systemen"],"pt":["Estruturando módulos Go como limites de dependência","Organizando pacotes por responsabilidade de domínio","Implementando padrões de tratamento de erros idiomáticos","Projetando sistemas concorrentes mantidos"],"ru":["Структурирование модулей Go в качестве границ зависимостей","Организация пакетов по ответственности домена","Реализация идиоматических шаблонов обработки ошибок","Проектирование поддерживаемых конкурирующих систем"],"ar":["هيكلة الوحدات النمطية Go كحدود للتبعيات","تنظيم الحزم حسب مسؤولية المجال","تنفيذ أنماط معالجة الأخطاء المتوافقة","تصميم أنظمة متزامنة قابلة للصيانة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Go-specific patterns only","Requires Go module compatibility","Focuses on backend systems programming"],"zh":["仅适用于Go特定的模式","需要Go模块兼容性","专注于后端系统编程"],"ja":["Go特有のパターンのみ","Goモジュールとの互換性が必要","バックエンドシステムプログラミングに焦点を当てている"],"ko":["Go 특정 패턴만 해당","Go 모듈 호환성 필요","백엔드 시스템 프로그래밍에 중점"],"es":["Patrones específicos de Go solo","Requiere compatibilidad con módulos de Go","Se centra en la programación de sistemas de backend"],"fr":["Modèles spécifiques à Go uniquement","Nécessite la compatibilité des modules Go","Se concentre sur la programmation de systèmes de backend"],"de":["Nur Go-spezifische Muster","Erfordert Go-Modul-Kompatibilität","Konzentriert sich auf die Systemprogrammierung von Backend-Systemen"],"pt":["Padrões específicos do Go apenas","Exige compatibilidade com o módulo Go","Concentra-se na programação de sistemas de backend"],"ru":["Только шаблоны, специфичные для Go","Требует совместимости с модулем Go","Сосредоточен на программировании бэкенд-систем"],"ar":["أنماطเฉพาะ لجو فقط","يتطلب توافقًا مع الوحدة النمطية Go","يركز على برمجة أنظمة الخلفية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Tyler-R-Kendrick/agent-skills/microsoft-foundry', 'community', 'Tyler-R-Kendrick', 'agent-skills', 'Tyler-R-Kendrick/agent-skills', 'microsoft-foundry', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.481Z', '2026-02-18T09:44:50.189Z', NULL, '{"id":"Tyler-R-Kendrick/agent-skills/microsoft-foundry","name":"microsoft-foundry","description":{"zh":"Microsoft Foundry 技术技能帮助开发人员发现和部署 AI 模型，构建 RAG 应用，并创建 AI 代理","ja":"Microsoft Foundry 技術スキルは、開発者が AI モデルを発見およびデプロイし、RAG アプリケーションを構築し、AI エージェントを作成するのに役立ちます","ko":"마이크로소프트 파운드리 기술 스킬은 개발자가 AI 모델을 발견하고 배포하고, RAG 애플리케이션을 구축하고, AI 에이전트를 생성하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"La herramienta Microsoft Foundry es un conjunto de recursos para desarrolladores que buscan trabajar con IA y crear aplicaciones personalizadas","fr":"L''outil Microsoft Foundry est un ensemble de ressources pour les développeurs qui cherchent à travailler avec l''IA et à créer des applications personnalisées","de":"Das Microsoft Foundry-Tool ist eine Sammlung von Ressourcen für Entwickler, die mit IA arbeiten und benutzerdefinierte Anwendungen erstellen möchten","pt":"O Microsoft Foundry é uma plataforma que ajuda os desenvolvedores a trabalhar com recursos de IA, incluindo descoberta e implantação de modelos, criação de aplicativos RAG e agentes de IA.","ru":"Microsoft Foundry - это платформа, которая помогает разработчикам работать с ресурсами ИИ, включая открытие и развертывание моделей, создание приложений RAG и агентов ИИ.","ar":"مايكروسوفت فاوندري هو منصة تساعد المطورين على العمل مع موارد الذكاء الاصطناعي، بما في ذلك اكتشاف وتنفيذ النماذج، وإنشاء تطبيقات RAG ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي.","en":"My personal agent-skills."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Microsoft Foundry 技术技能","ja":"マイクロソフト ファウンドリー スキル","ko":"마이크로소프트 파운드리 기술 스킬","es":"Herramienta Microsoft Foundry para desarrolladores","fr":"Outil Microsoft Foundry pour les développeurs","de":"Microsoft Foundry-Tool für Entwickler","pt":"Microsoft Foundry: Desenvolvimento de IA","ru":"Microsoft Foundry: Разработка ИИ","ar":"مايكروسوفت فاوندري: تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"microsoft-foundry"},"description":{"zh":"Microsoft Foundry 技术技能帮助开发人员发现和部署 AI 模型，构建 RAG 应用，并创建 AI 代理","ja":"Microsoft Foundry 技術スキルは、開発者が AI モデルを発見およびデプロイし、RAG アプリケーションを構築し、AI エージェントを作成するのに役立ちます","ko":"마이크로소프트 파운드리 기술 스킬은 개발자가 AI 모델을 발견하고 배포하고, RAG 애플리케이션을 구축하고, AI 에이전트를 생성하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"La herramienta Microsoft Foundry es un conjunto de recursos para desarrolladores que buscan trabajar con IA y crear aplicaciones personalizadas","fr":"L''outil Microsoft Foundry est un ensemble de ressources pour les développeurs qui cherchent à travailler avec l''IA et à créer des applications personnalisées","de":"Das Microsoft Foundry-Tool ist eine Sammlung von Ressourcen für Entwickler, die mit IA arbeiten und benutzerdefinierte Anwendungen erstellen möchten","pt":"O Microsoft Foundry é uma plataforma que ajuda os desenvolvedores a trabalhar com recursos de IA, incluindo descoberta e implantação de modelos, criação de a...","ru":"Microsoft Foundry - это платформа, которая помогает разработчикам работать с ресурсами ИИ, включая открытие и развертывание моделей, создание приложений RAG ...","ar":"مايكروسوفت فاوندري هو منصة تساعد المطورين على العمل مع موارد الذكاء الاصطناعي، بما في ذلك اكتشاف وتنفيذ النماذج، وإنشاء تطبيقات RAG ووكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي.","en":"My personal agent-skills."},"definition":{"en":"My personal agent-skills."},"features":{"zh":["发现和部署 AI 模型","构建 RAG 应用","创建 AI 代理","评估工作流","故障排除"],"ja":["AI モデルを発見およびデプロイ","RAG アプリケーションを構築","AI エージェントを作成","評価ワークフロー","トラブルシューティング"],"ko":["AI 모델을 발견하고 배포","RAG 애플리케이션을 구축","AI 에이전트를 생성","평가 워크플로","트러블슈팅"],"es":["Descubrimiento y despliegue de modelos de IA","Creación de aplicaciones RAG con índices de conocimiento y búsqueda vectorial","Creación de agentes de IA con herramientas como Azure","Flujos de trabajo de evaluación y depuración","Acceso a la catalogación de modelos de IA de Microsoft Foundry"],"fr":["Découverte et déploiement de modèles d''IA","Création d''applications RAG avec des indexes de connaissances et des recherches vectorielles","Création d''agents d''IA avec des outils comme Azure","Flux de travail d''évaluation et de débogage","Accès à la catalogisation de modèles d''IA de Microsoft Foundry"],"de":["Entdeckung und Bereitstellung von IA-Modellen","Erstellung von RAG-Anwendungen mit Wissensindizes und Vektor-Suche","Erstellung von IA-Agenten mit Tools wie Azure","Arbeitsabläufe für Bewertung und Fehlersuche","Zugriff auf die Katalogisierung von IA-Modellen von Microsoft Foundry"],"pt":["Descoberta e implantação de modelos de IA","Criação de aplicativos RAG com índices de conhecimento e busca vetorial","Criação de agentes de IA com ferramentas como Azure","Fluxos de trabalho de avaliação e depuração","Recursos de modelo e implantação"],"ru":["Открытие и развертывание моделей ИИ","Создание приложений RAG с индексами знаний и векторной поиской","Создание агентов ИИ с помощью инструментов như Azure","Потоки работы оценки и отладки","Ресурсы модели и развертывания"],"ar":["اكتشاف وتنفيذ نماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي","إنشاء تطبيقات RAG باستخدام فهارس المعرفة والبحث المتجه","إنشاء وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي باستخدام أدوات مثل Azure","تدفقات العمل للتقييم والتصحيح","موارد نموذج وتنفيذ"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Microsoft Foundry","AI 模型","RAG 应用","AI 代理","评估工作流","故障排除","开发者工具"],"ja":["Microsoft Foundry","AI モデル","RAG アプリケーション","AI エージェント","評価ワークフロー","トラブルシューティング","開発者ツール"],"ko":["마이크로소프트 파운드리","AI 모델","RAG 애플리케이션","AI 에이전트","평가 워크플로","트러블슈팅","개발자 도구"],"es":["Microsoft Foundry","desarrollo de IA","aplicaciones RAG","agentes de IA","modelos de IA","Azure","desarrollo de software","herramientas de IA","recursos de IA"],"fr":["Microsoft Foundry","développement d''IA","applications RAG","agents d''IA","modèles d''IA","Azure","développement de logiciels","outils d''IA","ressources d''IA"],"de":["Microsoft Foundry","IA-Entwicklung","RAG-Anwendungen","IA-Agenten","IA-Modelle","Azure","Software-Entwicklung","IA-Tools","IA-Ressourcen"],"pt":["Microsoft Foundry","desenvolvimento de IA","modelos de IA","aplicativos RAG","agentes de IA","Azure","índices de conhecimento","busca vetorial"],"ru":["Microsoft Foundry","разработка ИИ","модели ИИ","приложения RAG","агенты ИИ","Azure","индекса знаний","векторная поиска"],"ar":["مايكروسوفت فاوندري","تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","نماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطبيقات RAG","وكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","Azure","فهارس المعرفة","البحث المتجه"]}},"owner":"Tyler-R-Kendrick","repo":"agent-skills","repoPath":"Tyler-R-Kendrick/agent-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.481Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"microsoft-foundry","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Microsoft Foundry Skill\n\nThis skill helps developers work with Microsoft Foundry resources, covering model discovery and deployment, RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) applications, AI agent creation, evaluation workflows, and troubleshooting.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user wants to:\n\n- **Discover and deploy AI models** from the Microsoft Foundry catalog\n- **Build RAG applications** using knowledge indexes and vector search\n- **Create AI agents** with tools like Azu","body":"# Microsoft Foundry Skill\n\nThis skill helps developers work with Microsoft Foundry resources, covering model discovery and deployment, RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) applications, AI agent creation, evaluation workflows, and troubleshooting.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when the user wants to:\n\n- **Discover and deploy AI models** from the Microsoft Foundry catalog\n- **Build RAG applications** using knowledge indexes and vector search\n- **Create AI agents** with tools like Azure AI Search, web search, or custom functions\n- **Evaluate agent performance** using built-in evaluators\n- **Set up monitoring** and continuous evaluation for production agents\n- **Troubleshoot issues** with deployments, agents, or evaluations\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n### Azure Resources\n- An Azure subscription with an active account\n- Appropriate permissions to create Microsoft Foundry resources (e.g., Azure AI Owner role)\n- Resource group for organizing Foundry resources\n\n### Tools\n- **Azure CLI** installed and authenticated (`az login`)\n- **Azure Developer CLI (azd)** for deployment workflows (optional but recommended)\n\n### Language-Specific Requirements\n\nFor SDK examples and implementation details in specific programming languages, refer to:\n- **Python**: See [language/python.md](language/python.md) for Python SDK setup, authentication, and examples\n\n## Core Workflows\n\n### 1. Getting Started - Model Discovery and Deployment\n\n#### Use Case\nA developer new to Microsoft Foundry wants to explore available models and deploy their first one.\n\n#### Step 1: List Available Resources\n\nFirst, help the user discover their Microsoft Foundry resources.\n\n**Using Azure CLI:**\n\n##### Bash\n```bash\n# List all Microsoft Foundry resources in subscription\naz resource list \\\n  --resource-type \"Microsoft.CognitiveServices/accounts\" \\\n  --query \"[?kind==''AIServices''].{Name:name, ResourceGroup:resourceGroup, Location:location}\" \\\n  --output table\n\n# List resources in a specific resource group\naz resource list \\\n  --resource-group <resource-group-name> \\\n  --resource-type \"Microsoft.CognitiveServices/accounts\" \\\n  --output table\n```\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse the `foundry_resource_get` MCP tool to get detailed information about a specific Foundry resource, or to list all resources if no name is provided.\n\n#### Step 2: Browse Model Catalog\n\nHelp users discover available models, including information about free playground support.\n\n**Key Points to Explain:**\n- Some models support **free playground** for prototyping without costs\n- Models can be filtered by **publisher** (e.g., OpenAI, Meta, Microsoft)\n- Models can be filtered by **license type**\n- Model availability varies by region\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse the `foundry_models_list` MCP tool:\n- List all models: `foundry_models_list()`\n- List free playground models: `foundry_models_list(search-for-free-playground=true)`\n- Filter by publisher: `foundry_models_list(publisher=\"OpenAI\")`\n- Filter by license: `foundry_models_list(license=\"MIT\")`\n\n**Example Output Explanation:**\nWhen listing models, explain to users:\n- Models with free playground support can be used for prototyping at no cost\n- Some models support GitHub token authentication for easy access\n- Check model capabilities and pricing before production deployment\n\n#### Step 3: Deploy a Model\n\nGuide users through deploying a model to their Foundry resource.\n\n**Using Azure CLI:**\n\n##### Bash\n```bash\n# Deploy a model (e.g., gpt-4o)\naz cognitiveservices account deployment create \\\n  --name <foundry-resource-name> \\\n  --resource-group <resource-group-name> \\\n  --deployment-name gpt-4o-deployment \\\n  --model-name gpt-4o \\\n  --model-version \"2024-05-13\" \\\n  --model-format OpenAI \\\n  --sku-capacity 10 \\\n  --sku-name Standard\n\n# Verify deployment status\naz cognitiveservices account deployment show \\\n  --name <foundry-resource-name> \\\n  --resource-group <resource-group-name> \\\n  --deployment-name gpt-4o-deployment\n```\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse the `foundry_models_deploy` MCP tool with parameters:\n- `resource-group`: Resource group name\n- `deployment`: Deployment name\n- `model-name`: Model to deploy (e.g., \"gpt-4o\")\n- `model-format`: Format (e.g., \"OpenAI\")\n- `azure-ai-services`: Foundry resource name\n- `model-version`: Specific version\n- `sku-capacity`: Capacity units\n- `scale-type`: Scaling type\n\n**Deployment Verification:**\nExplain that when deployment completes, `provisioningState` should be `Succeeded`. If it fails, common issues include:\n- Insufficient quota\n- Region capacity limitations\n- Permission issues\n\n#### Step 4: Get Resource Endpoint\n\nUsers need the project endpoint to connect their code to Foundry.\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse the `foundry_resource_get` MCP tool to retrieve resource details including the endpoint.\n\n**Expected Output:**\nThe endpoint will be in format: `https://<resource>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project-name>`\n\nSave this endpoint as it''s needed for subsequent API and SDK calls.\n\n### 2. Building RAG Applications with Knowledge Indexes\n\n#### Use Case\nA developer wants to build a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) application using their own documents.\n\n#### Understanding RAG and Knowledge Indexes\n\n**Explain the Concept:**\nRAG enhances AI responses by:\n1. **Retrieving** relevant documents from a knowledge base\n2. **Augmenting** the AI prompt with retrieved context\n3. **Generating** responses grounded in factual information\n\n**Knowledge Index Benefits:**\n- Supports keyword, semantic, vector, and hybrid search\n- Enables efficient retrieval of relevant content\n- Stores metadata for better citations (document titles, URLs, file names)\n- Integrates with Azure AI Search for production scenarios\n\n#### Step 1: List Existing Knowledge Indexes\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse `foundry_knowledge_index_list` with your project endpoint to list knowledge indexes.\n\n#### Step 2: Inspect Index Schema\n\nUnderstanding the index structure helps optimize queries.\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse the `foundry_knowledge_index_schema` MCP tool with your project endpoint and index name to get detailed schema information.\n\n**Schema Information Includes:**\n- Field definitions and data types\n- Searchable attributes\n- Vectorization configuration\n- Retrieval mode support (keyword, semantic, vector, hybrid)\n\n#### Step 3: Create an Agent with Azure AI Search Tool\n\n**Implementation:**\n\nTo create a RAG agent with Azure AI Search tool integration:\n\n1. **Initialize the AI Project Client** with your project endpoint and credentials\n2. **Get the Azure AI Search connection** from your project\n3. **Create the agent** with:\n   - Agent name\n   - Model deployment\n   - Clear instructions (see best practices below)\n   - Azure AI Search tool configuration with:\n     - Connection ID\n     - Index name\n     - Query type (HYBRID recommended)\n\n**For SDK Implementation:** See [language/python.md](language/python.md#rag-applications-with-python-sdk)\n\n**Key Best Practices:**\n- **Always request citations** in agent instructions\n- Use **hybrid search** (AzureAISearchQueryType.HYBRID) for best results\n- Instruct the agent to say \"I don''t know\" when information isn''t in the index\n- Format citations consistently for easy parsing\n\n#### Step 4: Test the RAG Agent\n\n**Testing Process:**\n\n1. **Query the agent** with a test question\n2. **Stream the response** to get real-time output\n3. **Capture citations** from the response annotations\n4. **Validate** that citations are properly formatted and included\n\n**For SDK Implementation:** See [language/python.md](language/python.md#testing-the-rag-agent)\n\n**Troubleshooting RAG Issues:**\n\n| Issue | Possible Cause | Resolution |\n|-------|---------------|------------|\n| No citations in response | Agent instructions don''t request citations | Update instructions to explicitly request citation format |\n| \"Index not found\" error | Wrong index name or connection | Verify `AI_SEARCH_INDEX_NAME` matches index in Azure AI Search |\n| 401/403 authentication error | Missing RBAC permissions | Assign project managed identity **Search Index Data Contributor** role |\n| Poor retrieval quality | Query type not optimal | Try HYBRID query type for better results |\n\n### 3. Creating Your First AI Agent\n\n#### Use Case\nA developer wants to create an AI agent with tools (web search, function calling, file search).\n\n#### Step 1: List Existing Agents\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse `foundry_agents_list` with your project endpoint to list existing agents.\n\n#### Step 2: Create a Basic Agent\n\n**Implementation:**\n\nCreate an agent with:\n- **Model deployment name**: The model to use\n- **Agent name**: Unique identifier\n- **Instructions**: Clear, specific guidance for the agent''s behavior\n\n**For SDK Implementation:** See [language/python.md](language/python.md#basic-agent)\n\n#### Step 3: Create an Agent with Custom Function Tools\n\nAgents can call custom functions to perform actions like querying databases, calling APIs, or performing calculations.\n\n**Implementation Steps:**\n\n1. **Define custom functions** with clear docstrings describing their purpose and parameters\n2. **Create a function toolset** with your custom functions\n3. **Create the agent** with the toolset and instructions on when to use the tools\n\n**For SDK Implementation:** See [language/python.md](language/python.md#agent-with-custom-function-tools)\n\n#### Step 4: Create an Agent with Web Search\n\n**Implementation:**\n\nCreate an agent with web search capabilities by adding a Web Search tool:\n- Optionally specify user location for localized results\n- Provide instructions to always cite web sources\n\n**For SDK Implementation:** See [language/python.md](language/python.md#agent-with-web-search)\n\n#### Step 5: Interact with the Agent\n\n**Interaction Process:**\n\n1. **Create a conversation thread** for the agent interaction\n2. **Add user messages** to the thread\n3. **Run the agent** to process the messages and generate responses\n4. **Check run status** for success or failure\n5. **Retrieve messages** to see the agent''s responses\n6. **Cleanup** by deleting the agent when done\n\n**For SDK Implementation:** See [language/python.md](language/python.md#interacting-with-agents)\n\n**Agent Best Practices:**\n\n1. **Clear Instructions**: Provide specific, actionable instructions\n2. **Tool Selection**: Only include tools the agent needs\n3. **Error Handling**: Always check `run.status` for failures\n4. **Cleanup**: Delete agents/threads when done to manage costs\n5. **Rate Limits**: Handle rate limit errors gracefully (status code 429)\n\n\n### 4. Evaluating Agent Performance\n\n#### Use Case\nA developer has built an agent and wants to evaluate its quality, safety, and performance.\n\n#### Understanding Agent Evaluators\n\n**Built-in Evaluators:**\n\n1. **IntentResolutionEvaluator**: Measures how well the agent identifies and understands user requests (score 1-5)\n2. **TaskAdherenceEvaluator**: Evaluates whether responses adhere to assigned tasks and system instructions (score 1-5)\n3. **ToolCallAccuracyEvaluator**: Assesses whether the agent makes correct function tool calls (score 1-5)\n\n**Evaluation Output:**\nEach evaluator returns:\n- `{metric_name}`: Numerical score (1-5, higher is better)\n- `{metric_name}_result`: \"pass\" or \"fail\" based on threshold\n- `{metric_name}_threshold`: Binarization threshold (default or user-set)\n- `{metric_name}_reason`: Explanation of the score\n\n#### Step 1: Single Agent Run Evaluation\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse the `foundry_agents_query_and_evaluate` MCP tool to query an agent and evaluate the response in one call. Provide:\n- Agent ID\n- Query text\n- Project endpoint\n- Azure OpenAI endpoint and deployment for evaluation\n- Comma-separated list of evaluators to use\n\n**Example Output:**\n```json\n{\n  \"response\": \"The weather in Seattle is currently sunny and 22°C.\",\n  \"evaluation\": {\n    \"intent_resolution\": 5.0,\n    \"intent_resolution_result\": \"pass\",\n    \"intent_resolution_threshold\": 3,\n    \"intent_resolution_reason\": \"The agent correctly identified the user''s intent to get weather information and provided a relevant response.\",\n    \"task_adherence\": 4.0,\n    \"task_adherence_result\": \"pass\",\n    \"tool_call_accuracy\": 5.0,\n    \"tool_call_accuracy_result\": \"pass\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Step 2: Evaluate Existing Response\n\nIf you already have the agent''s response, you can evaluate it directly.\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse the `foundry_agents_evaluate` MCP tool to evaluate a specific query/response pair with a single evaluator.\n\n**For SDK Implementation:** See [language/python.md](language/python.md#single-response-evaluation-using-mcp)\n\n#### Step 3: Batch Evaluation\n\nFor evaluating multiple agent runs across multiple conversation threads:\n\n1. **Convert agent thread data** to evaluation format\n2. **Prepare evaluation data** from multiple thread IDs\n3. **Set up evaluators** with appropriate configuration\n4. **Run batch evaluation** and view results in the Foundry portal\n\n**For SDK Implementation:** See [language/python.md](language/python.md#batch-evaluation)\n\n#### Interpreting Evaluation Results\n\n**Score Ranges (1-5 scale):**\n- **5**: Excellent - Agent perfectly understood and executed the task\n- **4**: Good - Minor issues, but overall successful\n- **3**: Acceptable - Threshold for passing (default)\n- **2**: Poor - Significant issues with understanding or execution\n- **1**: Failed - Agent completely misunderstood or failed the task\n\n**Common Evaluation Issues:**\n\n| Issue | Cause | Resolution |\n|-------|-------|------------|\n| Job stuck in \"Running\" | Insufficient model capacity | Increase model quota/capacity and rerun |\n| All metrics zero | Wrong evaluator or unsupported model | Verify evaluator compatibility with your model |\n| Groundedness unexpectedly low | Incomplete context/retrieval | Verify RAG retrieval includes sufficient context |\n| Evaluation missing | Not selected during setup | Rerun evaluation with required metrics |\n\n### 5. Troubleshooting Common Issues\n\n#### Deployment Issues\n\n**Problem: Deployment Stays Pending or Fails**\n\n##### Bash\n```bash\n# Check deployment status and details\naz cognitiveservices account deployment show \\\n  --name <resource-name> \\\n  --resource-group <resource-group> \\\n  --deployment-name <deployment-name> \\\n  --output json\n\n# Check account quota\naz cognitiveservices account show \\\n  --name <resource-name> \\\n  --resource-group <resource-group> \\\n  --query \"properties.quotaLimit\"\n```\n\n**Common Causes:**\n- Insufficient quota in the region\n- Region at capacity for the model\n- Permission issues\n\n**Resolution:**\n1. Check quota limits in Azure Portal\n2. Request quota increase if needed\n3. Try deploying to a different region\n4. Verify you have appropriate RBAC permissions\n\n#### Agent Response Issues\n\n**Problem: Agent Doesn''t Return Citations (RAG)**\n\n**Diagnostics:**\n1. Check agent instructions explicitly request citations\n2. Verify the tool choice is set to \"required\" or \"auto\"\n3. Confirm the Azure AI Search connection is configured correctly\n\n**Resolution:**\n\nUpdate the agent''s instructions to explicitly request citations in the format `[message_idx:search_idx†source]` and to only use the knowledge base, never the agent''s own knowledge.\n\n**For SDK Implementation:** See [language/python.md](language/python.md#update-agent-instructions)\n\n**Problem: \"Index Not Found\" Error**\n\n**Using MCP Tools:**\n\nUse the `foundry_knowledge_index_list` MCP tool to verify the index exists and get the correct name.\n\n**Resolution:**\n1. Verify `AI_SEARCH_INDEX_NAME` environment variable matches actual index name\n2. Check the connection points to correct Azure AI Search resource\n3. Ensure index has been created and populated\n\n**Problem: 401/403 Authentication Errors**\n\n**Common Cause:** Missing RBAC permissions\n\n**Resolution:**\n\n##### Bash\n```bash\n# Assign Search Index Data Contributor role to managed identity\naz role assignment create \\\n  --assignee <managed-identity-principal-id> \\\n  --role \"Search Index Data Contributor\" \\\n  --scope /subscriptions/<subscription-id>/resourceGroups/<rg>/providers/Microsoft.Search/searchServices/<search-service>\n\n# Verify role assignment\naz role assignment list \\\n  --assignee <managed-identity-principal-id> \\\n  --output table\n```\n\n#### Evaluation Issues\n\n**Problem: Evaluation Dashboard Shows No Data**\n\n**Common Causes:**\n- No recent agent traffic\n- Time range excludes the data\n- Ingestion delay\n\n**Resolution:**\n1. Generate new agent traffic (test queries)\n2. Expand the time range filter in the dashboard\n3. Wait a few minutes for data ingestion\n4. Refresh the dashboard\n\n**Problem: Continuous Evaluation Not Running**\n\n**Diagnostics:**\n\nCheck evaluation run status to identify issues. For SDK implementation, see [language/python.md](language/python.md#checking-evaluation-status).\n\n**Resolution:**\n1. Verify the evaluation rule is enabled\n2. Confirm agent traffic is flowing\n3. Check project managed identity has **Azure AI User** role\n4. Verify OpenAI endpoint and deployment are accessible\n\n#### Rate Limiting and Capacity Issues\n\n**Problem: Agent Run Fails with Rate Limit Error**\n\n**Error Message:** `Rate limit is exceeded` or HTTP 429\n\n**Resolution:**\n\n##### Bash\n```bash\n# Check current quota usage\naz cognitiveservices usage list \\\n  --name <resource-name> \\\n  --resource-group <resource-group>\n\n# Request quota increase (manual process in portal)\necho \"Request quota increase in Azure Portal under Quotas section\"\n```\n\n# Request quota increase (manual process in portal)\nWrite-Output \"Request quota increase in Azure Portal under Quotas section\"\n```\n\n**Best Practices:**\n- Implement exponential backoff retry logic\n- Use Dynamic Quota when available\n- Monitor quota usage proactively\n- Consider multiple deployments across regions\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### Common Environment Variables\n\n```bash\n# Foundry Project\nPROJECT_ENDPOINT=https://<resource>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project>\nMODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME=gpt-4o\n\n# Azure AI Search (for RAG)\nAZURE_AI_SEARCH_CONNECTION_NAME=my-search-connection\nAI_SEARCH_INDEX_NAME=my-index\n\n# Evaluation\nAZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://<resource>.openai.azure.com\nAZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o\n```\n\n### Useful MCP Tools Quick Reference\n\n**Resource Management**\n- `foundry_resource_get` - Get resource details and endpoint\n\n**Models**\n- `foundry_models_list` - Browse model catalog\n- `foundry_models_deploy` - Deploy a model\n- `foundry_models_deployments_list` - List deployed models\n\n**Knowledge & RAG**\n- `foundry_knowledge_index_list` - List knowledge indexes\n- `foundry_knowledge_index_schema` - Get index schema\n\n**Agents**\n- `foundry_agents_list` - List agents\n- `foundry_agents_connect` - Query an agent\n- `foundry_agents_query_and_evaluate` - Query and evaluate\n\n**OpenAI Operations**\n- `foundry_openai_chat_completions_create` - Create chat completions\n- `foundry_openai_embeddings_create` - Create embeddings\n\n### Language-Specific Quick References\n\nFor SDK-specific details, authentication, and code examples:\n- **Python**: See [language/python.md](language/python.md)\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n### Documentation Links\n- [Microsoft Foundry Documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/)\n- [Microsoft Foundry Quickstart](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/quickstarts/get-started-code)\n- [RAG and Knowledge Indexes](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/concepts/retrieval-augmented-generation)\n- [Agent Evaluation Guide](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/ai-foundry/how-to/develop/agent-evaluate-sdk)\n\n### GitHub Samples\n- [Microsoft Foundry Samples](https://github.com/azure-ai-foundry/foundry-samples)\n- [Azure Search OpenAI Demo](https://github.com/Azure-Samples/azure-search-openai-demo)\n- [Azure Search Classic RAG](https://github.com/Azure-Samples/azure-search-classic-rag)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:44:50.189Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents focused on model discovery and deployment, such as those utilizing RAG applications and Azu tools for AI agent creation.","zh":"适合专注于模型发现和部署的AI代理，例如使用RAG应用程序和Azu工具进行AI代理创建的代理。","ja":"モデル発見と展開に焦点を当てたAIエージェントに適しています。たとえば、RAGアプリケーションやAzuツールを使用してAIエージェントを作成するようなものです。","ko":"모델 발견 및 배포에 중점을 둔 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다. 예를 들어, RAG 애플리케이션 및 Azu 툴을 사용하여 AI 에이전트를 생성하는 경우와 같습니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA centrados en el descubrimiento y despliegue de modelos, como aquellos que utilizan aplicaciones RAG y herramientas Azu para la creación de agentes de IA.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA axés sur la découverte et le déploiement de modèles, tels que ceux utilisant des applications RAG et des outils Azu pour la création d''agents IA.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents, die auf Modellentdeckung und -bereitstellung fokussiert sind, wie z.B. solche, die RAG-Anwendungen und Azu-Tools für die Erstellung von KI-Agents verwenden.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA focados na descoberta e implantação de modelos, como aqueles que utilizam aplicações RAG e ferramentas Azu para criação de agentes de IA.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, ориентированных на открытие и развертывание моделей, таких как те, которые используют приложения RAG и инструменты Azu для создания агентов ИИ.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي التي تركز على اكتشاف النماذج وتحديدها، مثل تلك التي تستخدم تطبيقات RAG وأدوات Azu لإنشاء عمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to discover and deploy AI models from the Microsoft Foundry catalog, build RAG applications using knowledge indexes and vector search, and create AI agents with advanced evaluation workflows and troubleshooting capabilities using Microsoft Foundry resources.","zh":"赋予代理从Microsoft Foundry目录中发现和部署AI模型的能力，使用知识索引和向量搜索构建RAG应用程序，并使用Microsoft Foundry资源创建具有高级评估工作流和故障排除功能的AI代理。","ja":"Microsoft FoundryカタログからAIモデルを発見して展開する機能をエージェントに与え、ナレッジインデックスとベクトル検索を使用してRAGアプリケーションを構築し、Microsoft Foundryリソースを使用して高度な評価ワークフローとトラブルシューティング機能を持つAIエージェントを作成する。","ko":"에이전트가 Microsoft Foundry 카탈로그에서 AI 모델을 발견하고 배포할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 지식 색인 및 벡터 검색을 사용하여 RAG 애플리케이션을 구축하고, Microsoft Foundry 리소스를 사용하여 고급 평가 워크플로 및 문제 해결 기능이 있는 AI 에이전트를 생성할 수 있습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes para descubrir y desplegar modelos de IA del catálogo de Microsoft Foundry, construir aplicaciones RAG utilizando índices de conocimiento y búsqueda vectorial, y crear agentes de IA con flujos de trabajo de evaluación avanzados y capacidades de solución de problemas utilizando recursos de Microsoft Foundry.","fr":"Permet aux agents de découvrir et de déployer des modèles d''IA à partir du catalogue Microsoft Foundry, de construire des applications RAG en utilisant des index de connaissances et des recherches vectorielles, et de créer des agents d''IA avec des flux de travail d''évaluation avancés et des capacités de dépannage en utilisant les ressources Microsoft Foundry.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, KI-Modelle aus dem Microsoft-Foundry-Katalog zu entdecken und bereitzustellen, RAG-Anwendungen mithilfe von Wissensindizes und Vektorsuche zu erstellen und KI-Agents mit erweiterten Bewertungsworkflows und Fehlersuche-Funktionen mithilfe von Microsoft-Foundry-Ressourcen zu erstellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a descobrirem e implantarem modelos de IA do catálogo da Microsoft Foundry, construir aplicações RAG usando índices de conhecimento e busca vetorial, e criar agentes de IA com fluxos de trabalho de avaliação avançados e capacidades de solução de problemas usando recursos da Microsoft Foundry.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью открывать и развертывать модели ИИ из каталога Microsoft Foundry, создавать приложения RAG с использованием индексов знаний и векторного поиска, а также создавать агентов ИИ с расширенными рабочими процессами оценки и возможностями устранения неполадок с использованием ресурсов Microsoft Foundry.","ar":"تمكّن العاملين من اكتشاف وتحديد نماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي من فهرس Microsoft Foundry، وبناء تطبيقات RAG باستخدام فهارس المعرفة والبحث المتجه، وإنشاء عمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي مع سير عمل تقييم متقدم وقدرات فحص الأخطاء باستخدام موارد Microsoft Foundry."},"useCases":{"en":["Deploying AI models from the Microsoft Foundry catalog for enhanced predictive analytics","Building RAG applications with knowledge indexes for improved information retrieval","Creating and evaluating AI agents using Azu and other Microsoft Foundry tools for streamlined AI development"],"zh":["将Microsoft Foundry目录中的AI模型部署以实现增强的预测分析","使用知识索引构建RAG应用程序以改进信息检索","使用Azu和其他Microsoft Foundry工具创建和评估AI代理以实现流畅的AI开发"],"ja":["Microsoft FoundryカタログのAIモデルを展開して予測分析の強化に役立てる","ナレッジインデックスを使用してRAGアプリケーションを構築し、情報の取得を改善する","Azuや他のMicrosoft Foundryツールを使用してAIエージェントを作成・評価し、AI開発をスムーズにする"],"ko":["Microsoft Foundry 카탈로그의 AI 모델을 배포하여 예측 분석을 개선합니다.","지식 색인을 사용하여 RAG 애플리케이션을 구축하고 정보 검색을 개선합니다.","Azu 및 기타 Microsoft Foundry 도구를 사용하여 AI 에이전트를 생성 및 평가하여 AI 개발을 간소화합니다."],"es":["Desplegar modelos de IA del catálogo de Microsoft Foundry para una analítica predictiva mejorada","Construir aplicaciones RAG con índices de conocimiento para una recuperación de información mejorada","Crear y evaluar agentes de IA utilizando Azu y otras herramientas de Microsoft Foundry para un desarrollo de IA optimizado"],"fr":["Déployer des modèles d''IA à partir du catalogue Microsoft Foundry pour une analyse prédictive améliorée","Construire des applications RAG avec des index de connaissances pour une récupération d''informations améliorée","Créer et évaluer des agents d''IA en utilisant Azu et d''autres outils Microsoft Foundry pour un développement d''IA rationalisé"],"de":["KI-Modelle aus dem Microsoft-Foundry-Katalog bereitzustellen, um eine verbesserte Vorhersageanalyse zu ermöglichen","RAG-Anwendungen mit Wissensindizes zu erstellen, um eine verbesserte Informationsbeschaffung zu ermöglichen","KI-Agents zu erstellen und zu bewerten, indem Azu und andere Microsoft-Foundry-Tools für einen optimierten KI-Entwicklungsprozess verwendet werden"],"pt":["Implantação de modelos de IA do catálogo da Microsoft Foundry para análise preditiva aprimorada","Construção de aplicações RAG com índices de conhecimento para recuperação de informações aprimorada","Criação e avaliação de agentes de IA usando Azu e outras ferramentas da Microsoft Foundry para desenvolvimento de IA otimizado"],"ru":["Развертывание моделей ИИ из каталога Microsoft Foundry для повышения прогностического анализа","Создание приложений RAG с индексами знаний для улучшения извлечения информации","Создание и оценка агентов ИИ с использованием Azu и других инструментов Microsoft Foundry для оптимизации разработки ИИ"],"ar":["تثبيت نماذج الذكاء الاصطناعي من فهرس Microsoft Foundry للحصول على تحليل تنبؤي محسّن","بناء تطبيقات RAG مع فهارس المعرفة لتحسين استرجاع المعلومات","إنشاء وتقييم عمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي باستخدام Azu وأدوات Microsoft Foundry الأخرى من أجل تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي المتكامل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to Microsoft Foundry resources and catalog","Limited to RAG applications and AI agent creation using specified tools"],"zh":["需要访问Microsoft Foundry资源和目录","仅限于使用指定工具进行RAG应用程序和AI代理创建"],"ja":["Microsoft Foundryリソースおよびカタログへのアクセスが必要","指定されたツールを使用したRAGアプリケーションおよびAIエージェントの作成に限定される"],"ko":["Microsoft Foundry 리소스 및 카탈로그에 액세스해야 합니다.","지정된 도구를 사용하여 RAG 애플리케이션 및 AI 에이전트를 생성하는 것에 한정됩니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso a recursos y catálogo de Microsoft Foundry","Limitado a aplicaciones RAG y creación de agentes de IA utilizando herramientas especificadas"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux ressources et au catalogue Microsoft Foundry","Limité aux applications RAG et à la création d''agents d''IA en utilisant des outils spécifiés"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf Microsoft-Foundry-Ressourcen und -Katalog","Begrenzt auf RAG-Anwendungen und Erstellung von KI-Agents unter Verwendung spezifizierter Tools"],"pt":["Requer acesso a recursos e catálogo da Microsoft Foundry","Limitado a aplicações RAG e criação de agentes de IA usando ferramentas especificadas"],"ru":["Требует доступа к ресурсам и каталогу Microsoft Foundry","Ограничен приложениями RAG и созданием агентов ИИ с использованием указанных инструментов"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى موارد وفهرس Microsoft Foundry","محدود بتطبيقات RAG وإنشاء عمليات وكيل الذكاء الاصطناعي باستخدام الأدوات المحددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Velocity-Alpha/ai-recap-newsletter/design', 'community', 'Velocity-Alpha', 'ai-recap-newsletter', 'Velocity-Alpha/ai-recap-newsletter', 'design', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.481Z', '2026-02-18T09:44:42.028Z', NULL, '{"id":"Velocity-Alpha/ai-recap-newsletter/design","name":"design","description":{"zh":"AI 设计系统是一个强调编辑性、水彩灵魂和静默自信的设计哲学","ja":"AI デザインシステムは、編集性、水彩の魂、静かな自信を強調する設計哲学です","ko":"AI 디자인 시스템은 편집성, 수채화의 영혼, 조용한 자신감을 강조하는 디자인 철학입니다","es":"El sistema de diseño de AI Recap combina ilustraciones en acuarela con tipografía minimalista para crear una experiencia de usuario única","fr":"Le système de conception de AI Recap combine des illustrations en aquarelle avec une typographie minimaliste pour créer une expérience utilisateur unique","de":"Das Designsystem von AI Recap kombiniert Aquarell-Illustrationen mit minimalistischer Typografie, um eine einzigartige Benutzererfahrung zu schaffen","pt":"O sistema de design do AI Recap é baseado em uma filosofia editorial, com ilustrações em água e uma interface do usuário quente e orgânica.","ru":"Система дизайна AI Recap основана на редакционной философии, с иллюстрациями в водяных тонах и теплым, органическим пользовательским интерфейсом","ar":"نظام تصميم تلخيص الذكاء الاصطناعي يعتمد على فلسفة تحريرية، مع رسومات مائية وواجهة مستخدم دافئة وعضوية","en":"Repo for the AI Recap Newsletter"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AI 设计系统","ja":"AI デザインシステム","ko":"AI 디자인 시스템","es":"Diseño de AI Recap: sistema de diseño editorial","fr":"Conception de AI Recap : système de design éditorial","de":"Design von AI Recap: Editoriales Designsystem","pt":"Design de Sistema AI Recap","ru":"Дизайн системы AI Recap","ar":"تصميم نظام تلخيص الذكاء الاصطناعي","en":"design"},"description":{"zh":"AI 设计系统是一个强调编辑性、水彩灵魂和静默自信的设计哲学","ja":"AI デザインシステムは、編集性、水彩の魂、静かな自信を強調する設計哲学です","ko":"AI 디자인 시스템은 편집성, 수채화의 영혼, 조용한 자신감을 강조하는 디자인 철학입니다","es":"El sistema de diseño de AI Recap combina ilustraciones en acuarela con tipografía minimalista para crear una experiencia de usuario única","fr":"Le système de conception de AI Recap combine des illustrations en aquarelle avec une typographie minimaliste pour créer une expérience utilisateur unique","de":"Das Designsystem von AI Recap kombiniert Aquarell-Illustrationen mit minimalistischer Typografie, um eine einzigartige Benutzererfahrung zu schaffen","pt":"O sistema de design do AI Recap é baseado em uma filosofia editorial, com ilustrações em água e uma interface do usuário quente e orgânica.","ru":"Система дизайна AI Recap основана на редакционной философии, с иллюстрациями в водяных тонах и теплым, органическим пользовательским интерфейсом","ar":"نظام تصميم تلخيص الذكاء الاصطناعي يعتمد على فلسفة تحريرية، مع رسومات مائية وواجهة مستخدم دافئة وعضوية","en":"Repo for the AI Recap Newsletter"},"definition":{"en":"Repo for the AI Recap Newsletter"},"features":{"zh":["编辑性设计","水彩灵魂","静默自信","手工制作的用户体验","独特的设计哲学"],"ja":["編集性デザイン","水彩の魂","静かな自信","手作りのユーザーエクスペリエンス","ユニークな設計哲学"],"ko":["편집성 디자인","수채화의 영혼","조용한 자신감","수제로 제작된 사용자 경험","고유한 디자인 철학"],"es":["Ilustraciones en acuarela","Tipografía minimalista","Diseño editorial","Experiencia de usuario única","Estética inspirada en Monocle y Morning Brew"],"fr":["Illustrations en aquarelle","Typographie minimaliste","Conception éditoriale","Expérience utilisateur unique","Esthétique inspirée de Monocle et Morning Brew"],"de":["Aquarell-Illustrationen","Minimalistische Typografie","Editorisches Design","Einzigartige Benutzererfahrung","Ästhetik inspiriert von Monocle und Morning Brew"],"pt":["Filosofia editorial","Ilustrações em água","Interface do usuário quente e orgânica","Tipografia e espaço em branco como elementos principais","Cores suportam estrutura e ação"],"ru":["Редакционная философия","Иллюстрации в водяных тонах","Теплый, органический пользовательский интерфейс","Типография и пробел как основные элементы","Цвета поддерживают структуру и действие"],"ar":["فلسفة تحريرية","رسومات مائية","واجهة مستخدم دافئة وعضوية","طباعة ونوعية المسافة كعناصر رئيسية","الألوان تدعم البنية والعمل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI 设计系统","编辑性设计","水彩灵魂","静默自信","手工制作的用户体验","独特的设计哲学","设计系统"],"ja":["AI デザインシステム","編集性デザイン","水彩の魂","静かな自信","手作りのユーザーエクスペリエンス","ユニークな設計哲学","設計システム"],"ko":["AI 디자인 시스템","편집성 디자인","수채화의 영혼","조용한 자신감","수제로 제작된 사용자 경험","고유한 디자인 철학","디자인 시스템"],"es":["diseño de AI","sistema de diseño editorial","ilustraciones en acuarela","tipografía minimalista","experiencia de usuario","estética de Monocle","estética de Morning Brew"],"fr":["conception de AI","système de conception éditorial","illustrations en aquarelle","typographie minimaliste","expérience utilisateur","esthétique de Monocle","esthétique de Morning Brew"],"de":["Design von AI","editorisches Designsystem","Aquarell-Illustrationen","minimalistische Typografie","Benutzererfahrung","Ästhetik von Monocle","Ästhetik von Morning Brew"],"pt":["design de sistema","AI Recap","filosofia editorial","ilustrações em água","interface do usuário","tipografia","espaço em branco","cores"],"ru":["система дизайна","AI Recap","редакционная философия","иллюстрации в водяных тонах","пользовательский интерфейс","типография","пробел","цвета"],"ar":["تصميم نظام","تلخيص الذكاء الاصطناعي","فلسفة تحريرية","رسومات مائية","واجهة المستخدم","طباعة","نوعية المسافة","الألوان"]}},"owner":"Velocity-Alpha","repo":"ai-recap-newsletter","repoPath":"Velocity-Alpha/ai-recap-newsletter","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.481Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"design","description":"Design philosophy and design tokens for the AI Recap Newsletter project.","bodyPreview":"# AI Recap Design System\n\n## Philosophy\n\n**Editorial, not startup.** We''re a daily briefing, not a SaaS product. Think *Monocle* meets *Morning Brew* — authoritative, warm, handcrafted.\n\n**Watercolor soul.** Our illustrations use loose watercolor washes in muted blues, rusts, and sages. The UI should feel like it belongs alongside them — soft edges, organic warmth, zero corporate sterility.\n\n**Quiet confidence.** Let typography and whitespace do the work. Color supports structure and action, nev","body":"# AI Recap Design System\n\n## Philosophy\n\n**Editorial, not startup.** We''re a daily briefing, not a SaaS product. Think *Monocle* meets *Morning Brew* — authoritative, warm, handcrafted.\n\n**Watercolor soul.** Our illustrations use loose watercolor washes in muted blues, rusts, and sages. The UI should feel like it belongs alongside them — soft edges, organic warmth, zero corporate sterility.\n\n**Quiet confidence.** Let typography and whitespace do the work. Color supports structure and action, never decoration.\n\n---\n\n## Tailwind & CSS Tokens\n\nThis project uses **Tailwind CSS 4**. Most tokens are defined as CSS variables in [app/globals.css](app/globals.css) and are automatically available via Tailwind utilities or as `var(--token-name)`.\n\n### Backgrounds\n| Token | Hex | Tailwind Utility | Usage |\n|-------|-----|------------------|-------|\n| `--bg-main` | `#FAFAF8` | `bg-background` | Page background (warm paper) |\n| `--bg-warm` | `#F7F6F3` | `bg-secondary` | Section alternation, inputs |\n| `--bg-card` | `#FFFFFF` | `bg-card` | Cards, elevated surfaces |\n\n### Text\n| Token | Hex | Tailwind Utility | Usage |\n|-------|-----|------------------|-------|\n| `--text-primary` | `#2C3E4A` | `text-foreground` | Headlines, body copy |\n| `--text-secondary` | `#5A6B78` | `text-secondary` | Descriptions, metadata |\n| `--text-muted` | `#8A9BA8` | `text-muted-foreground` | Captions, timestamps, labels |\n\n### Watercolor Palette\nUse these for accents and decoration. They are available as standard CSS variables.\n\n| Token | Hex | Character |\n|-------|-----|-----------|\n| `--watercolor-blue` | `#A8C5D9` | Cool, calm — product tags |\n| `--watercolor-blue-deep` | `#6B9BB8` | Stronger blue moments |\n| `--watercolor-rust` | `#C4A484` | Warm, earthy — funding tags |\n| `--watercolor-rust-deep` | `#B8956E` | Richer terracotta |\n| `--watercolor-sage` | `#9DB4A0` | Organic, trustworthy — policy tags |\n| `--watercolor-ink` | `#3D4F5F` | Deep contrast — subscribe section |\n\n### Functional\n| Token | Hex | Tailwind | Usage |\n|-------|-----|----------|-------|\n| `--accent-primary` | `#5A7A8A` | `color-primary` | Links, secondary actions |\n| `--accent-warm` | `#B8856E` | - | Live indicators, primary CTAs |\n| `--border` | `#D4DDE3` | `border-border` | Visible dividers |\n| `--border-light` | `#E8EDF0` | `border-muted` | Subtle separators |\n\n---\n\n## Typography\n\n### Fonts\n| Role | Family | Token | Tailwind Utility |\n|------|--------|-------|------------------|\n| Display | Libre Baskerville | `--font-serif` | `font-serif` |\n| Body/UI | Source Sans 3 | `--font-sans` | `font-sans` |\n\n### Style Rules\n- **Serif** for editorial content: headlines, card titles, pull quotes. Use `font-serif`.\n- **Sans** for UI: buttons, navigation, labels, body copy. Use `font-sans`.\n- **Never uppercase serif.** Uppercase is reserved for sans-serif labels/tags only.\n\n---\n\n## Spacing & Layout\n\nSpacing tokens map to rem values for consistency:\n\n| Token | Value | Tailwind Usage |\n|-------|-------|----------------|\n| `--space-xs` | 8px (0.5rem) | `p-[var(--space-xs)]` |\n| `--space-sm` | 16px (1rem) | `gap-4` or `gap-[var(--space-sm)]` |\n| `--space-md` | 24px (1.5rem) | `p-6` or `p-[var(--space-md)]` |\n| `--space-lg` | 40px (2.5rem) | `my-10` or `my-[var(--space-lg)]` |\n\n---\n\n## Radius & Shadows\n\n| Token | Value | Usage |\n|-------|-------|-------|\n| `--radius` | 4px | Buttons, inputs, tags (`rounded`) |\n| `--radius-lg` | 8px | Cards, modals (`rounded-lg`) |\n\n### Shadows\nDefined in components, not as global Tailwind tokens yet.\n- **Card**: `0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)`\n- **Elevated**: `0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.06), 0 20px 48px rgba(0,0,0,0.08)`\n\n---\n\n## Watercolor Animation Patterns\n\nUse these classes for the signature watercolor feel:\n\n```css\n/* Signature Watercolor Blob */\n.watercolor-blob {\n  position: absolute;\n  border-radius: 50%;\n  filter: blur(40px);\n  opacity: 0.12;\n  pointer-events: none;\n}\n```\n\n- **Avoid saturated colors**: Never use default Tailwind blues or reds.\n- **Background**: Always default to `--bg-main` (#FAFAF8).\n\n---\n\n## Do / Don''t\n\n### Do\n- Use `font-serif` for headlines.\n- Use `bg-background` for the main page.\n- Apply watercolor tones as subtle accents.\n\n### Don''t\n- Uppercase serif type.\n- Use sharp corners (min 4px radius).\n- Overuse shadows.\n\n---\n\n## Brand Voice (for reference)\n\n**Tone**: Informed, concise, subtly warm. A knowledgeable colleague, not a hype machine.\n\n**Headlines**: Declarative, present-tense. *\"Anthropic closes $3B round\"* not *\"Anthropic has just closed...\"*\n\n**CTAs**: Direct but unhurried. *\"Subscribe free\" / \"Full briefing →\"*\n\n---\n\n*Last updated: February 2026*\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:44:42.028Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Creative Agents needing bespoke visual identity and typography capabilities.","zh":"适合需要定制视觉身份和字体能力的创意代理","ja":"創造性エージェントが独自のビジュアルアイデンティティとタイポグラフィ機能を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"맞춤형 시각적 정체성 및 타이포그래피 기능이 필요한 창의적인 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes creativos que necesitan una identidad visual y capacidades tipográficas personalizadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents créatifs ayant besoin d''une identité visuelle et de capacités typographiques sur mesure.","de":"Perfekt für kreative Agenten, die eine maßgeschneiderte visuelle Identität und Typografie-Fähigkeiten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Criativos que necessitam de identidade visual personalizada e capacidades de tipografia.","ru":"Идеально подходит для Креативных Агентов, которым требуются индивидуальная визуальная идентичность и возможности типографики.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الإبداعيين الذين يحتاجون إلى هوية بصرية مخصصة وقدرات طباعة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft warm, handcrafted designs using watercolor-inspired illustrations and soft-edged UI elements, leveraging typography and whitespace to convey quiet confidence, with support for muted color palettes and organic structures.","zh":"赋予代理商使用水彩启发的插图和软边界UI元素来制作温暖的手工设计的能力，利用字体和空白空间来传达安静的自信，并支持柔和的色彩调色板和有机结构","ja":"水彩によるイラストレーションやソフトエッジのUI要素を使用して、手作りのウォームデザインを作成し、タイポグラフィーと空白スペースを使用して静かな自信を伝え、柔らかい色のパレットや有機構造をサポートするエージェントの力を高める","ko":"수동으로 제작한 따뜻한 디자인을 만들기 위해 에이전트에게 수채화에서 영감을 얻은 일러스트와 부드러운 에지의 UI 요소를 사용할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 타이포그래피와 공백을 사용하여 조용한 자신감을 전달하고, 무디한 색상 팔레트와 유기적 구조를 지원한다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear diseños cálidos y artesanales utilizando ilustraciones inspiradas en la acuarela y elementos de interfaz de usuario con bordes suaves, aprovechando la tipografía y el espacio en blanco para transmitir confianza tranquila, con soporte para paletas de colores apagadas y estructuras orgánicas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des conceptions chaleureuses et artisanales en utilisant des illustrations inspirées de l''aquarelle et des éléments d''interface utilisateur à bords doux, en exploitant la typographie et les espaces blancs pour transmettre une confiance discrète, avec un support pour les palettes de couleurs sourdes et les structures organiques.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, warme, handgefertigte Designs zu erstellen, die von Wasserfarben inspirierte Illustrationen und UI-Elemente mit weichen Kanten verwenden, die Typografie und den Leerzeichen nutzen, um stille Zuversicht zu vermitteln, mit Unterstützung für gedämpfte Farbpaletten und organische Strukturen.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem designs quentes e personalizados usando ilustrações inspiradas em aquarela e elementos de interface do usuário com bordas suaves, aproveitando a tipografia e o espaço em branco para transmitir confiança silenciosa, com suporte a paletas de cores suaves e estruturas orgânicas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать теплые, ручные дизайны, используя иллюстрации, вдохновленные акварелью, и элементы интерфейса пользователя с мягкими краями, используя типографику и пробел для передачи тихой уверенности, с поддержкой приглушенных цветовых палитр и органических структур.","ar":"يمكن للوكلاء من خلاله设计ات دافئة ومصممة يدوياً باستخدام رسومات متأثرة بالTransparent و مكونات واجهة المستخدم ذات الحواف الناعمة، واستخدام الطباعة و الفراغات للتحقق من الثقة الصامتة، مع دعم لوحات الألوان المعتدلة و الهياكل العضوية."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating editorial-style layouts with loose watercolor washes","Creating authoritative, warm, and inviting typography","Designing UI elements with soft edges and organic warmth"],"zh":["生成带有松散水彩洗涤的编辑样式布局","创建权威、温暖、亲切的字体","设计具有软边缘和有机温暖的UI元素"],"ja":["水彩ワッシュの緩い編集スタイルレイアウトを生成する","権威的で暖かく迎え入れるタイポグラフィーを作成する","ソフトエッジと有機的な温かみを持つUI要素を設計する"],"ko":["편집 스타일 레이아웃을 자유로운 수채색 세척으로 생성","권위적이고 따뜻하며 초대하는 타이포그래피를 생성","부드러운 에지와 유기적인 따뜻함을 가진 UI 요소를 디자인"],"es":["Generar diseños de estilo editorial con lavados de acuarela sueltos","Crear tipografía autorizada, cálida e invitadora","Diseñar elementos de la interfaz de usuario con bordes suaves y calor orgánico"],"fr":["Générer des dispositions de style éditorial avec des lavis d''aquarelle lâches","Créer une typographie autoritaire, chaleureuse et accueillante","Concevoir des éléments d''interface utilisateur avec des bords doux et une chaleur organique"],"de":["Erstellen von redaktionellen Layouts mit lockerer Wasserfarb-Wäsche","Erstellen von autorisierter, warmer und einladender Typografie","Entwerfen von Benutzeroberflächenelementen mit weichen Kanten und organischem Wärme"],"pt":["Gerar layouts de estilo editorial com lavagens de aquarela soltas","Criar tipografia autoritária, quente e convidativa","Projetar elementos de interface do usuário com bordas suaves e calor orgânico"],"ru":["Генерировать редакционные макеты с свободными акварельными промывками","Создавать авторитетную, теплую и привлекательную типографику","Разрабатывать элементы интерфейса пользователя с мягкими краями и органическим теплом"],"ar":["генерировать تصاميم منشورات بال Transparent و الماء","إنشاء طباعة معتمدة و دافئة و مُستقبل","تصميم مكونات واجهة المستخدم ذات الحواف الناعمة و الدفء العضوي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires aesthetic sensitivity to watercolor and muted color palettes","Limited to editorial and non-corporate design applications"],"zh":["需要对水彩和柔和色彩调色板有美学敏感性","仅限编辑和非企业设计应用"],"ja":["水彩や柔らかい色のパレットに対する美的感覚性が必要","編集および非企業向けデザインアプリケーションに限定"],"ko":["수채색과 무디한 색상 팔레트에 대한 미적 감각이 필요","편집 및 비기업 디자인 응용 프로그램에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere sensibilidad estética a la acuarela y a las paletas de colores apagadas","Limitado a aplicaciones de diseño editorial y no corporativas"],"fr":["Nécessite une sensibilité esthétique à l''aquarelle et aux palettes de couleurs sourdes","Limité aux applications de conception éditoriale et non corporative"],"de":["Erfordert ästhetische Sensibilität für Wasserfarbe und gedämpfte Farbpaletten","Begrenzt auf redaktionelle und nicht-korporative Desig nanwendungen"],"pt":["Requer sensibilidade estética para aquarela e paletas de cores suaves","Limitado a aplicações de design editorial e não corporativo"],"ru":["Требует эстетической чувствительности к акварели и приглушенным цветовым палитрам","Ограничен редакционными и некорпоративными приложениями дизайна"],"ar":["يتطلب حساسية جمالية للرسومات المائية و لوحات الألوان المعتدلة","محدود لتطبيقات التصميم Editorial و غير الشركات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
