imisation"],"de":["Erweiterte Datenanalyse","Intelligente Speicherung","Erstellung von benutzerdefinierten Fähigkeiten","Integration mit Windsurf AI","Leistungsanalyse und Optimierung"],"pt":["Pausa de conversa AI","Análise de dados","Armazenamento inteligente","Otimização de desempenho","Integração com Windsurf AI"],"ru":["Пауза разговора AI","Анализ данных","Интеллектуальное хранилище","Оптимизация производительности","Интеграция с Windsurf AI"],"ar":["تعليق المحادثة AI","تحليل البيانات","تخزين ذكي","تحسين الأداء","التكامل مع Windsurf AI"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Skill Creator","智能数据管理","AI开发环境","开发效率","数据分析","智能存储","AI对话"],"ja":["スキルクリエイター","智能データ管理","AI開発環境","開発効率","データ分析","スマートストレージ","AI対話"],"ko":["스킬 크리에이터","智能 데이터 관리","인공지능 개발 환경","개발 효율성","데이터 분석","스마트 스토리지","인공지능 대화"],"es":["creación de habilidades","análisis de datos","gestión de almacenamiento","Windsurf AI","desarrollo de habilidades","inteligencia artificial","análisis de rendimiento"],"fr":["création de compétences","analyse de données","gestion de stockage","Windsurf AI","développement de compétences","intelligence artificielle","analyse de performances"],"de":["Erstellung von Fähigkeiten","Datenanalyse","Speicherung","Windsurf AI","Entwicklung von Fähigkeiten","künstliche Intelligenz","Leistungsanalyse"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de habilidades","gestão de dados","Windsurf AI","inteligência artificial","análise de dados","otimização de desempenho"],"ru":["разработка навыков","управление данными","Windsurf AI","искусственный интеллект","анализ данных","оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["تطوير المهارات","إدارة البيانات","Windsurf AI","الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحليل البيانات","تحسين الأداء"]}},"owner":"congwa","repo":"wdm","repoPath":"congwa/wdm","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   ├── description: (required)\n│   │   └── compatibility: (optional, rarely needed)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields (required), plus optional fields like `license`, `metadata`, and `compatibility`. Only `name` and `description` are read by Claude to determine when the skill triggers, so be clear and comprehensive about what the skill is and when it should be used. The `compatibility` field is for noting environment requirements (target product, system packages, etc.) but most skills don''t need it.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:51:47.811Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude and Windsurf needing advanced skill development and data management capabilities.","zh":"非常适合像 Claude 和 Windsurf 这样的 AI 代理，它们需要高级技能开发和数据管理能力。","ja":"Claude と Windsurf のような高度なスキル開発とデータ管理機能を必要とする AI エージェントに最適です。","ko":"클라우드와 윈드서프 같은 고급 스킬 개발과 데이터 관리 기능이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude y Windsurf que necesitan un desarrollo de habilidades avanzado y capacidades de gestión de datos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude et Windsurf ayant besoin d''un développement de compétences avancé et de capacités de gestion de données.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agenten wie Claude und Windsurf, die ein fortschrittliches Skill-Development und Datenmanagement benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de IA como Claude e Windsurf que necessitam de desenvolvimento de habilidades avançadas e capacidades de gerenciamento de dados.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude и Windsurf, которым требуются передовые возможности развития навыков и управления данными.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude و Windsurf الذين يحتاجون إلى تطوير مهارات متقدمة وقدرات إدارة البيانات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create effective skills with specialized knowledge, workflows, and tools, utilizing AI conversation pause feedback, intelligent storage cleaning, and comprehensive data analysis, including modular and self-contained packages that extend capabilities.","zh":"赋予代理创建有效技能的能力，利用专门的知识、工作流程和工具，包括 AI 对话暂停反馈、智能存储清理和全面数据分析，包括模块化和自包含的包以扩展功能。","ja":"エージェントが専門知識、ワークフロー、ツールを利用して効果的なスキルを作成できるようにします。AI 会話一時停止フィードバック、インテリジェントストレージクリーン、包括的なデータ分析、および機能を拡張するモジュラーで自己完結したパッケージを含みます。","ko":"에이전트가 전문 지식, 워크플로, 도구를 사용하여 효과적인 스킬을 생성할 수 있도록 합니다. AI 대화 일시 중지 피드백, 지능형 스토리지 정리, 포괄적인 데이터 분석, 및 기능을 확장하는 모듈화되고 자체 포함된 패키지를 포함합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear habilidades efectivas con conocimientos especializados, flujos de trabajo y herramientas, utilizando la retroalimentación de pausa de conversación de IA, la limpieza de almacenamiento inteligente y el análisis de datos integral, incluyendo paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que amplían las capacidades.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des compétences efficaces avec des connaissances spécialisées, des flux de travail et des outils, en utilisant la rétroaction de pause de conversation d''IA, le nettoyage de stockage intelligent et l''analyse de données complète, y compris des packages modulaires et autonomes qui étendent les capacités.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, effektive Fähigkeiten mit spezialisierten Kenntnissen, Workflows und Tools zu erstellen, indem es die Konversations-Pausen-Rückmeldung von KI, die intelligente Speicherbereinigung und die umfassende Datenanalyse nutzt, einschließlich modularer und selbstenthaltener Pakete, die die Fähigkeiten erweitern.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem habilidades eficazes com conhecimento especializado, fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas, utilizando feedback de pausa de conversa de IA, limpeza de armazenamento inteligente e análise de dados abrangente, incluindo pacotes modulares e autocontidos que estendem as capacidades.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать эффективные навыки со специализированными знаниями, рабочими процессами и инструментами, используя обратную связь паузы разговора ИИ, интеллектуальную очистку хранилища и комплексный анализ данных, включая модульные и самодостаточные пакеты, которые расширяют возможности.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء مهارات فعالة مع معرفة متخصصة وعمليات عمل وأدوات، باستخدام ملاحظات توقف المحادثة الاصطناعية، وتنظيف التخزين الذكي والتحليل الشامل للبيانات، بما في ذلك الحزم المودULAR وذاتية الإحتوي التي تمديد القدرات."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating modular skills for specialized domains","Developing workflows for procedural knowledge","Analyzing conversation data for improved agent performance"],"zh":["为专业领域创建模块化技能","为程序化知识开发工作流程","分析对话数据以提高代理性能"],"ja":["専門ドメイン用のモジュラー スキルを作成する","手続き型知識のためのワークフローを開発する","エージェントのパフォーマンスを向上させるための会話データを分析する"],"ko":["전문 분야를 위한 모듈화된 스킬을 생성하는 것","절차적 지식의 워크플로를 개발하는 것","에이전트의 성능을 개선하기 위한 대화 데이터를 분석하는 것"],"es":["Creación de habilidades modulares para dominios especializados","Desarrollo de flujos de trabajo para conocimiento procedural","Análisis de datos de conversación para mejorar el rendimiento del agente"],"fr":["Création de compétences modulaires pour des domaines spécialisés","Développement de flux de travail pour des connaissances procédurales","Analyse de données de conversation pour améliorer les performances de l''agent"],"de":["Erstellung modulare Fähigkeiten für spezialisierte Domänen","Entwicklung von Workflows für prozedurales Wissen","Analyse von Konversationsdaten zur Verbesserung der Leistung des Agents"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades modulares para domínios especializados","Desenvolvimento de fluxos de trabalho para conhecimento procedural","Análise de dados de conversa para melhoria do desempenho do agente"],"ru":["Создание модульных навыков для специализированных доменов","Разработка рабочих процессов для процедурных знаний","Анализ данных разговора для улучшения производительности агента"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات مودULAR لمناطق متخصصة","تطوير عمليات عمل للمعرفة الإجرائية","تحليل بيانات المحادثة لتحسين أداء الوكيل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Windsurf AI development environment","Limited to Claude''s capabilities and extensions"],"zh":["需要 Windsurf AI 开发环境","仅限 Claude 的功能和扩展"],"ja":["Windsurf AI 開発環境が必要","Claude の機能と拡張機能のみ"],"ko":["윈드서프 AI 개발 환경이 필요함","클라우드의 기능 및 확장 기능만 지원"],"es":["Requiere entorno de desarrollo de IA Windsurf","Limitado a las capacidades y extensiones de Claude"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement de développement d''IA Windsurf","Limité aux capacités et extensions de Claude"],"de":["Benötigt Windsurf-KI-Entwicklungsumgebung","Begrenzt auf die Fähigkeiten und Erweiterungen von Claude"],"pt":["Requer ambiente de desenvolvimento de IA Windsurf","Limitado às capacidades e extensões do Claude"],"ru":["Требуется среда разработки ИИ Windsurf","Ограничен возможностями и расширениями Claude"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة تطوير ال IA Windsurf","محدود بقدرات وامتدادات Claude"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/dev-commands', 'community', 'Paxeer-Network', 'Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol', 'dev-commands', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z', '2026-02-18T09:52:08.132Z', NULL, '{"id":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol/dev-commands","name":"dev-commands","description":{"es":"Nuestro protocolo de futuros sintéticos permite a los traders abrir posiciones con apalancamiento. Los comandos de desarrollo facilitan la creación de aplicaciones de trading","fr":"Notre protocole de futures synthétiques permet aux traders d''ouvrir des positions avec effet de levier. Les commandes de développement facilitent la création d''applications de trading","de":"Unser synthetisches Futures-Protokoll ermöglicht es Tradern, mit Hebelwirkung zu handeln. Die Entwickler-Befehle erleichtern die Erstellung von Trading-Anwendungen","pt":"O conjunto de comandos de desenvolvimento dev-commands permite criar aplicações de desktop e web com facilidade. Inclui comandos para iniciar o desenvolvimento de aplicações de desktop e web","ru":"Набор команд разработки dev-commands позволяет создавать приложения для рабочего стола и веб-приложения с легкостью. Включает команды для запуска разработки приложений для рабочего стола и веб-приложений","ar":"مجموعة أوامر التطوير dev-commands تسمح بإنشاء تطبيقات سطح المكتب والويب بسهولة. تشمل أوامر لبدء التطوير لتطبيقات سطح المكتب والويب","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a cus..."},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Comandos de desarrollo para traders","fr":"Commandes de développement pour traders","de":"Entwickler-Befehle für Trader","pt":"Comandos de Desenvolvimento para Plataformas","ru":"Команды разработки для платформ","ar":"أوامر التطوير للبرامج","en":"dev-commands"},"description":{"es":"Nuestro protocolo de futuros sintéticos permite a los traders abrir posiciones con apalancamiento. Los comandos de desarrollo facilitan la creación de aplica...","fr":"Notre protocole de futures synthétiques permet aux traders d''ouvrir des positions avec effet de levier. Les commandes de développement facilitent la création...","de":"Unser synthetisches Futures-Protokoll ermöglicht es Tradern, mit Hebelwirkung zu handeln. Die Entwickler-Befehle erleichtern die Erstellung von Trading-Anwen...","pt":"O conjunto de comandos de desenvolvimento dev-commands permite criar aplicações de desktop e web com facilidade. Inclui comandos para iniciar o desenvolvimen...","ru":"Набор команд разработки dev-commands позволяет создавать приложения для рабочего стола и веб-приложения с легкостью. Включает команды для запуска разработки ...","ar":"مجموعة أوامر التطوير dev-commands تسمح بإنشاء تطبيقات سطح المكتب والويب بسهولة. تشمل أوامر لبدء التطوير لتطبيقات سطح المكتب والويب","en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collater..."},"definition":{"en":"A synthetic perpetual futures protocol supporting RWA assets, crypto, stocks, and indexes. Traders open leveraged long/short positions (up to 1000x) collateralized by stablecoins held in per-user on-chain vaults. A central liquidity vault acts as counterparty to all trades. Pricing combines a custom oracle, a Virtual AMM , and TWAP smoothing."},"features":{"es":["Protocolo de futuros sintéticos","Apalancamiento de hasta 1000x","Bóveda de liquidez centralizada","Oracle personalizado","Suavizado de TWAP"],"fr":["Protocole de futures synthétiques","Effet de levier jusqu''à 1000x","Vautier de liquidité centralisée","Oracle personnalisé","Lissage de TWAP"],"de":["Synthetisches Futures-Protokoll","Hebelwirkung von bis zu 1000x","Zentralisierte Liquiditäts-Vault","Benutzerdefinierter Oracle","TWAP-Glättung"],"pt":["Iniciar desenvolvimento de aplicações de desktop com `yarn app:desktop`","Iniciar desenvolvimento de aplicações web com `yarn app:web`","Resolução de problemas comuns como conflitos de versão do Node","Otimização do tempo de inicialização do aplicativo","Suporte a desenvolvimento de aplicações de desktop e web"],"ru":["Запуск разработки приложений для рабочего стола с `yarn app:desktop`","Запуск разработки веб-приложений с `yarn app:web`","Решение общих проблем, таких как конфликты версий Node","Оптимизация времени запуска приложения","Поддержка разработки приложений для рабочего стола и веб-приложений"],"ar":["تشغيل التطوير لتطبيقات سطح المكتب مع `yarn app:desktop`","تشغيل التطوير لتطبيقات الويب مع `yarn app:web`","حل المشكلات الشائعة مثل تعارض إصدارات Node","تحسين وقت تشغيل التطبيق","دعم تطوير تطبيقات سطح المكتب وتطبيقات الويب"]},"keywords":{"es":["desarrollo de trading","futuros sintéticos","apalancamiento","oracle personalizado","suavizado de TWAP","bóveda de liquidez centralizada"],"fr":["développement de trading","futures synthétiques","effet de levier","oracle personnalisé","lissage de TWAP","vautier de liquidité centralisée"],"de":["Trading-Entwicklung","synthetische Futures","Hebelwirkung","benutzerdefinierter Oracle","TWAP-Glättung","zentralisierte Liquiditäts-Vault"],"pt":["comandos de desenvolvimento","desenvolvimento de aplicações","yarn app:desktop","yarn app:web","desenvolvimento de desktop","desenvolvimento web","otimização de aplicativos","resolução de problemas"],"ru":["команды разработки","разработка приложений","yarn app:desktop","yarn app:web","разработка для рабочего стола","веб-разработка","оптимизация приложений","решение проблем"],"ar":["أوامر التطوير","تطوير التطبيقات","yarn app:desktop","yarn app:web","تطوير سطح المكتب","تطوير الويب","تحسين التطبيقات","حل المشكلات"]}},"owner":"Paxeer-Network","repo":"Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","repoPath":"Paxeer-Network/Sidiora-Perpetual-Protocol","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dev-commands","description":"Development commands for monorepo projects. Use when running dev servers, building apps, linting, testing, or troubleshooting build issues. Triggers on yarn, dev, build, lint, test, desktop, mobile, web, extension, ios, android, compile, bundle.","bodyPreview":"# Development Commands\n\n## Application Development Commands\n\n**PLATFORM-SPECIFIC DEVELOPMENT** (adapt command names to your project):\n- `yarn app:desktop` - Start desktop Electron app development\n  - **Runtime**: 30-60 seconds to start\n  - **Common issues**: Node version conflicts, missing native dependencies\n  - **Troubleshooting**: Run `yarn clean && yarn reinstall` if startup fails\n\n- `yarn app:web` - Start web development server\n  - **Runtime**: 15-30 seconds to start\n  - **Common issues**:","body":"# Development Commands\n\n## Application Development Commands\n\n**PLATFORM-SPECIFIC DEVELOPMENT** (adapt command names to your project):\n- `yarn app:desktop` - Start desktop Electron app development\n  - **Runtime**: 30-60 seconds to start\n  - **Common issues**: Node version conflicts, missing native dependencies\n  - **Troubleshooting**: Run `yarn clean && yarn reinstall` if startup fails\n\n- `yarn app:web` - Start web development server\n  - **Runtime**: 15-30 seconds to start\n  - **Common issues**: Port already in use, webpack/bundler compilation errors\n  - **Troubleshooting**: Kill existing processes on port, check console for specific errors\n\n- `yarn app:ext` - Start browser extension development\n  - **Runtime**: 20-40 seconds to start\n  - **Common issues**: Manifest v3 validation errors, permission issues\n  - **Troubleshooting**: Check extension manifest validity, verify content security policy\n\n- `yarn app:ios` - Start iOS mobile development\n  - **Runtime**: 1-2 minutes (includes Metro bundler)\n  - **Common issues**: Xcode setup, simulator issues, pod install failures\n  - **Prerequisites**: Xcode installed, iOS simulator available\n\n- `yarn app:android` - Start Android mobile development\n  - **Runtime**: 1-2 minutes (includes Metro bundler)\n  - **Common issues**: Android SDK path, emulator setup, gradle build failures\n  - **Prerequisites**: Android Studio, SDK tools, emulator configured\n\n## Build Commands\n\n**PRODUCTION BUILDS** (Use for final validation):\n- `yarn app:desktop:build` - Build desktop app for all platforms\n  - **Runtime**: 5-10 minutes (multi-platform build)\n  - **Output**: Platform-specific installers in `apps/desktop/dist/`\n  - **Common issues**: Code signing, platform-specific dependencies\n\n- `yarn app:ext:build` - Build browser extension\n  - **Runtime**: 2-3 minutes\n  - **Output**: Extension packages in `apps/ext/dist/`\n  - **Common issues**: Manifest validation, content security policy violations\n\n- `yarn app:web:build` - Build web application\n  - **Runtime**: 3-5 minutes\n  - **Output**: Static files in `apps/web/dist/`\n  - **Common issues**: Bundle size limits, missing environment variables\n\n- `yarn app:native-bundle` - Bundle React Native app\n  - **Runtime**: 3-5 minutes\n  - **Common issues**: Native module linking, Metro bundler errors\n\n## Development Tools & Quality Assurance\n\n### Pre-commit Commands (Local Development)\n\n**Use these for fast pre-commit validation:**\n- `yarn lint:staged` - Lint only staged files (fast, recommended for pre-commit)\n- `yarn tsc:staged` - Type check staged files\n\n**Pre-commit workflow:**\n```bash\nyarn lint:staged && yarn tsc:staged && git commit -m \"your message\"\n```\n\n### CI Commands (Full Project Check)\n\n**These run in CI pipeline, not for local pre-commit:**\n- `yarn lint` - **CI ONLY** comprehensive linting\n  - **Expected runtime**: 5-10 minutes\n  - **Zero tolerance**: ALL warnings and errors MUST be fixed\n- `yarn lint:only` - Quick lint check (all files)\n- `yarn tsc:only` - Full TypeScript type check\n- `yarn test` - Test execution\n\n### Other Tools\n\n- `yarn clean` - Clean all build artifacts and node_modules\n- `yarn reinstall` - Full clean install (use when dependency issues occur)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Jest configuration in `jest.config.js`\n- Test setup in `jest-setup.js`\n- Tests located in `__tests__/` or `@tests/` directories within packages\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:52:08.132Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing streamlined application development with Electron and web development servers.","zh":"非常适合需要使用Electron和Web开发服务器进行流线化应用开发的全栈代理。","ja":"ElectronとWeb開発サーバーを使用したストリームライン化されたアプリケーション開発が必要なフルスタックエージェントに最適です。","ko":"Electron과 웹 개발 서버를 사용하여 스트림 라인화된 애플리케이션 개발이 필요한 풀 스택 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Full Stack que necesitan un desarrollo de aplicaciones optimizado con Electron y servidores de desarrollo web.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full Stack nécessitant un développement d''applications rationalisé avec Electron et des serveurs de développement web.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agenten, die eine optimierte Anwendungsentwicklung mit Electron und Web-Entwicklungsservern benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que necessitam de desenvolvimento de aplicativos simplificado com Electron e servidores de desenvolvimento web.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Full Stack, которым необходим упрощенный разработка приложений с помощью Electron и веб-серверов.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطبيق الكامل الذي يحتاج إلى تطور تطبيق مبسط مع إلكترون وخادم تطور الويب."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to accelerate development workflows using yarn commands, such as `yarn app:desktop` for desktop Electron app development and `yarn app:web` for web development, leveraging Node and native dependencies for efficient project setup and troubleshooting.","zh":"赋予代理人使用yarn命令加速开发工作流的能力，例如使用`yarn app:desktop`进行桌面Electron应用开发，使用`yarn app:web`进行Web开发，利用Node和本地依赖项实现高效的项目设置和故障排除。","ja":"エージェントがyarnコマンドを使用して開発ワークフローを加速できるようにし、例えば、`yarn app:desktop`を使用してデスクトップElectronアプリケーションを開発し、`yarn app:web`を使用してWeb開発を行い、Nodeとネイティブ依存関係を利用してプロジェクトの設定とトラブルシューティングを効率化します。","ko":"에이전트가 yarn 명령을 사용하여 개발 워크플ロー를 가속화 할 수 있도록 하여, 예를 들어 `yarn app:desktop`을 사용하여 데스크탑 Electron 애플리케이션 개발을하고, `yarn app:web`을 사용하여 웹 개발을 انجام하며, Node와 네이티브 종속성을 활용하여 프로젝트 설정과 문제 해결을 효율적으로 수행합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes acelerar los flujos de trabajo de desarrollo utilizando comandos de yarn, como `yarn app:desktop` para el desarrollo de aplicaciones de escritorio Electron y `yarn app:web` para el desarrollo web, aprovechando Node y dependencias nativas para una configuración y depuración de proyectos eficientes.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''accélérer les flux de travail de développement en utilisant des commandes yarn, telles que `yarn app:desktop` pour le développement d''applications de bureau Electron et `yarn app:web` pour le développement web, en exploitant Node et les dépendances natives pour une configuration et une dépannage de projet efficaces.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Entwicklungsworkflows mit yarn-Befehlen wie `yarn app:desktop` für die Entwicklung von Electron-Desktop-Anwendungen und `yarn app:web` für die Web-Entwicklung zu beschleunigen, indem es Node und native Abhängigkeiten für eine effiziente Projektsetup und Fehlerbehebung nutzt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a acelerar fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento usando comandos yarn, como `yarn app:desktop` para desenvolvimento de aplicativos de área de trabalho Electron e `yarn app:web` para desenvolvimento web, aproveitando Node e dependências nativas para configuração eficiente de projetos e solução de problemas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам ускорять рабочие процессы разработки с помощью команд yarn, таких как `yarn app:desktop` для разработки настольных приложений Electron и `yarn app:web` для веб-разработки, используя Node и родные зависимости для эффективной настройки проектов и устранения неполадок.","ar":"يمكن للوكيل تسريع تدفقات العمل التطويرية باستخدام أوامر yarn، مثل `yarn app:desktop` لتطوير تطبيقات سطح المكتب إلكترون وأوامر `yarn app:web` لتطوير الويب، واستخدام عقدة والاعتماديات الأصلية لإعداد مشروع فعال وتحليل المشاكل."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing desktop Electron app development with `yarn app:desktop`","Launching web development servers using `yarn app:web`","Troubleshooting startup issues with `yarn clean && yarn reinstall`"],"zh":["使用`yarn app:desktop`初始化桌面Electron应用开发","使用`yarn app:web`启动Web开发服务器","使用`yarn clean && yarn reinstall`故障排除启动问题"],"ja":["`yarn app:desktop`を使用してデスクトップElectronアプリケーション開発を初期化する","`yarn app:web`を使用してWeb開発サーバーを起動する","`yarn clean && yarn reinstall`を使用して起動時の問題をトラブルシューティングする"],"ko":["`yarn app:desktop`을 사용하여 데스크탑 Electron 애플리케이션 개발을 초기화하는 것","`yarn app:web`을 사용하여 웹 개발 서버를 시작하는 것","`yarn clean && yarn reinstall`을 사용하여 시작 시 문제를 해결하는 것"],"es":["Inicializar el desarrollo de aplicaciones de escritorio Electron con `yarn app:desktop`","Iniciar servidores de desarrollo web con `yarn app:web`","Solucionar problemas de inicio con `yarn clean && yarn reinstall`"],"fr":["Initialiser le développement d''applications de bureau Electron avec `yarn app:desktop`","Lancer des serveurs de développement web avec `yarn app:web`","Résoudre les problèmes de démarrage avec `yarn clean && yarn reinstall`"],"de":["Initialisieren der Entwicklung von Electron-Desktop-Anwendungen mit `yarn app:desktop`","Starten von Web-Entwicklungsservern mit `yarn app:web`","Beheben von Startproblemen mit `yarn clean && yarn reinstall`"],"pt":["Inicializar o desenvolvimento de aplicativos de área de trabalho Electron com `yarn app:desktop`","Iniciar servidores de desenvolvimento web usando `yarn app:web`","Solucionar problemas de inicialização com `yarn clean && yarn reinstall`"],"ru":["Инициализировать разработку настольных приложений Electron с помощью `yarn app:desktop`","Запустить веб-серверы разработки с помощью `yarn app:web`","Устранить проблемы запуска с помощью `yarn clean && yarn reinstall`"],"ar":["ت 초기ية تطوير تطبيقات سطح المكتب إلكترون باستخدام `yarn app:desktop`","تشغيل خادم تطور الويب باستخدام `yarn app:web`","تحليل مشاكل التشغيل باستخدام `yarn clean && yarn reinstall`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires compatible Node version","Dependent on native dependencies","Specific to Electron and web development environments"],"zh":["需要兼容的Node版本","依赖于本地依赖项","特定于Electron和Web开发环境"],"ja":["互換性のあるNodeバージョンが必要","ネイティブ依存関係に依存している","ElectronとWeb開発環境に特有"],"ko":["호환되는 Node 버전이 필요함","네이티브 종속성에 의존함","Electron과 웹 개발 환경에 특정"],"es":["Requiere una versión compatible de Node","Dependiente de dependencias nativas","Específico para entornos de desarrollo de Electron y web"],"fr":["Nécessite une version compatible de Node","Dépendant des dépendances natives","Spécifique aux environnements de développement Electron et web"],"de":["Benötigt eine kompatible Node-Version","Abhängig von nativen Abhängigkeiten","Spezifisch für Electron- und Web-Entwicklungsumgebungen"],"pt":["Exige versão compatível do Node","Depende de dependências nativas","Específico para ambientes de desenvolvimento Electron e web"],"ru":["Требует совместимой версии Node","Зависит от родных зависимостей","Конкретно для сред разработки Electron и веб"],"ar":["يتطلب إصدارًا متوافقًا من عقدة","يعتمد على الاعتماديات الأصلية","محدد للبيئات التطويرية إلكترون وتطوير الويب"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('brtstore4340-glitch/pos-gem/tailwind-design-system', 'community', 'brtstore4340-glitch', 'pos-gem', 'brtstore4340-glitch/pos-gem', 'tailwind-design-system', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z', '2026-02-18T09:52:03.804Z', NULL, '{"id":"brtstore4340-glitch/pos-gem/tailwind-design-system","name":"tailwind-design-system","description":{"zh":"Tailwind 设计系统是一个构建生产就绪的设计系统的解决方案，包括设计令牌、组件变体、响应式模式和无障碍功能","ja":"Tailwind デザインシステムは、デザイン トークン、コンポーネント バリアント、レスポンシブ パターン、無障碍機能などを含む生産準備のデザインシステムを構築するためのソリューションです","ko":"Tailwind 디자인 시스템은 디자인 토큰, 컴포넌트 변형, 반응형 패턴, 접근성 기능 등을 포함하여 프로덕션 준비 디자인 시스템을 구축하는 솔루션입니다","es":"Tailwind Design System es una herramienta para crear sistemas de diseño personalizados con Tailwind CSS, incluyendo tokens de diseño, variantes de componentes y patrones responsivos","fr":"Tailwind Design System est un outil pour créer des systèmes de design personnalisés avec Tailwind CSS, y compris des jetons de conception, des variantes de composants et des modèles responsives","de":"Tailwind Design System ist ein Werkzeug zum Erstellen benutzerdefinierter Designsysteme mit Tailwind CSS, einschließlich Design-Tokens, Komponenten-Varianten und responsiven Mustern","pt":"O sistema de design Tailwind é uma ferramenta para criar sistemas de design personalizados e responsivos com Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Дизайн-система Tailwind - это инструмент для создания индивидуальных и адаптивных систем дизайна с помощью Tailwind CSS.","ar":"نظام تصميم Tailwind هو أداة لإنشاء أنظمة تصميم مخصصة ومتجاوبة مع Tailwind CSS.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Tailwind 设计系统 - 构建生产就绪的设计系统","ja":"Tailwind デザインシステム - 生産準備のデザインシステムを構築","ko":"Tailwind 디자인 시스템 - 프로덕션 준비 디자인 시스템 구축","es":"Sistema de diseño Tailwind: construye sistemas de diseño ...","fr":"Système de design Tailwind: créez des systèmes de design ...","de":"Tailwind-Design-System: Erstellen Sie benutzerdefinierte ...","pt":"Sistema de Design Tailwind","ru":"Дизайн-система Tailwind","ar":"نظام تصميم Tailwind","en":"tailwind-design-system"},"description":{"zh":"Tailwind 设计系统是一个构建生产就绪的设计系统的解决方案，包括设计令牌、组件变体、响应式模式和无障碍功能","ja":"Tailwind デザインシステムは、デザイン トークン、コンポーネント バリアント、レスポンシブ パターン、無障碍機能などを含む生産準備のデザインシステムを構築するためのソリューションです","ko":"Tailwind 디자인 시스템은 디자인 토큰, 컴포넌트 변형, 반응형 패턴, 접근성 기능 등을 포함하여 프로덕션 준비 디자인 시스템을 구축하는 솔루션입니다","es":"Tailwind Design System es una herramienta para crear sistemas de diseño personalizados con Tailwind CSS, incluyendo tokens de diseño, variantes de componente...","fr":"Tailwind Design System est un outil pour créer des systèmes de design personnalisés avec Tailwind CSS, y compris des jetons de conception, des variantes de c...","de":"Tailwind Design System ist ein Werkzeug zum Erstellen benutzerdefinierter Designsysteme mit Tailwind CSS, einschließlich Design-Tokens, Komponenten-Varianten...","pt":"O sistema de design Tailwind é uma ferramenta para criar sistemas de design personalizados e responsivos com Tailwind CSS.","ru":"Дизайн-система Tailwind - это инструмент для создания индивидуальных и адаптивных систем дизайна с помощью Tailwind CSS.","ar":"نظام تصميم Tailwind هو أداة لإنشاء أنظمة تصميم مخصصة ومتجاوبة مع Tailwind CSS.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["设计令牌","组件变体","响应式模式","无障碍功能","暗黑模式和色彩方案"],"ja":["デザイン トークン","コンポーネント バリアント","レスポンシブ パターン","無障碍機能","ダーク モードとカラースキーム"],"ko":["디자인 토큰","컴포넌트 변형","반응형 패턴","접근성 기능","다크 모드와 색상 스키마"],"es":["Tokens de diseño personalizados","Variantes de componentes","Patrones responsivos","Accesibilidad mejorada","Implementación de temas y esquemas de color"],"fr":["Jetons de conception personnalisés","Variantes de composants","Modèles responsives","Accessibilité améliorée","Mise en œuvre de thèmes et de schémas de couleur"],"de":["Benutzerdefinierte Design-Tokens","Komponenten-Varianten","Responsives Muster","Verbesserte Zugänglichkeit","Implementierung von Themen und Farbschemata"],"pt":["Criação de bibliotecas de componentes com Tailwind","Implementação de tokens de design e temas","Criação de componentes responsivos e acessíveis","Padrões de UI personalizados","Migração para ou extensão do Tailwind CSS","Configuração de modo escuro e esquemas de cores"],"ru":["Создание библиотек компонентов с Tailwind","Реализация токенов дизайна и тем","Создание адаптивных и доступных компонентов","Индивидуальные шаблоны UI","Миграция на или расширение Tailwind CSS","Настройка темного режима и цветовых схем"],"ar":["إنشاء مكتبات مكونات مع Tailwind","تنفيذ رموز التصميم والألوان","إنشاء مكونات متجاوبة وسهلة الوصول","نماذج واجهة المستخدم المخصصة","هجرة إلى أو توسيع Tailwind CSS","تكوين الوضع الداكن وألوان الخلفية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Tailwind CSS","设计系统","生产就绪","设计令牌","组件变体","响应式模式","无障碍功能"],"ja":["Tailwind CSS","デザインシステム","生産準備","デザイン トークン","コンポーネント バリアント","レスポンシブ パターン","無障碍機能"],"ko":["Tailwind CSS","디자인 시스템","프로덕션 준비","디자인 토큰","컴포넌트 변형","반응형 패턴","접근성 기능"],"es":["Tailwind CSS","sistema de diseño","tokens de diseño","componentes personalizados","responsividad","accesibilidad","temas y esquemas de color"],"fr":["Tailwind CSS","système de design","jetons de conception","composants personnalisés","responsivité","accessibilité","thèmes et schémas de couleur"],"de":["Tailwind CSS","Design-System","Design-Tokens","benutzerdefinierte Komponenten","Responsivität","Zugänglichkeit","Themen und Farbschemata"],"pt":["Tailwind CSS","sistema de design","tokens de design","componentes responsivos","acessibilidade","bibliotecas de componentes","temas personalizados","modo escuro","esquemas de cores"],"ru":["Tailwind CSS","дизайн-система","токены дизайна","адаптивные компоненты","доступность","библиотеки компонентов","индивидуальные темы","темный режим","цветовые схемы"],"ar":["Tailwind CSS","نظام تصميم","رموز التصميم","مكونات متجاوبة","إمكانية الوصول","مكتبات المكونات","ألوان مخصصة","الوضع الداكن","ألوان الخلفية"]}},"owner":"brtstore4340-glitch","repo":"pos-gem","repoPath":"brtstore4340-glitch/pos-gem","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tailwind-design-system","description":"Build scalable design systems with Tailwind CSS, design tokens, component libraries, and responsive patterns. Use when creating component libraries, implementing design systems, or standardizing UI patterns.","bodyPreview":"# Tailwind Design System\n\nBuild production-ready design systems with Tailwind CSS, including design tokens, component variants, responsive patterns, and accessibility.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Creating a component library with Tailwind\n- Implementing design tokens and theming\n- Building responsive and accessible components\n- Standardizing UI patterns across a codebase\n- Migrating to or extending Tailwind CSS\n- Setting up dark mode and color schemes\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Design Token Hie","body":"# Tailwind Design System\n\nBuild production-ready design systems with Tailwind CSS, including design tokens, component variants, responsive patterns, and accessibility.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Creating a component library with Tailwind\n- Implementing design tokens and theming\n- Building responsive and accessible components\n- Standardizing UI patterns across a codebase\n- Migrating to or extending Tailwind CSS\n- Setting up dark mode and color schemes\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Design Token Hierarchy\n\n```\nBrand Tokens (abstract)\n    └── Semantic Tokens (purpose)\n        └── Component Tokens (specific)\n\nExample:\n    blue-500 → primary → button-bg\n```\n\n### 2. Component Architecture\n\n```\nBase styles → Variants → Sizes → States → Overrides\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\n// tailwind.config.ts\nimport type { Config } from \"tailwindcss\";\n\nconst config: Config = {\n  content: [\"./src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx,mdx}\"],\n  darkMode: \"class\",\n  theme: {\n    extend: {\n      colors: {\n        // Semantic color tokens\n        primary: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--primary))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--primary-foreground))\",\n        },\n        secondary: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--secondary))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--secondary-foreground))\",\n        },\n        destructive: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--destructive))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--destructive-foreground))\",\n        },\n        muted: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--muted))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--muted-foreground))\",\n        },\n        accent: {\n          DEFAULT: \"hsl(var(--accent))\",\n          foreground: \"hsl(var(--accent-foreground))\",\n        },\n        background: \"hsl(var(--background))\",\n        foreground: \"hsl(var(--foreground))\",\n        border: \"hsl(var(--border))\",\n        ring: \"hsl(var(--ring))\",\n      },\n      borderRadius: {\n        lg: \"var(--radius)\",\n        md: \"calc(var(--radius) - 2px)\",\n        sm: \"calc(var(--radius) - 4px)\",\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  plugins: [require(\"tailwindcss-animate\")],\n};\n\nexport default config;\n```\n\n```css\n/* globals.css */\n@tailwind base;\n@tailwind components;\n@tailwind utilities;\n\n@layer base {\n  :root {\n    --background: 0 0% 100%;\n    --foreground: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --primary: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --primary-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --secondary: 210 40% 96.1%;\n    --secondary-foreground: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --muted: 210 40% 96.1%;\n    --muted-foreground: 215.4 16.3% 46.9%;\n    --accent: 210 40% 96.1%;\n    --accent-foreground: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --destructive: 0 84.2% 60.2%;\n    --destructive-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --border: 214.3 31.8% 91.4%;\n    --ring: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --radius: 0.5rem;\n  }\n\n  .dark {\n    --background: 222.2 84% 4.9%;\n    --foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --primary: 210 40% 98%;\n    --primary-foreground: 222.2 47.4% 11.2%;\n    --secondary: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;\n    --secondary-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --muted: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;\n    --muted-foreground: 215 20.2% 65.1%;\n    --accent: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;\n    --accent-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --destructive: 0 62.8% 30.6%;\n    --destructive-foreground: 210 40% 98%;\n    --border: 217.2 32.6% 17.5%;\n    --ring: 212.7 26.8% 83.9%;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: CVA (Class Variance Authority) Components\n\n```typescript\n// components/ui/button.tsx\nimport { cva, type VariantProps } from ''class-variance-authority''\nimport { forwardRef } from ''react''\nimport { cn } from ''@/lib/utils''\n\nconst buttonVariants = cva(\n  // Base styles\n  ''inline-flex items-center justify-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-md text-sm font-medium ring-offset-background transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50'',\n  {\n    variants: {\n      variant: {\n        default: ''bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90'',\n        destructive: ''bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground hover:bg-destructive/90'',\n        outline: ''border border-input bg-background hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground'',\n        secondary: ''bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground hover:bg-secondary/80'',\n        ghost: ''hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground'',\n        link: ''text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline'',\n      },\n      size: {\n        default: ''h-10 px-4 py-2'',\n        sm: ''h-9 rounded-md px-3'',\n        lg: ''h-11 rounded-md px-8'',\n        icon: ''h-10 w-10'',\n      },\n    },\n    defaultVariants: {\n      variant: ''default'',\n      size: ''default'',\n    },\n  }\n)\n\nexport interface ButtonProps\n  extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>,\n    VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants> {\n  asChild?: boolean\n}\n\nconst Button = forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(\n  ({ className, variant, size, asChild = false, ...props }, ref) => {\n    const Comp = asChild ? Slot : ''button''\n    return (\n      <Comp\n        className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, size, className }))}\n        ref={ref}\n        {...props}\n      />\n    )\n  }\n)\nButton.displayName = ''Button''\n\nexport { Button, buttonVariants }\n\n// Usage\n<Button variant=\"destructive\" size=\"lg\">Delete</Button>\n<Button variant=\"outline\">Cancel</Button>\n<Button asChild><Link href=\"/home\">Home</Link></Button>\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Compound Components\n\n```typescript\n// components/ui/card.tsx\nimport { cn } from ''@/lib/utils''\nimport { forwardRef } from ''react''\n\nconst Card = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>>(\n  ({ className, ...props }, ref) => (\n    <div\n      ref={ref}\n      className={cn(\n        ''rounded-lg border bg-card text-card-foreground shadow-sm'',\n        className\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  )\n)\nCard.displayName = ''Card''\n\nconst CardHeader = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>>(\n  ({ className, ...props }, ref) => (\n    <div\n      ref={ref}\n      className={cn(''flex flex-col space-y-1.5 p-6'', className)}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  )\n)\nCardHeader.displayName = ''CardHeader''\n\nconst CardTitle = forwardRef<HTMLHeadingElement, React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLHeadingElement>>(\n  ({ className, ...props }, ref) => (\n    <h3\n      ref={ref}\n      className={cn(''text-2xl font-semibold leading-none tracking-tight'', className)}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  )\n)\nCardTitle.displayName = ''CardTitle''\n\nconst CardDescription = forwardRef<HTMLParagraphElement, React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLParagraphElement>>(\n  ({ className, ...props }, ref) => (\n    <p\n      ref={ref}\n      className={cn(''text-sm text-muted-foreground'', className)}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  )\n)\nCardDescription.displayName = ''CardDescription''\n\nconst CardContent = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>>(\n  ({ className, ...props }, ref) => (\n    <div ref={ref} className={cn(''p-6 pt-0'', className)} {...props} />\n  )\n)\nCardContent.displayName = ''CardContent''\n\nconst CardFooter = forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>>(\n  ({ className, ...props }, ref) => (\n    <div\n      ref={ref}\n      className={cn(''flex items-center p-6 pt-0'', className)}\n      {...props}\n    />\n  )\n)\nCardFooter.displayName = ''CardFooter''\n\nexport { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardDescription, CardContent, CardFooter }\n\n// Usage\n<Card>\n  <CardHeader>\n    <CardTitle>Account</CardTitle>\n    <CardDescription>Manage your account settings</CardDescription>\n  </CardHeader>\n  <CardContent>\n    <form>...</form>\n  </CardContent>\n  <CardFooter>\n    <Button>Save</Button>\n  </CardFooter>\n</Card>\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Form Components\n\n```typescript\n// components/ui/input.tsx\nimport { forwardRef } from ''react''\nimport { cn } from ''@/lib/utils''\n\nexport interface InputProps extends React.InputHTMLAttributes<HTMLInputElement> {\n  error?: string\n}\n\nconst Input = forwardRef<HTMLInputElement, InputProps>(\n  ({ className, type, error, ...props }, ref) => {\n    return (\n      <div className=\"relative\">\n        <input\n          type={type}\n          className={cn(\n            ''flex h-10 w-full rounded-md border border-input bg-background px-3 py-2 text-sm ring-offset-background file:border-0 file:bg-transparent file:text-sm file:font-medium placeholder:text-muted-foreground focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50'',\n            error && ''border-destructive focus-visible:ring-destructive'',\n            className\n          )}\n          ref={ref}\n          aria-invalid={!!error}\n          aria-describedby={error ? `${props.id}-error` : undefined}\n          {...props}\n        />\n        {error && (\n          <p\n            id={`${props.id}-error`}\n            className=\"mt-1 text-sm text-destructive\"\n            role=\"alert\"\n          >\n            {error}\n          </p>\n        )}\n      </div>\n    )\n  }\n)\nInput.displayName = ''Input''\n\n// components/ui/label.tsx\nimport { cva, type VariantProps } from ''class-variance-authority''\n\nconst labelVariants = cva(\n  ''text-sm font-medium leading-none peer-disabled:cursor-not-allowed peer-disabled:opacity-70''\n)\n\nconst Label = forwardRef<HTMLLabelElement, React.LabelHTMLAttributes<HTMLLabelElement>>(\n  ({ className, ...props }, ref) => (\n    <label ref={ref} className={cn(labelVariants(), className)} {...props} />\n  )\n)\nLabel.displayName = ''Label''\n\n// Usage with React Hook Form\nimport { useForm } from ''react-hook-form''\nimport { zodResolver } from ''@hookform/resolvers/zod''\nimport * as z from ''zod''\n\nconst schema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(''Invalid email address''),\n  password: z.string().min(8, ''Password must be at least 8 characters''),\n})\n\nfunction LoginForm() {\n  const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors } } = useForm({\n    resolver: zodResolver(schema),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className=\"space-y-4\">\n      <div className=\"space-y-2\">\n        <Label htmlFor=\"email\">Email</Label>\n        <Input\n          id=\"email\"\n          type=\"email\"\n          {...register(''email'')}\n          error={errors.email?.message}\n        />\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"space-y-2\">\n        <Label htmlFor=\"password\">Password</Label>\n        <Input\n          id=\"password\"\n          type=\"password\"\n          {...register(''password'')}\n          error={errors.password?.message}\n        />\n      </div>\n      <Button type=\"submit\" className=\"w-full\">Sign In</Button>\n    </form>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Pattern 4: Responsive Grid System\n\n```typescript\n// components/ui/grid.tsx\nimport { cn } from ''@/lib/utils''\nimport { cva, type VariantProps } from ''class-variance-authority''\n\nconst gridVariants = cva(''grid'', {\n  variants: {\n    cols: {\n      1: ''grid-cols-1'',\n      2: ''grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2'',\n      3: ''grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3'',\n      4: ''grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4'',\n      5: ''grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-5'',\n      6: ''grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-6'',\n    },\n    gap: {\n      none: ''gap-0'',\n      sm: ''gap-2'',\n      md: ''gap-4'',\n      lg: ''gap-6'',\n      xl: ''gap-8'',\n    },\n  },\n  defaultVariants: {\n    cols: 3,\n    gap: ''md'',\n  },\n})\n\ninterface GridProps\n  extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>,\n    VariantProps<typeof gridVariants> {}\n\nexport function Grid({ className, cols, gap, ...props }: GridProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className={cn(gridVariants({ cols, gap, className }))} {...props} />\n  )\n}\n\n// Container component\nconst containerVariants = cva(''mx-auto w-full px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8'', {\n  variants: {\n    size: {\n      sm: ''max-w-screen-sm'',\n      md: ''max-w-screen-md'',\n      lg: ''max-w-screen-lg'',\n      xl: ''max-w-screen-xl'',\n      ''2xl'': ''max-w-screen-2xl'',\n      full: ''max-w-full'',\n    },\n  },\n  defaultVariants: {\n    size: ''xl'',\n  },\n})\n\ninterface ContainerProps\n  extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>,\n    VariantProps<typeof containerVariants> {}\n\nexport function Container({ className, size, ...props }: ContainerProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className={cn(containerVariants({ size, className }))} {...props} />\n  )\n}\n\n// Usage\n<Container>\n  <Grid cols={4} gap=\"lg\">\n    {products.map((product) => (\n      <ProductCard key={product.id} product={product} />\n    ))}\n  </Grid>\n</Container>\n```\n\n### Pattern 5: Animation Utilities\n\n```typescript\n// lib/animations.ts - Tailwind CSS Animate utilities\nimport { cn } from ''./utils''\n\nexport const fadeIn = ''animate-in fade-in duration-300''\nexport const fadeOut = ''animate-out fade-out duration-300''\nexport const slideInFromTop = ''animate-in slide-in-from-top duration-300''\nexport const slideInFromBottom = ''animate-in slide-in-from-bottom duration-300''\nexport const slideInFromLeft = ''animate-in slide-in-from-left duration-300''\nexport const slideInFromRight = ''animate-in slide-in-from-right duration-300''\nexport const zoomIn = ''animate-in zoom-in-95 duration-300''\nexport const zoomOut = ''animate-out zoom-out-95 duration-300''\n\n// Compound animations\nexport const modalEnter = cn(fadeIn, zoomIn, ''duration-200'')\nexport const modalExit = cn(fadeOut, zoomOut, ''duration-200'')\nexport const dropdownEnter = cn(fadeIn, slideInFromTop, ''duration-150'')\nexport const dropdownExit = cn(fadeOut, ''slide-out-to-top'', ''duration-150'')\n\n// components/ui/dialog.tsx\nimport * as DialogPrimitive from ''@radix-ui/react-dialog''\n\nconst DialogOverlay = forwardRef<\n  React.ElementRef<typeof DialogPrimitive.Overlay>,\n  React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof DialogPrimitive.Overlay>\n>(({ className, ...props }, ref) => (\n  <DialogPrimitive.Overlay\n    ref={ref}\n    className={cn(\n      ''fixed inset-0 z-50 bg-black/80'',\n      ''data-[state=open]:animate-in data-[state=closed]:animate-out'',\n      ''data-[state=closed]:fade-out-0 data-[state=open]:fade-in-0'',\n      className\n    )}\n    {...props}\n  />\n))\n\nconst DialogContent = forwardRef<\n  React.ElementRef<typeof DialogPrimitive.Content>,\n  React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof DialogPrimitive.Content>\n>(({ className, children, ...props }, ref) => (\n  <DialogPortal>\n    <DialogOverlay />\n    <DialogPrimitive.Content\n      ref={ref}\n      className={cn(\n        ''fixed left-[50%] top-[50%] z-50 grid w-full max-w-lg translate-x-[-50%] translate-y-[-50%] gap-4 border bg-background p-6 shadow-lg'',\n        ''data-[state=open]:animate-in data-[state=closed]:animate-out'',\n        ''data-[state=closed]:fade-out-0 data-[state=open]:fade-in-0'',\n        ''data-[state=closed]:zoom-out-95 data-[state=open]:zoom-in-95'',\n        ''data-[state=closed]:slide-out-to-left-1/2 data-[state=closed]:slide-out-to-top-[48%]'',\n        ''data-[state=open]:slide-in-from-left-1/2 data-[state=open]:slide-in-from-top-[48%]'',\n        ''sm:rounded-lg'',\n        className\n      )}\n      {...props}\n    >\n      {children}\n    </DialogPrimitive.Content>\n  </DialogPortal>\n))\n```\n\n### Pattern 6: Dark Mode Implementation\n\n```typescript\n// providers/ThemeProvider.tsx\n''use client''\n\nimport { createContext, useContext, useEffect, useState } from ''react''\n\ntype Theme = ''dark'' | ''light'' | ''system''\n\ninterface ThemeProviderProps {\n  children: React.ReactNode\n  defaultTheme?: Theme\n  storageKey?: string\n}\n\ninterface ThemeContextType {\n  theme: Theme\n  setTheme: (theme: Theme) => void\n  resolvedTheme: ''dark'' | ''light''\n}\n\nconst ThemeContext = createContext<ThemeContextType | undefined>(undefined)\n\nexport function ThemeProvider({\n  children,\n  defaultTheme = ''system'',\n  storageKey = ''theme'',\n}: ThemeProviderProps) {\n  const [theme, setTheme] = useState<Theme>(defaultTheme)\n  const [resolvedTheme, setResolvedTheme] = useState<''dark'' | ''light''>(''light'')\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const stored = localStorage.getItem(storageKey) as Theme | null\n    if (stored) setTheme(stored)\n  }, [storageKey])\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const root = window.document.documentElement\n    root.classList.remove(''light'', ''dark'')\n\n    let resolved: ''dark'' | ''light''\n\n    if (theme === ''system'') {\n      resolved = window.matchMedia(''(prefers-color-scheme: dark)'').matches\n        ? ''dark''\n        : ''light''\n    } else {\n      resolved = theme\n    }\n\n    root.classList.add(resolved)\n    setResolvedTheme(resolved)\n  }, [theme])\n\n  const value = {\n    theme,\n    setTheme: (newTheme: Theme) => {\n      localStorage.setItem(storageKey, newTheme)\n      setTheme(newTheme)\n    },\n    resolvedTheme,\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <ThemeContext.Provider value={value}>{children}</ThemeContext.Provider>\n  )\n}\n\nexport const useTheme = () => {\n  const context = useContext(ThemeContext)\n  if (!context) throw new Error(''useTheme must be used within ThemeProvider'')\n  return context\n}\n\n// components/ThemeToggle.tsx\nimport { Moon, Sun } from ''lucide-react''\nimport { useTheme } from ''@/providers/ThemeProvider''\n\nexport function ThemeToggle() {\n  const { resolvedTheme, setTheme } = useTheme()\n\n  return (\n    <Button\n      variant=\"ghost\"\n      size=\"icon\"\n      onClick={() => setTheme(resolvedTheme === ''dark'' ? ''light'' : ''dark'')}\n    >\n      <Sun className=\"h-5 w-5 rotate-0 scale-100 transition-all dark:-rotate-90 dark:scale-0\" />\n      <Moon className=\"absolute h-5 w-5 rotate-90 scale-0 transition-all dark:rotate-0 dark:scale-100\" />\n      <span className=\"sr-only\">Toggle theme</span>\n    </Button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Utility Functions\n\n```typescript\n// lib/utils.ts\nimport { type ClassValue, clsx } from \"clsx\";\nimport { twMerge } from \"tailwind-merge\";\n\nexport function cn(...inputs: ClassValue[]) {\n  return twMerge(clsx(inputs));\n}\n\n// Focus ring utility\nexport const focusRing = cn(\n  \"focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2\",\n  \"focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2\",\n);\n\n// Disabled utility\nexport const disabled = \"disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50\";\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Use CSS variables** - Enable runtime theming\n- **Compose with CVA** - Type-safe variants\n- **Use semantic colors** - `primary` not `blue-500`\n- **Forward refs** - Enable composition\n- **Add accessibility** - ARIA attributes, focus states\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t use arbitrary values** - Extend theme instead\n- **Don''t nest @apply** - Hurts readability\n- **Don''t skip focus states** - Keyboard users need them\n- **Don''t hardcode colors** - Use semantic tokens\n- **Don''t forget dark mode** - Test both themes\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Tailwind CSS Documentation](https://tailwindcss.com/docs)\n- [CVA Documentation](https://cva.style/docs)\n- [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/)\n- [Radix Primitives](https://www.radix-ui.com/primitives)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:52:03.804Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing streamlined CSS styling with Tailwind CSS","zh":"非常适合需要简化CSS样式的前端代理，使用Tailwind CSS","ja":"フロントエンドエージェントがTailwind CSSを使用してCSSスタイリングを스트リーミングする必要がある場合に最適","ko":"프론트엔드 에이전트가 Tailwind CSS를 사용하여 CSS 스타일링을 스트리밍해야 하는 경우에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes Frontend que necesitan un estilo de CSS simplificado con Tailwind CSS","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend ayant besoin d''un style de CSS simplifié avec Tailwind CSS","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agenten, die ein vereinfachtes CSS-Design mit Tailwind CSS benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de estilização de CSS simplificada com Tailwind CSS","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, которым необходим упрощенный стиль CSS с помощью Tailwind CSS","ar":"مثالي لعميل واجهة المستخدم الأمامية الذي يحتاج إلى تنسيق CSS مبسط مع Tailwind CSS"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build production-ready design systems with Tailwind CSS, including design tokens, component variants, responsive patterns, and accessibility, utilizing CSS libraries and protocols","zh":"赋予代理构建生产就绪的设计系统的能力，使用Tailwind CSS，包括设计令牌、组件变体、响应式模式和无障碍，利用CSS库和协议","ja":"Tailwind CSSを使用して、デザイントークン、コンポーネントのバリアント、レスポンシブパターン、アクセシビリティを含む、生産就緒のデザインシステムを構築するエージェントの能力を付与する、CSSライブラリとプロトコルを利用","ko":"에이전트가 Tailwind CSS를 사용하여 디자인 토큰, 컴포넌트 변형, 반응형 패턴 및 접근성을 포함하는 生産就緒의 디자인 시스템을 구축할 수 있는 능력을 부여함, CSS 라이브러리 및 프로토콜을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear sistemas de diseño listos para producción con Tailwind CSS, incluyendo tokens de diseño, variantes de componentes, patrones responsivos y accesibilidad, utilizando 