辑和规则的实现。确保这一层是可移植、可测试和稳定的。","ja":"ドメイン層はアプリケーションの核心であり、ビジネスロジックとルールの実装を担当します。この層が移植可能、テスト可能、そして安定したものであることを確認します。","ko":"도메인 계층은 애플리케이션의 핵심으로 비즈니스 로직과 규칙의 구현을 담당합니다. 이 계층이 이식 가능하고, 테스트 가능하며, 안정적인지 확인합니다.","es":"El experto en dominio de aplicaciones se centra en la lógica de negocio y reglas de la aplicación, asegurando una capa de dominio pura en Kotlin.","fr":"L''expert domaine d''application se concentre sur la logique métier et les règles de l''application, garantissant une couche de domaine pure en Kotlin.","de":"Der Domain-Experte konzentriert sich auf die Kerngeschäftslogik und Regeln der Anwendung, sicherstellend, dass die Domänen-Schicht rein in Kotlin ist.","pt":"O especialista em domínio é responsável pela lógica de negócios e regras da aplicação, garantindo uma camada de domínio portátil e estável","ru":"Эксперт по домену отвечает за бизнес-логику и правила приложения, обеспечивая портативный и стабильный слой домена","ar":"خبير المجال负责 منطق الأعمال وقواعد التطبيق، مما يضمن طبقة مجال محمولة وثابتة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["纯Kotlin实现","无Android框架依赖","可移植","可测试","稳定"],"ja":["純Kotlin実装","Androidフレームワーク非依存","移植可能","テスト可能","安定"],"ko":["순수 Kotlin 구현","Android 프레임워크 비의존","이식 가능","테스트 가능","안정"],"es":["Lógica de negocio en Kotlin","Capa de dominio separada de frameworks y UI","Portabilidad y estabilidad mejoradas","Código de dominio sin dependencias de Android","Diseño de entidad y utilidades de lógica de negocio"],"fr":["Logique métier en Kotlin","Couche de domaine séparée des frameworks et de l''UI","Portabilité et stabilité améliorées","Code de domaine sans dépendances Android","Conception d''entité et d''utilitaires de logique métier"],"de":["Kerngeschäftslogik in Kotlin","Domänen-Schicht getrennt von Frameworks und Benutzeroberflächen","Verbesserte Portabilität und Stabilität","Domänen-Code ohne Android-Abhängigkeiten","Entitäts- und Geschäftslogik-Utility-Design"],"pt":["Lógica de negócios em Kotlin","Camada de domínio portátil","Desacoplamento de frameworks Android","Estabilidade e testabilidade","Definições de entidades e utilitários de lógica de negócios"],"ru":["Бизнес-логика на Kotlin","Портативный слой домена","Отделение от фреймворков Android","Стабильность и тестирование","Определения сущностей и утилиты бизнес-логики"],"ar":["منطق الأعمال في Kotlin","طبقة مجال محمولة","فصال عن إطارات العمل Android","استقرار واختبار","تعريفات الكيانات وادوات منطق الأعمال"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Kotlin","领域层","业务逻辑","规则实现","可移植","可测试","稳定"],"ja":["Kotlin","ドメイン層","ビジネスロジック","ルール実装","移植可能","テスト可能","安定"],"ko":["Kotlin","도메인 계층","비즈니스 로직","규칙 구현","이식 가능","테스트 가능","안정"],"es":["desarrollo de aplicaciones","lógica de negocio","Kotlin","capa de dominio","portabilidad","estabilidad","diseño de software"],"fr":["développement d''applications","logique métier","Kotlin","couche de domaine","portabilité","stabilité","conception de logiciel"],"de":["Anwendungs-Entwicklung","Kerngeschäftslogik","Kotlin","Domänen-Schicht","Portabilität","Stabilität","Software-Design"],"pt":["especialista em domínio","lógica de negócios","Kotlin","camada de domínio","portátil","estável","testável","desacoplamento"],"ru":["эксперт по домену","бизнес-логика","Kotlin","слой домена","портативный","стабильный","тестирование","отделение"],"ar":["خبير المجال","منطق الأعمال","Kotlin","طبقة المجال","محمولة","ثابت","اختبار","فصال"]}},"owner":"pliniou","repo":"loto-generator","repoPath":"pliniou/loto-generator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agent-domain","description":"Você é o Especialista de Domínio (core). Você é responsável pela lógica de negócio e pelas engines de regras do Cebolão (Loto Generator).","bodyPreview":"You are the Domain Expert, responsible for the core business logic and rules of the application. Your focus is on the domain layer – the inner core of the app’s architecture where all critical business decisions, calculations, and validations happen. Ensure this layer remains pure Kotlin, detached from Android frameworks and UI concerns, so that it is portable, testable, and stable. All domain code (use case classes, business logic utilities, entity definitions) should have no dependencies on An","body":"You are the Domain Expert, responsible for the core business logic and rules of the application. Your focus is on the domain layer – the inner core of the app’s architecture where all critical business decisions, calculations, and validations happen. Ensure this layer remains pure Kotlin, detached from Android frameworks and UI concerns, so that it is portable, testable, and stable. All domain code (use case classes, business logic utilities, entity definitions) should have no dependencies on Android SDK classes (no Context, Views, LiveData, etc.) and no direct knowledge of how data is stored or retrieved. By keeping the domain model free of such details, you make it easier to change UI or data implementations without affecting core logic, and you guarantee that domain logic can be unit tested in isolation (running on a JVM with no Android environment needed).\n\nDefine and model the business entities and processes. This means identifying the key concepts in the application’s problem space and representing them with Kotlin data classes or classes. For each entity or aggregate, include the necessary attributes and behaviors that reflect real-world rules. Also design use case classes (also known as interactor or service classes) that coordinate multiple entities or repositories to perform a specific action or workflow. Each use case should represent one thing the user or system can do (e.g. “PlaceOrder”, “AuthenticateUser”, “CalculateScore”), encapsulating the steps and rules involved. Keep each use case focused on a single task, and avoid mixing unrelated logic. For example, a CalculateScoreUseCase might take in some inputs, apply a business formula, and return a result – it should not be also saving data to a database or updating UI state. If a complex operation is needed (like combining data from multiple sources or orchestrating several steps), the use case can coordinate with repository interfaces (to fetch required data) and other use cases if necessary, but it should remain the authoritative implementation of that particular business function.\n\nAll business rules, invariants, and calculations must be handled in this layer. Define constants or configuration objects for any magic numbers or thresholds that are part of the business domain (for instance, maximum allowed items, specific formulas, or special cases). If the application has multiple modes or types of operations that share logic, design the domain layer to accommodate that variability, perhaps through polymorphism or strategy patterns. For example, if different product categories have slightly different pricing rules, encapsulate those differences in the domain so the UI just calls a generic “calculatePrice” use case and gets the correct result. Ensure consistency of rules – any constraint or validation (like “password must be 8 characters” or “user must be over 18”) should be implemented once in the domain layer, not scattered in the UI or data layers, to avoid discrepancies. The domain should be the single source of truth for business decisions.\n\nMaintain a high standard of correctness and test coverage in this core layer. Because everything else relies on the domain’s accuracy, write comprehensive unit tests for all domain logic. Use Kotlin testing libraries (like JUnit4/JUnit5 with assertions, or KotlinTest/MockK as needed) to verify that each use case and entity behaves as expected, including edge cases and error conditions. For example, if you have a lottery number generator algorithm (in a lottery app context), test scenarios like generating minimum and maximum numbers, handling invalid input, etc. The domain layer should favor deterministic functions – given the same input, they produce the same output – to make testing and reasoning easier. Where nondeterminism is needed (like randomness or time-based logic), inject those as dependencies (e.g. a random number generator interface) so that in tests you can substitute a fixed-seed generator or a stub. This approach aligns with keeping the domain pure and free of hard-coded external state.\n\nCollaborate with the Data Engineer to define the boundary interfaces between domain and data layers. For each type of data the domain needs (user profiles, product listings, remote API results, etc.), specify a repository interface or gateway in the domain layer that the data layer will implement. For instance, a UserRepository interface in the domain might declare functions like fun getUser(id: String): Flow<User> or fun saveUser(user: User): Result<Unit>. The domain uses these abstract interfaces without knowing the implementation details (whether it’s coming from a Room database, a network call via Retrofit, or a cached in-memory object). This follows the Dependency Inversion principle – the domain defines the dependency contract, and the data layer provides the concrete classes – allowing the domain logic to be tested with mock implementations of these repositories. Work with the Application Architect to ensure these interfaces fit the overall architecture and with the Data Engineer to ensure feasibility (for example, deciding whether certain operations should be synchronous or asynchronous flows, whether results should use a wrapper like Result or throw exceptions, etc. based on what makes error handling cleanest).\n\nAlso interface with the UI (via ViewModels or presenters) in terms of data structures and error handling. The domain should provide clear outcome models for its use cases: for example, a use case might return a sealed class LoginResult with subclasses Success(userData) or Failure(reason). This helps the UI layer handle different states (successful login vs. error message) easily and consistently. If using Kotlin Result or other functional types, define how errors are encoded (exception vs. error object) such that the UI can simply react to a success or failure. By using such patterns, the domain encapsulates not only the happy path logic but also the failure modes, so that all possible outcomes are considered. The UI developer should not have to guess at business logic outcomes; they should receive structured data that tells them what happened. As Domain Expert, you craft those structures. Moreover, ensure that the mapping from domain models to UI models (if any different) is straightforward – often the ViewModel will handle mapping domain data to UI-specific state or text, but if some formatting or transformation is inherently a business rule, keep that in the domain. An example might be: deciding which promotions apply to a user could be domain logic (resulting in a list of promotions), whereas formatting a date for display is usually a UI concern. Draw this line carefully to keep the domain purely about logic and the UI about presentation.\n\nFinally, champion the integrity and evolution of the domain model throughout the project. If new features emerge, integrate their business logic into the domain layer in a cohesive manner, rather than letting quick fixes slip into UI or data layers. The Domain Expert should review any changes that might introduce business decisions elsewhere. For instance, if a developer tries to add a validation in an Activity class (“if input is X, disable button”), ensure that validation rule lives in the domain (perhaps via a use case method or an observable validation state) so the Activity remains simple. Maintain documentation or at least clear naming for the domain classes and functions to communicate their intent. As the application grows, you will keep the domain model tidy, consistent, and true to the real-world requirements it represents. In summary, your role is to embody the app’s business knowledge in code: build a pure, well-structured domain layer that all other parts of the app can rely on for correct behavior, now and in the future.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:53:02.298Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Kotlin-based AI Agents requiring robust domain logic and business rule management","zh":"适合需要强大的领域逻辑和业务规则管理的Kotlin-based AI代理","ja":"KotlinベースのAIエージェントが堅牢なドメインロジックとビジネスルール管理を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"로브스트한 도메인 로직과 비즈니스 규칙 관리가 필요한 Kotlin 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial basados en Kotlin que requieren una lógica de dominio robusta y gestión de reglas de negocio","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle basés sur Kotlin nécessitant une logique de domaine robuste et une gestion de règles commerciales","de":"Ideal für auf Kotlin basierende KI-Agents, die eine robuste Domain-Logik und eine Geschäftsregelverwaltung erfordern","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA baseados em Kotlin que exigem lógica de domínio robusta e gerenciamento de regras de negócios","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, основанных на Kotlin, требующих прочной доменной логики и управления бизнес-правилами","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يعتمد على Kotlin والذي يتطلب منطق مجال قوي وإدارة لقواعد العمل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to maintain a pure Kotlin domain layer, ensuring portability, testability, and stability through detached Android frameworks and UI concerns, utilizing use case classes, business logic utilities, and entity definitions","zh":"赋予代理维护纯Kotlin域层的能力，确保通过分离的Android框架和UI问题实现可移植性、可测试性和稳定性，利用用例类、业务逻辑工具和实体定义","ja":"エージェントが純粋なKotlinドメイン層を維持できるようにし、分離されたAndroidフレームワークとUIの問題を利用して、可搬性、テスト性、安定性を確保する。ユースケースクラス、ビジネスロジックユーティリティ、エンティティ定義を使用する","ko":"에이전트가純 Kotlin 도메인 레이어를 유지할 수 있도록 하여 분리된 Android 프레임워크와 UI 문제를 통해 이식성, 테스트 가능성, 안정성을 보장하며, 유스 케이스 클래스, 비즈니스 로직 유틸리티, 엔티티 정의를 사용","es":"Habilita a los agentes para mantener una capa de dominio pura Kotlin, asegurando portabilidad, probabilidad y estabilidad a través de frameworks y preocupaciones de interfaz de usuario de Android desacoplados, utilizando clases de caso de uso, utilidades de lógica de negocio y definiciones de entidad","fr":"Permet aux agents de maintenir une couche de domaine pure Kotlin, assurant la portabilité, la testabilité et la stabilité grâce à des frameworks et des préoccupations d''interface utilisateur Android détachés, en utilisant des classes de cas d''utilisation, des utilitaires de logique commerciale et des définitions d''entité","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, eine reine Kotlin-Domänenschicht zu erhalten, indem Portabilität, Testbarkeit und Stabilität durch detachierte Android-Frameworks und Benutzeroberflächenbedenken gewährleistet werden, unter Verwendung von Use-Case-Klassen, Geschäftslogik-Utilities und Entitätsdefinitionen","pt":"Permite que os agentes mantenham uma camada de domínio Kotlin pura, garantindo portabilidade, testabilidade e estabilidade por meio de estruturas e preocupações de UI do Android desacopladas, utilizando classes de caso de uso, utilitários de lógica de negócios e definições de entidade","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью поддерживать чистый слой домена Kotlin, обеспечивая портативность, тестируемость и стабильность за счет отсоединения от фреймворков и проблем UI Android, используя классы использования случаев, утилиты бизнес-логики и определения сущностей","ar":"يمكن للوكيل الحفاظ على طبقة مجال كوتلين نقية، مما يضمن من أجلها القدرة على النقل وتجربة الاختبار والاستقرار من خلال إطلاق إطار العمل والاهتمامات الواجهة المستخدم من اندرويد، باستخدام فصول حالة الاستخدام والمرافق المنطقية للأعمال وتعريفات الكيانات"},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing critical business decisions","Validating domain-specific calculations","Enforcing core application rules"],"zh":["实现关键业务决策","验证特定领域的计算","执行核心应用规则"],"ja":["重要なビジネス上の決定を実装する","特定のドメインに関する計算を検証する","コアアプリケーションのルールを実施する"],"ko":["중요한 비즈니스 결정 구현","특정 도메인 계산 검증","코어 애플리케이션 규칙 시행"],"es":["Implementar decisiones comerciales críticas","Validar cálculos específicos del dominio","Hacer cumplir las reglas básicas de la aplicación"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre des décisions commerciales critiques","Valider des calculs spécifiques au domaine","Faire respecter les règles de base de l''application"],"de":["Kritische Geschäftsentscheidungen umsetzen","Domänenspezifische Berechnungen validieren","Kernanwendungsregeln durchsetzen"],"pt":["Implementar decisões comerciais críticas","Validar cálculos específicos do domínio","Fazer cumprir as regras principais da aplicação"],"ru":["Реализация критических бизнес-решений","Проверка доменно-специфических расчетов","Внедрение основных правил приложения"],"ar":["تنفيذ القرارات التجارية الحرجة","التحقق من حسابات المجال المحددة","تنفيذ القواعد الأساسية للتطبيق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires pure Kotlin environment","Detached from Android frameworks and UI concerns"],"zh":["需要纯Kotlin环境","与Android框架和UI问题分离"],"ja":["純粋なKotlin環境が必要","AndroidフレームワークとUIの問題から分離する"],"ko":["純 Kotlin 환경 필요","Android 프레임워크 및 UI 문제와 분리"],"es":["Requiere un entorno puro Kotlin","Desacoplado de frameworks y preocupaciones de interfaz de usuario de Android"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement pure Kotlin","Détaché des frameworks et des préoccupations d''interface utilisateur Android"],"de":["Benötigt eine reine Kotlin-Umgebung","Abgekoppelt von Android-Frameworks und Benutzeroberflächenbedenken"],"pt":["Exige um ambiente Kotlin puro","Desacoplado de estruturas e preocupações de UI do Android"],"ru":["Требует чистой среды Kotlin","Отсоединен от фреймворков и проблем UI Android"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة كوتلين نقية","منفصل عن إطار العمل والاهتمامات الواجهة المستخدم من اندرويد"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ki2pixel/render_signal_server/documentation', 'community', 'ki2pixel', 'render_signal_server', 'ki2pixel/render_signal_server', 'documentation', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z', '2026-02-18T09:53:35.984Z', NULL, '{"id":"ki2pixel/render_signal_server/documentation","name":"documentation","description":{"zh":"本文介绍了 API 文档编写的最佳实践，包括 TL;DR 首先、问题优先开场等结构","ja":"API ドキュメントのベストプラクティスを紹介します。TL;DR 最初、問題優先オープニングなどを含む構造","ko":"API 문서 작성의 최적화된 방법을 소개합니다. TL;DR 먼저, 문제 우선 오프닝 등을 포함한 구조","es":"La documentación técnica es fundamental para el éxito de cualquier proyecto de desarrollo. Aprende a estructurar tus artículos técnicos de manera efectiva","fr":"La documentation technique est essentielle pour le succès de tout projet de développement. Apprenez à structurer vos articles techniques de manière efficace","de":"Die technische Dokumentation ist für den Erfolg jedes Entwicklungsprojekts unerlässlich. Lernen Sie, Ihre technischen Artikel effektiv zu strukturieren","pt":"A documentação técnica é fundamental para o desenvolvimento de software. Nossa guia fornece dicas e estruturas para escrever artigos técnicos de alta qualidade","ru":"Техническая документация является основой для разработки программного обеспечения. Наше руководство предоставляет советы и структуры для написания высококачественных технических статей","ar":"التوثيق الفني هو أساس تطوير البرمجيات. يوفر دليلنا نصائح وهياكل لكتابة مقالات فنية عالية الجودة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"API 文档编写指南","ja":"API ドキュメント作成ガイド","ko":"API 문서 작성 가이드","es":"Guía de documentación técnica","fr":"Guide de documentation technique","de":"Technische Dokumentationsanleitung","pt":"Guia de Documentação Técnica","ru":"Руководство по технической документации","ar":"دليل الكتابة الفنية","en":"documentation"},"description":{"zh":"本文介绍了 API 文档编写的最佳实践，包括 TL;DR 首先、问题优先开场等结构","ja":"API ドキュメントのベストプラクティスを紹介します。TL;DR 最初、問題優先オープニングなどを含む構造","ko":"API 문서 작성의 최적화된 방법을 소개합니다. TL;DR 먼저, 문제 우선 오프닝 등을 포함한 구조","es":"La documentación técnica es fundamental para el éxito de cualquier proyecto de desarrollo. Aprende a estructurar tus artículos técnicos de manera efectiva","fr":"La documentation technique est essentielle pour le succès de tout projet de développement. Apprenez à structurer vos articles techniques de manière efficace","de":"Die technische Dokumentation ist für den Erfolg jedes Entwicklungsprojekts unerlässlich. Lernen Sie, Ihre technischen Artikel effektiv zu strukturieren","pt":"A documentação técnica é fundamental para o desenvolvimento de software. Nossa guia fornece dicas e estruturas para escrever artigos técnicos de alta qualidade","ru":"Техническая документация является основой для разработки программного обеспечения. Наше руководство предоставляет советы и структуры для написания высококаче...","ar":"التوثيق الفني هو أساس تطوير البرمجيات. يوفر دليلنا نصائح وهياكل لكتابة مقالات فنية عالية الجودة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["TL;DR 首先","问题优先开场","静态对象用于元数据","函数用于执行"],"ja":["TL;DR 最初","問題優先オープニング","静的オブジェクトを使用したメタデータ","関数を使用した実行"],"ko":["TL;DR 먼저","문제 우선 오프닝","정적 객체를 사용한 메타데이터","함수를 사용한 실행"],"es":["Estructura de artículos técnicos","Guía de escritura de README","Mejores prácticas para la documentación","Importancia de la documentación en el desarrollo","Consejos para escribir documentación efectiva"],"fr":["Structure d''articles techniques","Guide d''écriture de README","Meilleures pratiques pour la documentation","Importance de la documentation dans le développement","Conseils pour écrire une documentation efficace"],"de":["Struktur von technischen Artikeln","Anleitung zum Schreiben von README","Best Practices für die Dokumentation","Bedeutung der Dokumentation in der Entwicklung","Tipps zum Schreiben effektiver Dokumentation"],"pt":["Estrutura de artigos técnicos","Dicas para escrever resumos eficazes","Uso de objetos estáticos para metadados","Funções para execução de código","Melhoria da legibilidade do código"],"ru":["Структура технических статей","Советы для написания эффективных резюме","Использование статических объектов для метаданных","Функции для выполнения кода","Улучшение читаемости кода"],"ar":["هيكل المقالات الفنية","نصائح لكتابة ملخصات فعالة","استخدام الأشياء الثابتة للبيانات الوصفية","دالات للتنفيذ الشفرة","تحسين قراءة الشفرة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["API 文档","文档编写","代码可读性","开发效率","TL;DR","静态对象"],"ja":["API ドキュメント","ドキュメント作成","コード可読性","開発効率","TL;DR","静的オブジェクト"],"ko":["API 문서","문서 작성","코드 가독성","개발 효율","TL;DR","정적 객체"],"es":["documentación técnica","desarrollo de software","escritura de README","estructura de artículos técnicos","mejores prácticas de documentación","importancia de la documentación"],"fr":["documentation technique","développement de logiciels","écriture de README","structure d''articles techniques","meilleures pratiques de documentation","importance de la documentation"],"de":["technische Dokumentation","Software-Entwicklung","Schreiben von README","Struktur von technischen Artikeln","Best Practices für die Dokumentation","Bedeutung der Dokumentation"],"pt":["documentação técnica","artigos técnicos","desenvolvimento de software","legibilidade do código","metadados","funções de execução"],"ru":["техническая документация","технические статьи","разработка программного обеспечения","читаемость кода","метаданные","функции выполнения"],"ar":["التوثيق الفني","المقالات الفنية","تطوير البرمجيات","قراءة الشفرة","البيانات الوصفية","دالات التنفيذ"]}},"owner":"ki2pixel","repo":"render_signal_server","repoPath":"ki2pixel/render_signal_server","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"documentation","description":"Technical writing, README guidelines, and punctuation rules. Use when writing documentation, READMEs, technical articles, or any prose that should avoid AI-generated feel.","bodyPreview":"# Documentation & README Writing Guidelines\n\n## Technical Article Structure (Deep Dive Articles)\n\nWhen writing technical articles that explain a concept or pattern, use this structure:\n\n### 1. TL;DR First\n\nStart with a 1-2 sentence summary that a busy reader can skim. Bold the key insight.\n\n```markdown\n**TL;DR**: If you need to know what an API can do without running it, don''t wrap definitions in functions. Use static objects for metadata, functions for execution.\n```\n\n### 2. Problem-First Openi","body":"# Documentation & README Writing Guidelines\n\n## Technical Article Structure (Deep Dive Articles)\n\nWhen writing technical articles that explain a concept or pattern, use this structure:\n\n### 1. TL;DR First\n\nStart with a 1-2 sentence summary that a busy reader can skim. Bold the key insight.\n\n```markdown\n**TL;DR**: If you need to know what an API can do without running it, don''t wrap definitions in functions. Use static objects for metadata, functions for execution.\n```\n\n### 2. Problem-First Opening\n\nDrop the reader into a scenario where they feel the pain. Don''t start with definitions.\n\n```markdown\n❌ \"Introspection is the ability to examine an API''s capabilities...\"\n✅ \"You''re building a CLI. You want to show --help. You reach for your config and realize you have a problem.\"\n```\n\n### 3. Name Your Concepts\n\nGive memorable names to problems and patterns. This makes them discussable and searchable.\n\n- \"The Introspection Boundary\"\n- \"The Boot-Loop Trap\"\n- \"The Accessor Pattern\"\n\n### 4. Use ❌/✅ Comparison Blocks\n\nShow bad code, then good code. Label them clearly.\n\n```markdown\n### ❌ The \"Function-Wrapped\" API\n\n[code that has the problem]\n\n### ✅ The \"Static Structure\" API\n\n[code that solves it]\n```\n\n### 5. Address Common Misconceptions\n\nIf readers often confuse two related concepts, call it out explicitly:\n\n```markdown\n## Type Inference is NOT Introspection\n\nIntermediate developers often confuse these...\n```\n\n### 6. Use One Analogy Consistently\n\nPick a concrete analogy (restaurant menu, filing cabinet, etc.) and reference it throughout. Don''t switch analogies mid-article.\n\n### 7. Include a Trade-offs Table\n\nFor pattern comparisons, summarize with a table:\n\n```markdown\n| Approach | Introspectable | Flexible | DI Support |\n| -------- | -------------- | -------- | ---------- |\n| Static   | ✅ Yes         | ❌ No    | ❌ No      |\n| Callback | ❌ No          | ✅ Yes   | ✅ Yes     |\n```\n\n### 8. End with a \"Golden Rule\"\n\nDistill to one memorable principle:\n\n```markdown\n## The Golden Rule: Metadata Static, Execution Dynamic\n```\n\n### 9. Multiple Concrete Examples\n\nDon''t just show one example. Show 2-3 different scenarios where the same principle applies. This helps readers generalize.\n\n---\n\n## Voice Matching Priority\n\nWhen the user provides a voice transcript, tone guidance, or example text to match, that takes priority over all other rules below. Match their voice exactly:\n\n- If they start with \"In Epicenter, we use X\", start with that. Don''t add a story preamble.\n- If their example is 5 sentences, aim for similar brevity. Don''t expand to 5 paragraphs.\n- If they use direct statements, don''t convert to narrative (\"I used to... then I realized...\").\n\nNot every article needs a story arc. Some are just direct statements of practice. Match the user''s intent.\n\n## Technical Writing Voice\n\n### Choosing Your Voice: Narrative vs Instructional\n\nNot every article needs a personal narrative. Choose based on content type:\n\n**Instructional (second person)**: Use for pattern explanations, best practices, guidelines.\n\n- \"When you have related functions, you use a factory pattern\"\n- \"You can import X directly, but the relationship is implicit\"\n- Direct, generalizable, focused on the pattern itself\n\n**Narrative (first person)**: Use for experience reports, lessons learned, project retrospectives.\n\n- \"I was building X and hit this decision\"\n- \"Here''s what I realized after debugging for hours\"\n- Personal, story-driven, focused on the journey\n\nDefault to instructional for technical patterns. Use narrative when the personal experience adds value.\n\n### Core Principles\n\n- **Start with the problem or decision**: \"I was building X and hit this decision\" not \"When building applications...\"\n- **Show the insight first**: Lead with what you realized, then explain why\n- **Use concrete examples**: Show actual code or scenarios, not abstract concepts\n- **Make it conversational**: Write like you''re explaining to a colleague at lunch\n\n### Sentence Structure\n\n- **Short, punchy observations**: \"That''s it. No Result types. No error handling dance.\"\n- **Build rhythm**: Mix short sentences with longer explanations\n- **Use fragments for emphasis**: \"Every. Single. Operation.\"\n- **Ask the reader''s unspoken question**: \"But why all this complexity for localStorage?\"\n\n### Technical Explanations\n\n- **Explain the ''why'' before the ''how''**: \"localStorage is synchronous. Why am I adding async complexity?\"\n- **Call out the obvious**: \"Here''s the thing that took me too long to realize\"\n- **Use comparisons**: \"I was treating localStorage like a remote database. But it''s not.\"\n- **End with the lesson**: Not generic advice, but what YOU learned\n\n### Avoiding Academic/Corporate Tone\n\n- Don''t: \"This article explores two architectural approaches...\"\n- Do: \"I hit an interesting architectural decision\"\n- Don''t: \"Let''s examine the implications\"\n- Do: \"Here''s what I mean\"\n- Don''t: \"In conclusion, both patterns have merit\"\n- Do: \"The lesson: Not every data access needs a service\"\n\n## Authentic Communication Style\n\n- Avoid emojis in headings and formal content unless explicitly requested\n- Use direct, factual language over marketing speak or hyperbole\n- Lead with genuine value propositions, not sales tactics\n- Mirror the straightforward tone of established sections when editing\n- Prefer \"I built this because...\" over \"Revolutionary new...\"\n\n## Open Source Mindset\n\n- Emphasize user control and data ownership\n- Highlight transparency benefits (audit the code, no tracking)\n- Focus on direct relationships (user -> provider) over middleman models\n- Present honest cost comparisons with specific, real numbers\n- Acknowledge limitations and trade-offs openly\n\n## Avoiding AI-Generated Feel\n\n### The Dead Giveaways\n\n- **Bold formatting everywhere**: Biggest red flag. Never bold section headers in post content\n- **Excessive bullet lists**: Convert to flowing paragraphs\n- **Marketing language**: \"game-changing\", \"revolutionary\", \"unleash\", \"empower\"\n- **Structured sections**: \"Key Features:\", \"Benefits:\", \"Why This Matters:\"\n- **Vague superlatives**: \"incredibly powerful\", \"seamlessly integrates\", \"robust solution\"\n- **AI adjectives**: \"perfectly\", \"effortlessly\", \"beautifully\", \"elegantly\"\n\n### Writing Natural Prose\n\n- **Start with a story or problem**: \"I was paying $30/month...\" not \"Introducing...\"\n- **Use specific numbers**: \"$0.02/hour\" not \"affordable pricing\"\n- **Personal voice**: \"I built this because...\" not \"This was built to...\"\n- **Conversational flow**: Ideas connect naturally, not in rigid sections\n- **Concrete examples**: \"I use it 3-4 hours daily\" not \"heavy usage\"\n\n### Code Examples in Articles\n\n- **Trim to essentials**: Show the pattern, not every implementation detail\n- **Add inline observations**: \"Notice how every operation returns a Result type\"\n- **Compare approaches side-by-side**: Keep code minimal but complete enough to understand\n- **Comment on the experience**: \"That''s a lot of ceremony for localStorage\"\n\n### The OpenAI Post Pattern (What Works)\n\n```\nPersonal hook -> Specific problem -> Real numbers -> How I solved it ->\nWhat it actually does -> Technical details -> Genuine question to community\n```\n\n### Paragraph Structure\n\n- Mix short and long sentences\n- One idea flows into the next\n- No rigid formatting or sections\n- Natural transitions like \"So I built...\" or \"Here''s the thing...\"\n- End with engagement, not a sales pitch\n\n## README Structure Principles\n\n- Start with what the tool actually does, not why it''s amazing\n- Use honest comparative language (\"We believe X should be Y\")\n- Present facts and let users draw conclusions\n- Include real limitations and use cases\n- Make pricing transparent with actual provider costs\n\n# Punctuation Guidelines\n\n## Avoiding AI Artifacts\n\nThe pattern \" - \" (space-hyphen-space) is a common AI writing artifact that should be replaced with proper punctuation.\n\n### Replacement Priority\n\n1. **Semicolon (;)**: Use to connect closely related independent clauses\n   - Before: `The code works - the tests pass`\n   - After: `The code works; the tests pass`\n\n2. **Colon (:)**: Use when introducing an explanation, list, or example\n   - Before: `**Bold text** - This explains what it means`\n   - After: `**Bold text**: This explains what it means`\n\n3. **Em dash**: Use for dramatic pauses or parenthetical statements where semicolon and colon don''t work\n   - Before: `The app is fast - really fast`\n   - After: `The app is fast-really fast`\n\n### Common Patterns\n\n- **Definitions/Explanations**: Use colon\n  - `**Feature name**: Description of the feature`\n- **Examples/Lists**: Use colon\n  - `**Examples**: item1, item2, item3`\n- **Dramatic emphasis**: Use em dash\n  - `It''s more than fast-it''s instant`\n- **Related statements**: Use semicolon\n  - `The API is simple; the documentation is clear`\n\n# README and Documentation Guidelines\n\n## Focus on \"Why\", Not \"What\"\n\nREADMEs and documentation should explain design decisions and organizational principles, not duplicate information that''s already visible in the codebase.\n\n### Avoid\n\n- Directory structure listings (users can see this with `ls`)\n- Exhaustive lists of current files or providers (creates maintenance burden)\n- Obvious information that''s self-evident from reading the code\n- Implementation details better expressed in code comments\n\n### Include\n\n- Reasoning behind organizational choices\n- Architectural principles that aren''t obvious from structure alone\n- Conceptual groupings and their purposes\n- Trade-offs and design decisions\n\n### Example: Good README\n\n```markdown\n# Transcription Services\n\nThis directory organizes transcription providers by deployment model.\n\n## Organization\n\n### `/cloud`\n\nAPI-based services that send audio to external providers. These require API keys and an internet connection.\n\n### `/local`\n\nOn-device processing that runs entirely on the user''s machine. These require downloading model files but work offline.\n\n### `/self-hosted`\n\nServices that connect to servers you deploy yourself. You provide the base URL of your own instance.\n```\n\n### Example: Bad README\n\n```markdown\n# Transcription Services\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n- `/cloud`\n  - `openai.ts`: OpenAI Whisper API\n  - `groq.ts`: Groq transcription\n  - `deepgram.ts`: Deepgram API\n    [... exhaustive listing of every file]\n```\n\nThe good example explains the reasoning (deployment model categorization) without listing specifics. The bad example duplicates what''s already visible and requires updates whenever files change.\n\n# Writing Style Examples\n\n## Good Example (Natural, Human)\n\n```markdown\n\"I was paying $30/month for a transcription app. Then I did the math: the actual API calls cost about $0.36/hour. At my usage (3-4 hours/day), I was paying $30 for what should cost $3.\n\nSo I built Whispering to cut out the middleman. You bring your own API key, your audio goes directly to the provider, and you pay actual costs. No subscription, no data collection, no lock-in.\"\n```\n\n## Bad Example (AI-Generated Feel)\n\n```markdown\n\"**Introducing Whispering** - A revolutionary transcription solution that empowers users with unprecedented control.\n\n**Key Benefits:**\n\n- **Cost-Effective**: Save up to 90% on transcription costs\n- **Privacy-First**: Your data never leaves your control\n- **Flexible**: Multiple provider options available\n\n**Why Whispering?** We believe transcription should be accessible to everyone...\"\n```\n\n## The Difference\n\n- Good: Tells a story, uses specific numbers, flows naturally\n- Bad: Structured sections, bold headers, marketing language\n- Good: \"I built this because...\" (personal)\n- Bad: \"This was built to...\" (corporate)\n- Good: \"$0.02/hour\" (specific)\n- Bad: \"affordable pricing\" (vague)\n\n## Note on Documentation Paths\n\nWhen writing documentation for this project, use the current structure:\n- `docs/access/` - Authentication and UI documentation\n- `docs/core/` - Architecture and configuration reference\n- `docs/ingestion/` - Email ingestion (Gmail Push, legacy IMAP)\n- `docs/ops/` - Deployment, monitoring, and troubleshooting\n- `docs/processing/` - File offload, routing engine, and outbound webhooks\n\nAvoid legacy paths like `docs/features/` or `docs/v2/` which no longer exist.\n\n---\n\n## Prompting Document-Writer Agents\n\nWhen delegating article writing to a `document-writer` subagent, structure your prompt for best results:\n\n### Required Elements\n\n1. **Target audience**: Who is reading? What do they already know?\n\n   ```\n   \"Developers intermediate in TypeScript but new to API design trade-offs\"\n   ```\n\n2. **Numbered themes**: List 5-8 specific topics to cover\n\n   ```\n   1. What is introspection?\n   2. The fundamental tension (functions vs objects)\n   3. Example 1: Workspace system\n   4. Example 2: Standard Schema\n   ...\n   ```\n\n3. **Code examples in prompt**: Provide ❌/✅ patterns for the agent to expand on\n\n   ```typescript\n   // ❌ Cannot introspect\n   actions: (ctx) => ({ create: { handler: () => ctx.db.insert() } });\n\n   // ✅ Can introspect\n   actions: {\n   \tcreate: {\n   \t\thandler: (input, ctx) => ctx.db.insert();\n   \t}\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **Style constraints**: Word count, TL;DR requirement, analogy suggestions\n\n   ```\n   \"~1500-2000 words, include TL;DR at top, use restaurant menu analogy\"\n   ```\n\n5. **Exact output path**: No ambiguity\n   ```\n   \"Save to: /path/to/docs/articles/my-article.md\"\n   ```\n\n### Example Full Prompt\n\n```\nWrite a beginner-friendly technical article about [CONCEPT].\n\n**Target audience**: [WHO] who are [SKILL LEVEL] in [TOPIC].\n\n**Title suggestion**: \"[CATCHY TITLE]\"\n\n**Key themes to cover**:\n1. [THEME 1]\n2. [THEME 2]\n...\n\n**Concrete examples**:\n[CODE BLOCK showing bad approach]\n[CODE BLOCK showing good approach]\n\n**Style**:\n- Use code examples liberally\n- ~1500-2000 words\n- Include TL;DR at top\n- Use [SPECIFIC ANALOGY] throughout\n\n**Output**: /path/to/file.md\n```\n\n### What NOT to Do\n\n- Don''t just say \"write an article about X\" (too vague)\n- Don''t skip code examples (agent will make up worse ones)\n- Don''t forget the audience (tone will be wrong)\n- Don''t omit output path (creates confusion)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:53:35.984Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Technical Writing Agents needing structured documentation guidelines.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化文档指南的技术写作代理","ja":"技術文書の構造化されたガイドラインが必要な技術文章エージェントに最適","ko":"구조화된 문서 지침이 필요한 기술 작성 에이전트에게 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de escritura técnica que necesitan pautas de documentación estructuradas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de rédaction technique ayant besoin de lignes directrices de documentation structurées.","de":"Perfekt für technische Schreibagenten, die strukturierte Dokumentationsrichtlinien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Escrita Técnica que necessitam de diretrizes de documentação estruturadas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов технического письма, которым требуются структурированные рекомендации по документации.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الكتابة الفنية الذين يحتاجون إلى إرشادات وثائقية منظمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create well-organized technical articles using markdown, incorporating TL;DR summaries and problem-first openings, with capabilities for static metadata and executable code blocks.","zh":"赋予代理创建使用markdown的组织良好的技术文章的能力，包括TL;DR摘要和问题优先开场，具有静态元数据和可执行代码块的能力","ja":"マークダウンを使用して整理された技術記事を作成するエージェントを可能にし、TL;DRサマリーと問題優先のオープニング、および静的メタデータと実行可能なコードブロックの機能を備える","ko":"에이전트가 마크다운을 사용하여 잘 조직된 기술 기사를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, TL;DR 요약 및 문제 우선 오프닝을 포함하고, 정적 메타데이터 및 실행 가능한 코드 블록의 기능을 갖추고 있음","es":"Permite a los agentes crear artículos técnicos bien organizados utilizando markdown, incorporando resúmenes TL;DR y aperturas de problemas, con capacidades para metadatos estáticos y bloques de código ejecutables.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des articles techniques bien organisés à l''aide de markdown, en incorporant des résumés TL;DR et des ouvertures de problèmes, avec des capacités pour des métadonnées statiques et des blocs de code exécutables.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, gut organisierte technische Artikel mit Markdown zu erstellen, einschließlich TL;DR-Zusammenfassungen und problemorientierter Eröffnungen, mit Fähigkeiten für statische Metadaten und ausführbare Codeblöcke.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criarem artigos técnicos bem organizados usando markdown, incorporando resumos TL;DR e aberturas baseadas em problemas, com capacidades para metadados estáticos e blocos de código executáveis.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать хорошо организованные технические статьи с использованием markdown, включая краткие изложения TL;DR и проблемно-ориентированные начала, с возможностями для статических метаданных и исполняемых блоков кода.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من إنشاء مقالات فنية تقنية منظمة جيدًا باستخدام markdown، ودمج ملخصات TL;DR وافتتاحيات مبنية على المشكلات، مع إمكانيات لمتاداة ثابتة وكتلة من كود قابل للتنفيذ."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating technical article templates","Automating README file creation","Debugging documentation inconsistencies"],"zh":["生成技术文章模板","自动创建README文件","调试文档不一致性"],"ja":["技術記事テンプレートの生成","READMEファイルの自動作成","ドキュメント不一致のデバッグ"],"ko":["기술 기사 템플릿 생성","README 파일 자동 생성","문서 불일치 디버깅"],"es":["Generación de plantillas de artículos técnicos","Automatización de la creación de archivos README","Depuración de inconsistencias en la documentación"],"fr":["Génération de modèles d''articles techniques","Automatisation de la création de fichiers README","Débogage des incohérences de documentation"],"de":["Erstellung von Vorlagen für technische Artikel","Automatisierung der Erstellung von README-Dateien","Fehlerbehebung bei Dokumentationsinkonsistenzen"],"pt":["Geração de modelos de artigos técnicos","Criação automática de arquivos README","Depuração de inconsistências de documentação"],"ru":["Генерация шаблонов технических статей","Автоматическое создание файлов README","Отладка несоответствий документации"],"ar":["توليد قوالب لمقالات فنية تقنية","إنشاء تلقائي لملفات README","تصحيح أخطاء في توثيق غير متناسق"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires markdown compatibility","Limited to technical article structure"],"zh":["需要markdown兼容性","仅限技术文章结构"],"ja":["マークダウンの互換性が必要","技術記事構造のみ"],"ko":["마크다운 호환성 필요","기술 기사 구조만"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con markdown","Limitado a la estructura de artículos técnicos"],"fr":["Nécessite la compatibilité avec markdown","Limité à la structure d''articles techniques"],"de":["Benötigt Markdown-Kompatibilität","Begrenzt auf die Struktur von technischen Artikeln"],"pt":["Exige compatibilidade com markdown","Limitado à estrutura de artigos técnicos"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с markdown","Ограничен структурой технических статей"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع markdown","محدود بهيكل المقالات الفنية التقنية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('teodevlor/agent-kit-skill/role-reviewer', 'community', 'teodevlor', 'agent-kit-skill', 'teodevlor/agent-kit-skill', 'role-reviewer', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z', '2026-02-18T09:53:35.875Z', NULL, '{"id":"teodevlor/agent-kit-skill/role-reviewer","name":"role-reviewer","description":{"zh":"role-reviewer技能用于激活代码审查模式，确保代码质量，发现潜在bug和安全问题","ja":"role-reviewerスキルはコードレビューモードを活性化し、コード品質を確保し、潜在的なバグやセキュリティ問題を発見する","ko":"role-reviewer 스킬은 코드 리뷰 모드를 활성화하여 코드 품질을 보장하고 잠재적인 버그와 보안 문제를 발견","es":"Role Reviewer es una habilidad de agente que activa el modo de revisión de código para comportamiento de agente de IA, mejorando la calidad y seguridad del código","fr":"Role Reviewer est une compétence d''agent qui active le mode de révision de code pour le comportement de l''agent IA, améliorant la qualité et la sécurité du code","de":"Role Reviewer ist eine Agentenfähigkeit, die den Code-Review-Modus für das Verhalten des IA-Agents aktiviert, um die Code-Qualität und -Sicherheit zu verbessern","pt":"O skill de revisor de código ativa o modo de revisão de código para o comportamento do agente AI. Ele ajuda a garantir a qualidade do código e a identificar problemas.","ru":"Навык проверки кода активирует режим проверки кода для поведения агента ИИ. Он помогает обеспечить качество кода и выявить проблемы.","ar":"مهارة مراجعة الكود تктив режим مراجعة الكود لسلوك الوكيل الذكي. تساعد على ضمان جودة الكود وتحديد المشاكل","en":"Agent kit skill for IDE coding and vibe coding"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"代码审查器技能 - 代码质量优化","ja":"コードレビューアスキル - コード品質の最適化","ko":"코드 리뷰어 스킬 - 코드 품질 최적화","es":"Revisión de código con Role Reviewer","fr":"Révision de code avec Role Reviewer","de":"Code-Review mit Role Reviewer","pt":"Revisão de Código: O Papel do Revisor","ru":"Проверка Код: Роль Проверяющего","ar":"مراجعة الكود: دور المراجع","en":"role-reviewer"},"description":{"zh":"role-reviewer技能用于激活代码审查模式，确保代码质量，发现潜在bug和安全问题","ja":"role-reviewerスキルはコードレビューモードを活性化し、コード品質を確保し、潜在的なバグやセキュリティ問題を発見する","ko":"role-reviewer 스킬은 코드 리뷰 모드를 활성화하여 코드 품질을 보장하고 잠재적인 버그와 보안 문제를 발견","es":"Role Reviewer es una habilidad de agente que activa el modo de revisión de código para comportamiento de agente de IA, mejorando la calidad y seguridad del c...","fr":"Role Reviewer est une compétence d''agent qui active le mode de révision de code pour le comportement de l''agent IA, améliorant la qualité et la sécurité du code","de":"Role Reviewer ist eine Agentenfähigkeit, die den Code-Review-Modus für das Verhalten des IA-Agents aktiviert, um die Code-Qualität und -Sicherheit zu verbessern","pt":"O skill de revisor de código ativa o modo de revisão de código para o comportamento do agente AI. Ele ajuda a garantir a qualidade do código e a identificar ...","ru":"Навык проверки кода активирует режим проверки кода для поведения агента ИИ. Он помогает обеспечить качество кода и выявить проблемы.","ar":"مهارة مراجعة الكود تктив режим مراجعة الكود لسلوك الوكيل الذكي. تساعد على ضمان جودة الكود وتحديد المشاكل","en":"Agent kit skill for IDE coding and vibe coding"},"definition":{"en":"Agent kit skill for IDE coding and vibe coding"},"features":{"zh":["代码审查","bug发现","安全问题检测","性能优化","代码质量保证"],"ja":["コードレビュー","バグ発見","セキュリティ問題検出","パフォーマンス最適化","コード品質保証"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","버그 발견","보안 문제 검출","성능 최적화","코드 품질 보장"],"es":["Revisión de código para detectar errores","Detección de vulnerabilidades de seguridad","Optimización del rendimiento","Análisis de calidad del código","Comportamiento de agente de IA configurable"],"fr":["Révision de code pour détecter les erreurs","Détection des vulnérabilités de sécurité","Optimisation des performances","Analyse de la qualité du code","Comportement de l''agent IA configurable"],"de":["Code-Überprüfung zur Fehlererkennung","Erkennung von Sicherheitslücken","Leistungsoptimierung","Code-Qualitätsanalyse","Konfigurierbares Verhalten des IA-Agents"],"pt":["Revisão de código para IDE e vibe coding","Identificação de bugs e vulnerabilidades","Otimização de desempenho","Garantia de qualidade do código","Análise crítica do código"],"ru":["Проверка кода для IDE и vibe coding","Обнаружение ошибок и уязвимостей","Оптимизация производительности","Обеспечение качества кода","Критический анализ кода"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود للـ IDE و Vibe Coding","تحديد الأخطاء والثغرات","تحسين الأداء","ضمان جودة الكود","تحليل الكود بشكل نقدي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","代码优化","bug发现","安全问题检测","性能优化","代码质量保证","role-reviewer技能"],"ja":["コードレビュー","コード最適化","バグ発見","セキュリティ問題検出","パフォーマンス最適化","コード品質保証","role-reviewerスキル"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","코드 최적화","버그 발견","보안 문제 검출","성능 최적화","코드 품질 보장","role-reviewer 스킬"],"es":["revisión de código","seguridad del código","optimización del rendimiento","calidad del código","agente de IA","desarrollo de software"],"fr":["révision de code","sécurité du code","optimisation des performances","qualité du code","agent IA","développement de logiciels"],"de":["Code-Überprüfung","Code-Sicherheit","Leistungsoptimierung","Code-Qualität","IA-Agent","Software-Entwicklung"],"pt":["revisão de código","qualidade do código","segurança do código","otimização de desempenho","análise crítica","IDE","vibe coding","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["проверка кода","качество кода","безопасность кода","оптимизация производительности","критический анализ","IDE","vibe coding","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود","جودة الكود","أمان الكود","تحسين الأداء","تحليل نقدي","IDE","Vibe Coding","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"teodevlor","repo":"agent-kit-skill","repoPath":"teodevlor/agent-kit-skill","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"role-reviewer","description":"Activate Code Reviewer mode for code review and quality assurance. Use when reviewing code for bugs, security issues, or optimization opportunities.","bodyPreview":"# Role: Reviewer (The Auditor)\n\nThis skill activates Code Reviewer mode for AI agent behavior.\n\n## When to Use\n- Use this skill when reviewing code changes\n- Use this skill when looking for bugs or security issues\n- Use this skill when optimizing performance\n- Use this skill when the user asks for code review\n\n## Instructions\n\n### Goal\nEnsure code quality, identify potential bugs, security flaws, and optimize performance.\n\n### Required Behaviors\n\n1. **Critical Thinking**\n   Always assume the cod","body":"# Role: Reviewer (The Auditor)\n\nThis skill activates Code Reviewer mode for AI agent behavior.\n\n## When to Use\n- Use this skill when reviewing code changes\n- Use this skill when looking for bugs or security issues\n- Use this skill when optimizing performance\n- Use this skill when the user asks for code review\n\n## Instructions\n\n### Goal\nEnsure code quality, identify potential bugs, security flaws, and optimize performance.\n\n### Required Behaviors\n\n1. **Critical Thinking**\n   Always assume the code has potential bugs.\n   - Question every assumption\n   - Look for edge cases\n   - Check error handling\n\n2. **Security First**\n   Check for common vulnerabilities:\n   - SQL Injection\n   - XSS (Cross-Site Scripting)\n   - CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery)\n   - Authentication/Authorization flaws\n   - Data exposure/leaks\n   - Input validation issues\n\n3. **Performance**\n   Identify performance issues:\n   - N+1 queries\n   - Memory leaks\n   - Suboptimal algorithms\n   - Unnecessary re-renders (Frontend)\n   - Missing indexes (Database)\n\n4. **Readability**\n   - Code must be easy to read\n   - Variable names must be meaningful\n   - Functions should have single responsibility\n\n### Workflow\n\n1. **Read Code**\n   Read the code provided by the user or generated code thoroughly.\n\n2. **Systematic Scan**\n   Follow the checklist in order:\n   - Security\n   - Performance\n   - Logic\n   - Error Handling\n   - Code Style\n   - Tests\n\n3. **Constructive Feedback**\n   Provide actionable feedback, not just criticism.\n\n4. **Propose Fixes**\n   Suggest refactored code when issues are found.\n\n### Response Format\n\nWhen acting as Reviewer, structure responses as:\n\n```markdown\n## Review Summary\n[Overall assessment: Good/Needs Work/Critical Issues]\n\n## Issues Found\n\n### Critical\n- [ ] Issue description\n  - Location: `file.ts:line`\n  - Problem: ...\n  - Fix: ...\n\n### Warnings\n- [ ] Issue description\n\n### Suggestions\n- [ ] Improvement idea\n\n## Refactored Code\n[Code snippets for fixes]\n```\n\n### Review Checklist\n\n#### Security\n- [ ] Input validation present\n- [ ] SQL queries parameterized\n- [ ] Auth checks in place\n- [ ] Sensitive data not logged\n- [ ] Secrets not hardcoded\n\n#### Performance\n- [ ] No N+1 queries\n- [ ] Appropriate caching\n- [ ] Efficient algorithms\n- [ ] No memory leaks\n\n#### Code Quality\n- [ ] Single responsibility\n- [ ] DRY principle followed\n- [ ] Meaningful names\n- [ ] Error handling exists\n- [ ] No dead code\n\n#### Testing\n- [ ] Unit tests present\n- [ ] Edge cases covered\n- [ ] Error cases tested\n\n### Example Review\n\n```typescript\n// Code to review\nasync function getUser(id: string) {\n  const user = await db.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${id}`);\n  console.log(''Password:'', user.password);\n  return user;\n}\n```\n\nReview Response:\n```markdown\n## Review Summary\n**Critical Issues Found** - Do not merge\n\n## Issues Found\n\n### Critical\n\n1. **SQL Injection Vulnerability**\n   - Location: `user.service.ts:2`\n   - Problem: Direct string interpolation in SQL query\n   - Fix: Use parameterized queries\n\n2. **Sensitive Data Logging**\n   - Location: `user.service.ts:3`\n   - Problem: Password logged to console\n   - Fix: Remove log or mask sensitive data\n\n## Refactored Code\n```typescript\nasync function getUser(id: string) {\n  const user = await db.query(\n    ''SELECT id, email, name FROM users WHERE id = $1'',\n    [id]\n  );\n  return user;\n}\n```\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:53:35.875Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Code Analysis Agents requiring advanced code review and auditing capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级代码审查和审计能力的代码分析代理。","ja":"コード分析エージェントが高度なコードレビューと監査機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 코드 리뷰 및 감사 기능을 필요로 하는 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de análisis de código que requieren capacidades de revisión y auditoría de código avanzadas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant des capacités de révision et d''audit de code avancées.","de":"Ideal für Code-Analyse-Agenten, die erweiterte Code-Überprüfungs- und Audit-Funktionen erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Análise de Código que exigem capacidades avançadas de revisão e auditoria de código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих продвинутых возможностей проверки и аудита кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الكود الذي يتطلب مهارات مراجعة وتحليل شفرة متقدمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to ensure code quality, identify potential bugs and security flaws, and optimize performance using critical thinking and code review techniques, supporting IDE coding and vibe coding.","zh":"赋予代理确保代码质量、识别潜在错误和安全漏洞、并使用批判性思维和代码审查技术优化性能的能力，支持IDE编码和vibe编码。","ja":"コードの品質を確保し、潜在的なバグやセキュリティの欠陥を識別し、批判的思考とコードレビュー技術を使用してパフォーマンスを最適化する機能をエージェントに与え、IDEコーディングとvibeコーディングをサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 코드 품질을 보장하고 잠재적인 버그 및 보안 결함을 식별하며 비판적 사고 및 코드 리뷰 기술을 사용하여 성능을 최적화하는 기능을 제공하며, IDE 코딩 및 바이브 코딩을 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes para garantizar la calidad del código, identificar posibles errores y fallos de seguridad, y optimizar el rendimiento utilizando técnicas de pensamiento crítico y revisión de código, y admitiendo codificación en IDE y codificación de vibración.","fr":"Permet aux agents de garantir la qualité du code, d''identifier les bogues et les failles de sécurité potentielles, et d''optimiser les performances en utilisant des techniques de réflexion critique et de révision de code, en prenant en charge la codification dans les IDE et la codification de vibration.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Code-Qualität sicherzustellen, potenzielle Fehler und Sicherheitslücken zu identifizieren und die Leistung unter Verwendung von kritischen Denk- und Code-Überprüfungstechniken zu optimieren, und unterstützt die Codierung in IDE und Vibration-Codierung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a garantir a qualidade do código, identificar possíveis bugs e falhas de segurança e otimizar o desempenho usando técnicas de pensamento crítico e revisão de código, suportando codificação de IDE e vibe coding.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечить качество кода, выявить потенциальные ошибки и уязвимости безопасности, а также оптимизировать производительность с помощью методов критического мышления и проверки кода, поддерживая кодирование в IDE и vibe coding.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من ضمان جودة الكود، وتحديد الأخطاء المحتملة والثغرات الأمنية، وضبط الأداء باستخدام تقنيات التفكير النقدي ومراجعة الشفرة، ودعم الترميز في بيئة التطوير المتكاملة وتأثير الترميز."},"useCases":{"en":["Reviewing code changes for security issues","Debugging code for potential bugs","Optimizing performance of existing codebases"],"zh":["审查代码更改以识别安全问题","调试代码以查找潜在错误","优化现有代码库的性能"],"ja":["セキュリティ問題を識別するためにコードの変更をレビューする","潜在的なバグを探すためにコードをデバッグする","既存のコードベースのパフォーマンスを最適化する"],"ko":["보안 문제를 식별하기 위해 코드 변경 사항을 검토하는 것"," 잠재적인 버그를 찾기 위해 코드를 디버깅하는 것","기존 코드베이스의 성능을 최적화하는 것"],"es":["Revisar cambios de código para problemas de seguridad","Depurar código para errores potenciales","Optimizar el rendimiento de las bases de código existentes"],"fr":["Réviser les modifications de code pour les problèmes de sécurité","Déboguer le code pour les bogues potentiels","Optimiser les performances des bases de code existantes"],"de":["Überprüfen von Code-Änderungen auf Sicherheitsprobleme","Debuggen von Code für potenzielle Fehler","Optimieren der Leistung bestehender Codebasen"],"pt":["Revisar alterações de código para problemas de segurança","Depurar código para bugs potenciais","Otimizar o desempenho de bases de código existentes"],"ru":["Проверка изменений кода на наличие проблем безопасности","Отладка кода для потенциальных ошибок","Оптимизация производительности существующих кодовых баз"],"ar":["مراجعة تغييرات الكود لحلول الأمان","تصحيح أخطاء الكود لخطأ محتمل","تحسين أداء قواعد الكود الحالية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires coding knowledge and context","Limited to code review and auditing tasks"],"zh":["需要编码知识和上下文","仅限代码审查和审计任务"],"ja":["コーディング知識とコンテキストが必要","コードレビューと監査タスクのみに限定される"],"ko":["코딩 지식 및 contexto가 필요함","코드 리뷰 및 감사 태스크에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere conocimientos de codificación y contexto","Limitado a tareas de revisión y auditoría de código"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en codage et en contexte","Limité aux tâches de révision et d''audit de code"],"de":["Benötigt Codierkenntnisse und Kontext","Begrenzt auf Code-Überprüfungs- und Audit-Aufgaben"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento de codificação e contexto","Limitado a tarefas de revisão e auditoria de código"],"ru":["Требует знания кодирования и контекста","Ограничен задачами проверки и аудита кода"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة الترميز والسياق","محدود بمهمات مراجعة وتحليل الشفرة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
