ير","en":"slabbed-ceiling-support"},"description":{"zh":"slabbed-ceiling-support技能允许需要天井附着的块在顶部板和双板下放置和生存","ja":"スラブ式天井サポートの機能により、天井附着が必要なブロックを上部スラブとダブルスラブの下に配置して生存できます","ko":"슬래브식 천장 지원 기술을 통해 천장 부착이 필요한 블록을 상단 슬래브와 더블 슬래브 아래에 배치하고 생存할 수 있습니다","es":"El skill slabbed-ceiling-support permite a los bloques que requieren sujeción al techo colocarse y sobrevivir bajo losas y dobles losas.","fr":"Le skill slabbed-ceiling-support permet aux blocs nécessitant un attachement au plafond de être placés et de survivre sous les dalles et doubles dalles.","de":"Der Skill slabbed-ceiling-support ermöglicht es Blöcken, die eine Deckenbefestigung erfordern, unter Slabs und Doppelslabs platziert und überleben zu können.","pt":"O suporte de teto para lajes permite que blocos sejam colocados e sobrevivam sob lajes duplas. Isso é possível graças à implementação de mixins que verificam...","ru":"Поддержка потолка для плит позволяет размещать и сохранять блоки под двойными плитами. Это стало возможным благодаря реализации миксинов, проверяющих твердос...","ar":"دعم السقف للبلاط يسمح بوضع الكتل ونجاتها تحت البلاط المزدوج. هذا يتم بفضل تنفيذ الخلطات التي تحقق من صلابة جوانب البلاط","en":"Put things on slabs!"},"definition":{"en":"Put things on slabs!"},"features":{"zh":["允许需要天井附着的块在顶部板和双板下放置","支持不同类型的侧面形状","实现块在顶部板和双板下的生存","无需额外的mixin","使用SlabSupportStateMixin和SlabSupportBlockMixin","提高游戏体验"],"ja":["天井附着が必要なブロックを上部スラブとダブルスラブの下に配置","様々な側面形状をサポート","上部スラブとダブルスラブの下でのブロックの生存","追加のmixin不要","SlabSupportStateMixinとSlabSupportBlockMixinを使用","ゲーム体験の向上"],"ko":["천장 부착이 필요한 블록을 상단 슬래브와 더블 슬래브 아래에 배치","다양한 측면 형상을 지원","상단 슬래브와 더블 슬래브 아래에서의 블록 생存","추가 mixin 불필요","SlabSupportStateMixin과 SlabSupportBlockMixin 사용","게임 경험 향상"],"es":["Permite a los bloques que requieren sujeción al techo colocarse en losas y dobles losas","Funciona sin mixins adicionales","Soporta todos los tipos de formas de losas","Permite la colocación de cadenas, letreros colgantes y lámparas","Mejora la estabilidad de los bloques en losas y dobles losas"],"fr":["Permet aux blocs nécessitant un attachement au plafond d''être placés sur les dalles et doubles dalles","Fonctionne sans mixins supplémentaires","Prend en charge tous les types de formes de dalles","Permet la pose de chaînes, de panneaux suspendus et de lanternes","Améliore la stabilité des blocs sur les dalles et doubles dalles"],"de":["Ermöglicht es Blöcken, die eine Deckenbefestigung erfordern, auf Slabs und Doppelslabs platziert zu werden","Funktioniert ohne zusätzliche Mixins","Unterstützt alle Arten von Slab-Formen","Ermöglicht die Platzierung von Ketten, hängenden Schildern und Laternen","Verbessert die Stabilität von Blöcken auf Slabs und Doppelslabs"],"pt":["Permite que blocos sejam colocados sob lajes duplas","Verifica a solidez das laterais das lajes","Implementação de mixins para suporte de teto","Compatibilidade com diferentes tipos de lajes","Suporte a blocos que requerem fixação no teto"],"ru":["Позволяет размещать блоки под двойными плитами","Проверяет твердость сторон плит","Реализация миксинов для поддержки потолка","Совместимость с разными типами плит","Поддержка блоков, требующих крепления к потолку"],"ar":["يسمح بوضع الكتل تحت البلاط المزدوج","يتحقق من صلابة جوانب البلاط","تنفيذ الخلطات لدعم السقف","التوافق مع أنواع مختلفة من البلاط","دعم الكتل التي تتطلب تثبيتًا في السقف"]},"keywords":{"zh":["slabbed-ceiling-support","minecraft","游戏开发","天井附着","块放置","生存机制","SlabSupportStateMixin","SlabSupportBlockMixin"],"ja":["スラブ式天井サポート","minecraft","ゲーム開発","天井附着","ブロック配置","生存メカニズム","SlabSupportStateMixin","SlabSupportBlockMixin"],"ko":["슬래브식 천장 지원","minecraft","게임 개발","천장 부착","블록 배치","생존 메커니즘","SlabSupportStateMixin","SlabSupportBlockMixin"],"es":["soporte de techo para losas","slabbed-ceiling-support","bloques que requieren sujeción al techo","losas y dobles losas","mixins","estabilidad de bloques","desarrollo de juegos","programación de juegos"],"fr":["support de plafond pour dalles","slabbed-ceiling-support","blocs nécessitant un attachement au plafond","dalles et doubles dalles","mixins","stabilité des blocs","développement de jeux","programmation de jeux"],"de":["Deckenstütze für Slabs","slabbed-ceiling-support","Blöcke die eine Deckenbefestigung erfordern","Slabs und Doppelslabs","Mixins","Stabilität von Blöcken","Spieleentwicklung","Spieleprogrammierung"],"pt":["suporte de teto para lajes","desenvolvimento de jogos","blocos de jogo","lajes duplas","mixins de suporte de teto","desenvolvimento de minecraft"],"ru":["поддержка потолка для плит","разработка игр","блоки игры","двойные плиты","миксины поддержки потолка","разработка майнкрафта"],"ar":["دعم السقف للبلاط","تطوير الألعاب","كتل اللعبة","البلاط المزدوج","خلطات دعم السقف","تطوير ماين كرافت"]}},"owner":"joolbits","repo":"slabbed","repoPath":"joolbits/slabbed","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"slabbed-ceiling-support","description":"Add hanging/ceiling attachment support for blocks under top slabs, using SlabSupport.isCeilingSupportSurface as the single source of truth.","bodyPreview":"# Slabbed — Skill: Ceiling Support\n\n## Goal\nAllow blocks that require ceiling attachment (chains, hanging signs, lanterns) to place on and survive under top slabs and double slabs.\n\n## Key finding (2026-02-07)\nAnalysis showed that ceiling support **already works** without additional mixins:\n- `SlabSupportStateMixin.isSideSolid` returns true for `Direction.DOWN` on top slabs (all `SideShapeType` variants)\n- `SlabSupportBlockMixin.sideCoversSmallSquare` returns true for `Direction.DOWN` on top sla","body":"# Slabbed — Skill: Ceiling Support\n\n## Goal\nAllow blocks that require ceiling attachment (chains, hanging signs, lanterns) to place on and survive under top slabs and double slabs.\n\n## Key finding (2026-02-07)\nAnalysis showed that ceiling support **already works** without additional mixins:\n- `SlabSupportStateMixin.isSideSolid` returns true for `Direction.DOWN` on top slabs (all `SideShapeType` variants)\n- `SlabSupportBlockMixin.sideCoversSmallSquare` returns true for `Direction.DOWN` on top slabs\n- Top slab collision shape `[0,0.5,0 → 1,1,1]` natively satisfies `isSideSolid(DOWN, CENTER)` via shape cache\n- `ChainBlock` has no `canPlaceAt` override — places anywhere\n- `HangingSignBlock.canPlaceAt` checks `isSideSolid(pos.up(), DOWN, CENTER)` — satisfied by top slabs natively\n- Lanterns use `sideCoversSmallSquare(DOWN)` — covered by `SlabSupportBlockMixin`\n\n## When to use this skill\nWhen adding ceiling-attachment support for a new block type under top slabs.\n\n## Hard stops\n- Ceiling support leaks to bottom slabs, stairs, fences, walls, or panes\n- Baseline full-block behavior changes\n- Build fails\n\n## Steps\n1. Test whether existing `isSideSolid` / `sideCoversSmallSquare` changes already enable placement\n2. If not: check what placement method the block uses (`isSideSolid`, `sideCoversSmallSquare`, or custom)\n3. If custom: add a narrow per-block mixin (`canPlaceAt` inject with early return) routing through `SlabSupport`\n4. Verify survival after neighbor updates (break and replace the slab above)\n5. Verify visual alignment (flush against slab bottom)\n6. Build gate\n7. Test matrix\n8. Commit + tag\n\n## Note on `isCeilingSupportSurface`\nA dedicated `SlabSupport.isCeilingSupportSurface(BlockView, BlockPos)` helper was planned but is NOT needed currently. The existing shared hooks cover all known ceiling-attachment blocks. Only add this helper if a future block requires a custom check that the shared hooks don''t cover.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:53:37.237Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Minecraft Modding Agents needing advanced block placement capabilities with ceiling support for top slabs and double slabs.","zh":"非常适合需要高级块放置功能的Minecraft模组代理，特别是支持天花板的顶部板和双板。","ja":"Minecraft Moddingエージェントが高級なブロック配置機能を必要とする場合、天井サポートを備えたトップスラブとダブルスラブに最適です。","ko":"고급 블록 배치 기능이 필요한 Minecraft 모드 에이전트에게 적합하며, 천장 지원을 갖춘 상단 슬래브와 이중 슬래브를 제공합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de modificación de Minecraft que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de colocación de bloques con soporte de techo para losas superiores y dobles.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de modification de Minecraft ayant besoin de capacités avancées de placement de blocs avec un support de plafond pour les dalles supérieures et les dalles doubles.","de":"Perfekt für Minecraft-Modding-Agents, die erweiterte Blockplatzierungsfunktionen mit Deckenunterstützung für oberen Slabs und Doppelslabs benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Modding de Minecraft que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de colocação de blocos com suporte ao teto para lajes superiores e lajes duplas.","ru":"Идеально для агентов моддинга Minecraft, которым требуются продвинутые возможности размещения блоков с поддержкой потолка для верхних плиток и двойных плиток.","ar":"مثالي لعميل إضافة Minecraft الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لوضع الكتلة مع دعم السقف للبلاط العلوي والبلاط المزدوج."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to place blocks requiring ceiling attachment, such as chains, hanging signs, and lanterns, utilizing SlabSupportStateMixin and SlabSupportBlockMixin with Direction.DOWN and SideShapeType variants.","zh":"赋予代理放置需要天花板附着的块，例如链条、悬挂标志和灯笼，利用SlabSupportStateMixin和SlabSupportBlockMixin，包括Direction.DOWN和SideShapeType变体。","ja":"エージェントに、チェーン、サイン、ランタンなどの天井への付着が必要なブロックを配置する能力を与え、SlabSupportStateMixinとSlabSupportBlockMixinを使用し、Direction.DOWNとSideShapeTypeのバリアントを利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 천장 부착이 필요한 블록을 배치할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. 체인, 간판, 등과 같은 블록을 SlabSupportStateMixin과 SlabSupportBlockMixin을 사용하여 배치하며, Direction.DOWN과 SideShapeType의 변형을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a colocar bloques que requieren sujeción al techo, como cadenas, letreros colgantes y lámparas, utilizando SlabSupportStateMixin y SlabSupportBlockMixin con variantes de Direction.DOWN y SideShapeType.","fr":"Permet aux agents de placer des blocs nécessitant une fixation au plafond, tels que des chaînes, des panneaux suspendus et des lanternes, en utilisant SlabSupportStateMixin et SlabSupportBlockMixin avec des variantes de Direction.DOWN et SideShapeType.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Blöcke zu platzieren, die eine Deckenbefestigung erfordern, wie Ketten, hängende Schilder und Laternen, unter Verwendung von SlabSupportStateMixin und SlabSupportBlockMixin mit Direction.DOWN- und SideShapeType-Varianten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a colocar blocos que exigem fixação no teto, como correntes, placas penduradas e lanternas, utilizando SlabSupportStateMixin e SlabSupportBlockMixin com variantes de Direction.DOWN e SideShapeType.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью размещать блоки, требующие крепления к потолку, такие как цепи, висящие знаки и фонари, используя SlabSupportStateMixin и SlabSupportBlockMixin с вариантами Direction.DOWN и SideShapeType.","ar":"يمكّن الوكيل من وضع الكتل التي تتطلب附ها إلى السقف ، مثل السلاسل واللوحات المعلقة والفوانيس ، باستخدام SlabSupportStateMixin و SlabSupportBlockMixin مع متغيرات Direction.DOWN و SideShapeType."},"useCases":{"en":["Placing hanging decorations under top slabs","Attaching chains to double slabs for complex structures","Surviving block placement under ceiling attachments without additional mixins"],"zh":["在顶部板下放置悬挂装饰","将链条附着到双板以创建复杂结构","在不使用额外混入的情况下在天花板附着下放置块"],"ja":["トップスラブの下にハングデコレーションを配置する","ダブルスラブにチェーンを付けて複雑な構造を作る","追加のミックスインを使用せずに天井の付着下でブロックを配置する"],"ko":["상단 슬래브 아래에 매달린 장식을 배치하는 것","이중 슬래브에 체인을 부착하여 복잡한 구조를 만드는 것","추가 mixin을 사용하지 않고 천장 부착 아래에서 블록을 배치하는 것"],"es":["Colocar decoraciones colgantes bajo losas superiores","Adjuntar cadenas a las losas dobles para estructuras complejas","Sobrevivir a la colocación de bloques bajo accesorios de techo sin mixins adicionales"],"fr":["Placer des décorations suspendues sous les dalles supérieures","Attacher des chaînes aux dalles doubles pour des structures complexes","Survivre au placement de blocs sous les accessoires de plafond sans mixins supplémentaires"],"de":["Hängende Dekorationen unter oberen Slabs platzieren","Ketten an Doppelslabs für komplexe Strukturen anhängen","Überleben der Blockplatzierung unter Deckenbefestigungen ohne zusätzliche Mixins"],"pt":["Colocação de decorações penduradas sob lajes superiores","Fixação de correntes em lajes duplas para estruturas complexas","Sobrevivência à colocação de blocos sob acessórios do teto sem mixins adicionais"],"ru":["Размещение висящих декоративных элементов под верхними плитками","Присоединение цепей к двойным плиткам для сложных конструкций","Выживание при размещении блоков под потолочными приспособлениями без дополнительных миксинов"],"ar":["وضع الزينة المعلقة تحت البلاط العلوي","تركيب السلاسل إلى البلاط المزدوج من أجل الهياكل المعقدة","البقاء على قيد الحياة عند وضع الكتل تحت ملحقات السقف دون مزيج إضافي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Minecraft modding environment","Limited to top slabs and double slabs","Dependent on SlabSupportStateMixin and SlabSupportBlockMixin functionality"],"zh":["需要Minecraft模组环境","仅限顶部板和双板","依赖于SlabSupportStateMixin和SlabSupportBlockMixin的功能"],"ja":["Minecraft Modding環境が必要","トップスラブとダブルスラブのみに制限される","SlabSupportStateMixinとSlabSupportBlockMixinの機能に依存する"],"ko":["Minecraft 모드 환경이 필요함","상단 슬래브와 이중 슬래브만으로 제한됨","SlabSupportStateMixin과 SlabSupportBlockMixin의 기능에 의존함"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de modificación de Minecraft","Limitado a losas superiores y dobles","Dependiente de la funcionalidad de SlabSupportStateMixin y SlabSupportBlockMixin"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement de modification de Minecraft","Limité aux dalles supérieures et doubles","Dépendant de la fonctionnalité de SlabSupportStateMixin et SlabSupportBlockMixin"],"de":["Benötigt eine Minecraft-Modding-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf oberen Slabs und Doppelslabs","Abhängig von der Funktionalität von SlabSupportStateMixin und SlabSupportBlockMixin"],"pt":["Exige ambiente de modding do Minecraft","Limitado a lajes superiores e lajes duplas","Dependente da funcionalidade do SlabSupportStateMixin e SlabSupportBlockMixin"],"ru":["Требует среды моддинга Minecraft","Ограничен верхними плитками и двойными плитками","Зависит от функциональности SlabSupportStateMixin и SlabSupportBlockMixin"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة إضافة Minecraft","محدود للبلاط العلوي والبلاط المزدوج","يعتمد على وظيفة SlabSupportStateMixin و SlabSupportBlockMixin"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":35}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('twj0/2026mcm/skill-creator', 'community', 'twj0', '2026mcm', 'twj0/2026mcm', 'skill-creator', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z', '2026-02-18T09:53:46.840Z', NULL, '{"id":"twj0/2026mcm/skill-creator","name":"skill-creator","description":{"zh":"技能创建器提供创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","ja":"スキルクリエイターは、開発者がClaudeの能力を拡張するための効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供します","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자가 Claude의 능력을 확장하기 위한 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"El Creador de Habilidades es un paquete modular que proporciona conocimientos especializados y flujos de trabajo para desarrolladores.","fr":"Le Créateur de Compétences est un paquet modulaire qui fournit des connaissances spécialisées et des flux de travail pour les développeurs.","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein modulares Paket, das spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Arbeitsabläufe für Entwickler bereitstellt.","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes, estendendo as capacidades do Claude com conhecimento especializado e fluxos de trabalho.","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков, расширяя возможности Claude с помощью специализированных знаний и рабочих процессов.","ar":"مبتكر المهارات يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة، توسع قدرات Claude مع المعرفة المتخصصة والتدفقات العملية.","en":"2026年美国大学生数学建模|C题|Dancing with the Stars|2026年美赛C题"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"技能创建器：开发者指南","ja":"スキルクリエイター：開発者向けガイド","ko":"스킬 생성기: 개발자 가이드","es":"Creador de Habilidades: Guía para Desarrolladores","fr":"Créateur de Compétences: Guide pour Développeurs","de":"Fähigkeits-Ersteller: Anleitung für Entwickler","pt":"Criador de Habilidades: Guia para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Создатель Навыков: Руководство для Разработчиков","ar":"مبتكر المهارات: دليل للمطورين","en":"skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"技能创建器提供创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","ja":"スキルクリエイターは、開発者がClaudeの能力を拡張するための効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供します","ko":"스킬 생성기는 개발자가 Claude의 능력을 확장하기 위한 효과적인 스킬을 생성하는 데 필요한 가이드를 제공합니다","es":"El Creador de Habilidades es un paquete modular que proporciona conocimientos especializados y flujos de trabajo para desarrolladores.","fr":"Le Créateur de Compétences est un paquet modulaire qui fournit des connaissances spécialisées et des flux de travail pour les développeurs.","de":"Der Fähigkeits-Ersteller ist ein modulares Paket, das spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Arbeitsabläufe für Entwickler bereitstellt.","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes, estendendo as capacidades do Claude com conhecimento especializado e fluxos de trabalho.","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков, расширяя возможности Claude с помощью специализированных знаний и рабочих проце...","ar":"مبتكر المهارات يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة، توسع قدرات Claude مع المعرفة المتخصصة والتدفقات العملية.","en":"2026年美国大学生数学建模|C题|Dancing with the Stars|2026年美赛C题"},"definition":{"en":"2026年美国大学生数学建模|C题|Dancing with the Stars|2026年美赛C题"},"features":{"zh":["提供创建有效技能的指南","帮助开发者扩展Claude的能力","支持多种工作流","提供专业知识和工具"],"ja":["効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供","開発者がClaudeの能力を拡張することを支援","複数のワークフローをサポート","専門知識とツールを提供"],"ko":["有效한 스킬을 생성하기 위한 가이드 제공","개발자가 Claude의 능력을 확장하는 것을 지원","다양한 워크플로우 지원","전문 지식과 도구 제공"],"es":["Flujos de trabajo especializados","Conocimientos y herramientas especializados","Paquetes modulares y autocontenidos","Amplía las capacidades de Claude","Guía para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Flux de travail spécialisés","Connaissances et outils spécialisés","Paquets modulaires et autocontenus","Étend les capacités de Claude","Guide pour développeurs"],"de":["Spezialisierte Arbeitsabläufe","Spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Tools","Modulare und selbstenthaltene Pakete","Erweitert die Kapazitäten von Claude","Anleitung für Entwickler"],"pt":["Fornece orientação para criar habilidades eficazes","Estende as capacidades do Claude com conhecimento especializado","Oferece fluxos de trabalho especializados","Permite a criação de habilidades personalizadas","Integra-se com o Claude para melhorar a produtividade"],"ru":["Предоставляет руководство для создания эффективных навыков","Расширяет возможности Claude с помощью специализированных знаний","Предлагает специализированные рабочие процессы","Позволяет создавать индивидуальные навыки","Интегрируется с Claude для повышения производительности"],"ar":["يوفر إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة","يتوسع قدرات Claude مع المعرفة المتخصصة","يقدم تدفقات عملية متخصصة","يسمح بإنشاء مهارات مخصصة","يتكامل مع Claude لتحسين الإنتاجية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创建器","开发者工具","Claude能力扩展","技能开发","工作流支持"],"ja":["スキルクリエイター","開発ツール","Claudeの能力拡張","スキル開発","ワークフローサポート"],"ko":["스킬 생성기","개발자 도구","Claude 능력 확장","스킬 개발","워크플로우 지원"],"es":["creador de habilidades","desarrollo de habilidades","guía para desarrolladores","conocimientos especializados","flujos de trabajo","Claude","desarrollo de software","tecnologías de inteligencia artificial"],"fr":["créateur de compétences","développement de compétences","guide pour développeurs","connaissances spécialisées","flux de travail","Claude","développement de logiciels","technologies d''intelligence artificielle"],"de":["Fähigkeits-Ersteller","Fähigkeits-Entwicklung","Anleitung für Entwickler","spezialisierte Kenntnisse","Arbeitsabläufe","Claude","Software-Entwicklung","Künstliche-Intelligenz-Technologien"],"pt":["Skill Creator","Desenvolvimento de Habilidades","Conhecimento Especializado","Fluxos de Trabalho","Produtividade","Claude","Habilidades Eficazes"],"ru":["Создатель Навыков","Разработка Навыков","Специализированные Знания","Рабочие Процессы","Производительность","Claude","Эффективные Навыки"],"ar":["مبتكر المهارات","تطوير المهارات","المعرفة المتخصصة","التدفقات العملية","الإنتاجية","Claude","المهارات الفعالة"]}},"owner":"twj0","repo":"2026mcm","repoPath":"twj0/2026mcm","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.482Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### Concise is Key\n\nThe context window is a public good. Skills share the context window with everything else Claude needs: system prompt, conversation history, other Skills'' metadata, and the actual user request.\n\n**Default assumption: Claude is already very smart.** Only add context Claude doesn''t already have. Challenge each piece of information: \"Does Claude really need this explanation?\" and \"Does this paragraph justify its token cost?\"\n\nPrefer concise examples over verbose explanations.\n\n### Set Appropriate Degrees of Freedom\n\nMatch the level of specificity to the task''s fragility and variability:\n\n**High freedom (text-based instructions)**: Use when multiple approaches are valid, decisions depend on context, or heuristics guide the approach.\n\n**Medium freedom (pseudocode or scripts with parameters)**: Use when a preferred pattern exists, some variation is acceptable, or configuration affects behavior.\n\n**Low freedom (specific scripts, few parameters)**: Use when operations are fragile and error-prone, consistency is critical, or a specific sequence must be followed.\n\nThink of Claude as exploring a path: a narrow bridge with cliffs needs specific guardrails (low freedom), while an open field allows many routes (high freedom).\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\nEvery SKILL.md consists of:\n\n- **Frontmatter** (YAML): Contains `name` and `description` fields. These are the only fields that Claude reads to determine when the skill gets used, thus it is very important to be clear and comprehensive in describing what the skill is, and when it should be used.\n- **Body** (Markdown): Instructions and guidance for using the skill. Only loaded AFTER the skill triggers (if at all).\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n#### What to Not Include in a Skill\n\nA skill should only contain essential files that directly support its functionality. Do NOT create extraneous documentation or auxiliary files, including:\n\n- README.md\n- INSTALLATION_GUIDE.md\n- QUICK_REFERENCE.md\n- CHANGELOG.md\n- etc.\n\nThe skill should only contain the information needed for an AI agent to do the job at hand. It should not contain auxilary context about the process that went into creating it, setup and testing procedures, user-facing documentation, etc. Creating additional documentation files just adds clutter and confusion.\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window)\n\n#### Progressive Disclosure Patterns\n\nKeep SKILL.md body to the essentials and under 500 lines to minimize context bloat. Split content into separate files when approaching this limit. When splitting out content into other files, it is very important to reference them from SKILL.md and describe clearly when to read them, to ensure the reader of the skill knows they exist and when to use them.\n\n**Key principle:** When a skill supports multiple variations, frameworks, or options, keep only the core workflow and selection guidance in SKILL.md. Move variant-specific details (patterns, examples, configuration) into separate reference files.\n\n**Pattern 1: High-level guide with references**\n\n```markdown\n# PDF Processing\n\n## Quick start\n\nExtract text with pdfplumber:\n[code example]\n\n## Advanced features\n\n- **Form filling**: See [FORMS.md](FORMS.md) for complete guide\n- **API reference**: See [REFERENCE.md](REFERENCE.md) for all methods\n- **Examples**: See [EXAMPLES.md](EXAMPLES.md) for common patterns\n```\n\nClaude loads FORMS.md, REFERENCE.md, or EXAMPLES.md only when needed.\n\n**Pattern 2: Domain-specific organization**\n\nFor Skills with multiple domains, organize content by domain to avoid loading irrelevant context:\n\n```\nbigquery-skill/\n├── SKILL.md (overview and navigation)\n└── reference/\n    ├── finance.md (revenue, billing metrics)\n    ├── sales.md (opportunities, pipeline)\n    ├── product.md (API usage, features)\n    └── marketing.md (campaigns, attribution)\n```\n\nWhen a user asks about sales metrics, Claude only reads sales.md.\n\nSimilarly, for skills supporting multiple frameworks or variants, organize by variant:\n\n```\ncloud-deploy/\n├── SKILL.md (workflow + provider selection)\n└── references/\n    ├── aws.md (AWS deployment patterns)\n    ├── gcp.md (GCP deployment patterns)\n    └── azure.md (Azure deployment patterns)\n```\n\nWhen the user chooses AWS, Claude only reads aws.md.\n\n**Pattern 3: Conditional details**\n\nShow basic content, link to advanced content:\n\n```markdown\n# DOCX Processing\n\n## Creating documents\n\nUse docx-js for new documents. See [DOCX-JS.md](DOCX-JS.md).\n\n## Editing documents\n\nFor simple edits, modify the XML directly.\n\n**For tracked changes**: See [REDLINING.md](REDLINING.md)\n**For OOXML details**: See [OOXML.md](OOXML.md)\n```\n\nClaude reads REDLINING.md or OOXML.md only when the user needs those features.\n\n**Important guidelines:**\n\n- **Avoid deeply nested references** - Keep references one level deep from SKILL.md. All reference files should link directly from SKILL.md.\n- **Structure longer reference files** - For files longer than 100 lines, include a table of contents at the top so Claude can see the full scope when previewing.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nSkill creation involves these steps:\n\n1. Understand the skill with concrete examples\n2. Plan reusable skill contents (scripts, references, assets)\n3. Initialize the skill (run init_skill.py)\n4. Edit the skill (implement resources and write SKILL.md)\n5. Package the skill (run package_skill.py)\n6. Iterate based on real usage\n\nFollow these steps in order, skipping only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Include information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Learn Proven Design Patterns\n\nConsult these helpful guides based on your skill''s needs:\n\n- **Multi-step processes**: See references/workflows.md for sequential workflows and conditional logic\n- **Specific output formats or quality standards**: See references/output-patterns.md for template and example patterns\n\nThese files contain established best practices for effective skill design.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAdded scripts must be tested by actually running them to ensure there are no bugs and that the output matches what is expected. If there are many similar scripts, only a representative sample needs to be tested to ensure confidence that they all work while balancing time to completion.\n\nAny example files and directories not needed for the skill should be deleted. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Guidelines:** Always use imperative/infinitive form.\n\n##### Frontmatter\n\nWrite the YAML frontmatter with `name` and `description`:\n\n- `name`: The skill name\n- `description`: This is the primary triggering mechanism for your skill, and helps Claude understand when to use the skill.\n  - Include both what the Skill does and specific triggers/contexts for when to use it.\n  - Include all \"when to use\" information here - Not in the body. The body is only loaded after triggering, so \"When to Use This Skill\" sections in the body are not helpful to Claude.\n  - Example description for a `docx` skill: \"Comprehensive document creation, editing, and analysis with support for tracked changes, comments, formatting preservation, and text extraction. Use when Claude needs to work with professional documents (.docx files) for: (1) Creating new documents, (2) Modifying or editing content, (3) Working with tracked changes, (4) Adding comments, or any other document tasks\"\n\nDo not include any other fields in YAML frontmatter.\n\n##### Body\n\nWrite instructions for using the skill and its bundled resources.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce development of the skill is complete, it must be packaged into a distributable .skill file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a .skill file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.skill`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution. The .skill file is a zip file with a .skill extension.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:53:46.840Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Developer Agents needing to create specialized knowledge workflows and tools for Claude.","zh":"非常适合需要为 Claude 创建专用知识工作流和工具的开发者代理","ja":"Claude 向けの専用の知識ワークフローとツールを作成する必要がある Developer エージェントに最適","ko":"클라우드용 전문 지식 워크플로 및 도구를 생성해야 하는 개발자 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollador que necesitan crear flujos de trabajo y herramientas de conocimiento especializado para Claude.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de créer des flux de travail et des outils de connaissances spécialisées pour Claude.","de":"Perfekt für Entwickleragenten, die spezialisierte Wissensworkflows und -tools für Claude erstellen müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedor que precisam criar fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas de conhecimento especializado para Claude.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-разработчиков, которым необходимо создавать специализированные рабочие процессы и инструменты знаний для Claude.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذي يحتاج إلى إنشاء تدفقات عمل ومهارات معرفة متخصصة لشركة Claude."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized agents equipped with procedural knowledge, providing modular and self-contained packages that extend capabilities, utilizing specialized workflows and multi-domain knowledge.","zh":"赋予代理转变为具有程序化知识的专用代理的能力，提供模块化和自包含的软件包，以扩展功能，利用专用工作流和多域知识","ja":"手続き型の知識を備えた専門エージェントへの転換を可能にし、能力を拡張するモジュラーで自己完結したパッケージを提供し、専門のワークフローとマルチドメインの知識を利用する","ko":"수행 지식을 갖춘 전문 에이전트로 전환할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 기능을 확장하고 모듈화된 자체 포함 패키지를 제공하며 전문 워크플로 및 다중 도메인 지식을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformarse en agentes especializados equipados con conocimiento procedimental, proporcionando paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que amplían las capacidades, utilizando flujos de trabajo especializados y conocimiento multidominio.","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en agents spécialisés équipés de connaissances procédurales, fournissant des packages modulaires et autocontenus qui étendent les capacités, en utilisant des flux de travail spécialisés et des connaissances multidomaines.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, sich in spezialisierte Agenten mit prozeduralem Wissen zu verwandeln, indem sie modulare und selbstenthaltene Pakete bereitstellen, die die Fähigkeiten erweitern, unter Nutzung spezialisierter Workflows und multidomänenbezogenen Wissens.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a se transformarem em agentes especializados equipados com conhecimento procedural, fornecendo pacotes modulares e autocontidos que estendem as capacidades, utilizando fluxos de trabalho especializados e conhecimento multi-domínio.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью превратиться в специализированных агентов, оснащенных процедурными знаниями, предоставляя модульные и самодостаточные пакеты, расширяющие возможности, используя специализированные рабочие процессы и многодоменные знания.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على التحول إلى وكلاء متخصصين مجهزين بالمعرفة الإجرائية، وتوفير حزم متوافرة وذاتية الحص895، التي توسع القدرات، باستخدام تدفقات العمل المتخصصة ومعرفة متعددة المجالات."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating onboarding guides for specific domains","Developing modular packages for specialized tasks","Extending agent capabilities with procedural knowledge"],"zh":["为特定领域创建入门指南","为专用任务开发模块化软件包","使用程序化知识扩展代理功能"],"ja":["特定ドメインのガイドを作成する","専用タスク用のモジュラー化されたパッケージを開発する","手続き型の知識を使用してエージェントの機能を拡張する"],"ko":["특정 영역에 대한 온보딩 가이드 생성","전문 작업을 위한 모듈 패키지 개발","수행 지식을 사용하여 에이전트 기능 확장"],"es":["Crear guías de incorporación para dominios específicos","Desarrollar paquetes modulares para tareas especializadas","Ampliar las capacidades de los agentes con conocimiento procedimental"],"fr":["Créer des guides d''intégration pour des domaines spécifiques","Développer des packages modulaires pour des tâches spécialisées","Étendre les capacités des agents avec des connaissances procédurales"],"de":["Erstellen von Einführungsleitfäden für spezifische Domänen","Entwickeln von modularen Paketen für spezialisierte Aufgaben","Erweitern der Agentenfähigkeiten mit prozeduralem Wissen"],"pt":["Criar guias de integração para domínios específicos","Desenvolver pacotes modulares para tarefas especializadas","Estender as capacidades do agente com conhecimento procedural"],"ru":["Создание руководств по интеграции для конкретных доменов","Разработка модульных пакетов для специализированных задач","Расширение возможностей агента с помощью процедурных знаний"],"ar":["إنشاء دليل إرشادي للنطاقات المحددة","تطوير حزم متوافرة لمهام متخصصة","توسيع قدرات الوكيل بمعرفة إجرائية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude''s capabilities as a foundation","Limited to providing specialized knowledge and workflows"],"zh":["需要以 Claude 的功能为基础","仅限提供专用知识和工作流"],"ja":["Claude の機能を基盤として必要","専門知識とワークフローを提供することのみに限定"],"ko":["클라우드의 기능을 기반으로 필요","전문 지식 및 워크플로 제공에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere las capacidades de Claude como base","Limitado a proporcionar conocimiento y flujos de trabajo especializados"],"fr":["Nécessite les capacités de Claude comme base","Limité à fournir des connaissances et des flux de travail spécialisés"],"de":["Erfordert die Fähigkeiten von Claude als Grundlage","Begrenzt auf die Bereitstellung spezialisierter Wissen und Workflows"],"pt":["Exige as capacidades do Claude como base","Limitado a fornecer conhecimento e fluxos de trabalho especializados"],"ru":["Требует возможностей Claude в качестве основы","Ограничен предоставлением специализированных знаний и рабочих процессов"],"ar":["يتطلب قدرات Claude كأساس","محدود بتوفير معرفة وتدفق عمل متخصص"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
