ターフェース設計は、ユーザーインターフェースを構築する学問であり、一貫性と効率性の高いユーザーエクスペリエンスを提供することを目指しています","ko":"인터페이스 디자인은 사용자 인터페이스를 구축하는 학문으로 일관성과 효율성을 갖춘 사용자 경험을 제공하는 것을 목표로 합니다","es":"El diseño de interfaz se centra en crear interfaces de usuario personalizadas y coherentes para dashboards y aplicaciones","fr":"La conception d''interface se concentre sur la création d''interfaces utilisateur personnalisées et cohérentes pour les tableaux de bord et les applications","de":"Das Benutzeroberflächendesign konzentriert sich auf die Erstellung benutzerdefinierter und konsistenter Schnittstellen für Dashboards und Anwendungen","pt":"Desenvolva interfaces de usuário personalizadas e consistentes para melhorar a experiência do usuário","ru":"Разрабатывайте адаптированные и последовательные интерфейсы для улучшения опыта пользователя","ar":"قم بإنشاء واجهات مستخدم مخصصة ومتسقة لتحسين تجربة المستخدم","en":"Sistema de ingeniería hidráulica en redes de distribución de agua potable en el Perú"},"definition":{"en":"Sistema de ingeniería hidráulica en redes de distribución de agua potable en el Perú"},"features":{"zh":["一致的设计语言","高效的用户体验","灵活的布局","清晰的导航","响应式设计"],"ja":["一貫性のあるデザイン言語","効率的なユーザーエクスペリエンス","柔軟なレイアウト","明確なナビゲーション","レスポンシブデザイン"],"ko":["일관된 디자인 언어","효율적인 사용자 경험","유연한 레이아웃","명확한 내비게이션","반응형 디자인"],"es":["Diseño de interfaces de usuario personalizadas","Creación de dashboards y paneles de administración","Desarrollo de aplicaciones SaaS","Mejora de la experiencia del usuario","Diseño de interfaces de datos"],"fr":["Conception d''interfaces utilisateur personnalisées","Création de tableaux de bord et de panneaux d''administration","Développement d''applications SaaS","Amélioration de l''expérience utilisateur","Conception d''interfaces de données"],"de":["Erstellung benutzerdefinierter Benutzeroberflächen","Erstellung von Dashboards und Administrationsbereichen","Entwicklung von SaaS-Anwendungen","Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung","Erstellung von Daten-Schnittstellen"],"pt":["Criação de interfaces personalizadas","Desenvolvimento de dashboards e painéis de administração","Design de interfaces para aplicativos SaaS","Otimização da experiência do usuário","Desenvolvimento de interfaces consistentes"],"ru":["Создание адаптированных интерфейсов","Разработка панелей управления и административных панелей","Дизайн интерфейсов для приложений SaaS","Оптимизация опыта пользователя","Разработка последовательных интерфейсов"],"ar":["تصميم واجهات مخصصة","تطوير لوحات التحكم وأدوات الإدارة","تصميم واجهات لتطبيقات SaaS","تحسين تجربة المستخدم","تطوير واجهات متسقة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["界面设计","用户体验","交互设计","一致性设计","高效设计","灵活布局","清晰导航"],"ja":["インターフェース設計","ユーザーエクスペリエンス","インタラクション設計","一貫性設計","効率的な設計","柔軟なレイアウト","明確なナビゲーション"],"ko":["인터페이스 디자인","사용자 경험","상호작용 디자인","일관성 디자인","효율적인 디자인","유연한 레이아웃","명확한 내비게이션"],"es":["diseño de interfaz","interfaces de usuario","dashboards","paneles de administración","aplicaciones SaaS","experiencia del usuario","diseño de interfaces de datos"],"fr":["conception d''interface","interfaces utilisateur","tableaux de bord","panneaux d''administration","applications SaaS","expérience utilisateur","conception d''interfaces de données"],"de":["Benutzeroberflächendesign","Benutzeroberflächen","Dashboards","Administrationsbereiche","SaaS-Anwendungen","Benutzererfahrung","Erstellung von Daten-Schnittstellen"],"pt":["design de interface","interfaces de usuário","dashboards","painéis de administração","aplicativos SaaS","experiência do usuário","desenvolvimento de interfaces"],"ru":["дизайн интерфейса","интерфейсы пользователя","панели управления","административные панели","приложения SaaS","опыт пользователя","разработка интерфейсов"],"ar":["تصميم الواجهة","واجهات المستخدم","لوحات التحكم","أدوات الإدارة","تطبيقات SaaS","تجربة المستخدم","تطوير الواجهات"]}},"owner":"Mikisbell","repo":"HidroAliaga","repoPath":"Mikisbell/HidroAliaga","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"interface-design","description":"This skill is for interface design — dashboards, admin panels, apps, tools, and interactive products. NOT for marketing design (landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns).","bodyPreview":"# Interface Design\n\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\n\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\n\n---\n\n# The Problem\n\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\n\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state your intent — and","body":"# Interface Design\n\nBuild interface design with craft and consistency.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Use for:** Dashboards, admin panels, SaaS apps, tools, settings pages, data interfaces.\n\n**Not for:** Landing pages, marketing sites, campaigns. Redirect those to `/frontend-design`.\n\n---\n\n# The Problem\n\nYou will generate generic output. Your training has seen thousands of dashboards. The patterns are strong.\n\nYou can follow the entire process below — explore the domain, name a signature, state your intent — and still produce a template. Warm colors on cold structures. Friendly fonts on generic layouts. \"Kitchen feel\" that looks like every other app.\n\nThis happens because intent lives in prose, but code generation pulls from patterns. The gap between them is where defaults win.\n\nThe process below helps. But process alone doesn''t guarantee craft. You have to catch yourself.\n\n---\n\n# Where Defaults Hide\n\nDefaults don''t announce themselves. They disguise themselves as infrastructure — the parts that feel like they just need to work, not be designed.\n\n**Typography feels like a container.** Pick something readable, move on. But typography isn''t holding your design — it IS your design. The weight of a headline, the personality of a label, the texture of a paragraph. These shape how the product feels before anyone reads a word. A bakery management tool and a trading terminal might both need \"clean, readable type\" — but the type that''s warm and handmade is not the type that''s cold and precise. If you''re reaching for your usual font, you''re not designing.\n\n**Navigation feels like scaffolding.** Build the sidebar, add the links, get to the real work. But navigation isn''t around your product — it IS your product. Where you are, where you can go, what matters most. A page floating in space is a component demo, not software. The navigation teaches people how to think about the space they''re in.\n\n**Data feels like presentation.** You have numbers, show numbers. But a number on screen is not design. The question is: what does this number mean to the person looking at it? What will they do with it? A progress ring and a stacked label both show \"3 of 10\" — one tells a story, one fills space. If you''re reaching for number-on-label, you''re not designing.\n\n**Token names feel like implementation detail.** But your CSS variables are design decisions. `--ink` and `--parchment` evoke a world. `--gray-700` and `--surface-2` evoke a template. Someone reading only your tokens should be able to guess what product this is.\n\nThe trap is thinking some decisions are creative and others are structural. There are no structural decisions. Everything is design. The moment you stop asking \"why this?\" is the moment defaults take over.\n\n---\n\n# Intent First\n\nBefore touching code, answer these. Not in your head — out loud, to yourself or the user.\n\n**Who is this human?**\nNot \"users.\" The actual person. Where are they when they open this? What''s on their mind? What did they do 5 minutes ago, what will they do 5 minutes after? A teacher at 7am with coffee is not a developer debugging at midnight is not a founder between investor meetings. Their world shapes the interface.\n\n**What must they accomplish?**\nNot \"use the dashboard.\" The verb. Grade these submissions. Find the broken deployment. Approve the payment. The answer determines what leads, what follows, what hides.\n\n**What should this feel like?**\nSay it in words that mean something. \"Clean and modern\" means nothing — every AI says that. Warm like a notebook? Cold like a terminal? Dense like a trading floor? Calm like a reading app? The answer shapes color, type, spacing, density — everything.\n\nIf you cannot answer these with specifics, stop. Ask the user. Do not guess. Do not default.\n\n## Every Choice Must Be A Choice\n\nFor every decision, you must be able to explain WHY.\n\n- Why this layout and not another?\n- Why this color temperature?\n- Why this typeface?\n- Why this spacing scale?\n- Why this information hierarchy?\n\nIf your answer is \"it''s common\" or \"it''s clean\" or \"it works\" — you haven''t chosen. You''ve defaulted. Defaults are invisible. Invisible choices compound into generic output.\n\n**The test:** If you swapped your choices for the most common alternatives and the design didn''t feel meaningfully different, you never made real choices.\n\n## Sameness Is Failure\n\nIf another AI, given a similar prompt, would produce substantially the same output — you have failed.\n\nThis is not about being different for its own sake. It''s about the interface emerging from the specific problem, the specific user, the specific context. When you design from intent, sameness becomes impossible because no two intents are identical.\n\nWhen you design from defaults, everything looks the same because defaults are shared.\n\n## Intent Must Be Systemic\n\nSaying \"warm\" and using cold colors is not following through. Intent is not a label — it''s a constraint that shapes every decision.\n\nIf the intent is warm: surfaces, text, borders, accents, semantic colors, typography — all warm. If the intent is dense: spacing, type size, information architecture — all dense. If the intent is calm: motion, contrast, color saturation — all calm.\n\nCheck your output against your stated intent. Does every token reinforce it? Or did you state an intent and then default anyway?\n\n---\n\n# Product Domain Exploration\n\nThis is where defaults get caught — or don''t.\n\nGeneric output: Task type → Visual template → Theme\nCrafted output: Task type → Product domain → Signature → Structure + Expression\n\nThe difference: time in the product''s world before any visual or structural thinking.\n\n## Required Outputs\n\n**Do not propose any direction until you produce all four:**\n\n**Domain:** Concepts, metaphors, vocabulary from this product''s world. Not features — territory. Minimum 5.\n\n**Color world:** What colors exist naturally in this product''s domain? Not \"warm\" or \"cool\" — go to the actual world. If this product were a physical space, what would you see? What colors belong there that don''t belong elsewhere? List 5+.\n\n**Signature:** One element — visual, structural, or interaction — that could only exist for THIS product. If you can''t name one, keep exploring.\n\n**Defaults:** 3 obvious choices for this interface type — visual AND structural. You can''t avoid patterns you haven''t named.\n\n## Proposal Requirements\n\nYour direction must explicitly reference:\n- Domain concepts you explored\n- Colors from your color world exploration\n- Your signature element\n- What replaces each default\n\n**The test:** Read your proposal. Remove the product name. Could someone identify what this is for? If not, it''s generic. Explore deeper.\n\n---\n\n# The Mandate\n\n**Before showing the user, look at what you made.**\n\nAsk yourself: \"If they said this lacks craft, what would they mean?\"\n\nThat thing you just thought of — fix it first.\n\nYour first output is probably generic. That''s normal. The work is catching it before the user has to.\n\n## The Checks\n\nRun these against your output before presenting:\n\n- **The swap test:** If you swapped the typeface for your usual one, would anyone notice? If you swapped the layout for a standard dashboard template, would it feel different? The places where swapping wouldn''t matter are the places you defaulted.\n\n- **The squint test:** Blur your eyes. Can you still perceive hierarchy? Is anything jumping out harshly? Craft whispers.\n\n- **The signature test:** Can you point to five specific elements where your signature appears? Not \"the overall feel\" — actual components. A signature you can''t locate doesn''t exist.\n\n- **The token test:** Read your CSS variables out loud. Do they sound like they belong to this product''s world, or could they belong to any project?\n\nIf any check fails, iterate before showing.\n\n---\n\n# Craft Foundations\n\n## Subtle Layering\n\nThis is the backbone of craft. Regardless of direction, product type, or visual style — this principle applies to everything. You should barely notice the system working. When you look at Vercel''s dashboard, you don''t think \"nice borders.\" You just understand the structure. The craft is invisible — that''s how you know it''s working.\n\n### Surface Elevation\n\nSurfaces stack. A dropdown sits above a card which sits above the page. Build a numbered system — base, then increasing elevation levels. In dark mode, higher elevation = slightly lighter. In light mode, higher elevation = slightly lighter or uses shadow.\n\nEach jump should be only a few percentage points of lightness. You can barely see the difference in isolation. But when surfaces stack, the hierarchy emerges. Whisper-quiet shifts that you feel rather than see.\n\n**Key decisions:**\n- **Sidebars:** Same background as canvas, not different. Different colors fragment the visual space into \"sidebar world\" and \"content world.\" A subtle border is enough separation.\n- **Dropdowns:** One level above their parent surface. If both share the same level, the dropdown blends into the card and layering is lost.\n- **Inputs:** Slightly darker than their surroundings, not lighter. Inputs are \"inset\" — they receive content. A darker background signals \"type here\" without heavy borders.\n\n### Borders\n\nBorders should disappear when you''re not looking for them, but be findable when you need structure. Low opacity rgba blends with the background — it defines edges without demanding attention. Solid hex borders look harsh in comparison.\n\nBuild a progression — not all borders are equal. Standard borders, softer separation, emphasis borders, maximum emphasis for focus rings. Match intensity to the importance of the boundary.\n\n**The squint test:** Blur your eyes at the interface. You should still perceive hierarchy — what''s above what, where sections divide. But nothing should jump out. No harsh lines. No jarring color shifts. Just quiet structure.\n\nThis separates professional interfaces from amateur ones. Get this wrong and nothing else matters.\n\n## Infinite Expression\n\nEvery pattern has infinite expressions. **No interface should look the same.**\n\nA metric display could be a hero number, inline stat, sparkline, gauge, progress bar, comparison delta, trend badge, or something new. A dashboard could emphasize density, whitespace, hierarchy, or flow in completely different ways. Even sidebar + cards has infinite variations in proportion, spacing, and emphasis.\n\n**Before building, ask:**\n- What''s the ONE thing users do most here?\n- What products solve similar problems brilliantly? Study them.\n- Why would this interface feel designed for its purpose, not templated?\n\n**NEVER produce identical output.** Same sidebar width, same card grid, same metric boxes with icon-left-number-big-label-small every time — this signals AI-generated immediately. It''s forgettable.\n\nThe architecture and components should emerge from the task and data, executed in a way that feels fresh. Linear''s cards don''t look like Notion''s. Vercel''s metrics don''t look like Stripe''s. Same concepts, infinite expressions.\n\n## Color Lives Somewhere\n\nEvery product exists in a world. That world has colors.\n\nBefore you reach for a palette, spend time in the product''s world. What would you see if you walked into the physical version of this space? What materials? What light? What objects?\n\nYour palette should feel like it came FROM somewhere — not like it was applied TO something.\n\n**Beyond Warm and Cold:** Temperature is one axis. Is this quiet or loud? Dense or spacious? Serious or playful? Geometric or organic? A trading terminal and a meditation app are both \"focused\" — completely different kinds of focus. Find the specific quality, not the generic label.\n\n**Color Carries Meaning:** Gray builds structure. Color communicates — status, action, emphasis, identity. Unmotivated color is noise. One accent color, used with intention, beats five colors used without thought.\n\n---\n\n# Before Writing Each Component\n\n**Every time** you write UI code — even small additions — state:\n\n```\nIntent: [who is this human, what must they do, how should it feel]\nPalette: [colors from your exploration — and WHY they fit this product''s world]\nDepth: [borders / shadows / layered — and WHY this fits the intent]\nSurfaces: [your elevation scale — and WHY this color temperature]\nTypography: [your typeface — and WHY it fits the intent]\nSpacing: [your base unit]\n```\n\nThis checkpoint is mandatory. It forces you to connect every technical choice back to intent.\n\nIf you can''t explain WHY for each choice, you''re defaulting. Stop and think.\n\n---\n\n# Design Principles\n\n## Token Architecture\n\nEvery color in your interface should trace back to a small set of primitives: foreground (text hierarchy), background (surface elevation), border (separation hierarchy), brand, and semantic (destructive, warning, success). No random hex values — everything maps to primitives.\n\n### Text Hierarchy\n\nDon''t just have \"text\" and \"gray text.\" Build four levels — primary, secondary, tertiary, muted. Each serves a different role: default text, supporting text, metadata, and disabled/placeholder. Use all four consistently. If you''re only using two, your hierarchy is too flat.\n\n### Border Progression\n\nBorders aren''t binary. Build a scale that matches intensity to importance — standard separation, softer separation, emphasis, maximum emphasis. Not every boundary deserves the same weight.\n\n### Control Tokens\n\nForm controls have specific needs. Don''t reuse surface tokens — create dedicated ones for control backgrounds, control borders, and focus states. This lets you tune interactive elements independently from layout surfaces.\n\n## Spacing\n\nPick a base unit and stick to multiples. Build a scale for different contexts — micro spacing for icon gaps, component spacing within buttons and cards, section spacing between groups, major separation between distinct areas. Random values signal no system.\n\n## Padding\n\nKeep it symmetrical. If one side has a value, others should match unless content naturally requires asymmetry.\n\n## Depth\n\nChoose ONE approach and commit:\n- **Borders-only** — Clean, technical. For dense tools.\n- **Subtle shadows** — Soft lift. For approachable products.\n- **Layered shadows** — Premium, dimensional. For cards that need presence.\n- **Surface color shifts** — Background tints establish hierarchy without shadows.\n\nDon''t mix approaches.\n\n## Border Radius\n\nSharper feels technical. Rounder feels friendly. Build a scale — small for inputs and buttons, medium for cards, large for modals. Don''t mix sharp and soft randomly.\n\n## Typography\n\nBuild distinct levels distinguishable at a glance. Headlines need weight and tight tracking for presence. Body needs comfortable weight for readability. Labels need medium weight that works at smaller sizes. Data needs monospace with tabular number spacing for alignment. Don''t rely on size alone — combine size, weight, and letter-spacing.\n\n## Card Layouts\n\nA metric card doesn''t have to look like a plan card doesn''t have to look like a settings card. Design each card''s internal structure for its specific content — but keep the surface treatment consistent: same border weight, shadow depth, corner radius, padding scale.\n\n## Controls\n\nNative `<select>` and `<input type=\"date\">` render OS-native elements that cannot be styled. Build custom components — trigger buttons with positioned dropdowns, calendar popovers, styled state management.\n\n## Iconography\n\nIcons clarify, not decorate — if removing an icon loses no meaning, remove it. Choose one icon set and stick with it. Give standalone icons presence with subtle background containers.\n\n## Animation\n\nFast micro-interactions, smooth easing. Larger transitions can be slightly longer. Use deceleration easing. Avoid spring/bounce in professional interfaces.\n\n## States\n\nEvery interactive element needs states: default, hover, active, focus, disabled. Data needs states too: loading, empty, error. Missing states feel broken.\n\n## Navigation Context\n\nScreens need grounding. A data table floating in space feels like a component demo, not a product. Include navigation showing where you are in the app, location indicators, and user context. When building sidebars, consider same background as main content with border separation rather than different colors.\n\n## Dark Mode\n\nDark interfaces have different needs. Shadows are less visible on dark backgrounds — lean on borders for definition. Semantic colors (success, warning, error) often need slight desaturation. The hierarchy system still applies, just with inverted values.\n\n---\n\n# Avoid\n\n- **Harsh borders** — if borders are the first thing you see, they''re too strong\n- **Dramatic surface jumps** — elevation changes should be whisper-quiet\n- **Inconsistent spacing** — the clearest sign of no system\n- **Mixed depth strategies** — pick one approach and commit\n- **Missing interaction states** — hover, focus, disabled, loading, error\n- **Dramatic drop shadows** — shadows should be subtle, not attention-grabbing\n- **Large radius on small elements**\n- **Pure white cards on colored backgrounds**\n- **Thick decorative borders**\n- **Gradients and color for decoration** — color should mean something\n- **Multiple accent colors** — dilutes focus\n- **Different hues for different surfaces** — keep the same hue, shift only lightness\n\n---\n\n# Workflow\n\n## Communication\nBe invisible. Don''t announce modes or narrate process.\n\n**Never say:** \"I''m in ESTABLISH MODE\", \"Let me check system.md...\"\n\n**Instead:** Jump into work. State suggestions with reasoning.\n\n## Suggest + Ask\nLead with your exploration and recommendation, then confirm:\n```\n\"Domain: [5+ concepts from the product''s world]\nColor world: [5+ colors that exist in this domain]\nSignature: [one element unique to this product]\nRejecting: [default 1] → [alternative], [default 2] → [alternative], [default 3] → [alternative]\n\nDirection: [approach that connects to the above]\"\n\n[Ask: \"Does that direction feel right?\"]\n```\n\n## If Project Has system.md\nRead `.interface-design/system.md` and apply. Decisions are made.\n\n## If No system.md\n1. Explore domain — Produce all four required outputs\n2. Propose — Direction must reference all four\n3. Confirm — Get user buy-in\n4. Build — Apply principles\n5. **Evaluate** — Run the mandate checks before showing\n6. Offer to save\n\n---\n\n# After Completing a Task\n\nWhen you finish building something, **always offer to save**:\n\n```\n\"Want me to save these patterns for future sessions?\"\n```\n\nIf yes, write to `.interface-design/system.md`:\n- Direction and feel\n- Depth strategy (borders/shadows/layered)\n- Spacing base unit\n- Key component patterns\n\n### What to Save\n\nAdd patterns when a component is used 2+ times, is reusable across the project, or has specific measurements worth remembering. Don''t save one-off components, temporary experiments, or variations better handled with props.\n\n### Consistency Checks\n\nIf system.md defines values, check against them: spacing on the defined grid, depth using the declared strategy throughout, colors from the defined palette, documented patterns reused instead of reinvented.\n\nThis compounds — each save makes future work faster and more consistent.\n\n---\n\n# Deep Dives\n\nFor more detail on specific topics:\n- `references/principles.md` — Code examples, specific values, dark mode\n- `references/validation.md` — Memory management, when to update system.md\n- `references/critique.md` — Post-build craft critique protocol\n\n# Commands\n\n- `/interface-design:status` — Current system state\n- `/interface-design:audit` — Check code against system\n- `/interface-design:extract` — Extract patterns from code\n- `/interface-design:critique` — Critique your build for craft, then rebuild what defaulted\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:56:28.891Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for UI-focused AI Agents needing advanced dashboard design capabilities for water distribution systems","zh":"非常适合需要高级仪表盘设计功能的面向用户界面的AI代理，尤其适用于水资源分配系统","ja":"UIに焦点を当てたAIエージェントが高度なダッシュボード設計機能を必要とする水配布システムに最適","ko":"고급 대시보드 설계 기능이 필요한 UI 중심의 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며,尤其은 수자원 분배 시스템에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de inteligencia artificial enfocados en la interfaz de usuario que necesitan capacidades de diseño de panel de control avanzadas para sistemas de distribución de agua","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle axés sur l''interface utilisateur nécessitant des capacités de conception de tableau de bord avancées pour les systèmes de distribution d''eau","de":"Perfekt für benutzeroberflächenorientierte KI-Agents, die erweiterte Dashboard-Designfunktionen für Wasserverteilungssysteme benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA com foco em UI que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de design de dashboard para sistemas de distribuição de água","ru":"Идеально подходит для AI-агентов, ориентированных на UI, требующих передовых возможностей проектирования панелей управления для систем распределения воды","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي ذوي واجهة المستخدم التي تحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة لتصميم لوحة القيادة لأنظمة توزيع المياه"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to craft consistent and user-friendly interfaces for dashboards, admin panels, and SaaS apps using protocols like data interfaces, leveraging thousands of dashboard patterns for generic output generation","zh":"赋予代理创建一致且用户友好的仪表盘、管理面板和SaaS应用程序的界面使用像数据接口这样的协议，并利用成千上万的仪表盘模式进行通用输出生成","ja":"エージェントがデータインターフェイスなどのプロトコルを使用して、一貫性のあるユーザーフレンドリーなダッシュボード、管理パネル、SaaSアプリのインターフェイスを作成できるようにし、汎用的な出力生成のための数千のダッシュボードパターンを利用する","ko":"에이전트가 데이터 인터페이스와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 일관된 사용자 친화적인 대시보드, 관리 패널 및 SaaS 애플리케이션의 인터페이스를 생성할 수 있도록 하며, 일반적인 출력 생성을 위해 수천 개의 대시보드 패턴을 활용","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear interfaces consistentes y fáciles de usar para paneles de control, paneles de administración y aplicaciones SaaS utilizando protocolos como interfaces de datos, aprovechando miles de patrones de panel de control para la generación de salida genérica","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des interfaces cohérentes et conviviales pour les tableaux de bord, les panneaux d''administration et les applications SaaS en utilisant des protocoles tels que les interfaces de données, en exploitant des milliers de modèles de tableau de bord pour la génération de sortie générique","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, konsistente und benutzerfreundliche Schnittstellen für Dashboards, Admin-Panel und SaaS-Apps zu erstellen, indem sie Protokolle wie Daten-Schnittstellen verwenden und dabei Tausende von Dashboard-Mustern für die generische Ausgabengenerierung nutzen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar interfaces consistentes e amigáveis para dashboards, painéis de administração e aplicativos SaaS usando protocolos como interfaces de dados, aproveitando milhares de padrões de dashboard para geração de saída genérica","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать последовательные и удобные интерфейсы для панелей управления, административных панелей и приложений SaaS, используя протоколы, такие как интерфейсы данных, используя тысячи шаблонов панели управления для генерации общего вывода","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من创ación واجهات متسقة وسهلة الاستخدام للوحات القيادة وألواح الإدارة وتطبيقات SaaS باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل واجهات البيانات، وتستفيد من آلاف أنماط لوحة القيادة لتوليد مخرجات عامة"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing intuitive dashboards for water distribution monitoring","Generating consistent admin panels for system management","Creating data interfaces for hydraulic system engineering"],"zh":["为水资源分配监测设计直观的仪表盘","为系统管理生成一致的管理面板","为水力系统工程创建数据接口"],"ja":["水配布システムのモニタリング用に直感的なダッシュボードを設計する","システム管理用に一貫性のある管理パネルを生成する","水力システムエンジニアリング用にデータインターフェイスを作成する"],"ko":["수자원 분배 모니터링을 위한 직관적인 대시보드 설계","시스템 관리를 위한 일관된 관리 패널 생성","수력 시스템 엔지니어링을 위한 데이터 인터페이스 생성"],"es":["Diseñar paneles de control intuitivos para el monitoreo de la distribución de agua","Generar paneles de administración coherentes para la gestión del sistema","Crear interfaces de datos para la ingeniería de sistemas hidráulicos"],"fr":["Concevoir des tableaux de bord intuitifs pour la surveillance de la distribution d''eau","Générer des panneaux d''administration cohérents pour la gestion du système","Créer des interfaces de données pour l''ingénierie des systèmes hydrauliques"],"de":["Intuitive Dashboards für die Überwachung der Wasserverteilung entwerfen","Konsistente Admin-Panel für die Systemverwaltung generieren","Daten-Schnittstellen für die Ingenieure von Hydrauliksystemen erstellen"],"pt":["Projeto de dashboards intuitivos para monitoramento da distribuição de água","Geração de painéis de administração consistentes para gerenciamento de sistema","Criação de interfaces de dados para engenharia de sistemas hidráulicos"],"ru":["Проектирование интуитивных панелей управления для мониторинга системы распределения воды","Генерация последовательных административных панелей для управления системой","Создание интерфейсов данных для инженерии гидравлических систем"],"ar":["تصميم لوحات قيادة متوافقة لمراقبة نظام توزيع المياه","توليد ألواح إدارة متسقة لإدارة النظام","إنشاء واجهات البيانات لهندسة الأنظمة الهيدروليكية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not suitable for landing pages, marketing sites, or campaigns","Redirects non-dashboard design tasks to `/frontend-design`"],"zh":["不适合登陆页面、营销网站或活动","将非仪表盘设计任务重定向到 `/frontend-design`"],"ja":["ランディングページ、マーケティングサイト、またはキャンペーンには不適","ダッシュボード以外の設計タスクを `/frontend-design` にリダイレクト"],"ko":["랜딩 페이지, 마케팅 사이트 또는 캠페인에는 적합하지 않음","대시보드 이외의 디자인 작업을 `/frontend-design`로 리디렉션"],"es":["No es adecuado para páginas de destino, sitios de marketing o campañas","Redirige las tareas de diseño que no son de panel de control a `/frontend-design`"],"fr":["N''est pas adapté pour les pages de destination, les sites de marketing ou les campagnes","Redirige les tâches de conception qui ne sont pas de conception de tableau de bord vers `/frontend-design`"],"de":["Nicht geeignet für Ziel-Seiten, Marketing-Seiten oder Kampagnen","Leitet Aufgaben, die kein Dashboard-Design sind, an `/frontend-design` weiter"],"pt":["Não é adequado para páginas de destino, sites de marketing ou campanhas","Redireciona tarefas de design não relacionadas a dashboard para `/frontend-design`"],"ru":["Не подходит для страниц приземления, маркетинговых сайтов или кампаний","Перенаправляет задачи дизайна, не связанные с панелью управления, в `/frontend-design`"],"ar":["لا يصلح للصفحات الهبوطية أو المواقع التسويقية أو الحملات","يعيد توجيه مهام تصميم غير متعلقة بلوحة القيادة إلى `/frontend-design`"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('SlySlayer32/dashboard-link-saas/request-enhancer', 'community', 'SlySlayer32', 'dashboard-link-saas', 'SlySlayer32/dashboard-link-saas', 'request-enhancer', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z', '2026-02-18T09:56:47.381Z', NULL, '{"id":"SlySlayer32/dashboard-link-saas/request-enhancer","name":"request-enhancer","description":{"es":"Request Enhancer es una plataforma SaaS que transforma solicitudes en prompts detallados para una asistencia AI óptima.","fr":"Request Enhancer est une plateforme SaaS qui transforme les requêtes en prompts détaillés pour une assistance AI optimale.","de":"Request Enhancer ist eine SaaS-Plattform, die Anfragen in detaillierte Prompts für eine optimale AI-Unterstützung umwandelt.","pt":"O Request Enhancer é uma plataforma que transforma pedidos em prompts detalhados para desenvolvimento de SaaS","ru":"Request Enhancer - это платформа, которая преобразует запросы в подробные подсказки для разработки SaaS","ar":"مُحسّن الطلب هو منصة تحول الطلبات إلى مساعدات مفصلة لتطوير سaaS","en":"SaaS platform for delivering personalized daily dashboards via SMS"},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Request Enhancer: Mejora de solicitudes para SaaS","fr":"Request Enhancer : Amélioration des requêtes pour SaaS","de":"Request Enhancer: Anfrageverbesserung für SaaS","pt":"Request Enhancer: Otimização de Pedidos para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Request Enhancer: Улучшение Запросов для Разработчиков","ar":"مُحسّن الطلب: تحسين الطلبات للמطورين","en":"request-enhancer"},"description":{"es":"Request Enhancer es una plataforma SaaS que transforma solicitudes en prompts detallados para una asistencia AI óptima.","fr":"Request Enhancer est une plateforme SaaS qui transforme les requêtes en prompts détaillés pour une assistance AI optimale.","de":"Request Enhancer ist eine SaaS-Plattform, die Anfragen in detaillierte Prompts für eine optimale AI-Unterstützung umwandelt.","pt":"O Request Enhancer é uma plataforma que transforma pedidos em prompts detalhados para desenvolvimento de SaaS","ru":"Request Enhancer - это платформа, которая преобразует запросы в подробные подсказки для разработки SaaS","ar":"مُحسّن الطلب هو منصة تحول الطلبات إلى مساعدات مفصلة لتطوير سaaS","en":"SaaS platform for delivering personalized daily dashboards via SMS"},"definition":{"en":"SaaS platform for delivering personalized daily dashboards via SMS"},"features":{"es":["Integración con CleanConnect","Enfoque empresarial mejorado","Asignación automática de lista de verificación V1","Evaluación y mitigación de riesgos"],"fr":["Intégration avec CleanConnect","Focus commercial amélioré","Mapping automatique de la liste de vérification V1","Évaluation et atténuation des risques"],"de":["Integration mit CleanConnect","Verbesserter Geschäftsfokus","Automatische Zuordnung der V1-Checkliste","Risikobewertung und -minimierung"],"pt":["Integração com CleanConnect","Foco empresarial para fundadores não técnicos","Mapeamento automático de checklist V1","Estratégia de avaliação e mitigação de riscos"],"ru":["Интеграция с CleanConnect","Бизнес-фокус для нетехнических основателей","Автоматическое сопоставление чек-листа V1","Стратегия оценки и смягчения рисков"],"ar":["التكامل مع CleanConnect","التركيز التجاري للمؤسسين غير التقنيين","تعيين خريطة تفصيلية للقائمة المرجعية V1","استراتيجية تقييم والتخفيف من المخاطر"]},"keywords":{"es":["SaaS","asistencia AI","solicitudes personalizadas","desarrollo de software","optimización de solicitudes","CleanConnect","lista de verificación V1","evaluación de riesgos"],"fr":["SaaS","assistance AI","requêtes personnalisées","développement de logiciels","optimisation des requêtes","CleanConnect","liste de vérification V1","évaluation des risques"],"de":["SaaS","AI-Unterstützung","personalisierte Anfragen","Softwareentwicklung","Anfrageoptimierung","CleanConnect","V1-Checkliste","Risikobewertung"],"pt":["request enhancer","desenvolvimento de SaaS","pedidos personalizados","assistência AI","vibe coding","CleanConnect","fundadores não técnicos"],"ru":["Request Enhancer","разработка SaaS","персонализированные запросы","помощь ИИ","vibe coding","CleanConnect","нетехнические основатели"],"ar":["مُحسّن الطلب","تطوير سaaS","طلبات مخصصة","مساعدة إيه آي","كودينج الفايب","CleanConnect","مؤسسون غير تقنيين"]}},"owner":"SlySlayer32","repo":"dashboard-link-saas","repoPath":"SlySlayer32/dashboard-link-saas","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"request-enhancer","description":"Automatically rewrites, expands, and enhances user requests using proper linguistics and structured input for optimal vibe coding and SaaS development results","version":"2.0","bodyPreview":"# Request Enhancer Skill v2.0\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nThis skill automatically transforms user requests into well-structured, detailed prompts that follow best practices for vibe coding and SaaS development. It enhances clarity, adds context, and structures requests for optimal AI assistance.\r\n\r\n**Key Improvements in v2.0:**\r\n- Integrated with CleanConnect memory bank system\r\n- Enhanced business focus for non-technical founder\r\n- Automatic V1 checklist mapping\r\n- Risk assessment and mitigation strategi","body":"# Request Enhancer Skill v2.0\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nThis skill automatically transforms user requests into well-structured, detailed prompts that follow best practices for vibe coding and SaaS development. It enhances clarity, adds context, and structures requests for optimal AI assistance.\r\n\r\n**Key Improvements in v2.0:**\r\n- Integrated with CleanConnect memory bank system\r\n- Enhanced business focus for non-technical founder\r\n- Automatic V1 checklist mapping\r\n- Risk assessment and mitigation strategies\r\n- Progress tracking integration\r\n\r\n## Enhancement Process\r\n\r\n### 1. Request Analysis\r\n- Identify the core intent and objectives\r\n- Detect implicit requirements and assumptions\r\n- Assess technical complexity and domain\r\n- Identify missing context that would be helpful\r\n\r\n### 2. Linguistic Enhancement\r\n- Improve clarity and specificity\r\n- Add proper technical terminology where appropriate\r\n- Structure sentences for unambiguous interpretation\r\n- Ensure professional yet approachable tone\r\n\r\n### 3. Structural Improvements\r\n- Add clear objectives and success criteria\r\n- Include relevant context about the project/environment\r\n- Specify constraints and preferences\r\n- Organize into logical sections with clear headings\r\n\r\n### 4. Best Practices Integration\r\n- Include relevant architectural considerations\r\n- Add security and performance implications\r\n- Suggest testing strategies\r\n- Reference project-specific standards and patterns\r\n\r\n## Enhanced Request Template v2.0\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\n## Objective\r\n[Clear, specific statement of what needs to be accomplished]\r\n\r\n## Business Context\r\n- **User**: Non-technical founder building CleanConnect SaaS\r\n- **Goal**: [Business outcome this enables]\r\n- **Impact**: [Why this matters for the business]\r\n- **Timeline**: [Urgency level: Immediate/This week/Soon]\r\n\r\n## Project Context\r\n- **Project**: CleanConnect - Multi-tenant SaaS for workforce management\r\n- **Tech Stack**: Hono + Supabase + React + TypeScript + pnpm\r\n- **Current Phase**: [Foundation/V1 Build/V2]\r\n- **Recent Progress**: [What was just completed]\r\n\r\n## V1 Checklist Mapping\r\n- **Checklist Item**: [Exact item from plan/]\r\n- **Phase Number**: [Current phase from plan/PLAN_INDEX.md]\r\n- **Complexity**: [Simple/Medium/Complex]\r\n- **Estimated Time**: [Time estimate in hours]\r\n- **Dependencies**: [What needs to be done first]\r\n\r\n## Requirements\r\n### Must-Haves (Non-negotiable)\r\n- [Critical requirements that must be met]\r\n\r\n### Should-Haves (Important)\r\n- [Important features that should be included]\r\n\r\n### Could-Haves (Nice to have)\r\n- [Optional features if time permits]\r\n\r\n## Technical Constraints\r\n- Must follow Zapier-style layering\r\n- All database queries scoped by organizationId\r\n- No vendor SDK calls outside adapters/\r\n- Use fixed tech stack only\r\n- Validate inputs with Zod\r\n\r\n## Risk Assessment\r\n- **Risk Level**: [Low/Medium/High]\r\n- **Potential Issues**: [What could go wrong]\r\n- **Mitigation**: [How we''ll prevent problems]\r\n- **Confidence**: [1-10 confidence level]\r\n\r\n## Success Criteria\r\n- [Measurable outcomes that indicate success]\r\n- [How to verify the implementation works]\r\n- [What the user should be able to do]\r\n\r\n## Testing Strategy\r\n- **Unit Tests**: [What needs unit testing]\r\n- **Integration Tests**: [What needs integration testing]\r\n- **Manual Testing**: [How to manually verify]\r\n\r\n## Next Steps\r\n1. [Immediate first action]\r\n2. [What needs to be decided]\r\n3. [What I need from you]\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Implementation Guidelines v2.0\r\n\r\nWhen enhancing requests:\r\n\r\n1. **Founder-First Communication**: \r\n   - Use simple, non-technical language\r\n   - Focus on business outcomes\r\n   - Provide confidence levels\r\n   - Celebrate small wins\r\n\r\n2. **Memory Integration**: \r\n   - Check activeContext.md for current work\r\n   - Reference previous decisions\r\n   - Maintain continuity\r\n   - Update memory after completion\r\n\r\n3. **Risk-Aware Planning**: \r\n   - Always assess risk level\r\n   - Provide mitigation strategies\r\n   - Flag potential blockers early\r\n   - Offer backup options\r\n\r\n4. **Architecture Compliance**: \r\n   - Enforce Zapier-style layering\r\n   - Ensure tenant scoping\r\n   - Use fixed tech stack\r\n   - Follow established patterns\r\n\r\n5. **Progress Tracking**: \r\n   - Map to V1 checklist\r\n   - Estimate complexity realistically\r\n   - Track completion percentage\r\n   - Document lessons learned\r\n\r\n## Example Transformations\r\n\r\n### Before:\r\n\"make a user login thing\"\r\n\r\n### After:\r\n```markdown\r\n## Objective\r\nImplement a secure user authentication system with login and registration functionality for the CleanConnect SaaS platform.\r\n\r\n## Context\r\n- Project: CleanConnect - Multi-tenant SaaS for workforce management\r\n- Tech Stack: Hono (backend) + Supabase (database/auth) + React (frontend) + TypeScript\r\n- Current State: Basic project structure exists, Supabase configured\r\n- Business Impact: Critical for user onboarding and data security\r\n\r\n## Requirements\r\n### Functional Requirements\r\n- User registration with email verification\r\n- Login with email/password\r\n- Password reset functionality\r\n- Session management with JWT tokens\r\n- Multi-tenant isolation by organizationId\r\n\r\n### Technical Requirements\r\n- Use Supabase Auth for authentication\r\n- Implement RLS policies for data isolation\r\n- Secure session handling with httpOnly cookies\r\n- Rate limiting on auth endpoints\r\n- OAuth providers (Google, Microsoft) for enterprise\r\n\r\n### Constraints\r\n- Must follow existing authentication patterns in AGENTS.md\r\n- All database queries must be scoped by organizationId\r\n- No vendor SDK calls outside adapters layer\r\n\r\n## Success Criteria\r\n- Users can register and verify email\r\n- Login works with correct credentials\r\n- Invalid attempts are properly handled\r\n- Sessions persist correctly across refreshes\r\n- Data isolation between organizations is enforced\r\n\r\n## Preferred Approach\r\n- Follow the authentication flow outlined in docs/ARCHITECTURE_BLUEPRINT.md\r\n- Use Zod for input validation\r\n- Implement proper error handling with stable error codes\r\n- Add comprehensive logging for security events\r\n\r\n## Testing Strategy\r\n- Unit tests for auth utilities\r\n- Integration tests for login/registration flows\r\n- Security tests for common vulnerabilities\r\n- Test multi-tenant data isolation\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Automatic Invocation\r\n\r\n**CRITICAL: This skill runs AUTOMATICALLY on EVERY user message before any other processing.**\r\n\r\nThis skill is triggered:\r\n- On ALL user messages (no exceptions)\r\n- Before any other tool or skill runs\r\n- Even for seemingly simple requests\r\n\r\nThe only exceptions are:\r\n- Messages starting with `/no-enhance`\r\n- Messages to other agents/skills that explicitly bypass enhancement\r\n\r\n## Enhancement Rules for CleanConnect v2.0\r\n\r\n### Mandatory Fields to Add:\r\n1. **Business Context**: Why this matters for the founder\r\n2. **Risk Assessment**: Risk level and mitigation strategies\r\n3. **Phase Number**: From plan/PLAN_INDEX.md (not just V1)\r\n4. **Dependencies**: What needs to be done first\r\n5. **Confidence Level**: 1-10 scale for success\r\n\r\n### Auto-Correction Logic:\r\n- If request is vague → Enhance with business context\r\n- If request lacks risk → Add risk assessment\r\n- If request jumps ahead → Realign to current phase\r\n- If request is too broad → Break into smaller tasks\r\n- If request lacks testing → Add comprehensive testing strategy\r\n- If request ignores constraints → Add technical constraints section\r\n\r\n### Memory Integration:\r\n- Check `.windsurf/active/activeContext.md` for current work\r\n- Reference previous decisions from memory bank\r\n- Maintain continuity across sessions\r\n- Update memory after task completion\r\n\r\n### Founder-Friendly Output:\r\n- Use analogies instead of technical terms\r\n- Focus on outcomes and business value\r\n- Provide clear next steps\r\n- Include celebration points for progress\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n- This skill runs before any other processing\r\n- The enhanced request becomes the new prompt for Cascade\r\n- Users can still manually invoke with @request-enhancer\r\n- Enhancements are conservative - when in doubt, keep it simple\r\n- v2.0 includes improved business focus and risk management\r\n- Integrated with memory bank for context continuity\r\n- Designed specifically for non-technical founder workflow\r\n\r\n## Version History\r\n\r\n- v1.0: Initial implementation with basic enhancement\r\n- v2.0: Added business focus, risk assessment, memory integration, and founder-friendly communication\r\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:56:47.381Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, and Claude Code needing advanced request clarification and structuring for optimal SaaS development and vibe coding","zh":"非常适合像Cursor、Windsurf和Claude Code这样的AI代理，需要高级请求澄清和结构化以实现最佳的SaaS开发和vibe编码","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、Claude CodeなどのAIエージェントに最適で、最適なSaaS開発とVibeコーディングのために高度なリクエストの明確化と構造化が必要","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 최적의 SaaS 개발과바이브 코딩을 위해 고급 요청澄清 및 구조화가 필요","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf y Claude Code que necesitan una clarificación y estructuración de solicitudes avanzadas para un desarrollo de SaaS óptimo y codificación de vibración","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf et Claude Code nécessitant une clarification et une structuration de demandes avancées pour un développement SaaS optimal et une codification de vibe","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf und Claude Code, die eine erweiterte Anfrageklärung und -strukturierung für eine optimale SaaS-Entwicklung und Vibe-Codierung benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf e Claude Code que necessitam de esclarecimento e estruturação avançados de solicitações para desenvolvimento de SaaS otimizado e codificação de vibração","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf и Claude Code, требующих расширенного уточнения и структуризации запросов для оптимального развития SaaS и виброкодирования","ar":"مثالي لعميل آي آي مثل Cursor و Windsurf و Claude Code الذين يحتاجون إلى توضيح وتشكيل متقدم للطلبات من أجل تطوير برنامج معالجة الخدمات وترميز الاهتزاز الأمثل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform user requests into well-structured prompts with enhanced clarity, context, and risk assessment, leveraging CleanConnect memory bank system and automatic V1 checklist mapping for streamlined development","zh":"赋予代理将用户请求转化为结构清晰、上下文明确、风险评估增强的提示，利用CleanConnect内存银行系统和自动V1检查清单映射进行流畅开发","ja":"エージェントがユーザーのリクエストを明確性、コンテキスト、リスク評価の強化された構造化されたプロンプトに変換できるようにし、CleanConnectメモリバンクシステムと自動V1チェックリストマッピングを使用して開発をストリームライン化","ko":"에이전트가 사용자 요청을 명확성, contexto, 리스크 평가가 강화된 구조화된 프롬프트로 변환할 수 있도록 하며, CleanConnect 메모리 뱅크 시스템과 자동 V1 체크리스트 매핑을 사용하여 개발을 원활하게进行","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar las solicitudes de los usuarios en instrucciones bien estructuradas con una claridad, contexto y evaluación de riesgos mejorados, aprovechando el sistema de banco de memoria CleanConnect y el mapeo de lista de verificación automática V1 para un desarrollo optimizado","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer les demandes des utilisateurs en invites bien structurées avec une clarté, un contexte et une évaluation des risques améliorés, en exploitant le système de banque de mémoire CleanConnect et la mise en correspondance automatique de la liste de vérification V1 pour un développement optimisé","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Benutzeranfragen in gut strukturierte Aufforderungen mit verbesserter Klarheit, Kontext und Risikobewertung umzuwandeln, indem es das CleanConnect-Speichersystem und die automatische V1-Prüfliste-Zuordnung für eine optimierte Entwicklung nutzt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar solicitações de usuário em prompts bem estruturados com clareza, contexto e avaliação de risco aprimorados, utilizando o sistema de banco de memória CleanConnect e mapeamento automático de lista de verificação V1 para desenvolvimento em fluxo contínuo","ru":"Позволяет агентам преобразовывать запросы пользователей в хорошо структурированные подсказки с улучшенной ясностью, контекстом и оценкой риска, используя систему банка памяти CleanConnect и автоматическое сопоставление контрольного списка V1 для оптимизированного развития","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تحويل طلبات المستخدم إلى توجيهات منظمة جيدًا مع وضوح وسياق وتقييم مخاطر محسّن، باستخدام نظام بنك الذاكرة CleanConnect وتنفيذ تلقائي للخارطة البديلة V1 من أجل تطوير سلس"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating request enhancement for non-technical founders","Generating detailed prompts with integrated risk mitigation strategies","Structuring requests for optimal AI assistance in SaaS platforms"],"zh":["为非技术创始人自动增强请求","生成具有集成风险缓解策略的详细提示","为SaaS平台的最佳AI辅助结构请求"],"ja":["非技術の創設者向けのリクエスト強化の自動化","統合リスク緩和戦略を備えた詳細なプロンプトの生成","SaaSプラットフォームにおける最適なAIアシストのためのリクエスト構造化"],"ko":["비기술 창립자를 위한 요청 향상 자동화","통합 리스크 완화 전략을 갖춘 상세한 프롬프트 생성","SaaS 플랫폼에서 최적의 AI 보조를 위한 요청 구조화"],"es":["Automatizar la mejora de solicitudes para fundadores no técnicos","Generar instrucciones detalladas con estrategias de mitigación de riesgos integradas","Estructurar solicitudes para una asistencia de IA óptima en plataformas SaaS"],"fr":["Automatiser l''amélioration des demandes pour les fondateurs non techniques","Générer des invites détaillées avec des stratégies de mitigation des risques intégrées","Structurer les demandes pour une assistance IA optimale sur les plateformes SaaS"],"de":["Automatisierung der Anfrageverbesserung für nicht-technische Gründer","Erzeugen detaillierter Aufforderungen mit integrierten Risikominderungsstrategien","Strukturieren von Anfragen für eine optimale KI-Unterstützung in SaaS-Plattformen"],"pt":["Automatizar a melhoria de solicitações para fundadores não técnicos","Gerar prompts detalhados com estratégias de mitigação de riscos integradas","Estruturar solicitações para assistência de IA otimizada em plataformas SaaS"],"ru":["Автоматизировать улучшение запросов для не технических основателей","Генерировать подробные подсказки с интегрированными стратегиями смягчения рисков","Структурировать запросы для оптимальной помощи ИИ на платформах SaaS"],"ar":["أتمتة تحسين الطلبات للأصحاب غير التقنيين","إنتاج توجيهات مفصلة مع استراتيجيات تخفيف المخاطر المتكاملة","هيكلة الطلبات من أجل مساعدة آي آي أمثل في منصات السaaS"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with CleanConnect memory bank system","Optimized for non-technical founders and SaaS development"],"zh":["需要集成CleanConnect内存银行系统","针对非技术创始人和SaaS开发进行优化"],"ja":["CleanConnectメモリバンクシステムとの統合が必要","非技術の創設者とSaaS開発のために最適化"],"ko":["CleanConnect 메모리 뱅크 시스템과의 통합이 필요","비기술 창립자와 SaaS 개발을 위해 최적화"],"es":["Requiere integración con el sistema de banco de memoria CleanConnect","Optimizado para fundadores no técnicos y desarrollo de SaaS"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec le système de banque de mémoire CleanConnect","Optimisé pour les fondateurs non techniques et le développement de SaaS"],"de":["Erfordert Integration mit dem CleanConnect-Speichersystem","Optimiert für nicht-technische Gründer und SaaS-Entwicklung"],"pt":["Requer integração com o sistema de banco de memória CleanConnect","Otimizado para fundadores não técnicos e desenvolvimento de SaaS"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с системой банка памяти CleanConnect","Оптимизирован для не технических основателей и развития SaaS"],"ar":["يتطلب تكاملًا مع نظام بنك الذاكرة CleanConnect","مُحسّن للاصحاب غير التقنيين وتطوير برنامج معالجة الخدمات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Ejyke90/naija-conflict-tracker/openspec-explore', 'community', 'Ejyke90', 'naija-conflict-tracker', 'Ejyke90/naija-conflict-tracker', 'openspec-explore', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z', '2026-02-18T09:56:55.916Z', NULL, '{"id":"Ejyke90/naija-conflict-tracker/openspec-explore","name":"openspec-explore","description":{"zh":"openspec-explore 模式允许您探索代码库，思考和设计，创建 OpenSpec 文档，但不允许实现代码","ja":"openspec-explore モードでは、コードベースを探索し、思考と設計を行い、OpenSpec ドキュメントを作成できますが、コードの実装はできません","ko":"openspec-explore 모드에서는 코드베이스를 탐색하고 생각하고 설계하고 OpenSpec 문서를 생성할 수 있지만 코드를 구현할 수 없습니다","es":"openspec-explore es un modo de exploración que permite a los desarrolladores pensar libremente y visualizar sin implementar código. Permite la creación de artefactos OpenSpec como propuestas y diseños","fr":"openspec-explore est un mode d''exploration qui permet aux développeurs de réfléchir librement et de visualiser sans implémenter de code. Il permet la création d''artefacts OpenSpec tels que des propositions et des conceptions","de":"openspec-explore ist ein Entdeckungsmodus, der es Entwicklern ermöglicht, frei zu denken und zu visualisieren, ohne Code zu implementieren. Er ermöglicht die Erstellung von OpenSpec-Artefakten wie Vorschlägen und Entwürfen","pt":"O openspec-explore é um modo de exploração que permite aos desenvolvedores pensar e visualizar livremente sem implementar código. Ele é ideal para investigar a base de código e criar artefatos OpenSpec.","ru":"Openspec-explore - это режим исследования, который позволяет разработчикам свободно мыслить и визуализировать без реализации кода. Он идеален для изучения кодовой базы и создания артефактов OpenSpec.","ar":"openspec-explore هو وضع الاستكشاف الذي يسمح للمطورين بالتفكير والتصور بحرية دون تنفيذ التعليمات البرمجية. إنه مثالي للتحقيق في قاعدة الشفرة وإنشاء مواصفات مفتوحة.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-explore 模式：探索与思考","ja":"openspec-explore モード：探索と思考","ko":"openspec-explore 모드: 탐색 및 사고","es":"openspec-explore: Modo de exploración para desarrolladores","fr":"openspec-explore : Mode d''exploration pour les développeurs","de":"openspec-explore: Entdeckungsmodus für Entwickler","pt":"openspec-explore: Modo de Exploração para Desenvolvedores","ru":"openspec-explore: Режим исследования для разработчиков","ar":"openspec-explore: وضع الاستكشاف لل مطورين","en":"openspec-explore"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-explore 模式允许您探索代码库，思考和设计，创建 OpenSpec 文档，但不允许实现代码","ja":"openspec-explore モードでは、コードベースを探索し、思考と設計を行い、OpenSpec ドキュメントを作成できますが、コードの実装はできません","ko":"openspec-explore 모드에서는 코드베이스를 탐색하고 생각하고 설계하고 OpenSpec 문서를 생성할 수 있지만 코드를 구현할 수 없습니다","es":"openspec-explore es un modo de exploración que permite a los desarrolladores pensar libremente y visualizar sin implementar código. Permite la creación de ar...","fr":"openspec-explore est un mode d''exploration qui permet aux développeurs de réfléchir librement et de visualiser sans implémenter de code. Il permet la créatio...","de":"openspec-explore ist ein Entdeckungsmodus, der es Entwicklern ermöglicht, frei zu denken und zu visualisieren, ohne Code zu implementieren. Er ermöglicht die...","pt":"O openspec-explore é um modo de exploração que permite aos desenvolvedores pensar e visualizar livremente sem implementar código. Ele é ideal para investigar...","ru":"Openspec-explore - это режим исследования, который позволяет разработчикам свободно мыслить и визуализировать без реализации кода. Он идеален для изучения ко...","ar":"openspec-explore هو وضع الاستكشاف الذي يسمح للمطورين بالتفكير والتصور بحرية دون تنفيذ التعليمات البرمجية. إنه مثالي للتحقيق في قاعدة الشفرة وإنشاء مواصفات مف...","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["探索代码库","思考和设计","创建 OpenSpec 文档","不允许实现代码","支持搜索代码","支持阅读文件"],"ja":["コードベースを探索する","思考と設計を行う","OpenSpec ドキュメントを作成する","コードの実装をしない","コードの検索をサポートする","ファイルの読み取りをサポートする"],"ko":["코드베이스를 탐색한다","생각하고 설계한다","OpenSpec 문서를 생성한다","코드를 구현하지 않는다","코드 검색을 지원한다","파일 읽기를 지원한다"],"es":["Modo de exploración para desarrolladores","Permite la creación de artefactos OpenSpec","No requiere implementación de código","Permite la investigación y visualización de la base de código","Soporta la creación de propuestas y diseños"],"fr":["Mode d''exploration pour les développeurs","Permet la création d''artefacts OpenSpec","N''exige pas d''implémentation de code","Permet la recherche et la visualisation de la base de code","Prend en charge la création de propositions et de conceptions"],"de":["Entdeckungsmodus für Entwickler","Ermöglicht die Erstellung von OpenSpec-Artefakten","Erfordert keine Code-Implementierung","Ermöglicht die Recherche und Visualisierung der Codebasis","Unterstützt die Erstellung von Vorschlägen und Entwürfen"],"pt":["Permite pensar e visualizar livremente sem implementar código","Ideal para investigar a base de código","Criação de artefatos OpenSpec","Não permite a escrita de código","Permite a leitura de arquivos e busca de código"],"ru":["Позволяет свободно мыслить и визуализировать без реализации кода","Идеален для изучения кодовой базы","Создание артефактов OpenSpec","Не позволяет писать код","Позволяет читать файлы и искать код"],"ar":["يسمح بالتفكير والتصور بحرية دون تنفيذ التعليمات البرمجية","مثالي للتحقيق في قاعدة الشفرة","إنشاء مواصفات مفتوحة","لا يسمح بكتابة التعليمات البرمجية","يسمح بقراءة الملفات و البحث عن التعليمات البرمجية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-explore","代码库探索","思考和设计","OpenSpec 文档","代码实现","搜索代码","阅读文件","开发者工具"],"ja":["openspec-explore","コードベース探索","思考と設計","OpenSpec ドキュメント","コード実装","コード検索","ファイル読み取り","開発者ツール"],"ko":["openspec-explore","코드베이스 탐색","생각과 설계","OpenSpec 문서","코드 구현","코드 검색","파일 읽기","개발자 도구"],"es":["openspec-explore","modo de exploración","desarrolladores","artefactos OpenSpec","investigación de código","visualización de código","creación de propuestas","creación de diseños"],"fr":["openspec-explore","mode d''exploration","développeurs","artefacts OpenSpec","recherche de code","visualisation de code","création de propositions","création de conceptions"],"de":["openspec-explore","Entdeckungsmodus","Entwickler","OpenSpec-Artefakte","Code-Recherche","Code-Visualisierung","Vorschlagserstellung","Entwurfsstellung"],"pt":["openspec-explore","modo de exploração","desenvolvedores","investigação de código","artefatos OpenSpec","desenvolvimento de software","engenharia de software"],"ru":["openspec-explore","режим исследования","разработчики","исследование кода","артефакты OpenSpec","разработка программного обеспечения","инженерия программного обеспечения"],"ar":["openspec-explore","وضع الاستكشاف","المطورين","التحقيق في الشفرة","مواصفات مفتوحة","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"Ejyke90","repo":"naija-conflict-tracker","repoPath":"Ejyke90/naija-conflict-tracker","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-explore","description":"Enter explore mode - a thinking partner for exploring ideas, investigating problems, and clarifying requirements. Use when the user wants to think through something before or during a change.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Enter explore mode. Think deeply. Visualize freely. Follow the conversation wherever it goes.\n\n**IMPORTANT: Explore mode is for thinking, not implementing.** You may read files, search code, and investigate the codebase, but you must NEVER write code or implement features. If the user asks you to implement something, remind them to exit explore mode first (e.g., start a change with `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff`). You MAY create OpenSpec artifacts (proposals, designs, specs) if the user asks—that''s c","body":"Enter explore mode. Think deeply. Visualize freely. Follow the conversation wherever it goes.\n\n**IMPORTANT: Explore mode is for thinking, not implementing.** You may read files, search code, and investigate the codebase, but you must NEVER write code or implement features. If the user asks you to implement something, remind them to exit explore mode first (e.g., start a change with `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff`). You MAY create OpenSpec artifacts (proposals, designs, specs) if the user asks—that''s capturing thinking, not implementing.\n\n**This is a stance, not a workflow.** There are no fixed steps, no required sequence, no mandatory outputs. You''re a thinking partner helping the user explore.\n\n---\n\n## The Stance\n\n- **Curious, not prescriptive** - Ask questions that emerge naturally, don''t follow a script\n- **Open threads, not interrogations** - Surface multiple interesting directions and let the user follow what resonates. Don''t funnel them through a single path of questions.\n- **Visual** - Use ASCII diagrams liberally when they''d help clarify thinking\n- **Adaptive** - Follow interesting threads, pivot when new information emerges\n- **Patient** - Don''t rush to conclusions, let the shape of the problem emerge\n- **Grounded** - Explore the actual codebase when relevant, don''t just theorize\n\n---\n\n## What You Might Do\n\nDepending on what the user brings, you might:\n\n**Explore the problem space**\n- Ask clarifying questions that emerge from what they said\n- Challenge assumptions\n- Reframe the problem\n- Find analogies\n\n**Investigate the codebase**\n- Map existing architecture relevant to the discussion\n- Find integration points\n- Identify patterns already in use\n- Surface hidden complexity\n\n**Compare options**\n- Brainstorm multiple approaches\n- Build comparison tables\n- Sketch tradeoffs\n- Recommend a path (if asked)\n\n**Visualize**\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│     Use ASCII diagrams liberally        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                         │\n│   ┌────────┐         ┌────────┐        │\n│   │ State  │────────▶│ State  │        │\n│   │   A    │         │   B    │        │\n│   └────────┘         └────────┘        │\n│                                         │\n│   System diagrams, state machines,      │\n│   data flows, architecture sketches,    │\n│   dependency graphs, comparison tables  │\n│                                         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Surface risks and unknowns**\n- Identify what could go wrong\n- Find gaps in understanding\n- Suggest spikes or investigations\n\n---\n\n## OpenSpec Awareness\n\nYou have full context of the OpenSpec system. Use it naturally, don''t force it.\n\n### Check for context\n\nAt the start, quickly check what exists:\n```bash\nopenspec list --json\n```\n\nThis tells you:\n- If there are active changes\n- Their names, schemas, and status\n- What the user might be working on\n\n### When no change exists\n\nThink freely. When insights crystallize, you might offer:\n\n- \"This feels solid enough to start a change. Want me to create one?\"\n  → Can transition to `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff`\n- Or keep exploring - no pressure to formalize\n\n### When a change exists\n\nIf the user mentions a change or you detect one is relevant:\n\n1. **Read existing artifacts for context**\n   - `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`\n   - `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`\n   - `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`\n   - etc.\n\n2. **Reference them naturally in conversation**\n   - \"Your design mentions using Redis, but we just realized SQLite fits better...\"\n   - \"The proposal scopes this to premium users, but we''re now thinking everyone...\"\n\n3. **Offer to capture when decisions are made**\n\n   | Insight Type | Where to Capture |\n   |--------------|------------------|\n   | New requirement discovered | `specs/<capability>/spec.md` |\n   | Requirement changed | `specs/<capability>/spec.md` |\n   | Design decision made | `design.md` |\n   | Scope changed | `proposal.md` |\n   | New work identified | `tasks.md` |\n   | Assumption invalidated | Relevant artifact |\n\n   Example offers:\n   - \"That''s a design decision. Capture it in design.md?\"\n   - \"This is a new requirement. Add it to specs?\"\n   - \"This changes scope. Update the proposal?\"\n\n4. **The user decides** - Offer and move on. Don''t pressure. Don''t auto-capture.\n\n---\n\n## What You Don''t Have To Do\n\n- Follow a script\n- Ask the same questions every time\n- Produce a specific artifact\n- Reach a conclusion\n- Stay on topic if a tangent is valuable\n- Be brief (this is thinking time)\n\n---\n\n## Handling Different Entry Points\n\n**User brings a vague idea:**\n```\nUser: I''m thinking about adding real-time collaboration\n\nYou: Real-time collab is a big space. Let me think about this...\n\n      COLLABORATION SPECTRUM\n      ════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n      Awareness          Coordination         Sync\n          │                   │                 │\n          ▼                   ▼                 ▼\n      ┌────────┐         ┌────────┐        ┌────────┐\n      │Presence│         │Cursors │        │  CRDT  │\n      │  \"3    │         │ Multi  │        │Conflict│\n      │online\" │         │ select │        │  free  │\n      └────────┘         └────────┘        └────────┘\n          │                   │                 │\n       trivial            moderate           complex\n\n      Where''s your head at?\n```\n\n**User brings a specific problem:**\n```\nUser: The auth system is a mess\n\nYou: [reads codebase]\n\n     ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n     │              CURRENT AUTH FLOW              │\n     └─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                        │\n          ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐\n          ▼             ▼             ▼\n     ┌─────────┐  ┌─────────┐  ┌─────────┐\n     │ Google  │  │  GitHub │  │  Email  │\n     │  OAuth  │  │  OAuth  │  │  Magic  │\n     └────┬────┘  └────┬────┘  └────┬────┘\n          │             │             │\n          └─────────────┼─────────────┘\n                        ▼\n                  ┌───────────┐\n                  │  Session  │\n                  └─────┬─────┘\n                        │\n                        ▼\n                  ┌───────────┐\n                  │   Perms   │\n                  └───────────┘\n\n     I see three tangles. Which one''s burning?\n```\n\n**User is stuck mid-implementation:**\n```\nUser: /opsx:explore add-auth-system\n      The OAuth integration is more complex than expected\n\nYou: [reads change artifacts]\n\n     You''re on task 4: \"Implement OAuth flow\"\n\n     Let me trace what''s involved...\n\n     [draws diagram, explores options, suggests paths]\n\n     Want to update the design to reflect this?\n     Or add a spike task to investigate?\n```\n\n**User wants to compare options:**\n```\nUser: Should we use Postgres or SQLite?\n\nYou: Generic answer is boring. What''s the context?\n\nUser: A CLI tool that tracks local dev environments\n\nYou: That changes everything.\n\n     ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n     │         CLI TOOL DATA STORAGE                  │\n     └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n     Key constraints:\n     • No daemon running\n     • Must work offline\n     • Single user\n\n                  SQLite          Postgres\n     Deployment   embedded ✓      needs server ✗\n     Offline      yes ✓           no ✗\n     Single file  yes ✓           no ✗\n\n     SQLite. Not even close.\n\n     Unless... is there a sync component?\n```\n\n---\n\n## Ending Discovery\n\nThere''s no required ending. Discovery might:\n\n- **Flow into action**: \"Ready to start? /opsx:new or /opsx:ff\"\n- **Result in artifact updates**: \"Updated design.md with these decisions\"\n- **Just provide clarity**: User has what they need, moves on\n- **Continue later**: \"We can pick this up anytime\"\n\nWhen it feels like things are crystallizing, you might summarize:\n\n```\n## What We Figured Out\n\n**The problem**: [crystallized understanding]\n\n**The approach**: [if one emerged]\n\n**Open questions**: [if any remain]\n\n**Next steps** (if ready):\n- Create a change: /opsx:new <name>\n- Fast-forward to tasks: /opsx:ff <name>\n- Keep exploring: just keep talking\n```\n\nBut this summary is optional. Sometimes the thinking IS the value.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Don''t implement** - Never write code or implement features. Creating OpenSpec artifacts is fine, writing application code is not.\n- **Don''t fake understanding** - If something is unclear, dig deeper\n- **Don''t rush** - Discovery is thinking time, not task time\n- **Don''t force structure** - Let patterns emerge naturally\n- **Don''t auto-capture** - Offer to save insights, don''t just do it\n- **Do visualize** - A good diagram is worth many paragraphs\n- **Do explore the codebase** - Ground discussions in reality\n- **Do question assumptions** - Including the user''s and your own\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:56:55.916Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Conceptual Agents needing advanced open-specification exploration and proposal generation capabilities.","zh":"适用于需要高级开放规范探索和提案生成能力的概念代理。","ja":"概念エージェントが高度なオープン仕様の探索と提案の生成機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"개념 에이전트가 고급开放规格 탐색 및 제안 생성 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes conceptuales que necesitan una exploración de especificación abierta avanzada y capacidades de generación de propuestas.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents conceptuels ayant besoin d''une exploration de spécification ouverte avancée et de capacités de génération de propositions.","de":"Ideal für konzeptionelle Agenten, die eine erweiterte offene Spezifikations-Exploration und Vorschlagsgenerierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Conceituais que necessitam de exploração de especificação aberta avançada e capacidades de geração de propostas.","ru":"Идеально для Концептуальных Агентов, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности исследования открытой спецификации и генерации предложений.","ar":"مثالي لعميل المفاهيم الذي يحتاج إلى استكشاف مواصفات مفتوحة متقدمة وقدرات توليد مقترحات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to think deeply and visualize freely, creating OpenSpec artifacts like proposals, designs, and specs, while investigating codebases and searching code without implementing features, utilizing file reading and code search protocols.","zh":"赋予代理深入思考和自由可视化的能力，创建开放规范文档，如提案、设计和规格，同时调查代码库并使用文件读取和代码搜索协议搜索代码，而无需实现功能。","ja":"エージェントに深く考え、自由に視覚化し、提案、設計、仕様などのOpenSpecアーティファクトを作成する能力を与え、コードベースを調査し、ファイル読み取りとコード検索プロトコルを使用してコードを検索しますが、機能を実装することはありません。","ko":"에이전트가 깊이 생각하고 자유롭게 시각화하여 오픈 규격 아티팩트를 생성 할 수있는 능력을 부여하여 코드베이스를 조사하고 파일 읽기 및 코드 검색 프로토콜을 사용하여 코드를 검색하지만 기능을 구현하지는 않습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes pensar profundamente y visualizar con libertad, creando artefactos OpenSpec como propuestas, diseños y especificaciones, mientras investigan repositorios de código y buscan código sin implementar características, utilizando protocolos de lectura de archivos y búsqueda de código.","fr":"Permet aux agents de réfléchir profondément et de visualiser librement, créant des artefacts OpenSpec tels que des propositions, des conceptions et des spécifications, tout en explorant les bases de code et en recherchant du code sans implémenter de fonctionnalités, en utilisant des protocoles de lecture de fichiers et de recherche de code.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, tief zu denken und frei zu visualisieren, indem sie OpenSpec-Artefakte wie Vorschläge, Entwürfe und Spezifikationen erstellen, während sie Codebasen untersuchen und Code suchen, ohne Funktionen zu implementieren, unter Verwendung von Dateilese- und Codesuche-Protokollen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a pensar profundamente e visualizar livremente, criando artefatos OpenSpec como propostas, projetos e especificações, enquanto investigam repositórios de código e procuram código sem implementar recursos, utilizando protocolos de leitura de arquivos e pesquisa de código.","ru":"Наделяет агентов способностью глубоко думать и свободно визуализировать, создавая артефакты OpenSpec, такие как предложения, проекты и спецификации, при этом исследуя кодовые базы и ища код без реализации функций, используя протоколы чтения файлов и поиска кода.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على التفكير بعمق والتصور بحرية، مما يخلق أشياء مفتوحة مثل المقترحات والتصاميم والمواصفات، في حين يقوم بالتحقيق في قواعد البيانات و البحث عن الكود دون تنفيذ الميزات، باستخدام بروتوكولات قراءة الملفات و البحث عن الكود."},"useCases":{"en":["Investigating codebases for potential improvements","Generating OpenSpec proposals for new features","Creating detailed design specs for complex systems"],"zh":["调查代码库以查找潜在的改进点","为新功能生成开放规范提案","为复杂系统创建详细的设计规格"],"ja":["潜在的な改善点を探すためのコードベースの調査","新しい機能のためのオープン仕様提案の生成","複雑なシステムの詳細な設計仕様の作成"],"ko":[" 잠재적인 개선점을 찾기위한 코드베이스 조사","새로운 기능에 대한 오픈 규격 제안 생성","복잡한 시스템에 대한 자세한 설계 사양 생성"],"es":["Investigar repositorios de código para mejoras potenciales","Generar propuestas OpenSpec para nuevas características","Crear especificaciones de diseño detalladas para sistemas complejos"],"fr":["Explorer les bases de code pour améliorations potentielles","Générer des propositions OpenSpec pour de nouvelles fonctionnalités","Créer des spécifications de conception détaillées pour des systèmes complexes"],"de":["Untersuchen von Codebasen für potenzielle Verbesserungen","Generieren von OpenSpec-Vorschlägen für neue Funktionen","Erstellen detaillierter Entwurfspezifikationen für komplexe Systeme"],"pt":["Investigação de repositórios de código para melhorias potenciais","Geração de propostas OpenSpec para novos recursos","Criação de especificações de projeto detalhadas para sistemas complexos"],"ru":["Изучение кодовых баз для потенциальных улучшений","Генерация предложений OpenSpec для новых функций","Создание подробных технических спецификаций для сложных систем"],"ar":["التحقيق في قواعد البيانات للتحسينات المحتملة","توليد مقترحات مفتوحة للميزات الجديدة","إنشاء مواصفات تصميم مفصلة لأنظمة معقدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Must not write code or implement features in explore mode","Requires user to exit explore mode for implementation using commands like /opsx:new or /opsx:ff"],"zh":["探索模式下不能编写代码或实现功能","需要用户退出探索模式以使用命令（如/opsx：new或/opsx：ff）进行实现"],"ja":["探索モードではコードを書いたり機能を実装したりできない","実装のために/opsx：newまたは/opsx：ffなどのコマンドを使用して探索モードを終了するためにユーザーが退出する必要がある"],"ko":["탐색 모드에서는 코드를 작성하거나 기능을 구현할 수 없음","구현을 위해 /opsx：new 또는 /opsx：ff와 같은 명령을 사용하여 탐색 모드를終了하기 위해 사용자가退出해야 함"],"es":["No debe escribir código ni implementar características en el modo de exploración","Requiere que el usuario salga del modo de exploración para la implementación utilizando comandos como /opsx:new o /opsx:ff"],"fr":["Ne doit pas écrire de code ni implémenter de fonctionnalités en mode d''exploration","Requiert que l''utilisateur quitte le mode d''exploration pour l''implémentation en utilisant des commandes comme /opsx:new ou /opsx:ff"],"de":["Darf keinen Code schreiben oder Funktionen in Explorationsmodus implementieren","Benötigt, dass der Benutzer den Explorationsmodus verlässt, um die Implementierung mithilfe von Befehlen wie /opsx:new oder /opsx:ff durchzuführen"],"pt":["Não deve escrever código ou implementar recursos no modo de exploração","Exige que o usuário saia do modo de exploração para implementação usando comandos como /opsx:new ou /opsx:ff"],"ru":["Не должно писать код или реализовывать функции в режиме исследования","Требует от пользователя выхода из режима исследования для реализации с использованием команд, таких как /opsx:new или /opsx:ff"],"ar":["لا يجب أن يكتب الكود أو ينفذ الميزات في وضع الاستكشاف","يتطلب من المستخدم الخروج من وضع الاستكشاف للتطبيق باستخدام أوامر مثل /opsx:new أو /opsx:ff"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
