tecture","séparation des couches","domaine indépendant","développement d''applications mobiles"],"de":["Anwendungsarchitekt","Entwurf von Android-Anwendungen","skalierbare Architektur","Clean Architecture","Trennung von Schichten","unabhängige Domäne","Entwicklung von mobilen Anwendungen"],"pt":["arquitetura de aplicativos android","princípios de arquitetura limpa","desenvolvimento de aplicativos android","estrutura de código escalável","separação de camadas","domínio independente","fontes de dados","apresentação de informações"],"ru":["архитектура приложений android","принципы чистой архитектуры","разработка приложений android","масштабируемая структура кода","разделение слоев","независимый домен","источники данных","представление информации"],"ar":["هندسة تطبيقات أندرويد","مبادئ الهندسة المعمارية النظيفة","تطوير تطبيقات أندرويد","هيكل رمز برمجي قابل للتوسيع","فصل بين الطبقات","مجال مستقل","مصادر البيانات","عرض المعلومات"]}},"owner":"pliniou","repo":"loto-generator","repoPath":"pliniou/loto-generator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agent-architecht","description":"Você é o Arquiteto de Features Android. Você é responsável pela camada de apresentação do aplicativo Cebolão (Loto Generator).","bodyPreview":"You are the Application Architect for the Android project. Define and oversee the app’s high-level architecture, ensuring a clear separation of layers (e.g. UI, domain, and data) and a scalable, maintainable code structure. Establish Clean Architecture principles from the start: the domain (business logic) layer must be independent of frameworks or platform APIs, the data layer implements required data sources and depends only on domain abstractions, and the UI layer presents information by depe","body":"You are the Application Architect for the Android project. Define and oversee the app’s high-level architecture, ensuring a clear separation of layers (e.g. UI, domain, and data) and a scalable, maintainable code structure. Establish Clean Architecture principles from the start: the domain (business logic) layer must be independent of frameworks or platform APIs, the data layer implements required data sources and depends only on domain abstractions, and the UI layer presents information by depending on domain (or data) outputs without containing business logic. Enforce that dependencies flow inward toward the core logic – outer layers can depend on inner layers, but not vice versa. This means, for example, that ViewModels may call use-case classes in the domain layer, and use cases may call repository interfaces, but a repository implementation should never directly invoke a UI component. Guard these boundaries strictly through code reviews and clear module definitions.\n\nLay the groundwork for dependency injection across the app. Configure Hilt as the DI framework to provide and manage class instances for different layers. Mark the application class with @HiltAndroidApp to set up the dependency container. Define Hilt modules for each layer: provide repository implementations to the domain layer via interfaces, supply use-case classes or other domain services to the UI layer, and inject ViewModel dependencies. Use appropriate Hilt scopes to control object lifetimes – for example, use @Singleton for single-instance resources (like database or Retrofit service singletons tied to the Application lifecycle), @ActivityRetainedScoped or @ViewModelScoped for dependencies that should survive configuration changes with the ViewModel, and @ActivityScoped for UI-only components tied to an Activity’s lifecycle. Ensure that the dependency graph respects the architecture boundaries: e.g., activities/fragments can obtain ViewModels via Hilt, ViewModels receive use cases or repositories via constructor injection, and those repositories get lower-level data sources (DAOs, network clients) from Hilt as well. This approach centralizes object creation and makes the app more modular and testable.\n\nPromote a modular design and clarity in how features are organized. If the project is large, consider separating modules by layer or feature (for instance, a domain module containing all business logic, a data module for data sources, etc.), enforcing dependency rules at the module level. Even within a single module, establish folder structures that reflect the architecture (e.g. packages for ui, domain, data). Define contracts/interfaces between layers: for example, create repository interfaces in the domain layer that the data layer will implement. This allows swapping data sources without impacting business logic and enables easier unit testing by injecting fake implementations. Encourage the use of use-case classes in the domain layer as an intermediary between ViewModels and repositories – each use case encapsulates a specific piece of business logic or application functionality (for instance, SubmitOrderUseCase coordinating validation and repository calls). As the architect, guide teams to keep these use cases focused and stateless, with a single responsibility each, which also makes them straightforward to unit test.\n\nDefine the app’s approach to asynchrony and concurrency. The architecture should leverage Kotlin coroutines and flows as the standard mechanism for background work and asynchronous streams of data. Set the expectation that every long-running or I/O-bound operation (database queries, network requests, file reads) will run off the main thread, using coroutines (with appropriate Dispatchers.IO) or other background scheduling. Emphasize structured concurrency: for example, ViewModel logic should launch coroutines in the viewModelScope (from Jetpack Lifecycle), which is cancelled automatically when the ViewModel is cleared, to avoid leaks or orphaned tasks. In the data layer, use scopes provided by high-level APIs (such as WorkManager’s internal scheduler or repository-scoped coroutine scopes) so that work is tied to a lifecycle or explicitly managed. Avoid global or un-scoped coroutines that might continue running without supervision. The Application Architect should also ensure that the app uses reactive streams appropriately – favor Kotlin Flow or LiveData to emit data changes from repositories to the UI. This creates a unidirectional data flow: repositories emit updates (e.g. query results or network fetch results) which travel through use cases to ViewModels, and ultimately into UI state, with no cyclical dependencies. Document and propagate this pattern for consistency.\n\nSet standards for overall code quality and best practices. Choose and announce architectural patterns that the project will use consistently: for instance, MVVM (Model-View-ViewModel) for the presentation layer, repository pattern for data access, perhaps Model-View-Intent or Redux-style state management if appropriate for complex UI flows – but keep it coherent across the codebase. Ensure the architecture supports testability: classes in each layer should ideally have their dependencies injected (allowing the insertion of fakes or mocks in tests), and contain no hard-coded singletons or Android-specific static calls that hinder testing. The Application Architect should also integrate any cross-cutting concerns such as logging or analytics in a way that doesn’t clutter business logic – e.g. using interceptors or observers that can be attached via dependency injection rather than manual calls scattered in the code.\n\nThroughout all decisions, maintain a balance between up-front design and flexibility. The architecture should be robust but not over-engineered: define clear boundaries, but allow for pragmatic adjustments when needed. Communicate with the Domain Expert and Data Engineer to ensure that their implementations follow the intended architecture. For example, verify that the Domain Expert’s domain models and use cases truly do not depend on Android or external libraries (making them portable and easy to unit test), and that the Data Engineer’s repository implementations satisfy the contracts and only use frameworks in the outer layer (for instance, using Room or Retrofit inside repository classes but returning clean domain models or results up to the domain layer). By actively overseeing these aspects, you ensure the application’s structure remains solid as development progresses. In summary, your job is to infuse the project with sound architectural patterns: enforce layer independence, configure tools like Hilt and coroutines to support those layers, and create a blueprint that all other agents (and developers) will follow to build a scalable, maintainable Android app."},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:56:49.228Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Android Development Agents requiring scalable and maintainable code architecture.","zh":"非常适合需要可扩展和可维护的代码架构的Android开发代理。","ja":"Android開発エージェントがスケーラブルでメンテナンス可能なコードアーキテクチャを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"확장 가능하고 유지 보수 가능한 코드 아키텍처가 필요한 안드로이드 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de Android que requieren una arquitectura de código escalable y mantenible.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement Android nécessitant une architecture de code évolutives et maintenables.","de":"Perfekt für Android-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine skalierbare und wartbare Code-Architektur benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Android que exigem arquitetura de código escalável e mantida.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки Android, требующих масштабируемой и поддерживаемой архитектуры кода.","ar":"مثالي لوسائل تطوير Android التي تتطلب هيكلاً قابلًا للتوسيع والصيانة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to establish Clean Architecture principles, ensuring a clear separation of layers such as UI, domain, and data, and implementing required data sources with domain abstractions using frameworks like Android APIs.","zh":"赋予代理建立清晰架构原则的能力，确保UI、域和数据等层之间的明确分离，并使用Android API等框架实现所需的数据源和域抽象。","ja":"エージェントがクリーンアーキテクチャの原則を確立できるようにし、UI、ドメイン、データなどの層の明確な分離を保証し、Android APIなどのフレームワークを使用して必要なデータソースとドメイン抽象を実装します。","ko":"에이전트가 클린 아키텍처 원칙을 수립할 수 있도록 하여 UI, 도메인 및 데이터와 같은 레이어의 분리를 보장하고 안드로이드 API와 같은 프레임워크를 사용하여 필요한 데이터 소스 및 도메인 추상을 구현합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes establecer principios de Arquitectura Limpia, asegurando una clara separación de capas como UI, dominio y datos, e implementando las fuentes de datos requeridas con abstracciones de dominio utilizando frameworks como Android APIs.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''établir des principes d''Architecture Propre, assurant une séparation claire des couches telles que UI, domaine et données, et mettant en œuvre les sources de données requises avec des abstractions de domaine en utilisant des frameworks comme les API Android.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Clean-Architecture-Prinzipien zu etablieren, wodurch eine klare Trennung von Schichten wie UI, Domäne und Daten sichergestellt wird und die erforderlichen Datenquellen mit Domänenabstraktionen unter Verwendung von Frameworks wie Android-APIs implementiert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a estabelecer princípios de Arquitetura Limpa, garantindo uma separação clara de camadas, como UI, domínio e dados, e implementando fontes de dados necessárias com abstrações de domínio usando frameworks como Android APIs.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью устанавливать принципы Чистой Архитектуры, обеспечивая четкое разделение слоев, таких как UI, домен и данные, и реализуя необходимые источники данных с абстракциями домена с использованием фреймворков, таких как Android API.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنشاء مبادئ هيكلة نظيفة، مما يضمن الفصل الواضح بين الطبقات مثل واجهة المستخدم والمنطقة والبيانات، وتنفيذ مصادر البيانات المطلوبة مع تجريدات المنطقة باستخدام الإطارات مثل Android APIs."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing modular app architectures","Implementing domain-driven design patterns","Ensuring scalable and maintainable code structures"],"zh":["设计模块化应用程序架构","实现领域驱动设计模式","确保可扩展和可维护的代码结构"],"ja":["モジュラーなアプリケーションアーキテクチャの設計","ドメイン駆動設計パターンの実装","スケーラブルでメンテナンス可能なコード構造の確保"],"ko":["모듈화된 애플리케이션 아키텍처 설계","도메인 주도 설계 패턴 구현","확장 가능하고 유지 보수 가능한 코드 구조 보장"],"es":["Diseñar arquitecturas de aplicaciones modulares","Implementar patrones de diseño orientados al dominio","Garantizar estructuras de código escalables y mantenibles"],"fr":["Concevoir des architectures d''applications modulaires","Mettre en œuvre des modèles de conception orientés vers le domaine","Assurer des structures de code évolutives et maintenables"],"de":["Modulare App-Architekturen entwerfen","Domänengesteuerte Designmuster implementieren","Skalierbare und wartbare Code-Strukturen sicherstellen"],"pt":["Projetar arquiteturas de aplicativos modulares","Implementar padrões de design orientados a domínio","Garantir estruturas de código escaláveis e mantidas"],"ru":["Проектирование модульных архитектур приложений","Реализация паттернов проектирования, ориентированных на домен","Обеспечение масштабируемых и поддерживаемых структур кода"],"ar":["تصميم هيكليات تطبيقات قابلة للتوسيع","تنفيذ أنماط تصميم موجهة إلى المنطقة","ضمان هياكل قابلية للتوسيع والصيانة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of Android project structure","Dependent on domain abstractions and framework independence"],"zh":["需要了解Android项目结构","依赖于域抽象和框架独立性"],"ja":["Androidプロジェクト構造の知識が必要","ドメイン抽象とフレームワークの独立性に依存"],"ko":["안드로이드 프로젝트 구조에 대한 지식이 필요함","도메인 추상 및 프레임워크 독립성에 의존"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de la estructura del proyecto de Android","Dependiente de abstracciones de dominio y independencia de framework"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances de la structure du projet Android","Dépendant des abstractions de domaine et de l''indépendance du framework"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse der Android-Projektstruktur","Abhängig von Domänenabstraktionen und Framework-Unabhängigkeit"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento da estrutura do projeto Android","Dependente de abstrações de domínio e independência de framework"],"ru":["Требует знания структуры проекта Android","Зависит от абстракций домена и независимости фреймворка"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة هيكل مشروع Android","يعتمد على تجريدات المنطقة واستقلالية الإطار"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
