de contradicciones de biomas","Identificación del write path correcto","Bloqueo del write path en el punto de estrangulamiento más seguro","Soporte para mundos de estilo globo","Funcionamiento determinista"],"fr":["Résolution des contradictions de biomes","Identification du write path correct","Blocage du write path au point de strangulation le plus sûr","Prise en charge des mondes de style globe","Fonctionnement déterministe"],"de":["Lösung von Biom-Konflikten","Identifizierung des richtigen Write-Pfads","Blockierung des Write-Pfads am sichersten Engpass","Unterstützung für Globus-Style-Welten","Deterministisches Verhalten"],"pt":["Biomas determinísticos baseados em latitude","Resolução de contradições de biomas","Compatibilidade com mundos de estilo globo","Regras de superfície personalizáveis","Suporte a blocos e biomas personalizados"],"ru":["Детерминированные биомы на основе широты","Решение противоречий биомов","Совместимость с мирами стиля глобуса","Настраиваемые правила поверхности","Поддержка пользовательских блоков и биомов"],"ar":["بيئات محددة بالاتجاه","حل تعارضات البيئات","توافق مع عوالم نمط الكرة الأرضية","قواعد سطح قابلة للتعديل","دعم الكتل والبيئات المخصصة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Minecraft Fabric 模组","latitude-write-path-guards","生物群落带","方块异常","globe-style 世界","Minecraft 模组开发","Fabric 模组"],"ja":["Minecraft Fabric モッド","latitude-write-path-guards","バイオームバンド","ブロックの異常","globe-style 世界","Minecraft モッド開発","Fabric モッド"],"ko":["Minecraft Fabric 모드","latitude-write-path-guards","생물군계 대역","블록異常","globe-style 세계","Minecraft 모드 개발","Fabric 모드"],"es":["Minecraft Fabric mod","biomas deterministas","write path","contradicciones de biomas","mundos de estilo globo","mods de Minecraft"],"fr":["mod Minecraft Fabric","biomes déterministes","write path","contradictions de biomes","mondes de style globe","mods Minecraft"],"de":["Minecraft Fabric-Mod","deterministische Biome","Write-Pfad","Biom-Konflikte","Globus-Style-Welten","Minecraft-Mods"],"pt":["Minecraft Fabric","mod latitude-write-path-guards","biomas determinísticos","mundos de estilo globo","regras de superfície","blocos personalizados","biomas personalizados"],"ru":["Minecraft Fabric","мод latitude-write-path-guards","детерминированные биомы","миры стиля глобуса","правила поверхности","пользовательские блоки","пользовательские биомы"],"ar":["ماينكرافت فابريك","مود latitude-write-path-guards","بيئات محددة","عوالم نمط الكرة الأرضية","قواعد السطح","كتل مخصصة","بيئات مخصصة"]}},"owner":"joolbits","repo":"latitude","repoPath":"joolbits/latitude","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"latitude-write-path-guards","description":"Canonical debugging + fix strategy for “wrong blocks in the wrong place” bugs. Forces evidence-first identification of the write path and mandates minimal, choke-point fixes (feature cancel / ChunkRegion / ProtoChunk). Forbids guessing via biome reassignment or pipeline invention.","bodyPreview":"# Latitude — Write-Path Guards (Authoritative)\n\nThis skill is used when:\n- a block appears where it should be impossible (snow/powder snow in warm bands, ice in tropics, etc.)\n- a “biome says X but blocks say Y” contradiction occurs\n- a symptom persists despite precipitation/surface-rule changes\n\n**Core rule:** Do not guess the cause. Identify the **write path** that placed the block, then block/rewrite it at the narrowest safe choke point.\n\n---\n\n## Definitions\n- **Base biome:** vanilla biome se","body":"# Latitude — Write-Path Guards (Authoritative)\n\nThis skill is used when:\n- a block appears where it should be impossible (snow/powder snow in warm bands, ice in tropics, etc.)\n- a “biome says X but blocks say Y” contradiction occurs\n- a symptom persists despite precipitation/surface-rule changes\n\n**Core rule:** Do not guess the cause. Identify the **write path** that placed the block, then block/rewrite it at the narrowest safe choke point.\n\n---\n\n## Definitions\n- **Base biome:** vanilla biome selection prior to Latitude override (often logged as `base=`).\n- **Out biome:** Latitude-selected biome returned to generation (often logged as `out=` / what F3 shows).\n- **Write path:** the actual code path that calls `setBlockState` to place the offending block.\n\n---\n\n## Mandatory protocol (evidence-first)\n\n### Step 1 — Capture the symptom precisely\nRecord:\n- offending block(s) (e.g., `powder_snow`, `snow_block`)\n- coords (x,y,z)\n- F3 biome (out biome)\n- zone/band if available\n\nNo fix proposals until these exist.\n\n### Step 2 — Determine write path\nAllowed methods (choose the least invasive that gives proof):\n\n**A) Single-shot logs (preferred)**\n- Add a guard that logs once when it sees the offending block type.\n- Include:\n  - block id\n  - pos\n  - band/zone result\n  - (optional) chunk origin\n\n**B) Stack trace capture (nuclear, one-time)**\n- On first sighting, throw a controlled exception or log a stack trace.\n- Use only once, then remove.\n\n**C) Counter overlay**\n- Maintain counters for:\n  - calls\n  - matches\n  - rewrites\n- Expose via debug HUD/actionbar behind a flag.\n\n---\n\n## Allowed choke points (use this order)\n\n### 1) Feature-level cancel (best when a known offender exists)\nExamples:\n- `FreezeTopLayerFeature` (snow/ice)\n- other single features when proven by stack trace\n\nRule:\n- Cancel only in the disallowed bands/zones.\n- Log once behind a debug flag.\n\n### 2) `ChunkRegion#setBlockState` rewrite (best general guard)\n- Catches many feature/placement writes during generation.\n- Use `@ModifyVariable` or `@Redirect` carefully.\n- Must be non-recursive.\n\n### 3) `ProtoChunk#setBlockState` rewrite (good for direct chunk writes)\n- Catches many worldgen surface placements.\n- Often simpler than MaterialRules interception.\n\n### 4) Biome precipitation hooks (last resort, limited scope)\n- Only affects weather-driven snow layers / precipitation checks.\n- Does not stop worldgen-placed `snow_block` or `powder_snow`.\n\n---\n\n## Band/zone gating rules (no hardcoding)\nWarm-band detection must:\n- derive radius from world border:\n  - `radius = world.getWorldBorder().getSize() * 0.5` \n- compute:\n  - `t = abs(z) / radius` \n- determine zone using the same helper/constants used by Latitude (do not duplicate thresholds unless unavoidable).\n\nIf a helper is not available, the assistant must:\n- locate it in code first, or\n- mark thresholds as UNKNOWN and ask for the file/constant.\n\n---\n\n## Canonical rewrite policy (snow family)\nWhen in warm bands (equator/tropics/subtropics as defined by Latitude):\n\n- `POWDER_SNOW` -> `AIR` \n- `SNOW` (layer) -> `AIR` \n- `SNOW_BLOCK` -> `DIRT` above sea level, else `STONE` \n\nAll logging must be behind `-Dlatitude.debugSnowGuard=true` (or equivalent).\n\n---\n\n## Required safety constraints\n- Guard must be **non-recursive** (do not call the same setBlockState path in a way that re-triggers).\n- Guard must be band-gated (never global nukes unless explicitly set as a one-run diagnostic).\n- Debug output must be gated and off by default for release.\n- Fix must not change biome eligibility tables to hide the symptom.\n\n---\n\n## Forbidden fixes\n- “Just move snowy biomes out of warm bands” (unless authority table explicitly says so)\n- Reordering worldgen stages without proof\n- Intercepting deep MaterialRules nested types unless all choke points above are proven insufficient\n- Shipping with debug spam enabled\n\n---\n\n## Output format expected from the assistant\nWhen asked to fix a block-placement bug, the assistant must produce:\n\n1) **Hypothesis list** (max 3) tied to evidence\n2) **Chosen choke point** and why\n3) **Exact file(s) + mixin target + method descriptor**\n4) **One commit plan** + test step\n5) **Rollback path** (revert commit / toggle flag)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:56:08.240Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Minecraft Fabric modding agents needing deterministic latitude-based biome management.","zh":"非常适合需要确定性纬度基于生物群落管理的Minecraft Fabric模组代理。","ja":"Minecraft Fabricモッドのエージェントが決定論的な緯度に基づくバイオーム管理を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"결정론적 위도 기반 생물군계 관리가 필요한 Minecraft Fabric 모드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de modificación de Minecraft Fabric que necesitan una gestión de biomas determinista basada en latitud.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de modification Minecraft Fabric qui ont besoin d''une gestion de biomes déterministe basée sur la latitude.","de":"Perfekt für Minecraft Fabric-Modding-Agents, die eine deterministische Breiten-basierte Biomanagement benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de modding Minecraft Fabric que necessitam de gerenciamento de biomas baseado em latitude determinístico.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов моддинга Minecraft Fabric, требующих детерминированного управления биомами на основе широты.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة المناطق الحيوية القائمة على خط العرض بشكل محدد في تعديلات ماين كرافت فابريك."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce deterministic latitude-based biome bands for globe-style worlds, resolving contradictions between biomes and block placements using write-path guards, and leveraging core rules to identify and rewrite blocks at the narrowest safe choke point, ensuring consistency with vanilla biome settings and precipitation/surface rules.","zh":"赋予代理执行确定性纬度基于生物群落带的能力，用于全球风格的世界，使用写路径守卫解决生物群落和方块放置之间的矛盾，并利用核心规则来识别和重写方块在最狭窄的安全瓶颈点，确保与原版生物群落设置和降水/表面规则的一致性。","ja":"決定論的な緯度に基づくバイオームバンドをグローブスタイルのワールドに適用する機能をエージェントに与え、バイオームとブロックの配置の矛盾を書き込みパスガードを使用して解決し、コアルールを使用してブロックを最も狭い安全なボトルネックポイントで識別して書き直すことで、バニラバイオーム設定と降水/表面ルールとの一致性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 결정론적 위도 기반 생물군계 띠를 구형 세계에 적용할 수 있는 기능을 제공하여, 쓰기 경로 감시자를 사용하여 생물군계와 블록 배치 간의 모순을 해결하고, 핵심 규칙을 사용하여 블록을 가장 좁은 안전한 병목 지점에서 식별하고 다시 작성하여, 바닐라 생물군계 설정 및 강수/표면 규칙과 일관성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar bandas de biomas deterministas basadas en la latitud para mundos de estilo globo, resolviendo contradicciones entre biomas y colocaciones de bloques utilizando guardias de ruta de escritura, y aprovechando las reglas básicas para identificar y reescribir bloques en el punto de estrangulamiento más seguro y estrecho, garantizando la consistencia con la configuración de biomas y reglas de precipitación/superficie de vanilla.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des bandes de biomes déterministes basées sur la latitude pour les mondes de style globe, en résolvant les contradictions entre les biomes et les placements de blocs à l''aide de gardes de chemin d''écriture, et en exploitant les règles de base pour identifier et réécrire les blocs au point de contrainte le plus étroit et le plus sûr, garantissant la cohérence avec les paramètres de biomes et les règles de précipitation/surface de vanilla.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, deterministische Breiten-basierte Biome-Bänder für Globus-Style-Welten durchzusetzen, Widersprüche zwischen Biomen und Blockplatzierungen unter Verwendung von Schreibpfadwächtern aufzulösen und Kernregeln zu nutzen, um Blöcke am schmalsten sicheren Engpass zu identifizieren und neu zu schreiben, um die Konsistenz mit Vanilla-Biome-Einstellungen und Niederschlags/Oberflächenregeln sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor bandas de biomas baseadas em latitude de forma determinística para mundos do tipo globo, resolvendo contradições entre biomas e posicionamentos de blocos usando guardas de caminho de escrita, e aproveitando regras centrais para identificar e reescrever blocos no ponto de estrangulamento seguro mais estreito, garantindo consistência com configurações de bioma vanilla e regras de precipitação/superfície.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью устанавливать детерминированные латитудные биомные полосы для миров в стиле глобуса, разрешая противоречия между биомами и блоками с помощью охранников записи пути, и используя основные правила для выявления и переписывания блоков в самой узкой безопасной точке сужения, обеспечивая согласованность с настройками биома vanilla и правилами осадков/поверхности.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من فرض حزم المناطق الحيوية القائمة على خط العرض بشكل محدد لمundos من نوع الكرة الأرضية، وحل التناقضات بين المناطق الحيوية وتركيب الكتل باستخدام حارس مسار الكتابة، واستغلال القواعد الأساسية لتحديد وإعادة كتابة الكتل في نقطة الخنق الأكثر أمانًا، وضمان الاتساق مع إعدادات المناطق الحيوية الفانيليا وقواعد الهطول/السطح."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging biome-block contradictions in Minecraft Fabric mods","Enforcing deterministic latitude-based biome bands for custom globe-style worlds","Resolving symptoms persisting despite precipitation/surface-rule changes"],"zh":["调试Minecraft Fabric模组中的生物群落-方块矛盾","执行自定义全球风格世界中的确定性纬度基于生物群落带","解决尽管降水/表面规则更改仍然存在的症状"],"ja":["Minecraft Fabricモッドのバイオームとブロックの矛盾をデバッグする","カスタムグローブスタイルワールドの決定論的な緯度に基づくバイオームバンドを適用する","降水/表面ルールの変更にもかかわらず残っている症状を解決する"],"ko":["Minecraft Fabric 모드의 생물군계-블록 모순을 디버깅하는 것","사용자 정의 구형 세계의 결정론적 위도 기반 생물군계 띠를 적용하는 것","강수/표면 규칙이 변경되더라도 남아있는 증상을 해결하는 것"],"es":["Depuración de contradicciones entre biomas y bloques en mods de Minecraft Fabric","Aplicación de bandas de biomas deterministas basadas en la latitud para mundos de estilo globo personalizados","Resolución de síntomas persistentes a pesar de los cambios en las reglas de precipitación/superficie"],"fr":["Débogage des contradictions entre les biomes et les blocs dans les mods Minecraft Fabric","Application de bandes de biomes déterministes basées sur la latitude pour des mondes de style globe personnalisés","Résolution des symptômes persistants malgré les modifications des règles de précipitation/surface"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung bei Widersprüchen zwischen Biomen und Blöcken in Minecraft Fabric-Mods","Durchsetzung deterministischer Breiten-basierter Biome-Bänder für benutzerdefinierte Globus-Style-Welten","Auflösung persistierender Symptome trotz Änderungen an den Niederschlags-/Oberflächenregeln"],"pt":["Depuração de contradições entre biomas e blocos em mods Minecraft Fabric","Impor bandas de biomas baseadas em latitude de forma determinística para mundos personalizados do tipo globo","Resolução de sintomas persistentes apesar das alterações nas regras de precipitação/superfície"],"ru":["Отладка противоречий между биомами и блоками в модах Minecraft Fabric","Установление детерминированных латитудных биомных полос для пользовательских миров в стиле глобуса","Разрешение симптомов, сохраняющихся несмотря на изменения в правилах осадков/поверхности"],"ar":["تصحيح التناقضات بين المناطق الحيوية والكتل في تعديلات ماين كرافت فابريك","فرض حزم المناطق الحيوية القائمة على خط العرض بشكل محدد لمundos مخصصة من نوع الكرة الأرضية","حل الأعراض التي تستمر على الرغم من التغييرات في قواعد الهطول/السطح"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Minecraft Fabric modding environment","Limited to globe-style worlds","Dependent on vanilla biome settings and core rules"],"zh":["需要Minecraft Fabric模组环境","仅限全球风格世界","依赖于原版生物群落设置和核心规则"],"ja":["Minecraft Fabricモッド環境が必要","グローブスタイルワールドのみ","バニラバイオーム設定とコアルールに依存"],"ko":["Minecraft Fabric 모드 환경이 필요","구형 세계만 해당","바닐라 생물군계 설정 및 핵심 규칙에 의존"],"es":["Requiere entorno de modificación de Minecraft Fabric","Limitado a mundos de estilo globo","Dependiente de la configuración de biomas y reglas básicas de vanilla"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement de modification Minecraft Fabric","Limité aux mondes de style globe","Dépendant des paramètres de biomes et des règles de base de vanilla"],"de":["Benötigt Minecraft Fabric-Modding-Umgebung","Begrenzt auf Globus-Style-Welten","Abhängig von Vanilla-Biome-Einstellungen und Kernregeln"],"pt":["Exige ambiente de modding Minecraft Fabric","Limitado a mundos do tipo globo","Dependente de configurações de bioma vanilla e regras centrais"],"ru":["Требует среды моддинга Minecraft Fabric","Ограничен мировыми глобусами","Зависит от настроек биома vanilla и основных правил"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة تعديل ماين كرافت فابريك","محدود بمundos من نوع الكرة الأرضية","يعتمد على إعدادات المناطق الحيوية الفانيليا والقواعد الأساسية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Ejyke90/naija-conflict-tracker/openspec-onboard', 'community', 'Ejyke90', 'naija-conflict-tracker', 'Ejyke90/naija-conflict-tracker', 'openspec-onboard', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z', '2026-02-18T09:56:57.594Z', NULL, '{"id":"Ejyke90/naija-conflict-tracker/openspec-onboard","name":"openspec-onboard","description":{"zh":"本指南将引导您完成OpenSpec的第一个工作流程循环，包括初始化和运行","ja":"OpenSpecの最初のワークフローを通じて、プロジェクトを開始する方法を学びます","ko":"OpenSpec의 첫 번째 작업 흐름을 통해 초기화 및 실행 방법을 학습합니다","es":"OpenSpec Onboard es una guía que te lleva a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec. Incluye una experiencia de enseñanza práctica","fr":"OpenSpec Onboard est un guide qui vous accompagne tout au long de votre premier cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec. Il inclut une expérience d''enseignement pratique","de":"OpenSpec Onboard ist eine Anleitung, die Sie durch Ihren ersten kompletten OpenSpec-Arbeitsablauf führt. Enthält eine praktische Lernerfahrung","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que leva você através do seu primeiro ciclo de trabalho completo com OpenSpec, ensinando cada etapa do processo.","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard - это руководство, которое ведет вас через ваш первый полный цикл работы с OpenSpec, обучая каждому шагу процесса.","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يأخذك في جولة خلال دورة عمل OpenSpec الكاملة الأولى ، مع شرح كل خطوة في العملية.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenSpec入门指南","ja":"OpenSpecを開始する","ko":"OpenSpec 시작 가이드","es":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guía de inicio","fr":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guide de démarrage","de":"OpenSpec Onboard: Einrichtungsanleitung","pt":"OpenSpec Onboard: Guia de Inicialização","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard: Руководство по настройке","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard: دليل الإعداد","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"本指南将引导您完成OpenSpec的第一个工作流程循环，包括初始化和运行","ja":"OpenSpecの最初のワークフローを通じて、プロジェクトを開始する方法を学びます","ko":"OpenSpec의 첫 번째 작업 흐름을 통해 초기화 및 실행 방법을 학습합니다","es":"OpenSpec Onboard es una guía que te lleva a través de tu primer ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec. Incluye una experiencia de enseñanza práctica","fr":"OpenSpec Onboard est un guide qui vous accompagne tout au long de votre premier cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec. Il inclut une expérience d''enseigneme...","de":"OpenSpec Onboard ist eine Anleitung, die Sie durch Ihren ersten kompletten OpenSpec-Arbeitsablauf führt. Enthält eine praktische Lernerfahrung","pt":"O OpenSpec Onboard é um guia que leva você através do seu primeiro ciclo de trabalho completo com OpenSpec, ensinando cada etapa do processo.","ru":"OpenSpec Onboard - это руководство, которое ведет вас через ваш первый полный цикл работы с OpenSpec, обучая каждому шагу процесса.","ar":"OpenSpec Onboard هو دليل يأخذك في جولة خلال دورة عمل OpenSpec الكاملة الأولى ، مع شرح كل خطوة في العملية.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["初始化OpenSpec","运行OpenSpec工作流程","检查OpenSpec状态","自动化任务","提高开发效率"],"ja":["OpenSpecの初期化","OpenSpecワークフローの実行","OpenSpecの状態を確認","タスクの自動化","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["OpenSpec 초기화","OpenSpec 작업 흐름 실행","OpenSpec 상태 확인","작업 자동화","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Guía paso a paso para configurar OpenSpec","Experiencia de enseñanza práctica en el código","Verificación del estado de inicialización de OpenSpec","Flujo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec"],"fr":["Guide étape par étape pour configurer OpenSpec","Expérience d''enseignement pratique dans le code","Vérification de l''état d''initialisation d''OpenSpec","Flux de travail complet avec OpenSpec"],"de":["Schritt-für-Schritt-Anleitung zur Konfiguration von OpenSpec","Praktische Lernerfahrung im Code","Überprüfung des Initialisierungsstatus von OpenSpec","Kompletter Arbeitsablauf mit OpenSpec"],"pt":["Verificação de inicialização do OpenSpec","Execução do comando `openspec init`","Ciclo de trabalho completo com OpenSpec","Explicação passo a passo do processo","Trabalho real no código do usuário"],"ru":["Проверка инициализации OpenSpec","Выполнение команды `openspec init`","Полный цикл работы с OpenSpec","Пошаговое объяснение процесса","Реальная работа над кодом пользователя"],"ar":["التحقق من إعداد OpenSpec","تشغيل الأمر `openspec init`","دورة عمل كاملة مع OpenSpec","شرح خطوة بخطوة للعملية","العمل الفعلي على رمز المستخدم"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","工作流程管理","自动化任务","开发工具","开发效率","初始化OpenSpec","运行OpenSpec"],"ja":["OpenSpec","ワークフロー管理","タスクの自動化","開発ツール","開発効率","OpenSpecの初期化","OpenSpecの実行"],"ko":["OpenSpec","워크플로우 관리","작업 자동화","개발 도구","개발 효율성","OpenSpec 초기화","OpenSpec 실행"],"es":["OpenSpec","desarrollo de software","flujo de trabajo","configuración","guía de inicio","ciclo de trabajo","desarrolladores"],"fr":["OpenSpec","développement de logiciels","flux de travail","configuration","guide de démarrage","cycle de travail","développeurs"],"de":["OpenSpec","Software-Entwicklung","Arbeitsablauf","Konfiguration","Einrichtungsanleitung","Arbeitszyklus","Entwickler"],"pt":["OpenSpec","inicialização","configuração","ciclo de trabalho","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["OpenSpec","инициализация","настройка","цикл работы","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["OpenSpec","الإعداد","التكوين","دورة العمل","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"Ejyke90","repo":"naija-conflict-tracker","repoPath":"Ejyke90/naija-conflict-tracker","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:56:57.594Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing guided OpenSpec workflow integration.","zh":"非常适合需要指导式OpenSpec工作流集成的开发代理","ja":"OpenSpecワークフローの統合をガイドする必要がある開発エージェントに最適","ko":"개발 에이전트가 가이드된 OpenSpec 워크플ロー 통합을 필요로 할 때 완벽함","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan integración de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec guiada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une intégration de workflow OpenSpec guidée.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine guidierte OpenSpec-Workflow-Integration benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de integração de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec orientada.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходима интеграция рабочего процесса OpenSpec с руководством.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى تكامل تدفق عمل OpenSpec الموجه."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to navigate the OpenSpec initialization process, execute status checks via `openspec status --json`, and handle conditional initialization with `openspec init`, streamlining project setup and workflow management.","zh":"赋予代理导航OpenSpec初始化过程的能力，通过`openspec status --json`执行状态检查，并通过`openspec init`处理有条件的初始化，从而简化项目设置和工作流管理","ja":"`openspec status --json`経由でステータスチェックを実行し、`openspec init`経由で条件付き初期化を処理することで、OpenSpecの初期化プロセスをエージェントがナビゲートできるようにし、プロジェクトの設定とワークフローの管理を効率化する","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 초기화过程을 탐색하고 `openspec status --json`을 통해 상태 확인을 수행하며 `openspec init`을 통해 조건부 초기화를 처리하여 프로젝트 설정 및 워크플로우 관리를简化할 수 있도록 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a navegar por el proceso de inicialización de OpenSpec, ejecutar controles de estado a través de `openspec status --json` y manejar la inicialización condicional con `openspec init`, racionalizando la configuración del proyecto y la administración del flujo de trabajo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de naviguer dans le processus d''initialisation d''OpenSpec, d''exécuter des vérifications d''état via `openspec status --json` et de gérer l''initialisation conditionnelle avec `openspec init`, rationalisant ainsi la configuration du projet et la gestion du workflow.","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, den OpenSpec-Initialisierungsprozess zu navigieren, Statuschecks über `openspec status --json` auszuführen und bedingte Initialisierung mit `openspec init` zu handhaben, wodurch die Projektkonfiguration und die Workflowverwaltung rationalisiert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a navegar pelo processo de inicialização do OpenSpec, executar verificações de status por meio de `openspec status --json` e lidar com inicialização condicional com `openspec init`, racionalizando a configuração do projeto e o gerenciamento do fluxo de trabalho.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью ориентироваться в процессе инициализации OpenSpec, выполнять проверки статуса через `openspec status --json` и обрабатывать условную инициализацию с помощью `openspec init`, оптимизируя настройку проекта и управление рабочим процессом.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من التنقل في عملية تهيئة OpenSpec، وتنفيذ فحص الحالة عبر `openspec status --json`، وتعامل التهيئة الشرطية مع `openspec init`، وتبسيط إعداد المشروع وإدارة تدفق العمل."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Debugging OpenSpec setup issues","Guiding users through first-time OpenSpec workflow cycles"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化OpenSpec","调试OpenSpec设置问题","引导用户完成首次OpenSpec工作流循环"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトでOpenSpecを初期化する","OpenSpecの設定に関する問題をデバッグする","ユーザーを最初のOpenSpecワークフロー周期に沿って導く"],"ko":["새로운 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","OpenSpec 설정 문제 디버깅","사용자를 첫 번째 OpenSpec 워크플로우 주기에 따라 안내"],"es":["Inicializar OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Depurar problemas de configuración de OpenSpec","Guía a los usuarios a través de los primeros ciclos de flujo de trabajo de OpenSpec"],"fr":["Initialiser OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Déboguer les problèmes de configuration d''OpenSpec","Guider les utilisateurs à travers les premiers cycles de workflow OpenSpec"],"de":["OpenSpec in neuen Projekten initialisieren","OpenSpec-Setup-Probleme debuggen","Benutzer durch die ersten OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklen führen"],"pt":["Inicializando OpenSpec em novos projetos","Depurando problemas de configuração do OpenSpec","Orientando usuários através dos primeiros ciclos de fluxo de trabalho do OpenSpec"],"ru":["Инициализация OpenSpec в новых проектах","Отладка проблем настройки OpenSpec","Руководство пользователями через первые циклы рабочего процесса OpenSpec"],"ar":["تثبيت OpenSpec في المشاريع الجديدة","تصحيح مشاكل إعداد OpenSpec","توجيه المستخدمين من خلال دورات العمل الأولية ل OpenSpec"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec installation","Project must support command-line interface for `openspec` commands"],"zh":["需要OpenSpec安装","项目必须支持命令行接口以使用`openspec`命令"],"ja":["OpenSpecのインストールが必要","プロジェクトが`openspec`コマンドを使用するためのコマンドラインインターフェースをサポートしている必要がある"],"ko":["OpenSpec 설치가 필요","프로젝트가 `openspec` 명령어를 사용하기 위한 명령줄 인터페이스를 지원해야 함"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de OpenSpec","El proyecto debe admitir la interfaz de línea de comandos para los comandos `openspec`"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation d''OpenSpec","Le projet doit prendre en charge l''interface de ligne de commande pour les commandes `openspec`"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von OpenSpec","Das Projekt muss die Kommandozeilenoberfläche für `openspec`-Befehle unterstützen"],"pt":["Requer instalação do OpenSpec","O projeto deve suportar interface de linha de comando para comandos `openspec`"],"ru":["Требуется установка OpenSpec","Проект должен поддерживать командную строку для команд `openspec`"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت OpenSpec","يجب أن يدعم المشروع واجهة سطر الأوامر لأوامر `openspec`"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
