Umgebungsanalyse vor Anwendung von Regeln","Kompatibilität mit Node/TS, PHP/Laravel und mehr"],"pt":["Fornece padrões de codificação básicos","Aplicável a todos os projetos","Independente da pilha de tecnologia","Fundamento para habilidades específicas de pilha","Orientações para análise de ambiente"],"ru":["Предоставляет основные стандарты кодирования","Применяется ко всем проектам","Независимо от технологической стека","Основание для навыков, специфичных для стека","Руководство по анализу окружения"],"ar":["يوفر معايير الترميز الأساسية","ينطبق على جميع المشاريع","بغض النظر عن حزمة التكنولوجيا","أساس للمهارات الخاصة بحزمة","إرشادات لتحليل البيئة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["项目标准","编码规范","代码效率","技术栈","代码质量","开发者工具","编码助手","代码优化"],"ja":["プロジェクト標準","コード規則","コード効率","テクノロジー・スタック","コード品質","開発者ツール","コードアシスト","コード最適化"],"ko":["프로젝트 표준","코딩 규칙","코드 효율성","기술 스택","코드 품질","개발자 도구","코딩 도우미","코드 최적화"],"es":["estándares de proyecto","codificación","desarrollo de software","IDE","programación","Node/TS","PHP/Laravel"],"fr":["normes de projet","codage","développement de logiciels","IDE","programmation","Node/TS","PHP/Laravel"],"de":["Projektstandards","Codierung","Software-Entwicklung","IDE","Programmierung","Node/TS","PHP/Laravel"],"pt":["padrões de projeto","codificação","desenvolvimento de software","tecnologia","programação","desenvolvedores"],"ru":["стандарты проектов","кодирование","разработка программного обеспечения","технологии","программирование","разработчики"],"ar":["معايير المشروع","الترميز","تطوير البرمجيات","التكنولوجيا","البرمجة","المطورون"]}},"owner":"teodevlor","repo":"agent-kit-skill","repoPath":"teodevlor/agent-kit-skill","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"project-standards","description":"Core coding standards, SOLID principles, Clean Code, and naming conventions. Use this skill for any coding task to ensure consistency.","bodyPreview":"# Project Standards\n\nThis skill provides the foundational coding standards that apply to ALL projects regardless of tech stack.\n\n## When to Use\n- Use this skill for ANY coding task\n- This skill is the foundation that other stack-specific skills build upon\n- Always read this skill FIRST before reading stack-specific skills\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Analyze Environment First\nBefore applying any rules, READ the dependency files:\n- `package.json` (Node/TS projects)\n- `composer.json` (PHP/Laravel)\n- `","body":"# Project Standards\n\nThis skill provides the foundational coding standards that apply to ALL projects regardless of tech stack.\n\n## When to Use\n- Use this skill for ANY coding task\n- This skill is the foundation that other stack-specific skills build upon\n- Always read this skill FIRST before reading stack-specific skills\n\n## Instructions\n\n### 1. Analyze Environment First\nBefore applying any rules, READ the dependency files:\n- `package.json` (Node/TS projects)\n- `composer.json` (PHP/Laravel)\n- `go.mod` (Go projects)\n- `requirements.txt` / `pyproject.toml` (Python)\n\n**Principle:** Respect legacy. If the project already uses a specific library, USE IT.\n\n---\n\n## SOLID Principles (Strict Enforcement)\n\n### S - Single Responsibility\nA class/function must have ONE and only ONE reason to change.\n- *Violation:* A `UserService` that handles DB queries AND sends Emails.\n- *Fix:* Split into `UserRepository` and `EmailNotificationService`.\n\n### O - Open/Closed\nOpen for extension, closed for modification. Use Interfaces/Abstract classes.\n\n### L - Liskov Substitution\nSubtypes must be substitutable for their base types.\n\n### I - Interface Segregation\nClients should not be forced to depend on interfaces they do not use. Split large interfaces.\n\n### D - Dependency Inversion\nDepend on abstractions, not concretions.\n- *Rule:* Always inject dependencies via Constructor. Never use `new Class()` inside business logic.\n\n---\n\n## Clean Code Core\n\n- **DRY (Don''t Repeat Yourself):** Logic duplicated > 2 times must be extracted.\n- **KISS (Keep It Simple, Stupid):** Simplest solution is usually best. Avoid Over-Engineering.\n- **YAGNI (You Ain''t Gonna Need It):** Do not implement features \"just in case\".\n\n---\n\n## Function/Method Rules\n\n- **Max Lines:** < 30 lines ideally.\n- **Max Params:** < 3 parameters. Use DTO/Object if more needed.\n- **No Boolean Flags:** Split functions instead of `createUser(isSuperAdmin: boolean)`.\n\n---\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n### By Language\n| Category | JS/TS | Python | Go | PHP |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Files | `kebab-case` | `snake_case` | `snake_case` | `PascalCase` |\n| Classes | `PascalCase` | `PascalCase` | `PascalCase` | `PascalCase` |\n| Functions | `camelCase` | `snake_case` | `camelCase` | `camelCase` |\n| Variables | `camelCase` | `snake_case` | `camelCase` | `$camelCase` |\n| Constants | `SCREAMING_SNAKE` | `SCREAMING_SNAKE` | `PascalCase` | `SCREAMING_SNAKE` |\n\n### Structural Naming\n- **Helpers:** Module-specific support. Location: `modules/<name>/helpers/`\n- **Common/Shared:** Generic reusable. Location: `src/common/` or `src/shared/`\n- **Services:** Must end with `Service`, `Handler`, or `UseCase`.\n- **DTOs/Types:** Must include suffix (e.g., `user.dto.ts`, `order_response.go`).\n\n---\n\n## Comments & Documentation\n\n### Commenting Rules\n- **Zero-Comment Policy:** Do not comment obvious code.\n- **Complex Logic Only:** Only comment algorithms or counter-intuitive decisions.\n- **NO ICONS/EMOJIS:** Absolutely NO decorations in comments. Raw text only.\n  - Bad: `// Fast calculation function`\n  - Good: `// Uses binary search for O(log n) complexity.`\n\n### Function Documentation (JSDoc/GoDoc/Docstring)\n- **Public API Only:** Only document exported functions.\n- **Concise:** 1-2 sentences max. Do not restate parameter names.\n\n```ts\n// Bad: Redundant\n/**\n * Adds two numbers.\n * @param a First number\n * @param b Second number\n * @returns The sum\n */\nconst add = (a: number, b: number) => a + b;\n\n// Good: Necessary context only\n/**\n * Calculates tax based on local VAT rules (2024 reform).\n */\nconst calculateTax = (price: number, region: string) => { ... }\n```\n\n---\n\n## RESTful API Standards\n\n### HTTP Verbs\n- `GET` - Read (Idempotent, Safe)\n- `POST` - Create\n- `PUT` - Full Update\n- `PATCH` - Partial Update\n- `DELETE` - Remove\n\n### Status Codes\n- `200 OK` - Success (Read/Update)\n- `201 Created` - Success (Create)\n- `204 No Content` - Success (Delete)\n- `400 Bad Request` - Validation Error\n- `401 Unauthorized` - Auth missing\n- `403 Forbidden` - No permission\n- `404 Not Found` - Resource not exist\n- `500 Internal Server Error` - App crash\n\n### Response Envelope\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {},\n  \"meta\": { \"page\": 1, \"limit\": 10, \"total\": 100 },\n  \"error\": { \"code\": \"ERROR_CODE\", \"message\": \"...\", \"details\": [] },\n  \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-20T10:00:00Z\"\n}\n```\n\n### URL Naming\n- Collection: `/users` (Plural, kebab-case)\n- Resource: `/users/123`\n- Sub-resource: `/users/123/orders`\n\n---\n\n## Database Standards\n\n- **Naming:** `snake_case` for tables/columns.\n- **Primary Keys:** UUID (distributed) or BigInt.\n- **Audit Fields:** `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at` mandatory.\n\n---\n\n## Folder Structure\n\n### Option A: Feature-based (Recommended)\n```\nsrc/\n├── features/\n│   ├── auth/\n│   │   ├── components/\n│   │   ├── hooks/\n│   │   ├── api/\n│   │   └── index.ts\n│   └── dashboard/\n```\n\n### Option B: Layer-based (Classic)\n```\nsrc/\n├── components/\n├── pages/\n├── services/\n├── utils/\n└── hooks/\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:57:37.658Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Coding Agents needing standardized project structures and tech stack-agnostic guidelines.","zh":"适合需要标准化项目结构和技术栈无关指导的编码代理。","ja":"標準化されたプロジェクト構造とテクノロジースタックに依存しないガイドラインを必要とするコーディングエージェントに最適です。","ko":"표준화된 프로젝트 구조와 기술 스택에 종속되지 않는 가이드라인이 필요한 코딩 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de codificación que necesitan estructuras de proyectos estandarizadas y directrices agnósticas de pila de tecnología.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de codage nécessitant des structures de projet standardisées et des directives agnostiques de pile de technologie.","de":"Perfekt für Codierungsagenten, die standardisierte Projektstrukturen und technologieunabhängige Richtlinien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Codificação que necessitam de estruturas de projeto padronizadas e diretrizes agnósticas de pilha de tecnologia.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов кодирования, которым требуются стандартизированные структуры проектов и руководства, независимые от технологического стека.","ar":"مثالي для وكلاء الترميز الذين يحتاجون إلى هياكل مشروع معيارية ومبادئ توجيهية غير معتمدة على مجموعة التكنولوجيا."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply foundational coding standards across projects, utilizing dependency files like package.json and composer.json, ensuring consistency and readability in codebases.","zh":"赋予代理应用程序在项目中应用基础编码标准的能力，利用依赖文件如package.json和composer.json，确保代码库的一致性和可读性。","ja":"エージェントがプロジェクト全体で基本的なコーディング標準を適用できるようにし、依存ファイル zoals package.json と composer.json を使用してコードベースの 一貫性と可読性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 프로젝트 전반에 걸쳐 기본 코딩 표준을 적용할 수 있도록 하며, 의존성 파일(package.json 및 composer.json)을 사용하여 코드베이스의 일관성과 가독성을确保합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar estándares de codificación fundamentales en todos los proyectos, utilizando archivos de dependencia como package.json y composer.json, garantizando la coherencia y la legibilidad en las bases de código.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des normes de codage fondamentales à tous les projets, en utilisant des fichiers de dépendance tels que package.json et composer.json, garantissant la cohérence et la lisibilité des bases de code.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, grundlegende Codierungsstandards auf alle Projekte anzuwenden, indem sie Abhängigkeitsdateien wie package.json und composer.json verwenden, um Konsistenz und Lesbarkeit in den Codebasen sicherzustellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar padrões de codificação fundamentais em projetos, utilizando arquivos de dependência como package.json e composer.json, garantindo consistência e legibilidade nos repositórios de código.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять основные стандарты кодирования в проектах, используя файлы зависимостей, такие как package.json и composer.json, обеспечивая согласованность и читаемость в кодовых базах.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية تطبيق معايير الترميز الأساسية عبر المشاريع، باستخدام ملفات الإعتماد مثل package.json و composer.json، مما يضمن الاتساق وقابلية القراءة في قواعد البيانات البرمجية."},"useCases":{"en":["Standardizing project directory structures","Validating code formatting for Node/TS and PHP/Laravel projects","Ensuring tech stack-agnostic coding best practices"],"zh":["标准化项目目录结构","验证 Node/TS 和 PHP/Laravel 项目的代码格式","确保技术栈无关的编码最佳实践"],"ja":["プロジェクトディレクトリ構造を標準化する","Node/TS と PHP/Laravel プロジェクトのコード形式を検証する","テクノロジースタックに依存しないコーディングベストプラクティスを確保する"],"ko":["프로젝트 디렉토리 구조를 표준화하는 것","Node/TS 및 PHP/Laravel 프로젝트의 코드 형식을 검증하는 것","기술 스택에 종속되지 않는 코딩 모범 사례를 보장하는 것"],"es":["Estructuración estandarizada de directorios de proyectos","Validación del formato de código para proyectos Node/TS y PHP/Laravel","Garantía de las mejores prácticas de codificación agnósticas de la pila de tecnología"],"fr":["Structuration standardisée des répertoires de projets","Validation du formatage de code pour les projets Node/TS et PHP/Laravel","Garantie des meilleures pratiques de codage agnostiques de la pile de technologie"],"de":["Standardisierte Projektverzeichnisstrukturen","Validierung der Codeformatierung für Node/TS- und PHP/Laravel-Projekte","Sicherstellung technologieunabhängiger Codierungsbest Practices"],"pt":["Padronização de estruturas de diretórios de projeto","Validação de formatação de código para projetos Node/TS e PHP/Laravel","Garantia de práticas de codificação agnósticas de pilha de tecnologia"],"ru":["Стандартизация структур директорий проекта","Валидация форматирования кода для проектов Node/TS и PHP/Laravel","Обеспечение технологически независимых лучших практик кодирования"],"ar":["معايير هياكل دليل المشروع","تحقق من تنسيق الرمز للمشاريع Node/TS و PHP/Laravel","ضمان أفضل الممارسات البرمجية غير المعتمدة على مجموعة التكنولوجيا"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to project dependency files","Limited to coding tasks and IDE integration"],"zh":["需要访问项目依赖文件","仅限于编码任务和 IDE 集成"],"ja":["プロジェクトの依存ファイルへのアクセスが必要","コーディングタスクと IDE 統合に限定される"],"ko":["프로젝트 의존성 파일에 액세스해야 함","코딩 작업 및 IDE 통합에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a archivos de dependencia del proyecto","Limitado a tareas de codificación y integración de IDE"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès aux fichiers de dépendance du projet","Limité aux tâches de codage et à l''intégration de l''IDE"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Projektabhängigkeitsdateien","Begrenzt auf Codieraufgaben und IDE-Integration"],"pt":["Requer acesso a arquivos de dependência do projeto","Limitado a tarefas de codificação e integração com IDE"],"ru":["Требует доступа к файлам зависимостей проекта","Ограничен задачами кодирования и интеграцией с IDE"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى ملفات الإعتماد للمشروع","محدود بمهمات الترميز وتكامل البيئة التطويرية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
