chen Backend und Frontend"],"pt":["Tauri Event System","desenvolvimento de aplicações","comunicação backend-frontend","emissão de eventos","ouvidor de eventos","Tauri","React","Rust"],"ru":["Система событий Tauri","разработка приложений","общение backend-frontend","эмиссия событий","слушатель событий","Tauri","React","Rust"],"ar":["نظام أحداث Tauri","تطوير التطبيقات","التواصل بين الخلفية والواجهة","إصدار الأحداث","مستمع الأحداث","Tauri","React","Rust"]}},"owner":"TheerasakPing","repo":"video-downloader-tauri","repoPath":"TheerasakPing/video-downloader-tauri","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tauri-event-system","description":"Advanced Tauri event patterns for bidirectional communication, streaming data, window-to-window messaging, and custom event handling","version":"1.0.0","tags":"","bodyPreview":"# Tauri Advanced Event System\n\n## Event Fundamentals\n\n### Backend → Frontend Events\n\n**Basic event emission**:\n```rust\nuse tauri::Window;\n\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn start_download(\n    url: String,\n    window: Window,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    window.emit(\"download-started\", url)\n        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n\n    // Perform download...\n\n    window.emit(\"download-complete\", \"Success\")\n        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())\n}\n```\n\n**Frontend listener**:\n```typescript\nimport { listen, Un","body":"# Tauri Advanced Event System\n\n## Event Fundamentals\n\n### Backend → Frontend Events\n\n**Basic event emission**:\n```rust\nuse tauri::Window;\n\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn start_download(\n    url: String,\n    window: Window,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    window.emit(\"download-started\", url)\n        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n\n    // Perform download...\n\n    window.emit(\"download-complete\", \"Success\")\n        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())\n}\n```\n\n**Frontend listener**:\n```typescript\nimport { listen, UnlistenFn } from ''@tauri-apps/api/event'';\n\nconst unlisten = await listen<string>(''download-started'', (event) => {\n    console.log(''Download started:'', event.payload);\n});\n\n// Clean up when done\nunlisten();\n```\n\n## Structured Event Payloads\n\n### Typed Events with Serde\n\n**Backend**:\n```rust\nuse serde::Serialize;\n\n#[derive(Serialize, Clone)]\nstruct ProgressEvent {\n    current: usize,\n    total: usize,\n    percentage: f64,\n    message: String,\n    speed_mbps: Option<f64>,\n}\n\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn download_file(\n    url: String,\n    window: Window,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    let total_size = get_file_size(&url).await?;\n\n    for chunk in 0..total_size {\n        // Download chunk...\n\n        let progress = ProgressEvent {\n            current: chunk,\n            total: total_size,\n            percentage: (chunk as f64 / total_size as f64) * 100.0,\n            message: format!(\"Downloading... {}/{}\", chunk, total_size),\n            speed_mbps: Some(calculate_speed()),\n        };\n\n        window.emit(\"download-progress\", progress)\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n    }\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n**Frontend**:\n```typescript\ninterface ProgressEvent {\n    current: number;\n    total: number;\n    percentage: number;\n    message: string;\n    speed_mbps?: number;\n}\n\nconst unlisten = await listen<ProgressEvent>(''download-progress'', (event) => {\n    const { current, total, percentage, message, speed_mbps } = event.payload;\n\n    updateProgressBar(percentage);\n    updateStatus(message);\n\n    if (speed_mbps) {\n        updateSpeed(speed_mbps);\n    }\n});\n```\n\n### Complex Event Payloads\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Serialize, Clone)]\n#[serde(tag = \"type\", content = \"data\")]\nenum AppEvent {\n    UserLoggedIn { user_id: String, username: String },\n    UserLoggedOut { user_id: String },\n    DataSynced { items_count: usize, timestamp: String },\n    ErrorOccurred { code: String, message: String, recoverable: bool },\n}\n\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn perform_login(\n    username: String,\n    password: String,\n    window: Window,\n) -> Result<String, String> {\n    let user = authenticate(&username, &password).await?;\n\n    // Emit structured event\n    window.emit(\"app-event\", AppEvent::UserLoggedIn {\n        user_id: user.id.clone(),\n        username: user.username.clone(),\n    }).map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n\n    Ok(user.id)\n}\n```\n\n**Frontend**:\n```typescript\ntype AppEvent =\n    | { type: ''UserLoggedIn''; data: { user_id: string; username: string } }\n    | { type: ''UserLoggedOut''; data: { user_id: string } }\n    | { type: ''DataSynced''; data: { items_count: number; timestamp: string } }\n    | { type: ''ErrorOccurred''; data: { code: string; message: string; recoverable: boolean } };\n\nlisten<AppEvent>(''app-event'', (event) => {\n    const appEvent = event.payload;\n\n    switch (appEvent.type) {\n        case ''UserLoggedIn'':\n            handleLogin(appEvent.data.user_id, appEvent.data.username);\n            break;\n        case ''UserLoggedOut'':\n            handleLogout(appEvent.data.user_id);\n            break;\n        case ''DataSynced'':\n            showSyncSuccess(appEvent.data.items_count);\n            break;\n        case ''ErrorOccurred'':\n            handleError(appEvent.data);\n            break;\n    }\n});\n```\n\n## Streaming Data Patterns\n\n### Real-Time Data Stream\n\n```rust\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn stream_sensor_data(\n    sensor_id: String,\n    window: Window,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    let mut interval = tokio::time::interval(Duration::from_millis(100));\n\n    for _ in 0..100 {\n        interval.tick().await;\n\n        let reading = read_sensor(&sensor_id).await?;\n\n        window.emit(\"sensor-reading\", reading)\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n    }\n\n    window.emit(\"sensor-stream-ended\", sensor_id)\n        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())\n}\n```\n\n**Frontend with React**:\n```typescript\nimport { useEffect, useState } from ''react'';\nimport { listen } from ''@tauri-apps/api/event'';\n\ninterface SensorReading {\n    value: number;\n    timestamp: number;\n    unit: string;\n}\n\nfunction SensorMonitor() {\n    const [readings, setReadings] = useState<SensorReading[]>([]);\n\n    useEffect(() => {\n        let unlisten: UnlistenFn | undefined;\n\n        listen<SensorReading>(''sensor-reading'', (event) => {\n            setReadings(prev => [...prev.slice(-99), event.payload]);\n        }).then(fn => unlisten = fn);\n\n        return () => unlisten?.();\n    }, []);\n\n    return (\n        <div>\n            {readings.map((r, i) => (\n                <div key={i}>{r.value} {r.unit}</div>\n            ))}\n        </div>\n    );\n}\n```\n\n### Buffered Streaming\n\n```rust\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn stream_logs(\n    log_file: String,\n    window: Window,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    use tokio::io::{AsyncBufReadExt, BufReader};\n    use tokio::fs::File;\n\n    let file = File::open(log_file).await\n        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n\n    let reader = BufReader::new(file);\n    let mut lines = reader.lines();\n\n    let mut buffer = Vec::new();\n\n    while let Some(line) = lines.next_line().await\n        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())? {\n\n        buffer.push(line);\n\n        // Send in batches of 10 lines\n        if buffer.len() >= 10 {\n            window.emit(\"log-batch\", buffer.clone())\n                .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n            buffer.clear();\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Send remaining lines\n    if !buffer.is_empty() {\n        window.emit(\"log-batch\", buffer)\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n    }\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n## Multi-Window Communication\n\n### Broadcasting to All Windows\n\n```rust\nuse tauri::{AppHandle, Manager};\n\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn broadcast_message(\n    message: String,\n    app: AppHandle,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    // Emit to ALL windows\n    app.emit_all(\"broadcast\", message)\n        .map_err(|e| e.to_string())\n}\n```\n\n### Targeted Window Messaging\n\n```rust\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn send_to_window(\n    target_window: String,\n    message: String,\n    app: AppHandle,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    // Get specific window\n    if let Some(window) = app.get_window(&target_window) {\n        window.emit(\"private-message\", message)\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n        Ok(())\n    } else {\n        Err(format!(\"Window ''{}'' not found\", target_window))\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Window-to-Window via Backend\n\n**Window A (sender)**:\n```typescript\nimport { invoke } from ''@tauri-apps/api/core'';\n\nasync function sendToSettings(data: any) {\n    await invoke(''relay_to_settings'', { data });\n}\n```\n\n**Backend relay**:\n```rust\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn relay_to_settings(\n    data: serde_json::Value,\n    app: AppHandle,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    if let Some(settings_window) = app.get_window(\"settings\") {\n        settings_window.emit(\"data-update\", data)\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n**Window B (receiver - settings)**:\n```typescript\nimport { listen } from ''@tauri-apps/api/event'';\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n    let unlisten: UnlistenFn | undefined;\n\n    listen(''data-update'', (event) => {\n        console.log(''Received from main window:'', event.payload);\n        updateSettings(event.payload);\n    }).then(fn => unlisten = fn);\n\n    return () => unlisten?.();\n}, []);\n```\n\n## Frontend → Backend Events\n\n### Custom Frontend Events\n\n```typescript\nimport { emit } from ''@tauri-apps/api/event'';\n\n// Frontend emits event\nawait emit(''user-action'', {\n    action: ''button-click'',\n    button_id: ''save-button'',\n    timestamp: Date.now()\n});\n```\n\n**Backend listener**:\n```rust\nuse tauri::{Manager, Listener};\n\nfn main() {\n    tauri::Builder::default()\n        .setup(|app| {\n            let app_handle = app.handle();\n\n            // Listen for frontend events\n            app_handle.listen_global(\"user-action\", move |event| {\n                if let Some(payload) = event.payload() {\n                    println!(\"User action: {}\", payload);\n                    // Process event...\n                }\n            });\n\n            Ok(())\n        })\n        .run(tauri::generate_context!())\n        .expect(\"error while running tauri application\");\n}\n```\n\n## Advanced Listener Management\n\n### React Hook for Events\n\n```typescript\nimport { useEffect, useState } from ''react'';\nimport { listen, UnlistenFn } from ''@tauri-apps/api/event'';\n\nfunction useEvent<T>(eventName: string): T | null {\n    const [payload, setPayload] = useState<T | null>(null);\n\n    useEffect(() => {\n        let unlisten: UnlistenFn | undefined;\n\n        listen<T>(eventName, (event) => {\n            setPayload(event.payload);\n        }).then(fn => unlisten = fn);\n\n        return () => unlisten?.();\n    }, [eventName]);\n\n    return payload;\n}\n\n// Usage\nfunction ProgressDisplay() {\n    const progress = useEvent<ProgressEvent>(''download-progress'');\n\n    if (!progress) return null;\n\n    return (\n        <div>\n            Progress: {progress.percentage.toFixed(2)}%\n        </div>\n    );\n}\n```\n\n### Event Queue Pattern\n\n```typescript\nimport { listen } from ''@tauri-apps/api/event'';\n\nclass EventQueue<T> {\n    private queue: T[] = [];\n    private unlisten?: UnlistenFn;\n\n    async start(eventName: string) {\n        this.unlisten = await listen<T>(eventName, (event) => {\n            this.queue.push(event.payload);\n        });\n    }\n\n    dequeue(): T | undefined {\n        return this.queue.shift();\n    }\n\n    clear() {\n        this.queue = [];\n    }\n\n    stop() {\n        this.unlisten?.();\n    }\n\n    get length() {\n        return this.queue.length;\n    }\n}\n\n// Usage\nconst progressQueue = new EventQueue<ProgressEvent>();\nawait progressQueue.start(''download-progress'');\n\n// Process queue periodically\nsetInterval(() => {\n    while (progressQueue.length > 0) {\n        const event = progressQueue.dequeue();\n        processProgress(event);\n    }\n}, 100);\n```\n\n### One-Time Events\n\n```typescript\nimport { once } from ''@tauri-apps/api/event'';\n\n// Listen for event only once\nawait once<string>(''initialization-complete'', (event) => {\n    console.log(''App initialized:'', event.payload);\n    startApp();\n});\n```\n\n## Error Handling in Events\n\n### Safe Event Emission\n\n```rust\nasync fn emit_safe(window: &Window, event: &str, payload: impl Serialize) -> Result<(), String> {\n    window.emit(event, payload)\n        .map_err(|e| {\n            eprintln!(\"Failed to emit event ''{}'': {}\", event, e);\n            e.to_string()\n        })\n}\n\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn process_with_events(\n    window: Window,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    emit_safe(&window, \"processing-started\", \"Starting...\")\n        .await?;\n\n    // Process...\n\n    emit_safe(&window, \"processing-complete\", \"Done!\")\n        .await?;\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n## Performance Considerations\n\n### Throttling Events\n\n```rust\nuse std::time::{Duration, Instant};\n\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn high_frequency_updates(\n    window: Window,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    let mut last_emit = Instant::now();\n    let throttle_duration = Duration::from_millis(100);\n\n    for i in 0..10000 {\n        let value = compute_value(i);\n\n        // Only emit every 100ms\n        if last_emit.elapsed() >= throttle_duration {\n            window.emit(\"update\", value)\n                .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n            last_emit = Instant::now();\n        }\n    }\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n### Batching Events\n\n```rust\n#[tauri::command]\nasync fn batch_updates(\n    window: Window,\n) -> Result<(), String> {\n    let mut batch = Vec::new();\n\n    for item in process_items() {\n        batch.push(item);\n\n        // Emit in batches of 50\n        if batch.len() >= 50 {\n            window.emit(\"batch-update\", batch.clone())\n                .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n            batch.clear();\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Emit remaining items\n    if !batch.is_empty() {\n        window.emit(\"batch-update\", batch)\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?;\n    }\n\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Always clean up listeners** - Use `unlisten()` to prevent memory leaks\n2. **Type event payloads** - Define interfaces for type safety\n3. **Use structured events** - Tagged unions for multiple event types\n4. **Throttle high-frequency events** - Prevent overwhelming frontend\n5. **Batch when possible** - Reduce serialization overhead\n6. **Handle errors gracefully** - Log failed emissions, don''t crash\n7. **Use once() for one-time events** - Initialization, completion signals\n8. **Namespace event names** - Use prefixes like \"download:\", \"user:\", \"system:\"\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n❌ **Forgetting to unlisten**:\n```typescript\n// WRONG - memory leak\nfunction Component() {\n    listen(''my-event'', handler);  // Never cleaned up!\n}\n\n// CORRECT\nfunction Component() {\n    useEffect(() => {\n        let unlisten: UnlistenFn | undefined;\n        listen(''my-event'', handler).then(fn => unlisten = fn);\n        return () => unlisten?.();\n    }, []);\n}\n```\n\n❌ **Not handling serialization errors**:\n```rust\n// WRONG - struct can''t serialize\n#[derive(Clone)]  // Missing Serialize!\nstruct Event { }\n\nwindow.emit(\"event\", Event {});  // Runtime error!\n\n// CORRECT\n#[derive(Serialize, Clone)]\nstruct Event { }\n```\n\n❌ **Emitting too frequently**:\n```rust\n// WRONG - 10000 events in quick succession\nfor i in 0..10000 {\n    window.emit(\"update\", i);  // Overwhelming!\n}\n\n// CORRECT - throttle or batch\n```\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Events are async** - Backend → Frontend communication\n- **Always type payloads** - Use serde::Serialize + TypeScript interfaces\n- **Clean up listeners** - Call `unlisten()` in cleanup\n- **Throttle/batch** - High-frequency events need rate limiting\n- **Use structured payloads** - Tagged unions for multiple event types\n- **Window targeting** - `emit()` for specific, `emit_all()` for broadcast\n- **Frontend events** - Use `emit()` from frontend, listen in backend setup\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:58:50.304Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Multi-Language Agents needing seamless communication between Rust and JavaScript using Tauri''s event system","zh":"适用于需要在Rust和JavaScript之间实现无缝通信的多语言代理，使用Tauri的事件系统","ja":"RustとJavaScriptの間で無断通信を必要とするマルチ言語エージェントに最適で、Tauriのイベントシステムを使用","ko":"Rust와 JavaScript 사이의 무선통신이 필요한 멀티언어 에이전트에 적합하며 Tauri의 이벤트 시스템을 사용","es":"Ideal para agentes de varios idiomas que necesitan una comunicación sin problemas entre Rust y JavaScript utilizando el sistema de eventos de Tauri","fr":"Idéal pour les agents multilingues nécessitant une communication transparente entre Rust et JavaScript à l''aide du système d''événements Tauri","de":"Ideal für Mehrsprachige Agents, die eine nahtlose Kommunikation zwischen Rust und JavaScript unter Verwendung des Tauri-Ereignissystems benötigen","pt":"Ideal para agentes de multi-idioma que precisam de comunicação sem interrupção entre Rust e JavaScript usando o sistema de eventos do Tauri","ru":"Идеально для многоязычных агентов, требующих бесшовного общения между Rust и JavaScript с помощью системы событий Tauri","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المتعددين اللغات الذين يحتاجون إلى اتصال متواصل بين Rust و JavaScript باستخدام نظام أحداث Tauri"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to emit and listen to custom events between the backend and frontend, leveraging Tauri''s Window API and Rust''s async/await syntax for efficient event handling, and enabling real-time communication using protocols like WebSocket","zh":"赋予代理发出和监听自定义事件的能力，利用Tauri的Window API和Rust的异步/等待语法进行高效的事件处理，并使用WebSocket等协议实现实时通信","ja":"エージェントがバックエンドとフロントエンドの間でカスタムイベントを発行、リスニングできるようにし、TauriのWindow APIとRustの非同期/待機構文を利用して効率的なイベントハンドリングを実現し、WebSocketなどのプロトコルを使用してリアルタイム通信を可能に","ko":"에이전트가 백엔드와 프론트엔드 사이에서 사용자 지정 이벤트를発行하고 수신할 수 있도록 하며, Tauri의 Window API와 Rust의 비동기/대기 구문을 사용하여 효율적인 이벤트 처리를实现하고 WebSocket 등의 프로토콜을 사용하여 실시간 통신을 가능하게 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a emitir y escuchar eventos personalizados entre el backend y el frontend, aprovechando la API de ventana de Tauri y la sintaxis async/await de Rust para un manejo de eventos eficiente, y permitiendo la comunicación en tiempo real utilizando protocolos como WebSocket","fr":"Permet aux agents d''émettre et d''écouter des événements personnalisés entre le backend et le frontend, en exploitant l''API de fenêtre Tauri et la syntaxe async/await de Rust pour un traitement d''événements efficace, et en permettant la communication en temps réel à l''aide de protocoles comme WebSocket","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, benutzerdefinierte Ereignisse zwischen Backend und Frontend zu senden und zu hören, indem sie die Tauri-Fenster-API und die async/await-Syntax von Rust für eine effiziente Ereignisverarbeitung nutzen und Echtzeitkommunikation mithilfe von Protokollen wie WebSocket ermöglichen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a emitir e ouvir eventos personalizados entre o backend e o frontend, aproveitando a API da Janela do Tauri e a sintaxe async/await do Rust para manipulação eficiente de eventos, e permitindo a comunicação em tempo real usando protocolos como WebSocket","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью излучать и слушать пользовательские события между бэкендом и фронтендом, используя API окна Tauri и синтаксис async/await Rust для эффективной обработки событий, и позволяя осуществлять коммуникацию в реальном времени с использованием протоколов, таких как WebSocket","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من إرسال واستقبال أحداث مخصصة بين الخلفية والأمامية، مستفيدًا من واجهة برمجة تطبيقات نافذة Tauri وتنسيق async/await لغة Rust من أجل معالجة حدث فعالة، وتمكين الاتصال في الوقت الفعلي باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل WebSocket"},"useCases":{"en":["Handling download events in a video downloader app","Implementing real-time updates in a desktop application","Debugging event emissions and listener registrations"],"zh":["处理视频下载器应用中的下载事件","在桌面应用中实现实时更新","调试事件发射和监听器注册"],"ja":["ビデオダウンローダーアプリでのダウンロードイベントの処理","デスクトップアプリケーションでのリアルタイム更新の実装","イベント発行とリスナー登録のデバッグ"],"ko":["비디오 다운로더 애플리케이션에서 다운로드 이벤트 처리","데스크탑 애플리케이션에서 실시간 업데이트 구현","이벤트 발신 및 리스너 등록 디버깅"],"es":["Controlar eventos de descarga en una aplicación de descargador de videos","Implementar actualizaciones en tiempo real en una aplicación de escritorio","Depurar la emisión y el registro de eventos"],"fr":["Gérer les événements de téléchargement dans une application de téléchargement de vidéos","Mettre en œuvre des mises à jour en temps réel dans une application de bureau","Déboguer l''émission et l''enregistrement d''événements"],"de":["Download-Ereignisse in einer Videodownloader-App verwalten","Echtzeit-Updates in einer Desktop-Anwendung implementieren","Ereignisemissionen und -registrierungen debuggen"],"pt":["Manipulação de eventos de download em um aplicativo de downloader de vídeo","Implementação de atualizações em tempo real em um aplicativo de área de trabalho","Depuração de emissões de eventos e registros de ouvintes"],"ru":["Обработка событий скачивания в приложении для скачивания видео","Реализация обновлений в реальном времени в настольном приложении","Отладка излучения событий и регистрации слушателей"],"ar":["تعامل أحداث التحميل في تطبيق لتحميل الفيديو","تنفيذ التحديثات في الوقت الفعلي في تطبيق سطح المكتب","تصحيح أخطاء انبعاث الأحداث وتسجيل الاستماع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Tauri and Rust setup","Limited to Tauri-based applications","Frontend must be built with a compatible framework like React"],"zh":["需要Tauri和Rust的设置","仅限Tauri 기반应用","前端必须使用兼容框架如React构建"],"ja":["TauriとRustの設定が必要","Tauriベースのアプリケーションに限定","フロントエンドはReactなどの互換フレームワークで構築される必要"],"ko":["Tauri와 Rust의 설정이 필요","Tauri 기반 애플리케이션으로 제한","프론트엔드는 React와 같은 호환 프레임워크로 빌드되어야 함"],"es":["Requiere configuración de Tauri y Rust","Limitado a aplicaciones basadas en Tauri","El frontend debe estar construido con un marco compatible como React"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration Tauri et Rust","Limité aux applications basées sur Tauri","Le frontend doit être construit avec un framework compatible comme React"],"de":["Benötigt Tauri- und Rust-Setup","Begrenzt auf Tauri-basierte Anwendungen","Das Frontend muss mit einem kompatiblen Framework wie React erstellt werden"],"pt":["Requer configuração do Tauri e Rust","Limitado a aplicações baseadas em Tauri","A interface do usuário deve ser construída com um framework compatível como React"],"ru":["Требует настройки Tauri и Rust","Ограничен для приложений на основе Tauri","Интерфейс пользователя должен быть построен с помощью совместимого фреймворка, такого как React"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد Tauri و Rust","محدود للتطبيقات المستندة إلى Tauri","يجب بناء واجهة المستخدم مع إطار عمل متوافق مثل React"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
