ekturdiagrammen","Parsing von Terraform-Code","Visualisierung von Infrastrukturressourcen","Kompatibilität mit .tf- und .tfvars-Dateien","Darstellung von Modulen und Beziehungen"],"pt":["Geração de diagramas de arquitetura a partir de arquivos Terraform","Visualização de recursos de infraestrutura e módulos","Suporte a arquivos `.tf` e `.tfvars`","Análise de código Terraform para geração de diagramas","Integração com ferramentas de infraestrutura como código"],"ru":["Генерация диаграмм архитектуры из файлов Terraform","Визуализация ресурсов инфраструктуры и модулей","Поддержка файлов `.tf` и `.tfvars`","Анализ кода Terraform для генерации диаграмм","Интеграция с инструментами инфраструктуры как код"],"ar":["إنشاء مخططات هيكلية من ملفات تيراформ","تصوير موارد البنية التحتية والوحدات النمطية","دعم ملفات `.tf` و `.tfvars`","تحليل رمز تيراформ لإنشاء مخططات","التكامل مع أدوات البنية التحتية ككود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Terraform","Infrastructure-as-Code","HCL","Terraform .tf","Terraform .tfvars","Terraform "],"ja":["Terraform","Infrastructure-as-Code","HCL","Terraform .tf","Terraform .tfvars","Terraform "],"ko":["Terraform","Infrastructure-as-Code","HCL","Terraform .tf","Terraform .tfvars","Terraform "],"es":["Terraform","diagramas de arquitectura","infraestructura como código","HCL","visualización de infraestructura","generador de diagramas"],"fr":["Terraform","diagrammes d''architecture","infrastructure comme code","HCL","visualisation d''infrastructure","générateur de diagrammes"],"de":["Terraform","Architekturdiagramme","Infrastruktur als Code","HCL","Visualisierung von Infrastruktur","Diagramm-Generator"],"pt":["Terraform","Diagramas de arquitetura","Infraestrutura como código","Gerador de diagramas","Visualização de recursos","Arquivos TF","Arquivos TFVars"],"ru":["Terraform","Диаграммы архитектуры","Инфраструктура как код","Генератор диаграмм","Визуализация ресурсов","Файлы TF","Файлы TFVars"],"ar":["تيراформ","مخططات هيكلية","بنية تحتية ككود","مولد مخططات","تصوير موارد","ملفات تي إف","ملفات تي إف فيراس"]}},"owner":"gamingopgamingop","repo":"sarthak-skill-forge","repoPath":"gamingopgamingop/sarthak-skill-forge","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.483Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"terraform-diagrams","description":"Generates architecture diagrams from Terraform code. Use when user has .tf files or asks to visualize Terraform infrastructure.","version":"1.0.0","tags":"terraform, diagram, infrastructure, aws, azure, gcp, iac, hcl","bodyPreview":"# Terraform Diagram Generator\n\nGenerates architecture diagrams directly from Terraform `.tf` files. Specializes in parsing Terraform code and visualizing infrastructure resources, modules, and their relationships.\n\n## When to Use\n\nActivate this skill when:\n\n- User has Terraform files (`.tf`, `.tfvars`) and wants to visualize the infrastructure\n- User asks to \"diagram my Terraform\" or \"visualize this infrastructure\"\n- User mentions Terraform, HCL, or infrastructure-as-code\n- User wants to see the","body":"# Terraform Diagram Generator\n\nGenerates architecture diagrams directly from Terraform `.tf` files. Specializes in parsing Terraform code and visualizing infrastructure resources, modules, and their relationships.\n\n## When to Use\n\nActivate this skill when:\n\n- User has Terraform files (`.tf`, `.tfvars`) and wants to visualize the infrastructure\n- User asks to \"diagram my Terraform\" or \"visualize this infrastructure\"\n- User mentions Terraform, HCL, or infrastructure-as-code\n- User wants to see the architecture of their Terraform-managed resources\n\n## How It Works\n\nThis skill generates Terraform-specific diagrams by parsing Terraform code and calling the Eraser API directly:\n\n1. **Parse Terraform Files**: Identify resources, modules, data sources, and variables\n2. **Extract Relationships**: Map dependencies, resource connections, and module hierarchies\n3. **Generate Eraser DSL**: Create Eraser DSL code from Terraform resources\n4. **Call Eraser API**: Use `/api/render/elements` with `diagramType: \"cloud-architecture-diagram\"`\n\n## Instructions\n\nWhen the user provides Terraform code:\n\n1. **Parse the Terraform**\n\n   - Identify all `resource` blocks (AWS, Azure, GCP, etc.)\n   - Extract `module` blocks and their configurations\n   - Note `data` sources and their dependencies\n   - Identify `variable` and `output` definitions\n\n2. **Map Relationships**\n\n   - Track resource dependencies (e.g., `subnet_id = aws_subnet.public.id`)\n   - Group resources by provider (AWS, Azure, GCP)\n   - Identify VPCs/VNets as containers for other resources\n   - Note security groups, IAM roles, and networking rules\n\n3. **Generate Eraser DSL** Convert Terraform resources to Eraser DSL:\n\n   - **CRITICAL: Label Formatting Rules**\n     - Labels MUST be on a single line - NEVER use newlines inside label attributes\n     - Keep labels simple and readable - prefer separate labels over concatenating too much metadata\n     - Format DSL with proper line breaks (one node/group per line, but labels stay on single lines)\n     - If including metadata like CIDR blocks or instance types, include them in the same quoted label string: `[label: \"VPC 10.0.0.0/16\"]`\n\n   Example:\n\n   ```\n   main-vpc [label: \"VPC 10.0.0.0/16\"] {\n     public-subnet [label: \"Public Subnet 10.0.1.0/24\"] {\n       web-server [icon: aws-ec2, label: \"Web Server t3.micro\"]\n       load-balancer [icon: aws-elb]\n     }\n     private-subnet [label: \"Private Subnet\"] {\n       database [icon: aws-rds]\n     }\n   }\n   load-balancer -> web-server\n   web-server -> database\n   ```\n\n4. **Make the HTTP Request**\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: You MUST execute this curl command after generating the DSL. Never stop after generating DSL without making the API call.\n\n   **CRITICAL**: In the `X-Skill-Source` header below, you MUST replace the value with your AI agent name:\n   - If you are Claude (Anthropic), use: `claude`\n   - If you are running in Cursor, use: `cursor`\n   - If you are ChatGPT (OpenAI), use: `chatgpt`\n   - If you are Gemini (Google), use: `gemini`\n   - Otherwise, use your model/agent name in lowercase\n\n   ```bash\n   curl -X POST https://app.eraser.io/api/render/elements \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -H \"X-Skill-Source: eraser-skill\" \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer ${ERASER_API_KEY}\" \\\n     -d ''{\n       \"elements\": [{\n         \"type\": \"diagram\",\n         \"id\": \"diagram-1\",\n         \"code\": \"<your generated DSL>\",\n         \"diagramType\": \"cloud-architecture-diagram\"\n       }],\n       \"scale\": 2,\n       \"theme\": \"${ERASER_THEME:-dark}\",\n       \"background\": true\n     }''\n   ```\n\n5. **Track Sources During Analysis**\n\n   As you analyze Terraform files and resources to generate the diagram, track:\n\n   - **Internal files**: Record each Terraform file path you read and what resources were extracted (e.g., `infra/main.tf` - VPC and subnet definitions, `infra/rds.tf` - Database configuration)\n   - **External references**: Note any documentation, examples, or URLs consulted (e.g., Terraform AWS provider documentation, AWS architecture best practices)\n   - **Annotations**: For each source, note what it contributed to the diagram\n\n6. **Handle the Response**\n\n   **CRITICAL: Minimal Output Format**\n\n   Your response MUST always include these elements with clear headers:\n\n   1. **Diagram Preview**: Display with a header\n      ```\n      ## Diagram\n      ![{Title}]({imageUrl})\n      ```\n      Use the ACTUAL `imageUrl` from the API response.\n\n   2. **Editor Link**: Display with a header\n      ```\n      ## Open in Eraser\n      [Edit this diagram in the Eraser editor]({createEraserFileUrl})\n      ```\n      Use the ACTUAL URL from the API response.\n\n   3. **Sources section**: Brief list of files/resources analyzed (if applicable)\n      ```\n      ## Sources\n      - `path/to/file` - What was extracted\n      ```\n\n   4. **Diagram Code section**: The Eraser DSL in a code block with `eraser` language tag\n      ```\n      ## Diagram Code\n      ```eraser\n      {DSL code here}\n      ```\n      ```\n\n   5. **Learn More link**: `You can learn more about Eraser at https://docs.eraser.io/docs/using-ai-agent-integrations`\n\n   **Additional content rules:**\n   - If the user ONLY asked for a diagram, include NOTHING beyond the 5 elements above\n   - If the user explicitly asked for more (e.g., \"explain the architecture\", \"suggest improvements\"), you may include that additional content\n   - Never add unrequested sections like Overview, Security Considerations, Testing, etc.\n\n   The default output should be SHORT. The diagram image speaks for itself.\n\n7. **Handle Multiple Providers**\n   - If Terraform uses multiple providers, group by provider\n   - Create separate sections for AWS, Azure, GCP resources\n   - Show cross-provider connections if applicable\n\n## Terraform-Specific Tips\n\n- **Group by Module**: If modules are used, show module boundaries\n- **Show VPCs/VNets as Containers**: These should visually contain subnets and resources\n- **Include Data Flows**: Show how resources connect (e.g., ALB → EC2 → RDS)\n- **Highlight Security**: Include security groups, IAM roles, and network ACLs\n- **Show Resource Types**: Use provider-specific icons (AWS, Azure, GCP)\n- **Include CIDR Blocks**: Show network addressing for VPCs and subnets\n\n## Example: Multi-Provider Terraform\n\n### User Input\n\n```hcl\n# AWS Resources\nresource \"aws_vpc\" \"main\" {\n  cidr_block = \"10.0.0.0/16\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_subnet\" \"public\" {\n  vpc_id     = aws_vpc.main.id\n  cidr_block = \"10.0.1.0/24\"\n}\n\nresource \"aws_instance\" \"web\" {\n  subnet_id     = aws_subnet.public.id\n  instance_type = \"t3.micro\"\n}\n\n# Azure Resources (multi-provider)\nresource \"azurerm_resource_group\" \"main\" {\n  name     = \"rg-main\"\n  location = \"East US\"\n}\n\nresource \"azurerm_virtual_network\" \"main\" {\n  name                = \"vnet-main\"\n  resource_group_name  = azurerm_resource_group.main.name\n  address_space        = [\"10.1.0.0/16\"]\n}\n\n# Module usage\nmodule \"database\" {\n  source = \"./modules/rds\"\n  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id\n}\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\n1. Parses Terraform:\n\n   - **AWS**: VPC, subnet, EC2 instance\n   - **Azure**: Resource group, VNet (multi-provider setup)\n   - **Module**: Database module with dependency on VPC\n\n2. Generates DSL showing multi-provider and module structure:\n\n   ```\n   # AWS Resources\n   aws-vpc [label: \"AWS VPC 10.0.0.0/16\"] {\n     aws-subnet [label: \"Public Subnet 10.0.1.0/24\"] {\n       web-server [icon: aws-ec2, label: \"Web Server t3.micro\"]\n     }\n   }\n\n   # Azure Resources\n   resource-group [label: \"Resource Group rg-main\"] {\n     azure-vnet [label: \"Azure VNet 10.1.0.0/16\"]\n   }\n\n   # Module\n   database-module [label: \"Database Module\"] {\n     rds-instance [icon: aws-rds]\n   }\n\n   aws-vpc -> database-module\n   ```\n\n   **Important**: All label text must be on a single line within quotes. Terraform-specific: Show modules as containers, group by provider, include resource dependencies.\n\n3. Calls `/api/render/elements` with `diagramType: \"cloud-architecture-diagram\"`\n\n### Result\n\nUser receives a diagram showing:\n\n- VPC as a container\n- Public subnet nested inside VPC\n- EC2 instance in the subnet\n- Proper AWS styling\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:58:36.683Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cloud Infrastructure Agents needing automated Terraform visualization capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化Terraform可视化能力的云基础设施代理。","ja":"Terraformの自動可視化機能を必要とするクラウドインフラストラクチャエージェントに最適です。","ko":"자동화된 Terraform 시각화 기능이 필요한 클라우드 인프라 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de infraestructura en la nube que necesitan capacidades de visualización de Terraform automatizadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''infrastructure cloud ayant besoin de capacités de visualisation de Terraform automatisées.","de":"Perfekt für Cloud-Infrastruktur-Agents, die automatisierte Terraform-Visualisierungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Infraestrutura em Nuvem que necessitam de capacidades de visualização automatizada do Terraform.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов облачной инфраструктуры, которым необходимы автоматические возможности визуализации Terraform.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء البنية السحابية الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات ت Terraform التلقائي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate architecture diagrams directly from Terraform `.tf` files, specializing in parsing Terraform code and visualizing infrastructure resources, modules, and their relationships using HCL.","zh":"赋予代理直接从Terraform `.tf`文件生成架构图的能力，专门解析Terraform代码并使用HCL可视化基础设施资源、模块及其关系。","ja":"Terraform `.tf` ファイルから直接アーキテクチャ図を生成する機能をエージェントに与え、Terraform コードの解析と HCL を使用したインフラストラクチャ リソース、モジュール、およびその関係の可視化に特化しています。","ko":"Terraform `.tf` 파일로부터 직접 아키텍처 다이어그램을 생성하는 기능을 에이전트에게 제공하며, Terraform 코드를 파싱하고 HCL을 사용하여 인프라 리소스, 모듈 및 그들의 관계를 시각화하는 데 전문입니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes generar diagramas de arquitectura directamente desde archivos Terraform `.tf`, especializándose en el análisis de código Terraform y la visualización de recursos de infraestructura, módulos y sus relaciones utilizando HCL.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer des diagrammes d''architecture directement à partir de fichiers Terraform `.tf`, se spécialisant dans l''analyse de code Terraform et la visualisation des ressources d''infrastructure, des modules et de leurs relations à l''aide de HCL.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Architekturdiagramme direkt aus Terraform-`.tf`-Dateien zu generieren, spezialisiert auf die Analyse von Terraform-Code und die Visualisierung von Infrastruktur-Ressourcen, -Modulen und ihren Beziehungen unter Verwendung von HCL.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar diagramas de arquitetura diretamente a partir de arquivos Terraform `.tf`, especializando-se na análise de código Terraform e na visualização de recursos de infraestrutura, módulos e suas relações usando HCL.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать диаграммы архитектуры直接 из файлов Terraform `.tf`, специализируясь на парсинге кода Terraform и визуализации ресурсов инфраструктуры, модулей и их отношений с помощью HCL.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على генера générer مخططات الهندسة المعمارية مباشرة من ملفات Terraform `.tf` ، وتخصص في تحليل كود Terraform وتصوير الموارد البنية التحتية والوحدات والنظم العلاقات باستخدام HCL."},"useCases":{"en":["Visualizing infrastructure-as-code deployments","Generating diagrams from Terraform configurations","Debugging infrastructure issues through graphical representation"],"zh":["可视化基础设施即代码部署","从Terraform配置生成图表","通过图形表示调试基础设施问题"],"ja":["コードとしてのインフラストラクチャのデプロイの可視化","Terraformの設定から図を生成する","グラフィカルな表現を使用したインフラストラクチャの問題のデバッグ"],"ko":["인프라스트럭처 即 코드 배포 시각화","Terraform 구성에서 다이어그램 생성","그래픽 표현을 통한 인프라스트럭처 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Visualización de implementaciones de infraestructura como código","Generación de diagramas a partir de configuraciones de Terraform","Depuración de problemas de infraestructura a través de representación gráfica"],"fr":["Visualisation de déploiements d''infrastructure en tant que code","Génération de diagrammes à partir de configurations Terraform","Débogage de problèmes d''infrastructure via une représentation graphique"],"de":["Visualisierung von Infrastruktur-als-Code-Bereitstellungen","Erzeugung von Diagrammen aus Terraform-Konfigurationen","Fehlerbehebung bei Infrastrukturproblemen durch grafische Darstellung"],"pt":["Visualizar implantações de infraestrutura como código","Gerar diagramas a partir de configurações do Terraform","Depurar problemas de infraestrutura por meio de representação gráfica"],"ru":["Визуализировать развертывания инфраструктуры как код","Генерировать диаграммы из конфигураций Terraform","Отладить проблемы инфраструктуры с помощью графического представления"],"ar":["تجسير عمليات النشر البنية كود","توليد مخططات من-configurations التكوين Terraform","تصحيح الأخطاء في مشاكل البنية التحتية من خلال التمثيل الرسومي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Terraform files (`.tf`, `.tfvars`) as input","Limited to Terraform-based infrastructure visualization"],"zh":["需要Terraform文件（`.tf`，`.tfvars`）作为输入","仅限于Terraform基础设施可视化"],"ja":["入力としてTerraformファイル（`.tf`、`.tfvars`）が必要","Terraformベースのインフラストラクチャの可視化に限定される"],"ko":["입력으로 Terraform 파일(`.tf`, `.tfvars`)이 필요","Terraform 기반 인프라스트럭처 시각화에만 한정"],"es":["Requiere archivos Terraform (`.tf`, `.tfvars`) como entrada","Limitado a la visualización de infraestructura basada en Terraform"],"fr":["Nécessite des fichiers Terraform (`.tf`, `.tfvars`) comme entrée","Limité à la visualisation d''infrastructure basée sur Terraform"],"de":["Benötigt Terraform-Dateien (`.tf`, `.tfvars`) als Eingabe","Begrenzt auf die Visualisierung von Terraform-basierter Infrastruktur"],"pt":["Requer arquivos Terraform (`.tf`, `.tfvars`) como entrada","Limitado à visualização de infraestrutura baseada em Terraform"],"ru":["Требует файлов Terraform (`.tf`, `.tfvars`) в качестве входных данных","Ограничен визуализацией инфраструктуры на основе Terraform"],"ar":["يتطلب ملفات Terraform (`.tf` ، `.tfvars`) كمدخل","محدود إلى تمثيل البنية التحتية المعتمدة على Terraform"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
