on으로 사용 가능한 변경을 가져옴","AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자에게 변경을 선택하도록 함","구현 태스크를 가진 변경을 표시"],"es":["Verificación de cambios en la implementación","Lectura y edición de Markdown","Integración con Electron, React y TypeScript","Selección de cambios disponibles","Uso de la herramienta AskUserQuestion"],"fr":["Vérification des modifications dans l''implémentation","Lecture et édition de Markdown","Intégration avec Electron, React et TypeScript","Sélection des modifications disponibles","Utilisation de l''outil AskUserQuestion"],"de":["Überprüfung von Änderungen in der Implementierung","Lesen und Bearbeiten von Markdown","Integration mit Electron, React und TypeScript","Auswahl verfügbarer Änderungen","Verwendung des Tools AskUserQuestion"],"pt":["Leitura e edição de Markdown","Construído com Electron + React + TypeScript","Verificação de implementação contra especificações de alteração","Suporte à seleção de alterações","Integração com a ferramenta AskUserQuestion"],"ru":["Чтение и редактирование Markdown","Построен с помощью Electron + React + TypeScript","Проверка реализации против спецификаций изменения","Поддержка выбора изменений","Интеграция с инструментом AskUserQuestion"],"ar":["قراءة وتنقيح Markdown","مبني على Electron + React + TypeScript","التحقق من تنفيذ ضد مواصفات التغيير","دعم اختيار التغييرات","التكامل مع أداة AskUserQuestion"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-verify-change","技术验证工具","Electron","React","TypeScript","变更文档","实现验证"],"ja":["openspec-verify-change","技術検証ツール","Electron","React","TypeScript","変更文書","実装検証"],"ko":["openspec-verify-change","기술 검증 도구","Electron","React","TypeScript","변경 문서","구현 검증"],"es":["verificación de cambios","implementación de software","lectura de Markdown","edición de Markdown","Electron","React","TypeScript"],"fr":["vérification des modifications","implémentation de logiciel","lecture de Markdown","édition de Markdown","Electron","React","TypeScript"],"de":["Überprüfung von Änderungen","Implementierung von Software","Lesen von Markdown","Bearbeiten von Markdown","Electron","React","TypeScript"],"pt":["openspec-verify-change","verificação de implementação","especificações de alteração","Markdown","Electron","React","TypeScript","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["openspec-verify-change","проверка реализации","спецификации изменения","Markdown","Electron","React","TypeScript","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["openspec-verify-change","التحقق من تنفيذ","مواصفات التغيير","Markdown","Electron","React","TypeScript","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"AdJIa","repo":"markdown-x","repoPath":"AdJIa/markdown-x","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.486Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-verify-change","description":"Verify implementation matches change artifacts. Use when the user wants to validate that implementation is complete, correct, and coherent before archiving.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifa","body":"Verify that an implementation matches the change artifacts (specs, tasks, design).\n\n**Input**: Optionally specify a change name. If omitted, check if it can be inferred from conversation context. If vague or ambiguous you MUST prompt for available changes.\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **If no change name provided, prompt for selection**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get available changes. Use the **AskUserQuestion tool** to let the user select.\n\n   Show changes that have implementation tasks (tasks artifact exists).\n   Include the schema used for each change if available.\n   Mark changes with incomplete tasks as \"(In Progress)\".\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT guess or auto-select a change. Always let the user choose.\n\n2. **Check status to understand the schema**\n   ```bash\n   openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n   Parse the JSON to understand:\n   - `schemaName`: The workflow being used (e.g., \"spec-driven\", \"tdd\")\n   - Which artifacts exist for this change\n\n3. **Get the change directory and load artifacts**\n\n   ```bash\n   openspec instructions apply --change \"<name>\" --json\n   ```\n\n   This returns the change directory and context files. Read all available artifacts from `contextFiles`.\n\n4. **Initialize verification report structure**\n\n   Create a report structure with three dimensions:\n   - **Completeness**: Track tasks and spec coverage\n   - **Correctness**: Track requirement implementation and scenario coverage\n   - **Coherence**: Track design adherence and pattern consistency\n\n   Each dimension can have CRITICAL, WARNING, or SUGGESTION issues.\n\n5. **Verify Completeness**\n\n   **Task Completion**:\n   - If tasks.md exists in contextFiles, read it\n   - Parse checkboxes: `- [ ]` (incomplete) vs `- [x]` (complete)\n   - Count complete vs total tasks\n   - If incomplete tasks exist:\n     - Add CRITICAL issue for each incomplete task\n     - Recommendation: \"Complete task: <description>\" or \"Mark as done if already implemented\"\n\n   **Spec Coverage**:\n   - If delta specs exist in `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/`:\n     - Extract all requirements (marked with \"### Requirement:\")\n     - For each requirement:\n       - Search codebase for keywords related to the requirement\n       - Assess if implementation likely exists\n     - If requirements appear unimplemented:\n       - Add CRITICAL issue: \"Requirement not found: <requirement name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Implement requirement X: <description>\"\n\n6. **Verify Correctness**\n\n   **Requirement Implementation Mapping**:\n   - For each requirement from delta specs:\n     - Search codebase for implementation evidence\n     - If found, note file paths and line ranges\n     - Assess if implementation matches requirement intent\n     - If divergence detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Implementation may diverge from spec: <details>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Review <file>:<lines> against requirement X\"\n\n   **Scenario Coverage**:\n   - For each scenario in delta specs (marked with \"#### Scenario:\"):\n     - Check if conditions are handled in code\n     - Check if tests exist covering the scenario\n     - If scenario appears uncovered:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Scenario not covered: <scenario name>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Add test or implementation for scenario: <description>\"\n\n7. **Verify Coherence**\n\n   **Design Adherence**:\n   - If design.md exists in contextFiles:\n     - Extract key decisions (look for sections like \"Decision:\", \"Approach:\", \"Architecture:\")\n     - Verify implementation follows those decisions\n     - If contradiction detected:\n       - Add WARNING: \"Design decision not followed: <decision>\"\n       - Recommendation: \"Update implementation or revise design.md to match reality\"\n   - If no design.md: Skip design adherence check, note \"No design.md to verify against\"\n\n   **Code Pattern Consistency**:\n   - Review new code for consistency with project patterns\n   - Check file naming, directory structure, coding style\n   - If significant deviations found:\n     - Add SUGGESTION: \"Code pattern deviation: <details>\"\n     - Recommendation: \"Consider following project pattern: <example>\"\n\n8. **Generate Verification Report**\n\n   **Summary Scorecard**:\n   ```\n   ## Verification Report: <change-name>\n\n   ### Summary\n   | Dimension    | Status           |\n   |--------------|------------------|\n   | Completeness | X/Y tasks, N reqs|\n   | Correctness  | M/N reqs covered |\n   | Coherence    | Followed/Issues  |\n   ```\n\n   **Issues by Priority**:\n\n   1. **CRITICAL** (Must fix before archive):\n      - Incomplete tasks\n      - Missing requirement implementations\n      - Each with specific, actionable recommendation\n\n   2. **WARNING** (Should fix):\n      - Spec/design divergences\n      - Missing scenario coverage\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   3. **SUGGESTION** (Nice to fix):\n      - Pattern inconsistencies\n      - Minor improvements\n      - Each with specific recommendation\n\n   **Final Assessment**:\n   - If CRITICAL issues: \"X critical issue(s) found. Fix before archiving.\"\n   - If only warnings: \"No critical issues. Y warning(s) to consider. Ready for archive (with noted improvements).\"\n   - If all clear: \"All checks passed. Ready for archive.\"\n\n**Verification Heuristics**\n\n- **Completeness**: Focus on objective checklist items (checkboxes, requirements list)\n- **Correctness**: Use keyword search, file path analysis, reasonable inference - don''t require perfect certainty\n- **Coherence**: Look for glaring inconsistencies, don''t nitpick style\n- **False Positives**: When uncertain, prefer SUGGESTION over WARNING, WARNING over CRITICAL\n- **Actionability**: Every issue must have a specific recommendation with file/line references where applicable\n\n**Graceful Degradation**\n\n- If only tasks.md exists: verify task completion only, skip spec/design checks\n- If tasks + specs exist: verify completeness and correctness, skip design\n- If full artifacts: verify all three dimensions\n- Always note which checks were skipped and why\n\n**Output Format**\n\nUse clear markdown with:\n- Table for summary scorecard\n- Grouped lists for issues (CRITICAL/WARNING/SUGGESTION)\n- Code references in format: `file.ts:123`\n- Specific, actionable recommendations\n- No vague suggestions like \"consider reviewing\"\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T10:11:31.166Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing precise Markdown editing and change verification capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要精确Markdown编辑和变更验证能力的开发代理。","ja":"開発エージェントが正確なMarkdown編集と変更検証機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"개발 에이전트가 정밀한 Markdown 편집 및 변경 확인 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan edición de Markdown precisa y capacidades de verificación de cambios.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une édition de Markdown précise et de capacités de vérification de modifications.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine präzise Markdown-Bearbeitung und Änderungsüberprüfungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de edição de Markdown precisa e capacidades de verificação de alterações.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходимы точные возможности редактирования Markdown и проверки изменений.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النموزجين الذين يحتاجون إلى تحرير Markdown دقيق وقدرات التحقق من التغييرات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to verify implementation matches change artifacts using Electron, React, and TypeScript, with capabilities like running `openspec list --json` and utilizing the AskUserQuestion tool for user selection, all while handling Markdown files and JSON data.","zh":"赋予代理人使用Electron、React和TypeScript验证实现是否与变更工件相匹配的能力，包括运行`openspec list --json`和使用AskUserQuestion工具进行用户选择，同时处理Markdown文件和JSON数据。","ja":"Electron、React、TypeScriptを使用して実装が変更アーティファクトと一致することを検証する機能をエージェントに与え、`openspec list --json`の実行やAskUserQuestionツールを使用したユーザー選択などが可能となり、同時にMarkdownファイルやJSONデータを処理します。","ko":"에이전트가 Electron, React 및 TypeScript를 사용하여 구현이 변경 아티팩트와 일치하는지 확인할 수 있는 기능을 제공하며, `openspec list --json`을 실행하고 AskUserQuestion 도구를 사용하여 사용자 선택을 수행하는 등이 가능하며,同時に Markdown 파일과 JSON 데이터를 처리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a verificar que la implementación coincide con los artefactos de cambio utilizando Electron, React y TypeScript, con capacidades como la ejecución de `openspec list --json` y la utilización de la herramienta AskUserQuestion para la selección de usuarios, todo mientras maneja archivos Markdown y datos JSON.","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier que la mise en œuvre correspond aux artefacts de modification en utilisant Electron, React et TypeScript, avec des capacités telles que l''exécution de `openspec list --json` et l''utilisation de l''outil AskUserQuestion pour la sélection de l''utilisateur, le tout en gérant les fichiers Markdown et les données JSON.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, die Implementierung mit den Änderungsartefakten unter Verwendung von Electron, React und TypeScript zu überprüfen, mit Funktionen wie dem Ausführen von `openspec list --json` und der Verwendung des AskUserQuestion-Tools für die Benutzerauswahl, während es Markdown-Dateien und JSON-Daten bearbeitet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a verificar se a implementação corresponde aos artefatos de alteração usando Electron, React e TypeScript, com capacidades como executar `openspec list --json` e utilizar a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para seleção do usuário, tudo isso enquanto lida com arquivos Markdown e dados JSON.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проверять, соответствует ли реализация артефактам изменений, используя Electron, React и TypeScript, с возможностями, такими как запуск команды `openspec list --json` и использование инструмента AskUserQuestion для выбора пользователя, все это при работе с файлами Markdown и данными JSON.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التحقق من تطابق التنفيذ مع مكونات التغيير باستخدام Electron و React و TypeScript ، مع إمكانيات مثل تشغيل `openspec list --json` واستخدام أداة AskUserQuestion لتحديد المستخدم ، كل ذلك أثناء التعامل مع ملفات Markdown وبيانات JSON."},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying implementation changes against specs and design","Automating change artifact checks","Debugging implementation tasks using Markdown reading and editing"],"zh":["验证实现更改是否与规格和设计相符","自动化更改工件检查","使用Markdown读取和编辑调试实现任务"],"ja":["実装の変更が仕様と設計に合致することを検証する","変更アーティファクトのチェックを自動化する","Markdownの読み取りと編集を使用して実装タスクをデバッグする"],"ko":["구현 변경이 사양 및 설계와 일치하는지 확인","변경 아티팩트 확인 자동화","Markdown 읽기 및 편집을 사용하여 구현 작업 디버깅"],"es":["Verificar los cambios de implementación frente a las especificaciones y el diseño","Automatizar las comprobaciones de artefactos de cambio","Depurar tareas de implementación mediante la lectura y edición de Markdown"],"fr":["Vérifier les modifications d''implémentation par rapport aux spécifications et à la conception","Automatiser les vérifications des artefacts de modification","Déboguer les tâches d''implémentation en utilisant la lecture et l''édition de Markdown"],"de":["Überprüfen der Implementierungsänderungen gegenüber den Spezifikationen und dem Design","Automatisieren der Prüfungen von Änderungsartefakten","Fehlerbehebung von Implementierungsaufgaben unter Verwendung von Markdown-Lese- und Bearbeitungsfunktionen"],"pt":["Verificar alterações de implementação contra especificações e design","Automatizar verificações de artefatos de alteração","Depurar tarefas de implementação usando leitura e edição de Markdown"],"ru":["Проверять изменения реализации против спецификаций и дизайна","Автоматизировать проверки артефактов изменений","Отлаживать задачи реализации, используя чтение и редактирование Markdown"],"ar":["التحقق من التغييرات في التنفيذ مقابل المواصفات والتصميم","تأتمتة فحص مكونات التغيير","تصحيح أخطاء المهام التنفيذية باستخدام قراءة وتحرير Markdown"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Electron, React, and TypeScript compatibility","Must be able to run `openspec list --json` command","Limited to handling Markdown and JSON data formats"],"zh":["需要Electron、React和TypeScript兼容性","必须能够运行`openspec list --json`命令","仅限于处理Markdown和JSON数据格式"],"ja":["Electron、React、TypeScriptの互換性が必要","`openspec list --json`コマンドを実行できる必要がある","MarkdownとJSONデータ形式のみを処理可能"],"ko":["Electron, React 및 TypeScript 호환성이 필요","`openspec list --json` 명령을 실행할 수 있어야 함","Markdown 및 JSON 데이터 형식만 처리 가능"],"es":["Requiere compatibilidad con Electron, React y TypeScript","Debe poder ejecutar el comando `openspec list --json`","Limitado al manejo de formatos de datos Markdown y JSON"],"fr":["Nécessite une compatibilité avec Electron, React et TypeScript","Doit être en mesure d''exécuter la commande `openspec list --json`","Limité à la gestion des formats de données Markdown et JSON"],"de":["Benötigt Kompatibilität mit Electron, React und TypeScript","Muss das Kommando `openspec list --json` ausführen können","Begrenzt auf die Verarbeitung von Markdown- und JSON-Datenformaten"],"pt":["Exige compatibilidade com Electron, React e TypeScript","Deve ser capaz de executar o comando `openspec list --json`","Limitado ao tratamento de formatos de dados Markdown e JSON"],"ru":["Требует совместимости с Electron, React и TypeScript","Должен быть способен запускать команду `openspec list --json`","Ограничен обработкой форматов данных Markdown и JSON"],"ar":["يتطلب توافقًا مع Electron و React و TypeScript","يجب أن يكون قادرًا على تشغيل الأمر `openspec list --json`","محدود بمعالجة تنسيقات بيانات Markdown و JSON"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
