bash 도구를 사용하여 복잡한 작업을 자동화합니다","es":"La arquitectura nativa de agente permite la automatización de tareas complejas de manera autónoma y eficiente","fr":"L''architecture native d''agent permet l''automatisation de tâches complexes de manière autonome et efficace","de":"Die native Agentenarchitektur ermöglicht die Automatisierung komplexer Aufgaben auf autonome und effiziente Weise","pt":"A arquitetura nativa de agente permite a automação de tarefas complexas de forma autônoma, utilizando uma abordagem de codificação e ferramentas de sistema","ru":"Нативная архитектура агента позволяет автоматизировать сложные задачи самостоятельно, используя подход кодирования и системных инструментов","ar":"تسمح هندسة الوكلاء الأصلية بتأتمت المهام المعقدة بشكل مستقل، باستخدام نهج الترميز وأدوات النظام","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["使用LLM实现自动化","bash工具集成","复杂任务自动化","代码重构","文件管理","工作流自动化"],"ja":["LLMを使用した自動化","bashツールの統合","複雑なタスクの自動化","コードのリファクタリング","ファイル管理","ワークフローの自動化"],"ko":["LLM을 사용한 자동화","bash 도구 통합","복잡한 작업 자동화","코드 리팩토링","파일 관리","워크플로우 자동화"],"es":["Autonomía en la ejecución de tareas","Capacidad para refactorizar código","Gestión de archivos y flujos de trabajo","Integración con herramientas de línea de comandos","Ejecución de tareas complejas de manera eficiente"],"fr":["Autonomie dans l''exécution de tâches","Capacité à refactoriser du code","Gestion de fichiers et de flux de travail","Intégration avec des outils de ligne de commande","Exécution de tâches complexes de manière efficace"],"de":["Autonomie bei der Ausführung von Aufgaben","Fähigkeit, Code zu refactorisieren","Datei- und Workflow-Management","Integration mit Befehlszeilentools","Ausführung komplexer Aufgaben auf effiziente Weise"],"pt":["Automação de tarefas complexas","Utilização de codificação e ferramentas de sistema","Abordagem de aprendizado de máquina","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Flexibilidade e personalização"],"ru":["Автоматизация сложных задач","Использование кодирования и системных инструментов","Подход машинного обучения","Интеграция с инструментами разработки","Гибкость и настройка"],"ar":["تأتمت المهام المعقدة","استخدام الترميز وأدوات النظام","نهج التعلم الآلي","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير","المرونة والتخصيص"]},"keywords":{"zh":["原生架构代理","LLM","bash工具","自动化","代码重构","文件管理","工作流自动化","软件代理"],"ja":["ネイティブアーキテクチャエージェント","LLM","bashツール","自動化","コードのリファクタリング","ファイル管理","ワークフローの自動化","ソフトウェアエージェント"],"ko":["네이티브 아키텍처 에이전트","LLM","bash 도구","자동화","코드 리팩토링","파일 관리","워크플로우 자동화","소프트웨어 에이전트"],"es":["arquitectura de agente","automatización de tareas","Claude Code","agentes software","autonomía","eficiencia","refactorización de código","gestión de archivos"],"fr":["architecture d''agent","automatisation de tâches","Claude Code","agents logiciels","autonomie","efficacité","refactorisation de code","gestion de fichiers"],"de":["Agentenarchitektur","Automatisierung von Aufgaben","Claude Code","Software-Agenten","Autonomie","Effizienz","Code-Refactorisierung","Dateimanagement"],"pt":["arquitetura nativa de agente","automação de tarefas","codificação","ferramentas de sistema","aprendizado de máquina","desenvolvimento de software","integração de ferramentas"],"ru":["нативная архитектура агента","автоматизация задач","кодирование","системные инструменты","машинное обучение","разработка программного обеспечения","интеграция инструментов"],"ar":["هندسة وكلاء الأصل","تأتمت المهام","الترميز","أدوات النظام","التعلم الآلي","تطوير البرمجيات","التكامل مع الأدوات"]}},"owner":"ollieb89","repo":"orchestrator","repoPath":"ollieb89/orchestrator","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.486Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"agent-native-architecture","description":"Build applications where agents are first-class citizens. Use this skill when designing autonomous agents, creating MCP tools, implementing self-modifying systems, or building apps where features are outcomes achieved by agents operating in a loop.","bodyPreview":"<why_now>\n## Why Now\n\nSoftware agents work reliably now. Claude Code demonstrated that an LLM with access to bash and file tools, operating in a loop until an objective is achieved, can accomplish complex multi-step tasks autonomously.\n\nThe surprising discovery: **a really good coding agent is actually a really good general-purpose agent.** The same architecture that lets Claude Code refactor a codebase can let an agent organize your files, manage your reading list, or automate your workflows.","body":"<why_now>\n## Why Now\n\nSoftware agents work reliably now. Claude Code demonstrated that an LLM with access to bash and file tools, operating in a loop until an objective is achieved, can accomplish complex multi-step tasks autonomously.\n\nThe surprising discovery: **a really good coding agent is actually a really good general-purpose agent.** The same architecture that lets Claude Code refactor a codebase can let an agent organize your files, manage your reading list, or automate your workflows.\n\nThe Claude Code SDK makes this accessible. You can build applications where features aren''t code you write—they''re outcomes you describe, achieved by an agent with tools, operating in a loop until the outcome is reached.\n\nThis opens up a new field: software that works the way Claude Code works, applied to categories far beyond coding.\n</why_now>\n\n<core_principles>\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Parity\n\n**Whatever the user can do through the UI, the agent should be able to achieve through tools.**\n\nThis is the foundational principle. Without it, nothing else matters.\n\nImagine you build a notes app with a beautiful interface for creating, organizing, and tagging notes. A user asks the agent: \"Create a note summarizing my meeting and tag it as urgent.\"\n\nIf you built UI for creating notes but no agent capability to do the same, the agent is stuck. It might apologize or ask clarifying questions, but it can''t help—even though the action is trivial for a human using the interface.\n\n**The fix:** Ensure the agent has tools (or combinations of tools) that can accomplish anything the UI can do.\n\nThis isn''t about creating a 1:1 mapping of UI buttons to tools. It''s about ensuring the agent can **achieve the same outcomes**. Sometimes that''s a single tool (`create_note`). Sometimes it''s composing primitives (`write_file` to a notes directory with proper formatting).\n\n**The discipline:** When adding any UI capability, ask: can the agent achieve this outcome? If not, add the necessary tools or primitives.\n\nA capability map helps:\n\n| User Action | How Agent Achieves It |\n|-------------|----------------------|\n| Create a note | `write_file` to notes directory, or `create_note` tool |\n| Tag a note as urgent | `update_file` metadata, or `tag_note` tool |\n| Search notes | `search_files` or `search_notes` tool |\n| Delete a note | `delete_file` or `delete_note` tool |\n\n**The test:** Pick any action a user can take in your UI. Describe it to the agent. Can it accomplish the outcome?\n\n---\n\n### 2. Granularity\n\n**Prefer atomic primitives. Features are outcomes achieved by an agent operating in a loop.**\n\nA tool is a primitive capability: read a file, write a file, run a bash command, store a record, send a notification.\n\nA **feature** is not a function you write. It''s an outcome you describe in a prompt, achieved by an agent that has tools and operates in a loop until the outcome is reached.\n\n**Less granular (limits the agent):**\n```\nTool: classify_and_organize_files(files)\n→ You wrote the decision logic\n→ Agent executes your code\n→ To change behavior, you refactor\n```\n\n**More granular (empowers the agent):**\n```\nTools: read_file, write_file, move_file, list_directory, bash\nPrompt: \"Organize the user''s downloads folder. Analyze each file,\n        determine appropriate locations based on content and recency,\n        and move them there.\"\nAgent: Operates in a loop—reads files, makes judgments, moves things,\n       checks results—until the folder is organized.\n→ Agent makes the decisions\n→ To change behavior, you edit the prompt\n```\n\n**The key shift:** The agent is pursuing an outcome with judgment, not executing a choreographed sequence. It might encounter unexpected file types, adjust its approach, or ask clarifying questions. The loop continues until the outcome is achieved.\n\nThe more atomic your tools, the more flexibly the agent can use them. If you bundle decision logic into tools, you''ve moved judgment back into code.\n\n**The test:** To change how a feature behaves, do you edit prose or refactor code?\n\n---\n\n### 3. Composability\n\n**With atomic tools and parity, you can create new features just by writing new prompts.**\n\nThis is the payoff of the first two principles. When your tools are atomic and the agent can do anything users can do, new features are just new prompts.\n\nWant a \"weekly review\" feature that summarizes activity and suggests priorities? That''s a prompt:\n\n```\n\"Review files modified this week. Summarize key changes. Based on\nincomplete items and approaching deadlines, suggest three priorities\nfor next week.\"\n```\n\nThe agent uses `list_files`, `read_file`, and its judgment to accomplish this. You didn''t write weekly-review code. You described an outcome, and the agent operates in a loop until it''s achieved.\n\n**This works for developers and users.** You can ship new features by adding prompts. Users can customize behavior by modifying prompts or creating their own. \"When I say ''file this,'' always move it to my Action folder and tag it urgent\" becomes a user-level prompt that extends the application.\n\n**The constraint:** This only works if tools are atomic enough to be composed in ways you didn''t anticipate, and if the agent has parity with users. If tools encode too much logic, or the agent can''t access key capabilities, composition breaks down.\n\n**The test:** Can you add a new feature by writing a new prompt section, without adding new code?\n\n---\n\n### 4. Emergent Capability\n\n**The agent can accomplish things you didn''t explicitly design for.**\n\nWhen tools are atomic, parity is maintained, and prompts are composable, users will ask the agent for things you never anticipated. And often, the agent can figure it out.\n\n*\"Cross-reference my meeting notes with my task list and tell me what I''ve committed to but haven''t scheduled.\"*\n\nYou didn''t build a \"commitment tracker\" feature. But if the agent can read notes, read tasks, and reason about them—operating in a loop until it has an answer—it can accomplish this.\n\n**This reveals latent demand.** Instead of guessing what features users want, you observe what they''re asking the agent to do. When patterns emerge, you can optimize them with domain-specific tools or dedicated prompts. But you didn''t have to anticipate them—you discovered them.\n\n**The flywheel:**\n1. Build with atomic tools and parity\n2. Users ask for things you didn''t anticipate\n3. Agent composes tools to accomplish them (or fails, revealing a gap)\n4. You observe patterns in what''s being requested\n5. Add domain tools or prompts to make common patterns efficient\n6. Repeat\n\nThis changes how you build products. You''re not trying to imagine every feature upfront. You''re creating a capable foundation and learning from what emerges.\n\n**The test:** Give the agent an open-ended request relevant to your domain. Can it figure out a reasonable approach, operating in a loop until it succeeds? If it just says \"I don''t have a feature for that,\" your architecture is too constrained.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Improvement Over Time\n\n**Agent-native applications get better through accumulated context and prompt refinement.**\n\nUnlike traditional software, agent-native applications can improve without shipping code:\n\n**Accumulated context:** The agent can maintain state across sessions—what exists, what the user has done, what worked, what didn''t. A `context.md` file the agent reads and updates is layer one. More sophisticated approaches involve structured memory and learned preferences.\n\n**Prompt refinement at multiple levels:**\n- **Developer level:** You ship updated prompts that change agent behavior for all users\n- **User level:** Users customize prompts for their workflow\n- **Agent level:** The agent modifies its own prompts based on feedback (advanced)\n\n**Self-modification (advanced):** Agents that can edit their own prompts or even their own code. For production use cases, consider adding safety rails—approval gates, automatic checkpoints for rollback, health checks. This is where things are heading.\n\nThe improvement mechanisms are still being discovered. Context and prompt refinement are proven. Self-modification is emerging. What''s clear: the architecture supports getting better in ways traditional software doesn''t.\n\n**The test:** Does the application work better after a month of use than on day one, even without code changes?\n</core_principles>\n\n<intake>\n## What aspect of agent-native architecture do you need help with?\n\n1. **Design architecture** - Plan a new agent-native system from scratch\n2. **Files & workspace** - Use files as the universal interface, shared workspace patterns\n3. **Tool design** - Build primitive tools, dynamic capability discovery, CRUD completeness\n4. **Domain tools** - Know when to add domain tools vs stay with primitives\n5. **Execution patterns** - Completion signals, partial completion, context limits\n6. **System prompts** - Define agent behavior in prompts, judgment criteria\n7. **Context injection** - Inject runtime app state into agent prompts\n8. **Action parity** - Ensure agents can do everything users can do\n9. **Self-modification** - Enable agents to safely evolve themselves\n10. **Product design** - Progressive disclosure, latent demand, approval patterns\n11. **Mobile patterns** - iOS storage, background execution, checkpoint/resume\n12. **Testing** - Test agent-native apps for capability and parity\n13. **Refactoring** - Make existing code more agent-native\n\n**Wait for response before proceeding.**\n</intake>\n\n<routing>\n| Response | Action |\n|----------|--------|\n| 1, \"design\", \"architecture\", \"plan\" | Read [architecture-patterns.md](./references/architecture-patterns.md), then apply Architecture Checklist below |\n| 2, \"files\", \"workspace\", \"filesystem\" | Read [files-universal-interface.md](./references/files-universal-interface.md) and [shared-workspace-architecture.md](./references/shared-workspace-architecture.md) |\n| 3, \"tool\", \"mcp\", \"primitive\", \"crud\" | Read [mcp-tool-design.md](./references/mcp-tool-design.md) |\n| 4, \"domain tool\", \"when to add\" | Read [from-primitives-to-domain-tools.md](./references/from-primitives-to-domain-tools.md) |\n| 5, \"execution\", \"completion\", \"loop\" | Read [agent-execution-patterns.md](./references/agent-execution-patterns.md) |\n| 6, \"prompt\", \"system prompt\", \"behavior\" | Read [system-prompt-design.md](./references/system-prompt-design.md) |\n| 7, \"context\", \"inject\", \"runtime\", \"dynamic\" | Read [dynamic-context-injection.md](./references/dynamic-context-injection.md) |\n| 8, \"parity\", \"ui action\", \"capability map\" | Read [action-parity-discipline.md](./references/action-parity-discipline.md) |\n| 9, \"self-modify\", \"evolve\", \"git\" | Read [self-modification.md](./references/self-modification.md) |\n| 10, \"product\", \"progressive\", \"approval\", \"latent demand\" | Read [product-implications.md](./references/product-implications.md) |\n| 11, \"mobile\", \"ios\", \"android\", \"background\", \"checkpoint\" | Read [mobile-patterns.md](./references/mobile-patterns.md) |\n| 12, \"test\", \"testing\", \"verify\", \"validate\" | Read [agent-native-testing.md](./references/agent-native-testing.md) |\n| 13, \"review\", \"refactor\", \"existing\" | Read [refactoring-to-prompt-native.md](./references/refactoring-to-prompt-native.md) |\n\n**After reading the reference, apply those patterns to the user''s specific context.**\n</routing>\n\n<architecture_checklist>\n## Architecture Review Checklist\n\nWhen designing an agent-native system, verify these **before implementation**:\n\n### Core Principles\n- [ ] **Parity:** Every UI action has a corresponding agent capability\n- [ ] **Granularity:** Tools are primitives; features are prompt-defined outcomes\n- [ ] **Composability:** New features can be added via prompts alone\n- [ ] **Emergent Capability:** Agent can handle open-ended requests in your domain\n\n### Tool Design\n- [ ] **Dynamic vs Static:** For external APIs where agent should have full access, use Dynamic Capability Discovery\n- [ ] **CRUD Completeness:** Every entity has create, read, update, AND delete\n- [ ] **Primitives not Workflows:** Tools enable capability, don''t encode business logic\n- [ ] **API as Validator:** Use `z.string()` inputs when the API validates, not `z.enum()`\n\n### Files & Workspace\n- [ ] **Shared Workspace:** Agent and user work in same data space\n- [ ] **context.md Pattern:** Agent reads/updates context file for accumulated knowledge\n- [ ] **File Organization:** Entity-scoped directories with consistent naming\n\n### Agent Execution\n- [ ] **Completion Signals:** Agent has explicit `complete_task` tool (not heuristic detection)\n- [ ] **Partial Completion:** Multi-step tasks track progress for resume\n- [ ] **Context Limits:** Designed for bounded context from the start\n\n### Context Injection\n- [ ] **Available Resources:** System prompt includes what exists (files, data, types)\n- [ ] **Available Capabilities:** System prompt documents tools with user vocabulary\n- [ ] **Dynamic Context:** Context refreshes for long sessions (or provide `refresh_context` tool)\n\n### UI Integration\n- [ ] **Agent → UI:** Agent changes reflect in UI (shared service, file watching, or event bus)\n- [ ] **No Silent Actions:** Agent writes trigger UI updates immediately\n- [ ] **Capability Discovery:** Users can learn what agent can do\n\n### Mobile (if applicable)\n- [ ] **Checkpoint/Resume:** Handle iOS app suspension gracefully\n- [ ] **iCloud Storage:** iCloud-first with local fallback for multi-device sync\n- [ ] **Cost Awareness:** Model tier selection (Haiku/Sonnet/Opus)\n\n**When designing architecture, explicitly address each checkbox in your plan.**\n</architecture_checklist>\n\n<quick_start>\n## Quick Start: Build an Agent-Native Feature\n\n**Step 1: Define atomic tools**\n```typescript\nconst tools = [\n  tool(\"read_file\", \"Read any file\", { path: z.string() }, ...),\n  tool(\"write_file\", \"Write any file\", { path: z.string(), content: z.string() }, ...),\n  tool(\"list_files\", \"List directory\", { path: z.string() }, ...),\n  tool(\"complete_task\", \"Signal task completion\", { summary: z.string() }, ...),\n];\n```\n\n**Step 2: Write behavior in the system prompt**\n```markdown\n## Your Responsibilities\nWhen asked to organize content, you should:\n1. Read existing files to understand the structure\n2. Analyze what organization makes sense\n3. Create/move files using your tools\n4. Use your judgment about layout and formatting\n5. Call complete_task when you''re done\n\nYou decide the structure. Make it good.\n```\n\n**Step 3: Let the agent work in a loop**\n```typescript\nconst result = await agent.run({\n  prompt: userMessage,\n  tools: tools,\n  systemPrompt: systemPrompt,\n  // Agent loops until it calls complete_task\n});\n```\n</quick_start>\n\n<reference_index>\n## Reference Files\n\nAll references in `references/`:\n\n**Core Patterns:**\n- [architecture-patterns.md](./references/architecture-patterns.md) - Event-driven, unified orchestrator, agent-to-UI\n- [files-universal-interface.md](./references/files-universal-interface.md) - Why files, organization patterns, context.md\n- [mcp-tool-design.md](./references/mcp-tool-design.md) - Tool design, dynamic capability discovery, CRUD\n- [from-primitives-to-domain-tools.md](./references/from-primitives-to-domain-tools.md) - When to add domain tools, graduating to code\n- [agent-execution-patterns.md](./references/agent-execution-patterns.md) - Completion signals, partial completion, context limits\n- [system-prompt-design.md](./references/system-prompt-design.md) - Features as prompts, judgment criteria\n\n**Agent-Native Disciplines:**\n- [dynamic-context-injection.md](./references/dynamic-context-injection.md) - Runtime context, what to inject\n- [action-parity-discipline.md](./references/action-parity-discipline.md) - Capability mapping, parity workflow\n- [shared-workspace-architecture.md](./references/shared-workspace-architecture.md) - Shared data space, UI integration\n- [product-implications.md](./references/product-implications.md) - Progressive disclosure, latent demand, approval\n- [agent-native-testing.md](./references/agent-native-testing.md) - Testing outcomes, parity tests\n\n**Platform-Specific:**\n- [mobile-patterns.md](./references/mobile-patterns.md) - iOS storage, checkpoint/resume, cost awareness\n- [self-modification.md](./references/self-modification.md) - Git-based evolution, guardrails\n- [refactoring-to-prompt-native.md](./references/refactoring-to-prompt-native.md) - Migrating existing code\n</reference_index>\n\n<anti_patterns>\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n### Common Approaches That Aren''t Fully Agent-Native\n\nThese aren''t necessarily wrong—they may be appropriate for your use case. But they''re worth recognizing as different from the architecture this document describes.\n\n**Agent as router** — The agent figures out what the user wants, then calls the right function. The agent''s intelligence is used to route, not to act. This can work, but you''re using a fraction of what agents can do.\n\n**Build the app, then add agent** — You build features the traditional way (as code), then expose them to an agent. The agent can only do what your features already do. You won''t get emergent capability.\n\n**Request/response thinking** — Agent gets input, does one thing, returns output. This misses the loop: agent gets an outcome to achieve, operates until it''s done, handles unexpected situations along the way.\n\n**Defensive tool design** — You over-constrain tool inputs because you''re used to defensive programming. Strict enums, validation at every layer. This is safe, but it prevents the agent from doing things you didn''t anticipate.\n\n**Happy path in code, agent just executes** — Traditional software handles edge cases in code—you write the logic for what happens when X goes wrong. Agent-native lets the agent handle edge cases with judgment. If your code handles all the edge cases, the agent is just a caller.\n\n---\n\n### Specific Anti-Patterns\n\n**THE CARDINAL SIN: Agent executes your code instead of figuring things out**\n\n```typescript\n// WRONG - You wrote the workflow, agent just executes it\ntool(\"process_feedback\", async ({ message }) => {\n  const category = categorize(message);      // Your code decides\n  const priority = calculatePriority(message); // Your code decides\n  await store(message, category, priority);   // Your code orchestrates\n  if (priority > 3) await notify();           // Your code decides\n});\n\n// RIGHT - Agent figures out how to process feedback\ntools: store_item, send_message  // Primitives\nprompt: \"Rate importance 1-5 based on actionability, store feedback, notify if >= 4\"\n```\n\n**Workflow-shaped tools** — `analyze_and_organize` bundles judgment into the tool. Break it into primitives and let the agent compose them.\n\n**Context starvation** — Agent doesn''t know what resources exist in the app.\n```\nUser: \"Write something about Catherine the Great in my feed\"\nAgent: \"What feed? I don''t understand what system you''re referring to.\"\n```\nFix: Inject available resources, capabilities, and vocabulary into system prompt.\n\n**Orphan UI actions** — User can do something through the UI that the agent can''t achieve. Fix: maintain parity.\n\n**Silent actions** — Agent changes state but UI doesn''t update. Fix: Use shared data stores with reactive binding, or file system observation.\n\n**Heuristic completion detection** — Detecting agent completion through heuristics (consecutive iterations without tool calls, checking for expected output files). This is fragile. Fix: Require agents to explicitly signal completion through a `complete_task` tool.\n\n**Static tool mapping for dynamic APIs** — Building 50 tools for 50 API endpoints when a `discover` + `access` pattern would give more flexibility.\n```typescript\n// WRONG - Every API type needs a hardcoded tool\ntool(\"read_steps\", ...)\ntool(\"read_heart_rate\", ...)\ntool(\"read_sleep\", ...)\n// When glucose tracking is added... code change required\n\n// RIGHT - Dynamic capability discovery\ntool(\"list_available_types\", ...)  // Discover what''s available\ntool(\"read_health_data\", { dataType: z.string() }, ...)  // Access any type\n```\n\n**Incomplete CRUD** — Agent can create but not update or delete.\n```typescript\n// User: \"Delete that journal entry\"\n// Agent: \"I don''t have a tool for that\"\ntool(\"create_journal_entry\", ...)  // Missing: update, delete\n```\nFix: Every entity needs full CRUD.\n\n**Sandbox isolation** — Agent works in separate data space from user.\n```\nDocuments/\n├── user_files/        ← User''s space\n└── agent_output/      ← Agent''s space (isolated)\n```\nFix: Use shared workspace where both operate on same files.\n\n**Gates without reason** — Domain tool is the only way to do something, and you didn''t intend to restrict access. The default is open. Keep primitives available unless there''s a specific reason to gate.\n\n**Artificial capability limits** — Restricting what the agent can do out of vague safety concerns rather than specific risks. Be thoughtful about restricting capabilities. The agent should generally be able to do what users can do.\n</anti_patterns>\n\n<success_criteria>\n## Success Criteria\n\nYou''ve built an agent-native application when:\n\n### Architecture\n- [ ] The agent can achieve anything users can achieve through the UI (parity)\n- [ ] Tools are atomic primitives; domain tools are shortcuts, not gates (granularity)\n- [ ] New features can be added by writing new prompts (composability)\n- [ ] The agent can accomplish tasks you didn''t explicitly design for (emergent capability)\n- [ ] Changing behavior means editing prompts, not refactoring code\n\n### Implementation\n- [ ] System prompt includes dynamic context about app state\n- [ ] Every UI action has a corresponding agent tool (action parity)\n- [ ] Agent tools are documented in system prompt with user vocabulary\n- [ ] Agent and user work in the same data space (shared workspace)\n- [ ] Agent actions are immediately reflected in the UI\n- [ ] Every entity has full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete)\n- [ ] Agents explicitly signal completion (no heuristic detection)\n- [ ] context.md or equivalent for accumulated knowledge\n\n### Product\n- [ ] Simple requests work immediately with no learning curve\n- [ ] Power users can push the system in unexpected directions\n- [ ] You''re learning what users want by observing what they ask the agent to do\n- [ ] Approval requirements match stakes and reversibility\n\n### Mobile (if applicable)\n- [ ] Checkpoint/resume handles app interruption\n- [ ] iCloud-first storage with local fallback\n- [ ] Background execution uses available time wisely\n- [ ] Model tier matched to task complexity\n\n---\n\n### The Ultimate Test\n\n**Describe an outcome to the agent that''s within your application''s domain but that you didn''t build a specific feature for.**\n\nCan it figure out how to accomplish it, operating in a loop until it succeeds?\n\nIf yes, you''ve built something agent-native.\n\nIf it says \"I don''t have a feature for that\"—your architecture is still too constrained.\n</success_criteria>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T10:12:04.001Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for General-Purpose Agents needing autonomous multi-step task execution capabilities via bash and file tools","zh":"非常适合需要通过bash和文件工具实现自主多步任务执行的通用目的代理","ja":"bashとファイルツールを使用して自律的なマルチステップタスク実行を必要とする汎用エージェントに最適","ko":"bash와 파일 도구를 통해 자율적인 멀티스텝 태스크 실행을 필요로 하는 일반 목적 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Propósito General que necesitan capacidades de ejecución de tareas autónomas de varios pasos a través de bash y herramientas de archivos","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents à Usage Général ayant besoin de capacités d''exécution de tâches autonome à plusieurs étapes via bash et outils de fichiers","de":"Perfekt für Allzweckagenten, die autonome Ausführungsfähigkeiten für mehrschrittige Aufgaben über bash und Datei-Tools benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Propósito Geral que necessitam de capacidades de execução de tarefas autônomas multi-etapa via bash e ferramentas de arquivo","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов общего назначения, требующих автономных возможностей выполнения многоступенчатых задач через bash и файловые инструменты","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء العامة الغرض الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات تنفيذ المهام αυτόنوموس متعددة الخطوات من خلال bash وأدوات الملف"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to accomplish complex tasks autonomously using LLMs, accessing bash and file tools in a loop until objectives are achieved, and leveraging architectures like Claude Code for refactorization and workflow automation via protocols and file formats","zh":"赋予代理通过LLM、访问bash和文件工具在循环中直到实现目标，并利用像Claude Code这样的架构进行重构和工作流自动化的能力","ja":"エージェントに、LLMを使用してbashとファイルツールにアクセスし、オブジェクトを達成するまでループし、Claude Codeなどのアーキテクチャを使用してリファクタリングとワークフローの自動化を実現する能力を与える","ko":"에이전트가 LLM을 사용하여 bash와 파일 도구에 접근하고, 목표를 달성할 때까지 루프를 실행하며, Claude Code와 같은 아키텍처를 활용하여 리팩토링과 워크플로 자동화를 수행할 수 있는 능력을 부여","es":"Empodera a los agentes para realizar tareas complejas de forma autónoma utilizando LLM, accediendo a bash y herramientas de archivos en un bucle hasta que se logren los objetivos, y aprovechando arquitecturas como Claude Code para la refactorización y la automatización del flujo de trabajo a través de protocolos y formatos de archivo","fr":"Autonomise les agents pour réaliser des tâches complexes en utilisant les LLM, en accédant à bash et aux outils de fichiers dans une boucle jusqu''à ce que les objectifs soient atteints, et en exploitant des architectures comme Claude Code pour la refactorisation et l''automatisation du flux de travail via des protocoles et des formats de fichiers","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, komplexe Aufgaben autonom durchzuführen, indem LLM verwendet werden, auf bash und Datei-Tools in einer Schleife zugegriffen wird, bis die Ziele erreicht sind, und indem Architekturen wie Claude Code für die Refaktorierung und die Workflow-Automatisierung über Protokolle und Dateiformate genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar tarefas complexas de forma autônoma usando LLMs, acessando bash e ferramentas de arquivo em um loop até que os objetivos sejam alcançados, e aproveitando arquiteturas como Claude Code para refatoração e automação de fluxo de trabalho via protocolos e formatos de arquivo","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять сложные задачи автономно с помощью LLM, доступом к bash и файловым инструментам в цикле до достижения целей, и использует архитектуры như Claude Code для рефакторинга и автоматизации рабочих процессов через протоколы и форматы файлов","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنجاز مهام معقدة بشكل tự động باستخدام LLMs، وصول إلى bash وأدوات الملف في حلقة حتى تتحقق الأهداف، واستخدام الهياكل مثل Claude Code لتحديث وتنظيم تدفق العمل من خلال البروتوكولات وأشكال الملفات"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating workflow management","Organizing file systems","Refactoring codebases","Managing reading lists"],"zh":["自动化工作流管理","组织文件系统","重构代码库","管理阅读列表"],"ja":["ワークフローの自動化","ファイルシステムの整理","コードベースのリファクタリング","読書リストの管理"],"ko":["워크플로우 관리 자동화","파일 시스템 구성","코드베이스 리팩토링","읽기 목록 관리"],"es":["Automatización de la gestión del flujo de trabajo","Organización de sistemas de archivos","Refactorización de bases de código","Gestión de listas de lectura"],"fr":["Automatisation de la gestion du flux de travail","Organisation des systèmes de fichiers","Refactorisation des bases de code","Gestion des listes de lecture"],"de":["Automatisierung der Workflow-Verwaltung","Organisation von Dateisystemen","Refaktorierung von Codebasen","Verwaltung von Lese listen"],"pt":["Automatizar gerenciamento de fluxo de trabalho","Organizar sistemas de arquivos","Refatorar bases de código","Gerenciar listas de leitura"],"ru":["Автоматизация управления рабочим процессом","Организация файловых систем","Рефакторинг кодовых баз","Управление списками чтения"],"ar":["تأتمتة إدارة تدفق العمل","تنظيم أنظمة الملفات","إعادة هيكلة قواعد البيانات","إدارة قوائم القراءة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to bash and file tools","LLM capabilities necessary","Looping mechanism needed for objective achievement"],"zh":["需要访问bash和文件工具","需要LLM能力","需要循环机制来实现目标"],"ja":["bashとファイルツールへのアクセスが必要","LLMの機能が必要","オブジェクトを達成するためのループメカニズムが必要"],"ko":["bash와 파일 도구에 대한 접근이 필요","LLM 기능이 필요","목표를 달성하기 위한 루프 메커니즘 필요"],"es":["Requiere acceso a bash y herramientas de archivos","Se necesitan capacidades de LLM","Se necesita un mecanismo de bucle para el logro de objetivos"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès à bash et aux outils de fichiers","Des capacités de LLM sont nécessaires","Un mécanisme de boucle est nécessaire pour la réalisation des objectifs"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf bash und Datei-Tools","LLM-Fähigkeiten sind erforderlich","Ein Schleifmechanismus ist für die Erreichung der Ziele erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso a bash e ferramentas de arquivo","Capacidades LLM necessárias","Mecanismo de looping necessário para alcance de objetivos"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к bash и файловым инструментам","Необходимы возможности LLM","Необходим механизм цикла для достижения целей"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى bash وأدوات الملف","القدرات LLM ضرورية","آلية الحلق ضرورية لتحقيق الأهداف"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('hutchic/.cursor/ensure-feature-branch', 'community', 'hutchic', '.cursor', 'hutchic/.cursor', 'ensure-feature-branch', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.486Z', '2026-02-18T10:12:12.521Z', NULL, '{"id":"hutchic/.cursor/ensure-feature-branch","name":"ensure-feature-branch","description":{"zh":"确保功能分支是一种自动化技能，用于防止直接提交到主线或发布分支","ja":"機能ブランチの確保は、メインラインまたはリリースブランチへの直接コミットを防ぐ自動化スキルです","ko":"기능 분기 보장은 메인 라인 또는 릴리스 분기에直接 커밋하지 않도록 하는 자동화 기능입니다","es":"La herramienta de rama de función garantiza que los commits se realicen en una rama de función o de error, evitando así cambios directos en mainline o release.","fr":"L''outil de branche de fonctionnalité garantit que les commits sont effectués sur une branche de fonctionnalité ou de bogue, évitant ainsi les modifications directes sur mainline ou release.","de":"Das Feature-Branch-Tool stellt sicher, dass Commits in einem Feature- oder Fehlerbranch durchgeführt werden, wodurch direkte Änderungen an Mainline oder Release vermieden werden.","pt":"O skill ensure-feature-branch garante que o trabalho não seja comprometido ou enviado diretamente para a mainline ou release. Ele cria e verifica uma nova branch, se necessário.","ru":"Навык ensure-feature-branch гарантирует, что работа не будет зафиксирована или отправлена напрямую в mainline или release. Он создает и проверяет новую ветку, если это необходимо.","ar":"المهارة ensure-feature-branch تضمن أن لا يتم الالتزام أو الإرسال مباشرة إلى الخط الرئيسي أو الإصدار. إنها تخلق وتتحقق من فرع جديد إذا لزم الأمر.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"确保功能分支","ja":"機能ブランチの確保","ko":"기능 분기 보장","es":"Herramienta de rama de función: asegure su flujo de trabajo","fr":"Outil de branche de fonctionnalité: sécurisez votre workflow","de":"Feature-Branch-Tool: Sichern Sie Ihren Workflow","pt":"Garantir Ramo de Recurso com ensure-feature-branch","ru":"Обеспечить ветку функций с ensure-feature-branch","ar":"ضمان فرع الميزة مع ensure-feature-branch","en":"ensure-feature-branch"},"description":{"zh":"确保功能分支是一种自动化技能，用于防止直接提交到主线或发布分支","ja":"機能ブランチの確保は、メインラインまたはリリースブランチへの直接コミットを防ぐ自動化スキルです","ko":"기능 분기 보장은 메인 라인 또는 릴리스 분기에直接 커밋하지 않도록 하는 자동화 기능입니다","es":"La herramienta de rama de función garantiza que los commits se realicen en una rama de función o de error, evitando así cambios directos en mainline o release.","fr":"L''outil de branche de fonctionnalité garantit que les commits sont effectués sur une branche de fonctionnalité ou de bogue, évitant ainsi les modifications d...","de":"Das Feature-Branch-Tool stellt sicher, dass Commits in einem Feature- oder Fehlerbranch durchgeführt werden, wodurch direkte Änderungen an Mainline oder Rele...","pt":"O skill ensure-feature-branch garante que o trabalho não seja comprometido ou enviado diretamente para a mainline ou release. Ele cria e verifica uma nova br...","ru":"Навык ensure-feature-branch гарантирует, что работа не будет зафиксирована или отправлена напрямую в mainline или release. Он создает и проверяет новую ветку...","ar":"المهارة ensure-feature-branch تضمن أن لا يتم الالتزام أو الإرسال مباشرة إلى الخط الرئيسي أو الإصدار. إنها تخلق وتتحقق من فرع جديد إذا لزم الأمر.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["防止直接提交到主线或发布分支","自动创建和切换到新分支","支持pre-commit hook、命令或手动请求","确保工作不直接提交或推送到主线或发布分支","支持多种分支场景"],"ja":["メインラインまたはリリースブランチへの直接コミットを防ぐ","新しいブランチの自動作成と切替","pre-commit hook、コマンド、または手動リクエストのサポート","メインラインまたはリリースブランチへの直接コミットやプッシュを防ぐ","複数のブランチシナリオのサポート"],"ko":["메인 라인 또는 릴리스 분기에 직접 커밋하지 않도록 합니다","새로운 분기의 자동 생성 및 전환","pre-commit hook, 명령 또는 수동 요청의 지원","메인 라인 또는 릴리스 분기에 직접 커밋 또는 푸시하지 않도록 합니다","여러 분기 시나리오의 지원"],"es":["Evita commits directos en mainline o release","Crea y cambia a una nueva rama si es necesario","Se puede utilizar como parte de la automatización","Compatible con hooks de pre-commit","Funciona con solicitudes manuales"],"fr":["Évite les commits directs sur mainline ou release","Crée et bascule sur une nouvelle branche si nécessaire","Peut être utilisé comme partie de l''automatisation","Compatible avec les hooks de pré-commit","Fonctionne avec les requêtes manuelles"],"de":["Vermeidet direkte Commits auf Mainline oder Release","Erstellt und wechselt zu einem neuen Branch, wenn erforderlich","Kann als Teil der Automatisierung verwendet werden","Kompatibel mit Pre-Commit-Hooks","Funktioniert mit manuellen Anfragen"],"pt":["Garante que o trabalho não seja comprometido na mainline ou release","Cria e verifica uma nova branch, se necessário","Pode ser usado como parte de automação, como hook de pré-compromisso","Evita compromissos diretos na mainline ou release","Melhora a organização do código"],"ru":["Гарантирует, что работа не будет зафиксирована в mainline или release","Создает и проверяет новую ветку, если это необходимо","Может быть использован как часть автоматизации, например, хук pré-коммита","Избегает прямых коммитов в mainline или release","Улучшает организацию кода"],"ar":["تضمن أن لا يتم الالتزام بالعمل على الخط الرئيسي أو الإصدار","تخلق وتتحقق من فرع جديد، إذا لزم الأمر","يمكن استخدامها كجزء من الأتمتة، مثل hook الإلتزام المسبق","تجنب الالتزامات المباشرة في الخط الرئيسي أو الإصدار","تحسن تنظيم الرمز"]},"keywords":{"zh":["确保功能分支","自动化技能","git分支","pre-commit hook","代码审查","自动化测试","持续集成","devops"],"ja":["機能ブランチの確保","自動化スキル","gitブランチ","pre-commit hook","コードレビュー","自動テスト","継続的インテグレーション","devops"],"ko":["기능 분기 보장","자동화 기능","git 분기","pre-commit hook","코드 리뷰","자동 테스트","지속적 통합","devops"],"es":["rama de función","herramienta de rama de función","control de versiones","desarrollo de software","automatización","pre-commit hook"],"fr":["branche de fonctionnalité","outil de branche de fonctionnalité","contrôle de version","développement de logiciels","automatisation","hook de pré-commit"],"de":["Feature-Branch","Feature-Branch-Tool","Versionskontrolle","Softwareentwicklung","Automatisierung","Pre-Commit-Hook"],"pt":["ensure-feature-branch","git branch","mainline","release","compromisso","automatização","organização de código"],"ru":["ensure-feature-branch","git ветка","mainline","release","коммит","автоматизация","организация кода"],"ar":["ensure-feature-branch","فرع جيت","الخط الرئيسي","الإصدار","الالتزام","الأتمتة","تنظيم الرمز"]}},"owner":"hutchic","repo":".cursor","repoPath":"hutchic/.cursor","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.486Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ensure-feature-branch","description":"Ensure were on a feature or bug branch. If current branch is mainline (main, master, dev) or a release branch (release/*), create and checkout a new branch. Use when a workflow or user request should avoid committing or pushing directly to mainline or release.","bodyPreview":"# Ensure Feature Branch Skill\n\nEnsure the current branch is a feature or bug branch. If it is a mainline or release branch, create and checkout a new branch so commits are not made on mainline/release. Use this skill on its own or as part of any automation (e.g. pre-commit hook, command, or manual request).\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Use when you need to ensure work is not committed or pushed directly to mainline or release\n- Use when the user asks to commit/push and the current branch is main, master,","body":"# Ensure Feature Branch Skill\n\nEnsure the current branch is a feature or bug branch. If it is a mainline or release branch, create and checkout a new branch so commits are not made on mainline/release. Use this skill on its own or as part of any automation (e.g. pre-commit hook, command, or manual request).\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Use when you need to ensure work is not committed or pushed directly to mainline or release\n- Use when the user asks to commit/push and the current branch is main, master, dev, or release/*\n- Use in any workflow that requires a feature/bug branch before subsequent steps (e.g. stage, commit, push)\n\n## Mainline and Release Branches\n\nTreat these as **not** feature/bug branches; create a new branch if current branch is one of:\n\n- **Mainline**: `main`, `master`, `dev`\n- **Release**: Any branch matching `release/*` (e.g. `release/1.0`, `release/2.x`)\n\nRepos may use different default branch names (e.g. `trunk`, `development`). If the repo clearly uses another name as the primary integration branch, treat it as mainline.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Get current branch: `git branch --show-current`\n2. If it is a mainline or release branch (as above), create a new branch and checkout:\n   - **Branch name**: Infer from the changes (files/diff) a short kebab-case description. Use `feat/<description>` for features or `fix/<description>` for fixes. If the change type is unclear, use `feat/<description>` or a neutral `chore/<description>`.\n   - Run: `git checkout -b <branch-name>`\n3. If already on a feature/bug branch (e.g. `feat/...`, `fix/...`, or any branch not mainline/release), do nothing and proceed.\n\n## Notes\n\n- When used in a multi-step flow (e.g. before stage → commit → push), run this first so the first commit lands on the new branch.\n- Do not create a branch if already on a non-mainline, non-release branch (e.g. existing `feat/xyz` or an updatecli branch).\n\n## Related Artifacts\n\n- [Shipit Command](.cursor/commands/shipit.md)\n- [Stage Related Files Skill](.cursor/skills/git/stage-related-files/SKILL.md)\n- [Terse Semantic Commits Skill](.cursor/skills/git/terse-semantic-commits/SKILL.md)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T10:12:12.521Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Version Control Agents needing automated branch management capabilities.","zh":"适合需要自动分支管理功能的版本控制代理。","ja":"バージョン管理エージェントが自動ブランチ管理機能を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"자동 분기 관리 기능이 필요한 버전 제어 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de control de versiones que necesitan capacidades de gestión de ramas automatizadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de contrôle de version nécessitant des capacités de gestion de branches automatisées.","de":"Perfekt für Versionierungssysteme, die automatisierte Verzweigungsverwaltungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Controle de Versão que precisam de capacidades de gerenciamento de branch automatizado.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов системы контроля версий, которым необходимы автоматические возможности управления ветками.","ar":"مثالي لعميل نظام التحكم في الإصدار الذي يحتاج إلى قدرات إدارة الفرع الآلي."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to enforce feature branch workflows using pre-commit hooks and command-line interfaces, ensuring commits are not made directly to mainline or release branches via protocols like Git.","zh":"赋予代理人使用预提交钩子和命令行接口强制执行功能分支工作流程的能力，确保提交不会直接通过Git等协议提交到主线或发布分支。","ja":"事前コミットフックやコマンドラインインターフェイスを使用して機能ブランチのワークフローを強制する機能をエージェントに与え、Gitなどのプロトコルを介してコミットがメインラインまたはリリースブランチに直接行われないことを保証します。","ko":"기능 분기 워크플로우를 강제하는 기능을 에이전트에게 부여하여 Git과 같은 프로토콜을 통해 커밋이 메인 라인 또는 릴리즈 분기에 직접 수행되지 않도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar flujos de trabajo de ramas de características utilizando ganchos pre-commit y interfaces de línea de comandos, garantizando que los commits no se realicen directamente en las ramas principales o de lanzamiento a través de protocolos como Git.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer des flux de travail de branches de fonctionnalités à l''aide de crochets pre-commit et d''interfaces de ligne de commande, garantissant que les validations ne soient pas effectuées directement sur les branches principales ou de publication via des protocoles comme Git.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Workflows für Feature-Branches mithilfe von Pre-Commit-Hooks und Kommandozeilen-Schnittstellen durchzusetzen, sodass Commits nicht direkt an die Haupt- oder Release-Branches über Protokolle wie Git durchgeführt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a impor fluxos de trabalho de branch de recursos usando ganchos pré-compromisso e interfaces de linha de comando, garantindo que os compromissos não sejam feitos diretamente na linha principal ou nas branches de lançamento por meio de protocolos como o Git.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью обеспечивать соблюдение рабочих процессов веток функций с помощью крючков до фиксации и командных интерфейсов, гарантируя, что фиксации не производятся直接 в основную ветку или ветки релиза через протоколы như Git.","ar":"يعزز الوكيل القدرة على فرض سير عمل فرع الميزة باستخدام كوابص ما قبل الالتزام وواجهات سطر الأوامر، وضمان عدم إجراء الالتزامات مباشرة إلى الفرع الرئيسي أو إصدارات الفرع عبر بروتوكولات مثل Git."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating branch creation for new features","Validating branch types before committing changes","Preventing accidental pushes to mainline branches"],"zh":["为新功能自动创建分支","在提交更改之前验证分支类型","防止意外推送到主线分支"],"ja":["新機能の自動ブランチ作成","コミット変更前にブランチタイプを検証する","メインラインブランチへの誤ったプッシュを防ぐ"],"ko":["새로운 기능을 위한 자동 분기 생성","변경 사항을 커밋하기 전에 분기 유형을 확인","메인 라인 분기への 잘못된 푸시 방지"],"es":["Automatizar la creación de ramas para nuevas características","Validar los tipos de ramas antes de realizar cambios","Prevenir envíos accidentales a ramas principales"],"fr":["Automatiser la création de branches pour de nouvelles fonctionnalités","Valider les types de branches avant d''apporter des modifications","Empêcher les poussées accidentelles vers les branches principales"],"de":["Automatisieren der Erstellung von Verzweigungen für neue Funktionen","Überprüfen der Verzweigungstypen vor dem Einchecken von Änderungen","Verhindern von unbeabsichtigten Pushes an die Hauptverzweigungen"],"pt":["Automatizar a criação de branch para novos recursos","Validar tipos de branch antes de fazer alterações","Prevenir pushes acidentais para branches principais"],"ru":["Автоматизировать создание веток для новых функций","Проверять типы веток перед внесением изменений","Предотвращать случайные публикации в основные ветки"],"ar":["تأتمتة إنشاء الفرع για الميزات الجديدة","تحقق من أنواع الفروع قبل إجراء التغييرات","منع الالتزامات العرضية إلى الفروع الرئيسية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git version control system","Limited to feature and bug branch management"],"zh":["需要Git版本控制系统","仅限于功能和bug分支管理"],"ja":["Gitバージョン管理システムが必要","機能およびバグブランチ管理に限定される"],"ko":["Git 버전 제어 시스템이 필요함","기능 및 버그 분기 관리에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere el sistema de control de versiones Git","Limitado a la gestión de ramas de características y errores"],"fr":["Nécessite le système de contrôle de version Git","Limité à la gestion des branches de fonctionnalités et de bogues"],"de":["Erfordert das Git-Versionierungssystem","Begrenzt auf die Verwaltung von Feature- und Bug-Verzweigungen"],"pt":["Requer sistema de controle de versão Git","Limitado ao gerenciamento de branch de recursos e bugs"],"ru":["Требуется система контроля версий Git","Ограничен только управлением ветками функций и ошибок"],"ar":["يتطلب نظام التحكم في الإصدار Git","محدود فقط بإدارة فرع الميزة والخطأ"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('worm-13/pet-design-agent/image-quality-enhancement', 'community', 'worm-13', 'pet-design-agent', 'worm-13/pet-design-agent', 'image-quality-enhancement', 0, 0, 60, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.486Z', '2026-02-18T10:12:25.591Z', NULL, '{"id":"worm-13/pet-design-agent/image-quality-enhancement","name":"image-quality-enhancement","description":{"zh":"本技能利用Laplacian方差计算图像清晰度分数，并通过Real-ESRGAN对图像进行超分/增强","ja":"このスキルはラプラシアン方差を使用して画像のクオリティースコアを計算し、Real-ESRGANを使用して画像を超分/強化","ko":"이 기술은 라플라시안 분산을 사용하여 이미지의 퀄리티 점수를 계산하고 Real-ESRGAN을 사용하여 이미지의 초해상도/강화","es":"Nuestra herramienta de mejora de calidad de imagen utiliza Real-ESRGAN para evaluar y mejorar la calidad de las imágenes. Proporciona una imagen de entrada y ajusta la claridad según sea necesario.","fr":"Notre outil d''amélioration de la qualité d''image utilise Real-ESRGAN pour évaluer et améliorer la qualité des images. Fournissez une image d''entrée et ajustez la clarté selon les besoins.","de":"Unser Bildqualitätsverbesserungstool verwendet Real-ESRGAN, um die Qualität von Bildern zu bewerten und zu verbessern. Geben Sie ein Bild ein und passen Sie die Klarheit nach Bedarf an.","pt":"O skill de melhoria de qualidade de imagem utiliza o Real-ESRGAN para avaliar e melhorar a clareza das imagens, produzindo resultados de alta qualidade","ru":"Навык улучшения качества изображений использует Real-ESRGAN для оценки и улучшения четкости изображений, производя результаты высокого качества","ar":"مهارة تحسين جودة الصورة تستخدم Real-ESRGAN لتقييم و تحسين وضوح الصور، و إنتاج نتائج عالية الجودة","en":"ovo"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"图像清晰度提升技术","ja":"画像クオリティー向上技術","ko":"이미지 퀄리티 향상 기술","es":"Mejora de calidad de imagen con Real-ESRGAN","fr":"Amélioration de la qualité d''image avec Real-ESRGAN","de":"Bildqualitätsverbesserung mit Real-ESRGAN","pt":"Melhorar Qualidade de Imagem com Rea