omas 的编程哲学，强调 Domain-Driven Design 和 Functional Core 等原则","ja":"私の React ルールは Dave Thomas のコード哲学に基づいており、Domain-Driven Design と Functional Core などの原則を重視","ko":"私の React 규칙은 Dave Thomas의 코딩 철학을 기반으로 하며 Domain-Driven Design와 Functional Core 등을 강조합니다","es":"Reglas y principios de codificación para desarrollar aplicaciones React de manera efectiva","fr":"Règles et principes de codage pour développer des applications React de manière efficace","de":"Regeln und Codierprinzipien für die effektive Entwicklung von React-Anwendungen","pt":"Desenvolva aplicativos React com eficiência, seguindo princípios de design orientado a domínio e programação funcional","ru":"Разрабатывайте приложения React эффективно, следуя принципам домен-ориентированного дизайна и функционального программирования","ar":"قم ببناء تطبيقات React بفعالية، باتباع مبادئ التصميم الموجه إلى المجال والبرمجة الوظيفية","en":"Follow up with up Yihui to complete your personal AI programming practice"},"definition":{"en":"Follow up with up Yihui to complete your personal AI programming practice"},"features":{"zh":["Domain-Driven Design","Functional Core, Imperative Shell","Explicit Over Implicit","Composition Over Inheritance"],"ja":["ドメイン駆動設計","関数型コア、命令型シェル","明示的優先","コンポジション_over_継承"],"ko":["도메인 주도 설계","함수형 코어, 명령형 셸","명시적 우선","Composition Over Inheritance"],"es":["Diseño de dominio","Núcleo funcional, capa imperativa","Explicitar sobre implícito","Composición sobre herencia","Uso de versiones actualizadas de paquetes y bibliotecas"],"fr":["Conception de domaine","Noyau fonctionnel, couche impérative","Explicitation sur implicite","Composition sur héritage","Utilisation de versions mises à jour de paquets et de bibliothèques"],"de":["Domain-Design","Funktionales Kern, imperatives Shell","Explizit über Implizit","Komposition über Vererbung","Verwendung von aktuellen Versionen von Paketen und Bibliotheken"],"pt":["Design orientado a domínio","Programação funcional","Núcleo funcional, shell imperativo","Composição sobre herança","Explicitação sobre implicitação"],"ru":["Домен-ориентированный дизайн","Функциональное программирование","Функциональное ядро, императивная оболочка","Композиция над наследованием","Явное над неявным"],"ar":["تصميم موجه إلى المجال","البرمجة الوظيفية","النواة الوظيفية، الغلاف الامر","التركيب على الوراثة","التوضيح على الغموض"]},"keywords":{"zh":["React 编程","Domain-Driven Design","Functional Core","Explicit Over Implicit","Composition Over Inheritance","Dave Thomas"],"ja":["React プログラミング","ドメイン駆動設計","関数型コア","明示的優先","コンポジション_over_継承","Dave Thomas"],"ko":["React 프로그래밍","도메인 주도 설계","함수형 코어","명시적 우선","Composition Over Inheritance","Dave Thomas"],"es":["React","desarrollo de aplicaciones","mejores prácticas","principios de codificación","diseño de dominio","núcleo funcional","composición sobre herencia"],"fr":["React","développement d''applications","meilleures pratiques","principes de codage","conception de domaine","noyau fonctionnel","composition sur héritage"],"de":["React","Anwendungsentwicklung","beste Praktiken","Codierprinzipien","Domain-Design","funktionales Kern","Komposition über Vererbung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento React","melhores práticas","design orientado a domínio","programação funcional","ReactJS","desenvolvedores React"],"ru":["разработка React","лучшие практики","домен-ориентированный дизайн","функциональное программирование","ReactJS","разработчики React"],"ar":["التطوير التفاعلي","أفضل الممارسات","تصميم موجه إلى المجال","البرمجة الوظيفية","ReactJS","منطق التفاعل"]}},"owner":"Aafff623","repo":"yihui-vibe-coding-exer","repoPath":"Aafff623/yihui-vibe-coding-exer","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.486Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"my-react-rules","description":"This is a new rule","bodyPreview":"# Overview\n\n# Elixir and Phoenix Best Practices\n\n_Based on Dave Thomas'' (PragDave) coding philosophy_\nImportant: always use lates versions of packages and libraries, including Phoenix.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n- **Domain-Driven Design**: Organize code around business domains, not technical layers\n- **Functional Core, Imperative Shell**: Pure domain logic with side effects at boundaries\n- **Explicit Over Implicit**: Prefer clarity over magic\n- **Composition Over Inheritance**: Build systems from smal","body":"# Overview\n\n# Elixir and Phoenix Best Practices\n\n_Based on Dave Thomas'' (PragDave) coding philosophy_\nImportant: always use lates versions of packages and libraries, including Phoenix.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n- **Domain-Driven Design**: Organize code around business domains, not technical layers\n- **Functional Core, Imperative Shell**: Pure domain logic with side effects at boundaries\n- **Explicit Over Implicit**: Prefer clarity over magic\n- **Composition Over Inheritance**: Build systems from small, focused components\n- **Single Responsibility**: Each module and function should do one thing well\n- **Easy to Change**: Design for maintainability and future change\n- **Fail Fast**: Detect and handle errors as early as possible\n- **YAGNI**: Don''t build features until they''re needed\n\n## Project Structure\n\n- **Context-Based Organization**: Use Phoenix contexts to define domain boundaries\n  lib/my_app/\n  accounts/ # User management domain\n  billing/ # Payment processing domain\n  catalog/ # Product catalog domain\n\n- **API/Implementation Separation**: Public API modules delegate to implementation modules\n\n  # In MyApp.Accounts (API module)\n\n  defdelegate create_user(attrs), to: MyApp.Accounts.UserCreator\n\n- **Boundary Enforcement**: Use tools like NimbleOptions to validate inputs at boundaries\n\n## Coding Patterns\n\n- **Pattern Matching**: Use pattern matching in function heads for control flow\n- **Railway-Oriented Programming**: Chain operations with ''with'' for elegant error handling\n\n  with {:ok, user} <- find_user(id),\n  {:ok, updated} <- update_user(user, attrs) do\n  {:ok, updated}\n  end\n\n- **Type Specifications**: Add typespecs to all public functions\n\n  @spec create_user(user_attrs()) :: {:ok, User.t()} | {:error, Changeset.t()}\n\n- **Immutable Data Transformations**: Return new state rather than modifying existing state\n\n- **Data Validation**: Validate data at boundaries using Ecto.Changeset even outside of database contexts\n\n  def validate_attrs(attrs) do\n  {%{}, %{name: :string, email: :string}}\n  |> Ecto.Changeset.cast(attrs, [:name, :email])\n  |> Ecto.Changeset.validate_required([:name, :email])\n  |> Ecto.Changeset.validate_format(:email, ~r/@/)\n  end\n\n- **Result Tuples**: Return tagged tuples like ''{:ok, result}'' or ''{:error, reason}'' for operations that can fail\n\n## Process Design\n\n- **GenServer for State**: Use GenServers for stateful processes\n- **Supervision Trees**: Design proper supervision hierarchies\n- **Registry Pattern**: Use Registry for dynamic process lookup\n- **Task.Supervisor**: Use for concurrent, potentially failing operations\n- **Process Isolation**: Design processes to crash independently without affecting the whole system\n- **Let It Crash**: Embrace the \"let it crash\" philosophy with proper supervision\n\n## Phoenix Best Practices\n\n- **LiveView-First**: Use LiveView as the primary UI technology\n- **Function Components**: Use function components for reusable UI elements\n- **PubSub for Real-time**: Use Phoenix PubSub for real-time features\n- **Context Boundaries**: Respect context boundaries in controllers and LiveViews\n- **Thin Controllers**: Keep controllers thin, delegating business logic to contexts\n- **Security First**: Always consider security implications (CSRF, XSS, etc.)\n\n## Testing Strategies\n\n- **Test Public APIs**: Focus on testing public context APIs\n- **Mox for Dependencies**: Use Mox for mocking external dependencies\n- **Property-Based Testing**: Use StreamData for property-based tests\n- **Test Factories**: Use ExMachina for test data creation\n- **Test Readability**: Write tests that serve as documentation\n- **Arrange-Act-Assert**: Structure tests with clear setup, action, and verification phases\n\n## HTTP and API Integration\n\n- **Req for HTTP Clients**: Use Req instead of HTTPoison or Tesla\n- **Behaviours for API Clients**: Define behaviours for API clients to allow easy mocking\n- **Error Handling**: Handle network failures and unexpected responses gracefully\n- **Timeouts**: Always set appropriate timeouts for external calls\n- **Circuit Breakers**: Use circuit breakers for critical external services\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n- **Snake Case**: For variables and functions (''create_user'')\n- **Verb-First Functions**: Start function names with verbs (''create_user'', not ''user_create'')\n- **Plural for Collections**: Use plural for collections (''users'', not ''user'')\n- **Consistent Terminology**: Use consistent terms throughout the codebase\n- **Intention-Revealing Names**: Choose names that reveal intent, not implementation\n\n## Documentation and Quality\n\n- **Document Public Functions**: Add ''@doc'' to all public functions\n- **Examples in Docs**: Include examples in documentation\n- **Credo and Dialyzer**: Use for static analysis and type checking\n- **Consistent Formatting**: Use ''mix format'' to maintain consistent code style\n- **Continuous Refactoring**: Regularly improve code structure without changing behavior\n- **Comments**: Write comments only when necessary. Describe why, not what it does.\n\n## Performance Considerations\n\n- **Avoid N+1 Queries**: Use Ecto''s preloading and joins\n- **Pagination**: Paginate large result sets\n- **Background Jobs**: Use Oban for background processing\n- **Measure First**: Profile before optimizing\n- **Caching**: Apply strategic caching where appropriate\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T10:12:54.712Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full-stack Agents needing best practices in Elixir and Phoenix development","zh":"适合需要Elixir和Phoenix开发最佳实践的全栈代理","ja":"ElixirとPhoenix開発のベストプラクティスを必要とするフルスタックエージェントに最適","ko":"엘릭서와 피닉스 개발 모범 사례가 필요한 풀스택 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Full-stack que necesitan mejores prácticas en desarrollo de Elixir y Phoenix","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full-stack ayant besoin de meilleures pratiques dans le développement Elixir et Phoenix","de":"Perfekt für Full-stack-Agenten, die Best Practices in Elixir- und Phoenix-Entwicklung benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full-stack que necessitam de boas práticas em desenvolvimento Elixir e Phoenix","ru":"Идеально для полнофункциональных агентов, которым необходимы лучшие практики в разработке на Elixir и Phoenix","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الكاملين الذين يحتاجون إلى أفضل الممارسات في تطوير إликسيور وفينيكس"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to organize code around business domains using Domain-Driven Design, implement Functional Core, Imperative Shell architecture, and prefer Explicit Over Implicit coding principles, leveraging the latest versions of Phoenix and other packages","zh":"使代理能够使用领域驱动设计组织代码围绕业务域，实现函数核心、命令式外壳架构，并偏好显式优于隐式编码原则，利用最新版本的Phoenix和其他包","ja":"エージェントがドメイン駆動設計を使用してビジネスドメインを中心にコードを整理し、関数コア、イミュータブルシェルアーキテクチャを実装し、明示的を暗示的よりも優先するコーディング原則を使用し、最新バージョンのPhoenixおよびその他のパッケージを活用できる","ko":"에이전트가 도메인 주도 설계를 사용하여 비즈니스 도메인을 중심으로 코드를 구성하고 함수형 코어, 임시 셸 아키텍처를 구현하며 명시적 보다 암시적 코딩 원칙을 선호하여 최신 버전의 피닉스 및 기타 패키지를 활용할 수 있도록 함","es":"Permite a los agentes organizar el código alrededor de dominios empresariales utilizando Domain-Driven Design, implementar arquitectura de Núcleo Funcional, Capa Imperativa, y preferir principios de codificación Explícito sobre Implícito, aprovechando las últimas versiones de Phoenix y otros paquetes","fr":"Permet aux agents d''organiser le code autour de domaines métier en utilisant la conception pilotée par le domaine, de mettre en œuvre une architecture de noyau fonctionnel, coquille impérative, et de préférer les principes de codage explicite plutôt qu''implicite, en exploitant les dernières versions de Phoenix et d''autres packages","de":"Ermöglicht