rchy"},"description":{"zh":"Next.js 应用层次结构模板提供了一种快速构建干净的架构和提高性能的方法。","ja":"Next.js アプリ階層構造テンプレートは、クリーンなアーキテクチャを迅速に構築し、パフォーマンスを向上させるための方法を提供します。","ko":"Next.js 애플리케이션 계층 구조 템플릿은 빠르게 깨끗한 아키텍처를 구축하고 성능을 향상시키는 방법을 제공합니다.","es":"La jerarquía de componentes es fundamental para desarrollar aplicaciones Next.js escalables y mantenibles. Aprende los principios básicos","fr":"L''hiérarchie de composants est essentielle pour développer des applications Next.js évolutives et maintenables. Découvrez les principes de base","de":"Die Komponenten-Hierarchie ist entscheidend für die Entwicklung von skalierbaren und wartbaren Next.js-Anwendungen. Erfahren Sie die Grundlagen","pt":"A hierarquia de componentes é um conceito fundamental para desenvolvedores que buscam criar aplicações Next.js escaláveis e eficientes.","ru":"Иерархия компонентов является фундаментальной концепцией для разработчиков, которые стремятся создавать масштабируемые и эффективные приложения Next.js","ar":"هرمية المكونات هي مفهوم أساسي للمطورين الذين يسعون إلى إنشاء تطبيقات Next.js قابلة للتحجيم والفعالية","en":"Next.js App router repo template to start working faster in a very simple clean architecture and mcp skills."},"definition":{"en":"Next.js App router repo template to start working faster in a very simple clean architecture and mcp skills."},"features":{"zh":["服务器组件数据获取","原子设计","客户端组件钩子","性能和 SEO 优先","无 any 类型"],"ja":["サーバーコンポーネントによるデータ取得","アトミックデザイン","クライアントコンポーネントでのフック","パフォーマンスと SEO の優先","any タイプの使用禁止"],"ko":["서버 컴포넌트 데이터 가져오기","원자적 디자인","클라이언트 컴포넌트 훅","성능 및 SEO 우선","any 유형 사용 금지"],"es":["Diseño atómico","Componentes del servidor que recuperan datos","Hooks personalizados en componentes del cliente","Priorización del rendimiento y el SEO","Evitación del tipo ''any''"],"fr":["Conception atomique","Composants serveur qui récupèrent des données","Hooks personnalisés dans les composants client","Priorisation des performances et du SEO","Évitement du type ''any''"],"de":["Atomares Design","Server-Komponenten, die Daten abrufen","Benutzerdefinierte Hooks in Client-Komponenten","Priorisierung von Leistung und SEO","Vermeidung des Typs ''any''"],"pt":["Server Components que buscamos dados diretamente","Design Atômico para construir componentes reutilizáveis","Hooks personalizados em Componentes de Cliente","Otimização de desempenho e SEO","Proibição do uso de ''any''"],"ru":["Серверные компоненты, которые получают данные напрямую","Атомный дизайн для построения повторно используемых компонентов","Пользовательские хуки в клиентских компонентах","Оптимизация производительности и SEO","Запрет на использование ''any''"],"ar":["مكونات الخادم التي تحصل على البيانات مباشرة","تصميم ذري لبناء مكونات قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام","أقواس مخصصة في مكونات العميل","تحسين الأداء والتحسين لعمليات البحث","منع استخدام ''any''"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Next.js","应用层次结构","干净架构","性能优化","SEO","服务器组件","客户端组件","原子设计"],"ja":["Next.js","アプリ階層構造","クリーンアーキテクチャ","パフォーマンス最適化","SEO","サーバーコンポーネント","クライアントコンポーネント","アトミックデザイン"],"ko":["Next.js","애플리케이션 계층 구조","깨끗한 아키텍처","성능 최적화","SEO","서버 컴포넌트","클라이언트 컴포넌트","원자적 디자인"],"es":["jerarquía de componentes","diseño atómico","Next.js","componentes del servidor","hooks personalizados","rendimiento","SEO","desarrollo de aplicaciones web"],"fr":["hiérarchie de composants","conception atomique","Next.js","composants serveur","hooks personnalisés","performances","SEO","développement d''applications web"],"de":["Komponenten-Hierarchie","atomares Design","Next.js","Server-Komponenten","benutzerdefinierte Hooks","Leistung","SEO","Webanwendungsentwicklung"],"pt":["hierarquia de componentes","desenvolvimento de aplicações Next.js","design atômico","server components","otimização de desempenho","SEO","hooks personalizados","componentes reutilizáveis"],"ru":["иерархия компонентов","разработка приложений Next.js","атомный дизайн","серверные компоненты","оптимизация производительности","SEO","пользовательские хуки","повторно используемые компоненты"],"ar":["هرمية المكونات","تطوير تطبيقات Next.js","تصميم ذري","مكونات الخادم","تحسين الأداء","SEO","أقواس مخصصة","مكونات قابلة لإعادة الاستخدام"]}},"owner":"jorggerojas","repo":"next-skeleton-app","repoPath":"jorggerojas/next-skeleton-app","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.488Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"hierarchy","description":"Define the components hierarchy, how to use components inside pages and how to mix components and when its needed to create new ones.","bodyPreview":"# Component Hierarchy\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Server Components fetch data** - Server Components fetch data directly, Client Components receive data as props\n2. **Atomic Design** - Build from atoms → molecules → organisms → pages\n3. **Hooks in Client Components** - Custom hooks belong in Client Components (organisms), not Server Components\n4. **Performance & SEO first** - Always prioritize unless there''s an edge case\n5. **Never use `any`** - Under no circumstances\n\n## Atomic Design Hierarchy","body":"# Component Hierarchy\n\n## Core Principles\n\n1. **Server Components fetch data** - Server Components fetch data directly, Client Components receive data as props\n2. **Atomic Design** - Build from atoms → molecules → organisms → pages\n3. **Hooks in Client Components** - Custom hooks belong in Client Components (organisms), not Server Components\n4. **Performance & SEO first** - Always prioritize unless there''s an edge case\n5. **Never use `any`** - Under no circumstances\n\n## Atomic Design Hierarchy\n\n```txt\nPage (src/app/)\n└── Organism (large component with business logic)\n    └── Molecule (group of atoms with simple logic)\n        └── Atom (single UI element, no logic)\n```\n\n### Atoms\n\nSingle UI elements with no business logic. Receive props, render UI.\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/Button/Button.tsx\ninterface ButtonProps {\n  children: ReactNode;\n  onClick?: () => void;\n  variant?: \"primary\" | \"secondary\";\n  disabled?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport default function Button({ children, onClick, variant = \"primary\", disabled }: ButtonProps) {\n  return (\n    <button onClick={onClick} disabled={disabled} className={`btn btn-${variant}`}>\n      {children}\n    </button>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/Input/Input.tsx\ninterface InputProps {\n  value: string;\n  onChange: (value: string) => void;\n  placeholder?: string;\n  type?: \"text\" | \"email\" | \"password\";\n}\n\nexport default function Input({ value, onChange, placeholder, type = \"text\" }: InputProps) {\n  const handleChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {\n    onChange(e.target.value);\n  };\n\n  return <input type={type} value={value} onChange={handleChange} placeholder={placeholder} />;\n}\n```\n\n### Molecules\n\nGroup of atoms with simple interaction logic. No hooks, no data fetching.\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/SearchInput/SearchInput.tsx\nimport Input from \"../Input\";\nimport Button from \"../Button\";\n\ninterface SearchInputProps {\n  value: string;\n  onChange: (value: string) => void;\n  onSearch: () => void;\n  placeholder?: string;\n}\n\nexport default function SearchInput({ value, onChange, onSearch, placeholder }: SearchInputProps) {\n  const handleKeyDown = (e: React.KeyboardEvent) => {\n    if (e.key === \"Enter\") {\n      onSearch();\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex gap-2\" onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}>\n      <Input value={value} onChange={onChange} placeholder={placeholder} />\n      <Button onClick={onSearch}>Search</Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/UserCard/UserCard.tsx\nimport Avatar from \"../Avatar\";\nimport Badge from \"../Badge\";\n\ninterface UserCardProps {\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n  avatarUrl?: string;\n  role: \"admin\" | \"user\";\n}\n\nexport default function UserCard({ name, email, avatarUrl, role }: UserCardProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex items-center gap-4 p-4 border rounded\">\n      <Avatar src={avatarUrl} alt={name} />\n      <div>\n        <h3 className=\"font-bold\">{name}</h3>\n        <p className=\"text-gray-500\">{email}</p>\n      </div>\n      <Badge variant={role === \"admin\" ? \"primary\" : \"secondary\"}>{role}</Badge>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Organisms\n\nLarge components with business logic. Can use hooks, stores, and handle complex interactions.\n\n```tsx\n// src/ui/custom/UserList/UserList.tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useDebounce } from \"@/hooks\";\nimport { useUIStore } from \"@/stores\";\nimport SearchInput from \"../SearchInput\";\nimport UserCard from \"../UserCard\";\n\ninterface User {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n  avatarUrl?: string;\n  role: \"admin\" | \"user\";\n}\n\ninterface UserListProps {\n  users: User[];\n  onUserSelect: (user: User) => void;\n}\n\nexport default function UserList({ users, onUserSelect }: UserListProps) {\n  const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState(\"\");\n  const debouncedSearch = useDebounce(searchTerm, 300);\n  const { openModal } = useUIStore();\n\n  const filteredUsers = users.filter(\n    (user) =>\n      user.name.toLowerCase().includes(debouncedSearch.toLowerCase()) ||\n      user.email.toLowerCase().includes(debouncedSearch.toLowerCase())\n  );\n\n  const handleUserClick = (user: User) => {\n    onUserSelect(user);\n    openModal();\n  };\n\n  const handleSearch = () => {\n    // Optional: trigger immediate search\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"space-y-4\">\n      <SearchInput\n        value={searchTerm}\n        onChange={setSearchTerm}\n        onSearch={handleSearch}\n        placeholder=\"Search users...\"\n      />\n      <div className=\"space-y-2\">\n        {filteredUsers.map((user) => (\n          <div key={user.id} onClick={() => handleUserClick(user)} className=\"cursor-pointer\">\n            <UserCard {...user} />\n          </div>\n        ))}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Pages (Server Components)\n\nServer Components fetch data directly. Client Components receive data as props.\n\n```tsx\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\nimport { UserList } from \"@/components\";\n\nasync function getUsers() {\n  const res = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\", {\n    next: { revalidate: 60 },\n  });\n  return res.json();\n}\n\nexport default async function UsersPage() {\n  const users = await getUsers();\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-4\">Users</h1>\n      <UserList users={users} />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Pages (Client Components)\n\nWhen you need interactivity, use Client Components:\n\n```tsx\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\n\"use client\";\n\nimport { UserList } from \"@/components\";\nimport { useUsers } from \"@/hooks/users\";\n\nexport default function UsersPage() {\n  const { data: users, isLoading } = useUsers();\n\n  const handleUserSelect = (user: { id: string; name: string }) => {\n    console.log(\"Selected user:\", user.id);\n  };\n\n  if (isLoading) return <div>Loading...</div>;\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-4\">Users</h1>\n      <UserList users={users} onUserSelect={handleUserSelect} />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Data Flow\n\n```txt\nServer Data Flow (Server Components):\nAPI → Server Component (fetch) → Organism → Molecule → Atom\n                                 (props)    (props)   (props)\n\nClient Data Flow (Client Components):\nAPI → React Query Hook → Client Component → Organism → Molecule → Atom\n                         (props)           (props)    (props)   (props)\n\nClient State Flow:\nUser Action → Atom (onClick) → Molecule (handler) → Organism (hook/store) → UI Update\n```\n\n## When to Create a New Component\n\n| Scenario | Create New? | Level |\n|----------|-------------|-------|\n| Button with icon | No, add `icon` prop to Button | Atom |\n| Search bar (input + button) | Yes | Molecule |\n| Form with validation | Yes | Organism |\n| Repeating UI pattern (3+ times) | Yes | Appropriate level |\n| Single-use complex UI | Maybe, if >100 lines | Organism |\n\n## Hook Usage Rules\n\n| Component Level | Can Use Hooks? | Examples |\n|-----------------|----------------|----------|\n| Atom | No | Button, Input, Badge |\n| Molecule | Rarely (only `useState` for local UI) | SearchInput, FormField |\n| Organism | Yes | UserList, DataTable, Forms |\n| Page | Only for client-side mutations | useUsers.create() |\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ BAD: Hook in atom\nexport default function Button({ label }) {\n  const { isLoading } = useUIStore(); // DON''T\n  return <button>{label}</button>;\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Props in atom\nexport default function Button({ label, isLoading }) {\n  return <button disabled={isLoading}>{label}</button>;\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Hook in organism\nexport default function UserForm({ onSubmit }) {\n  const { isLoading, setLoading } = useUIStore();\n  const [formData, setFormData] = useState({});\n\n  const handleSubmit = async () => {\n    setLoading(true);\n    await onSubmit(formData);\n    setLoading(false);\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>\n      <Input value={formData.name} onChange={(v) => setFormData({ ...formData, name: v })} />\n      <Button isLoading={isLoading}>Submit</Button>\n    </form>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Server vs Client Data\n\n```tsx\n// ✅ GOOD: Server Component fetches data directly\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\nasync function getUsers() {\n  const res = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/users\");\n  return res.json();\n}\n\nexport default async function UsersPage() {\n  const users = await getUsers();\n  return <UserList users={users} />;\n}\n\n// ✅ GOOD: Client Component with hooks for interactivity\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\n\"use client\";\n\nimport { useUsers } from \"@/hooks/users\";\n\nexport default function UsersPage() {\n  const { data: users } = useUsers();\n  return <UserList users={users} />;\n}\n\n// Component receives data as props\nexport default function UserList({ users }: { users: User[] }) {\n  return <div>{users.map(...)}</div>;\n}\n```\n\n## Client-Side Mutations\n\nFor mutations (create, update, delete), use hooks in Client Components:\n\n```tsx\n// src/app/users/page.tsx\n\"use client\";\n\nimport { useUsers } from \"@/hooks/users\";\n\nexport default function UsersPage() {\n  const { data: users } = useUsers();\n  const createUser = useUsers.create();\n  const deleteUser = useUsers.delete();\n\n  const handleCreate = (data: CreateUserInput) => {\n    createUser.mutate(data);\n  };\n\n  const handleDelete = (id: string) => {\n    deleteUser.mutate(id);\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <UserForm onSubmit={handleCreate} />\n      <UserList users={users} onDelete={handleDelete} />\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n\n- **Server Components fetch data directly** - No hooks needed\n- **Client Components use hooks** - For interactivity and mutations\n- **Props down, events up** - Data flows down, actions bubble up via callbacks\n- **Keep atoms pure** - No side effects, no hooks, just UI\n- **Organisms are the brain** - Business logic lives here\n- **Test at the right level** - Unit test atoms, integration test organisms\n- **Never use `any`** - Define proper types for all props and state\n- **Handler naming** - `handle*` inside components, `on*` for props from parents\n- **Prefer composition** - Build complex UIs by combining simple components\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T10:24:11.854Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing structured Next.js app architecture and component organization","zh":"非常适合需要结构化 Next.js 应用程序架构和组件组织的前端代理","ja":"Next.js アプリケーションの構造化されたアーキテクチャとコンポーネントの組織化が必要なフロントエンド エージェントに最適","ko":"구조화된 Next.js 애플리케이션 아키텍처와 컴포넌트 조직화가 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes Frontend que necesitan una arquitectura de aplicaciones Next.js estructurada y organización de componentes","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui ont besoin d''une architecture d''applications Next.js structurée et d''une organisation de composants","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die eine strukturierte Next.js-App-Architektur und Komponentenorganisation benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de arquitetura de aplicativos Next.js estruturada e organização de componentes","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, которым необходима структурированная архитектура приложений Next.js и организация компонентов","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأمامية الذين يحتاجون إلى هيكل التطبيق Next.js المنظم وتنظيم المكونات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build scalable applications using Server Components, Atomic Design principles, and custom hooks in Client Components, prioritizing performance and SEO with strict type checking, never using ''any''","zh":"赋予代理构建可扩展应用程序的能力，使用服务器组件、原子设计原则和客户端组件中的自定义钩子，优先考虑性能和 SEO，并且严格的类型检查，从不使用 ''any''","ja":"Server Components、Atomic Design 原則、Client Components のカスタムフックを使用して、パフォーマンスと SEO を優先し、厳格な型チェックを行い、''any'' タイプを使用しないことで、拡張可能なアプリケーションの構築をエージェントに可能にする","ko":"서버 컴포넌트, 원자적 디자인 원칙, 클라이언트 컴포넌트의 커스텀 훅을 사용하여 확장 가능한 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 성능과 SEO를 우선하며, 엄격한 타입 체킹을 수행하고 ''any'' 타입을 사용하지 않음","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir aplicaciones escalables utilizando componentes del servidor, principios de diseño atómico y ganchos personalizados en componentes del cliente, priorizando el rendimiento y el SEO con una verificación de tipos estricta, nunca utilizando ''any''","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire des applications évolutives en utilisant des composants serveur, des principes de conception atomique et des crochets personnalisés dans des composants client, en donnant la priorité aux performances et au SEO avec une vérification de type stricte, sans jamais utiliser ''any''","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, skalierbare Anwendungen mit Serverkomponenten, atomaren Designprinzipien und benutzerdefinierten Hooks in Clientkomponenten zu erstellen, wobei Leistung und SEO mit strenger Typüberprüfung priorisiert werden, ohne ''any'' zu verwenden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir aplicações escaláveis usando Componentes de Servidor, princípios de Design Atômico e ganchos personalizados em Componentes de Cliente, priorizando o desempenho e o SEO com verificação de tipo estrita, nunca usando ''any''","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать масштабируемые приложения с помощью Компонентов Сервера, принципов Атомарного Дизайна и пользовательских крючков в Компонентах Клиента, отдающих приоритет производительности и SEO с помощью строгой проверки типов, никогда не используя ''any''","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على بناء تطبيقات قابلة للتوسيع باستخدام مكونات الخادم ومبادئ التصميم الذري والصوابة المخصصة في مكونات العميل، مع ưu tiên الأداء و تحسين محركات البحث مع التحقق الصارم من النوع، أبدا استخدام ''any''"},"useCases":{"en":["Building modular page structures with organisms and molecules","Implementing custom hooks for data fetching and manipulation","Optimizing application performance with Server Components"],"zh":["使用有机体和分子构建模块化的页面结构","实现自定义钩子以获取和操作数据","使用服务器组件优化应用程序性能"],"ja":["オーガニズムとモレキュールを使用してモジュラーなページ構造を構築する","カスタムフックを実装してデータの取得と操作を行う","Server Components を使用してアプリケーションのパフォーマンスを最適化する"],"ko":["유기체와 분자를 사용하여 모듈화된 페이지 구조 구축","데이터 가져오기 및 조작을 위한 커스텀 훅 구현","서버 컴포넌트를 사용하여 애플리케이션 성능 최적화"],"es":["Construir estructuras de página modulares con organismos y moléculas","Implementar ganchos personalizados para la captura y manipulación de datos","Optimizar el rendimiento de la aplicación con componentes del servidor"],"fr":["Construire des structures de page modulaires avec des organismes et des molécules","Mettre en œuvre des crochets personnalisés pour la récupération et la manipulation de données","Optimiser les performances de l''application avec des composants serveur"],"de":["Modulare Seitenstrukturen mit Organismen und Molekülen erstellen","Benutzerdefinierte Hooks für Datenabruf und -manipulation implementieren","Anwendungsleistung mit Serverkomponenten optimieren"],"pt":["Construir estruturas de página modulares com organismos e moléculas","Implementar ganchos personalizados para busca e manipulação de dados","Otimizar o desempenho da aplicação com Componentes de Servidor"],"ru":["Построение модульных структур страниц с помощью организмов и молекул","Реализация пользовательских крючков для извлечения и манипулирования данными","Оптимизация производительности приложения с помощью Компонентов Сервера"],"ar":["بناء هياكل صفحة قابلة للتعديل مع الكائنات الحية والجزيئات","تنفيذ صوابع مخصصة لاسترجاع وتنفيذ البيانات","تحسين أداء التطبيق باستخدام مكونات الخادم"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Next.js environment","Strict adherence to Atomic Design hierarchy","No use of ''any'' type"],"zh":["需要 Next.js 环境","严格遵守原子设计层次结构","不使用 ''any'' 类型"],"ja":["Next.js 環境が必要","Atomic Design の階層構造に厳格に従う","''any'' タイプを使用しない"],"ko":["Next.js 환경 필요","원자적 디자인 계층 구조를 엄격히 준수"," ''any'' 타입 사용 안함"],"es":["Requiere entorno Next.js","Cumplimiento estricto de la jerarquía de diseño atómico","No se utiliza el tipo ''any''"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement Next.js","Respect strict de la hiérarchie de conception atomique","Pas d''utilisation du type ''any''"],"de":["Erfordert Next.js-Umgebung","Strenger Einhaltung der Hierarchie des atomaren Designs","Keine Verwendung des Typs ''any''"],"pt":["Requer ambiente Next.js","Adesão estrita à hierarquia de Design Atômico","Nenhum uso do tipo ''any''"],"ru":["Требуется среда Next.js","Строгое соблюдение иерархии Атомарного Дизайна","Никакого использования типа ''any''"],"ar":["يتطلب بيئة Next.js","الالتزام الصارم بالتدرج الهرمي للتصميم الذري","لا استخدام لنوع ''any''"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('gitwalter/cursor-agent-factory/model-training', 'community', 'gitwalter', 'cursor-agent-factory', 'gitwalter/cursor-agent-factory', 'model-training', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.488Z', '2026-02-18T10:24:07.850Z', NULL, '{"id":"gitwalter/cursor-agent-factory/model-training","name":"model-training","description":{"zh":"模型训练技能提供了快速实现生产级PyTorch训练循环的方法，支持分布式训练、超参数优化和实验跟踪","ja":"モデルトレーニングスキルは、プロダクションレベルのPyTorchトレーニングループを迅速に実現する方法を提供します。分散トレーニング、ハイパーパラメーターの最適化、実験の追跡をサポート","ko":"모델 트레이닝 스킬은 생산급 PyTorch 트레이닝 루프를 빠르게 구현하는 방법을 제공합니다. 분산 트레이닝, 하이퍼파라미터 최적화, 실험 추적 지원","es":"El skill de entrenamiento de modelos permite implementar bucles de entrenamiento de PyTorch listos para producción con patrones modernos.","fr":"Le skill de formation de modèles permet d''implémenter des boucles d''entraînement PyTorch prêtes pour la production avec des modèles modernes.","de":"Das Modell-Training-Skill ermöglicht die Implementierung von PyTorch-Trainingsloops mit modernen Mustern für die Produktion.","pt":"Treinamento de modelos com PyTorch, incluindo loops de treinamento personalizados e distribuídos","ru":"Обучение моделей с помощью PyTorch, включая настраиваемые и распределенные циклы обучения","ar":"تدريب النماذج باستخدام PyTorch، بما في ذلك حلقات التدريب المخصصة والموزعة","en":" A configurable factory for generating Cursor IDE development agent systems. Creates .cursorrules, agents, skills, workflows, and templates for any tech stack. Supports blueprints for SAP, Python, Cloud-Native, and more. Includes refactoring capabilities for existing projects"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"模型训练技能 - PyTorch训练循环优化","ja":"モデルトレーニングスキル - PyTorchトレーニングループの最適化","ko":"모델 트레이닝 스킬 - PyTorch 트레이닝 루프 최적화","es":"Entrenamiento de Modelos con PyTorch","fr":"Entraînement de Modèles avec PyTorch","de":"Modell-Training mit PyTorch","pt":"Treinamento de Modelos com PyTorch","ru":"Обучение моделей с помощью PyTorch","ar":"تدريب النماذج باستخدام PyTorch","en":"model-training"},"description":{"zh":"模型训练技能提供了快速实现生产级PyTorch训练循环的方法，支持分布式训练、超参数优化和实验跟踪","ja":"モデルトレーニングスキルは、プロダクションレベルのPyTorchトレーニングループを迅速に実現する方法を提供します。分散トレーニング、ハイパーパラメーターの最適化、実験の追跡をサポート","ko":"모델 트레이닝 스킬은 생산급 PyTorch 트레이닝 루프를 빠르게 구현하는 방법을 제공합니다. 분산 트레이닝, 하이퍼파라미터 최적화, 실험 추적 지원","es":"El skill de entrenamiento de modelos permite implementar bucles de entrenamiento de PyTorch listos para producción con patrones modernos.","fr":"Le skill de formation de modèles permet d''implémenter des boucles d''entraînement PyTorch prêtes pour la production avec des modèles modernes.","de":"Das Modell-Training-Skill ermöglicht die Implementierung von PyTorch-Trainingsloops mit modernen Mustern für die Produktion.","pt":"Treinamento de modelos com PyTorch, incluindo loops de treinamento personalizados e distribuídos","ru":"Обучение моделей с помощью PyTorch, включая настраиваемые и распределенные циклы обучения","ar":"تدريب النماذج باستخدام PyTorch، بما في ذلك حلقات التدريب المخصصة والموزعة","en":" A configurable factory for generating Cursor IDE development agent systems. Creates .cursorrules, agents, skills, workflows, and templates for any tech stac..."},"definition":{"en":" A configurable factory for generating Cursor IDE development agent systems. Creates .cursorrules, agents, skills, workflows, and templates for any tech stack. Supports blueprints for SAP, Python, Cloud-Native, and more. Includes refactoring capabilities for existing projects"},"features":{"zh":["支持分布式训练","超参数优化","实验跟踪","混合精度训练","强大的检查点策略"],"ja":["分散トレーニングのサポート","ハイパーパラメーターの最適化","実験の追跡","混合精度トレーニング","強力なチェックポイント戦略"],"ko":["분산 트레이닝 지원","하이퍼파라미터 최적화","실험 추적","혼합 精度 트레이닝","강력한 체크 포인트 전략"],"es":["Bucles de entrenamiento de PyTorch listos para producción","Patrones modernos como Accelerate y distribuido","Optimización de hiperparámetros con Optuna","Seguimiento de experimentos","Entrenamiento de precisión mixta","Estrategias de puntos de control robustas"],"fr":["Boucles d''entraînement PyTorch prêtes pour la production","Modèles modernes comme Accelerate et distribué","Optimisation des hyperparamètres avec Optuna","Suivi des expériences","Entraînement de précision mixte","Stratégies de points de contrôle robustes"],"de":["PyTorch-Trainingsloops für die Produktion","Moderne Muster wie Accelerate und verteilt","Hyperparameter-Optimierung mit Optuna","Experimenten-Verfolgung","Mischpräzisions-Training","Robuste Checkpoint-Strategien"],"pt":["Loops de treinamento personalizados","Treinamento distribuído com DeepSpeed/FSDP","Otimização de hiperparâmetros com Optuna","Rastreamento de experimentos","Treinamento de precisão mista"],"ru":["Настраиваемые циклы обучения","Распределенное обучение с DeepSpeed/FSDP","Оптимизация гиперпараметров с Optuna","Отслеживание экспериментов","Обучение с смешанной точностью"],"ar":["حلقات التدريب المخصصة","التدريب الموزع مع DeepSpeed/FSDP","تحسين المعاملات Hyper مع Optuna","تتبع التجارب","التدريب بدقة مزيج"]},"keywords":{"zh":["PyTorch训练循环","分布式训练","超参数优化","实验跟踪","混合精度训练","模型训练技能"],"ja":["PyTorchトレーニングループ","分散トレーニング","ハイパーパラメーターの最適化","実験の追跡","混合精度トレーニング","モデルトレーニングスキル"],"ko":["PyTorch 트레이닝 루프","분산 트레이닝","하이퍼파라미터 최적화","실험 추적","혼합 精度 트레이닝","모델 트레이닝 스킬"],"es":["entrenamiento de modelos","PyTorch","aprendizaje automático","patrones modernos","Optuna","experimentos","precisión mixta","puntos de control"],"fr":["formation de modèles","PyTorch","apprentissage automatique","modèles modernes","Optuna","expériences","précision mixte","points de contrôle"],"de":["Modell-Training","PyTorch","maschinelles Lernen","moderne Muster","Optuna","Experimente","Mischpräzision","Checkpoint"],"pt":["treinamento de modelos","PyTorch","loops de treinamento","treinamento distribuído","otimização de hiperparâmetros","rastreamento de experimentos","desenvolvimento de modelos"],"ru":["обучение моделей","PyTorch","циклы обучения","распределенное обучение","оптимизация гиперпараметров","отслеживание экспериментов","разработка моделей"],"ar":["تدريب النماذج","PyTorch","حلقات التدريب","التدريب الموزع","تحسين المعاملات Hyper","تتبع التجارب","تنمية النماذج"]}},"owner":"gitwalter","repo":"cursor-agent-factory","repoPath":"gitwalter/cursor-agent-factory","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.488Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"model-training","description":"PyTorch training loops, distributed training with DeepSpeed/FSDP, hyperparameter tuning with Optuna, experiment tracking, mixed precision training, checkpointing","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Model Training Skill\n\nImplement production-ready PyTorch training loops with modern patterns including Accelerate, distributed training (DeepSpeed/FSDP), hyperparameter optimization with Optuna, experiment tracking, mixed precision training, and robust checkpointing strategies.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Training deep learning models from scratch\n- Implementing custom training loops\n- Setting up distributed training for large models\n- Optimizing hyperparameters systematically\n- Tracking experiments an","body":"# Model Training Skill\n\nImplement production-ready PyTorch training loops with modern patterns including Accelerate, distributed training (DeepSpeed/FSDP), hyperparameter optimization with Optuna, experiment tracking, mixed precision training, and robust checkpointing strategies.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Training deep learning models from scratch\n- Implementing custom training loops\n- Setting up distributed training for large models\n- Optimizing hyperparameters systematically\n- Tracking experiments and metrics\n- Training with mixed precision for efficiency\n- Implementing checkpointing and resume logic\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n```bash\npip install torch torchvision torchaudio\npip install accelerate transformers\npip install deepspeed  # For DeepSpeed\npip install optuna  # For hyperparameter tuning\npip install mlflow wandb  # For experiment tracking\npip install tensorboard  # For visualization\n```\n\n## Process\n\n### Step 1: Modern PyTorch Training Loop with Accelerate\n\nUse Accelerate for simplified distributed training:\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nfrom torch.utils.data import DataLoader, Dataset\nfrom accelerate import Accelerator\nfrom accelerate.utils import set_seed\nimport os\n\nclass SimpleDataset(Dataset):\n    \"\"\"Example dataset.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, size=1000):\n        self.data = torch.randn(size, 10)\n        self.labels = torch.randint(0, 2, (size,))\n    \n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.data)\n    \n    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n        return self.data[idx], self.labels[idx]\n\nclass SimpleModel(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Example model.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(10, 64)\n        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(64, 32)\n        self.fc3 = nn.Linear(32, 2)\n        self.relu = nn.ReLU()\n    \n    def forward(self, x):\n        x = self.relu(self.fc1(x))\n        x = self.relu(self.fc2(x))\n        x = self.fc3(x)\n        return x\n\ndef train_with_accelerate(\n    model: nn.Module,\n    train_loader: DataLoader,\n    val_loader: DataLoader,\n    num_epochs: int = 10,\n    learning_rate: float = 1e-3,\n    checkpoint_dir: str = \"./checkpoints\"\n):\n    \"\"\"Training loop with Accelerate.\"\"\"\n    # Initialize accelerator\n    accelerator = Accelerator(\n        gradient_accumulation_steps=4,\n        mixed_precision=\"fp16\",  # or \"bf16\" or None\n        log_with=\"tensorboard\",  # or \"wandb\", \"mlflow\"\n        project_dir=\"./logs\"\n    )\n    \n    # Set seed for reproducibility\n    set_seed(42)\n    \n    # Prepare model, optimizer, and dataloader\n    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=learning_rate)\n    criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n    \n    model, optimizer, train_loader, val_loader = accelerator.prepare(\n        model, optimizer, train_loader, val_loader\n    )\n    \n    # Training loop\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        model.train()\n        total_loss = 0\n        \n        for batch_idx, (data, target) in enumerate(train_loader):\n            # Forward pass\n            outputs = model(data)\n            loss = criterion(outputs, target)\n            \n            # Backward pass with gradient accumulation\n            accelerator.backward(loss)\n            \n            # Optimizer step (only after accumulation)\n            if (batch_idx + 1) % accelerator.gradient_accumulation_steps == 0:\n                optimizer.step()\n                optimizer.zero_grad()\n            \n            total_loss += loss.item()\n            \n            # Logging\n            if batch_idx % 100 == 0:\n                accelerator.log(\n                    {\"train_loss\": loss.item()},\n                    step=epoch * len(train_loader) + batch_idx\n                )\n        \n        # Validation\n        model.eval()\n        val_loss = 0\n        correct = 0\n        total = 0\n        \n        with torch.no_grad():\n            for data, target in val_loader:\n                outputs = model(data)\n                loss = criterion(outputs, target)\n                val_loss += loss.item()\n                \n                _, predicted = torch.max(outputs.data, 1)\n                total += target.size(0)\n                correct += (predicted == target).sum().item()\n        \n        avg_train_loss = total_loss / len(train_loader)\n        avg_val_loss = val_loss / len(val_loader)\n        accuracy = 100 * correct / total\n        \n        accelerator.log({\n            \"epoch\": epoch,\n            \"train_loss\": avg_train_loss,\n            \"val_loss\": avg_val_loss,\n            \"val_accuracy\": accuracy\n        }, step=epoch)\n        \n        # Save checkpoint\n        if accelerator.is_main_process:\n            checkpoint_path = os.path.join(checkpoint_dir, f\"checkpoint_epoch_{epoch}.pt\")\n            accelerator.save_state(checkpoint_path)\n            \n            # Save best model\n            if epoch == 0 or accuracy > best_accuracy:\n                best_accuracy = accuracy\n                accelerator.save_model(model, os.path.join(checkpoint_dir, \"best_model.pt\"))\n        \n        accelerator.print(f\"Epoch {epoch}: Train Loss={avg_train_loss:.4f}, \"\n                         f\"Val Loss={avg_val_loss:.4f}, Accuracy={accuracy:.2f}%\")\n    \n    accelerator.end_training()\n\n# Usage\nmodel = SimpleModel()\ntrain_dataset = SimpleDataset(size=1000)\nval_dataset = SimpleDataset(size=200)\ntrain_loader = DataLoader(train_dataset, batch_size=32, shuffle=True)\nval_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, batch_size=32, shuffle=False)\n\ntrain_with_accelerate(\n    model=model,\n    train_loader=train_loader,\n    val_loader=val_loader,\n    num_epochs=10,\n    learning_rate=1e-3\n)\n```\n\n### Step 2: Distributed Training with DeepSpeed\n\nImplement DeepSpeed ZeRO for large model training:\n\n```python\nimport deepspeed\nfrom deepspeed.ops.adam import FusedAdam\nimport json\n\ndef create_deepspeed_config(\n    zero_stage: int = 2,\n    offload_optimizer: bool = False,\n    offload_param: bool = False,\n    gradient_accumulation_steps: int = 1,\n    train_batch_size: int = 32,\n    learning_rate: float = 1e-3\n) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Create DeepSpeed configuration.\"\"\"\n    config = {\n        \"train_batch_size\": train_batch_size,\n        \"train_micro_batch_size_per_gpu\": train_batch_size,\n        \"gradient_accumulation_steps\": gradient_accumulation_steps,\n        \"optimizer\": {\n            \"type\": \"AdamW\",\n            \"params\": {\n                \"lr\": learning_rate,\n                \"betas\": [0.9, 0.999],\n                \"eps\": 1e-8,\n                \"weight_decay\": 0.01\n            }\n        },\n        \"scheduler\": {\n            \"type\": \"WarmupLR\",\n            \"params\": {\n                \"warmup_min_lr\": 0,\n                \"warmup_max_lr\": learning_rate,\n                \"warmup_num_steps\": 1000\n            }\n        },\n        \"zero_optimization\": {\n            \"stage\": zero_stage,\n            \"offload_optimizer\": {\n                \"device\": \"cpu\" if offload_optimizer else \"none\"\n            },\n            \"offload_param\": {\n                \"device\": \"cpu\" if offload_param else \"none\"\n            },\n            \"overlap_comm\": True,\n            \"contiguous_gradients\": True,\n            \"sub_group_size\": 1e9,\n            \"reduce_bucket_size\": \"auto\",\n            \"stage3_prefetch_bucket_size\": \"auto\",\n            \"stage3_param_persistence_threshold\": \"auto\",\n            \"stage3_max_live_parameters\": 1e9,\n            \"stage3_max_reuse_distance\": 1e9,\n            \"stage3_gather_16bit_weights_on_model_save\": True\n        },\n        \"gradient_clipping\": 1.0,\n        \"fp16\": {\n            \"enabled\": True,\n            \"loss_scale\": 0,\n            \"loss_scale_window\": 1000,\n            \"initial_scale_power\": 16,\n            \"hysteresis\": 2,\n            \"min_loss_scale\": 1\n        },\n        \"wall_clock_breakdown\": False\n    }\n    return config\n\ndef train_with_deepspeed(\n    model: nn.Module,\n    train_loader: DataLoader,\n    config_path: str = \"deepspeed_config.json\"\n):\n    \"\"\"Training with DeepSpeed.\"\"\"\n    # Save config\n    config = create_deepspeed_config(zero_stage=2, offload_optimizer=False)\n    with open(config_path, \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(config, f, indent=2)\n    \n    # Initialize DeepSpeed\n    model_engine, optimizer, train_loader, _ = deepspeed.initialize(\n        model=model,\n        model_parameters=model.parameters(),\n        training_data=train_dataset,\n        config=config_path\n    )\n    \n    # Training loop\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        model_engine.train()\n        for batch_idx, (data, target) in enumerate(train_loader):\n            # Forward pass\n            outputs = model_engine(data)\n            loss = criterion(outputs, target)\n            \n            # Backward pass\n            model_engine.backward(loss)\n            \n            # Optimizer step\n            model_engine.step()\n            \n            # Logging\n            if batch_idx % 100 == 0:\n                print(f\"Epoch {epoch}, Batch {batch_idx}, Loss: {loss.item()}\")\n        \n        # Save checkpoint\n        model_engine.save_checkpoint(\n            save_dir=f\"./checkpoints/epoch_{epoch}\",\n            tag=f\"epoch_{epoch}\"\n        )\n```\n\n### Step 3: Distributed Training with FSDP (Fully Sharded Data Parallel)\n\nUse PyTorch FSDP for efficient distributed training:\n\n```python\nfrom torch.distributed.fsdp import FullyShardedDataParallel as FSDP\nfrom torch.distributed.fsdp import ShardingStrategy\nfrom torch.distributed.fsdp.wrap import transformer_auto_wrap_policy\nimport torch.distributed as dist\n\ndef train_with_fsdp(\n    model: nn.Module,\n    train_loader: DataLoader,\n    num_epochs: int = 10\n):\n    \"\"\"Training with FSDP.\"\"\"\n    # Initialize distributed\n    dist.init_process_group(backend=\"nccl\")\n    \n    # Auto-wrap policy for transformer layers\n    auto_wrap_policy = transformer_auto_wrap_policy\n    \n    # Create FSDP model\n    model = FSDP(\n        model,\n        sharding_strategy=ShardingStrategy.FULL_SHARD,\n        auto_wrap_policy=auto_wrap_policy,\n        mixed_precision=torch.distributed.fsdp.MixedPrecision(\n            param_dtype=torch.float16,\n            reduce_dtype=torch.float16,\n            buffer_dtype=torch.float16\n        ),\n        device_id=torch.cuda.current_device()\n    )\n    \n    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n    \n    # Training loop\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        model.train()\n        for batch_idx, (data, target) in enumerate(train_loader):\n            data = data.cuda()\n            target = target.cuda()\n            \n            optimizer.zero_grad()\n            outputs = model(data)\n            loss = criterion(outputs, target)\n            loss.backward()\n            optimizer.step()\n            \n            if batch_idx % 100 == 0:\n                print(f\"Epoch {epoch}, Batch {batch_idx}, Loss: {loss.item()}\")\n        \n        # Save checkpoint\n        if dist.get_rank() == 0:\n            save_policy = torch.distributed.fsdp.FullStateDictConfig(offload_to_cpu=True)\n            with FSDP.state_dict_type(model, StateDictType.FULL_STATE_DICT, save_policy):\n                state_dict = model.state_dict()\n                torch.save(state_dict, f\"./checkpoints/epoch_{epoch}.pt\")\n    \n    dist.destroy_process_group()\n```\n\n### Step 4: Hyperparameter Tuning with Optuna\n\nSystematic hyperparameter optimization:\n\n```python\nimport optuna\nfrom optuna.trial import TrialState\nimport joblib\n\ndef objective(trial: optuna.Trial, train_loader: DataLoader, val_loader: DataLoader):\n    \"\"\"Optuna objective function.\"\"\"\n    # Suggest hyperparameters\n    learning_rate = trial.suggest_loguniform(\"learning_rate\", 1e-5, 1e-2)\n    batch_size = trial.suggest_categorical(\"batch_size\", [16, 32, 64, 128])\n    weight_decay = trial.suggest_loguniform(\"weight_decay\", 1e-6, 1e-3)\n    dropout_rate = trial.suggest_uniform(\"dropout_rate\", 0.0, 0.5)\n    \n    # Create model with suggested dropout\n    model = SimpleModel()\n    # Add dropout layers based on dropout_rate\n    \n    # Create optimizer\n    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(\n        model.parameters(),\n        lr=learning_rate,\n        weight_decay=weight_decay\n    )\n    \n    # Training loop (simplified)\n    num_epochs = 5  # Fewer epochs for hyperparameter search\n    best_val_loss = float(\"inf\")\n    \n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        model.train()\n        for data, target in train_loader:\n            optimizer.zero_grad()\n            outputs = model(data)\n            loss = criterion(outputs, target)\n            loss.backward()\n            optimizer.step()\n        \n        # Validation\n        model.eval()\n        val_loss = 0\n        with torch.no_grad():\n            for data, target in val_loader:\n                outputs = model(data)\n                loss = criterion(outputs, target)\n                val_loss += loss.item()\n        \n        avg_val_loss = val_loss / len(val_loader)\n        \n        # Report intermediate value\n        trial.report(avg_val_loss, epoch)\n        \n        # Pruning\n        if trial.should_prune():\n            raise optuna.TrialPruned()\n        \n        if avg_val_loss < best_val_loss:\n            best_val_loss = avg_val_loss\n    \n    return best_val_loss\n\ndef run_hyperparameter_search(\n    train_loader: DataLoader,\n    val_loader: DataLoader,\n    n_trials: int = 50,\n    study_name: str = \"hyperparameter_study\"\n):\n    \"\"\"Run hyperparameter optimization.\"\"\"\n    # Create study\n    study = optuna.create_study(\n        direction=\"minimize\",\n        study_name=study_name,\n        pruner=optuna.pruners.MedianPruner(n_startup_trials=5, n_warmup_steps=3)\n    )\n    \n    # Optimize\n    study.optimize(\n        lambda trial: objective(trial, train_loader, val_loader),\n        n_trials=n_trials,\n        timeout=3600  # 1 hour timeout\n    )\n    \n    # Print results\n    print(\"Number of finished trials: \", len(study.trials))\n    print(\"Number of pruned trials: \", len([t for t in study.trials if t.state == TrialState.PRUNED]))\n    print(\"Number of complete trials: \", len([t for t in study.trials if t.state == TrialState.COMPLETE]))\n    \n    print(\"\\nBest trial:\")\n    trial = study.best_trial\n    print(f\"  Value: {trial.value}\")\n    print(\"  Params: \")\n    for key, value in trial.params.items():\n        print(f\"    {key}: {value}\")\n    \n    # Save study\n    joblib.dump(study, f\"{study_name}.pkl\")\n    \n    # Visualize\n    try:\n        import optuna.visualization as vis\n        fig = vis.plot_optimization_history(study)\n        fig.show()\n    except:\n        pass\n    \n    return study\n\n# Usage\nstudy = run_hyperparameter_search(train_loader, val_loader, n_trials=50)\nbest_params = study.best_params\n```\n\n### Step 5: Experiment Tracking with MLflow\n\nTrack experiments and metrics:\n\n```python\nimport mlflow\nimport mlflow.pytorch\nfrom mlflow.tracking import MlflowClient\n\ndef train_with_mlflow(\n    model: nn.Module,\n    train_loader: DataLoader,\n    val_loader: DataLoader,\n    experiment_name: str = \"model_training\",\n    run_name: str = None\n):\n    \"\"\"Training with MLflow tracking.\"\"\"\n    # Set experiment\n    mlflow.set_experiment(experiment_name)\n    \n    # Start run\n    with mlflow.start_run(run_name=run_name):\n        # Log hyperparameters\n        mlflow.log_params({\n            \"learning_rate\": 1e-3,\n            \"batch_size\": 32,\n            \"num_epochs\": 10,\n            \"optimizer\": \"AdamW\"\n        })\n        \n        # Training loop\n        optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n        criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n        \n        for epoch in range(10):\n            model.train()\n            train_loss = 0\n            \n            for data, target in train_loader:\n                optimizer.zero_grad()\n                outputs = model(data)\n                loss = criterion(outputs, target)\n                loss.backward()\n                optimizer.step()\n                train_loss += loss.item()\n            \n            # Validation\n            model.eval()\n            val_loss = 0\n            correct = 0\n            total = 0\n            \n            with torch.no_grad():\n                for data, target in val_loader:\n                    outputs = model(data)\n                    loss = criterion(outputs, target)\n                    val_loss += loss.item()\n                    \n                    _, predicted = torch.max(outputs.data, 1)\n                    total += target.size(0)\n                    correct += (predicted == target).sum().item()\n            \n            # Log metrics\n            mlflow.log_metrics({\n                \"train_loss\": train_loss / len(train_loader),\n                \"val_loss\": val_loss / len(val_loader),\n                \"val_accuracy\": 100 * correct / total\n            }, step=epoch)\n        \n        # Log model\n        mlflow.pytorch.log_model(model, \"model\")\n        \n        # Log artifacts\n        mlflow.log_artifact(\"./checkpoints/best_model.pt\")\n        \n        # Register model (optional)\n        mlflow.pytorch.log_model(\n            model,\n            \"model\",\n            registered_model_name=\"SimpleModel\"\n        )\n    \n    print(f\"MLflow run completed. View at: {mlflow.get_tracking_uri()}\")\n\n# Usage\ntrain_with_mlflow(model, train_loader, val_loader, experiment_name=\"my_experiment\")\n```\n\n### Step 6: Mixed Precision Training\n\nImplement automatic mixed precision (AMP):\n\n```python\nfrom torch.cuda.amp import autocast, GradScaler\n\ndef train_with_amp(\n    model: nn.Module,\n    train_loader: DataLoader,\n    num_epochs: int = 10\n):\n    \"\"\"Training with automatic mixed precision.\"\"\"\n    model = model.cuda()\n    optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=1e-3)\n    criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n    scaler = GradScaler()  # For gradient scaling\n    \n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        model.train()\n        for batch_idx, (data, target) in enumerate(train_loader):\n            data, target = data.cuda(), target.cuda()\n            \n            optimizer.zero_grad()\n            \n            # Forward pass with autocast\n            with autocast():\n                outputs = model(data)\n                loss = criterion(outputs, target)\n            \n            # Backward pass with scaler\n            scaler.scale(loss).backward()\n            scaler.step(optimizer)\n            scaler.update()\n            \n            if batch_idx % 100 == 0:\n                print(f\"Epoch {epoch}, Batch {batch_idx}, Loss: {loss.item()}\")\n```\n\n### Step 7: Checkpointing and Resume Strategies\n\nRobust checkpointing with resume capability:\n\n```python\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nclass CheckpointManager:\n    \"\"\"Manage model checkpoints and resume training.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, checkpoint_dir: str = \"./checkpoints\"):\n        self.checkpoint_dir = Path(checkpoint_dir)\n        self.checkpoint_dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n        self.best_loss = float(\"inf\")\n    \n    def save_checkpoint(\n        self,\n        model: nn.Module,\n        optimizer: torch.optim.Optimizer,\n        epoch: int,\n        loss: float,\n        is_best: bool = False,\n        metadata: dict = None\n    ):\n        \"\"\"Save checkpoint.\"\"\"\n        checkpoint = {\n            \"epoch\": epoch,\n            \"model_state_dict\": model.state_dict(),\n            \"optimizer_state_dict\": optimizer.state_dict(),\n            \"loss\": loss,\n            \"best_loss\": self.best_loss,\n            \"metadata\": metadata or {}\n        }\n        \n        # Save regular checkpoint\n        checkpoint_path = self.checkpoint_dir / f\"checkpoint_epoch_{epoch}.pt\"\n        torch.save(checkpoint, checkpoint_path)\n        \n        # Save best model\n        if is_best or loss < self.best_loss:\n            self.best_loss = loss\n            best_path = self.checkpoint_dir / \"best_model.pt\"\n            torch.save(checkpoint, best_path)\n            print(f\"Saved best model with loss: {loss:.4f}\")\n        \n        # Save latest checkpoint\n        latest_path = self.checkpoint_dir / \"latest_checkpoint.pt\"\n        torch.save(checkpoint, latest_path)\n    \n    def load_checkpoint(\n        self,\n        model: nn.Module,\n        optimizer: torch.optim.Optimizer = None,\n        checkpoint_path: str = None,\n        resume: bool = True\n    ):\n        \"\"\"Load checkpoint.\"\"\"\n        if checkpoint_path is None:\n            checkpoint_path = self.checkpoint_dir / \"latest_checkpoint.pt\"\n        \n        if not os.path.exists(checkpoint_path):\n            print(f\"No checkpoint found at {checkpoint_path}\")\n            return 0\n        \n        checkpoint = torch.load(checkpoint_path)\n        model.load_state_dict(checkpoint[\"model_state_dict\"])\n        \n        if optimizer and resume:\n            optimizer.load_state_dict(checkpoint[\"optimizer_state_dict\"])\n        \n        start_epoch = checkpoint[\"epoch\"] + 1 if resume else 0\n        self.best_loss = checkpoint.get(\"best_loss\", float(\"inf\"))\n        \n        print(f\"Loaded checkpoint from epoch {checkpoint[''epoch'']}\")\n        print(f\"Resume training from epoch {start_epoch}\")\n        \n        return start_epoch\n\n# Usage in training loop\ncheckpoint_manager = CheckpointManager()\n\n# Resume training\nstart_epoch = checkpoint_manager.load_checkpoint(model, optimizer, resume=True)\n\nfor epoch in range(start_epoch, num_epochs):\n    # Training...\n    val_loss = validate(model, val_loader)\n    \n    # Save checkpoint\n    is_best = val_loss < checkpoint_manager.best_loss\n    checkpoint_manager.save_checkpoint(\n        model=model,\n        optimizer=optimizer,\n        epoch=epoch,\n        loss=val_loss,\n        is_best=is_best,\n        metadata={\"learning_rate\": optimizer.param_groups[0][\"lr\"]}\n    )\n```\n\n## Output\n\nAfter training, you''ll have:\n\n1. **Trained Model** - Optimized model weights\n2. **Checkpoints** - Regular and best model checkpoints\n3. **Training Logs** - Metrics, losses, and training history\n4. **Hyperparameter Results** - Optimal hyperparameters from tuning\n5. **Experiment Tracking** - MLflow/W&B runs with all metrics\n6. **Resume Capability** - Ability to resume training from checkpoints\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- Always use Accelerate for simplified distributed training\n- Implement proper checkpointing and resume logic\n- Track experiments with MLflow or W&B\n- Use mixed precision (AMP) for faster training\n- Optimize hyperparameters systematically with Optuna\n- Validate data before training\n- Monitor for overfitting with validation metrics\n- Use gradient accumulation for effective larger batch sizes\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Anti-Pattern | Fix |\n|--------------|-----|\n| No checkpointing | Save checkpoints regularly |\n| No experiment tracking | Use MLflow/W&B |\n| Hardcoded hyperparameters | Use Optuna for optimization |\n| No validation | Always validate during training |\n| Sync operations in training loop | Use async/overlap operations |\n| No gradient scaling with AMP | Always use GradScaler |\n\n## Related\n\n- Knowledge: `{directories.knowledge}/pytorch-patterns.json`, `{directories.knowledge}/model-training-patterns.json`\n- Skill: `model-fine-tuning`\n- Skill: `llm-evaluation`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T10:24:07.850Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Deep Learning Agents needing advanced PyTorch training capabilities with Accelerate and distributed training support","zh":"适合需要高级 PyTorch 训练功能和分布式训练支持的深度学习代理","ja":"PyTorch の高度なトレーニング機能と分散トレーニングのサポートを必要とするディープラーニングエージェントに最適","ko":"고급 PyTorch 훈련 기능과 분산 훈련 지원이 필요한 딥러닝 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de aprendizaje profundo que necesitan capacidades de entrenamiento avanzadas de PyTorch con Accelerate y soporte de entrenamiento distribuido","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''apprentissage profond nécessitant des capacités de formation avancées de PyTorch avec Accelerate et un support de formation distribuée","de":"Perfekt für Deep-Learning-Agents, die erweiterte PyTorch-Trainingsfunktionen mit Accelerate und Unterstützung für verteiltes Training benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de aprendizado profundo que necessitam de capa